window.AKK_BEAUTIFUL_MOTHER_FORCE_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_BEAUTIFUL_MOTHER_FORCE_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":101,"title":"Chapter 101","paragraphs":["Ever since the fire stick incident, Dai Li's position in Qin Qinian's heart had skyrocketed.","Not to mention she was the first woman he knew who dared to call his father by his given name and even kicked him.","What did Lady Dai take seriously?","Itching with curiosity, Qin Qinian immediately lightened his footsteps, quietly approached the courtyard entrance, and crouched there to eavesdrop.","As a result, he listened for quite a while, but Uncle Mo just kept repeating the same two sentences like a broken record: something about Lady Dai taking it seriously, and something about regretting his thoughtless words at the time.","Then the others offered comfort one after another, saying things like nothing happened now, so it didn't matter.","It made Qin Qinian feel terrible just listening to it.","What on earth was going on!","Could they explain the cause and effect clearly! Speaking in riddles like this was truly maddening.","Seeing that they seemed about to change the subject, Qin Qinian got anxious and simply jumped out, \"Uncle Mo, what guilty conscience do you have? What did Lady Dai take seriously?\"","In the courtyard, several people were all startled.","There were patrols in the mansion day and night, and anyone slightly suspicious would be caught. But apparently, this did not include the well-known restless Third Young Master. As long as he didn't climb over the wall, the patrols wouldn't bother him at all.","Mo Yanyun looked at the suddenly appearing youth, his pupils shaking with shock, directly freezing in place.","The others also had faces full of astonishment, secretly thinking \"oh no\" in unison.","The courtyard was dead silent, the few people frozen in place like stone statues, with only two withered yellow leaves blowing and rolling on the ground by the autumn wind.","Qin Qinian tilted his head, \"Why aren't any of you talking?\"","The mountains and rivers in Mo Yanyun's heart collapsed, the sound of the crash deafening.","\"Ahem, it's because Lao Mo previously recommended a delicacy to Lady Dai, and Lady Dai took it seriously, but it turned out there was a difference in taste between the north and south, so it didn't suit her appetite,\" Feng Feng coughed to cover up.","Qin Qinian was dissatisfied, \"Do you still think I'm a child? I'm not that easy to fool. Lady Dai is very gentle, she wouldn't mind such a trivial matter. And it wouldn't cause Uncle Mo to not get a good night's sleep since entering the mansion?\"","Mo Yanyun: \"...\"","Seeing them not speaking, Qin Qinian turned to leave, \"If you won't tell me, I'll go ask her. She even taught me how to make fire sticks today. She's willing to teach me such secrets, so she must be willing to tell me other things.\"","His leaving scared Mo Yanyun out of his wits.","Mo Yanyun was still standing in place, but the person had already been gone for a while.","Seeing this, Bai Jianping and Feng Feng quickly rushed forward together, each grabbing one of Qin Qinian's arms, forcefully dragging him back.","\"Third Young Master, you absolutely must not mention this matter to Lady Dai,\" Bai Jianping said in a low voice.","\"Why?\" Qin Qinian pouted, \"You won't tell me, and you won't let me ask anyone else?\"","Feng Feng drew a sharp breath, \"Do you know Lady Dai's background?\"","Qin Qinian paused, feeling there was a hidden meaning in his words, \"I don't know. What is her background?\"","In the early years, his eldest uncle died in battle, and his father became the heir of the clan. Later, his grandfather and grandmother passed away one after another, and his father took on the entire Qin clan by himself.","Since then, he had fought in the north and south, suppressing bandits in Mount Bolei in the south, fiercely attacking the northern tribes in the north, and dealing with the difficulties of Bingzhou and Jizhou.","Compared to other clan leaders or powerful figures, his father's offspring and concubines were pitifully few. He only had one biological son, and the concubines in the backyard could be counted on one hand.","And in this world, there were only a few ways for concubines to enter the backyard: buying them with gold and silver, being given as gifts by friends, or being rewarded by elders in the clan or superiors.","Oh, and there was also when a daughter of a humble family caught someone's eye and was taken away with a promise of money. This could barely be classified under buying with gold and silver.","Qin Qinian asked, \"Was she given to my father by officials from other provinces?\"","Several people shook their heads in unison.","\"If she wasn't a gift from a friend, could she have been bought?\" Qin Qinian said.","After speaking, he felt it was impossible. Lady Dai was more beautiful than any woman he had ever seen. Such a great beauty had no reason to be without a husband, and her son was already so old.","Even if his father really bought her, there was no reason to bring her son back as well.","\"I know!\" Qin Qinian made a fist with his right hand and struck his left palm.","\"It must be that Lady Dai's family encountered bandits on the road, and in the midst of danger, when her life was hanging by a thread, my father appeared out of nowhere and played the hero saving the beauty! Lady Dai fell in love with my father at first sight, was deeply grateful, and offered herself to him. Plus, her husband happened to perish, so she and her son followed my father,\" Qin Qinian said with certainty.","Mo Yanyun: \"...\"","Bai Jianping: \"...\"","Feng Feng: \"...\"","Kuang Ye: \"...\"","The surroundings were dead silent. Qin Qinian looked at this one, then at that one, \"What are these expressions on your faces? Am I wrong?\"","\"Your imagination is quite good, but next time, don't guess,\" Bai Jianping wiped his face.","Qin Qinian frowned, unhappy, \"You won't tell me, and you won't let me guess. Isn't it a hero saving a beauty? That doesn't make sense! My father has unparalleled martial arts and illustrious military merits. Isn't it normal for a woman to be infatuated with him in times of danger?\"","Seeing them not speaking again, Qin Qinian was extremely confused, \"So what exactly is her background?\"","Seeing that he wouldn't give up until he reached the Yellow River, Feng Feng knew that the Third Young Master wouldn't get an answer from them and would definitely go ask Lady Dai.","But was that something he could ask?!","Feng Feng sighed heavily, \"Then I'll make a long story short. Third Young Master, just listen to it as a story, and let it go after you hear it.\"","Actually, Lady Dai's background was previously a mystery in the eyes of Feng Feng and the others, as well as Mo Yanyun, who had stayed in the Jiang Mansion with Qin Shaozong.","But after the dragon bone waterwheel was introduced, they all unanimously believed that Lady Dai was a woman from a hidden village, who came out to find her son and offer treasures along the way, only to happen upon their Lord.","As a result, the Lord immediately grabbed her and wouldn't let go.","Qin Qinian urged, \"Alright, then hurry up and tell me.\"","\"Lady Dai is the descendant of a great hermit. She came out to find her son and offer treasures. The world-renowned Xian stone was created by her hands, and the previous dragon bone waterwheel was also presented by her to the Lord,\" Feng Feng said.","Qin Qinian drew a sharp breath.","Feng Feng looked away, not daring to look at Qin Qinian, \"After seeing Lady Dai, the Lord forced her to stay. She left twice, but both times the Lord led troops to chase her back.\"","Qin Qinian froze for a few breaths, then jumped up as if pricked by a needle, sharply rebutting, \"Impossible! You must be talking nonsense. How could my father do such a shameless thing as forcibly taking another man's wife!\"","Everyone: \"...\"","How should they respond to this? It seemed inappropriate no matter how they responded.","\"Ancestor, I beg you to keep your voice down,\" Mo Yanyun almost knelt before him.","Kuang Ye's gentle puppy eyes darted around, directly skipping the middle and leaving a conclusion, \"Anyway, Lady Dai didn't want to move into the Lord's mansion, so the Lord chose a residence not far from the Ding Mansion, which also made it convenient to treat Young Master Qin's illness.\"","Normally, at this point, the Third Young Master's attention should have shifted elsewhere.","For example, asking about Young Master Qin's illness, or asking about the various past events between Lady Dai and the Lord. Asking anything was fine, as long as he didn't focus on the matters of \"Lao Mo\" and \"Lady Dai taking it seriously\" anymore.","However, today the Third Young Master, perhaps overwhelmed by the massive amount of information, simply threw it all to the back of his mind and went straight back to the beginning.","He muttered, \"So what does it have to do with Uncle Mo, and what did Lady Dai take 'seriously'?\"","Kuang Ye: \"...\"","Qin Qinian muttered to himself, \"Could it be that Uncle Mo told her that the people in my father's manor are hard to get along with?\"","The others jumped in fright; this was not something to be spoken blindly.","\"Of course not,\" Feng Feng said hastily.","Seeing that Qin Qinian wanted to get to the bottom of it, Kuang Ye simply said, \"It's because Lady Dai was reluctant to come back at first, and Lao Mo, at his wits' end, casually said that living outside was freer and she wouldn't have to abide by the rules of the Marquis's Manor.\"","Qin Qinian suddenly understood; so that was it.","\"So in the end, the reason Lady Dai is here now is partly due to Lao Mo, which is why he's been losing sleep and appetite over it,\" Kuang Ye said.","Finally, they begged him not to tell anyone else about this, saying that after all, this was a private matter between the Marquis and Lady Dai, and it wouldn't be appropriate for others to hear.","Qin Qinian nodded repeatedly and then left.","Mo Yanyun and the others breathed a sigh of relief, feeling like they had survived.","But they never expected that while Qin Qinian indeed didn't tell \"others,\" he went straight back to find Dai Li.","Lady Dai was the person involved, so she didn't count as an \"other,\" right?","...","\"...So, you were really forced to stay by my father?\" Qin Qinian sat upright and still.","Compared to the previous time when Qin Shaozong had practically forced his head down to bow, Qin Qinian was much more restrained now, even carrying an indescribable sense of caution.","Dai Li could see that he was sitting on pins and needles, and connecting it to how he had rushed over just now and couldn't hold back from asking about her and Qin Shaozong right away.","She guessed this child had heard something from elsewhere.","Dai Li picked up the cup on the table and took a sip, speaking under the other's nervous gaze, \"At first, yes, but later the Marquis and I reached another agreement, so it's a different matter.\"","The poison in Zhou Zhou's body was something she hadn't anticipated, and the way things had spiraled out of control to this day was completely outside her plans.","As for the future...","The current Dai Li hadn't thought about the future; her mind was entirely focused on quickly curing her son's Gu poison so he could live the rest of his life in peace.","Qin Qinian's face burned hot.","Recalling the words he had said before, he felt as if ants were crawling all over him, not just crawling, but biting him hard.","Previously, he had boasted shamelessly, saying his father would kick her out of the manor and that she wouldn't even have a place to cry. But it wasn't that she wanted to stay here; it was clearly his father who wouldn't let her leave.","They say a son paying his father's debts is perfectly justified. Not only did he not pay his father's debts, but he actually spoke wildly to her. No wonder his father had even said he wouldn't let him go to the military camp in the future.","\"I, I didn't mean to say those things that day...\" Qin Qinian lowered his head.","He didn't specify which day, but Dai Li understood immediately. Because it wasn't hard to guess; apart from the first day when this young man had \"spouted nonsense,\" he had been quite well-behaved around her for the past few days.","Dai Li wouldn't hold a grudge against a child, \"It's fine.\"","\"Could I ask you some other questions?\" Qin Qinian asked softly.","Dai Li glanced at the sky outside.","Her son's treatment took four hours at a time, and there was still a bit of time left before it ended, so she could chat with this kid for a bit longer, \"Ask away, but I might not answer you.\"","*","In the study.","\"Marquis, the Commandery Chief Clerk, Wei Congmu, requests an audience,\" Hu Bao reported.","Qin Shaozong, holding a brush, didn't stop his movements.","Qin Yunce turned to look at Qin Shaozong, \"Father, it seems Cai Yuan leaked a little information when he left, otherwise why would the Wei family come so quickly?\"","When Cai Yuan entered the room, Qin Yunce had been standing at the door and heard the conversation inside clearly. Cai Yuan wasn't a fool; he would never leak the matter of reorganizing the military farms, but he probably revealed some peripheral information.","For example, that he had met the Marquis of Wu'an.","Other people who came to visit were all received by Qin Yunce; none of them got to see Qin Shaozong.","\"It's entirely possible, and probably all sides are competing now,\" Qin Shaozong put down his wolf-hair brush and called his subordinate, \"Hu Bao, have someone deliver this stack of letters on the left to Qing Province by fast horse, the middle ones to Si Province, and the right ones to Ji Province.\"","Recently, the Xuan Cavalry had split into many small teams and, based on the information provided by Qin Yanzhou, headed straight for the various strongholds of the Green Lotus Sect.","They searched what needed to be searched and arrested who needed to be arrested.","Although they hadn't found that holy hand skilled in making medicine, it wasn't entirely fruitless. At the very least, during this search, they caught some people secretly forging armor.","Great Yan allowed private individuals to forge some short weapons, such as swords and bows, which were fine for self-defense or hunting. But it strictly forbade commoners from manufacturing defensive military weapons like leather armor.","Although Qin Shaozong had returned to Yuyang, his control over the other provinces hadn't relaxed at all. He had a cavalry unit dedicated to transmitting messages and kept a very tight grip on this aspect.","Anyone found privately forging armor was thrown into prison.","He wasn't in a hurry to chop off their heads, but he used heavy torture to make them spit out more information.","Since the Green Lotus Sect dared to target the Ding Manor, repeatedly poisoning and assassinating, he could also make them restless.","Hu Bao cupped his hands in obedience.","After giving the orders, Qin Shaozong stood up from his seat, \"Yunce, you receive Wei Congmu. Just say a few words and dismiss him.\"","\"Yes, Father,\" Qin Yunce watched the tall back leave, taking a long time to look away.","He never doubted his uncle's methods; as long as his uncle wanted something, those things would eventually go his way, even if there were heavy obstacles.","He felt that the Marquis's Manor might soon have a mistress.","Qin Yunce covered his lips and coughed twice, then got up and went to the main hall, \"Go invite the Commandery Chief Clerk in.\"","\"Yes.\"","...","Qin Shaozong left the main hall, estimating that the brat Qin Yanzhou's acupuncture session was about to end. She would definitely go to pick him up, and if he went back to the main courtyard now, he would probably be a step late, so he might as well go straight there.","The pavilion where the acupuncture was taking place was on the other side. After leaving the study, Qin Shaozong didn't follow the corridor properly but cut straight through the other pavilions.","Pavilions didn't just have one entrance; they often had small back doors. Qin Shaozong walked through the pavilions.","Just as he reached the middle section, the man vaguely heard voices coming from next door. His five senses were much sharper than an ordinary person's, so he immediately recognized Mo Yanyun's voice.","The sound reaching here wasn't very clear, and at first, Qin Shaozong didn't intend to pay attention to it.","Conversations between military generals were too common. Those with good relationships often gathered together to chat about everything under the sun.","But right at that moment, Qin Shaozong heard the words \"Lady Dai.\" Thinking of Mo Yanyun's past behavior regarding women, the man's footsteps paused, and his gaze darkened.","He didn't continue walking towards the entrance but leaned against the wall to listen quietly.","\"Fortunately, the Third Young Master believed what you said just now, Kuang Ye. If the Marquis had been present... heh, you wouldn't have been able to hide anything; he would have seen right through to see if there was a hidden story.\"","\"Lao Mo, be more careful in the future. Don't let your mouth run loose and say whatever comes to mind. Daring to make things up about the Marquis, I think you really have a death wish. You're lucky this time, otherwise, you really couldn't be saved.\"","They deliberately skirted around the main point in their conversation. Qin Shaozong listened for a while but couldn't glean any specific details.","The man raised a long eyebrow and pushed himself off the wall.","...","In the adjacent courtyard.","Bai Jianping patted Mo Yanyun on the shoulder. \"Fools have their own kind of luck. Anyway, this matter is in the past now. None of us should ever bring it up again.\"","\"How exactly is it in the past? Why don't you enlighten me.\" A deep male voice drifted in from the courtyard entrance.","In that instant, it was as if a bolt of lightning had struck. The few men in the courtyard felt their hair stand on end as they froze dead in their tracks.","One breath, two breaths...","Bai Jianping swiftly retracted the hand still resting on Mo Yanyun's shoulder, simultaneously taking a step to the side to put some distance between them.","The others moved in unison with him, everyone darting away in a flash. An empty circle instantly formed around Mo Yanyun.","Mo Yanyun himself was still completely bewildered.","Qin Shaozong's gaze swept over the group. One by one, they hastily bowed their heads, staring at the dirt as if there were silver coins to be found.","\"Mo Yanyun, you are the one involved. You tell me.\"","Qin Shaozong called him out directly. \"Tell me the truth, and don't bother spinning lies. If there is even a single false word, you can kiss your Commandant title goodbye and go back to plowing the fields.\"","Mo Yanyun's face turned pale, then green, then pale again.","For a moment, he genuinely didn't know if it would be better to go back to farming or to confess everything. With the former, he might lose his military post, but at least he would keep his life. As for the latter... that was hard to say."]},{"number":102,"title":"Chapter 102","paragraphs":["The courtyard was dead silent. After Qin Shaozong said \"go back to farming,\" he stopped speaking and just stood quietly at the courtyard gate, looking at Mo Yanyun.","The aura of a ruler who had fought his way out of a storm of blood and gore was heavy and overwhelming, like mountains and seas. Even without saying a word, just staring coldly at someone was enough to make them break out in a cold sweat.","Mo Yanyun was sweating profusely. He kept his head down, glancing out of the corners of his eyes to the left and right, but could only see the tips of his brothers' boots.","Each one was standing further away than the last, and some were even quietly shuffling further away.","Mo Yanyun was screaming in panic internally. Great, they had promised to share blessings and hardships, but now that disaster was upon him, they were all scattering?","Feng Feng was still sneaking away, thinking to himself that taking a blade for him on the battlefield was fine, but facing the Lord's furious wrath... well, he'd better bear it alone.","These heavy thoughts passed in merely a few breaths.","Mo Yanyun thought left and right but couldn't find a way out. Finally, he simply fell to his knees with a thud before Qin Shaozong. \"This subordinate begs the Lord for forgiveness. I ask the Lord to consider that the situation was urgent at the time, and I had no choice but to take a risky move. Please spare my life.\"","Originally, Qin Shaozong only felt that Mo Yanyun was hiding something. Since the matter involved his wife, and hearing that they had previously fooled Qin San, he had developed a bit of curiosity.","At first, he didn't think it was a big deal. The reason he acted so sternly was purely because he disliked subordinates deceiving him, and he wanted to know everything related to her.","As a result, Mo Yanyun even said things like \"spare my life.\" Qin Shaozong immediately realized that the severity of this matter might far exceed his expectations.","His mind raced through countless twists and turns, but Qin Shaozong remained expressionless. \"What risky move did you make?\"","Mo Yanyun swallowed hard. \"Back when Lady Dai left Xiagu with Young Master Qin, after I was discovered tailing them in the eastern suburbs, Lady Dai said those things to me...\"","Qin Shaozong knew what she had said.","She said she was unwilling to be a concubine.","Thinking about it now, there must have been a continuation, but Mo Yanyun hadn't mentioned it at the time.","Qin Shaozong merely hummed in response, showing no emotional fluctuation.","Mo Yanyun's head drooped even lower. \"Lady Dai seemed determined to leave. I couldn't help but tell her that the Lord's manor hadn't had a mistress for many years, and with your attitude towards her, she could walk sideways in the manor in the future without any problems. Lady Dai was still unwilling at the time, so I... I told her that it wouldn't be impossible for her and Young Master Qin to live outside.\"","The veins on Qin Shaozong's forehead throbbed.","No wonder she wanted to live outside the manor; so this was the source.","Seeing Qin Shaozong's face darken, Kuang Ye and the others knew things were bad. They frequently looked at Mo Yanyun, trying to give him a look.","He should have stopped here, because it was enough. The following words absolutely could not be said.","But Mo Yanyun was kneeling with his head down, a grown man wishing he could shrink into the ground.","His personality was more straightforward than the others, lacking their slickness. Feng Feng and the others thought they should sugarcoat it, but Mo Yanyun was solely focused on how to say the rest as tactfully as possible.","\"I praised your stern heroics and extraordinary appearance to Lady Dai. In terms of power and looks, no one in the entire North can match you. If she lived outside and occasionally met with you, she definitely wouldn't lose out...\" Mo Yanyun's voice grew lower and lower.","Qin Shaozong was such a sharp person. First there was \"living outside,\" then \"looks\" and \"lose out.\"","Especially the phrase \"lose out,\" which was like a little man armed with sharp blades, dancing madly on his nerves.","Qin Shaozong's mind buzzed.","He, the dignified patriarch of the Qin clan, had once flattened nations infested with hungry wolves with his iron cavalry. Step by step on the battlefield, he earned the Han Emperor's enfeoffment, and now controlled vast territories north of Yanzhou.","What did she mean by not losing out? Was he putting up a sign to sell himself?","He knew very well that Mo Yanyun's words had definitely been polished; the original words must have been even more explicit and wanton.","Qin Shaozong flew into a rage. \"Mo Yanyun, are you tired of living? If there's nothing else in this world you're attached to, just say it, and I'll end you with one strike.\"","Mo Yanyun was terrified. \"Lord, please spare my life for the sake of Lady Dai living peacefully since returning to Yuyang.\"","Hearing this, Bai Jianping and the others nearby twitched their lips.","What was this fool saying? Lady Dai living peacefully was partly because she had nowhere to run, but mainly because the Lord was helping treat Young Master Qin's illness.","Look at what he was saying, as if he had made some massive contribution.","The courtyard was silent for a moment before Qin Shaozong spoke. \"What was her reaction at the time?\"","Everyone was stunned.","\"Lady Dai didn't reply,\" Mo Yanyun recalled.","Qin Shaozong asked again, \"Did she show any surprise or shyness on her face?\"","Mo Yanyun tried hard to remember. \"It seems not.\"","\"You're in charge of cleaning the manor's stables for this month and the next,\" Qin Shaozong said coldly.","With that, he turned and left. The autumn wind lifted a corner of his black robe, its arc looking cold and severe.","In the courtyard, Mo Yanyun looked up in disbelief. \"I... I don't have to go back home to farm?\"","Compared to going home to farm and never being able to earn military merits on the battlefield again, what was washing stables for two months!","Just as he finished speaking, someone kicked him in the rear from behind. \"You really lucked out. It seems the Lord is in an exceptionally good mood today, to have so much thunder but so little rain.\"","Mo Yanyun fell flat on his face, but he wasn't angry. He chuckled cheerfully, \"Perhaps the Lord felt my words made a bit of sense, or maybe it was for Lady Dai's sake that he let me off the hook.\"","He let out a long breath. \"Regardless, a heavy burden has been lifted from my mind. I can sleep soundly tonight.\"","\"Sleep my ass, you have to go wash the stables tonight.\"","...","When Dai Li arrived at the pavilion courtyard, her son's treatment had not yet ended.","She waited for a while. She didn't see Qin Yanzhou come out, but instead saw Qin Shaozong walking in from outside.","His clothes were mostly black and gray. The heavy colors matched his own oppressive aura. Combined with the intimidation brought by his height, whenever he appeared, it was hard for anyone to ignore him.","\"Madam,\" a deep male voice came, revealing no obvious emotion.","Dai Li had spent day and night with him, and immediately sensed something different in his tone. She turned to look into those brown eyes and didn't speak, waiting for his next words.","Qin Shaozong indeed had a follow-up. \"Back at the Ding residence, Madam once said, 'If only there were an airplane here, traveling back and forth between the north and south in a single day wouldn't be a problem.' Madam, what is an airplane, and why wouldn't traveling between the north and south in a single day be a problem?\"","Dai Li froze. This matter had passed for over a week. She had felt terrible right after muttering it back then.","Qin Shaozong was so close to her at the time; he definitely heard it. But strangely, she waited and waited, day after day, yet never heard him mention it at all.","Since he didn't bring it up, Dai Li was happy to be at ease and certainly wouldn't take the initiative to talk about it.","She thought the page had been turned, never expecting him to bring it up now, remembering it word for word until this moment.","Dai Li pursed her lips, trying to bluff her way through. \"What airplane? What traveling between the north and south? I never said such a thing.\"","Qin Shaozong stared at her unblinkingly. \"Aside from me, there was also a maid who heard it at the time. Does Madam wish to see her?\"","Dai Li's brow twitched, not expecting there to be another witness. \"Then she...\"","\"Even if she tells others, they would only think she is speaking nonsense and wouldn't believe her.\" Qin Shaozong spun the jade thumb ring on his finger.","Dai Li swallowed the rest of her words.","\"Madam,\" he said, the two heavy words pressing down.","Dai Li furrowed her brows and then relaxed them, truly unable to grasp this man's thoughts.","If he was just intensely curious, why didn't he ask back then, choosing instead to wait until now? Could it be that something happened just now that provoked him...","There was no one else around. Nianxia and Bipo were waiting outside and hadn't followed Dai Li in. Qin Qinian had gone off to show off his fire starter and hadn't accompanied her either.","They were the only two in the courtyard.","It was as if the secret of the \"Peach Blossom Spring\" was known only to the two of them.","Dai Li sighed, knowing he wouldn't rest until he got an answer. \"Qin Changgeng, you can think of an airplane as being made of iron, capable of carrying many people at once, and controlled by humans... like a Quru.\"","She hesitated slightly on the last word.","Quru was a strange bird from the Classic of Mountains and Seas. This bizarre bird looked like a wild duck, had a white head, and possessed three feet.","Dai Li's answer was quite abstract, but Qin Shaozong didn't accuse her of speaking nonsense. Instead, he asked, \"A Quru is a bird that can soar through the highest heavens. Madam says the airplane is made of iron. Doesn't that mean it weighs thousands of tons itself?\"","Dai Li nodded. \"Indeed.\"","Qin Shaozong asked again, \"Since it can carry many people, how big is it?\"","Dai Li recalled the behemoths she used to ride. \"There are large ones and small ones; it cannot be generalized. The largest can be up to eight zhang tall, with a wingspan of about twenty-one zhang, and a length from head to tail of around fifteen zhang, capable of carrying nearly a thousand people at once. The smallest is less than two zhang long and can only carry one person.\"","Qin Shaozong fell silent.","Dai Li glanced at him, completely understanding his silence at this moment.","In the world of the ancients, saying that thousands of tons of iron could fly in the sky was really no different from claiming to summon wind and rain, achieve immortality, or ascend to the heavens to become an immortal.","How to put it? Although she had briefly told him about the \"Peach Blossom Spring\" before, it was simply not on the same scale.","The matter of the \"airplane\" and \"traveling back and forth between the north and south in a single day\" could not be glossed over. Dai Li currently lacked the energy to make up a story to deceive him, so she decided to just tell the truth.","As for whether he believed it or not, that was Qin Shaozong's own business.","Of course, Dai Li was also prepared for him to continue asking questions.","This man was ambitious; what he plotted for was not merely a corner of the land or a small city.","From the Northern Lands, to selling refined salt to merchants across the realm with Ying Commandery as the core, and then to allying with Qingzhou to jointly attack Yanzhou.","Every step he took landed precisely on the path to hegemony. This path was paved with blood and rain, swords and shadows, where the slightest carelessness would lead to eternal damnation.","And now, a fork had appeared on this long, thorny path. Standing at this intersection, one could vaguely see a quiet shortcut, unknown to outsiders.","In Dai Li's expectations, Qin Shaozong would have many questions next.","He might ask how airplanes are built. What weapons are used in the Peach Blossom Spring? Or he might ask again where the Peach Blossom Spring is, and besides her, who else comes from that isolated utopia.","However...","\"Madam, in this world there are brothels for men. Are there brothels for women in the Peach Blossom Spring?\" After a long silence, Qin Shaozong blurted out this sentence.","At this moment, Dai Li's eyes widened slightly, unable to stop the astonishment from showing on her face.","Her expression was so shocked, as if she were meeting him for the first day, that Qin Shaozong couldn't help but laugh, instantly dissipating nearly half of the suffocating gloom gathered in his chest.","\"Why is Madam looking at me like that?\" Qin Shaozong chuckled.","He clearly understood her bewilderment and current silence, yet he still asked despite knowing the answer.","Dai Li opened her mouth, having much she wanted to say, but failed to utter a single sentence.","Qin Shaozong looked up at the sky. The azure dome was cloudless for miles, as clean as a boundless scroll waiting for someone to freely splash ink and paint the rivers and mountains of the entire world.","\"A true man born in troubled times should carry a three-foot sword to establish unparalleled merits. Forcing a woman to be used for one's own ends is the behavior of a base villain. Dai Li, I admit that the various rarities in the Peach Blossom Spring are exceptionally unique, and every single one invites exploration. If you are willing to tell me, I will naturally be overjoyed and treat it as a precious treasure. But if you do not wish to speak of it, let it be. I will just treat it as a dream, a beautiful dream that the common people of the world might have in the future.\"","Dai Li's pupils trembled slightly.","It was hard for her to describe the feeling of this moment. It was somewhat like a sudden realization, suddenly understanding why the Northern Army was full of talents, and why even someone as noble and pure as the clear breeze and bright moon like Nalan Zhi was willing to serve him.","In his bones, Qin Shaozong possessed a considerable degree of arrogance, which was his sense of responsibility as a person in power. He could shoulder burdens himself, possessed certain principles, and disdained crossing the line.","It also felt like a touch from time, as if an invisible screen had suddenly risen between her and him.","The long river of time was entirely compressed within it; he stood on this side from a thousand years ago, and she stood on the other side, a thousand years in the future.","With their conversation, and with that final word \"future,\" this invisible barrier rippled like water.","Every ripple was a fold in time, sweeping across thousands of years, reflecting the rise and fall of dynasties.","Finally, a new era appeared in the ripples, where a forest of high-rise buildings could be faintly seen, and countless women wearing professional attire moved in and out of government offices and workplaces.","Dai Li smiled unconsciously. \"Yes, it is indeed a beautiful dream of the future.\"","Qin Shaozong looked at the upward curve of her lips, feeling a strange and unfamiliar sensation at this moment.","It wasn't a cold alienation that pushed people thousands of miles away, but something profoundly mysterious. She was clearly close at hand, yet at this moment, she was enveloped in an unattainable sense of distance.","\"Creak.\" At this time, the door over there opened.","Qin Yanzhou and Ding Luying came out one after the other.","Seeing this, Dai Li hurried up to meet them. As she walked past Qin Shaozong, she casually tossed back a few words: \"There are indeed brothels for women there, quite a few of them, for one to choose as they please. However, the past has become the wind, and there is nothing more to say about it now.\"","Qin Shaozong's face instantly darkened, and a spiderweb of cracks immediately appeared on the jade thumb ring in his hand.","A breeze blew past, curling up a corner of the woman's dress ahead, and scattering the fine jade dust falling from between the man's fingers behind.","*","Meanwhile, on the other side.","Wei Congmu walked out of the Qin Manor with a face full of sorrow. He had unexpectedly still failed to see the Marquis of Wu'an this time.","Could that Cai Yuan be bluffing?","In fact, he probably hadn't seen the Marquis of Wu'an at all. What he said earlier about meeting him and receiving guidance was likely just a ploy to make him burn with anxiety.","Thinking that the matter regarding his younger brother remained unresolved, Wei Congmu suddenly felt a wave of headache.","However, two days later, the Wei family was shocked to discover that what they had to worry about was not just the mess of Wei Conglin killing someone after drinking. It also included some of the Wei family's farmlands and various unspeakable illicit dealings hidden from outsiders.","Cai Yuan, as the Agricultural Commandant, was in charge of military agricultural colonies and grain production.","The colony farming system was implemented by the imperial court to accumulate grain to feed the army, utilizing soldiers and landless peasants to reclaim and cultivate wasteland. This system could be divided into three types: military colonies, civilian colonies, and merchant colonies.","The so-called military colonies involved soldiers transforming into farmers during non-combat periods, with the land cultivated entirely by the military.","Civilian colonies were managed by agricultural officials who recruited commoners to farm. After submitting a portion of the harvested grain to the state, the hired farmers kept the rest for themselves.","As for merchant colonies, they were not much different from civilian ones, except the initiatives were led by merchants seeking the lucrative profits of state salt licenses rather than by agricultural officials.","Overall, under strict supervision, this system was tantamount to installing several tireless grain-producing machines, constantly churning out food day and night.","However, everything has its pros and cons, and the colony farming system had its drawbacks as well.","Although the commoners participating in the colonies were exempt from military service and corvee labor, once supervision became lax, the system became highly susceptible to corruption and exploitation.","The prominent noble families had existed for a long time. Like towering trees, their roots plunged deep into the lower echelons of society, twisted and thoroughly intertwined with one another.","When water is too clear, there are no fish. It was not that Qin Shaozong was unaware of the dirty deeds and corruption hidden within; he could only tighten their leashes from time to time to keep them in check.","This time, a conflict happened to break out between the Cai and Wei families. While having the Cai family demonstrate his stance, Qin Shaozong conveniently used their hands to purge a batch of corrupt parasites.","It was truly killing two birds with one stone."]},{"number":103,"title":"Chapter 103","paragraphs":["Days passed by, and in a flash, a month and a half had gone.","Qiao Wangfei, who had been sent south, would send back letters by fast horse every ten days, reporting the situation along the way and the medicinal materials collected.","The list of medicinal materials would be sent directly to Dai Li.","Dai Li also had a copy of the three-page list of medicinal materials written by Mr. Ding earlier, and she would read it twice a day.","The happiest thing was to hold the letters from Qiao Wangfei and Jin Duole in one hand and a cinnabar pen in the other, and put small red checks on the spread-out list.","For all the medicinal materials that had been found and met the required quantity, Dai Li marked them all with small red checks.","After carefully reading all the letters, Dai Li would recopy three lists and write down all the collected ones.","Two copies were rushed to Qiao Wangfei and Jin Duole by fast horse to synchronize their information databases, and the other copy was kept for herself.","There were still twenty-two days left, less than a month. Dai Li sat in front of the desk, holding a wolf-hair brush, copying the last list.","She hoped that when the next letter came, they would all disappear from the mulberry paper.","There were hurried footsteps outside, and Nianxia rushed in at this time. She had just called out \"Madam\" when she found that Qin Shaozong was also there. She couldn't help but behave much better and didn't dare to shout like before.","Dai Li was writing and didn't look up.","Qin Shaozong looked at Nianxia, \"Why are you in such a hurry?\"","There was no displeasure on his face, but Nianxia was terrified and subconsciously lowered her head to avoid those oppressive brown eyes.","\"Lord Marquis, just now when I went out to the market to buy things, I was accidentally bumped by a young lady in the crowd. Later, I realized that there was an extra piece of silk in the basket.\" Nianxia said.","More than a month had passed, and the Marquis of Wu'an had completely \"turned the corner\". The mansion was not under martial law as it was at the beginning, and there were more servants going out to purchase than before.","The servants were accompanied by guards, so they were not worried about being caught and interrogated on the way. It was just that in a crowded place like the downtown area, pushing and shoving were inevitable when passing by.","After returning to the mansion, Nianxia was surprised to find something else in the basket—","An extra piece of silk.","There were words on the cloth. Nianxia didn't know how to read, so she hurriedly came to Dai Li.","Dai Li thought of how the Green Lotus Sect had previously used a silk letter, and she immediately stopped writing, \"Bring it to me to see.\"","Nianxia hurriedly presented it.","Qin Shaozong said expressionlessly, \"Before leaving the mansion, I had already instructed you to pay more attention to the people who came into contact with you. Why did you still let others take advantage of the loophole?\"","It was not a heavy sentence, but it scared Nianxia so much that her legs trembled, \"Lord, Lord Marquis, the young lady I bumped into at that time was brightly dressed, with fair skin and no calluses on her hands. She looked like a noble lady from a wealthy family, so I...\"","\"Forget it, it's normal to be careless for a moment. The weather is getting cooler. Nianxia, go to the kitchen and ask them to put two more slices of ginger in the soup to dispel the cold.\"","Dai Li said.","Nianxia felt as if she had been granted amnesty and hurried away.","Dai Li turned the silk over, face up.","Perhaps to cover people's eyes and ears at first, they didn't use cinnabar as ink this time, but a plant dye with a color similar to silk.","[Polygonum multiflorum, musk. The Marquis of Wu'an doesn't have enough.]","It was as if something exploded in Dai Li's mind, deafening her to the sounds around her and the words of anyone else.","The reason was none other than that there were indeed these two medicinal materials in the list of medicinal materials she had just recopied and hadn't found yet.","Polygonum multiflorum was known as one of the four major fairy grasses, and its preciousness went without saying.","What bothered Dai Li even more was that Polygonum multiflorum seemed to grow mostly in the south. At least Jin Duole had been searching in the north for fifty-five days and only found a piece of Polygonum multiflorum smaller than a baby's palm.","As for musk, it had to be extracted from the growth glands or scent glands of male musk deer, and a male deer could produce at most thirty grams. Therefore, musk was listed as a \"top-grade medicine\" in the Shennong Ben Cao Jing, and only the nobility and the royal family could have it.","The plain hand holding the silk tightly was suddenly held.","The palm covered with thick calluses wrapped around her, and a steady stream of warmth came over. With a little clever force, it loosened her knuckles that were white from tightening.","\"Madam, we still have time.\" Qin Shaozong was originally sitting beside Dai Li, but now he spread his arms and pulled her into his arms.","The black robe and the smoky purple skirt overlapped. From a distance, it looked like a picture scroll blending dark and bright colors. The dark color was the trunk on the unlit side, supporting that bright color like a flower.","Dai Li subconsciously tightened her grip on his hand, \"There are still twenty-two days before the deadline given by Mr. Ding. The time is neither near nor far. The Green Lotus Sect dares to send a message at this time, so they must be confident. The musk produced by a single musk deer is not much, and it is as timid as a mouse. Its hearing and smell are very developed, and it is extremely difficult to catch.\"","\"Don't worry, it will be solved.\" Qin Shaozong said in a low voice.","Suddenly, Dai Li let go of his hand and turned sideways to look at him, \"Qin Changgeng, I want to...\"","\"You can't.\" He interrupted Dai Li rarely.","Dai Li frowned her fine eyebrows, \"I haven't even finished speaking.\"","\"You don't need to finish. Don't I know what you're thinking?\" Qin Shaozong curled his lips, but the smile didn't reach his eyes, \"You want to see the people of the Green Lotus Sect.\"","Dai Li's breathing stagnated slightly, and she subconsciously looked away. It was an instinctive escape when what was in her heart was seen through.","\"Dai Li, don't even think about it.\"","Qin Shaozong pinched her chin with two fingers and turned her head back, looking directly into those dark eyes, \"Yuyang has a population of more than 400,000. I can only say that there are fewer pests of the Green Lotus Sect here than elsewhere, but I can't guarantee that it's completely clean. The Green Lotus Sect is full of tricks. What's the difference between Madam looking for them and sending a sheep into the tiger's mouth?\"","Unable to turn her head, Dai Li simply stopped turning and looked at him deeply, \"Qin Changgeng, if you let me watch helplessly as Zhou Zhou has no medicine to cure him, I can't do it.\"","She didn't shout or scream, but every word carried an unquestionable determination.","\"Can you solve the problem by delivering yourself to their door? When they catch you and turn around to threaten that kid Qin Yanzhou and me with you, what do you want us to do?\" Qin Shaozong let go of her jaw.","Dai Li pursed her lips and didn't speak. Her eyes were a little erratic, and she couldn't help falling into his hypothesis.","She wasn't infected with the Gu worm, so she couldn't figure out the pain of the Gu poison that her son lightly brushed off every time.","But she knew it must be very uncomfortable. Otherwise, why would Zhou Zhou's face be pale the day after every poison attack, and it was almost difficult for him to swallow lunch?","\"There's still time, I can solve it.\" The man's lips pressed against the forehead of the woman in his arms, kissing the small red mole between her eyebrows, \"Dai Li, believe me.\"","The door of the main room wasn't closed. Neither Dai Li nor Qin Shaozong saw that at this time, a slender figure stood on the side of the main room, taking their conversation into his ears.","Qin Yanzhou slowly lowered his eyelashes and left as quietly as he had come.","...","\"Hey, Qin Yanzhou, where are you going?\" Qin Qinian's curiosity was instantly piqued when he saw Qin Yanzhou heading straight toward the side door.","His father's \"critical period\" had passed, and he was no longer grounded, allowed to leave the mansion, just not too frequently. The last time Qin Qinian left the mansion was two days ago, going out to chat with friends.","He had left the mansion several times, but he had never seen Qin Yanzhou go out once.","Did this person have friends in Yuyang?","Probably not, he had only come to Yuyang with Madam Dai a month ago.","Seeing Qin Yanzhou going out now, Qin Qinian was greatly surprised.","Qin Yanzhou didn't answer him, just walked straight ahead.","Qin Qinian caught up, talking to him as they walked: \"Are you going out to stroll around the market, or to buy something? If it's the former, I can introduce you to some good places. As for the latter, why do you need to go yourself, just let the servants go.\"","Qin Yanzhou walked forward silently, passing the guards and stepping out of the mansion.","Qin Qinian's mouth didn't stop: \"It's almost time for dinner in an hour. I heard Madam Dai instructing the kitchen to make ancient hotpot this morning. Let's go early and return early, don't miss the delicious food.\"","Qin Yanzhou didn't make a sound the first two times, but this time the young man softly agreed.","Qin Qinian chuckled, \"Madam Dai said she would improve the ancient hotpot. Tell me about the improved version first.\"","Qin Qinian followed Qin Yanzhou all the way, never figuring out what this person was doing out of the mansion.","Saying he was buying things, it didn't look like it.","He just walked around the stores, seeming more interested in the shop assistants and shopkeepers than the goods.","\"Qin Yanzhou, don't just look and not buy. Whatever you like, I'll pay for it. I've saved a lot of money. The military rewards and such from before, I haven't spent much, and I'm not like Wei Xiaowu who always likes to listen to those expensive tunes.\" Qin Qinian stated that his little treasury was quite abundant.","He always had an inexplicable sense of guilt and a bit of a sense of mission.","The former might come from the disrespect to Madam Dai when they first met, or the unexpected knowledge that his father had actually snatched someone else's wife, thus generating an endless stream of guilt of a son paying his father's debts.","The latter came from what Madam Dai said to him that day.","Even today, Qin Qinian didn't understand. Obviously, that day he wanted to ask her some questions, but as they chatted, the focus unconsciously fell entirely on Qin Yanzhou.","Even though a month and a half had passed, Qin Qinian still clearly remembered that day.","The afternoon sunlight slipped in from the window, falling on the woman's skirt with dark patterns, the reflected shimmering light depicting her features very clearly.","When speaking of Qin Yanzhou, she was gentle and soft-spoken, her eyebrows and eyes filled with unstoppable tenderness, her whole person seeming to be enveloped in a soft and charming halo.","Qin Qinian also couldn't explain why, even though the \"Zhou Zhou\" in the other party's mouth was not him, but when he was looked at by her, he became dizzy, like soaking in warm soup.","She said to let him talk more with Qin Yanzhou in the future, and he nodded without thinking.","She said she and Qin Yanzhou had been separated for ten whole years, and those ten years Qin Yanzhou had suffered a lot, so his personality had become reticent, hoping he would be more tolerant, and he also nodded without hesitation at the time.","Later, other things were said, all about Qin Yanzhou.","Later, Qin Qinian recalled it several times, feeling that it might be what the teacher called \"a loving mother loves her son, not for a reward\", she just instinctively loved and protected her child.","When his biological mother passed away from illness, he was less than two years old, and Qin Qinian had no memory of his biological mother. But he felt that if his mother was alive, she would most likely love him as Madam Dai loved Qin Yanzhou.","Okay, it didn't matter if he couldn't get it before, just based on his father's determined momentum, he felt that Madam Dai had a slight possibility of becoming his mother.","While suffering from moral condemnation, Qin Qinian awkwardly developed some secret expectations.","Qin Yanzhou, my father is in a high position of power and is invincible in battle, I will let him cover you in the future; can you share half of your mother with me...","*","Several streets away in the city.","A maid dressed as a servant walked in front, leading a petite figure wearing a veiled hat from a back alley into the back door of a bookstore.","After entering the bookstore, the \"maid\" took the initiative to step aside, curtsying to the latter, \"The gentlemen are on the third floor, Miss, please.\"","The girl didn't say a word, going upstairs alone. After reaching this floor, she took off the veiled hat on her head.","The sheer fabric fluttered, revealing a young and pretty face, she was about sixteen years old, exactly the age of a flower, but at this moment she was expressionless, cold as a piece of black ice.","There was a large hall on the third floor, at this moment the doors of the hall were wide open, and the little girl walked straight in.","There were people in the hall, one wearing a purple robe, one wearing white clothes, both young men in their early twenties, looking closely, their faces actually had five or six points of similarity.","The room was elegant, with paintings and calligraphy hanging on the walls, incense burners placed in the four corners, agarwood lingering, soaking the whole room.","Seeing the girl come in, Diting in white clothes smiled and said: \"Miss Fan is back, how did it go, was it smooth?\"","This visitor was exactly Fan Muqi, Fan Tianshi's eighth child.","Fan Muqi was expressionless: \"Everything went smoothly.\"","The young man in the purple robe smiled, \"It seems that Fan of Yanzhou's spirit in heaven is blessing Miss with everything going smoothly.\"","Hearing the other party mention her father, Fan Muqi's eyes darkened.","When Yanzhou was defeated, all the male members of the Fan family were killed. Perhaps feeling that women couldn't accomplish anything, whether it was the concubines in the Fan mansion or other unmarried girls, they all narrowly escaped.","Fan Muqi was a legitimate daughter, her biological mother, Lady Ji, was still alive.","The Fan and Ji families were a prominent family marriage, the current dynasty encouraged widows to remarry, and widows remarrying were everywhere. After Fan Tianshi died, Lady Ji was taken back by her mother's family.","When Lady Ji left, she originally wanted to take Fan Muqi with her.","However, the night before departure, a group of night travelers sneaked into the inn. And learning of her father's defeat, and even the war between the two sides was due to that person, Fan Muqi felt a ball of poisonous fire burning in her chest.","She favored him greatly, ordering people in the Fan mansion to take good care of him. The Fan mansion raised him for seven years, from twelve to nineteen, providing him with food and drink, teaching him martial arts.","Hateful that he was actually a hidden spy planted early by the Marquis of Wu'an.","Seven years, more than two thousand five hundred days and nights, thanks to him for enduring it!","So when the Green Lotus Sect came looking, Fan Muqi agreed without much thought, she only left a letter for her mother, then followed the visitor without hesitation.","She wanted revenge, seeking Quanjie to avenge the murder of her father and brother!","\"What do you want to do next?\" Fan Muqi knew that her relationship with the Green Lotus Sect was more of utilization than cooperation.","But she didn't care, as long as she could make the Marquis of Wu'an and Quanjie pay the price, she was willing to do anything.","\"After Cai Yuan visited the Marquis of Wu'an, he suddenly intensified his efforts to rectify the civilian and commercial agricultural colonies, with the Wei family bearing the brunt of it. First, Wei Conglin accidentally killed someone, and then the Cai family made their move through the colonies. For the Marquis of Wu'an to go around in such a massive circle...\" White Elephant, clad in a purple robe, stroked his chin.","Diting casually picked up the conversation, \"He wants to take a wife.\"","The other prominent families in the commandery were ill-informed, believing that the Marquis of Wu'an had truly been severely injured after returning from the battlefield. However, those who had been forced out of Yanzhou knew his actual condition better than anyone else.","Diting continued, \"The Marquis of Wu'an is clearly safe and sound. By hiding away in his manor and only manipulating things from behind the scenes, he obviously intends to drive the Wei family into a corner. I imagine it will not be long before he leaks his intentions to the Wei family.\"","Once his intentions were revealed, faced with a series of major events that could shake their very foundations, the Wei family would certainly have no other choice.","\"Since that is the case, we must strike first to gain the upper hand.\"","The Qin Manor, Main Chambers.","\"Madam, the Wei family has sent you a calling card,\" Nianxia said.","Daili was puzzled. \"For me?\"","Nianxia nodded. \"Yes. The manor guards said a maidservant delivered it, and she repeatedly emphasized that it was meant for you.\"","Daili took the calling card and unfolded it. Upon clearly seeing the sender's name, her delicate eyebrows rose slightly.","The calling card belonged to the fifth young lady of the Wei family, Wei Cheng."]},{"number":104,"title":"Chapter 104","paragraphs":["Dai Li didn't know Wei Cheng, but hearing that the other party's surname was \"Wei\", she instantly knew this was Qin Qinian's maternal family.","But why was the other party sending her a visiting card? If anyone should receive it, it should be Qin Qinian.","Looking at the time on the visiting card, it was for the afternoon of the next day.","Dai Li closed the visiting card, \"Alright, I understand.\"","Nianxia wasn't a local of Yuyang, and initially didn't know the Wei family either. But later, as she went out of the mansion more often, she heard a lot of gossip in the marketplace and roughly understood the connections.","\"Madam, if you don't want to see her, you might as well just decline,\" Nianxia whispered.","Dai Li smiled, \"Let's see later.\"","And the \"later\" Dai Li spoke of was during dinner that evening, when she directly brought the matter up at the dining table.","As the autumn colors deepened, the weather grew colder day by day. In the cold weather, food cooled quickly once taken off the stove, and gourmands obsessed with delicious food racked their brains to figure out how to eat piping hot dishes in the dead of winter.","Thus, the earliest hot pot appeared during the Zhou and Shang dynasties. Yes, it was the bronze ding widely known to the world.","Although this thing was later mostly used for inscribing merits and achievements, in the earliest times, it was indeed used as a cooking tool, used by nobles to boil vegetables and meat.","Later, developing into the Han dynasty, nobles still used copper pots, but with many improvements. The inside was divided into two parts, one part holding seasonings and the other part holding food.","Seasonings could dye the food with other flavors, so this era also called it \"dyeing\", and the hot pot was called a \"dyeing stove\", or \"antique stew\".","As for the latter name, it was also quite interesting, taken from the homophone of the \"gudong\" sound when food was dropped into the pot.","It was unknown since when Qin Shaozong and Dai Li stopped eating separate meals and sat together at a square or round table to eat.","Later, after returning to Yuyang, with Qin Yunce and Qin Qinian added to the dining table, Qin Shaozong had someone make a new round table, so the five of them sitting around it wouldn't feel crowded.","With just the right number of people, one stove wasn't enough, so two were placed on the table.","Dai Li and Qin Shaozong shared one, while the three teenagers shared another.","An array of plates and dishes of different sizes were spread out on the table, some holding raw meat slices, with a wide variety of meat. Mutton and pork went without saying, and today there was also beef from a cow that had died of illness; fish balls and shrimp balls were placed on the side, and vegetables occupied another corner.","Qin Qinian was eating noisily, not even raising his head.","Just then...","\"During the day, I received a visiting card from the Fifth Lady of the Wei family. I haven't replied to her yet. Marquis, do you think I should reply later?\" A gentle female voice sounded at this moment.","The table instantly quieted down a lot, with only the sound of someone chewing still echoing.","But soon, it seemed he received a kick under the table from his elder brother beside him, and the sound stopped. The owner of the sound raised his head in astonishment, \"Madam Dai, my aunt sent you a visiting card?\"","Dai Li only nodded, not saying anything else.","Generally speaking, when a visiting card was sent over, if one wanted the other party to come visit, a timely reply was required.","Just as Qin Qinian's words \"Did she send it to the wrong person?\" were about to tumble out of his throat, he was stepped on again under the table.","The teenager subconsciously turned his head to look at his elder brother beside him, only to see that the latter, like Qin Yanzhou, was looking at the two elders, waiting for them to speak.","Qin Qinian: \"...\" Fine.","The bone broth in the iron pot was still bubbling and boiling, with cooked shrimp balls floating on it, which were quickly picked up by a pair of jade chopsticks.","The jade chopsticks holding the shrimp ball took a trip through the seasoning compartment on the stove, and then placed it in another small bowl of Dai Li's.","\"If she wants to come, let her come. As the hostess of the mansion, there's no harm in you seeing her,\" Qin Shaozong's voice was very calm.","Dai Li paused, then gave him a heads-up, \"I can see her, but I must state in advance, I'll only treat her as an ordinary guest.\"","\"That's how it should be,\" Qin Shaozong said lightly. \"Qin San, tomorrow when your aunt comes to visit, don't go wandering outside. Stay in the mansion and receive the guest with Madam.\"","Qin Qinian's cheeks were stuffed full, like a hamster. Unable to speak, he just nodded repeatedly.","After instructing his youngest son, Qin Shaozong looked at Dai Li again, \"Does Madam need me to make an appearance tomorrow?\"","Dai Li answered with a question, \"Have your injuries healed?\"","This man had been cooped up in the mansion for over a month. Officials coming to visit the sick were in an endless stream, but only a sparse few were personally summoned by him. Dai Li didn't know exactly what he was scheming, but he was definitely laying out a plan.","Could he just walk around casually halfway through laying out his plan?","Qin Shaozong smiled, \"It's been over a month. If I still can't move, people outside will scold me for smashing old Mr. Ding's signboard.\"","\"As you wish,\" Dai Li didn't care.","Qin Qinian looked at Dai Li, then at Qin Shaozong. The brief two-sentence conversation made him feel...","His father actually quite wanted to go meet the guest with Madam Dai tomorrow.","The autumn sky grew dark late. After the meal, the sky looked dark, but it wasn't yet curfew time. Dai Li wrote a reply card and had someone deliver it.","While Dai Li was writing the reply card, Qin Shaozong took Qin Yunce for a stroll in the mansion to relax.","He didn't go to the study, just casually chatting: \"Yunce, write a letter to your aunt. Tell her I've just recovered from my illness, and ask her to bring her younger daughter to Yuyang for a short stay of a few days. Your aunt loves collecting medicinal herbs the most. Ask her if the Shi mansion has musk and fleeceflower root. If they do, ask her not to be stingy and bring them all over.\"","Qin Shaozong's mother had three children. He was the second, with an elder brother above him and a younger sister of the same mother below him.","Leaving aside the elder brother who died in battle for now, the younger sister married a subordinate of Father Qin surnamed Shi after coming of age.","The Shi family had considerable influence in Nanyu Commandery and was a prominent local clan. That subordinate had already risen to the position of Commandery Sima and was a good-looking young talent. All things considered, it was a good match.","The distance between Yuyang and Nanyu was neither close nor far, requiring a four-day carriage ride. Qin Hongying, who had married out, came back to Yuyang at most once or twice a year.","As if remembering something, Qin Shaozong added, \"Send the letter out of the city urgently tonight. After the guards arrive in Nanyu, have them stand by at the Shi mansion and depart to come back with Hongying.\"","A trace of surprise flashed through Qin Yunce's eyes, but he nodded in agreement, \"Yes, Father.\"","The guards waiting at the Shi mansion would be a completely silent urging. Seeing this, his aunt would definitely just simply pack two sets of clothes and hurriedly return with his cousin.","Qin Shaozong: \"Go do it.\"","Qin Yunce cupped his hands and took his leave.","Qin Shaozong stood under the corridor, the heavy night colors reflecting in his eyes, dyeing those brown eyes obscure and unclear.","...","The night passed in the blink of an eye. The morning sun rose high, and the east was bright.","Yuyang today was no different from yesterday. There were still teams of soldiers intercepting merchant caravans to requisition medicinal herbs at high prices, and there were also Qin Shaozong's confidants, led by Kuang Ye, successively visiting the prominent clans in the commandery.","As soon as they opened their mouths, they wanted to purchase fleeceflower root and musk.","The prominent clans gasped inwardly; these two were both precious items.","If they gave them, the other party was purchasing them, so they couldn't sell much of a favor; if they didn't give them, with the Marquis of Wu'an previously in critical condition, refusing them when they came to the door to collect medicine now would inevitably offend people.","How the prominent clans' heads ached, Dai Li didn't know. In the afternoon today, a carriage hanging the Zou family's plaque arrived at the side door of the Qin residence as scheduled.","Wei Cheng is the fifth lady of the middle generation of the Wei family, married into the Zou family. And it was precisely because Wei Conglin attended the birthday banquet of his good friend Zou Yude that a major event happened later.","The gatekeeper had already known in advance that a distinguished guest was visiting today, and as soon as the Zou family's carriage arrived, he greeted them.","Wei Cheng stepped out of the carriage, and before she could speak, she looked up and saw Qin Qinian standing by the side door. She paused slightly before smiling.","\"Aunt,\" Qin Qinian stepped forward cheerfully.","The young man, who often mingled in the army, did not know how to be subtle. After greeting her, he asked, \"If you wanted to see me, why did you send the visiting card to Madam Dai? You sent it to the wrong place. You should have sent it to me.\"","Wei Cheng smiled and said, \"Besides coming to see you, I also came to see her. I heard that my brother-in-law brought back a beauty when he returned to Yuyang this time. It is rumored outside that she is a rare beauty in the North. I was curious, so I came to take a look on the way. But considering that she is probably older than you, this visiting card can only be given to her.\"","She did not use the excuse of \"visiting the sick\" for Qin Shaozong, because only the male members of the Zou and Wei families who held official positions were qualified to send such visiting cards.","Qin Qinian suddenly realized, \"So that's it. Madam Dai mentioned this at the dinner table last night, and I almost thought you sent the wrong visiting card. So it wasn't a mistake.\"","These words made Wei Cheng's eyebrows twitch.","Mentioned this at the dinner table? They dined together? Not only did they dine together, but there was actually a sentence \"So it wasn't a mistake\" afterwards.","How could it not be a mistake?","That woman was just a favored concubine, a mere concubine. How could she climb over her master's head? In terms of status, she could not catch up with the legitimate son of the Lord of the North even on horseback.","But her nephew not only did not feel that it was inappropriate, but his words and attitude were also very close to her. She had only been in Yuyang for a little over a month, and she could actually make Qinian treat her like this. Did she give him an ecstasy potion?","Wei Cheng's thoughts turned and turned, and she felt that something was wrong, but she smiled and handed over a heavy booklet, \"Qinian, this is the gift list. Take a look.\"","Qin Qinian took it and flipped through it casually, \"Aunt, why do you bring things every time you visit?\"","\"What are you talking about, child? How can anyone visit without bringing gifts? Although your brother-in-law's house lacks nothing, I, as your aunt, treat you as my own son. Naturally, I want to bring all the things in my house over every time to make you happy,\" Wei Cheng smiled.","\"You really don't have to do this,\" Qin Qinian shook his head.","He had no pursuit of worldly possessions. His greatest wish was to make contributions on the battlefield like his father and awe the four directions.","Wei Cheng motioned for the servants to carry the things in, \"After all, this place is not the Lord's Mansion. Living outside is quite inconvenient. Although it can't be said that there is a lack of food and clothing, it is certainly not as convenient as at home. It is better to prepare more just in case.\"","\"We really don't lack anything. Father is almost moving everything from the Lord's Mansion over,\" Qin Qinian sighed.","Wei Cheng frowned imperceptibly, \"Qinian, why doesn't your brother-in-law live in the Lord's Mansion?\"","More than a month had passed, and Qin Qinian had already forgotten Mo Yanyun's instructions that day. Besides, the person asking the question was his own aunt, \"Madam Dai feels more comfortable living outside, so she lives outside.\"","Wei Cheng was dumbfounded and shocked for a long time before she recovered.","While they were talking, the two turned from the small side door to the front courtyard, and passed through the front courtyard to the main hall.","\"Qinian, that Madam Dai...\" Wei Cheng's words stopped abruptly.","There was no need to inquire further, because she had already seen the person.","Sitting at the head of the main hall ahead was a woman with a beautiful face. She had purple clothes and dark hair, and her appearance was bright and beautiful, like a blooming peony on a golden jade platform.","Looking at her appearance, she was quite young, but looking into those slightly upturned peach blossom eyes, one could see the calmness and gentleness precipitated by time, which was completely different from a young girl.","She was radiant, like a glowing pearl, and it seemed that the entire main hall brightened a bit.","Without noticing Wei Cheng's astonishment, Qin Qinian, who brought people back, introduced to Dai Li: \"Madam Dai, this is my aunt, my mother's legitimate younger sister.\"","Then he turned his head and formally introduced Dai Li to Wei Cheng.","Dai Li looked at Wei Cheng. The other party looked about thirty years old, with a beautiful face, wearing a falling horse bun, and her head was dotted with various gold and jade hairpins. She wore a green lotus-colored curved hem long dress with dark patterns flowing light on the clothes, which was very rich.","\"Madam Wei, please sit down,\" Dai Li smiled at her, and then called Nianxia beside her to serve tea to Wei Cheng.","They didn't know each other before, and she wasn't rushing to curry favor with the other party, so Dai Li wasn't very enthusiastic, just not impolite.","The women of the Qin family all married into other commanderies, and Wei Cheng had always been unmatched in the circle of noblewomen in Yuyang. She was used to being flattered, and now that she was given the cold shoulder, she felt uncomfortable in her heart.","At the same time, she suddenly felt that her father was not shooting without a target.","Three days ago, a daughter of the Wei family who married far away to Yanzhou returned to visit her relatives and brought back a lot of news.","According to the other party, the Marquis of Wu'an used surprise troops to win in Yanzhou, and it took less than ten days to break through the dangerous pass in front of Bairi City. Then he led his troops all the way to the border of Si and Yan provinces, beating the Sizhou army to a steady retreat, fleeing and dying. Even the third son of Governor Xie of Sizhou was captured alive by him.","With such an unstoppable momentum, how could the Marquis of Wu'an be seriously injured?","Once suspicion arose, her father connected all sorts of things, including Cai Yuan being able to go in to visit the sick, while their Wei family could only see Qin Yunce, and the subsequent change in the Cai family's usual style, targeting their family in many ways regarding farmland.","The Wei family, which was already restless, was suddenly enveloped in a cloud of suspicion.","Another day, not knowing what news her father received, he actually sent someone to call her back from the Zou family early in the morning. The first sentence he said when he saw her was:","The Marquis of Wu'an wants to remarry!","At first, Wei Cheng absolutely didn't believe it.","There was no prominent family with the surname Dai in the North, so that Dai family must have been born into a small family. It was already a compliment for a daughter of a small family to be a noble concubine, and she actually wanted to be the legitimate wife?","Not to mention, the Marquis of Wu'an had promised in his early years that if he remarried, he would only marry a daughter of the Wei family.","Shocked and angry in her heart, Wei Cheng smiled and sat down, \"It's rumored outside that my brother-in-law brought back a great beauty. I also heard Qinian mention you just now. He said you are gentle and easy to get along with. I also thought to myself how could there be such a perfect woman, but seeing you today, there actually is.\"","Qin Qinian hadn't said this just now, but it didn't prevent him from recalling the various things in the past month. Hearing this, he nodded.","\"You flatter me. I'm just an ordinary person. I wouldn't dare to claim to be perfect,\" Dai Li also began to flatter commercially, but what she praised was Qin Qinian, \"That child Qinian is kind-hearted. Even ordinary things can be seen by him as a flower.\"","Wei Cheng pursed her lips and smiled, \"That's true.\"","Qin Qinian was dizzy.","After going back and forth with a few pleasantries, Wei Cheng said: \"Nursing the sick is the most exhausting, but Madam Dai is still radiant. Is this because you are naturally beautiful, or because my brother-in-law can't bear to let you serve in front of the bed?\"","Dai Li's eyebrows raised slightly, and she didn't choose either, \"It should be because old Mr. Ding's medical skills are superb. After a dose of medicine, the Marquis' wound no longer hurts, and he falls asleep immediately. He doesn't even know when thunder roars outside.\"","Wei Cheng sighed as if worried, \"Nursing the sick is still hard work. Why don't you send someone back to the Lord's Mansion and call Pingzhi over? She is the most docile and can endure hardships the most.\"","The other party's tone was full of concern, but Dai Li instinctively felt that the \"Pingzhi\" she mentioned was probably not an ordinary person.","Dai Li did not ask further, but instead looked at Qin Qinian beside her. \"Qinian, what do you think about calling Pingzhi over here?\"","Caught off guard by the question, Qin Qinian first let out an \"Ah,\" looking completely bewildered. \"Who is Pingzhi?\"","Wei Cheng let out a helpless laugh. \"Technically, she is also your aunt, Qinian. However, I am your mother's full sister, while she is a cousin, so the relationship is a bit more distant.\"","Dai Li's expression shifted slightly as she roughly understood the situation.","Qin Qinian still had not wrapped his head around it. \"My cousin-aunt? Why would she be in the Marquis's estate?\"","\"When your mother passed away from illness, you were not even two years old. Shortly after, when the eldest young master of the Qin family had that incident, the estate was thrown into complete chaos. Father was worried that no one would take care of you, so he discussed it with the Marquis and sent Pingzhi over to look after you,\" Wei Cheng said with a smile.","Dai Li picked up her teacup and took a light sip.","The \"Wei Pingzhi\" she spoke of was likely the illegitimate daughter of the Wei family whom they had originally wanted to marry off to Qin Shaozong as his primary wife.","However, Qin Shaozong had been unwilling to let an illegitimate daughter occupy the position of his main wife, fearing it would make the Qin family a laughingstock among other prominent families, and thus he had rejected the Wei family's request.","Looking at it now, although he had not married the Wei daughter, he had still brought her back to the estate.","Qin Qinian's expression turned a bit strange. \"Aunt, are you talking about Concubine Li? She seems to be the only person in the estate who comes from the Wei family. Is she actually my cousin-aunt?\"","These words made Wei Cheng's heart skip a beat.","Li? Why would Wei Pingzhi be known as \"Concubine Li\" in the Marquis's estate? Was that Concubine Li really Wei Pingzhi?","Moreover, all these years, her nephew actually had no idea that his cousin-aunt was living in the estate.","This was simply too bizarre.","Wei Cheng could not help but feel a pang of regret. Had she known this, she would not have worried about her nephew's attention being divided by another aunt, deliberately avoiding any mention of Wei Pingzhi every time she saw him.","Wait, Wei Pingzhi's biological mother seemed to be... surnamed Li.","Out of the corner of her eye, Dai Li caught sight of a tall figure emerging from the side corridor. She turned her head and, unsurprisingly, met a pair of light brown eyes.","Yesterday, he had asked if she needed him to step in, and at the time, she had told him to do as he pleased. Since he had gone to the study this afternoon, she thought he would not come.","\"Father, you are here.\" Qin Qinian also saw Qin Shaozong.","From just the brief exchange between aunt and nephew, Dai Li had already sensed the undercurrents surging beneath the surface.","Unwilling to get involved, now that Qin Shaozong was here, Dai Li immediately tossed the problem to him. Still unaccustomed to referring to other women by their clan names, she simply said, \"My Lord Marquis, Madam Wei suggested having Wei Pingzhi come here to serve.\"","Qin Shaozong paused his steps. \"Who is Wei Pingzhi?\"","Dai Li: \"...\"","This father and son truly were cut from the same cloth.","A few moments of eerie silence fell over the hall, until Qin Qinian finally whispered, \"Father, Wei Pingzhi should be Concubine Li.\"","During Qin Qinian's early childhood, he, his elder brother, and his elder sister were all raised by Nanny Chen, who was their grandmother's trusted dowry maid.","Therefore, he did not know much about this Concubine Li. He only knew that such a person existed in the estate; after all, how could a son be overly curious about his father's concubines?","Qin Shaozong's expression remained placid. \"There is no need. She already has her new place to go.\""]},{"number":105,"title":"Chapter 105","paragraphs":["Wei Cheng couldn't hear the phrase \"new place.\" Looking at Qin Shaozong, besides being shocked that he didn't even recognize the name, she was also astonished by his... condition.","The man, over eight feet tall, wore a black robe. His ink-black hair was tied high with a crown and kerchief. His complexion was normal, heroic and majestic. With a ring-pommel sword hanging at his waist, his presence was as heavy as a mountain. He didn't look like a weak, injured person at all.","Not injured?","Then why had the news that the Marquis of Wu'an was hanging by a thread spread like wildfire earlier?","Could it be fake? Or did Old Mr. Ding's miraculous medical skills snatch him back from the King of Hell's palace?","Wei Cheng snapped back to her senses and hurriedly stood up from her seat, bowing to Qin Shaozong. \"I pay my respects to the Marquis. May the Marquis enjoy good health and long-lasting blessings.\"","While lowering her head to bow, Wei Cheng kept secretly observing the head seat, surprised to find that the woman sitting there didn't move at all, as if she were glued to the chair.","And the man turned a blind eye to it, obviously used to it.","Used to her casualness, her casualness in all aspects, regardless of whether outsiders were present.","\"Sit.\" Qin Shaozong walked over and sat down beside Dai Li. \"I haven't seen Old Chief Clerk Wei for a long time. How has he been lately?\"","Old Chief Clerk Wei was the father of Wei Cheng and the Wei brothers.","Hearing this, Wei Cheng immediately showed a sorrowful expression. \"My father has been unable to swallow food lately...\"","Before she could finish the second half of her sentence, the man at the head seat interrupted, \"That might be because he is old and his teeth are bad.\"","Dai Li's hand holding the teacup trembled, and a little tea splashed out, dampening a small dark patch on her sleeve. She lowered her eyes to look at the cup, feeling very glad she hadn't had time to drink it yet.","Qin Changgeng's words were truly as unpleasant as always.","Just as she finished muttering in her heart, the person beside her looked her way.","Dai Li also turned her head, and their eyes met.","Qin Shaozong reached out and pulled a handkerchief from the small pouch at Dai Li's waist, using her handkerchief to wipe her sleeve. \"Madam's clothes are wet. Why don't you return to your room to change first?\"","Dai Li looked down.","It was indeed wet, but only a tiny patch, not even a quarter of the size of a palm. Perhaps if she sat here a little longer, it would be dried by the wind.","However...","\"That's fine too.\" Dai Li was happy to be at ease.","This Madam Wei's purpose for visiting was not simple. The Wei family were his in-laws, so she would leave it to him to deal with.","Thus, amidst Wei Cheng's dumbfounded stare, Dai Li leisurely left with two maids.","Wei Cheng gasped inwardly, unable to believe that she didn't even turn her head back.","Less than the time it takes to drink a cup of tea after Dai Li left, Qin Shaozong also left the main hall on the pretext of feeling unwell, leaving only his youngest son to continue entertaining the guest.","Dai Li had just returned to the main courtyard when Qin Shaozong followed right behind her.","\"Madam, in a few days, my younger sister will bring her daughter to stay at the manor for a short while,\" Qin Shaozong said as he sat down beside her.","Dai Li now got a headache just hearing about guests. This one was even more of a heavyweight; not only was she bringing her daughter to stay, but she was also his biological sister.","Given her current relationship with him, she could completely imagine that his sister would ask her many roundabout questions after seeing her.","Dai Li propped her forehead with her hand, her eyelashes drooping low, only looking at the sandalwood desk in front of her. \"Qin Changgeng, can't you go back to your Marquis Manor? You go back with Yun Ce, Qi Nian, and the others. When your sister comes, you can receive them there. I am not one of your people. I don't understand your twists and turns, and I can't handle it.\"","Regarding the guest reception today, Dai Li pondered over it on her way back. The more she thought about it, the more she felt he had an ulterior motive today.","Qin Shaozong was no idle man.","He made a special appearance and left after less than a moment. No matter how you looked at it, it seemed he was using Madam Wei as a medium to pass on some kind of message to the outside world.","But to be honest, Dai Li had absolutely no interest in the struggles among the prominent families of Yuyang. She didn't care which family gained the upper hand in the power struggles, nor was she interested in Qin Shaozong's future plans.","Previously, she had thought too simply, feeling that receiving a guest would just be like receiving an ordinary visitor. However, upon seeing her today, she felt something unusual after just a few words.","She treated the other party as a normal visitor, but the other party was not simply there for a chat.","\"Madam, I let Hongying come back this time mainly so she can recognize someone.\" Qin Shaozong held her other hand.","Dai Li tried to pull her hand back. \"Recognize who? Your sister is married off to another commandery. According to your rules here, she probably won't come back more than a few times a year. Why bother me?\"","\"She indeed won't come back many times, but she eventually needs to recognize the matriarch of the Marquis Manor.\" Qin Shaozong slid his long fingers through hers, intertwining his fingers with her pale, soft hand.","Dai Li froze. When she realized what his words meant, her originally weak attempt to pull back her hand suddenly turned into a lightning-fast retraction, as if she had been bitten by a snake.","Qin Shaozong didn't expect her reaction to be so drastic. He instinctively grabbed at it, but only managed to catch her fingertips.","Holding onto those pinkish-white fingertips tightly, his dark, large palm was like a tiger clamping down on its prey, refusing to let go. After pulling it back, his hand opened wide like a tiger's maw and completely enveloped hers.","\"Dai Li, what do you mean by this?\" He stared at her intently.","This question was asked despite knowing the answer. With how she shrank back as if seeing a ghost just now, how could he not understand?","She was unwilling to marry him, avoiding the position of the Marquis Manor's matriarch like a venomous snake or scorpion!","Dai Li's hand was held tightly by him. That burning, sharp gaze fell upon her, as if it wanted to melt her.","It wasn't that she didn't feel it, but she still didn't look at him. She continued to lower her head and look at the desk, as if she could stare a flower out of it.","\"Dai Li!\" He rarely called her by her full name.","Every time he called her like this, what he was about to say to her was definitely out of the ordinary.","Dai Li's eyelashes trembled slightly. She finally turned her head to look at Qin Shaozong, her eyes filled with deep helplessness. \"Qin Changgeng, that's not good.\"","When she initially said she \"would not be a concubine,\" aside from it being the most basic principle for her as someone with a modern soul, it was also an explanation she was forced to give when she was pestered endlessly by Mo Yanyun back then.","Not being a concubine was just the baseline; it didn't mean that satisfying this condition equated to being able to marry. She had never thought about marrying a native, feudal man either.","Ultimately, her views were different from his.","Some might feel that these words carried little weight and were harmless. But it wasn't so. A clash of values was like sprinkling a handful of sand, soil, and seeds between two people. At first, it might seem inconsequential.","As the days passed one by one, those discomforts and contradictions would grow wildly like weeds, eventually maturing into towering trees that neither side could endure or ignore.","The gap between the ancients' values and hers spanned a thousand years, like a massive chasm.","She couldn't cross it. She couldn't accept the three obediences and four virtues, nor her own man having a flock of wives and concubines. Qin Shaozong also couldn't understand being faithful to one person until the end, or why he needed to show respect to a young woman whose status and position were vastly inferior to his own.","These were all unsolvable problems.","Right now, she only wanted to quickly remove the Gu worm from Zhouzhou's body. As for the rest, whether it was his relatives or those concubines in his backyard, as long as they didn't hover around in front of her, she could bury her head in the sand like an ostrich and endure it for a while, for the sake of the painstaking efforts he had made for Zhouzhou.","\"What is not good about it?\" Qin Shaozong asked in a deep voice.","If a year ago, someone had told him that he would painstakingly set a trap for the prominent families of Yuyang, just to break his past promise of definitely marrying a daughter of the Wei family, he would certainly have laughed at them for spouting nonsense.","If someone had further told him that the lady he offered the position of the marchioness of the Marquis's estate to would dismiss it with disdain, and even reject him right away, he would have flown into a rage and twisted that person's head off to use as a wine goblet.","Yet now, apart from feeling the absurdity of it all, Qin Shaozong only felt an unspeakable frustration.","\"We are not suitable for each other,\" Dai Li simply said.","He pressed on, \"Your husband, I presume, will never have the chance to see you again. What is the difference between that and being dead? Meanwhile, the position of my wife remains empty. You are a widow and I am a widower. How are we not suitable?\"","\"It's not just about that. There are thousands upon thousands of widows and widowers in this world. If losing a spouse is the only criterion for pairing up, it would be far too absurd and arbitrary.\" As the last word fell, Dai Li clearly saw the veins throbbing on the side of his neck.","Qin Shaozong felt a rush of anger shoot straight to his head. The fury exploded in his chest, forming countless sharp, thorny balls that made him almost want to vomit blood.","Arbitrary.","How could she say it was arbitrary!","He forcefully suppressed his anger. \"The matters of the Wei family are being handled, the renovation of the Marquis's estate is already on the schedule, and those concubines in the backyard have their own places to go. Tell me, Madam, which of these things is arbitrary?\"","He knew that Peach Blossom Spring was extraordinary. Her hands were almost completely free of calluses, showing that she did not engage in manual labor.","With a solid family background, being learned, intelligent, and extremely beautiful, such a woman would be quite proud. The chances of her sharing a husband with others were very slim.","Besides, with her around, keeping Concubine Li or Concubine Du was useless. If they were to be dismissed, so be it. Let them go out and eat someone else's rice.","Dai Li froze, suddenly remembering something. Back on the boat, Diting had said that the Marquis of Wu'an once had an agreement with the Wei family; if he were to remarry, he could only marry a Wei daughter.","And he said the concubines had their own places to go. Could it be that he dismissed them?","Dai Li admitted that for a man who had been bathed in a feudal environment since the day he was born to go to such lengths for her, she was not entirely untouched.","She also admitted that she quite liked Qin Shaozong now, but it was the most superficial kind of affection, staying entirely on a physical level. It was purely because this man was strong enough, skilled enough, and in tune with her in bed.","This superficial affection was replaceable. If not him, it could be someone else. There was truly no reason it had to be him.","Moreover, in this era, there was only the practice of divorcing a wife, with no concept of an amicable separation. The system of amicable separation was not officially written into the law and protected by the government until the Tang Dynasty.","Qin Shaozong was passionate about her now, but what about the future? She didn't doubt his sincerity, but sincerity easily changes.","\"Qin Changgeng, let's not talk about this for now, alright? Zhouzhou's Gu poison hasn't been removed yet, and I have no mind to think about anything else right now,\" Dai Li said softly.","Her voice was very light, like the soft clouds in the sky drifting with light rain, and like the breeze brushing past the windowsill.","The ball of fire in Qin Shaozong's chest rolled back and forth a few times, burning so much that his heart, liver, spleen, and lungs ached.","Outside the window, the continuous chirping and twittering of birds reached Qin Shaozong's ears, only making him feel more irritated.","It was truly damn annoying.","The man took a deep breath and exhaled. After all, he was not a reckless and impulsive youth. He had the composure appropriate for his age and understood very well that some things could be said as a joke on ordinary days, but absolutely could not be said now.","This fox was already unwilling. If he provoked her with words again, she would probably hide in her hole and refuse to even peek out in the future.","\"Fine, then we'll talk about it after Qin Yanzhou recovers from his illness.\" He compromised.","Dai Li gave him a surprised look.","Qin Shaozong was truly angered into a laugh by Dai Li's look.","In her eyes, was he really such an unreasonable and dictatorial person?","Dai Li watched the fire in his eyes flare up and opened her mouth to explain, but the large hand that had been holding her suddenly pulled her with force.","Amidst Dai Li's exclamation, her smoky purple robes flipped in an arc as she plunged into the arms of the man beside her. The latter clamped one arm around her waist, lifted her chin with the other hand, and lowered his head to kiss her.","This kiss undoubtedly carried anger. The flames churning and clamoring in Qin Shaozong's chest seemed to burn over through their connection.","Dai Li was swept up by him, bitten, and sucked. Her back pressed against his long arm, while her front was tightly pasted against him.","In the bright afternoon sunlight, the room was very well-lit, showing every detail clearly. And as always, he did not close his eyes when he kissed.","Those narrow brown eyes locked tightly onto her. Compared to the beginning, they now held many heavy emotions that could not be melted away, like thick ink.","Dai Li half-lowered her eyelids, not fully closing her eyes either. She only lowered her gaze, avoiding Qin Shaozong's eyes.","Suddenly, he hastily ended the kiss and pulled back a little, but his long arms still tightly encircled her.","\"We can discuss that matter later, but Madam, grant me one request first.\" His breathing was heavy, and his chest heaved violently. It was hard to tell if it was because his anger had not dissipated, or if he was stifled by a hidden fire.","Dai Li felt it might be both, but she turned her head away. \"I've already promised you so much before, why do you still want more?\"","She was referring to when he caught her in Nanyang County, and she had agreed to many things on the bed.","\"Not those.\" He leaned in, his kiss falling on her round earlobe. He first gave it a peck, then took it into his mouth, stroking it twice with the tip of his tongue before lightly biting it with his canine teeth.","A numbing tickle spread over her ear, reaching the back of her head and then the top, bringing about an electric shiver. Unable to break free, Dai Li could only say, \"Tell me what it is first.\"","\"Madam, promise me first,\" he said instead.","Dai Li really couldn't figure out what kind of medicine this man was selling in his gourd. If it was a serious matter, this wasn't the right state to discuss serious matters.","If it was about matters in bed, she had already agreed to them earlier.","Dai Li pursed her lips and said nothing.","Qin Shaozong pulled back a bit, straightened her up, and cupped her chin with his palm. He lightly pinched her fair cheeks with two fingers, making her red lips part slightly with a soft pop. \"Speak. Say yes.\"","Dai Li: \"...Alright then.\"","\"Madam, call me Husband.\" His true intention was finally revealed."]},{"number":106,"title":"Chapter 106","paragraphs":["Daili was stunned, not expecting his request to be a \"husband\".","This kind of thing was said with the mouth, and didn't require doing anything, just touching the upper and lower lips together.","But in the afternoon when the sun was strong, Daili looked into those light brown eyes, as if she saw a mirror. In the center of the mirror were two shrunken versions of herself.","He was very serious, not joking at all.","Some words seemed to grow thorns, stuck in her throat, unable to be said. Her red lips moved slightly, and Daili looked away, \"Why are you suddenly saying this?\"","Qin Shaozong's eyes darkened, and his long fingers pinched her cheeks again, tightening and loosening, pinching her mouth into a goldfish mouth again, \"What did Madam promise me just now? Say something nice quickly.\"","After looking away, the discomfort disappeared. Not only was her cheek pinched, but this person was also playing around. Daili immediately reached out and pushed him, \"You let go first.\"","Qin Shaozong let go as requested, but still stared at her intently.","Daili lowered her eyes, and her gaze fell on his animal head belt. There was a tiger head carved on it, and the exposed tiger teeth were long, extraordinarily ferocious and intimidating, just like his majestic aura without being angry.","He didn't speak, and didn't urge her.","Not looking at him, she felt much better. Daili helplessly called out, \"Husband...\"","The two words were said very softly, lightly, as if a stronger wind could blow them away.","But Qin Shaozong heard it.","The anger and gloom in his chest slowly turned into powder in these two words, and then blown by the wind, there was no trace left. It was a very comfortable feeling, somewhat similar to a triumphant return from the battlefield.","The damn bird outside the window was still calling, but its call was much nicer than before.","Okay, step by step, he never lacked patience.","\"Yeah.\" He replied first, his spine straightened, and his sitting posture was more upright than before. When he spoke again, there was a faint smile in his voice, \"What are Madam's orders?\"","The tense atmosphere began to flow, the ice and snow melted, and it returned to its previous peacefulness.","Daili raised her eyes and met his smiling eyes. The two small figures in the mirror were very clear, just like before.","Daili sighed silently in her heart.","*","A few days later.","A carriage escorted by a group of cavalry arrived at the side door of the Qin residence. It entered through the side door and was led to a pavilion courtyard by the guards.","The carriage door opened.","Hu Bao respectfully said, \"Madam Qin, please.\"","A tall figure in maple red stepped down from the carriage first, \"Where is my second brother?\"","\"The Marquis is in the main courtyard,\" Hu Bao replied.","Thinking that they had arrived a bit earlier than expected, Hu Bao added a sentence, \"You go to the main hall and wait a moment, I'll go inform the Marquis.\"","\"No need, I'll go directly to the main courtyard. He has an injury and shouldn't move around.\" Qin Hongying refused, and then said to the young girl who was getting off the carriage, \"Rongrong, let's go to the main courtyard to visit your second uncle first.\"","Knowing her daughter's habit of speaking surprisingly, Qin Hongying exhorted, \"Don't speak nonsense when the time comes. You can walk sideways in Nanyu Commandery, but not here.\"","Shi Rongyue had been lifting the curtain to look since just now, and the doubt in her heart reached its peak when the carriage entered the mansion, \"Mother, this place doesn't seem to be the Marquis's mansion.\"","Qin Hongying was stunned, her slender eyes swept around, and she realized belatedly that although this pavilion courtyard was elegant, it was very unfamiliar, not the courtyard she lived in before she got married.","Before Qin Hongying could ask, Hu Bao said, \"Since returning to Yuyang, the Marquis has always stayed here.\"","Meaning you didn't come to the wrong place.","Qin Hongying's heart, which had been bumping along the way, rose again. More than a month ago, the news of the Marquis of Wu'an being seriously ill and seeking medicine came from Yuyang, spreading to the surrounding commanderies and counties, causing a huge uproar.","When she first heard the news, she was burning with anxiety and wrote a letter, having someone deliver it overnight to Yuyang.","Her second brother's reply was delivered quickly, with only three words written in vigorous strokes on the paper: Won't die.","Qin Hongying saw it, okay, then it's fine.","With her second brother's temperament, being able to say this proved that everything was still fine, maybe he was still plotting something. She then only ordered someone to bring some medicinal materials back to Yuyang, and didn't go there herself.","However, a few days ago, she received a second letter.","The writer was Yun Ce, but the tone was exactly like her strong second brother. The letter said \"just recovered from illness\", but asked her to bring precious medicinal materials such as Polygonum multiflorum and musk.","Could it be that he doesn't have long to live?","\"Madam Qin, the Marquis is actually not injured,\" Hu Bao explained.","Qin Hongying was stunned, alternating between anger and joy, \"Since second brother is not injured, why did he say he just recovered from illness, and asked me to bring medicinal materials over?\"","Hu Bao lowered his head, \"It's a long story, why don't you ask the Marquis yourself later.\"","Qin Hongying: \"Lead me to the main courtyard.\"","...","Daili was informed by Qin Shaozong this morning that his younger sister would arrive today, but the estimated arrival time was at Shen hour (3-5 pm). She then took a nap according to her usual habit, anyway, there was still time.","As for the argument about marriage the day before yesterday, the two of them tacitly did not bring it up again later.","Footsteps approached from outside, and Qin Shaozong, who was sitting at the desk in the outer room reading a letter, looked up at the sound.","The place where the desk was placed directly faced the door. Through the open door, he could see the visitor outside. And from a distance, two pairs of similarly shaped eyes met.","Qin Hongying was completely relieved, and she suddenly felt annoyed, \"Second brother called me back from Nanyu in such a hurry, is it just to have me watch you review memorials?\"","Qin Hongying was angry and dared to speak with hidden barbs, but the young girl beside her had to salute properly, \"Greetings, second uncle.\"","\"Lower your voice.\" Qin Shaozong's gaze returned to the desk, and he finished writing a letter with a few strokes.","Qin Hongying raised her eyebrows slightly, \"What, are you keeping a mistress in a golden house?\"","After saying this, she realized that this room was quite different.","There was a vase more than half a person tall in the corner, a wooden rack supporting an incense cage next to it, and landscape paintings hung on the wall. In addition, a soft couch was set up by the window, and a lotus-cyan mink blanket was placed on the couch.","And on the other side of the soft couch armrest, there was a novel small table with small wooden wheels underneath that was obviously movable. There were two books on the table, and a small wooden box that looked like it contained snacks.","It was too soft, completely unlike the style of a widower military general.","A picture inexplicably floated in Qin Hongying's mind. A slender lady sat on the soft couch by the window, holding a book in her hand, the wooden box on the movable small table opened, and candied fruit and other snacks could be vaguely seen inside.","She was reading a book, occasionally eating snacks, and then taking a sip of hot tea; while the man sitting at the desk not far away looked up at her during a break from reviewing documents.","Qin Hongying's hair stood on end from her own inexplicable imagination.","What kind of person is her second brother?","Except for close relatives, he is the most distinct and has a strong sense of territory. She remembered that after her second brother got married, he lived in a courtyard by himself and did not live with her second sister-in-law.","She hadn't not seen his room, it was hard, with all kinds of weapons placed in it. Rather than a place to sleep, it was more like an armory.","Why now...","\"Qin Changgeng, has your sister arrived at the mansion?\" Daili was woken up by the talking outside.","She had just woken up and was still groggy, thinking it was Nianxia or Bipo coming to report.","It went quiet outside.","Soon, Dai Li, sitting on the bed clutching her quilt, saw Qin Shaozong part the bead curtain and enter the inner room.","\"Hongying arrived at the manor early.\" Qin Shaozong took the dress from the clothes rack and handed it to Dai Li.","Dai Li rubbed her eyes, taking the skirt while looking out the window. \"It seems earlier than expected.\"","\"Probably the driver was in a hurry and cracked the whip so hard it sparked.\" Qin Shaozong stood by watching her get up, completely omitting the fact that someone was waiting outside.","Since he didn't mention it, Dai Li assumed his sister was drinking tea in the main hall. Besides, if he wasn't in a hurry, why should she be? So, she moved slowly.","After putting on her outer clothes, Dai Li brushed through her hair.","Having not left the manor today, she hadn't asked Nianxia to style her hair into a bun, merely tying it casually with a hair ribbon. The ribbon had been pulled off before her nap, and now that she was to meet a guest, she naturally couldn't go with her hair completely loose.","\"Nianxia,\" Dai Li called out.","There was no answer from outside.","Dai Li paused. Not Nianxia? Then she'd try the other. She called for Bipo.","But there was still no answer.","Qin Shaozong chuckled softly. \"They went to the kitchen to prepare the meal. They aren't in the courtyard right now.\"","Qin Hongying had arrived early and hadn't had lunch yet, so Qin Shaozong had sent the two maids to the kitchen.","\"Then what about my hair...\" Dai Li completely didn't expect anyone to be outside, thinking Nianxia and Bipo had just left after passing the message.","\"I'll tie it for you, Madam,\" Qin Shaozong suddenly offered with interest.","Dai Li was guided by him to the vanity mirror and sat down, half-doubting. \"Do you know how to style a hair bun?\"","\"No,\" he admitted honestly.","Qin Shaozong had never done it before, though he had watched the maids style her hair many times.","\"Then no, don't mess around.\" Dai Li snatched the hair ribbon back from him. Men were clumsy; if he pulled her hair, she'd be the one hurting.","She gathered her long hair into a ponytail. \"This will do for now. I'll go find Nianxia to style it for me, and you go to the main hall to see your sister. She's here to see you anyway; she won't mind if I don't go out with you.\"","Qin Shaozong thought of Qin Hongying's expression just now and said meaningfully, \"That might not be the case.\"","After getting dressed, Dai Li followed Qin Shaozong out.","Qin Shaozong was very tall and broadly built. Dai Li was a head shorter than him, and walking behind him, her view forward was completely blocked.","It wasn't until Qin Shaozong stepped aside that Dai Li saw two unfamiliar women.","One was in her early thirties, tall and voluptuous, with narrow dark eyes. She wore a maple-red dress, exuding a sharp, cold edge amidst her flamboyant appearance.","The other was a pretty young girl, perhaps not yet fully grown, with a cute, round little face. She was currently staring at her curiously with large light-brown eyes.","Dai Li: \"...\"","Dai Li froze in place for a couple of seconds, stiffly turning her head to look at Qin Shaozong beside her. The latter seemed completely oblivious to her embarrassment and began introducing them.","\"Hongying, this is my wife, Dai Li.\"","He then introduced Qin Hongying and Shi Rongyue to Dai Li.","Dai Li: \"...Hello.\"","Qin Hongying looked Dai Li up and down, then looked at Qin Shaozong, the amusement in her eyes so rich it almost spilled over.","So her second brother really was hiding a great beauty.","But before she could speak, she heard her brother ask, \"Hongying, how much fleeceflower root and musk did you bring?\"","The Qin family was a lineage of military generals guarding the borders. In the early years, before the northern lands were pacified, the uncles of the Qin clan all had to go to the battlefield. Qin Hongying had developed a habit of collecting medicinal herbs since childhood, delivering some to her father or brother today, and to other uncles tomorrow.","Dai Li's eyes instantly lit up.","In the following quarter of an hour, Qin Shaozong witnessed for the first time Dai Li's fiery enthusiasm and unparalleled social skills.","When this little fox wanted to coax someone, she could probably coax the birds right out of the trees.","In just a quarter of an hour, she had become so close to Qin Hongying that it seemed like they had known each other for over a decade and were the best of friends, holding hands as they chatted.","A vein throbbed on Qin Shaozong's forehead.","The smile on Qin Hongying's lips never faded. She found Dai Li's personality very interesting. Moreover, being showered with attention by a stunningly radiant beauty was indeed something hard to resist.","Of course, the sight of her second brother holding his breath and forcing himself to endure his annoyance without an outburst was truly a rare treat.","A moment later, two brocade boxes brought all the way from Nanyu Commandery were presented to Dai Li.","Dai Li opened them, the eagerness in her eyes growing even stronger.","Fleeceflower root is a knotweed plant, generally reddish-brown with wrinkled grooves on its surface. The piece of fleeceflower root Qin Hongying brought was exceptionally large, at least as thick as an adult man's arm, easily weighing several pounds.","As for the musk beside it. Processed musk is a brown, lumpy solid, and the amount of musk Qin Hongying brought was also considerable, feeling heavy in the hand.","With these two portions of medicinal herbs, even if Ding Luying asked for double the original amount, they could easily satisfy the demand.","Dai Li could almost hear the sound of a heavy boulder lifting from her heart.","\"Second Brother, this is the first time in over thirty years you've asked me for anything. Here, all the fleeceflower root and musk in the Shi Manor are right here. I'm being quite generous, aren't I?\" Qin Hongying directed her words to Qin Shaozong, but her eyes remained fixed on Dai Li.","Although there was an underlying meaning when she said this, it was not a lie.","In Qin Hongying's memory, let alone after her second brother took up the mantle of the family, even when their eldest brother was still alive, her second brother had never asked her for anything. This second brother of hers had been proud and fiercely independent all his life. He only ever supported and protected his younger sister, never stooping to ask for anything in return.","This was the first time, and precisely because of this, she set out for Yuyang immediately after receiving the news.","Dai Li noticed Qin Hongying's gaze and understood that most of those words were meant for her.","She hesitated for a moment.","Should she respond to that? If she did, in what capacity?","If she didn't, this was Zhou Zhou's life-saving medicine...","\"Indeed, it's very generous. Consider me indebted to you this time,\" a deep male voice sounded.","Qin Hongying was even more surprised inwardly, but she said, \"We're siblings, there's no such thing as owing debts. I didn't even know how to thank you for that matter with Changfeng earlier, how could I ask for a favor from you now?\"","\"By the way, Second Brother, Hu Bao said you've been staying here ever since you returned to Yuyang. Why aren't you staying at the Marquis Manor? How can outside accommodations be as comfortable as home?\" Qin Hongying found it strange.","Qin Shaozong hadn't let Dai Li answer just now, but now he passed the buck to her. \"Ask her.\"","Dai Li: \"...\"","Qin Hongying smoothly followed up, \"Why is that?\"","\"...The Marquis Manor is undergoing renovations,\" Dai Li simply said.","Qin Hongying smiled with deep meaning, \"Then move back once the renovations are done. The Marquis Manor is much bigger than here.\"","Dai Li remained silent.","Someone arrived outside at this moment; it was Qin Yunce, who had come to pay his respects after hearing that his aunt had arrived at the manor.","After he paid his respects and exchanged pleasantries with the mother and daughter, Qin Hongying asked in confusion, \"Where is Qinian? Why don't I see him? Did he run off to the military camp again?\"","Qin Shaozong: \"He and that boy Qin Yanzhou have been running out every few days recently. You arrived earlier than expected, so the two of them probably haven't returned yet.\"","Both Qin Hongying and Shi Rongyue froze.","Qin Yanzhou?","Surnamed Qin, a son of the Qin family? Why would he be with Qi Nian? And why did she say \"the two of them\"—does that mean they came back together?","Speak of the devil, and he shall appear.","\"Father!\"","Before the person even stepped into the main courtyard, his cracking adolescent voice rang out.","\"Ouch! Qin Yanzhou, what did you hit me for? Oh, oh, I forgot your mother takes a nap around this time. It is just my first time doing something this huge with you, so I got a little too excited! Hey, how are you so smart? To think you actually managed to find their trail...\"","The voice gradually lowered until his words faded completely out of earshot.","However, it was not long before two silhouettes, one tall and one short, passed through the moon gate and entered the courtyard.","The taller young man had a face as flawless as jade and features as refined as a painting. However, his expression was stoic and his complexion pale, as if he were shrouded in the frigid snow of a high mountain.","The slightly shorter youth wore a fitted martial arts outfit in contrasting black and red, his long hair half-tied up. The entire way inside, he kept his head turned to chat with the person beside him, completely ignoring where he was walking.","Suddenly, the taller young man stopped in his tracks.","The exact moment he paused, Qin Qi Nian reached out and threw an arm around his shoulders in a chummy, brotherly fashion. The youth grinned, flashing a row of white teeth, clearly quite satisfied with his successful sneak attack, even if the height difference made the gesture look rather awkward.","The moment Qin Hongying saw the two walk in, her pupils shrank. She instinctively looked at Dai Li beside her, uncharacteristically unable to hide the astonishment written across her face.","With this mother and son appearing at the same time, anyone could tell at a glance that they were blood relatives.","Her second brother was not injured, yet he had been collecting medicinal herbs on a massive scale, even going so far as to break his own rules and ask her, his biological sister, for help. Looking again at Dai Li's eager excitement just now, it turned out that the one who needed those precious treasures was someone else entirely.","And this person was not even her second brother's woman, but his woman's son.","Was her second brother really racking his brains and exhausting his efforts just to help someone else raise a child?"]},{"number":107,"title":"Chapter 107","paragraphs":["\"Aunt? You arrived early?!\"","Qin Qinian finally saw Qin Hongying in the room. After a moment of pleasant surprise, he quickly straightened up and greeted her formally.","Shi Rongyue also curtsied to him. \"Third Cousin.\"","Qin Qinian smiled brightly, completely oblivious to the strange expression on his aunt's face. \"Rongrong has grown a bit taller than last year.\"","Shi Rongyue's eyes curved into crescents. \"You too, Third Cousin.\"","As they spoke, she secretly observed the unfamiliar young man out of the corner of her eye. After the initial greetings, he hadn't spoken another word, just standing quietly beside the beautiful madam.","Seeming to notice her gaze, he looked up at her. In that instant, Shi Rongyue felt as if she had fallen into a cold, deep pool, the pitch-black water enveloping and drowning her from all sides.","But it lasted only a breath. He looked away, the pool dried up, and everything returned to normal.","Shi Rongyue, however, stood frozen in place.","Because her parents were deeply in love and her mother's family was very powerful, she lived much more freely in the Shi family than most young ladies. In her early years, her father would sometimes bring her along to receive guests. She had met many people, but none as... tranquil as him.","Yes, tranquil.","Cold as a block of ice, showing no obvious emotions. But even as an ice block, he was the best-looking one.","She took another curious peek.","This time, he didn't look back.","Over there, Qin Shaozong had already finished introducing Qin Yanzhou to Qin Hongying, only mentioning that he was Daili's son, that he had now taken Nalan Zhi as his master, and his position in the army.","Qin Hongying's expression grew even stranger.","Just then, Nianxia returned, announcing that the meal was ready.","Qin Hongying temporarily suppressed her bellyful of doubts and simply said, \"After a year apart, Second Brother is much kinder than before.\"","Saying \"kinder\" was putting it mildly; he was ridiculously generous. If it were just widely collecting medicinal herbs, such rare items could still be measured in silver.","But Nalan Zhi?","How could a renowned scholar of his caliber easily accept a disciple? Not to mention he had never taken one before.","And a military position in the North, regardless of rank, was a kind of resource. If there were intentions to support him in the future, he could absolutely soar to great heights.","This was incomparable to medicinal herbs bought with money.","Qin Shaozong heard the hidden meaning in her words but asked in return, \"Oh? How was I before? Tell me.\"","Qin Hongying was speechless.","\"I'm a bit hungry. Rongrong and I will go eat first,\" Qin Hongying changed the subject, preparing to leave with her daughter.","\"Hongying, there is one more thing,\" Qin Shaozong said.","Qin Hongying stopped in her tracks, feeling quite surprised.","Given Daili's eager attitude toward the medicinal herbs earlier, she thought her second brother had summoned her solely for the herb collection.","It wasn't?","Qin Hongying asked, \"What else is there?\"","Qin Shaozong didn't care whether the juniors were present or not. \"A few days ago, Qin San's biological aunt, who misses him, came to visit. After her last visit, she casually arranged for a next time. If she comes again in a few days, you and Madam will host her together.\"","Daili hadn't expected that she would have a part to play in hosting his younger sister's visitor. She immediately looked at Qin Shaozong. But the latter was looking at Qin Hongying.","She and Qin Shaozong stood close, less than half an arm's length apart, their hanging robes just barely touching. In a place no one could see, Qin Shaozong raised his hand and lightly patted Daili's lower back.","For some reason, Daili inexplicably understood that he was telling her not to speak just yet.","She had just obtained the Fleeceflower Root and Musk through his hands.","Fine, she wouldn't speak.","The siblings looked at each other with similar long eyes. Qin Hongying raised her eyebrows slightly, her mind racing.","It was understandable for her to host Qinian's biological aunt, considering there was no main mistress in the estate, she was a daughter of the Qin family, and the biological sister of her second brother. But bringing Daili along...","Thinking of all the broken rules, Qin Hongying had an absurd guess in her heart, but she agreed crisply, \"Alright, no problem.\"","After the two left, five people remained in the room.","Daili looked at the two brocade boxes over and over again. \"Zhou Zhou, the Fleeceflower Root and Musk have both been found. The remaining herbs are not as precious as these two. Tomorrow, when Old Mr. Ding comes to give you acupuncture, you can tell him this good news.\"","Ever since she learned that a whole string of herbs was needed to remove the Gu worm, Daili's heart had never truly settled.","She didn't deny that Qin Shaozong had power and influence, but some things couldn't be solved by power. Like time...","Qin Yanzhou froze, instinctively looking at Qin Shaozong.","He remembered standing by the door of the main room that day, hearing the conversation between the two inside.","His mother's words still rang in his ears. Even though he couldn't see her then, just from that sentence—\"Qin Changgeng, if you make me watch Zhou Zhou suffer with no cure, I cannot do it\"—he could imagine her tearful eyes at that moment.","This man had told his mother to trust him.","Trust?","Two light words, easy to say, but how difficult to achieve.","Meeting his complicated gaze, Qin Shaozong only said lightly, \"I have never broken a promise I made to your mother.\"","Then Qin Shaozong glanced at the three juniors. \"Do you have any important matters?\"","The word \"important\" carried a hint of shooing them away.","Qin Yunce didn't; he had only come to pay his respects after hearing that his aunt and cousin had come to the main courtyard.","He didn't, but Qin Qinian said excitedly, \"Yes, yes, yes, there's a huge matter!\"","Daili looked at the joyful youth, then at her own son, thinking that since the two came together just now, could this matter...","Qin Qinian said as if claiming credit, \"Father, Qin Yanzhou found several strongholds of the Green Lotus Sect in the county. He's amazing! He just walks into a shop, says a few words to the shopkeeper, and can sniff out clues like a hound finding prey.\"","Daili was speechless. I really thank you.","\"Qinian, how are you speaking?\" Qin Yunce tried hard to smooth things over. \"That's not how you praise someone. If Mr. Mi finds out you don't even know how to speak properly, he'll make you copy books again.\"","Qin Qinian instantly shrank his neck. \"Brother, the point isn't that I don't know how to praise people, it's that he found the Green Lotus Sect strongholds!\"","Because their father loathed sects, the Green Lotus Sect had a weak presence in the North. But that didn't mean Qin Qinian knew nothing about it. The Green Lotus Sect blended into the lower and middle classes, making their whereabouts incredibly secretive, harder to find than ants.","But speaking of this, Qin Qinian realized belatedly, \"Qin Yanzhou, how do you know so much about the Green Lotus Sect? Could it be that you used to...\"","\"Qinian.\" Seeing things going south, Qin Yunce cut him off. \"Let's get back to business. Father, since we now know the strongholds of the Green Lotus Sect, how about sending troops to arrest them?\"","Qin Shaozong turned his thumb ring, not responding to Qin Yunce's suggestion, but instead looking at Qin Qinian and Qin Yanzhou. \"What do you two think?\"","Qin Qinian said without hesitation, \"Arrest them, of course.\"","\"Hold off for now. Since they dared to send a message to Mother, they must be confident that Mother will go beg them when the time comes. It's better to play along, enter their trap, and then play the mantis stalking the cicada, unaware of the oriole behind,\" Qin Yanzhou said deeply.","Daili looked at her son in astonishment.","Message?","After coming to Yuyang, the Green Lotus Sect had only sent her a message once. It was the piece of silk cloth Nianxia had presented earlier.","Only she and Qin Changgeng knew about that. How could Zhou Zhou...","Qin Shaozong raised his long eyebrows slightly. The broken tail of his left eyebrow looked like a blade drawn just a fraction from its sheath. Under the gaze of the others, he said something completely unrelated to the topic at hand: \"So there is nothing wrong with your tongue after all, seeing as you can say so much in one breath. Why do you usually act like a sealed gourd, unable to utter a single squeak even if beaten with a stick?\"","Qin Yunce: \"...\"","Qin Yanzhou pursed his lips.","Daili still stood very close to Qin Shaozong. Just now, when he raised his hand to pat her lower back, no one had noticed.","Now, Daili also raised her hand behind him, touching the edge of the leather belt at his lower back, and gave him a pinch through his clothes.","Qin Shaozong: \"...\"","Qin Shaozong cleared his throat softly. \"Going with the flow is an excellent plan. Your aunt has been an avid collector of medicinal herbs for many years, and ordinary people are not allowed into her treasure trove. Presumably, the Qinglian Cult does not know how much she has in her possession. Now that she has come to Yuyang, the other side must already know her itinerary. Tomorrow, I will have my men stop searching for fleeceflower root and only continue looking for musk. This will make them think we have only acquired enough fleeceflower root.\"","The words \"your aunt\" were directed at Qin Yanzhou. The young man lowered his eyes and said nothing else.","Qin Shaozong added, \"During the days your cousin stays at the manor, you may show her around.\"","The Qin brothers voiced their agreement.","To stop the search for fleeceflower root, he needed to send messages not only to Jin Duole but also to Qiao Wangfei, who was far away in the south.","Qin Shaozong later went to his study. After finishing the two letters, he put down his wolf-hair brush and picked up the tiger-shaped brush rest on the desk.","His long, dark fingers stroked the brush rest, rubbing over the alternating yellow and black stripes of the tiger's back. Perhaps because it was frequently played with by its owner, this brush rest had become glossier than it originally was.","Looking at the small brush rest, Qin Shaozong suddenly clicked his tongue softly. \"You certainly are precious.\"","After being with her for so long, she had only given him this broken little brush rest.","Other than this, nothing.","\"This stingy temper of yours, sooner or later I will correct it.\" Closing his large hand around it, Qin Shaozong called Hu Bao in from outside.","\"My Lord, what are your orders?\"","Qin Shaozong handed over the two previously written letters. \"Have someone ride at top speed to deliver these to Jin Duole and Qiao Wangfei respectively.\"","Hu Bao took the letters but did not immediately turn around, waiting for his superior's further instructions.","Qin Shaozong said, \"Have Wei Qing come to the study. Go.\"","\"Understood.\"","\"Wei Qing, the Lord wants you to go to the study.\" Hu Bao found the man in another courtyard.","When he found him, Wei Qing was not the only one in the courtyard; Feng Feng and the others were also there, gathered together chatting.","The called man was slightly stunned. Before he could speak, Mo Yanyun asked, \"Did the Lord say what it is about?\"","Hu Bao replied, \"He did not.\"","Not only Wei Qing, but the others were also full of doubts.","\"Old Wei, has that younger brother of yours been bullying men and women again?\" Feng Feng stroked his chin.","Among the four garrison commanders of the Xuanxiao Cavalry in the east, south, west, and north, Wei Qing was actually slightly more distant from their superior compared to Bai Jianping, Feng Feng, and Qiao Wangfei.","The reason was simple: he came from a prominent family and had the best background among the four commanders.","He was already a garrison commander. If he also became the Marquis of Wu'an's absolute top confidant in the eyes of others, the Wei family would likely become too arrogant.","Even if those matters had nothing to do with Wei Qing and were not his wish, he could not stop others from using his name to throw their weight around.","Hearing this, Wei Qing frowned. \"After he committed evil last time, I went back and broke his legs. He clearly promised me that he would turn over a new leaf and start anew.\"","\"Could it be that he didn't learn his lesson after his injuries healed?\"","\"I will go over first and see,\" Wei Qing said.","On the way to the study, Wei Qing thought and thought, but even when he arrived at the study, he still could not figure out the reason.","The study door was wide open. He walked straight in, saluted Qin Shaozong who was sitting behind the desk, and asked, \"My Lord, for what matter were you looking for me?\"","Qin Shaozong said, \"Go close the door.\"","Wei Qing went back to close the door.","Once the door was closed, only the two of them were left in the room.","Silence flooded the room, so quiet that one could hear a pin drop. The man behind the desk did not speak immediately.","Wei Qing was already a little nervous, and now seeing his superior looking at him in silence, a layer of cold sweat broke out on his back.","What matter could be so critical that the usually decisive Lord would actually hesitate? Could it be that those bastards in the Wei family had pierced the heavens this time, and he, the unlucky commander, was going to be implicated?","Wei Qing's nerves were taut, and his fingers curled involuntarily. With all the previous mistakes of the Wei family as a warning, unable to bear the heavy burden, he simply dropped to one knee to plead for punishment:","\"I beg the Lord, for the sake of the hard work your subordinate has put in over the years even if there is no great merit, please do not let the innocent suffer.\"","\"The matter I am about to ask you, once you step out of this door, you must not speak of it to outsiders.\"","The two voices rang out almost simultaneously.","Wei Qing froze, then shot up to his feet, wishing he could swallow the words he had just said.","This didn't sound like the Wei family's messy affairs at all!","Qin Shaozong did not mind his subordinate's recklessness. \"I remember that your marriage with your esteemed wife had quite a few twists and turns at the beginning. She was unwilling to marry you, but later you two became a harmonious and deeply loving couple. Jinsong, is there a secret to this change?\""]},{"number":108,"title":"Chapter 108","paragraphs":["Wei Qing was the eldest illegitimate son of the Wei family. After the death of his favored biological mother, his position as a thorn in his legitimate mother's side became even more precarious. It just so happened that the Northern Kingdom invaded at that time, and Youzhou was conscripting soldiers on a large scale. Through a series of mishaps, Wei Qing signed up.","Regardless of the hidden machinations behind his enlistment, the fact remained that he ended up on the battlefield. Relying on his own abilities, he carved out a path to survival. As the years passed, he accumulated a significant amount of military merit and was promoted step by step. Finally, after the old garrison commander of the Xuanxiao Cavalry's northern camp retired, he successfully filled the vacancy.","The family situations of military generals were practically open secrets. After all, when they gathered to chat after meals, they couldn't discuss the refined arts of zither, chess, calligraphy, and painting, so they could only talk about other things.","For instance, when Feng Feng first began to show his talent, a minor official caught him under the examination board as a son-in-law, marrying his daughter to him and betting on this promising young man.","Bai Jianping's wife was a female herb gatherer. At that time, he was not yet a commander. He had followed the army into the mountains to suppress bandits, but due to his superior's poor command, he fell into an enemy trap. After falling off a cliff, he was rescued by the herb gatherer. Later, he relentlessly pestered her to pledge herself to him. They had three daughters after marriage, and he never took concubines to try for a son even after rising to power.","As for Wei Qing, his first wife was his cousin.","Wei Qing froze in place. No, he wasn't just frozen; he was completely dumbfounded.","In his mind, even if the Lord wasn't seeking him out to settle scores with the Wei family, he would at least be assigning him a secret mission. But he never expected that the Lord would actually ask about his family matters.","And specifically, about his history with his wife.","If Mo Yanyun or anyone else had asked this, Wei Qing wouldn't have found it strange at all.","But this was Qin Shaozong.","The Lord never paid attention to the women in their chambers; he neither inquired nor interfered.","Wei Qing stood there blankly. Qin Shaozong didn't rush him, merely toying with the tiger-shaped brush rest in his palm.","By the time the small brush rest had been turned over for the third time, Wei Qing, standing a short distance away, finally snapped back to his senses.","...At that time, my family suffered some misfortunes. Her aunt didn't want her to marry me and arranged for her to meet another of her cousins. The family Wei Qing referred to was not the Wei family, but the small household consisting of him and his biological mother.","Qin Shaozong stopped rubbing the brush rest. She took a liking to the other cousin?","Marriage arrangements were certainly the orders of parents and the words of matchmakers, but if it was an alliance between relatives, it was inevitable for the younger generation to meet.","Wei Qing slightly lowered his head.","Seeing his expression, Qin Shaozong knew he had guessed right.","At that time, I wasn't her best option, and I was going to join the army shortly after. I had no reason to drag her down. Later, as I built my career and established merits by the Lord's side, I was no longer the man I used to be, so I... snatched her back. Wei Qing stealthily observed his superior's expression.","Snatching another man's wife could only be described as dishonorable.","Yet, coincidentally, there were two people in this room, and both had committed this highly dishonorable act.","Qin Shaozong straightened his spine slightly, losing his previous languid demeanor. What happened next?","Wei Qing then recounted the general course of events, including how he planned before acting, sent people to carefully investigate his wife's former husband, and found a young woman to appear in the guise of his former confidante, seducing the man until he intended to divorce his wife.","If it were anyone else, Wei Qing would absolutely never speak of this, as it was too despicable. But who could blame him when there was a fellow conspirator sitting right in front of him.","The Lord had always been unconventional in his military campaigns, caring only about the final results. Whether the Lord's final actions would be even more despicable than his own was actually hard to say.","...In short, I forcefully married her first, and then cherished and valued her, giving her whatever she liked, and then had a child or two with her. Women always care about their children; some even value them more than their husbands. If you treat the child well, sometimes she will be happier than if she had received a treasure herself. After a long time, she naturally won't dwell on or care about the past, Wei Qing concluded.","Qin Shaozong's eyes darkened. I understand.","After Wei Qing left, Qin Shaozong sat behind his desk for a long time. The man picked up his brush, dipped it in ink, and wrote three characters on the mulberry paper spread across the desk.","Looking at the name, the man's gaze was obscure and unreadable.","The last time she saw Wei Cheng, Dai Li had only sat for a short while before excusing herself. Later, when Qin Shaozong mentioned that the other party had arranged another meeting, Dai Li thought it might just be a casual pleasantry, but she didn't expect the visiting card to be sent over again.","It was addressed to her once again.","Let her come. After all, she is Qinian's biological aunt; it wouldn't be good to refuse, Qin Hongying said, looking at the visiting card.","Dai Li picked up a brush to write.","Qin Hongying was talking to her from the side. As Dai Li responded while writing the reply, she momentarily lost focus and wrote two simplified Chinese characters.","What character is this? As soon as Qin Hongying asked, she watched helplessly as Dai Li crossed it out and casually took a fresh sheet of paper as if nothing had happened.","Qin Hongying was speechless.","Hongying, you mentioned before that your riding skills are excellent. Could you teach me how to ride a horse? Dai Li changed the subject.","In the past, she hadn't thought riding a horse was important, but after that time fleeing for her life, she suddenly realized that this skill was quite useful in ancient times.","Since returning from Bairi City, Zhouzhou's Gu poison had left her overwhelmed. Now that everything seemed to be going smoothly, she could spare some energy to plan for the future.","Qin Hongying let out a laugh. You really are an interesting person.","To be caught red-handed and still be able to change the subject so calmly and naturally. Could it be that she was highly experienced, having been caught too many times by her second brother in the past?","During her short stay at the manor over the past two days, Qin Hongying had gained a superficial understanding of Dai Li's background. When she first heard about it, she was amazed and inexplicably understood her second brother's obsession.","Even putting aside Dai Li's beautiful appearance, the matter of the salt rocks alone was enough for her second brother to keep her bound to his side.","Alright, I'll teach you another day, Qin Hongying agreed.","After the reply was sent out, Wei Cheng came to visit again the following day.","Just like last time, as if she feared Qin Qinian was lacking food and clothing here, she arrived with generous gifts.","But unlike last time, she didn't come alone. Accompanying her was a young woman with an outstanding appearance.","The woman wore a married woman's hair bun and a mica-colored long skirt. Her attire was plain and elegant, adorned only with a finely carved orchid jade hairpin on her head and a white jade bracelet on her pale wrist.","The beautiful woman had clear, expressive eyes and willow-leaf eyebrows. With her brows slightly furrowed, she naturally exuded a delicate and pitiful aura.","Qin Qinian came to the side door to receive them just like before, but seeing another person step down from the carriage, he couldn't help but freeze. He took a few extra glances, feeling that the young woman looked somewhat familiar, as if he had seen her somewhere before.","After greeting Wei Cheng, Qin Qinian asked, Aunt, have you brought a friend to visit?","What nonsense are you spouting, child? This is your Aunt Pingzhi, Wei Cheng playfully scolded.","Seeing Qin Qinian's astonishment, she smiled and added, After my sister passed away, your maternal grandfather and your father made an agreement to let Pingzhi take care of you and your father. Now that your brother-in-law is injured, how could Pingzhi be absent?","Prompted by her words, Qin Qinian finally remembered.","This was Concubine Li!","Qin Qinian's mind was in a mess. He felt that something was amiss, but with his elders present, and both of them being his aunts, it was difficult for him to ask, Why did you bring her directly out of the Marquis's manor?","The young man scratched his head. Aunts, please come in first. My older aunt and Lady Dai are already in the main hall.","Wei Cheng's expression changed drastically. Your older aunt is back?","Yuyang Commandery was incredibly large, and the number of convoys entering and exiting every day was unknown. A few days ago, it was rumored that a cavalry unit had escorted a carriage into the Qin Manor, but the identity of the person inside the carriage remained unknown.","Her father had guessed that it might be someone like Nalan Zhi, a strategist who had previously accompanied the army south, returning a step behind the others and coming to visit the lord upon his return.","But now, it turned out that the person in the carriage was Qin Hongying.","Qin Qinian nodded. My aunt and cousin have come back to visit my father. They will be staying at the manor for a short while.","Wei Cheng's mind raced. Finally, she looked at Wei Pingzhi, who had remained silent all along, thinking to herself: could Qin Hongying, as a younger sister, really extend her reach into her older brother's inner courtyard? There was no such reasoning.","Her father was right. The Marquis of Wu'an had already made his intention to remarry plainly known, from something as major as instructing the Cai family to apply pressure, to something as minor as relocating all the concubines out of the Marquis's estate.","When it came to taking a wife, he seemed determined to see it through. And their Wei family absolutely could not just sit and wait for their doom!","After all, the title of the main wife of the Marquis's estate was not merely an honorific; it involved the transition of power in Yuyang, and even the entire northern region.","It could be said that however far the Marquis of Wu'an's future influence reached, the impact of this position would run just as deep. How could the Wei family willingly hand over the fat piece of meat they had enjoyed so much in the past to someone else?","As they walked into the front courtyard, Wei Cheng whispered to her younger concubine-born sister beside her, Other than here, there is nowhere else for you to settle down. Do you understand?","Wei Pingzhi furrowed her delicate brows and nodded. I understand.","Qin Hongying and Dai Li were already in the main hall. Seeing Wei Cheng arrive arm in arm with an unfamiliar young woman, Dai Li's brow twitched slightly. Her intuition told her that today's reception would probably not follow the usual protocols.","After years apart, Fifth Lady Wei, you have truly changed a lot, Qin Hongying said, sizing up Wei Cheng.","Both were legitimate daughters, and the Qin and Wei families were both prominent clans in Yuyang. Before the young ladies were married, they inevitably mingled in the same social circles.","Qin Hongying did not particularly like Wei Cheng. In truth, she did not have much of an issue with her personally; it was mainly because the Wei family had taken advantage of their misfortune back then, adopting an overly haughty posture.","From then on, she felt quite apathetic toward anyone from the Wei family. As for now, with her second brother's instructions beforehand...","Wei Cheng smiled and exchanged pleasantries, flattering her. You haven't changed a bit. Even after giving birth to three children, your appearance is exactly as it was back then, and your aura is even more striking than before.","You really have changed. You never used to speak so glibly, Qin Hongying laughed. Her gaze shifted to Wei Pingzhi, sharply picking out a trace or two of resemblance in their facial features.","She narrowed her eyes, the corners of her eyes lifting in a slightly sharp curve. You, Fifth Lady Wei, truly have a grand entourage. Bringing so many maidservants here, are you afraid there is no one in the estate for you to order around?","Wei Cheng rejoiced inwardly, thinking this played right into her hands. She smiled and was about to reply, but unexpectedly, the other party's speech sped up—","Fifth Lady Wei, you can rest completely assured. My second brother was worried that his sweetheart wouldn't be served properly, so he specially transferred a large number of maidservants from the Marquis's estate, in addition to buying servants from out of town. Sigh, the whole estate is full of people now, so packed that there's barely any room to stand.","Dai Li had originally been sitting to the side, acting as a decorative vase.","For today's reception, with Qin Shaozong's sister present, she consciously placed herself in a supporting role.","The moment the two sides met and she heard the conversation between Qin Hongying and Wei Cheng, she thought to herself that even a supporting role was unnecessary. Qin Hongying was more than capable of handling it alone, allowing her to slack off to her heart's content.","But before she could slack off for long, she was struck by Qin Hongying's phrase his sweetheart.","Dai Li's mouth twitched. She tried her best to resist the urge to turn and look at Qin Hongying, maintaining her polite, faint smile.","The young woman who had come in with Wei Cheng had not been introduced, but Dai Li felt her identity was not hard to guess. Not only was Qin Qinian frequently looking at her, seeming to want to speak but hesitating, but her nose also bore some resemblance to Wei Cheng's.","A subtle gaze came from below. Just as Dai Li met it, the other party lowered her eyes and looked away.","Dai Li could only see the woman lowering her head meekly, her delicate brows slightly furrowed, looking like a fragile little white flower that could not withstand the wind and rain.","Dai Li: ...","Qin Hongying, who was speaking to Wei Cheng, waved her hand. So there's no need for your servants here. Have the two of them wait outside for you. I guarantee that once they step out, you'll still have plenty of servants at your disposal.","Wei Cheng's gaze sharpened. She realized that the situation was not playing right into her hands at all. The other party had clearly perceived Wei Pingzhi's identity and was simply denying her the chance to introduce her, directly treating the person as a servant and driving her out.","But was she just an ordinary maidservant?","The Wei family had gone to great lengths to find the residence where Wei Pingzhi was staying after being moved out of the Marquis's estate, and it wasn't just to have her kicked out of the Qin manor after less than a quarter of an hour.","Ah, Hongying, you haven't met her, so it's quite normal that you don't recognize my sister. Back in the day, Pingzhi almost became your second sister-in-law. It was only because my brother-in-law still missed my older sister and couldn't bear to let anyone else take her place as his wife that he only took her in as a concubine, having her enter the estate to take care of Qinian, Wei Cheng said with a smile.","She was laying the matter completely out in the open.","Qin Hongying frowned imperceptibly.","The next moment, she heard the woman opposite her say, Years ago, my brother-in-law promised our Wei family that if he ever remarried, he would only marry a daughter of the Wei family. For the past fifteen years, my brother-in-law has kept his promise and never gone back on his word. Now that he is injured on the battlefield, how can Pingzhi, as a Wei daughter in his inner courtyard, stand by and do nothing?","On the words kept his promise and never gone back on his word, her tone was slightly emphasized.","Qin Hongying's gaze grew cold.","Sitting in the seat of honor, Dai Li watched as Wei Cheng's words seemed to act like a gust of wind, causing the little white flower seated below to slightly raise her head.","The woman timidly stole a glance at her, and upon being discovered, lowered her head as if frightened.","Dai Li was quite curious. Looking at Wei Pingzhi's appearance, she seemed about twenty-five or twenty-six. Being born into a wealthy family, her actual age was probably a bit older. For a woman of this age to be so timid even during a normal reception was surprising.","Was this done on purpose, or had she been trapped in a palm-sized inner courtyard all her life, rarely seeing anyone?","If it was the former, Qin Shaozong himself wasn't even here; even if she burst into tears on the spot, he wouldn't see it.","If it was the latter, the Wei family definitely had more than one concubine-born daughter. For Wei Pingzhi to stand out among all the other concubine-born daughters back then, it surely took more than just her beauty.","Logically speaking, if she was scheming to take over the position of the main wife, there was no reason for her not to know how to behave when meeting guests.","Could it be that this act was meant for her to see?","Dai Li's pupils trembled slightly as realization seemed to dawn on her.","While Dai Li was studying Wei Pingzhi, Qin Hongying also spared a fraction of her attention to observe Dai Li.","What she saw gave her a great shock; this was no small matter.","This sweetheart of her second brother was quite unusual!","An ordinary woman, deeply in love with her husband, upon suddenly seeing his past concubine—and being told by others that this concubine who had delivered herself to the door almost became her husband's main wife back in the day, coupled with the fact that the woman intended to stay—would certainly find the sight of her completely grating.","Yet, this sweetheart merely showed a look of pure curiosity.","A flash of lightning crossed Qin Hongying's mind, and she suddenly understood something.","If her second brother only wanted the fleeceflower root and musk, he could have easily sent someone to fetch them; there was no need to have her, his younger sister, make the trip personally.","But the reality was the opposite. Not only had she come, but she had also been entrusted by her second brother with the task of receiving the visiting Wei family.","Because he clearly knew that Daili had no desire to deal with the situation, and was even worried she might be tricked by the Wei family into letting them into the estate, he had summoned her, his younger sister living far away in another province, all the way back to act as the vanguard.","Qin Hongying was utterly dumbfounded. Her myriad of complicated feelings ultimately condensed into a single thought: what goes around comes around, and the heavens spare no one. To think that someone as domineering as her second brother would actually see a day like this."]},{"number":109,"title":"Chapter 109","paragraphs":["Having thousands of emotions in her heart was one thing, but on the surface, Qin Hongying looked at Wei Cheng with sharp eyes. \"Old Mr. Ding has miraculous medical skills, and my second brother's injury is no longer a major problem. What exactly happened in the past, the younger generation doesn't know, and those who don't understand the inside story don't know either, but don't you and I know the inside story?\"","The Wei family put on such a high air back then, demanding that the second brother marry the concubine-born daughter of the Wei family as a second wife was only one of the conditions, and there were two, three, four, five, and six more to follow.","Without waiting for Wei Cheng to speak, Qin Hongying said displeasedly, \"My second brother has a strong personality and dislikes others threatening him the most. In the past, bandits in the Bolei Mountain and Tianze Mountain range became a disaster. My second brother originally only wanted to send his subordinates to suppress the bandits, but those two bandit leaders didn't know the immensity of heaven and earth, and actually sent a letter to my second brother, intending to ask for an official post so as to give themselves a proper title. They even boasted that if the second brother didn't agree, they would lead troops to slaughter all the surrounding common people. Heh, what do you guess the result was, Fifth Lady Wei?\"","When Qin Hongying mentioned \"Bolei Mountain and Tianze Mountain range\", Dai Li recalled some old memories.","That was more than half a year ago. At that time, she fled from Nankang Commandery to Taiping Commandery, and was caught by Qin Shaozong in Taiping Commandery. The troops of the salt smuggler Li Zan came upon hearing the news, and Qin Shaozong took her to climb the mountain to hide.","In that small cave, the guard told her that the bandit suppression campaign back then was personally led by Qin Shaozong, and several Jingguan were built in a row. For more than ten years since then, there has been no bandit disaster in those two places.","Wei Cheng seemed to have heard of this, and her face turned slightly pale.","Qin Hongying sneered and said, \"After my second brother received the letter from the bandit leader, he was furious, scolding them for their wishful thinking. He immediately changed the commander before the battle and personally put on armor to go into battle.\"","Qin Hongying also emphasized the four words \"wishful thinking\".","\"Fifth Lady Wei, have you ever seen a Jingguan? A small mountain piled up with heads, each head bloody. When the heads were cut off, those bandits still had their eyes wide open, terrified and dying with remaining grievances. Several Jingguan lined up in a row, and the blood dyed the surrounding land red, even converging into a red stream. Even the land was soaked soft by the blood. When you stepped on it, blood would seep out from the side of your boots with a 'zi' sound, and sometimes you could even see some minced meat.\" Qin Hongying sighed as if reminiscing.","Dai Li couldn't help but turn her head, with a little imperceptible suspicion in her eyes.","This eldest miss spoke as if she had been there in person. But if Qin Shaozong was the commander, would he let his sister go with him?","But regardless of whether it was true or false, the power of Qin Hongying's words was extraordinary. The blood color on the faces of the Wei sisters faded little by little, one paler than the other.","Wei Cheng's lips trembled, but she couldn't speak.","Chun Ri","Qin Hongying stared at her without blinking, the implication in her eyes even stronger. \"So, those who threaten my second brother are really trying to be clever but ending up making a fool of themselves. What kind of temper does my second brother have? He has been a tough bone since childhood. If you talk to him nicely, he can still give you a way out for the sake of your obedience. If you don't know what's good for you and insist on poking his reverse scale, then it's really...\"","Qin Hongying didn't say what it really was, but only replaced it with a sneer.","The delicate bodies of the Wei sisters trembled, like yellow leaves hanging on the treetops.","And just when Dai Li suspected whether these two would be scared out of their wits in the main hall—","\"Pingzhi!\" Wei Cheng saw the person beside her go soft, and was shocked at first.","But later she reacted, restraining the bright light in her eyes to support the person. \"Pingzhi, what's wrong with you? Is it a relapse of your old illness? Don't be afraid. The best doctor in Yuyang is in this mansion. Your brother-in-law is magnanimous and kind-hearted, and he will definitely be able to help you turn danger into safety.\"","Dai Li: \"...\"","Qin Hongying: \"...\"","Qin Hongying was really laughed out of anger.","She married the legitimate eldest son of the Shi family back then. Her husband was a subordinate of her father, which was considered a marriage down. After marriage, her husband's backyard was clean. Her mother-in-law and uncle treated her like a biological daughter. Her several sisters-in-law respected and feared her, and even if they had ulterior motives, they didn't dare to play tricks in front of her.","Seeing less after marriage didn't mean she couldn't understand.","Thinking back to the time after her twin brother died in battle, for a period of time, all the monsters and demons of the collateral branches of the Qin family came out and made a big fuss in front of her.","But that was more than ten years ago. This daughter of the Wei family was fine. After more than ten years, she helped her review the feeling of being designed, and the method used was so clumsy.","\"Aunt, this...\" Qin Qinian was dumbfounded and didn't know what to do.","He subconsciously took a few steps forward, wanting to help Wei Pingzhi up, but felt it was inappropriate.","Qin Hongying turned her head and said to Qin Qinian: \"Qinian, you run fast, go quickly to find Old Mr. Ding. When he came to the mansion earlier, he was accompanied by two servants who understand medical principles. You let one of the servants bring the needle box and come with you, and wake the person up first.\"","Qin Qinian ran out like a gust of wind.","And as soon as the words \"needle box\" came out, Wei Cheng clearly saw Wei Pingzhi's eyelashes tremble.","She quickly stopped him and said: \"There's no need to let the servants come. I just looked at it. Pingzhi shouldn't be suffering from a relapse of an old illness, but just fainted from fright. It's better to find a courtyard for her to rest. When she's well rested, she will naturally wake up.\"","\"Inappropriate. My second brother previously said that a sick person must not be moved without authorization. If she accidentally bumps into somewhere and aggravates her condition, it will be too late for regrets.\" Qin Hongying said with a half-smile: \"Second brother is experienced in hundreds of battles and has rich experience. He certainly won't make a mistake. Fifth Lady Wei, am I right?\"","Having just said \"give a way out for the sake of obedience\", now Wei Cheng really didn't have the courage to shake her head.","The situation was in a stalemate for a while. Dai Li personally watched a small-scale inner courtyard struggle at the scene, and sighed repeatedly in her heart, feeling even more that the main wife of a wealthy family was not easy to be.","Today this one faints, tomorrow that one has body aches, it's really not peaceful.","Qin Shaozong wasn't here, and he didn't know what Dai Li was thinking. If he knew, he would probably be so angry that a breath of air would rush straight to the top of his head.","Not long after, Qin Qinian returned with an attendant carrying a medicine box.","\"This Junior Lady Wei looks sickly. Don't be stingy, be sure to give her a few more needles.\" Qin Hongying smiled from the side.","Although he was an attendant, how could someone who could accompany Ding Luying be an ordinary doctor. The other party didn't rashly insert the needles, but first felt the pulse. As soon as this pulse was explored, he knew what was going on.","Wealthy and powerful families have always had many struggles, and doctors didn't dare to say too much, but carefully said: \"Madam Qin, she is fine.\"","Qin Hongying urged: \"If she's fine, hurry up and give her two needles. As long as you wake her up, it's fine. My second brother is now spending money like water everywhere to seek famous medicines, and the pressure to support the family is quite high. The mansion can no longer support other people.\"","Doctor: \"...\"","Dai Li touched her nose.","\"Stick the needles. If there's a problem, it's on me. Even if you hit some acupoint and make her half paralyzed, it doesn't matter. Anyway, my dowry is generous. At worst, I'll take this woman back to Nanyu Commandery, casually find a manor, and send two or three slaves to serve her for a lifetime.\" Qin Hongying said lightly.","As soon as these words fell, the person who had been \"unconscious\" just now made a movement.","Wei Cheng secretly gritted her teeth, but there was nothing she could do. She could only feign pleasant surprise, \"Pingzhi, you're awake? Good thing it was just a minor ailment. If something bad had happened, how could I explain it to my brother-in-law? After all, you have served in the Marquis's manor for so many years; even if you have no merit, you have worked hard!\"","Qin Hongying couldn't even be bothered to reply to this. \"Since you are feeling unwell, go back and get more rest. Don't run around everywhere, otherwise, if something bad happens, you can only blame yourself for not listening to others' advice.\"","Having said that, Qin Hongying called her nephew's name, \"Qinian, see them out.\"","At first, Qin Qinian truly thought Wei Pingzhi was unwell, but after that scene, even a fool could see through the act.","Feeling played, Qin Qinian was not very happy, but the other party was his elder, so he could only say, \"Aunt, please come with me.\"","With the situation turning out like this, Wei Cheng knew she could not stay any longer today. \"Qinian, your Aunt Pingzhi and I will go back first. We will come see you another day.\"","Qin Qinian hesitated to speak.","After leaving the main hall, Wei Cheng showed a sorrowful expression. \"Qinian, the Wei family is your mother's clan; this is an unbreakable bloodline. We will always be in the same boat. In the future, whatever you seek, the Wei family will spare no effort to plan for you.\"","Qin Qinian was sixteen years old. He wasn't old, but he couldn't be considered young either.","At his age, there were already people automatically gathering around him. Whether it was to eat, drink, and play together, or to help him plan for the future, a faction had formed with Qin Qinian at its core.","It wasn't that Qin Qinian didn't know certain things. Just like now, even though Wei Cheng spoke tactfully, he still heard the implied meaning.","The young man shook his head. \"Aunt, you don't need to do this. Father has already made decisions on many matters. I trust his judgment, and as a son, I only need to obey his arrangements.\"","Wei Cheng felt resentful that he failed to meet her expectations. \"Qinian! Yanzhou has already been taken by your father, and he will definitely not stop there in the future. You are his only biological son; no one is more legitimate than you. How can there be any reason to hand over such a massive family estate to someone else?\"","Qin Qinian just smiled and said nothing.","Seeing his foolishly happy and carefree appearance, Wei Cheng almost lost her breath. \"You treat others well, but who knows what they secretly think of you! Qinian, even if you don't plan for your own future, you must consider your deceased mother and your relatives. The honor and disgrace of the entire Wei family rest entirely on your shoulders!\"","Qin Qinian said with a headache, \"Aunt, please spare me. My first, second, and third uncles all have children, and my older male cousins are all older than me. It's not my turn to carry the honor and disgrace of the Wei family.\"","Wei Cheng hadn't felt much when Qin Hongying made veiled sarcastic remarks at her in the main hall earlier. But hearing her nephew's words now, her vision truly went black, she felt dizzy, and almost collapsed to the ground.","When Daili returned to the main courtyard, she saw that Qin Shaozong was surprisingly there.","She didn't know since when, but he increasingly liked coming to the main courtyard to handle official business.","Letters were moved here to be answered. While Daili took her afternoon nap, Qin Shaozong would sit by the desk in the outer room to process official affairs. Sometimes, when guards brought urgent letters into the manor and couldn't find him in the study, they would immediately come to the main courtyard.","Seeing Daili return at this moment, Qin Shaozong asked, \"Madam is back. How did it go?\"","Daili told the truth, \"Quite spectacular.\"","Qin Shaozong's brush-wielding hand paused slightly. On the not-so-smooth mulberry paper, this pause caused an obvious break in a stroke.","Finishing the character expressionlessly, Qin Shaozong put down his wolf-hair brush and patted the seat next to him. \"Come, Madam, come over and tell me, why do you say it was spectacular?\"","Daili didn't think much of it; she was used to it.","When this man handled official business in the main courtyard, he would occasionally assign her small tasks, such as sealing letters with clay.","Daili walked over, sat down, and sighed, \"A sharp tongue is like a dragon-spring sword, killing without drawing blood. You weren't there, so you don't know how formidable your sister is. With just a few short sentences, she made Wei Pingzhi, who had fainted and intended to stay in the manor, wake right back up.\"","After briefly explaining, Daili further praised Qin Hongying's combat power, \"Hongying is quick-witted and handles things with ease. She truly is worthy of being the matriarch of a noble family.\"","Qin Shaozong was certain. He indeed heard a sense of rejoicing in her few short sighs.","Rejoicing that she wasn't the one who had to deal with these troublesome matters.","Qin Shaozong's face darkened slightly. He had Hongying come to Yuyang, but not to scare Daili into staying far away from the position of the matriarch. \"There won't be so many matters in the future.\"","Daili muttered something softly.","Her voice was small and mumbled, but Qin Shaozong heard it clearly.","She said: It's not up to you.","Did these words mean that if she didn't nod, she simply wouldn't take the position of the matriarch, and therefore it wasn't up to him?","Or did it mean that this matriarch position was destined to be burdened with numerous affairs, and it wouldn't magically become unbusy just because he said \"there won't be so many matters\"?","\"Seal these.\" Qin Shaozong placed a stack of letters in front of Daili.","Daili began to fiddle with the sealing clay.","Qin Shaozong stopped writing letters. Instead, he sat to the side, rolled up her naturally hanging skirt ribbon with one hand, wrapped it around his fingers, and watched her while playing with it.","For some reason, Daili felt the creeps from his gaze at this very moment, and her sixth sense's alarm was blaring.","It wasn't as if she hadn't helped him seal letters before, nor was it that she had never been watched by him.","However, the feeling this time was quite different.","If forced to make an analogy, it was like being stared at by a starving tiger in the night. Those tiger eyes, emitting an eerie, cold light, carefully scrutinized every part, occasionally nudging with its nose, seeming to consider the most suitable place to take a bite.","After sealing three letters in a row, Daili could no longer stand his gaze, which was so vastly different from usual.","She didn't know what this man was brewing, but it was definitely about her, and to her, it might not be a good thing.","\"Qin Changgeng, I suddenly remembered there are some things I need to instruct Zhou Zhou about. I'll go find him first. I'll help you with these letters when I come back.\" Daili put down the things and wanted to leave.","The man who had previously been playing with her waist sash around his fingers now grabbed her sash and gave it a light tug.","Daili's footsteps paused slightly.","He immediately let go, and the crimson waist sash uncoiled and scattered. Then, a large, dark hand with distinct knuckles reached over and precisely grabbed Daili's arm, forcefully pulling her back just as she had stood up.","The force of his pull was controlled exceptionally well; it only made Daili sit back in her original position without falling toward him.","\"Madam, I have an important matter to discuss with you.\" Seeing her gaze drifting toward the door, Qin Shaozong added, \"This matter involves Qin Yanzhou.\"","Daili was stunned. \"It involves Zhou Zhou? What is it?\"","\"The amount of musk is insufficient,\" he said thus.","\"How is that possible?\" Daili's first reaction was to question it.","She was completely clear about every medicinal herb and its required amount on the three lists of medicinal materials written by Old Mister Ding.","Only later did she learn that the musk and fleeceflower root Qin Hongying brought that day were things she had started saving since her youth. She had saved them for over twenty years, and they were all in those two brocade boxes.","The amount was absolutely enough; she had seen it with her own eyes.","\"Not enough,\" Qin Shaozong repeated. His tone was calm, yet it carried an unquestionable dominance.","Dai Li gazed into those light-colored eyes, her emotions churning. She suddenly felt a profound sense of absurdity, as if he were deliberately twisting the truth.","If he said it was not enough, then even enough would become not enough.","\"Qin Changgeng...\" Dai Li's lips parted slightly.","Qin Shaozong stared at her intently. \"Musk is expensive and unsafe to be left out, so I had it stored away in the treasury of the Marquis Manor. And this treasury, other than myself, can only be opened by the Lady of the House.\""]},{"number":110,"title":"Chapter 110","paragraphs":["The main room was completely silent. The faint fragrance wafting from the incense burner in the corner seemed to be the only movement in this still, picture-like scene.","Outside the window, a squirrel was chattering in the tree. To Daili, every sound felt like a falling pinecone, thumping heavily against her heart and causing it to sink deeper and deeper.","Just now, when he said for the second time that the \"quantity was insufficient,\" her heart had skipped a beat, bringing a vague, ominous premonition.","With his final sentence, \"Only the legal wife can open it,\" the mist clouding her eyes vanished. She finally saw the giant tiger lurking in the depths of the jungle.","Its maw was wide open, just waiting for her to walk right into it.","Daili opened her mouth to say something, but felt it would be futile.","She knew very well that he wouldn't listen to any of her polite refusals; he would only stubbornly and willfully do exactly as he pleased.","A profound sense of powerlessness washed over Daili.","Qin Shaozong had originally been holding her arm, but now his large hand moved forward, covering her soft, pale hand and wrapping it completely in his grasp. \"What is Madam's decision? If it is difficult to choose, there is no harm in thinking it over. There are still eleven days left until the deadline given by Old Mister Ding.\"","Daili raised her eyes to look at him. \"Have you given me any room to choose?\"","It seemed like a choice, but there was no choice at all. Just as she had said from the beginning: she could never just stand by and watch Zhouzhou go without his medicine.","Whether it was the Green Lotus Cult or Qin Shaozong, as long as they could help Zhouzhou safely pass this dangerous hurdle, she was willing to make a deal with them.","The former harbored unpredictable intentions, while the latter also had his own motives. It was just that what they plotted for was different.","\"Naturally, there is room for choice. Whether the door to this storehouse opens or not is entirely up to Madam,\" Qin Shaozong said.","Daili tried to withdraw her hand, but he pinched her fingertips. \"Qin Changgeng!\"","Her calling of his name carried a hint of fiery anger.","Hearing this, Qin Shaozong released her hand. \"I shall await Madam's good news.\"","After saying this, the man picked up the teapot on the table and poured Daili a cup of hot tea. \"Madam, the autumn weather is dry, making it easy to get agitated. Have some tea to soothe yourself.\"","The fire in Daili's heart, fueled by his cup of tea, burned all the way from her stomach to the top of her head.","What was this? Getting the upper hand and then acting innocent?","She could endure many things, including but not limited to the series of humiliating treaties she was forced to sign after he caught her in Nanyang County. She could even patiently receive guests alongside Qin Hongying, people she shouldn't have been responsible for hosting.","But there was one thing she absolutely could not endure.","He was using Zhouzhou's life-saving medicine as a bargaining chip!","Today it was Zhouzhou's medicine; tomorrow, would he use Zhouzhou's life as a threat?","Daili picked up the teacup on the table and violently threw its contents right at Qin Shaozong.","Caught off guard, the veins in the man's arms bulged in a defensive reflex, but he forcefully restrained his movements, closed his eyes, and took the cup of hot water to the face.","The hot tea soaked his temples and his broken eyebrow, trickling down his cheeks to his neck, dampening his collar.","Daili smashed the empty cup against Qin Shaozong's chest. \"Qin Changgeng, if you ever use Zhouzhou's matters to threaten me again, I will drag you down to hell with me!\"","Having said her piece, Daili stormed out of the main room without looking back.","Qin Shaozong wiped his face and looked at her retreating figure. He clicked his tongue softly. \"That precious son of hers really can't be spoken of at all.\"","Qin Manor, the study.","\"Second Brother, you were looking for me?\" Qin Hongying pushed open the door and entered the study.","Qin Shaozong was the only one in the study. Seeing his sister enter, he lifted his chin slightly, gesturing to the seat opposite him. \"Sit.\"","Qin Hongying thought of the guests they had just received and assumed Qin Shaozong had called her to ask about the situation. Without waiting for him to ask, she said directly, \"Rest assured, I didn't let her suffer any losses. It was an easy fight, the advantage was ours. Wei Wu's little tricks are nothing to worry about.\"","After saying this, her curiosity took over, and she leaned forward. \"Second Brother, where exactly did you bring Daili back from? She looks far too young to have such an old son, and her son's surname is also Qin. Is he really related to you...\"","That young man named Qin Yanzhou was clearly older than Qinian, and looked to be about the same age as Yunce.","Her second brother had married at the age of seventeen. Before getting married, he had left the North to travel through the southern provinces. Could it be that he had met a confidante on the road back then?","But it was also strange. If she was a former lover, why was Daili so cold towards him?","Furthermore, Qin Yanzhou's appearance bore absolutely no resemblance to her second brother. Even his lower face, which didn't resemble his mother's, showed not the slightest trace of her second brother's features.","It just didn't look like it.","\"She is the descendant of a hermit,\" was all Qin Shaozong said in response.","As to how she came to be here, and the matter of Qin Yanzhou, he offered no answers whatsoever.","Qin Hongying was instantly displeased. She had put in so much effort outside to shelter his sweetheart from the wind and rain, yet he refused to reveal even a tiny bit of information. \"Second Brother, you're being unkind.\"","Qin Shaozong picked up a tiger-shaped brush rest. \"Is Rongrong engaged yet?\"","The Great Yan Dynasty had a law: if a woman was fifteen or older and remained unmarried, she was subjected to a five-fold calculation. This meant paying five times the standard poll tax. While this five-fold amount would be a significant expense for a commoner's household, it was less than a drop in the bucket for noble and wealthy families.","Noble daughters usually married later, but no matter how late, their engagements would be arranged in advance.","The sixteen-year-old Shi Rongyue was not yet married, but normally speaking, she should already be engaged.","\"She is. She's engaged to the legitimate heir of the Zheng family in Nanyu. Her father and I didn't want her to marry so far away.\" Qin Hongying nodded. Just as she finished speaking, she suddenly asked in surprise, \"Second Brother, what do you mean by asking this?\"","There weren't as many prominent families in Nanyu Commandery as in Yuyang, and the two commanderies weren't too far apart. Qin Shaozong thought for a moment and remembered. \"The Zheng family of Nanyu... that's the family of Commandery Governor Zheng, correct?\"","Qin Hongying neither nodded nor shook her head, but instead nervously asked for the second time, \"Second Brother, what do you mean by asking if Rongrong is engaged? Give me a straight answer quickly.\"","If Rongrong could marry back into the Qin family, marrying her cousin, that would be the best possible outcome. She would definitely live a very comfortable life in the future. Moreover, her second brother's power was far beyond what a mere governor could compare to.","Previously, she hadn't been completely opposed to the idea of marrying her daughter back into the Qin family. Yunce was three years older than Rongrong, making them a perfect match in age.","But with the precedent of their eldest brother dying in battle, her second brother had many reservations about Yunce's marriage. He wasn't as overbearing as normal parents; he would listen to Yunce's own wishes.","And Yunce only saw Rongrong as a younger sister, with no romantic feelings whatsoever.","As for Qinian, he was the same age as Rongrong, which was also suitable.","Unfortunately, the Qin and Wei families had arranged a marriage for them when they were babies. Although this arranged marriage came to nothing due to the early death of that particular Wei daughter, the Wei family later played dumb, attempting to blur the lines of the engagement from a specific young lady to any daughter of the Wei family.","Her second brother didn't seem to be in a hurry regarding Qinian's marriage. He was in a subtle stalemate with the Wei family and had made no moves.","Since neither of her two biological nephews was a viable option, Qin Hongying didn't plan to look at the collateral branches either.","There was no need. Not to mention that there were no outstanding young talents in the collateral branches that caught her eye, the relationships there were much more complicated. Marrying her daughter into such a situation would do more harm than good.","But now, why did it sound like her second brother had changed his mind?","\"When is the wedding set for?\" Qin Shaozong asked.","Qin Hongying answered truthfully, \"Next summer.\"","Qin Shaozong twisted the jade thumb ring on his finger. \"Break off the engagement with the Zheng family. I will send someone to cancel it on our behalf, so they won't be able to blame the Shi family.\"","Qin Hongying's pupils shrank sharply, a stormy wave of emotion surging in her eyes. \"Second Brother, are you planning to have Rongrong marry into the Qin family? Do you want her to marry Qi Nian? Are you going to deal with the Wei family at the same time this time?\"","She was so agitated that she fired off three questions in a row.","Qin Shaozong only answered the first one. \"She will marry into the Qin family.\"","Qin Hongying's heart finally settled. Her second brother never made promises lightly, but he always kept his word.","With his assurance, Rongrong's marriage was practically set in stone.","As for the Zheng family, the young master of the Zheng family was indeed quite good, but how could he compare to the reliability of her own nephew?","Fortunately, she and her husband had planned to wait until they returned to Nanyu before arranging a meeting between Rongrong and the Zheng family's young master. Since the two juniors had not yet met, handling certain matters was entirely just a discussion between the elders.","\"Second Brother, why did you suddenly change your mind? When I asked you last time, you said there was no rush,\" Qin Hongying asked curiously.","Qin Shaozong still did not answer this question directly. He merely said, \"After breaking the engagement with the Zheng family, do not rush to arrange another one immediately, otherwise it will be bad for Rongrong's reputation. She might not necessarily marry Qi Nian. Let the younger generation spend some time together first.\"","Qin Hongying's heart skipped a beat, and doubts began to bubble up one after another.","If not Qi Nian, did that mean Yun Ce? Had Yun Ce changed his mind?","But she had only been staying here with her daughter for a few days. Yun Ce was always reserved; there was no reason for him to fast-forward to developing romantic feelings for Rongrong and expressing a desire to take a wife to her second brother.","Moreover, her second brother's words were so ambiguous. If she didn't know his character, she would have thought he was playing a trick on her.","Qin Hongying was full of questions, but no matter how she pressed, she could not get a clear answer out of him.","*","Several days passed in the blink of an eye.","The ancient city of Yuyang Commandery was bustling with endless streams of carriages and horses. Every day, after the dawn broke in the east, it was as if an invisible scroll of a prosperous cityscape slowly unrolled, depicting a vibrancy identical to the day before.","Inside a corner private room on the second floor of a certain eatery in the city.","\"They have stopped searching for fleeceflower root. This is not good.\" Diting sat at the table, holding a white Go piece, his eyes lowered toward the chessboard.","Bai Xiang, holding a black piece, was also studying the board. \"It is said that Madam Qin has a habit of collecting herbs. Her coming to Yuyang this time is definitely at the invitation of the Marquis of Wu'an. The fleeceflower root they lack has likely been supplied by her. However, as long as they do not have enough musk, Madam Dai will eventually come to our side.\"","Slender fingers placed a white piece onto the board, producing a soft clink of jade.","\"The Marquis of Wu'an is incredibly cunning. Just like the battle of Bairi City back then, who could have imagined that he would neither forcefully attack Bairi Pass nor build a pontoon bridge to cross the river, but instead lead his troops on a grueling multi-day march through desolate mountain paths to flank Bairi City from behind?\" Diting shook his head and said, \"Whether they have obtained enough musk is hard to say.\"","\"The Red Gallbladder poison in Mingdeng's body has at most eight days left. If it is not removed within eight days, he will surely die.\" Bai Xiang sighed with deep emotion. \"For things to develop to this point is something I never anticipated. Having known him for nearly ten years, I truly treated him as my own brother.\"","A complex emotion flickered across Diting's face as well, but it ultimately settled into calmness. \"Those walking different paths cannot make plans together.\"","Bai Xiang chuckled dryly. \"It is still too early to draw conclusions about our paths. Mingdeng only chose his mother, not the Marquis of Wu'an. If Madam Dai is willing to come, he will definitely return to the Green Lotus Sect.\"","Diting, however, shook his head again. \"If you had met Madam Dai, you would know that the Marquis of Wu'an will never let her leave under any circumstances.\"","Just as Bai Xiang opened his mouth to speak, the sound of hurried footsteps came from outside.","Soon, a servant dressed as a young attendant entered the room.","\"Sir, he has left the estate again. This time, apart from the Third Young Master of the Qin family, there is also a young lady accompanying them,\" the servant reported.","No specific name was mentioned, only a \"he,\" yet the two men in the room understood perfectly.","\"Alright, you may step down.\"","After the servant left, Bai Xiang tapped the table lightly with his finger. \"How many times is this?\"","Diting looked thoughtful. \"At least the third time we have received such news. Mingdeng is not an active person. For him to frequently leave the estate to roam the markets is highly suspicious.\"","Bai Xiang argued, \"But it's hard to say for sure. The Third Young Master of the Qin family is naturally lively and playful. He has been cooped up in the estate for nearly two months; it is quite normal for him to want to go out.\"","\"Mingdeng is exceptionally familiar with our sect. With his repeated excursions, I worry he is looking for us.\" Diting lowered his eyes and placed a piece on the board. \"Since we previously sent a letter to Madam Dai, he must know that there are traces of our sect in Yuyang Commandery.\"","\"Then what do you intend to do?\" Bai Xiang placed a piece casually.","\"Uncle once said that in all matters, one must assume the worst-case scenario in order to remain invincible. Let us assume they have found enough musk and fleeceflower root, and let us also assume Mingdeng has found some traces of us...\" Diting picked up a white piece, the jade glowing with a warm luster between his fingers.","Bai Xiang asked, \"Then what should we do?\"","\"The Red Gallbladder will accelerate into its berserk phase if severely stimulated. Let us toss a stone to clear the path. He is with the Third Young Master of the Qin family, which is just perfect. Let them warm up together. Little Miss Fan has been clamoring quite loudly lately; let us send her this time,\" Diting smiled.","Bai Xiang understood and his expression instantly changed drastically. \"Must we really do this? If it's not controlled well, Mingdeng will surely die...\"","\"Bai Xiang, emotions do not build empires, and those with different aspirations cannot be friends.\" Diting raised his eyes calmly.","Bai Xiang choked for a moment before adding, \"I... I am just worried that if he dies, Madam Dai will suffer the pain of losing her son and will completely attach herself to the Marquis of Wu'an. By then, there will be no possibility of her submitting to our sect...\"","The Go match was not yet finished, but the victor was already apparent.","\"With Mingdeng's alertness, this will not take his life. By the way, I received a message from Uncle. The war in the south has concluded. Liu of Jingzhou was one step ahead, making Yi Province take the surname 'Liu' from now on. I must set off for Jingzhou today. You will take full charge of Yuyang. Handle everything according to what I said before, and do not let Uncle and me down.\" Diting clearly had no intention of continuing the game.","He rose from his seat, looking down at Bai Xiang from above. \"From the moment he defected, Mingdeng was no longer our brother. The benevolence of women will only ruin great plans. Please remember this, little brother.\""]},{"number":111,"title":"Chapter 111","paragraphs":["The main street was bustling with people. Qin Qinian walked in the middle, with Qin Yanzhou on his left and Shi Rongyue on his right.","The young man found everything interesting and novel. It was clearly the most ordinary scene, but touring the market with Qin Yanzhou and his little cousin, who rarely visited Yuyang, felt different.","\"Rongrong, just tell me whatever catches your eye. It is rare for you to visit Yuyang, so I must do my duty as a host,\" Qin Qinian remained as generous as ever.","Shi Rongyue glanced at him.","She and Qin Qinian were of the same age. Although their homes were not in the same commandery, it was definitely not accurate to say they were strangers.","When the Qin family faced a crisis back then, Qin Hongying, who had already married into the Shi family, returned to Yuyang with her daughter, who still needed constant care. During her short stay in Yuyang, Shi Rongyue was raised alongside Qin Qinian.","After that storm subsided, in the following years, Qin Hongying would bring her daughter back for a short stay every year. This was both to maintain affection with her second brother and to suppress certain restless members of the collateral branches, letting them know that the main branch was not devoid of people.","The Shi family had no objections to this and was even extremely willing.","After all, it was visibly apparent that the Qin clan was on the rise, and having a deep relationship with the Qin family's heir brought a hundred benefits and no harm.","Thus, Shi Rongyue followed her mother back to Yuyang every year, and these cousins met annually. When they were young, Qin Qinian even took Shi Rongyue climbing trees.","\"I have silver. Little cousin, you better keep a tight grip on your own coin pouch. Lest next time you go out playing with those cousins of yours from the Wei family, you get coaxed into blowing all your money on drinks with just a few words, and then have to go borrow from Eldest Cousin again.\"","Shi Rongyue's voice was soft and sweet, but her words almost made Qin Qinian jump.","\"That was an accident! Mainly because the shopkeeper said that after buying the wine, one could admire the elegance of what was supposedly the personal sword of the former dynasty's famous general, Guan Xin. I was moved. But who knew that so-called treasured sword was just a gimmick, completely fake, just used to pose as a lover of culture.\"","After explaining to Shi Rongyue, Qin Qinian looked at Qin Yanzhou for validation. \"Qin Yanzhou, you also like weapons, you can definitely understand how I felt at that time.\"","\"I cannot,\" the young man coldly tossed out two words.","Qin Qinian was shocked. \"That makes no sense. Last time I said I had a good saber and asked if you wanted to see it, you even said yes.\"","\"Places like eateries and taverns focus on food and drink. Even if they obtained a top-tier weapon, they wouldn't be able to keep it hidden. How could they be compared to private collectors?\" Qin Yanzhou said.","Shi Rongyue nodded repeatedly. \"Second Uncle is the only Marquis in the Northern lands, and he has always loved collecting treasures. How could a petty merchant have a treasure that even he doesn't possess? Little cousin, you must not let Second Uncle know about this, or you will have to copy books until you break two wolf-hair brushes again.\"","Qin Qinian: \"...\"","Thanks for the reminder, but it was too late; the books had already been copied.","An invisible dark cloud floated over, shrouding Qin Qinian's head, and it began to pour rain.","Seeing him feeling down, Shi Rongyue happened to spot a familiar noodle stall. The stall owner was still the familiar old man. She was both pleasantly surprised and comforting as she said, \"That noodle stall is actually still here! Old Man He's craftsmanship is better than the others. How about we go there to eat noodles? Little cousin...\"","At this point, Shi Rongyue quickened her pace slightly, bypassed Qin Qinian in the middle, and looked at the white-robed young man on the other side. \"Young Master Qin, how about I treat you both to noodle soup?\"","\"No need.\"","In the end, they still went to that noodle stall.","The stall was not large, consisting merely of a handcart and a few unfolded wooden tables. Compared to those multi-storied, spacious eateries, its scale was completely inadequate.","But the stall's wooden tables and chairs were wiped very clean. A few chairs had a smooth, lustrous sheen on their surfaces from frequent wiping.","It was early in the afternoon, not a typical mealtime, but half the tables and chairs at the stall had welcomed diners.","\"Young Lady,\" the maidservant following Shi Rongyue called out softly, clearly disagreeing with her eating at such a roadside stall.","\"What are you worrying about? When I came to Yuyang in the past, I also ate here. Besides, very few noble ladies in Yuyang recognize me, so even if I lose face, it won't fall on Third Miss Shi.\" Shi Rongyue muttered.","The commoners at the bottom were not as particular as the nobles. Nobles ate their meals separately, but down here, everyone sat at the same table.","The three of them shared a table. After ordering, Shi Rongyue only had to look up to see the faces of the two people opposite her. Her little cousin was talking to Young Master Qin. The latter tilted his head slightly, listening, occasionally replying with a word or two. The lines from his forehead to his jaw were extremely clear and smooth, like a master's most attentive brushstroke.","Looking closer, she was startled to realize that his eyelashes were very long, dark, and thick, looking exactly like Lady Dai's.","Shi Rongyue couldn't help but take a few more glances, silently reciting to herself many times that she was already engaged and couldn't let her imagination run wild, before finally gathering her thoughts.","The noodle soup was quickly brought over.","Folk noodle soup was still in the form of flatbread, with large pieces of bread soaked in bone broth. Although the noodle stall was small, this bone broth was brewed with considerable care, and they were generous with the seasonings. It was indeed much richer and more fragrant than other places.","Among the three, Qin Qinian had his back to the main street the most, while Qin Yanzhou and Shi Rongyue had less.","When they were less than halfway through their noodle soup, an unintentional upward glance caused Qin Yanzhou to completely freeze.","Shi Rongyue noticed his odd behavior and followed his gaze. Not far away stood a delicate young girl wearing a water-blue dress and a twisted gold wire jade hairpin shaped like a butterfly with a pearl in its mouth.","The young lady had fair skin, dressed opulently, and had a petite stature, not looking like a northerner.","Shi Rongyue's eyes met the other party's. At that moment, she inexplicably shuddered, as if being stared at by a snake flicking its scarlet tongue.","Shi Rongyue was certain that she saw hatred in the young girl's eyes.","But hatred towards her?","Why hate her? They were not related and had never met before.","Qin Yanzhou narrowed his eyes.","Although there was some distance and people were coming and going on the street, he was certain he hadn't recognized the wrong person. Whether it was her facial features or her dressing habits, that was Eighth Miss Fan.","Fan of Yanzhou was defeated in battle, and the male members of the Fan family were all eradicated by the Marquis of Wu'an. Logically speaking, this Eighth Miss Fan should have followed her mother, Lady Ji, back to the Ji family, rather than appearing thousands of miles away in Yuyang of Youzhou.","The Ji family would not bring her here, and it was absolutely impossible for a young girl like her to come to Youzhou alone. Someone must have helped her.","The Green Lotus Cult!","The white-robed young man suddenly put down his bowl and chopsticks, pulled out a handful of silver coins from his sleeve pocket, placed them on the table, and quickly stood up.","\"Hey, Qin Yanzhou, where are you going?\" Qin Qinian was quite startled.","Qin Yanzhou merely said, \"I spotted a target.\"","Having wandered around the city with him for the past few days, Qin Qinian immediately understood. He instantly dropped his chopsticks as well. \"Where? For you to say that, this person must be quite significant. Let's go catch them together!\"","While catching up to Qin Yanzhou in two steps, Qin Qinian remembered his little cousin was still there and was about to tell her to go back first.","But when he turned his head, he found that Shi Rongyue had arrived beside him at some unknown point, her round little face full of excitement. \"Hurry up and catch them!\"","Qin Qinian: \"...\"","How could he have forgotten that his little cousin had never been a quiet one since childhood? When he climbed trees to pick fruit as a child, she was the one standing below hitting the fruit with a bamboo pole.","Qin Yanzhou frowned, but seeing that Fan Muqi had disappeared in the distance, clearly having turned into an alley, he no longer had the time to persuade the other two to stay put and hurried to give chase.","As Qin Qinian walked, he turned to a servant and said, Go back and find Hu Bao. Have him bring men.","Neither he nor Qin Yanzhou were high-profile by nature, and since their investigation needed to be conducted in secret, they usually did not bring guards when they went out. Today, leaving the estate with Shi Rongyue, they had brought one servant out of consideration for the young lady, but only that one.","Counting the maid accompanying Shi Rongyue, the group only had two servants in total.","The servant hurriedly asked, Third Young Master, where should I look for you then?","Qin Qinian hesitated. In just that brief moment, he saw that Qin Yanzhou and Shi Rongyue had already pulled a short distance away from him. He immediately waved his hand. Search north from here, and tell Hu Bao to act according to the situation.","Sensing something amiss, the servant tried to advise against it.","Qin Qinian left him behind, saying, Rest assured, every patrol guard in Yuyang recognizes my face. Besides, with Qin Yanzhou's and my martial arts skills, if we really run into trouble, the two of us will join forces. Who could possibly stand against us?","Leaving those words behind, Qin Qinian ran off.","Despite Shi Rongyue being a young lady with a slightly chubby face, she had probably been running around with Qin Qinian since childhood, so her stamina was not lacking in the slightest.","At the very least, as they ran, her maid slowly fell behind, while she was still able to keep up with Qin Qinian.","The group ran past three streets and cut through two alleys.","After mistakenly catching three young women who wore the exact same clothes as Fan Muqi and had a similar build, Qin Yanzhou finally confirmed that the woman stepping off the donkey cart ahead was indeed Fan Muqi.","Fan Muqi was currently standing in front of a small house. She was not in a hurry to enter, nor did she show any panic about being caught.","As she watched the white-robed young man sprinting toward her, a myriad of emotions flickered across her face for a fleeting moment, but they were ultimately replaced by pure hatred.","She hesitated no longer and turned to enter the small house.","A moment later, Qin Yanzhou arrived at the house.","The stall where they had been eating noodle soup earlier was on the edge of the bustling market. Now, after running for a while, they had arrived in a different area, on the outskirts of a residential district where the lower-class commoners gathered.","The small house in front of Qin Yanzhou did not take up much space; it looked like nothing more than a two-courtyard compound.","The wooden door, riddled with a few wormholes, was half open. Through it, the situation inside the small courtyard could be seen. The courtyard was dead silent; let alone a person, there was not even a single bird.","Qin Yanzhou reached out and pushed the door open.","The wooden hinges turned, emitting a harsh, creaking sound as if bearing a heavy burden. As the half-door swung open, more of the courtyard's scenery was revealed.","Including Fan Muqi, who stood in the small hall ahead.","Qin Yanzhou strode inside, his gaze quickly sweeping the surroundings. Seeing that there was no one else in the courtyard or the front hall besides Fan Muqi, he asked, Who from the Green Lotus Cult has come to Yuyang, and where are they now?","His voice was like a frozen lake in winter, calm and without a single ripple.","Quanjie! Fan Muqi gritted her teeth so hard out of hatred that they made a grinding sound. Do you have nothing else to say to me?","Qin Yanzhou stepped forward, step by step, and continued to ask, Where are the others from the Green Lotus Cult?","As he advanced, Fan Muqi retreated inward, her eyes bloodshot. Seven years! My Fan family raised you for seven years! Yet you, not only did you show no gratitude, but you conspired with outsiders to murder my Fan family, causing my father's defeat in battle and the slaughter of all the brothers in my clan! Quanjie, committing such ungrateful and treacherous acts, when you wake up in the dead of night, do you not hear the wailing of wronged souls in your ears, making it impossible for you to sleep or eat in peace?","Qin Qinian and Shi Rongyue, who arrived right behind him, heard this exact speech the moment they entered the small house.","Both of them were taken aback.","Fan Muqi's eyes widened so much they seemed about to tear. My Fan family nurtured you for seven years, sent people to teach you martial arts, and devotedly cultivated you. Could all of that still not compare to the petty favors the Marquis of Wu'an bestowed upon you? What made you so desperate to be driven by him, to act as a pawn in his hand, that even after having your legs broken and being thrown at the gates of my Fan estate, you still chose to serve him like a loyal dog?","Qin Yanzhou's brow twitched slightly. I was never a hidden agent for the Marquis of Wu'an. When I entered the Fan estate as a mole back then, it was under the orders of the Six Paths of the Green Lotus Cult."]},{"number":112,"title":"Chapter 112","paragraphs":["\"Complete nonsense!\"","Fan Muqi was like a cat whose tail had been stepped on, her hair standing on end. \"If you are not the Marquis of Wu'an's spy, why did you follow him back to the North, and even move into his mansion after arriving in Yuyang?! You are clearly lying. You know that I am now working for Diting and the others, and you are trying to divide us.\"","Although they didn't know the full context, from Fan Muqi's words, Qin Qinian and Shi Rongyue managed to piece together the gist of it.","Defeat in battle? That most likely involved his father's (her second uncle's) military campaigns in the South.","\"You are being quite unreasonable. Qin Yanzhou's mother is in the mansion, keeping my father company; of course, he would be here too,\" Qin Qinian said with a frown.","Shi Rongyue added, \"The winner takes all. Your father was no match for my second uncle; a defeat is a defeat. If the Northern Army had lost, it's highly unlikely your father would have spared the Qin family.\"","Fan Muqi's mind buzzed violently, completely consumed by Qin Qinian's phrase \"Qin Yanzhou's mother.\"","Did Quanjie have a mother?","He shouldn't have one.","\"You are lying to me. If his mother is still alive, why hasn't she come to see him even once in seven whole years...\"","Fan Muqi muttered. After finishing her initial sentence, she seemed to draw strength from it, her gaze turning fierce. \"If he had a mother, and if she could stay by the Marquis of Wu'an's side as you claim, there is absolutely no way Quanjie would be sent away for seven years!\"","\"Qin Yanzhou was unfortunately abducted when he was young, and was only later found by his mother,\" Qin Qinian explained.","This was something he had learned after seeing Qin Yanzhou covered in scars and pestering him for the truth. After being asked for the eighteenth time, the other party finally told him that he had been abducted as a child and separated from his mother.","Hearing Qin Yanzhou's words at the time, he belatedly recalled that a missing person notice had been issued in the North a while ago. Later, when he went back to check, the notice was indeed looking for \"Qin Yanzhou,\" except the \"Qin Yanzhou\" on it was a nine-year-old child.","Qin Qinian didn't ask why the details didn't match, because he had already come up with a reason himself: it must have been to avoid drawing attention!","Of course, that wasn't important. What mattered was correcting this young lady who was slandering Qin Yanzhou.","Qin Qinian: \"A few months ago, the North entrusted a group of traveling merchants to distribute a missing person notice across the world, and he was the one they were looking for. Your surname is Fan, and there was a military defeat; your father is Fan of Yanzhou, right? That missing person notice must have reached Yanzhou as well. If you were in Yanzhou and paid any attention, you would definitely know about this.\"","Fan Muqi froze for a moment.","A missing person notice?","In the past, when she was still at home, she would occasionally go out to play with the young lady of the Li family. She seemed to recall hearing about a missing person notice in the commandery.","Seeing her expression, Shi Rongyue knew that Fan Muqi had probably heard of it.","The other party's father had been defeated in battle, so her family couldn't possibly have brought her to Yuyang. Moreover, Young Master Qin had previously mentioned the \"Green Lotus Sect.\" Could this girl be a member of the Green Lotus Sect?","Her second uncle was dedicated to suppressing the sect. If they could incite this young lady to defect, it would be a wonderful thing.","Thus, Shi Rongyue said, \"If you don't believe us, you can return to the Qin mansion with us and meet Lady Dai. She looks very much like Young Master Qin. Once you see her, you will know we are not lying. At that time, we hope you will cooperate and tell us everything you know about the Green Lotus Sect truthfully.\"","\"Yes, you can return to the mansion with us. However, you must watch your words in front of Lady Dai and not be stubborn anymore. Otherwise, if my father hears you speaking nonsense, he will twist your head off,\" Qin Qinian said seriously.","Fan Muqi shuddered all over, as if struck by an invisible, massive force, and stumbled backward a step.","She slowly lowered her eyes, avoiding looking at the three of them.","\"You just mentioned Diting. Has Diting also come to Yuyang? Where is he now?\" Qin Yanzhou took a step forward.","His step was like a sudden crash of thunder, startling the birds on the branches and snapping Fan Muqi out of her daze.","Fan Muqi stumbled back two steps, her expression changing repeatedly. There was shock and doubt, disbelief, as well as conflict and pain.","She suddenly looked up at Qin Yanzhou. Her gaze was complex, like a painting smeared with various colors.","Fan Muqi took a deep look at Qin Yanzhou. \"Didn't you want to know about Diting? He was originally in the bookstore, but it seems he left later. Come with me. There is a secret passage in this room; walking through it will take you to another place. There is another leader of the Green Lotus Sect there, who I observe is on equal footing with Diting.\"","Qin Qinian was suspicious. \"Are you really that kind-hearted?\"","From the beginning, she had been luring Qin Yanzhou to this place, and now she was asking them to take a secret passage. Could it be a trap?","Fan Muqi sneered. \"Originally, I wasn't. That secret passage is filled with hidden traps. Initially, Diting asked me to lure you here with the intention of killing you with those traps, but I have changed my mind now. Quanjie, since you keep saying you used to work for the Green Lotus Sect, then come with me to find him. I want to ask him clearly face to face.\"","With that, Fan Muqi turned and walked away.","Qin Yanzhou followed for two steps. Hearing footsteps behind him, he turned to look at Qin Qinian and Shi Rongyue. \"You two wait here.\"","\"No way!\"","Qin Qinian flatly refused. \"Although you're a good fighter, what if ten or eight people suddenly swarm in? Two fists are no match for four hands. If you're attacked from the front and back, there will always be blind spots. It's different if I go with you. We can stand back-to-back, invincible against the world.\"","\"It's still unknown whether there are truly no other people here. We cannot leave Miss Shi alone,\" Qin Yanzhou disagreed.","Qin Qinian paused.","That was true.","If he and Qin Yanzhou left, and some local ruffian popped up to do something untoward to Rongrong, he would have to apologize with his life.","\"Quanjie, are you coming or not? If not, then forget it,\" Fan Muqi said coldly from inside.","After saying this, she turned into the inner area, and her figure could no longer be seen.","Shi Rongyue glanced over there, then looked at Qin Yanzhou, her large light brown eyes reflecting the figure in front of her. \"How about we go together? We shouldn't miss this opportunity. If we let her slip away through the secret passage, we might not be able to find her again. It's better if I follow along too. Anyway, my little cousin has already informed the city patrols we just ran into, asking them to point the way for Captain Hu.\"","Qin Qinian perked up. \"Right, right. We've already told the city guards we saw along the way to run back. Hu Bao is receiving them one by one, so he'll definitely guess we're here. In a quarter of an hour at most, Hu Bao and his men will arrive.\"","Even if they were truly ambushed, they only needed to hold out for a quarter of an hour to wait for reinforcements.","Once reinforcements arrived, they could turn the tables and capture them all in one fell swoop. With severe interrogation, were they afraid they wouldn't uncover all of the Green Lotus Sect's forces in Yuyang?","Qin Yanzhou had arrived earlier than the two of them and didn't know what happened afterward. Hearing them say this now, he hesitated for a moment before finally nodding.","The group of three walked inside.","This was just a two-courtyard compound with limited space, and connected right next to it was the room.","The door to the room was wide open. In the spot where a bed had originally been placed, the bed was now moved aside, revealing a dark, eerie passage leading straight down.","The passage was more than eight feet wide, allowing two adult men to walk side by side. And Fan Muqi was currently standing at the entrance of the passage.","Seeing them come over together, with Shi Rongyue among them, Fan Muqi twitched the corners of her mouth, seemingly wanting to reveal a mocking smile, but ultimately failing. \"You really can't bear to leave her behind for even a moment.\"","Shi Rongyue sensed the other party's hostility. Initially puzzled, she then saw Fan Muqi looking at Qin Yanzhou and suddenly understood something.","However, Fan Muqi didn't seem to expect an answer. After dropping that sentence, she turned and entered the secret passage.","Qin Yanzhou followed, Shi Rongyue was in the middle, and Qin Qinian brought up the rear.","The passage initially slanted downwards. After descending several stone steps about the height of two people, the path leveled out, no longer as steep as before.","Qin Qinian kept an eye on his surroundings as they walked. Even when they first came down, he was quite surprised.","These were stone steps, not an ordinary dirt slope.","Building stone steps required transporting stones and carefully fitting them together. The manpower and resources spent were completely incomparable to simply piling up a dirt slope.","This secret passage was built with great care and looked very solid. Judging from the heavily worn stone steps, it had existed for at least a dozen years, if not longer.","It was highly likely that it had existed even before his father took over the entirety of Yuyang.","The further they went in, the wider the surroundings became, shaped like a funnel. There were no candlesticks or lamps set up along the four sides of the passage, but many small bronze mirror shards were cleverly installed everywhere.","Light was brought in from an unknown source, and after multiple refractions, it became an invisible lamp lingering in the passage. The surroundings were still dim, but not so dark that one couldn't see their own fingers.","There was no need to hold a torch to move forward.","Qin Qinian's expression was solemn. \"Miss Fan, do you know who built this passage, and when the construction started and finished?\"","Fan Muqi, who was in front, did not answer.","Shi Rongyue whispered, \"Little cousin, now is not the time to talk about this. Keep a close eye on her. She said earlier that she planned to assassinate Young Master Qin with a hidden mechanism. She changed her tune later, but who knows if...\"","Shi Rongyue walked in the middle, separated from Fan Muqi only by Qin Yanzhou. Coupled with the silence of the passage, although she lowered her voice, Fan Muqi still heard fragments of her words.","Fan Muqi turned her head in anger. The twisted gold wire and pearl-bearing butterfly jade hairpin on her head flapped its golden wings up and down with her dramatic turn. \"Do you see that small protruding stone five steps ahead? That is a mechanism!\"","Shi Rongyue immediately fell silent.","Qin Qinian looked nervously at the small protrusion. \"You, you come closer. Don't go near there.\"","Fan Muqi sneered. \"Rest assured. Since I said I would take you to find him and ask him clearly, I won't make a move against you right now.\"","From beginning to end, she only looked at Qin Yanzhou, and the word she used was 'you' in the singular, not referring to all of them, only to him.","Shi Rongyue pursed her lips.","After walking another distance, the area ahead became even more open. Entering this place, rows of multi-tiered shelves leaning against the wall unexpectedly appeared.","It was unknown how long those wooden shelves had been placed there, as they seemed covered in a thick layer of dust.","In addition, there were many open-mouthed, short-bellied small jars placed on the ground, containing some things inside. In the very center, there was a set of a table and chairs, and on the table unexpectedly sat a faintly glowing coiled-dragon lamp.","A candle was lit inside the lamp. Driven by the heat, the central axis rotated continuously, and the patterns on the lamp's surface rotated one by one.","Several scenes appeared successively: an adult man with an unseen face was leading three children. One of them was slightly shorter, and the other two were slightly taller, looking a bit older.","Turning to another picture: the man disappeared, leaving only the three children playing together. It was still the two taller ones and one shorter one. The taller ones wore white clothes, and the shorter one wore black clothes. Each of the three rode a small foal.","Turning to yet another picture: the child in black had grown up into a young man. Holding a sword in his hand, he was killing a person. Not far away, a young man in white was watching him.","The several pictures rotated continuously. In this dim room, this coiled-dragon lamp produced an indescribable eeriness, easily making people focus all their attention on it and ignore everything else.","For example, a string tied to the coiled-dragon lamp. And the things inside the small jars illuminated by the light, as well as the 'dust' scattered on the shelves.","The 'dust' was white, and the things in the open-mouthed small jars were also white.","And if one looked a little further inside, they could see two passages leading in different directions. That side was slightly darker, making it impossible to see what was inside.","Qin Yanzhou's pupils suddenly constricted.","\"The drawings on this lamp are so detailed; it wouldn't be an exaggeration to say they are lifelike. By the way, why put a lamp here? Could it be for illumination?\" Qin Qinian was puzzled.","\"It shouldn't be...\"","Before Shi Rongyue could finish her sentence, her wrist was suddenly grabbed, and she couldn't help but freeze.","The white-robed young man who was originally walking in front of her grabbed her with one hand and Qin Qinian with the other. Pulling one with each hand, he frantically ran back.","\"Hey, what are you doing, Qin Yanzhou! Why are we running? Weren't we going to find that Diting thing?\" Qin Qinian was confused. However, he didn't break free from Qin Yanzhou's hand and ran along with him.","Suddenly, a gust of wind blew from one of the unknown passages over there.","Shi Rongyue was stunned.","How could there suddenly be wind underground?","And after this gust of wind, Qin Qinian and Shi Rongyue both felt the young man pulling them suddenly yank them forward.","Originally behind Qin Yanzhou, after being yanked by him backhandedly, they both ended up in front of him.","\"Qin Yan...\"","\"Boom!!\"","A massive flash of fire and a deafening roar came from behind, and a terrifying blast of air rushed toward them from the rear.","Qin Yanzhou was blown by the blast wave, crashing into Shi Rongyue and Qin Qinian.","The initial explosion triggered a chain reaction. The stone passage shook, and the small bronze mirrors originally inlaid everywhere crashed to the ground, shattering into pieces.","Even the stone blocks overhead were impacted, smashing down with heavy thuds one after another.","The surroundings were pitch black. Shi Rongyue only felt that she was caged in a very small space, with a warm touch right next to her and a hurried breath hanging above her.","Suddenly, something warm fell onto her face.","The smell of blood rushed into Shi Rongyue's nose, and she snapped back to her senses in an instant. \"Young, Young Master Qin?\"","She tremblingly raised her hand. Unable to see in the dark, she only felt that she had touched a patch of warm, soft skin. The next moment, the figure that had been propped up over her and the person beside her collapsed.","Shi Rongyue's heart suddenly spasmed.","\"Qin Yanzhou!\" Qin Qinian was also startled, wanting to push him but not daring to act rashly.","Shi Rongyue didn't dare to move. She and Qin Qinian beside her each formed half of a human cushion to catch Qin Yanzhou.","After calling out \"Qin Yanzhou\" several times with no response, Qin Qinian began to panic. \"Qin Yanzhou, answer me, don't scare me! Saving my life is such a huge favor, you have to at least give me a chance to repay you...\"","\"Little cousin, he passed out. It's not what you think,\" Shi Rongyue said, moving her hand away from the pulse on the side of the young man's neck.","Qin Qinian's emotions fluctuated wildly, and a thin layer of cold sweat broke out on his forehead. He asked Shi Rongyue again, \"Rongrong, are you okay? Are you hurt anywhere?\"","\"No, Young Master Qin shielded me. I wasn't hit by the falling rocks,\" Shi Rongyue said softly.","Qin Qinian reached out, trying to feel his surroundings. \"It's blocked off here, and there's no room to maneuver. Let's just wait for rescue. Hu Bao and the others should be arriving soon.\""]},{"number":113,"title":"Chapter 113","paragraphs":["Hu Bao had just arrived at the door of the small house with his men. Before he could even enter, he suddenly heard a loud bang.","In that instant, the entire earth seemed to tremble. Everyone's first reaction was:","\"What's going on? Is it an earth dragon turning over (an earthquake)?\"","The accompanying guards were shocked.","But soon, Hu Bao denied this guess. Because a house not far away suddenly burst into flames, accompanied by a large amount of smoke billowing out.","How could an earth dragon turning over cause a fire? This was absolutely abnormal. It must be the work of some villain!","\"Quick, follow me in,\" Hu Bao led the way and rushed into the small house.","For Hu Bao, who was used to walking around large mansions, the two-courtyard house was quite small. Plus, he brought quite a few people with him this time, so they quickly discovered the downward passage.","\"Everyone, come here,\" Hu Bao raised his voice to gather his men.","After he said this, it wasn't just the soldiers who came with him who responded, but also the people in the passage.","\"Hu Bao! Is that Hu Bao?\"","Hu Bao was both surprised and delighted. \"Third Young Master, are you hurt?\"","Down below, Qin Qinian said, \"Rongrong and I are fine, but Qin Yanzhou fainted. I don't know if he was hit by a rock or bumped into something just now. We are trapped in a small corner, surrounded by rocks of different sizes. Hurry up and bring people to rescue us.\"","His voice was full of energy, and judging by the volume, he wasn't far from the exit.","But Qin Qinian's words made Hu Bao's vision go dark for a moment.","Young Master Qin was injured?","What was the difference between this and the Third Young Master getting hurt... No, it might be even worse.","Who in the residence didn't know that Madam Dai treated her son like a pearl in the palm of her hand? Now that this bright pearl was cracked, Madam Dai would probably shed tears like rain.","The sky above their heads would probably also be covered with dark clouds.","Hu Bao said sternly, \"Hurry up and save them!\"","The entrance to the passage was more than eight feet wide, allowing the guards to enter side by side. Using people as anchor points, they first passed the small stones out by hand.","Hu Bao saw that there were quite a few piles of dirt shaken down, so he ordered, \"Quick, go find a bucket.\"","In the dark.","Shi Rongyue listened to the approaching sounds outside and estimated the distance. \"Little Cousin, we should be less than a zhang away from the captain and the others.\"","Qin Qinian was still trying to feel his way around. \"Should be. Qin Yanzhou dragged us for quite a distance earlier. We've probably returned near the entrance.\"","Speaking of this, Qin Qinian still had lingering fears. \"Good thing we ran fast, otherwise we would have capsized in the gutter. By the way, what exactly happened? Why was there suddenly a loud bang? I even saw a fire dragon shooting straight up. It was terrifying.\"","Shi Rongyue didn't understand either. \"There must be some mystery behind it. Little Cousin, is that young lady already...\"","Qin Qinian was silent for a moment.","At that time, Qin Yanzhou was second in line, then Rongrong, and finally him bringing up the rear. Qin Yanzhou was holding one person with each hand, so he indeed didn't have a spare hand to care for the person at the very front.","Undoubtedly, the Fan family's daughter was an abandoned pawn. Judging by her previous words, she was probably deceived by the Green Lotus Sect.","\"We couldn't care about her at that time. After we get out, we'll have people dig further inside. If she still has a breath left, we can save her along the way. This woman knows quite a bit about the Green Lotus Sect. It would be good if she could survive.\" Qin Qinian sighed.","As soon as he finished speaking, Qin Qinian clearly felt movement from the rocks beside his hand.","\"Third Young Master!\"","Qin Qinian instantly perked up. \"You're here! Hurry up and dig it open.\"","In less than a quarter of an hour, a small hole was opened on the side, and the faint light of a fire stick shone through.","After digging it open, Hu Bao realized that the three of them were huddled in the first corner of the downward passage.","A stone slab tilted down from above, forming a small triangle with the wall to trap them inside. The stone slab was already pressing down very low, with its highest point no more than five feet above the ground.","Hu Bao broke out in a cold sweat, thinking to himself that it was a good thing the stone slab hadn't crushed down, otherwise they would have broken a few bones at least.","\"You guys hold up the upper end. Absolutely do not let it fall down. Where is that long stick from earlier? Bring it over and prop it up underneath.\" After arranging everything, Hu Bao said to the people inside, \"Third Young Master, you come out first.\"","Seeing the illuminated hole, Qin Qinian pushed Qin Yanzhou over while saying to Shi Rongyue, \"Rongrong, you take care of Qin Yanzhou for now. I'll come back and get him out later.\"","Shi Rongyue softly agreed.","After Qin Qinian left, Qin Yanzhou, losing half of his support, slid towards that side.","Sensing the abnormality, Shi Rongyue took the initiative to reach out, pulled the person back a bit, and continued to let herself act as a human cushion.","After Qin Qinian came out, he was also startled to see the stone slab tilted like this, and hurriedly said, \"Rongrong, move Qin Yanzhou over.\"","A bit of firelight reflected in. Whether it was the color of the fire or something else, the young girl's cheeks and neck were a bit red. Shi Rongyue lay on the ground, using all her strength to laboriously move the young man on top of her towards the hole.","She didn't expect him to be so heavy despite looking tall and thin. Shi Rongyue felt like she was moving a hard rock.","Hu Bao and Qin Qinian worked together outside to receive the person.","The soldiers outside lit a fire stick, and the firelight illuminated the young man's pale face. There were bloodstains on the corners of his mouth, and blood on his white robe, but not too much.","Hu Bao's heart skipped a beat. \"Third Young Master, I'll escort Young Master Qin back to the residence first, and return later. I'll leave the command here to you, is that alright?\"","Qin Qinian readily agreed. \"Alright, hurry back. Don't delay the treatment time! There's another young lady inside. I'll lead people to see if we can dig her out too.\"","Hu Bao was shocked. \"There's still someone inside? Who is it? Is it Miss Shi's maidservant?\"","But after asking the last question, he felt something was wrong.","He clearly met Miss Shi's personal maidservant on the way here just now, so who was the person inside?","Qin Qinian replied, \"It's the daughter of Fan of Yanzhou. Don't worry about this, hurry up and send Qin Yanzhou back. By the way, today isn't the day for his acupuncture treatment. Old Mr. Ding isn't at the residence, so you have to send someone else to invite him over.\"","Hu Bao accepted the order and left first with the unconscious Qin Yanzhou.","Qin Qinian helped Shi Rongyue out of the small, low hole. Just as he was about to speak, his expression suddenly changed, and he looked at her nervously. \"Rongrong, there's blood on your face. Where did you get hurt?\"","Shi Rongyue belatedly wiped her face. She looked down at the bright red on her palm. Her light brown eyes reflected the firelight and blood, like a blood-stained piece of amber.","The young lady slowly shook her head. \"It's not my blood, it's Young Master Qin's.\"","*","Qin Residence, Main Room.","Dai Li always had the habit of taking an afternoon nap. In autumn, the sky was high and the air was crisp, and the temperature was just right, making it quite pleasant to sleep.","Halfway through her sleep, Dai Li was suddenly awakened by a loud boom. She abruptly opened her eyes, hugged the quilt, and sat up, concentrating to feel her surroundings. Everything was quiet around her; it seemed the sound just now was merely a hallucination.","Footsteps approached from outside, and Dai Li saw Qin Shaozong.","Seeing that she was indeed awake, the man took the initiative to mention what had just happened. \"It wasn't an earth dragon turning over just now. It might be that a house somewhere in the county collapsed due to disrepair. Madam, please continue resting.\"","Dai Li lowered her eyes to look at the plain brocade quilt and murmured, \"I don't know why, but my heart is suddenly beating very fast.\"","\"How about having Ding Congjian come over later to check your pulse, Madam?\" Qin Shaozong poured her a cup of warm water and sat by the couch. After Dai Li took the cup, he naturally reached out to feel her forehead.","Dai Li turned her head to avoid his hand. \"I'm fine. It's probably just because I woke up suddenly and got scared.\"","Taking a casual sip of tea, Dai Li shoved the cup back into his hands and didn't hesitate to shoo him away. \"Go out and do your work. I'm going back to sleep.\"","Qin Shaozong took the cup and left.","Dai Li hugged the quilt and lay back down. Having been startled awake once, falling back asleep was not easy. Just as her drowsiness deepened and almost pulled her into dreamland, Dai Li heard a flurry of hurried footsteps.","It seemed Hu Bao had arrived and was reporting something to Qin Shaozong outside.","Dai Li hugged her quilt and rolled over, intending to continue sleeping, but she heard footsteps entering the room.","For some reason, Dai Li's heart skipped a beat, feeling an inexplicable unease. And this sense of unease peaked when Qin Shaozong scooped her up from the couch.","\"Madam, Hu Bao just reported that Qin Yanzhou was injured while pursuing the remnants of the Green Lotus Cult and is now unconscious. Hu Bao has already sent someone to bring old Mr. Ding to the estate; he will arrive shortly.\"","It was clearly autumn with pleasant temperatures, but Dai Li only felt that the sunlight slanting through the window could not melt the chill in the air. The cold wind poured into her lungs, and even her fingertips were freezing.","\"Zhou Zhou... Where is Zhou Zhou now? Has he returned to his courtyard?\" Dai Li struggled to get down from Qin Shaozong's embrace.","Qin Shaozong knew she would lose all composure whenever it came to her son. The last time she first heard news of Qin Yanzhou, she had sprained her ankle tripping on the footstool.","The man held her waist tightly, keeping her on the couch. \"Madam, put on your clothes first, and then I will take you to see him.\"","During her nap, Dai Li had taken off her outer garments and was now only wearing an apricot-colored inner robe. Her dress was casually draped over the nearby clothes rack. Qin Shaozong extended his long arm to grab it, unfurled it, and helped her put it on.","Once she was finally dressed, Dai Li waved off Qin Shaozong's hands and hurried outside.","Before returning to Yuyang, Qin Yanzhou had lived in the main courtyard with Dai Li and Qin Shaozong. He lived in the side room of the main courtyard, while they lived in the main room.","Later, with the arrival of Qin Qinian and Qin Yunce, Qin Shaozong found the three boys to be in the way. Moreover, the main courtyard only had left and right side rooms, not enough for the three of them. It wasn't good to move just one out alone, so he simply kicked all three out together.","Thus, Qin Yanzhou also got his own courtyard in this mansion.","By the time Dai Li arrived, Ding Lianxi, who happened to be on duty in the estate today, was already there and checking Qin Yanzhou's pulse.","Seeing her son lying motionless on the bed with a pale face and a smear of bright red on his collar, and then noticing Ding Lianxi frowning deeply as he checked the pulse, Dai Li suddenly felt a wave of dizziness.","A large, dark hand reached over, supporting Dai Li's lower back and half-embracing her. Qin Shaozong asked, \"Ding Congjian, how is the situation?\"","Previously, Ding Lianxi had checked Qin Yanzhou's pulse many times but failed to get a result. However, after receiving his grandfather's guidance day and night, he had somewhat grasped the trick.","Now, after taking the pulse for a moment, Ding Lianxi said, \"My Lord, my skills are shallow, but I faintly feel that the Red Gall has become even more violent. If this continues, I'm afraid the final deadline my grandfather predicted will be greatly shortened.\"","Dai Li was shocked, even stuttering when she spoke, \"Then, then how much time is left now?\"","Today was still eight days away from the deadline for collecting medicinal herbs given by Ding Luying. And five days ago, all the herbs had been collected, transitioning from the collection phase to the medicine-making phase.","In other words, they had gained back thirteen days. But if the final deadline was cut in half, or even more, the time left for Ding Luying to make the medicine and for subsequent treatment would still not be enough.","Ding Lianxi looked ashamed. \"As for exactly how much time is left, we will only know when my grandfather comes.\"","Dai Li asked nervously again, \"Besides the Red Gall being affected, does my son have any other injuries?\"","\"The young master's back was hit by a heavy object, causing some bruising, but it didn't hurt his heart or lungs, so it's not a major issue.\" Seeing Dai Li staring at the red on the young man's collar, Ding Lianxi explained, \"The reason he vomited blood is entirely because the Red Gall is acting up.\"","Right at this moment, the rumbling sound of carriage wheels reached the courtyard. It was the guards who had brought Ding Luying over, the carriage driving straight into Qin Yanzhou's courtyard.","Dai Li quickly welcomed him inside. After checking the pulse, the latter stroked his gray beard, looking somewhat peculiar.","\"Fortunately, the medicinal herbs were collected ahead of time. Now the Red Gall has been startled by a tremendous force. Although it is completely enraged, it has shifted from the abdominal cavity to the surface, attempting to head towards the heart meridian. Extracting the worm immediately at this time is actually more convenient than planned. And as for the young master, his body will be healthier in the future than expected,\" Ding Luying said.","Dai Li was stunned. Under the sudden transition from great sorrow to great joy, her legs went weak, and she barely managed to stand firm by holding onto the arm of the man beside her.","She said \"good\" several times in a row. \"Without further delay, I must trouble old Mr. Ding to extract the Gu worm for my son.\"","Indeed, there was no time to delay. After Ding Luying spoke, the entire courtyard immediately began operating at high speed.","Those fetching herbs fetched herbs, and those preparing tools prepared tools.","Watching the busy servants, Dai Li's heart gradually settled, and her chaotic thoughts slowly became calm and clear.","Just now, Hu Bao had said that Zhou Zhou was injured while pursuing the remnants of the Green Lotus Cult.","Remnants of the Green Lotus Cult?","Did Zhou Zhou discover members of the Green Lotus Cult in the commandery?","After discovering a few suspected strongholds last time, wasn't Zhou Zhou planning to play the mantis stalking the cicada, unaware of the oriole behind? What made him suddenly change his mind?","Could it be that he made a new discovery at the time?","A name surfaced in Dai Li's mind—","Diting.","Zhou Zhou might have discovered Diting's tracks!","If that was the case, Dai Li could completely understand why her son changed his plans halfway. Because once successful, the reward would be too great.","As the \"prince\" of the Green Lotus Cult, Diting's importance could not be underestimated. It could be said that if they could catch him, it would be equivalent to having the power to negotiate with the \"emperor\" of the Green Lotus Cult.","And what kind of place was Yuyang?","It was Qin Shaozong's stronghold!","As long as Diting's tracks were discovered and Zhou Zhou locked onto him, reinforcements would swarm in from all directions, and Diting would find it hard to fly away even if he had wings.","From the moment her son proposed to serve Qin Shaozong and act as his vanguard, Dai Li realized with absolute clarity:","Her Zhou Zhou had grown up; he was already a man. He no longer wanted to hide behind her like he did in childhood; he wanted to shield her from the wind and rain.","The Green Lotus Cult's abduction of her, the debt of gratitude to Qin Shaozong that was hard to repay, and even the threat conveyed in the letter from the Green Lotus Cult after they arrived in Yuyang—he had silently watched it all.","Her son was not good with words. Dai Li had no way of knowing whether he hated so much that he couldn't sleep night after night, or whether he repeatedly imagined how to exact revenge.","There must have been at least some of that; otherwise, why would he firmly pursue Diting's tracks when he clearly could have just stood by and watched?","A nineteen-year-old youth, his hot blood had not cooled. He might have had concerns, but he still dared to fight.","Dai Li understood his impatience, yet her heart ached for him beyond measure. But she also knew very well that she could not change her son's mind.","Until the Green Lotus Sect is eradicated, the lingering hatred will never fade away."]},{"number":114,"title":"Chapter 114","paragraphs":["Dai Li called Hu Bao over and asked about the situation at the time.","Hu Bao answered truthfully, \"Madam Dai, I am actually not very clear on the specific details. Initially, I received a message from the Third Young Master's attendant, asking me to bring men for support. When I followed him to a small noodle stall, we met a city guard who pointed the way. This happened one after another until we finally arrived at a small cabin. But before I could even enter, I suddenly heard a loud explosion.\"","When Hu Bao mentioned the loud explosion, both Dai Li and Qin Shaozong froze for a moment.","They both coincidentally thought of the booming sound from not long ago.","Hu Bao continued, \"At first, I thought it was an earthquake, but then I saw flames shooting up into the sky not far away, so I knew my guess was wrong. I immediately led my men quickly inside. There was a secret passage in that cabin, and part of it had collapsed. Young Master Qin and the others were trapped inside at the time.\"","For a moment, Dai Li thought it was explosives.","But as soon as this guess formed, she denied it.","The Sui Dynasty established the gunpowder system, and gunpowder only officially appeared in the Tang Dynasty. Bai Juyi wrote in his poem New Year's Eve, \"After the fire dies and the lamps go out at dawn, I will be an ordinary man of sixty.\" The phrase \"fire dies and lamps go out\" here refers to the firecrackers finishing and the lanterns burning out.","It wasn't until the Song Dynasty that gunpowder began to be widely used in the military, with the government taking the lead in building gunpowder workshops and creating a batch of firearms like cannons and rockets.","No matter how much the butterfly effect changed things, the timeline was far from reaching that point.","Besides, if the Green Lotus Sect really possessed such a weapon of mass destruction as explosives, why would they hide? Wouldn't it be easier to just send people to infiltrate the mansions of the major warlords and throw explosives inside to blow them all to death?","Dai Li furrowed her delicate brows in thought but couldn't figure out the reason.","Just then, two horses galloped closer outside. One of the riders was actually Shi Rongyue.","Shi Rongyue reined in her horse at the courtyard gate and dismounted on her own without anyone's help.","The young lady, who had been bright and beautiful when she left, now had a crooked hair bun with a jade hairpin dangling precariously. A few strands of black hair hung down from her temples, brushing across her small, dirty, ash-covered face.","Not only was she covered in dirt, but the hem of her skirt was also torn in many places by gravel or something else, and its bright colors were obscured by dust.","Seeing Qin Shaozong and Dai Li in the courtyard, Shi Rongyue was visibly stunned for a moment, looking dazed, but she quickly recovered and bowed to them.","\"Second Uncle, Madam Dai.\"","Her movements were standard; if one didn't look at her attire, there was absolutely nothing discourteous about her.","Dai Li was still thinking about the gunpowder. Now, seeing Shi Rongyue in such a sorry state, she knew she must have been at the scene, so she immediately called her by her pet name to come over. \"Rongrong, you were there, right? Tell me what happened then.\"","Shi Rongyue started from when Qin Yanzhou first saw Fan Muqi.","She recounted how they chased her and followed her into a seemingly abandoned house that had a secret passage; she also repeated Fan Muqi's words.","\"...My little cousin and I suggested she come with us to the mansion to see you. She seemed persuaded and gave up on using traps to kill Young Master Qin. Later, Young Master Qin asked her if Diting had come to Yuyang and where he was now. Lady Fan said he was originally in the bookstore but left later. However, through the secret passage in that house, one could reach another place. She also said there were traces of another minor leader there, whose status in the sect was on par with Diting,\" she recalled.","Hearing the word \"bookstore,\" Qin Shaozong raised his voice and called over Hu Bao, who hadn't left yet. \"Lead a squad of soldiers and immediately control all the bookstores in the county, as well as the places Qin Yanzhou paid attention to earlier. Lock down the city early today; only entry is allowed, no exit.\"","Pausing slightly, Qin Shaozong added, \"Send another squad to the large and small inns in the county, and keep a close eye on the travelers who settled there this afternoon.\"","Hu Bao cupped his hands in obedience.","Dai Li thought of Ding Lianxi saying her son was crushed by a heavy object, guessing that after they entered the passage, it collapsed, causing the Chidan poison in her son's body to accelerate its rampage.","But, the passage collapsed?","If the passage was visibly unreliable, Zhouzhou and the others would never have risked entering. So that passage must have been very sturdy initially. But if explosives hadn't appeared yet, what could have blown the passage into a collapse?","\"What did you encounter in the passage?\" Dai Li asked with a frown.","Speaking of this, Shi Rongyue was still confused. \"We went down the stone steps. That passage was equipped with many small bronze mirrors for lighting. By the light of the mirrors, we could barely see our surroundings. The passage was shaped like a funnel, narrow at first and then wide. Later, I saw many empty wooden shelves, all covered in dust, who knows how long they hadn't been moved.\"","Dai Li's red lips pressed tightly together.","Bronze mirrors for lighting, wooden shelves in the room, these all sounded very ordinary...","\"Besides the wooden shelves, there were many small open jars on the floor. In the center, there was a table and chairs, and on the table sat a coiled dragon lamp.\" Shi Rongyue carefully described the rotating scenes on the coiled dragon lamp.","\"Did you see clearly what was inside the small jars?\" Qin Shaozong asked.","\"It looked like some white stuff, but I didn't pay special attention to what exactly it was. I was focused on looking at the lamp at the time.\" Shi Rongyue felt a bit ashamed.","\"...Not long after seeing this coiled dragon lamp, for some reason, Young Master Qin suddenly grabbed me and my little cousin, turned around, and ran. Later, just as he threw us forward, there was a huge noise from behind. A stone slab from the ceiling collapsed. Fortunately, we had reached the corner by then, and the stone slab tilted into a small angle, which gave us a breathing space.\"","Dai Li was terrified hearing this.","Qin Shaozong also furrowed his long brows. \"You didn't see anyone else in the passage?\"","Shi Rongyue shook her head. \"No. At that time, besides that Lady Fan, only me, Young Master Qin, and my little cousin were there.\"","A blurry image suddenly popped into her mind, and Shi Rongyue hurriedly said, \"Right, when I was pulled away by Young Master Qin and turned around, I seemed to see that coiled dragon lamp slowly rising into the air. However, I don't know if my eyes played tricks on me. We'll have to wait for my little cousin to come back and ask him.\"","At that time, after rescuing Young Master Qin, her little cousin immediately sent him back to the mansion for medical treatment. Later, feeling that the place was dangerous and there might be remnants of the Green Lotus Sect, he told her to go back first while he stayed there to continue leading the troops in the excavation.","\"The lamp rose into the air?\" Dai Li muttered.","Suddenly she shuddered. \"Wait, Rongrong, when you say it slowly rose into the air, do you mean the whole lamp rose, or just the lampshade?\"","Shi Rongyue's small face scrunched up. \"It seems... not the whole thing! Yes, just the lampshade rose, because the scenes on the coiled dragon lamp became incomplete, leaving only a small half.\"","That scene was too bizarre. If Shi Rongyue hadn't been influenced by her mother since childhood and didn't really believe in supernatural things, she would have thought she encountered a monster.","Dai Li closed her eyes, and tiny nodes were connected by invisible threads. \"It was a dust explosion. You encountered a dust explosion. If I am not mistaken, there must have been wind blowing into the passage at that time.\"","Shi Rongyue's pupils contracted slightly. \"Yes, there was indeed a gust of wind blowing from behind. At the time, I even wondered why there would be wind underground. But why would a passing breeze cause the room to boom so loudly that even the stone slabs on the ceiling fell?\"","It was just a gust of wind, after all. The impact was simply too massive.","Qin Shaozong was also looking at Dai Li. \"Madam, what is a dust explosion?\"","\"A dust explosion occurs when combustible dust floats in a relatively enclosed space. When this dust encounters an open flame, the local temperature sharply rises, triggering an explosion. Rongrong, the white powder you saw earlier stored in small jars was actually flour,\" Dai Li explained.","The limited space of the room satisfied the condition of being relatively enclosed. When the lampshade of the coiled dragon lamp was lifted, an open flame appeared.","At the same time, wind was blown into the room. With all these conditions perfectly met, it would indeed trigger a dust explosion.","Shi Rongyue listened in a daze; this was an area she had never encountered before.","Hearing Dai Li's words, Qin Shaozong suddenly recalled a past event.","Six years ago, several incidents of \"divine miracles\" occurred in Jingzhou. Initially, members of the Qinglian Sect publicly declared that certain places had fallen out of the deities' favor, and that the gods would release earth dragons to punish those areas.","At first, not everyone believed it. That was until the \"earth dragon\" turned over at a specific location, precisely destroying houses while swallowing several people whole.","After the incident, the commoners were in an uproar, and the elites paled in fear.","At the time, he only thought the rumors were grossly exaggerated. After all, such things had happened frequently in the past, whether it was insects eating leaves to form characters, or fox cries coming from bonfires, all were meticulously orchestrated schemes designed to build momentum for those seeking power.","Therefore, when he heard of those \"divine miracles,\" he merely assumed they had deliberately found some dilapidated houses so the subsequent \"earth dragon\" could appear smoothly.","But looking back now, that was not the case at all. That so-called precise \"divine punishment\" was most likely the dust explosion his wife had just described.","\"This Qinglian Sect is full of tricks. If one doesn't understand the underlying mechanics, it's incredibly easy to be deceived,\" Qin Shaozong clicked his tongue softly.","Dai Li remembered that Shi Rongyue and Qin Qinian had been pulled away. She asked about Fan Muqi, \"What about the young lady from the Fan family? Is she still alive?\"","Shi Rongyue shook her head, saying she didn't know. \"When my little cousin told me to come back, I hadn't seen her dug out yet.\"","Meanwhile, on the other side.","Following the earlier cave-in, this secret passage had seen the light of day again. No, it couldn't exactly be called seeing the light of day, the ceiling above had collapsed, crushing and compressing more than half of the space below.","Fearing a second collapse, everyone moved to the very top to dig through the dirt.","A dirt-streaked Qin Qinian also moved up to direct the efforts. \"We can move the small stones, so clear those first. Go find more wooden buckets and shovels; it'll be easier to carry the small rocks in buckets.\"","The soldiers received their orders and went.","By the time they returned with the tools, the excavation progress had noticeably sped up.","The entire area had been cordoned off, but some curious commoners still gathered around to watch.","\"Isn't this Old Li's house? How did it collapse?\"","\"Probably because it's been empty for too long. I remember Old Li took his wife and children south over two months ago. When a house is left unoccupied, problems are bound to happen.\"","The soldiers waved them away. \"Go back to your homes. Don't gather here.\"","...","In the blink of an eye, over two hours had passed.","Suddenly, someone shouted, \"Third Young Master, we can see the young lady's dress hem!\"","Qin Qinian, who had just picked up his waterskin for a drink, felt a jolt of energy. Holding the waterskin, he hurried over. Indeed, amidst a pile of rubble not far away, a patch of aqua-blue fabric was visible. He led his men to move the rocks. As soon as the first slightly larger stone was shifted away, Qin Qinian saw bloodstains.","He paused for a second before digging even more frantically. \"Hey, how are you doing? Are you still alive?\"","\"I'm... doing okay.\"","Hearing her response, Qin Qinian worked with even more vigor. As he continued to clear the stones with his men, he kept talking to Fan Muqi. \"After this ordeal, you should finally believe that there are no good people in the Qinglian Sect. They were just using you as a pawn, exploiting you. If it weren't for our good luck, we really would have died here today. By the way, the bookstore you mentioned earlier, which specific bookstore is it?\"","\"The Laimo Bookstore in the west of the city,\" the voice from underneath replied weakly, though slightly better than at first.","Qin Qinian asked again, \"Do they only have one hideout? Besides that bookstore in the west, where else have you gone with them?\"","\"I was arranged to stay at the bookstore. Diting and White Elephant have a different residence. However...\" At this point, the person underneath coughed twice. The sound made Qin Qinian's heart leap into his throat, terrified she might suddenly die before finishing her sentence.","\"However what?\" the young man pressed.","\"They took a donkey cart every time they came. Twice, I noticed a few osmanthus petals stuck to the cart's wheels. There must be osmanthus trees near where they live. Also...\"","Her voice unexpectedly grew louder. \"Once, I needed to find them. The servant was ordered to pass on the message, and about half an hour later, I saw White Elephant. They must live not far from the bookstore!\"","After clearing away some of the surrounding stones, Qin Qinian finally saw clearly that Fan Muqi was pinned down by a rather large stone slab.","The slab had missed her head and was only crushing her from the waist down.","\"You guys lift from over there, and I'll lift from this side with them,\" Qin Qinian ordered. He then turned to Fan Muqi. \"Hold on just a little longer. Once you're out, I'll take you to get treated. Then you can tell me more inside information.\"","They were all strong, able-bodied elites, and they had tools on hand. Soon, the heavy stone slab pinning Fan Muqi was slowly shifted away.","Overjoyed, Qin Qinian was about to speak when he saw Fan Muqi suddenly vomit a mouthful of blood. The young girl, who had seemed so spirited just moments ago, now withered rapidly like a dying flower.","Qin Qinian froze in place. \"Wh-what's wrong with you?\"","Hu Bao, who had returned later, was also present.","He had followed Qin Shaozong onto the battlefield far more times than Qin Qinian had. He remembered one instance after a siege where, perhaps due to the city wall's long-standing disrepair, a small-scale collapse occurred, burying several soldiers who happened to be right below it.","Captives held value, so naturally, once everything settled down, they had to be rescued.","However, the men who had still been able to answer back died within a very short time after the heavy stone slabs were lifted off them.","Later, Hu Bao learned from Mr. Ding that blocked blood circulation could cause internal organs to undergo necrosis, which was no different from severe internal injuries.","\"Third Young Master, I'm afraid she won't survive,\" Hu Bao said."]},{"number":115,"title":"Chapter 115","paragraphs":["A swift horse, bathed in the afterglow of dusk, galloped through the side gate into the estate. The rider did not dismount upon entering, but rode straight to a certain courtyard.","\"How is Qin Yanzhou doing now?\" Qin Qinian asked the guards from horseback, craning his neck to peer inside as he spoke.","The door ahead was half-open, and figures could faintly be seen moving about inside. One silhouette was quite familiar; Qin Qinian recognized him as Ding Lianxi.","A guard replied, \"The young master's life is not in danger for now. However, from today until three days from now, Old Mr. Ding will be treating him day and night. We ask that the Third Young Master refrain from going in to visit at this time.\"","\"As long as he's alright.\" Unable to make out anything clearly, Qin Qinian had no choice but to turn his horse around and head toward the main courtyard.","...","\"Father!\"","His voice arrived before he did, his cracking, adolescent voice grating on the ears.","\"Father, I was just riding back and passed by a bookstore, where I saw many soldiers searching it. They told me later that you had ordered all the bookstores in the commandery to be secured,\" Qin Qinian said, rushing in hastily.","Qin Shaozong and Dai Li were both standing before a long desk. A map of Yuyang was spread out upon it, with several white jade chess pieces placed at various locations.","As Qin Qinian ran in, Dai Li was holding a white jade piece, just about to set it down.","\"Father, Madam Dai. Perhaps we don't need to search all the bookstores. I received news that the people of the Green Lotus Cult are staying at the Laimo Bookstore in the western part of the city.\"","Dai Li asked in surprise, \"Did Miss Fan tell you this? Is the information reliable? Could it be a trap to lure us away?\"","Shi Rongyue's previous recounting had made her realize that Miss Fan hated not only Zhou Zhou, but also Qin Shaozong, who had caused her father's defeat in battle.","Since she had previously been able to lure Zhou Zhou and the others into a secret passage, telling another lie now would hardly be out of character.","\"Probably not. She already knew at the time that the Green Lotus Cult was using her as a pawn, and she most likely believes that Qin Yanzhou infiltrated the Fan residence as a spy on their orders. She told me this because she can't wait to see us and the Green Lotus Cult tear each other apart,\" Qin Qinian said earnestly.","Dai Li was speechless. This child...","Qin Shaozong remained expressionless. \"Qin San, once this matter is settled, you will roll back to the Marquis's manor, study hard under Mi Yifan, and learn how to speak properly before you come out again.\"","Qin Qinian felt as if struck by lightning. He truly couldn't understand how a simple report had suddenly turned into a lecture about studying.","His gaze lost focus for a moment, but he forced himself to rally. \"Father, there is one more thing. At the time, Miss Fan said she noticed a few osmanthus petals stuck to the wheels of the donkey cart ridden by that minor cult leader named 'White Elephant'. She also mentioned that once, when she went looking for him, he appeared about two quarters of an hour later, leading her to guess that his true hiding place is not far from the bookstore.\"","Dai Li's eyes lit up. \"A two-quarter hour round trip by donkey cart... that means a one-way trip of about one quarter of an hour.\"","She looked down at the parchment map on the desk. Having just marked the bookstores one by one, she quickly found this Laimo Bookstore.","Laimo Bookstore was located in the western part of the city, situated next to a residential area for those with some modest wealth.","After all, paper was still not that cheap nowadays. Those who sought it out were certainly not the lower-class commoners who struggled daily just to put food on the table.","Centering on Laimo Bookstore, Dai Li estimated the speed of a donkey cart and drew a circle. \"He is very likely right here.\"","\"Father, there is no time to lose. Why don't we immediately take our troops and surround this area!\" Qin Qinian said excitedly.","Qin Shaozong twisted his jade thumb ring. \"No rush.\"","The youth froze, asking in confusion, \"Father, we finally know the specific bookstore and their general hiding place. Why not strike while the iron is hot?\"","\"We should indeed strike while the iron is hot, but not right now.\" Qin Shaozong turned to look out the window.","Dusk had arrived, and the sky was blanketed with vast swaths of brilliant sunset clouds, looking like the most precious final masterpiece of a renowned painter.","In a little while, the curfew would begin.","Qin Shaozong said, \"We wait for the curfew. After the curfew, people are not allowed to move about freely in the city. They will have no choice but to stay indoors and won't be able to head to a relay inn.\"","If they went to arrest them immediately, there was no guarantee the enemy wouldn't catch wind of it and hide straight in a relay inn instead of returning to their original residence. Although he had also dispatched troops to the relay inns just in case, there were at least a hundred relay inns, large and small, in the commandery. It would be troublesome.","\"White Elephant\" was merely a codename. As for this person's actual name, they had absolutely no information.","Qin Qinian suddenly understood, and then asked, \"Father, will you be leaving the estate tonight? If not, how about leaving tonight's pursuit entirely in my hands?\"","\"Alright, you take charge. This Laimo Bookstore is the focal point. After nightfall, first check the household registers of everyone in the bookstore. Those lowly servants are bound to be cult members. By following the vine to get the melon, you can force them to reveal the location of that residence. Of course, their words cannot be fully trusted; you must also divide your forces to search for houses nearby with osmanthus trees,\" Qin Shaozong instructed him.","Qin Qinian replied, \"Yes, sir!\"","Dai Li suddenly said, \"Qinian, let me go with you tonight. Zhou Zhou once told me that White Elephant and Diting are twins and look quite similar. I have seen what Diting looks like without a disguise, and I roughly know their methods of disguise. If I see White Elephant, I should be able to recognize him.\"","Wearing fish glue for a long time must be uncomfortable. Back when she was abducted onto the ship, traveling upstream westward from the port of Bairi City, the boat journey alone took nearly half a month.","Perhaps because she was the only outsider on board, and he didn't think she could escape, Diting did not wear a disguise at the time.","Upon hearing that she had seen Diting, Qin Qinian was immediately very willing. \"Alright, you can follow me then...\"","\"Madam.\" Qin Shaozong looked at Dai Li, who met his gaze without flinching.","\"My son was framed by him. Although by a twist of fate it made the pest eradication go smoother than expected, it doesn't erase their malicious intentions. Qin Changgeng, you ask me to stay in the estate and quietly await good news, but I absolutely cannot do that.\" Dai Li stared at him unblinking.","This wasn't the first time Qin Qinian had heard Dai Li call his father by his full courtesy name, including the surname, but every time it felt like a deafening thunderclap splitting the clouds and cracking stones, sending a great shock through his heart.","The youth lowered his head, keeping his eyes on his nose and his mind focused inward, not daring to look further.","\"I didn't say you couldn't go. I will leave the estate with you. Once we catch the person, Madam can torture him however you please.\" Qin Shaozong's tone carried a hint of helplessness.","Dai Li looked away. \"We're moving after curfew, right? Then hurry up and have someone serve the meal. We have an operation tonight, so we should eat early.\"","Today's dinner was served early. By the time they finished their evening meal, only a faint, shallow light remained in the sky outside.","Dai Li returned to her room and changed into a cobalt blue riding outfit. Her long hair was all coiled up on her head, secured with a silver snake hairpin. She wore no other hair accessories or earrings. Coupled with the fact that Dai Li was already tall, she looked incredibly heroic and dashing in this riding attire.","But when she raised her eyes, those peach blossom eyes with slightly upturned corners were like bright sunset clouds, possessing an indescribably radiant charm.","Qin Shaozong leaned against the window with his arms crossed, watching her change clothes and tie up her hair. \"Madam is in high spirits; tonight you will surely return in triumph.\"","Dai Li remained silent.","Dai Li's expression was complex. \"I think I finally understand.\"","Her tone held a hint of unspeakable sigh. Qin Shaozong raised an eyebrow. \"Understand what?\"","\"That occasional nonsense your son spouts definitely takes after you.\" Dai Li really didn't understand what causal relationship existed between those two words.","Qin Shaozong: \"...\"","The man was visibly silent for a moment, but quickly said, \"Qi Nian is also your son. Madam, do not forget what you promised me.\"","Dai Li pursed her lips, turned her head to the side, and stopped looking at him.","Seeing her expression, Qin Shaozong clicked his tongue softly.","Great, she was being stubborn again.","Not long ago, Qin Yanzhou returned injured, and Ding Luying stated bluntly that immediate parasite removal would yield the best results. This was a matter of vital importance and could not be delayed for a moment, so the parasite removal was arranged for today.","As for the two precious medicines, fleeceflower root and musk, they had already been sent to the Ding residence along with the rest of the batch when the other medicinal herbs were collected.","He had never mentioned this matter, and she had never asked about it since that day. However, Qin Shaozong knew that this sly fox must have already guessed a thing or two.","The situation just now had been critical, leaving no time to settle scores, but that didn't mean the matter was over.","\"Dai Li,\" Qin Shaozong said in a deep voice.","Dai Li paused, eventually turning her head back slowly.","He didn't say any more of those words that sounded so grating to her ears, but she knew what he meant.","Those narrow brown eyes locked onto her like an endless ocean, its surging waves threatening to pull her in.","Dai Li said softly, \"Can we talk about this when we get back?\"","Seeing her tone soften, Qin Shaozong knew when to stop pushing. \"Fine.\"","*","Just as the curfew began, the main gates of the Qin residence opened, and a squad of cavalry led by Qin Qinian filed out.","About half an hour later, the gates opened again, and Qin Shaozong and Dai Li led another group of men out of the estate.","Dai Li had only recently learned to ride, and she was mounted on a small black mare. The little mare trotted along with a clip-clop sound; although she had only recently reached adulthood, she was docile and steady. However, compared to the galloping steeds of the previous group, her speed was not very fast.","Qin Shaozong rode his horse, Red Wyrm, beside Dai Li, leading the group together with her.","While they were still a short distance from the Laimo Bookstore, Dai Li saw a brightly lit area ahead.","After nightfall, commoners who couldn't afford candles would go to rest early. After a good sleep, they would wake up to bright daylight, saving them the worry of lighting lamps.","The residents near the Laimo Bookstore were relatively wealthier, so scattered lights could still be seen.","The sound of hooves echoed through the quiet streets and alleys. Birds on the treetops tilted their heads in confusion, observing this group of night travelers.","The side doors of a few households quietly opened a crack, and a curious eye peeked out from the gap. Upon sensing a gaze sweeping over, they would shut the door with a frightened whoosh.","Qin Qinian, who had gone ahead to check the household registers, was already at the Laimo Bookstore. Seeing his father arrive, the youth hurriedly reported, \"Father, this bookstore has a total of four helpers and one shopkeeper. They have all been brought here.\"","Qin Shaozong dismounted.","Qin Qinian continued, \"The owner of this bookstore is surnamed Dong. Upon investigation, this person lives in the Second District of the West City. However, when I sent men to bring him over, we found that the Dong residence was an empty house with no one inside. I asked the neighbors, and they all said that the Dong family left three months ago.\"","Qin Shaozong said, \"Leave this place to me. Take some men and search for the osmanthus trees nearby.\"","Qin Qinian accepted the order.","Dai Li looked toward the bookstore with its wide-open doors, faintly making out the guards watching over several people. She also dismounted and entered the bookstore with Qin Shaozong.","Among the five captured individuals, the four helpers were guarded in pairs, while the shopkeeper was kept separately.","Dai Li's gaze swept over them; they varied in height and weight.","The four helpers all had dark complexions and thin frames. Some were as skinny as beanpoles, perfectly fitting the image of the lower class who struggled for their next meal.","After observing the helpers, she looked at the shopkeeper. He was a bit on the chubby side, short in stature, and currently breaking out in a cold sweat.","None of these five people had put on any disguises.","Her faint, almost imperceptible sliver of hope dashed, Dai Li looked at Qin Shaozong, signaling that he could begin questioning.","\"Noble sir, this humble one is honest and dutiful. I have always lived a grounded life and have never stepped out of line. May I ask why you are visiting late at night and have brought me and the several helpers from the shop here?\" the shopkeeper said while wiping his sweat.","Qin Shaozong asked directly, \"Has the owner of this bookstore or any of his friends been here recently?\"","The plump shopkeeper's pupils trembled slightly.","Qin Shaozong drew the ring-pommel dao from his waist. The blade reflected a startling cold gleam in the firelight, the sharp light shooting straight into the shopkeeper's eyes, making him shudder in terror.","In the next moment, the plump shopkeeper's body jolted.","He stood frozen in place like a stone statue, not daring to move an inch, terrified that a single careless movement might cause him to touch the blade that now rested on his shoulder, less than a finger's width from his neck.","\"Confess and you will be treated leniently. Not only will your entire family be pardoned, but you will also receive a reward. If you try to cover things up and attempt to deceive me with lies, I will let you know that sometimes, a quick death is a kind of fortune.\" Qin Shaozong looked down at him from above.","He hadn't worn armor when leaving the estate tonight, dressed only in an ordinary black robe. However, it couldn't conceal his tall and straight stature, as formidable as a mountain. Years of experience had settled into a heavy, oppressive aura.","Qin Shaozong's tone was not particularly harsh, yet it still made the plump shopkeeper's face turn as pale as gold paper.","The plump shopkeeper bit his lip tightly, seemingly struggling internally.","Qin Shaozong only waited for two breaths. When the plump shopkeeper failed to answer, he turned to look at the four helpers. \"The shopkeeper chooses to die. What about you? For the first among you to confess, I will likewise let bygones be bygones and grant a reward. As for the rest, you will receive sixty strokes of the cane and serve four years of hard labor. All male members of your families will share your guilt and be punished with four years, while the female members will serve two years.\"","Two years for the female family members. Assuming they survived these two years of penal labor, they would almost certainly marry someone else.","Marrying a man meant securing clothes to wear and food to eat.","With a husband still serving a sentence, it was no different from him being dead, as he could provide no financial support. The Great Yan government offices would give the green light to such women, allowing them to choose another spouse, remarry, and have children, thereby boosting the birth rate.","As soon as Qin Shaozong's words fell, the thinnest and weakest helper among them hurriedly said, \"Noble sir, I will tell you everything!\"","Watching his interrogation from the side, Dai Li was utterly amazed."]},{"number":116,"title":"Chapter 116","paragraphs":["Qin Shaozong withdrew his ring-pommel sword. Instead of letting the young servant report immediately, he said, \"Come with me.\"","He led the person up to the second floor. Daili, out of curiosity, followed them.","Once on the second floor, completely separated from the people below, Qin Shaozong finally said, \"Tell me the truth.\"","The young servant fell to his knees with a thud. \"Noble lord, everyone joined, I couldn't just stand out. I... I've only been at this bookstore for seven months. At first, I didn't join the owner and the others, but the owner and the manager sometimes didn't avoid me when they worshipped. They said the Unborn Venerable Mother advocates equality for everyone, and that as long as we believe in the religion, we can ascend to paradise after death.\"","Perhaps out of anxiety, he spoke incoherently, his words somewhat muddled.","Qin Shaozong did not interrupt him, and Daili was also listening.","\"About three months ago, the owner said he was going south to Jingzhou to visit relatives. Before leaving, he said some distant relatives might come to the bookstore and take over for him for a while, and told us to serve them well. About two months later, people really did come. Leading them were two young gentlemen, oh, and a young lady. They had the owner's token. That young lady later settled down in the bookstore; there is a room for her on the third floor,\" the young servant explained.","\"What are the names of the owner's distant relatives? Where did they stay later?\" Qin Shaozong asked.","The young servant shook his head. \"I don't know their exact names. I only know their surname is Bai, because I once heard the manager call them Young Master Bai. As for where they lived, I know even less. These two Young Master Bais were hosted entirely by the manager. They had the most contact with him, and except for the initial period, they rarely came to the bookstore later on. On the contrary, I was ordered around a few times by that young lady who settled here, but it was just serving tea and pouring water, nothing special.\"","Daili asked, \"What did those two Young Master Bais look like?\"","The young servant held it in for a long time, only managing to squeeze out the words, \"Regular features.\"","\"Is there nothing memorable about them?\" Daili asked seeing this.","The young servant nodded repeatedly, not daring to look directly at Daili, keeping his eyes on her jade pendant instead. \"Indeed. They looked quite ordinary, without any outstanding features.\"","Qin Shaozong asked, \"The young lady upstairs once sent someone to find them. Do you know about this?\"","The young servant nodded, saying he knew, and added that he happened to run into it once.","Qin Shaozong asked again, \"From the time that person was sent out to when Young Master Bai arrived at the bookstore, did it take about two quarters of an hour?\"","The young servant froze, frowning as he tried hard to recall. \"It seems... it seems so.\"","After that, Qin Shaozong asked a few more questions, such as who else in the bookstore had the most contact with them besides the manager; whether there were any outside visitors during the time those two stayed at the bookstore; how often they came to the bookstore; and whether the young lady upstairs went out frequently.","The young servant knew the answers to some questions, but was completely clueless about others.","Qin Shaozong didn't say much about this. Once he finished his questioning, he ordered the guards to watch the man, keeping him guarded alone on the second floor.","\"Madam, let's go downstairs first.\" Qin Shaozong took a torch from a guard's hand.","Daili asked him in a low voice, \"Qin Changgeng, do you still want to interrogate that manager?\"","From the young servant's words, the manager clearly knew a lot of information, perhaps even where they lived.","The stairs were not spacious, only wide enough for one burly man to pass. If two people were to walk side by side, one would have to be a petite woman. Daili and Qin Shaozong walked downstairs one after the other.","He held the torch from behind. The steps behind were naturally higher than those in front, and the firelight illuminated the path under Daili's feet with absolute clarity.","Regarding her question, the man replied, \"I will interrogate him, but for someone who refuses a toast only to be forced to drink a forfeit, I won't waste any more words on him.\"","The phrase refuses a toast only to be forced to drink a forfeit was said plainly, unemotionally deciding the future of a person, and even that of their entire family.","An invisible gust of wind blew past, brushing away the dust in a certain corner of Daili's memory.","Her memories uncontrollably drifted back to more than half a year ago. In that guest room, after the phrase refuses a toast only to be forced to drink a forfeit was spoken, a sharp blade flew in from the outside, humming as it nailed into the wall of the inner room.","At that moment, the trajectory of destiny deviated. The rest of her life completely headed in another direction she had never envisioned before.","Daili stopped and couldn't help but look back at Qin Shaozong behind her.","He held the torch, pulling it slightly inward, keeping it in a safe zone away from her.","Noticing her looking back, the man raised his long eyebrows. \"What is it?\"","Compared to his sharp coldness when they first met, the current Qin Shaozong was undoubtedly peaceful. The warm firelight danced in his eyes, and his amber-like brown pupils reflected the woman's silhouette, completely filled with the person in front of him.","He stood at a higher position, looking down at her. Although he was looking down from above, he lacked that intimidating coercion he had earlier when facing the fat manager.","Daili slowly shook her head and continued walking down.","When they returned to the first floor, the three young servants who were previously able to stand all fell to their knees with a thud. Speaking one after another, they spilled everything they knew like beans pouring out of a bamboo tube.","One said that a merchant surnamed Zhao from the east of the city had come to look for those two young gentlemen a few times, and each time he stayed on the third floor for at least half an hour before leaving.","Another said that the other party specifically left a servant for the young lady on the third floor to use for running errands and delivering messages.","Still another said that ever since the two young gentlemen appeared, a servant from a wealthy household frequently showed up at the bookstore.","\"Which wealthy household?\" Qin Shaozong, who had been watching coldly from the sidelines, suddenly spoke up.","The young servant who was addressed was initially overjoyed, but quickly shook his head in distress. \"I don't know. At the time, looking at that person, I only felt that his clothes were much better than ordinary people's. I also heard him constantly referring to a benefactor, so I knew he was a servant from a wealthy household.\"","\"What does this person look like?\" Qin Shaozong asked.","The young servant described him truthfully. Perhaps out of fear, his description was exceptionally detailed, even mentioning a large, hairy black mole on the side of the person's neck.","Qin Shaozong glanced at Hu Bao next to him, who nodded to indicate he had noted it down.","Right at this moment, a fast horse rode through the night.","\"Father, we found it!\" The newcomer was none other than Qin Qinian himself.","The youth, dressed in a black and red martial outfit, reined in his horse and said excitedly, \"Coincidentally, there are only two places nearby with osmanthus trees, and neither is by the roadside. One is an empty residence, and the other is occupied.\"","Qin Shaozong narrowed his eyes. \"Has anyone been sent to guard that empty residence?\"","Qin Qinian said he had.","This was Yuyang, his father's territory, and the last thing they lacked was soldiers. Although the first place was empty, just in case, he still sent people to guard it strictly.","Qin Shaozong turned his head to look at Daili. \"Madam, let's go over and take a look.\"","Daili naturally agreed.","Horses were much faster than donkey carts. In less than a quarter of an hour, Daili saw a residence heavily surrounded.","This place was not a slum. Looking around, one couldn't find a single-courtyard house; they were at least double-courtyard, or even triple-courtyard residences.","The surrounded residence was a triple-courtyard house. Both the front and back doors were guarded by soldiers holding torches and halberds.","The doors were wide open, allowing an unobstructed view straight inside. Before even dismounting, Daili saw about a dozen people gathered in the front hall, including men, women, the elderly, and the young.","\"Father, this family's surname is Shang. The entire household, including the servants, totals twenty-seven people. They are all here,\" Qin Qinian said as he dismounted his horse.","\"Are you certain no one was missed?\" Qin Shaozong asked.","Qin Qinian replied firmly, \"None. I had my men conduct a thorough search.\"","Dai Li followed the father and son inside.","Surrounding them were soldiers holding torches, the firelight clearly illuminating every fearful face.","The eldest was already in his fifties, and below him were several men in their thirties, their facial features showing some resemblance to one another.","Dai Li pursed her lips.","Qin Shaozong frowned his long eyebrows almost imperceptibly.","Unaware of their subtle reactions, Qin Qinian called out to Dai Li with enthusiasm, \"Madam Dai, quickly see if that White Elephant is among them.\"","Turning his head, he ordered the Shang family, \"All of you, raise your heads.\"","As Dai Li walked past the Shang family members, Qin Shaozong turned and walked toward a nearby osmanthus tree.","The tree was planted in the front courtyard, standing about ten feet tall. The blooming season for osmanthus was usually in September and October. Now, in late autumn, clusters of maple-red osmanthus flowers still hung on the branches.","A hue slightly lighter than fire adorned the entire tree, with some blossoms scattered on the ground. However, perhaps due to the diligent sweeping of the servants, there were not many petals on the ground.","Qin Shaozong lowered his gaze and inspected the ground for a moment, finding no wagon ruts. He called Hu Bao over. \"Where is this family's donkey?\"","Hu Bao replied, \"It's kept in the donkey shed in the backyard.\"","Asking nothing more, Qin Shaozong strode toward the backyard shed.","After examining the members of the Shang family one by one, Dai Li finally stopped in front of a young woman with her hair styled in a married woman's bun. She asked, \"Did you hear a loud crash this afternoon?\"","The young woman, confused but honest, nodded. \"I did, noble lady.\"","\"That loud noise came from a collapsing house.\" Dai Li looked directly into her eyes. \"To get to the bottom of it, two groups of outsiders came here, specializing in murder and robbery. However, they didn't expect the house they were in to be in such disrepair. They accidentally brought disaster upon themselves, which exposed their whereabouts.\"","Upon hearing about murder and robbery, the young woman's face turned pale. Perhaps because they were both women, and Dai Li's gentle, storytelling-like voice made her forget her fear, she couldn't help but ask, \"Have those thieves been caught?\"","Dai Li nodded. \"They have been caught, but only one group. The other group is still hiding in the county. Those thieves are very smooth talkers, highly skilled at striking up relationships and then lodging in people's homes. Tonight's search is entirely to catch these thieves. In the past two months, have you had any distant relatives or good friends come to visit?\"","\"No,\" the woman shook her head.","Dai Li lowered her eyes, turned to the wide-eyed Qin Qinian nearby, and shook her head. \"It's not this household.\"","Her lie just now was not particularly clever, but the other party was an ordinary young wife. With the terrifying search happening tonight, she was bound to be flustered.","If this family had truly taken White Elephant and his men in, after she asked that last question, the woman would have instinctively looked toward the male head of the household.","Whether out of pure confusion or seeking some sort of support, she definitely would not have shaken her head immediately.","At this time, Qin Shaozong returned from the backyard. \"It's not here.\"","Qin Qinian looked at Dai Li, then at his father, scratching his head in confusion. He couldn't figure it out, but he followed the crowd and withdrew from the family's front courtyard.","Qin Shaozong walked over to Dai Li's small mare and supported her as she mounted. Only after she was seated securely did he turn his head and ask, \"Qin San, where is the other household?\"","Qin Qinian pointed the way. \"Over here, follow me!\"","...","Looking down from high above, one could see an agile fire snake slithering through the massive city. At a certain moment, the fire snake seemed to discover a delicacy also wrapped in flames; it opened its jaws wide, swallowed it, and thoroughly merged into one.","\"My Lord,\" Wei Qing, who was guarding the place, cupped his hands in greeting.","Qin Shaozong asked, \"Has there been any unusual activity here?\"","Wei Qing replied that there had not been.","This was also a three-courtyard residence. Inspecting an empty house was much more convenient. Past the main gate were covered corridors on both sides. The ends of the corridors connected to the side rooms, and behind the festooned gate was the entrance to the inner residence.","Dai Li observed as she walked, noticing that the house was quite clean and didn't seem like it had been vacant for long.","\"Qinian, how long has this house been vacant?\" Dai Li asked.","However, after she spoke, the youth did not reply.","Just as Dai Li was about to turn her head, she heard the man beside her say flatly, \"That boy just hurriedly took some men elsewhere. He's already sixteen, yet his temper is still so impulsive.\"","His distaste was evident in his words.","Suddenly, a flash of inspiration crossed Dai Li's mind. She sharply realized that this might be a good opportunity.","A perfect opportunity to lay some groundwork.","\"He's only sixteen. Where I come from, whether it's young ladies or young gentlemen, sixteen is still an age of innocence. They study with their teachers every day, and after class, they gather with friends to play. When they've had their fun, they return to their respective homes to eat.\" Since there were others following behind them, Dai Li kept her voice somewhat low.","The night wind blew past, making her gentle, water-like voice even more indistinct.","Qin Shaozong's eyes flickered slightly. He turned to Wei Qing behind him and said, \"Lead your men to inspect elsewhere. You don't need to follow us.\"","Wei Qing originally wanted to leave some men for Qin Shaozong, but seeing his superior wave his hand, signaling him to take everyone away, he obliged.","Once Wei Qing and the others had left, Qin Shaozong finally said, \"According to what Madam just said, could it be that the young women in your Peach Blossom Spring can also study?\"","\"Of course they can,\" Dai Li smiled. \"Men and women share the same classrooms and receive equal pay for equal work. Furthermore, as long as a woman meets the physical requirements and has the desire to do so, she can don armor and go to battle to protect the country and its people. Where I'm from, female soldiers are not uncommon.\"","Qin Shaozong subconsciously furrowed his long brows tightly.","Obviously, he found Dai Li's words difficult to comprehend, let alone agree with.","Men and women in the same classroom, equal pay for equal work, and even female soldiers?","How could a woman go to the battlefield? It was utterly absurd! Bathing in blood on the battlefield and defending the homeland was a man's duty.","If a man couldn't even protect his own wife and daughters, and needed them to personally don armor and go to war, he would truly be unworthy of heaven, earth, and his ancestors. What face would he have left to live in this world?","He might as well just slit his own throat."]},{"number":117,"title":"Chapter 117","paragraphs":["The three-courtyard mansion was brightly lit. Soldiers holding torches patrolled everywhere, searching room by room. The commotion was quite loud, making the originally central area seem somewhat quieter by contrast.","There was a moon tonight, hanging high in the sky. The soft moonlight fell on the roofs, the trees, and the people.","The moonlight stretched out shadows of varying lengths behind the two people walking side by side. Qin Shaozong cast his eyes down at the ground.","The shadows on the ground were solid and real, without the slightest hint of falsehood.","She was right beside him, within arm's reach.","Yet, the things she had described were scenes he could neither understand nor imagine.","Daili glanced at him sideways, not surprised by Qin Shaozong's current silence.","Anyone would be unsettled upon hearing such bizarre things that completely subverted their worldview. It was only because he was no longer an impulsive youth that he could suppress all his shock, doubt, and objections within.","He did not speak, and neither did Daili, giving him time to process it.","After a long while, Daili saw the man beside her shake his head. Madam, I cannot understand.","Daili said calmly, Qin Changgeng, power is something you fight for. When female soldiers put on armor and go into battle, are they not fighting for a voice? Only by rewriting national policies and laws can everything else follow. But here, women are never given a chance from the very beginning—no chance to study, no chance to become officials, no chance to join the army. Nothing at all.","Qin Shaozong's expression shifted slightly, deep in thought.","Daili continued, You cannot understand the ways of the Peach Blossom Spring, just as I cannot get used to this place. This is completely normal because our environments are different. Just as Mozi said: Dyed in pale silk, it becomes pale; dyed in yellow, it becomes yellow. As the dye changes, so does the color.","Qin Shaozong was about to say something when he suddenly heard someone shout from nearby, There's a secret passage here!","Both of their gazes sharpened, and they immediately followed the sound.","It was Wei Qing who had discovered the secret passage.","Perhaps because he was frequently suppressed, both openly and secretly, by the legitimate sons of the Wei family during his childhood, Wei Qing had learned how to hide from a young age. He would hide himself so that others could not find him, thereby suffering less bullying.","Having hidden so much, his experience was remarkably rich.","Among the four squad leaders of the Xuanxiao Cavalry, Wei Qing was particularly outstanding at treasure hunting.","Back when Qin Shaozong conquered Bingzhou and moved into the provincial governor's mansion, they had originally just conducted a routine confiscation of the enemy's storehouses. Unexpectedly, after walking around the mansion a few times, Wei Qing actually discovered a hidden vault.","The value of the treasures inside this hidden vault was more than ten times that of what was found on the surface.","...","In the back garden.","Seeing Qin Shaozong and Daili approach, the torch-bearing soldiers automatically parted to make way.","Wei Qing reported, My Lord, this rockery formation is quite ingenious. It is roughly composed of four interconnected rockeries, pieced together into a small maze. The light inside is dim, and the paths zigzag and intersect. If not for careful inspection, it would be truly easy to miss the hidden mechanism.","Qin Qinian rubbed his hands together eagerly. Father, that White Elephant character must be hiding inside. May your son lead men down to capture him?","Qin Shaozong agreed.","Qin Qinian entered the secret passage holding a saber in one hand and a torch in the other. Worried about potential mishaps, Wei Qing followed closely behind him.","The firelight seemed to transform into a fierce beast; the moment it entered, it violently devoured the surrounding darkness.","Huh.","Daili faintly heard a sound of confusion drift up.","Without needing anyone else to pass on the message, Qin Qinian called out himself, Father, it's really quite spacious in here!","Daili suddenly remembered something and hurriedly took a few steps toward the entrance of the passage. But before she could enter, her arm was suddenly grasped by a large, dark-skinned hand.","He didn't use much force, merely stopping her from moving forward.","Unable to enter, Daili simply stood outside and said, Qinian, beware of a dust explosion. If you see any flour, evacuate immediately.","Got it! came the reply from below.","Almost as soon as the words fell, the clashing sound of swords and sabers rang out from underground, along with Qin Qinian's fierce shout, White Elephant, cease your arrogance!","The sounds of fighting grew increasingly intense. Amidst the battle, Qin Qinian could be heard continuously unleashing a verbal assault. For as long as the clashing of weapons rang out, he kept cursing.","His voice was loud and full of energy, without a single pause for breath.","Daili: ...","Daili listened for a moment and couldn't help but turn her head, whispering to the man behind her, Your son's way of handling enemies is rather novel.","The torch-bearing soldiers stood behind Qin Shaozong. The man's face was shrouded in darkness, his brown eyes obscure, making his expression hard to read clearly.","Madam. He dropped the heavy word.","He didn't say much, but Daili knew exactly what he meant. This man particularly disliked hearing phrases like your son, which drew such a clear line between them.","Daili said no more.","*","Inside the passage below.","The passage connected to a small chamber, where Qin Qinian was ambushed the moment he arrived.","There were five people in total. Four were dressed ordinarily and were clearly older than the fifth, who was dressed in luxurious clothing.","The guards engaged the four men in a chaotic brawl, while Qin Qinian focused his attacks on their leader. The youth held a saber in one hand and a torch in the other, attacking the young man in black with both hands simultaneously.","Wei Qing did not join the fray. He stood outside the circle of combat, watching the fight intently and ready to support Qin Qinian at a moment's notice.","And the more he watched, the more surprised he became.","This young man in black looked young, but his skills were not weak at all. Moreover, his martial arts style... was very familiar.","After observing for a moment, Wei Qing's pupils contracted slightly.","He remembered now. It was indeed familiar, because it was exceptionally similar to Young Master Qin's!","Qin Qinian's strike failed, and he was fiercely blocked and pushed back. Using the momentum of his retreat, the youth deflected most of the force, then lunged forward, spun around, raised his knee, and twisted his hips, delivering a heavy kick like a rabbit kicking a falcon. Scoundrel, eat my kick!","This series of movements was incredibly fast; his retreat and advance were as quick as a flash of lightning.","The young man in black, holding a saber in his right hand, possessed equally astonishing speed and even seemed to anticipate Qin Qinian's moves. As the heavy kick flew toward him, he crossed his arms, stacking them to form a point of impact, and forcefully withstood Qin Qinian's heavy kick.","His lower body was extremely stable. After taking the blow, he merely swayed slightly, not even taking a single step back.","Alright, you really do have some skills. It's a pity that those who aid evildoers will meet a bad end! Qin Qinian's fighting spirit surged. He forcibly changed his posture in mid-air and swung the torch in his hand fiercely. Scoundrel, eat my club!","The torch traced an arc of light, spilling countless sparks from its edges.","The flames were truly scorching. As the young man in black dodged sideways, he abruptly thrust his saber forward, precisely slicing off the head of the torch. However, he didn't expect Qin Qinian to be using a diversionary tactic—drawing his attention with the torch on one side while sneakily striking with the saber on the other.","This slash was clean and decisive. Even though the opponent quickly sensed something was wrong and twisted his waist to avoid a vital strike, he was ultimately a little too late.","The blade cut into flesh.","Qin Qinian grinned broadly. Seeing my young age, you got careless, didn't you? Hahaha.","...","Daili listened to the clanging sounds below and Qin Qinian's non-repeating verbal barrage, unwittingly becoming engrossed. By the time she snapped out of it, she suddenly felt an itch on the back of her hand.","Daili subconsciously scratched it.","She scratched again and again, feeling something was wrong. She looked down, and well, a mosquito bite had swelled up on the back of her hand.","It was a huge one, bright red.","Daili pressed a cross shape into the mosquito bite with her fingernail, but it only helped for a moment. A short while later, it started itching again. Furrowing her delicate brows, she scratched it once more in irritation.","Before Dai Li could scratch a second time, her hand was grasped.","Qin Shaozong was tall with long limbs, and his palms were unusually broad. At this moment, he spread his fingers, wrapping them around Dai Li's delicate hand from below. He pressed his thumb against the swollen mosquito bite, slowly rubbing it for her.","There was a thick layer of calluses on his hand, making it quite rough.","In the past, Dai Li used to despise it, always feeling that his hands were no different from sandpaper. When he deliberately teased her, they could drive her absolutely crazy.","But at this moment, she felt that those thick calluses weren't entirely useless.","At least they felt very comfortable when rubbing a mosquito bite.","\"Qin San, speed it up,\" Qin Shaozong said to the people below.","He had called Qin Qinian's name, but Wei Qing, who had entered with the young man, instantly caught his superior's underlying meaning.","They couldn't delay any longer.","Abandoning his previous role as a bystander, he immediately joined the fray.","About fifteen minutes later, Dai Li heard footsteps coming up. Soon, Qin Qinian returned to the surface, dragging a young man in black clothes who was tightly bound with hemp rope.","The man was dressed in black, making it hard to tell the extent of his injuries, but the path he was dragged up left a heavy trail of blood.","\"White Elephant, behave yourself!\" Seeing the man still trying to struggle, Qin Qinian gave him a kick.","Behind them, Wei Qing and the others also came up, each holding a person in one hand. Among those four, three were dead. Counting the one in Qin Qinian's hands, there were two survivors in total.","\"Tossing and turning all night, we finally caught someone. You're quite cunning, White Elephant, actually hiding underground. You almost managed to escape!\" The more Qin Qinian spoke, the angrier he got, and he couldn't resist kicking him again.","If they hadn't learned about the Laimo Bookstore and the osmanthus petals on the carriage wheels from Miss Fan; if it wasn't for the curfew, with his father specially setting up investigative guards in every street and alley; if they hadn't had the right time, place, and people, there really would have been a risk of letting them slip away.","\"Winners are kings, losers are bandits. Having fallen into your hands, I have nothing to say. Kill me or torture me as you please.\" The man spat out a mouthful of fresh blood.","\"Kill or torture? Heh, before you truthfully confess all the secrets of the Green Lotus Cult, don't even think about a quick death.\" Qin Qinian hurriedly pulled out a piece of coarse cloth, casually crumpled it into a ball, and stuffed it into the man's mouth to prevent him from biting his tongue to commit suicide.","\"Except for the one in Qin San's hands, take the others over there,\" Qin Shaozong suddenly said.","Qin Qinian froze, instinctively looking at the one in front of him, and then at the ones in Wei Qing and the others' hands.","Was there any difference?","It was just the difference between being alive and dead. Oh, at most, one of them had a palm chopped off.","Wei Qing was as meticulous as a strand of hair. He noticed that ever since they came up, Dai Li had been keeping her head down. She only looked at the small patch of ground beneath her feet, not even glancing in their direction.","He understood in his heart. Carrying the dead man in his hand, he quickly moved to the side, retreating far enough away.","The bloody smell lingering around her nose faded a bit. Dai Li suppressed her discomfort and looked up at the man at Qin Qinian's feet.","The man was dressed in black, his limbs intact. At a quick glance, one could only see the bright red exposed after his black clothes were slashed, and nothing more. Dai Li let her gaze rest only on his face.","Two soldiers holding torches stood on either side, the firelight illuminating the man's face very clearly. A large wad of coarse cloth was stuffed in his mouth, the fabric stretching his cheeks out of shape.","At first glance, Dai Li let out a puzzled hum. She looked at him more carefully, from his temples to his brows and eyes, to his nose, then to his mouth, and finally to the overall contour of his face.","\"Qinian, pull out that piece of cloth first,\" Dai Li said.","The young man didn't understand why, but he did as he was told.","After the cloth was removed, the young man's bulging cheeks returned to normal. He suddenly looked up, locking eyes with Dai Li. \"What are you looking at?\"","The more Dai Li looked, the more solemn her expression became. \"There is no disguise on his face, yet his features bear no resemblance to Diting. It's not him; he's not White Elephant.\"","The young man's pupils shrank for a moment.","\"He's not White Elephant?\" Qin Qinian was greatly shocked.","He wasn't the only one astonished; Qin Shaozong, Wei Qing, and the others were all stunned.","They had never seen White Elephant, nor had they seen his twin brother Diting. They didn't know what these two looked like previously, only hearing from a young servant that they were very young.","And the young man in front of them certainly fit the description of being young.","\"Speak quickly, where is the real White Elephant?\" Qin Qinian placed his blade against the man's neck.","The young man laughed aloud, revealing a mouthful of bloody teeth. \"Mister left long ago. Why would he sit around waiting for death?\"","Qin Qinian was furious and was just about to make him suffer when he suddenly heard a gentle female voice say, \"No, I think White Elephant should still be here. They are just a smokescreen.\"","Dai Li said with certainty, \"From the time we got the clue from Miss Fan to throwing the net now, less than a day has passed. There's a curfew tonight, and there are both stationary sentries and patrolling guards on the streets. Even if they knew we were coming to arrest them, they would have nowhere to run. White Elephant must still be here!\"","Qin Shaozong turned his jade thumb ring. \"Wei Qing, go down and search carefully. Don't miss a single spot.\"","After these words, the tightly bound young man visibly struggled for a moment.","Qin Qinian noticed it and was both surprised and angry. \"He really is here. Fortunately, Madam Dai has sharp eyes, otherwise we would have been fooled by you.\"","About half a quarter of an hour after Wei Qing went down, the sounds of fighting came from below.","Qin Qinian grabbed his blade and hurried down. Soon, he was heard roaring, \"Ha, there really is one who slipped through the net! I advise you to surrender quickly, or else you'll have plenty of suffering ahead of you.\"","Dai Li looked at the dim entrance of the passage. \"I'll go down and take a look too.\"","\"Madam,\" Qin Shaozong's tone showed his disapproval.","Dai Li, however, felt very safe. \"They invested heavily in the smokescreen, and their combat power is already depleted by more than ninety percent. Plus, Qinian just said there's only one of him.\"","Just as she finished speaking, a figure was seen running out of the passage.","Who else could it be but Qin Qinian.","\"While we were fighting, he suddenly spat out black blood and lost the strength to fight. I suspect he took poison earlier. Father, this person is very valuable. Should we go invite Mr. Ding to save him?\" the young man said.","Qin Shaozong, however, said, \"Since he already had the resolve to die, how could the poison he took be ordinary? I'm afraid it's too late to notify Ding Congjian now.\"","The opponent must have been very clear about the intensity of the interrogations in the North. Rather than suffering endless physical torment, it was better to seek a quick end now.","Qin Qinian muttered something under his breath.","While the father and son were talking, Dai Li suddenly entered the passage.","Seeing this, Qin Shaozong immediately followed close behind her.","After walking past the initial section, Dai Li arrived at a small platform.","The place was a mess. A torch head had fallen to the ground and was still burning brightly. The space here wasn't large; it was oval-shaped, with some tables and chairs arranged. In one corner, there was an open hidden door, suggesting someone had just been hiding there.","A few steps away, Wei Qing and Hu Bao flanked a figure on the left and right, trapping him in a corner.","The young man leaned against the wall, his long sword sheathed. At this moment, the tip of the sword rested on the ground, seemingly serving as a support. He was dressed in black and had fair skin. There was black blood at the corner of his mouth, and dark red bloodstains could also be seen on his neck where it wasn't covered by his clothes, likely accidentally smeared when he was vomiting blood earlier.","The very first time Dai Li laid eyes on him, she thought she was looking at Diting.","This place was not far below the surface; words spoken above ground could easily be heard down below. Everything Dai Li had just said up there had fallen completely into Bai Xiang's ears.","The moment Dai Li saw him, Bai Xiang saw her too.","Their gazes met in the air.","Looking at Dai Li's delicate features, he suddenly chuckled. The resemblance is indeed there. My skills were inferior, and I made a wrong move. I have nothing to say about losing to you this time.","With that laugh, he coughed up another mouthful of black blood.","Dai Li clenched her fists tightly, forcing herself not to look away. Did they pick him up ten years ago, or was it after the great famine?","It wasn't that her son had never told her about the past, but she later realized that those ten years had been heavily sugarcoated.","Those ten years were the past, yet they were also a hurdle she could never get over.","Bai Xiang smiled and shook his head. Madam Dai, I know what else you want to ask... cough, but I can only tell you that my uncle truly treated him as his own nephew. Not only because Mingdeng had great potential, but even more so because he was a natural-born believer. He once said he wanted to go to a place where everyone was equal, and he was only ten years old when he said that.","Dai Li's pupils trembled slightly, and her eyes instantly turned red.","No, that wasn't it.","At that time, her Zhou Zhou only wanted to go home.","A large, dark-skinned hand reached up and covered Dai Li's eyes. Almost in the next instant, she heard a violent, earth-shattering fit of coughing, sounding as if the person were about to cough their lungs out.","The scent of blood suddenly grew much thicker."]},{"number":118,"title":"Chapter 118","paragraphs":["When Dai Li returned to the Qin Manor, the moon had already hidden behind thick, heavy clouds. Without the bright moonlight, the sky looked as though it had been splashed with thick, unblendable ink, not letting a single trace of light seep through.","The heavy veil of the night mirrored Dai Li's current mood.","Her goal for tonight had been clear, and she had only visited three places in total. Furthermore, her stay at the Shang family's residence in the middle had been very brief, so returning to the manor now, it wasn't particularly late.","It was not yet midnight.","Dai Li did not head straight back to the main courtyard. Instead, weighed down by her thoughts, she rode her horse over to her son's courtyard.","She didn't go inside; she merely stopped at the entrance and looked in.","The night was deep, and everyone in the courtyard had already gone to rest. It was pitch black inside, making it impossible to see anything.","A cool breeze brushed past, sweeping up a few withered leaves. The wind was picking up. Qin Shaozong said, Madam, the night is deep and the dew is heavy. Let us go back.","Dai Li let out a soft, faint sigh. Tugging at the reins, she turned her horse around and headed back.","...","Nianxia and Bipo had been waiting in the main room all along. Seeing the two return, one hurried to boil water while the other fetched fresh clothes.","By the time Dai Li finally lay down on her bed, more than an hour had passed. Midnight had arrived. If there had been a moon outside the window, it would have begun its descent to the west by now.","Dai Li had never been one to stay up late, and she usually slept quite well. But tonight, lying on the bed, she kept her eyes closed for a long time without falling asleep.","She rolled over, changing her position.","Still unable to sleep, she continued tossing and turning, trying other positions.","Upon her fifth time rolling over, a long arm reached out from beside her, scooping her up along with her blanket. Madam, you have been tossing about like a pancake on a griddle. Whatever are you doing? Are you planning to catch the early morning market tomorrow?","The plain bed curtains were drawn, leaving the inside of the canopy in total darkness.","Dai Li couldn't see Qin Shaozong, but the warm breath constantly brushing against her ear made the man's presence exceedingly strong.","The late autumn in the North was piercingly cold. In such weather, Dai Li needed two blankets to feel warm, but Qin Shaozong was naturally hot-blooded and found two blankets stifling.","Eventually, they compromised: Dai Li wrapped herself in a small blanket, and then they shared a larger blanket over the both of them.","Now, caught off guard and pulled into his embrace, Dai Li was still rolled up in her small blanket. He held her tightly, pressing down on the corners of the blanket so she couldn't even free her hands.","Unable to free her hands, Dai Li could only say, Qin Changgeng, I don't think I will be able to sleep for a while. Why don't we sleep separately?","White Elephant was dead, but the words he spoke before dying were like a knife, stabbing fiercely at her heart. That unhealed wound was oozing venomous blood once again, burning her so much that she couldn't sleep.","Perfect. I can't sleep either. How about we have a little late-night chat, Madam? Qin Shaozong did not let go.","The moment she heard him mention a late-night chat, Dai Li naturally recalled what she had told him before they set out: Can we talk about this when we get back? Now, they were back...","Dai Li shrank her neck, burying the lower half of her face into the small blanket wrapped around her.","It was pitch black inside the bed curtains, but with her in his arms, how could Qin Shaozong fail to feel her little movements? Immediately, a vein throbbed on his forehead.","He suddenly felt that no matter how cunning White Elephant had been tonight, or how close he had come to escaping, it was nothing compared to how infuriating she was right now.","But he couldn't scold her, nor could he speak harshly to her.","Qin Shaozong took a deep breath. Just a few words about the Peach Blossom Spring. What do you say, Madam?","He would forever be curious about that place, and he would forever want to know everything concerning her.","Hearing him mention the Peach Blossom Spring, Dai Li hesitated before slowly poking her head out. She was indeed feeling miserable inside, and the infected blood oozing from her wound needed an outlet.","Dai Li asked him, What do you want to know?","Earlier, White Elephant said that Qin Yanzhou wanted to go to a place where everyone is equal. That must have been referring to the Peach Blossom Spring. In that place you came from, are all beings truly equal? His tone was thick with skepticism.","Dai Li pondered for a moment. How should I put it... Although social classes still exist, there are officials in charge of governance and ordinary people who just focus on their own lives, on the surface, everyone is the same. The commoners don't have to kneel when they see officials, nor do they have to refer to themselves as this humble commoner or this slave. The officials where I come from are called public servants of the people.","Those last few words struck Qin Shaozong as incredibly novel.","Public servants of the people?","They are officials, yet also servants.","However, Qin Shaozong quickly caught on to her other words. He mused, On the surface. That implies it isn't so in the shadows.","Dai Li: ...","Dai Li retorted with dissatisfaction, But it is still far better than here! Besides, everything is a process. Did iron tools exist from the very beginning? Taking a step further back, did bronze vessels just fall out of the sky out of nowhere? Didn't humanity first learn to use stones, and then learn to make fire? Then, step by step, they discovered natural copper ore, which eventually led to the smelting of bronze.","Qin Shaozong sighed in admiration, Heaven and Earth are the parents of all things; humanity is the soul of all things.","The corner of Dai Li's mouth twitched. She thought to herself that this man could truly never focus on the right point.","Take the essence and discard the dross. While I can't say the Peach Blossom Spring is perfect in every aspect, it genuinely ensures that every household has surplus food. You could say it has achieved tens of thousands of mansions to shelter all the poor scholars of the world, making them beam with joy. The threshold for education has also been lowered infinitely, and you can travel freely from one end of the world to the other.","A dark gleam flashed through Dai Li's eyes. Even marriage is about staying together if you get along, and parting ways if you don't. A man and a woman living together as husband and wife, if the woman feels the marriage can no longer continue, she can go to the government office to apply for a divorce and dissolve her marital ties with her husband. The same goes for the man. Both parties have this right.","...And in the Peach Blossom Spring, there is no such thing as the orders of parents and the words of matchmakers. Parents can only give their children advice; the final decision ultimately rests with the individual. Being so close to him, a steady stream of warmth radiated over to her, like having an electric blanket turned on to the perfect temperature. Dai Li comfortably narrowed her eyes.","Hearing this to the end, Qin Shaozong couldn't hold back a remark: Absurd.","Dai Li wasn't surprised by his reaction. What is absurd about it? Is blind marriage something to be proud of?","Qin Shaozong said in a deep voice, Marriage is not merely an affair between two people; it is a matter between two families. When two clans forge an alliance through marriage, it serves as both a support and an alliance for the future. If they later face life-or-death situations, or scenarios involving power struggles, this marital connection becomes a formidable support, perhaps even a lifesaving straw.","Dai Li sighed inwardly once again. The gap between her mindset and Qin Shaozong's was as wide as the Mariana Trench.","It wasn't just a difference in eras, but also a difference in social class. It was the meticulous calculation of someone who, having acquired privilege, deliberately sought to protect that privilege for the next generation.","From a macroscopic perspective, such things spanned across ancient and modern times and were not uncommon. After all, marriage alliances truly could concentrate, and even further expand, wealth and power.","But regarding the issue of parents having the absolute final say, Dai Li still had to refute him. Qin Changgeng, you have to understand that children who receive good guidance from their parents generally won't have terrible taste in partners. They won't end up falling for some unsavory character. But speaking solely of blind marriages, if you have absolutely no idea what kind of person the other party is before marrying them, and then you are thrown together to live your lives... not to mention the lack of mutual love, what if your living habits and values completely clash? Wouldn't you just become a resentful couple? You wouldn't even be able to treat each other with basic respect; you would just spend the rest of your lives tormenting each other. Why put yourselves through that?","I don't know which part of those words struck a nerve with Qin Shaozong, but he suddenly reacted strongly. The man had originally just been holding her, but now his arms tightened abruptly.","Dai Li felt as if she were entangled by a giant python, squeezed so hard through the quilt that it actually hurt a little.","The small quilt only wrapped around her hands, leaving her legs free. Dai Li immediately gave him a kick under the covers. \"A gentleman uses his words, not his fists. Just because you can't out-argue me doesn't mean you can get physical.\"","This man was highly active and had a well-defined, muscular physique; his whole body was incredibly solid. Dai Li kicked him on the calf. She didn't know if it hurt him, but her own toes certainly throbbed from the impact.","Qin Shaozong was already lying on his side. Taking advantage of Dai Li's kick, he clamped his legs together, trapping her foot between his calves.","With her lower half immobilized and her hands trapped by the small quilt, Dai Li couldn't break free. \"Qin Changgeng!\"","\"Did you choose your late husband yourself, Madam?\" he suddenly asked.","Hearing the words \"late husband,\" Dai Li thought for a moment that she had been careless earlier and accidentally let something slip.","She quickly sifted through her memories and realized she hadn't. From beginning to end, she had only ever told him that she and her husband had a conflict and separated because of it.","So right now, Qin Shaozong calling him her \"late husband\" was purely him being venomous and cursing the man.","Dai Li: \"...\"","\"He is living perfectly fine somewhere else. Qin Changgeng, don't talk nonsense.\" Dai Li believed that since she and Zhouzhou could wake up somewhere else, perhaps... Qin Zheyu could too.","Qin Shaozong gritted his back teeth. \"Defending him so fiercely... it seems he was.\"","\"The general environment is different, what's so strange about that?\" Dai Li continued. \"Where I come from, if you have feelings for someone, you can pursue them. If the pursuit is successful, the two become a couple. In this relationship, both parties interact and compromise further, learning about each other's hobbies, living habits, and family backgrounds. Some couples even live together; all of this is preparation for eventual marriage.\"","Every word Dai Li spoke was like a bolt of lightning. In Qin Shaozong's understanding, lightning bolts struck one after another, the thunder deafening.","The dim darkness inside the bed curtain washed over his rarely exposed emotions like a tide.","After a long while, Dai Li finally heard him say:","\"Utterly absurd!\"","These words were crushed to pieces between his teeth before being squeezed out.","Dai Li couldn't help but roll her eyes.","Earlier it was \"absurd,\" and now it was \"utterly absurd.\" It seemed he had upgraded to the comparative degree—no, the superlative degree.","Dai Li snorted softly. \"It's not absurd. Getting along before marriage is very important. If you find out you're not compatible, you can cut your losses in time and find someone else. It's good for both parties.\"","\"There is no rain without clouds in the sky, and no marriage without a matchmaker on earth. Living together so rashly, how is this any different from an illicit affair without a matchmaker?\" Qin Shaozong strongly disapproved.","The moment his phrase \"illicit affair without a matchmaker\" came out, Dai Li felt as if she could smell a decaying, suffocating stench of feudalism. His words left her dizzy and exasperated.","Dai Li grew furious listening to him, her tone becoming much heavier. \"Marriage is solemn, how can it be treated as a game? A couple is just a couple; usually, they only raise children together after becoming husband and wife. Qin Changgeng, you and I grew up in different environments for over thirty years. I can't explain this to you clearly. I can't change your mindset, and similarly, you can't change mine.\"","After saying this, Dai Li used her free foot to kick him, pushing against his solid calf. \"Let go.\"","Qin Shaozong didn't move. His breathing was rapid and heavy, as if a ball of roaring flames was churning and burning in his chest, only to be forcefully suppressed just as it was about to erupt.","Dai Li heard him take a deep breath and then slowly exhale.","After a long while, that heavy breathing gradually calmed down. \"Fine, let's put that aside for now. Tell me about something else, Madam.\"","Since he had calmed down on his own, Dai Li didn't add fuel to the fire. After their brief argument, the pent-up frustration in her chest seemed to have dissipated a bit, so she asked casually, \"What else do you want to hear?\"","\"Tell me about your late husband, Madam. How was his family background? Was he also in the military?\" His tone was very calm, even a bit flat.","But the word \"also\" in his sentence made Dai Li's eyelids twitch.","Why was this man asking this? Was his competitive spirit acting up?","\"The Peach Blossom Spring is very peaceful. At least the area where I lived hadn't seen war for decades. In such an environment where people live and work in peace, a hundred industries bloom, and every profession produces its own master. Therefore, many people don't take the military path,\" Dai Li said carefully.","As for his first question, she skipped it.","Qin Shaozong slightly raised an eyebrow and pressed further, \"If he wasn't in the military, then what did he do?\"","This man was getting to the bottom of things, acting as if he wouldn't rest tonight until he got an answer. Dai Li could only say, \"Didn't I mention before that traveling from south to north, if you ride the iron-forged 'Quru,' you can make a round trip in a single day? He used to be responsible for driving that 'Quru'.\"","Qin Shaozong fell silent for a moment before suddenly dropping a meaningful sentence, \"So he was a coachman.\"","Dai Li: \"...\""]},{"number":119,"title":"Chapter 119","paragraphs":["When a person is speechless to a certain extent, they really just want to laugh.","Dai Li sneered, \"Do you think being a captain is that easy? Strictly speaking, if you, Qin Changgeng, went to the selection, you would be eliminated in the first round.\"","\"Absolutely impossible. If he can be one, why can't I?\" Qin Shaozong said without a second thought.","Dai Li: \"Pilot recruitment is extremely strict. With your body full of scars, you couldn't be a pilot.\"","Qin Shaozong didn't understand what \"captain,\" \"pilot recruitment,\" and \"pilot\" meant, but that didn't stop him from understanding that his scars were the reason.","If it were anything else, he would definitely argue. But to a man who bathed in blood and killed enemies on the battlefield, scars were nothing less than medals of honor.","Thus, Qin Shaozong remained unfazed.","He said slowly, \"So he wasn't an official. I thought my wife would marry an official.\"","As someone in power, Qin Shaozong knew well that power could only be concentrated in the hands of a few administrators. Those who entered officialdom would ultimately be different from the common people, regardless of whether they served the country and the people, or corrupted the nation and harmed its citizens.","Dai Li was pulled into her memories by his words, unable to help but recall the past.","Actually, it wasn't that she didn't have the chance. It was just that after carefully weighing the pros and cons, she eventually gave up.","Back in her junior year of college, she had her third boyfriend, who was also her senior at the time. Only later did she find out that his family background was incredibly good, almost beyond her expectations.","He was an only child, and both his parents were civil servants. His father was in a department with real power, and his uncle's family ran a massive business. As for himself, he secured a job in a great unit right after graduation, strictly following in his father's footsteps. If he had a first major hurdle in life, it was probably... her.","He was dead set on marrying her, but his family unanimously opposed it. His domineering parents agreed that her background was too complicated and that she wouldn't be able to help their son's career.","Even though her boyfriend was very determined at the time—even putting on an attitude of fighting the whole world and refusing to marry anyone but her.","But she was tired.","She was exhausted by his relatives constantly seeking her out in secret, saying things that seemed peaceful but actually hid needles in the cotton. She was also keenly aware that if they really got married, as an only child, he could never completely cut ties with his family.","Unless it involved a necessary turning point in her destiny, she never compromised herself. Therefore, she initiated a breakup with this senior, the one she had chosen from a crowd of suitors and the one who suited her heart the most.","It was a cliff-like breakup; they broke up three times before it was truly over.","Although she later heard from friends about how he couldn't forget her, Dai Li never regretted her decision.","If it wasn't a good fit, it meant they weren't fated.","Life, after all, held many other possibilities.","Qin Shaozong astutely sensed that Dai Li's silence was somewhat unusual. He couldn't help but call out, \"Madam.\"","His voice wasn't loud, but in the quiet night, it was impossible not to hear.","Yet she didn't react, as if she were zoning out, her soul having drifted off to heaven knows where. Qin Shaozong instantly thought of her previous remarks about \"cutting losses in time,\" his brow twitching as a sudden guess formed in his mind.","She had said that being lovers didn't equate to marriage.","Could it be that before she married the biological father of that boy Qin Yanzhou, she had another man?","Perhaps, even more than one.","This fox had eight hundred schemes in her heart. She was the best at assessing situations, always wanting to slip away at the slightest sign of trouble. If the general environment of Peach Blossom Spring was so... unique, it was highly likely she had been picking and choosing.","After all, even a man holding great power like him, she looked down upon. If he hadn't held onto her so tightly, she would have run off to who knows where to live a carefree life long ago.","Qin Shaozong's face gradually darkened.","Dai Li pulled back her thoughts, unaware that the person beside her had let his imagination run wild. She just felt that his earlier remark, tinged with hypocritical regret, was very punchable.","How could the officials here be the same as those in later generations?","So Dai Li said, \"Here, you enter officialdom through the system of recommendation for filial piety and incorruptibility. This path is basically monopolized by the aristocratic groups. If the father is an official, through some maneuvering, the son can inherit his father's career. In their thirties, or even twenties, they can hold official positions with real power.\"","Take Qin Shaozong himself, for example. He went to the battlefield in his teens, and when he received the title of Marquis of Wu'an bestowed by the imperial court, he hadn't even reached his thirties.","This path paved with military merit was very swift. But putting aside this dangerous route, he could have also taken the path of inheritance, inheriting the official position of his father, who was the Governor of Youzhou at the time.","Don't talk about it being non-compliant. As long as the local tyrant Qin family was strong enough, he was the local emperor of the region. Not to mention that nowadays the sovereign was weak and the ministers were strong, and the imperial court's control over the local areas was almost non-existent.","Qin Shaozong hummed in agreement, acknowledging that what she said was a fact. He wanted to say something else, but was struck by a different kind of curiosity. \"Madam, doesn't Peach Blossom Spring select officials through recommendation?\"","Dai Li: \"Of course not. The recommendation system overly emphasizes moral character, but their actual governing ability remains to be seen. The probability of producing incompetents is very high. But Peach Blossom Spring is different. There is a very complete and rigorous system there, and everything is determined by exam scores. Whether you come from an aristocratic family or a commoner's home, as long as you want to enter officialdom, you have to take an exam. Only by relying on real talent and practical knowledge can one be selected based on merit.\"","Pausing for a moment, Dai Li added, \"Of course, because the procedures are complicated and the population is large, promotions are not very fast.\"","At the very least, you couldn't find a single man in the modern world like Qin Shaozong, who had firmly grasped the entire northern region before even reaching the age of forty.","Qin Shaozong let out a chuckle, a mix of sarcasm and smugness. \"I personally think that your last sentence is the most important.\"","Dai Li: \"...\"","\"You'd better have only heard the last sentence.\" Dai Li mimicked his sarcastic tone, and then used her other foot to kick his calf. \"I'm going to sleep. Qin Changgeng, let go of me.\"","\"Really sleeping? You're not going to keep tossing and turning like a pancake?\" Qin Shaozong released her leg.","Like a swimming fish, Dai Li pulled her leg back. Without answering his question, she rolled over to face away from him and buried her head to sleep.","Perhaps because they had just bickered a little, the pent-up frustration in her chest had found an outlet. Dai Li fell asleep much faster than expected, soon sinking into a deep slumber.","She was fast asleep, but the man beside her had lost all sleepiness and could even be described as fully energized.","Dai Li's recent words churned in Qin Shaozong's mind.","He chewed over every sentence over and over again, repeatedly refining them, until they were forged into a massive, nascent mace that smashed open the stubborn rock covering his mind above.","A brand-new, unprecedented, brilliant radiance fell into his eyes.","Everything is determined by exam scores.","Aristocrats and commoners are screened layer by layer, with the superior winning and the inferior eliminated. Appointing people solely on merit, fishing for talents from the lowest impoverished families.","That night, Qin Shaozong didn't sleep for a single quarter of an hour. Before dawn, he got up for his morning practice and then entered the study.","Everyone was very busy today.","Ding Luying was busy extracting the Gu worm, while Qin Shaozong, Nalan Zhi, and the other advisors stayed behind closed doors in the study. Wei Qing and several garrison chiefs led a team to the prominent families in the commandery, secretly searching among them for a servant with a black mole on the side of his neck.","Qin Qinian led men to post notices to reassure the public; Mo Yanyun was ordered to interrogate the survivors captured last night.","Some proceeded steadily, some were still ongoing, and some ended in disappointment.","Meanwhile.","After Qin Hongying and her daughter Shi Rongyue entered the manor, they resided together in another courtyard.","Last night, Qin Shaozong personally led troops out to make arrests, causing quite a commotion. Qin Hongying guessed that something major had happened in the commandery, but she wasn't worried in the slightest.","Her second brother had braved the wind and rain and seen all kinds of storms; he would definitely be able to handle it well. Right now, she was more concerned about other things—for instance, her daughter, who was sporting dark circles under her eyes.","The young girl sat opposite her eating breakfast. Her porcelain spoon stirred the porridge several times back and forth, but she hesitated to bring it to her mouth.","Qin Hongying's heart ached over her daughter's brush with danger yesterday. \"Rongrong, how about going to Doctor Ding for some soothing medicine after breakfast? You can take it and get a good sleep.\"","Shi Rongyue slowly shook her head. \"Mother, I'm fine.\"","Qin Hongying's thoughts turned a thousand times before she finally decided to cut the Gordian knot. \"Rongrong, there is something Mother needs to tell you in advance. There has been a change in your marriage arrangement.\"","Shi Rongyue was scooping her porridge. Hearing this, she raised her head listlessly. \"What change? Did something happen to the Zheng family that forces a delay?\"","If an elder in the family passed away, the younger generation would have to observe a mourning period.","\"No. Your second uncle had someone cancel your marriage to the young master of the Zheng family,\" Qin Hongying said.","\"Clang—\"","The porcelain spoon in Shi Rongyue's hand dropped into the bowl.","The meat porridge in the small bowl splashed out, and a little bit landed on the back of Shi Rongyue's hand.","The porridge had been stirred many times earlier and had long lost its original heat, leaving only a sticky, thick consistency.","\"S-Second Uncle had it canceled?\" Shi Rongyue was stunned. She stuttered slightly before finding her voice. \"Why would Second Uncle...\"","\"He said he wants you to marry back into our family,\" Qin Hongying spoke openly with her daughter.","There was nothing to hide about this matter. Her daughter had already reached the coming-of-age and was no longer a babbling toddler. Moreover, it was better to tell her early so she could mentally prepare herself and start cultivating feelings with Qinian sooner.","Qin Hongying stroked her chin. \"I guess he wants to marry you to Qinian. Although there is an order of seniority, you know Yunce's situation, not to mention his health has never been robust. He suffered a severe illness last winter and still hasn't fully recovered.\"","Speaking behind closed doors with her own daughter sitting opposite her, Qin Hongying spoke from the bottom of her heart: \"He is your biological uncle, and he certainly wouldn't bear to see you end up with a sickly husband. Qinian is the same age as you. Even though he had an arranged marriage since childhood and is currently somewhat entangled with the Wei family, based on my understanding of your second uncle, since he has been frequently letting the Wei family visit recently, he must be plotting something.\"","This was also something Qin Hongying had pondered for a long time before she finally discerned a different meaning—","Her second brother probably wanted to take a wife!","Otherwise, why would he feign illness, make her come to Yuyang, and secretly put pressure on the Wei family?","This time, as he handled his old promises, he would most likely resolve Qinian's childhood engagement as well.","Qin Hongying continued to her daughter, \"Rongrong, you were born into the Shi family of Nanyu. The Shi family has many military generals and was highly valued by your maternal grandfather in the past, and I am the biological sister of the Marquis of Wu'an. If you marry Qinian, the Shi family will become his wife's clan. With the Wei family's daughter having passed away from illness many years ago, we can completely suppress the Wei family. Now that your second uncle has taken charge and canceled the marriage between the Shi and Zheng families, I guess he should be paving the way for your younger cousin.\"","Yunce was sickly and weak; in terms of military achievements, he was inferior to Qinian. Furthermore, Yunce was her eldest brother's son. If the succession passed to Yunce...","Well, it wasn't impossible.","Her second brother had never been able to let go of what happened back then, always feeling it was his responsibility. Over the years, he had treated Yunce like his own son. As long as Yunce didn't acknowledge her eldest brother as his father when he reached adulthood, Yunce also had a great possibility of succeeding the title.","However, privately, Qin Hongying felt that her younger nephew had the biggest chance.","\"...Rongrong, you can interact more with your younger cousin on regular days.\" Qin Hongying had said quite a bit.","After finishing, she was startled to realize that her daughter was spacing out.","Blank and dazed, she seemed to have not yet recovered her senses. Her expression was a bit strange, and it was unknown where her thoughts had drifted.","\"Knock, knock—\"","Qin Hongying curled her fingers and tapped the tabletop.","\"Rongrong, did you hear clearly what I just told you?\"","\"Mother, when Second Uncle said he wanted me to marry back, did he specifically mention my younger cousin?\"","Two voices sounded at the same time.","Seeing that her daughter was listening, Qin Hongying's brows relaxed slightly. \"That he didn't. But your second uncle only has your younger cousin as his biological son, so he will inevitably plan more for him. You definitely won't go wrong listening to Mother. In all these years, when has your mother ever misjudged anything?\"","The young girl let out an \"mm,\" lowered her head to take a handkerchief, and slowly wiped away the specks of porridge on the back of her hand.","\"Actually, it's best for you to marry Qinian. I've watched that child Qinian grow up. Although his temper is a bit rash, he is ultimately reliable and responsible. His looks aren't bad either; he's a good husband.\" The more Qin Hongying spoke, the more satisfied she became.","Shi Rongyue kept her head down; her thoughts had been wandering for a while now."]},{"number":120,"title":"Chapter 120","paragraphs":["The study.","Mo Yanyun hurried inside. As soon as he entered the study, he blurted out, \"Bad news, My Lord.\"","Inside the study, besides Qin Shaozong and Nalan Zhi, there were two other men.","Both were dressed in the square hats and loose robes typical of scholars. One had just passed his thirties, with clear features and a handsome appearance. The other was older than Nalan Zhi, thin as a crane, with a long beard reaching his chest and bright eyes that concealed a sharp inner light.","The older man was from the prominent Cui clan of Hedong; his name was Cui Shengping, courtesy name Haiqing. It was said that when he was born, the Emperor of Han was committing absurd acts. His father, worried about the country and its people, angrily named his son Shengping, taking the last two words of a phrase meaning singing and dancing in celebration of peace, as a form of mockery.","The younger man did not come from a prestigious family. His name was Sheng Ran, courtesy name Zhongliang, and he had joined the Northern Army by chance.","\"...My Lord, during the interrogation just now, those two captives suddenly spat out black blood, tilted their necks, and died. I had specifically checked their teeth after catching them and kept them under strict guard,\" Mo Yanyun said, feeling utterly frustrated.","It had been hard enough to catch them, especially since they were Bai Xiang's trusted aides. They must have known a lot of things, but in less than a day, both of them were dead.","Hearing his subordinate's report, the man sitting behind the desk did not even twitch a brow; he simply turned his head to look out the window.","Outside the window, the sunlight was perfect, casting bright dappled shadows beneath the trees. It was now afternoon, and several hours had passed since the curfew was lifted and the city gates were opened.","Assuming the real Bai Xiang was not found last night, he could have left the city by now or moved to another inn within the commandery. By cutting off this lead in the afternoon, even if they noticed something, they would have lost the opportunity and never be able to catch him again.","Those people were abandoned pawns from the very beginning.","\"It was to be expected. If they are dead, so be it. Interrogate that fat shopkeeper; he might know quite a bit,\" Qin Shaozong said calmly.","As if remembering something, Qin Shaozong added, \"A merchant surnamed Zhao in the east of the city has visited the Laimo Bookstore several times. Have someone investigate him as well.\"","Mo Yanyun cupped his hands and accepted the order.","After he left, the few men returned to their previous topic.","Cui Shengping continued, \"My Lord, selecting talent through examinations is indeed highly promising. However, I personally believe this method is not suitable for implementation in the North for the time being. The Emperor of Han is still on the throne, and all new policies should be issued by the imperial court to be fully justified.\"","He stood up, bowed deeply to Qin Shaozong, and said solemnly, \"If the North raises its own banner, it will be easy for those with ulterior motives to make a fuss about it, perhaps even rallying other provinces to crusade against the disloyal. Therefore, I believe we should wait on this matter.\"","What they were waiting for, Cui Shengping did not explicitly say, but everyone present knew.","They were waiting for Qin Shaozong to ascend the throne and take that supreme position.","Sheng Ran pondered for a moment, truly reluctant to give up such a novel selection method. \"My Lord, why do we not try another approach, pretending to advance along one path while secretly taking another? Nowadays, all the great warlords are widely recruiting talents, and some even keep three thousand retainers. Many people have come to serve you before, but because they failed to meet your requirements, they all returned in defeat. This time, we can leak word to the public that we are recruiting a teacher for the Third Young Master Qin, thereby attracting talented scholars from all over the world to the North.\"","Anyone who paid even the slightest attention to current affairs knew that the Marquis of Wu'an in the North was extremely generous.","Whether it was the military generals who followed him into battle or the strategists who plotted behind the scenes, as long as he recognized them, they would receive many rewards every time they rendered meritorious service. These rewards were not limited to money and jewels, houses and servants, or fertile land and fine horses.","Such high treatment naturally attracted many famous scholars. Unfortunately, the Lord had high standards and was a very opinionated person himself, so very few could catch his eye.","Therefore, compared to the military generals, the number of people in his brain trust was pitifully small.","Nalan Zhi nodded. \"Zhongliang's method is worth a try. Tell the world that you are recruiting a teacher for the Third Young Master, and let it be known that you do not require someone who knows everything about astronomy and geography, as long as they excel in a specific field. When they arrive, we can test them specifically on the field they claim to be good at. If they are deemed suitable in the end, we can keep them and let them become pillars of that field in the future.\"","The Lord's ambitions would absolutely not stop at the North. When he ushered in a new era in the future, given the current state of impoverished people and exhausted resources, a hundred things would be waiting to be rebuilt.","Just taking the rivers that flooded from time to time as an example, someone would definitely need to be sent to control the waters then.","But where would the talents for water control come from? If they did not start gathering them now, they would inevitably be caught in a panic when the time came.","Qin Shaozong spun the jade thumb ring on his finger. \"It is indeed worth a try.\"","The few of them engaged in a more detailed discussion regarding this aspect. By the time the matter was basically finalized, the warm glow of the setting sun had quietly slipped into the room through the window.","\"...Let us slightly change the public excuse. Make it that we are recruiting teachers for all three: Qin Yunce, Qin Yanzhou, and Qin Qinian,\" Qin Shaozong said finally.","Nalan Zhi was slightly stunned.","Unless special circumstances occurred, a disciple would only call one person Master in his lifetime. This was the so-called principle of a teacher for a day is a father for a lifetime.","And the recruitment of teachers that Qin Shaozong just mentioned was for collective teaching, one teacher to multiple students, which was the model used in academies.","These two did not conflict.","But after having a Master, going to an academy was not impossible, but it had to be clearly discussed with the Master himself.","After all, eating at one house and suddenly smelling the food from another house, then silently taking your bowl to eat at the other house was inappropriate both in reason and in sentiment.","\"It is just a cover. Wugong, would you mind?\" Qin Shaozong looked at Nalan Zhi.","Sheng Ran was the youngest among them. Hearing Qin Shaozong's words, he hurriedly lowered his eyes to hide the astonishment within them.","Since the Lord had spoken to this extent, how could he, Nalan Wugong, possibly say he would mind?","Qin Yanzhou.","He had heard this boy's name many times, and each time shocked him more than the last.","First, the Lord acted as a middleman to have him take Nalan Wugong as his master. Then, he dispatched troops all over the country to collect medicinal herbs for him. Now, this boy's name was even added to this cover story.","The fact that the Eldest Young Master Qin recognized the Lord as his father had spread throughout the world. The Third Young Master Qin went without saying, as he was the Lord's biological son. Inserting Qin Yanzhou in the middle was clearly a subtle announcement to the world that this suddenly appearing Qin child was also his heir.","Nalan Zhi shook his head and said he would not mind.","Seeing this, Qin Shaozong smiled. \"I thought so too. Wugong, you are the most open-minded and would not fuss over such trivial matters. Furthermore, the idea of selecting talents through examinations was first proposed by Madam, so by both reason and sentiment, we cannot leave Qin Yanzhou out.\"","\"It was actually Madam Dai who proposed it first?\" Cui Shengping was astonished.","Nalan Zhi immediately smiled. \"She has always possessed extraordinary abilities. South of the Great Dipper, she stands alone.\"","Qin Shaozong nodded gladly. \"Indeed.\"","Cui Shengping and Sheng Ran exchanged a glance, both seeing deep thought and solemnity in each other's eyes.","\"My Lord, I heard that you had people renovate the Marquis's mansion. Please forgive my presumption, but are you planning to take a wife?\" Cui Shengping asked.","What he mentioned was renovate.","But anyone with discerning eyes could see that he was picking the smallest detail out of Qin Shaozong's many affairs to speak of.","Qin Shaozong did not deny it. \"I am indeed planning to.\"","Cui Shengping stared intently. He did not need to ask to know who his lord wanted to marry. My Lord, if you marry Lady Dai, what about Qin Yanzhou...","Naturally, he will have to call me father, Qin Shaozong cut him off.","He said it as a matter of course, making Cui Shengping's heart skip a beat.","My Lord... he wanted to say more.","But Qin Shaozong stood up from his seat, clearly indicating that the conversation was over. It is getting late. You should all go back and have your evening meal. If it gets any later, you will have to eat by lamplight.","Leaving these words behind, Qin Shaozong strode out of the study.","Three people remained in the study. After Qin Shaozong left, Nalan Zhi also got up and walked out.","Only two were left. Sheng Ran lowered his voice, Looking at our Lord's recent actions, that young master Qin will likely be treated no differently than his own sons in the future. He is older than the Third Young Master and looks about the same age as the Eldest Young Master, though I do not know his exact age. If he is older than the Eldest...","He did not finish, but Cui Shengping understood. So what if our Lord marries Lady Dai in the future? Even if Lady Dai possesses world-shaking talents, she does not come from a prestigious family; she is alone and lacks support. Young Master Qin does not have the Qin family bloodline, nor does he have a powerful wife's family backing him. The rule of succession by the eldest legitimate son will never apply to him. No matter how much our Lord plans for him now, his prospects are limited.","Sheng Ran hesitated a little. Are we certain that Young Master Qin is not of the Qin bloodline?","Young Master Qin was just about to reach adulthood. Counting backward, that would mean he was conceived nearly twenty years ago.","At that time, their Lord had indeed left the North, and the timeline barely fit. But given their Lord's cautious nature, he would absolutely not have produced an illegitimate eldest son before his legitimate heir was born.","Besides, Young Master Qin did not look like their Lord.","He could not possibly be their Lord's flesh and blood!","Cui Shengping shook his head and said, He shouldn't be. If he were our Lord's biological son, why would our Lord say what he just did? If he could call him father now, why wait until then?","Let us just wait and see.","...","The two chatted in low voices for a few more moments before leaving one after the other. Neither noticed a burly figure standing just outside the wall.","The study was guarded by personal guards. If an ordinary person lingered there, they would surely be questioned or driven away. But the man standing there was Qin Shaozong, the master of the entire North. Naturally, the guards would not step forward to disturb him.","There were windows on the east, west, and north sides of the study. Right now, only the east and west windows were open.","For an ordinary person, with the people inside lowering their voices and the nearby window closed, they certainly would not be able to hear a thing.","However, Qin Shaozong was no ordinary man. Those muffled yet discernible words drifted into his ears, and he heard every single one.","However long Sheng Ran and Cui Shengping talked inside, Qin Shaozong stood outside listening.","After the two left, he waited a moment longer before stepping out from behind the wall.","Qin Shaozong had not intentionally sneaked back to eavesdrop. He had been walking away when he suddenly realized he had forgotten something, which was why he returned to the study.","Hearing Cui and Sheng's conversation was a complete accident.","The man walked into the study with a calm expression. He took a thick stack of paper from a cabinet, fetched a brush, ink, and inkstone, packed them into a small cloth bag, and finally left.","There were only two days left until the Beginning of Winter. The closer it got to winter, the earlier the sky grew dark.","Qin Yanzhou was still undergoing treatment and stayed behind closed doors, not coming to the main hall for dinner. Qin Yunce and Qin Qinian did not come either today, not because anything happened to the brothers, but simply because they were ordered to eat on their own.","Tonight, only Dai Li and Qin Shaozong were at the dinner table.","As the weather turned colder, they were once again having hot pot.","The two sat facing each other across a table. A small stove was set up in the middle, surrounded by various meats and vegetables neatly arranged on small plates. A jug of wine rested by Qin Shaozong's hand.","The broth in the small stove was boiling, bubbling merrily, a perfect match for the dish's ancient name.","Without the younger generation present, Qin Shaozong was visibly more relaxed. Wielding his jade chopsticks, he fished a plump shrimp ball out of the hot broth, dipped it into a sauce bowl, and placed it into Dai Li's bowl.","Now that you have learned how to ride a horse, my lady, how about I take you hunting some day? Qin Shaozong knew she was from the South. Once winter sets in and the snow falls, the trees and the ground will be covered in white. It is stunningly beautiful. Moreover, the birds and beasts all store fat for the winter, making them incredibly plump and delicious.","Hunting... Dai Li's interest was piqued.","The modern world had its modern pastimes, and the ancient world had its own forms of entertainment.","Su Shi's famous poem about hunting, with lines like yellow hound on the left, falcon on the right and shooting the tiger to show the prowess of Sun, was well-known to later generations.","However, in her modern world, there were strict restrictions on hunting, and one could easily commit the crime of illegal poaching.","Therefore, even though Dai Li had tried scuba diving, skydiving, and surfing growing up, she had never gone hunting.","Seeing her keen interest, Qin Shaozong chuckled. There are tigers roaming the area east of Yuyang. Once I finish up a few matters at hand, I will hunt a tiger to make a winter cloak for you, my lady."]},{"number":121,"title":"Chapter 121","paragraphs":["A tiger?","Daili's first reaction was that Qin Shaozong had drank too much, spouting nonsense and making empty boasts under the influence of alcohol.","It was true that there was a saying, \"Watch Master Sun shoot the tiger himself,\" but the phrase implied a resolution rather than an accomplished fact. Besides, that was a tiger, the king of the forest. How could one simply hunt it down on a whim?","How could Qin Shaozong fail to see Daili's suspicion? His temples throbbed slightly. \"Does Madam not believe me? It's not as if I haven't successfully hunted a tiger before.\"","Daili remained silent, merely picking up a shrimp ball and eating it with slow, deliberate chews, offering no answer to whether she believed him or not. Her thick, dark eyelashes fluttered up occasionally, revealing obvious skepticism in her eyes.","\"How about Madam makes a bet with me? We'll bet on whether I can hunt down a tiger this year,\" Qin Shaozong suddenly proposed.","She didn't answer immediately, and Qin Shaozong didn't rush her, simply sitting opposite and watching her.","The woman's snow-white cheeks puffed out slightly, only subsiding after several rounds of chewing. A sudden itch arose at the tips of Qin Shaozong's fingers, an itch that seemed to morph into an invisible little snake, opening its mouth to bite his fingertip.","The fingertips connected to the meridians of his arm, causing the man's long arm to tremble imperceptibly. He rubbed his heavily calloused index finger and thumb together fiercely, quietly wearing away that strange sensation.","Daili swallowed the shrimp ball in her mouth. \"Alright, let's make a bet. But since it's a bet, there must be stakes.\"","Qin Shaozong raised his eyebrows slightly. \"Listening to Madam's tone, it seems you have already thought of the stakes.\"","Daili nodded. \"Of course. We bet on whether you can hunt a tiger. During the hunt, it doesn't matter if someone assists you, but you are not allowed to cheat, which includes but is not limited to bringing in a half-dead tiger beforehand, or preparing the spoils in advance...\"","Hearing this, he scoffed. \"It's just hunting a tiger. Why would I need to cheat?\"","Daili smiled as well, the corners of her eyes lifting in a sly little arc. \"The loser must promise the winner one thing, no matter what it is.\"","Upon hearing her last few words, Qin Shaozong immediately frowned. She had a notorious track record with far too many prior offenses. He unhesitatingly said no.","This \"no\" was loud and resolute, and Daili restrained her smile upon hearing it.","Qin Shaozong clicked his tongue softly. \"Madam has a habit of burning bridges after crossing them, followed by a hobby of going off to tour the mountains and waters without a word. Moreover, in another two days, that boy Qin Yanzhou will be recovered from his illness. How can you expect me to agree to 'no matter what it is'?\"","Daili naturally knew he was unwilling to let her go. She hid the sharp gleam in her eyes. \"We won't bet on whether I can tour the mountains and waters, nor will it involve any of your political affairs. That should be acceptable, right?\"","Qin Shaozong didn't immediately say whether it was acceptable. He picked up the wine cup by his hand, not draining it in one quick gulp, but sipping it slowly.","Various speculations surfaced and then vanished in his mind.","When the cup of wine was finished, the man set down the goblet.","The goblet clinked gently against the low table, and at the same time, Daili heard a deep \"Alright.\"","He had agreed.","Daili raised her smile again. \"No matter how many days the winter hunt is held, the time you can personally take the field—that is, the time you can hunt the tiger—is only one daylight period. Deal?\"","Not one day, but one daylight period.","In winter, the days are short and the nights are long. Strictly speaking, this daylight period was less than half a day. If this winter hunt was held on a grander scale, such as inviting the prominent families of Yuyang Commandery to participate together, some formalities would inevitably be indispensable.","All of those would take up time.","Qin Shaozong paused.","Her appearance and tone made her look exactly like a fox happily wagging its tail while digging a pit for him.","Seeing him silent, Daili began to flatter him. \"Everyone says the Marquis of Wu'an is both wise and brave, with unmatched valor, shining like the sun and illuminating the spring and autumn of the North. It's merely a tiger; how could it possibly stump you?\"","Qin Shaozong's Adam's apple bobbed up and down, the veins on the side of his neck bulging and then receding.","Seeing that he still wasn't speaking, Daili's eyes suddenly darted around, seemingly filled with invisible little hooks. \"Was what I just said correct, Husband?\"","His brown eyes tightened for a moment. The itch he had just wiped away returned with a vengeance, surging and swelling, spreading like wildfire from his arms to his spine, and then to his four limbs and hundreds of bones, making every single hair on Qin Shaozong's body tremble with excitement.","\"Indeed, it is correct,\" Qin Shaozong's voice grew a bit huskier.","Daili was quite satisfied. \"Then it's settled.\"","The gaze from across the table was burning, wrapping around her like fire. Daili was used to this kind of look and calmly continued picking up meat to eat.","By the time they were halfway through this meal of hot pot, the sky had turned completely dark. After finishing their meal, considering what had just transpired, Daili thought that, as usual, this man would lead her to the bed.","But today, he did not.","Several lamps were lit in the room, their bright glow illuminating the impeccably clean sandalwood table, bringing out a lustrous, oily wooden sheen.","Seeing Daili about to head towards the soft couch by the window, Qin Shaozong said to her, \"Madam, come here.\"","Daili merely turned her head, not going over immediately at first, until she saw the man pull out a bag from somewhere and take several items out of it one by one.","She saw a brush, ink, paper, and an inkstone.","What was this person doing?","Daili walked over. And when she drew near, she realized that what was on the desk was actually a marriage certificate.","The earliest marriage certificates appeared in the Zhou Dynasty, written on bamboo slips and issued by the Matchmaker Official, the person specifically in charge of managing marriages between men and women. Thus, in later generations, those who tied the red thread of marriage for others were also called matchmakers.","The Great Yan Dynasty considered the marriage certificate and the betrothal gifts as the conditions for establishing a marriage.","The general procedure was that the man's side would first deliver a Proposal Letter to the woman's side. If the woman agreed, she would write a Reply Letter in response. They would exchange each other's letters and attach a separate paper containing detailed information about both families.","Only when these three items were combined did they form an official marriage certificate.","Qin Shaozong's parents had already passed away, and it went without saying for Daili. Her only relative now was Qin Yanzhou, but it was absolutely impossible to let a junior handle such a matter.","Therefore, both the Proposal Letter and the Reply Letter were to be written by the two of them themselves.","Daili lowered her eyes, her gaze falling on the red paper, the texture of which was clearly much better than ordinary mulberry paper.","The Proposal Letter spread out on the desk was basically complete; only the date of the engagement remained.","\"I'm afraid it's too late to get married this year. We will set the wedding for next spring. What does Madam think?\" Qin Shaozong began to grind the ink.","Marriage required the Three Letters and Six Etiquettes. The more noble the family, the more complicated the process. It was only because Daili had no other clan members that some steps were simplified, saving a lot of time; otherwise, even next spring would be pushing it.","But Daili still felt it was fast. \"So soon?\"","Qin Shaozong's movements paused. \"Oh? Then how should the marriage process in your Peach Blossom Spring go?\"","Daili was speechless.","It was even faster. One just had to walk into the Civil Affairs Bureau, spend a little money on photos, and they could get married.","Daili had no expression on her face, but Qin Shaozong could tell at a glance. He let out a soft chuckle. \"It seems it's not as complicated as here.\"","\"Then let it be spring. The Beginning of Spring is an auspicious day; the wedding date is set for the Beginning of Spring.\" He made the final decision, then dipped his brush in ink and filled in the date on the Proposal Letter.","\"This is my first time writing a marriage proposal. I hope Madam will kindly accept it.\" The Proposal Letter was handed over.","Daili paused for a moment before finally taking it.","She stood opposite Qin Shaozong. Just a moment ago, this Betrothal Letter had been upside down from her perspective, but now it was turned right side up as it was handed to her.","It read:","A joyous day today, as the red thread ties our destinies, a perfect union of pearls and jade; forecasting the years to come, playing the lute and zither in harmony, flying wing to wing. Waiting until the seas dry up and the rocks decay, until the end of time, I shall walk hand in hand with you until our hair turns white.","Changgeng of the Qin clan takes this oath as a witness, earnestly beseeching Madam Dai Li to marry me as my wife on the Beginning of Spring in the 365th year of Yongqing.","I humbly wish Madam joy, peace, and good health.","This Betrothal Letter was not long; including the initial title, it was less than a hundred words. But every single character was profoundly powerful, not only in the forceful strokes that penetrated the paper, but also in the sheer power of the words themselves.","Dai Li's eyelashes fluttered slightly.","Her son was still undergoing treatment. Where could she run off to?","As for after Zhouzhou recovered, she seemed to have nowhere else to go either.","No, it wasn't that she had nowhere to go, but that she simply couldn't leave.","Back when she was abducted by the Green Lotus Sect, that had been the best opportunity to escape. With the Green Lotus Sect acting as a smokescreen, Qin Shaozong would have only searched for the sect members, never suspecting she had already shed her cicada shell and slipped away.","Now, without that cover, she and Zhouzhou were right in Yuyang Commandery, the very core of the northern territories. It was even more impossible to leave.","Dai Li heard a long, drawn-out sigh in her own heart.","\"Qin Changgeng, there is one thing I must make clear to you beforehand. If you feel it is inappropriate or impossible to achieve, then we can save ourselves the trouble of the Three Letters and Six Etiquettes and the wedding ceremony. We can just cancel it all.\" The ink on the marriage letter was not yet dry, so she couldn't fold it. Dai Li placed it back onto the desk.","Her tone was very flat, but Qin Shaozong could hear an unyielding persistence in it.","He set down his wolf-hair brush. \"Please speak your mind, Madam.\"","\"In the laws of Peach Blossom Spring, a married couple is just that—a couple. It is a monogamous system. There is no such thing as taking a concubine. In fact, regardless of whether one is a man or a woman, marrying multiple people is a violation of the law against bigamy. I know this is worlds apart from the Great Yan Dynasty, and I am well aware that you nobles are accustomed to having a courtyard full of beautiful women.\" At this point, Dai Li deliberately paused.","He did not speak, merely listening quietly.","Only then did Dai Li continue, \"But what others do is their business, it has nothing to do with me, and I cannot control them. However, my man must listen to me on this matter, otherwise, he is not fit to be my husband. Qin Changgeng, do you understand what I mean?\"","Qin Shaozong was both surprised and unsurprised.","He was surprised by the novelty of the marital customs in Peach Blossom Spring, but unsurprised that her previous husband had only had her.","Although this little fox knew how to assess a situation and was exceptionally good at pretending to be obedient, she was not without her pride. Her arrogance would never allow her to share a husband with anyone else.","\"The Marquis's estate has been cleared out. As for that Concubine Li you saw earlier, Madam Wei specially brought her over from elsewhere,\" Qin Shaozong said calmly.","When he said \"Concubine Li,\" Dai Li froze for a moment before realizing he meant Wei Pingzhi.","Recalling Wei Pingzhi showing up at her door, Dai Li asked, \"Where did you move them to?\"","Qin Shaozong leaned back into his cushioned chair, adding a touch of languor to his demeanor. \"I gave them money and houses, and let them go wherever they pleased. The current dynasty encourages women to remarry, and there are many wealthy men in Yuyang. They won't have to worry about finding a place to go.\"","After saying this, the man gestured toward the paper and brush on the desk. \"The Letter of Consent, Madam. If you please.\"","He had given his Betrothal Letter, and he wanted a Letter of Consent right away.","But Dai Li said, \"I won't give it to you that quickly.\"","Hearing this, Qin Shaozong knitted his long brows. \"Why?\"","Dai Li remained expressionless. \"...No reason.\"","She couldn't exactly tell him that she didn't know how to write a Letter of Consent.","But to Qin Shaozong's ears, this sounded like reluctance. Reluctance to write the Letter of Consent immediately, and reluctance to tell him why.","The man, who had been leaning against the soft seat, straightened up. \"Madam...\"","He had barely called out to her when he saw Dai Li neatly fold the Betrothal Letter on the desk, its ink now dry, and walk into the inner room without looking back.","Qin Shaozong stood up and followed her inside. \"Madam, if I cannot have this Letter of Consent today, then when will I have it?\"","\"We'll see,\" her answer sounded quite perfunctory.","The lamps in the inner room burned quietly, dragging their silhouettes onto the floor, and the shadow that entered second swiftly closed the distance to the one in front.","Beside the mirror stand was a multi-tiered wooden box. Most of it was used to store Dai Li's various pieces of jewelry, with one or two sparse compartments reserved for miscellaneous items.","Dai Li pulled open the top tier, first taking out a small pouch from the compartment, then placing the marriage letter inside, and finally pressing it down with the little pouch.","Just as she turned around, Dai Li bumped right into Qin Shaozong's chest.","The man stood firmly in place, raising his arms to naturally pull her into his embrace.","A wave of seething heat descended from above. Dai Li was enveloped in his shadow, with the hard edge of the table behind her and him right in front of her.","His back was to the lamp, so the light could only reflect from the other candlesticks to the side. The man's facial contours were sharp, his brow bone deep-set. Those narrow brown eyes resting on either side of the bridge of his nose seemed to become two pools of different colors in this moment.","One pool deep, one pool shallow, and both held her reflection. He said, \"Give me an exact time, Madam.\"","Dai Li was in a daze for a split second. She slowly lowered her eyes. \"I will give it to you after the winter hunt.\""]},{"number":122,"title":"Chapter 122","paragraphs":["Qin Shaozong's brows smoothed out, only to furrow once again.","The winter hunt?","Why wait until the winter hunt?","Recalling their recent bet, Qin Shaozong could not help but think of the promise the loser had to make to the winner.","The man's face darkened slightly as he laid it out plainly for her. Madam, the Marriage Proposal has already been sent out. As for the Betrothal Reply, you do not necessarily have to write it yourself. I can do it on your behalf.","The underlying meaning of his words was clear: whether there was a Betrothal Reply or not, she had to marry him.","Dai Li reached out and pressed her hands against his chest. Although his words were outrageously absurd, upon careful thought, they were not entirely surprising.","This man was completely unreasonable at times. She sighed helplessly, I know.","Qin Shaozong's brows relaxed. The long arm wrapped around her waist suddenly exerted force, lifting Dai Li up slightly. At the same time, his other hand swept down beneath her legs to support her.","Dai Li was suddenly suspended in the air before quickly landing on something solid; she was now sitting on the vanity table.","Sitting there, she was slightly taller than Qin Shaozong. His arms rested on either side of her, the base of his thumbs pressing against the outer sides of her legs. An endless stream of heat radiated over, carrying an indescribable, scorching intensity.","Dai Li looked up at him. Her current position made her a bit taller than him, giving her a downward vantage point. My Lord, what do you want now?","This insincere \"My Lord\" sounded somewhat piercing to the ear.","Caught off guard by the prick, Qin Shaozong laughed in exasperation. Madam, that is not how you addressed me just a moment ago.","He reached out and pinched her red lips, catching Dai Li's upper and lower lips between two fingers and squeezing lightly, forming them into a duck's beak. What you called me earlier, say it again for me to hear.","Dai Li knew he was fixated on the \"Husband\" she had uttered earlier. She turned her head to dodge his hand and jabbed at him with her words, Please mind your manners, My Lord. Do not go too far, lest you chill the hearts of your strategists.","There are even worse things. Would Madam care to try? Qin Shaozong said, not waiting for her reply.","He tilted Dai Li's chin up and skillfully parted her lips. The man's other hand wrapped around the back of her head, pressing her down so he could push in deeper, carefully plundering every inch of softness within her mouth.","A breeze swept past, rustling the lamps in the room and causing the flames to flicker.","The light danced, and the two tightly intertwined shadows on the floor shifted in depth. She and he were locked together, like two adjacent trees in an ancient forest, their vines inextricably intertwined.","The apricot-colored outer garment drifted down like a falling leaf. Under the flickering candlelight, a large expanse of snow-white skin was dazzling to the eye. It swayed slightly, rising and falling, measured inch by inch by lips and teeth, leaving behind a trail of vibrant marks.","The bronze mirror reflected a graceful figure with half-faded clothing. The apricot garment pooled around her waist like clouds, making it seem as if she were sinking into them.","The night was still very long.","Yuyang, the Wei Manor.","A servant rushed into the study, opening with, Master, disaster has struck! causing the several people inside to stiffen instinctively.","What has happened now? Wei Congmu rubbed his temples in a headache.","The third brother, Wei Congsen, said, Does Wei Qing have more demands? As long as it is not too excessive, try to satisfy him so he can finish his search and withdraw his troops quickly.","A day ago, the Xuanxiao Cavalry suddenly visited the major prominent families in the commandery, claiming that a group of assassins who had attempted to murder the Marquis of Wu'an were colluding with a certain family, and after failing, had hidden in one of their estates.","The Xuanxiao Cavalry were unlike ordinary soldiers. They were the sharpest blade in Qin Shaozong's hands and, to a certain extent, represented his personal will.","When the Xuanxiao Cavalry arrived, the prominent families were alarmed. Hearing they were there to catch assassins, they naturally would not turn them away.","A straight foot need not fear a crooked shoe; if they wanted to search, let them.","Every family opened their doors. The Wei family could not afford to be the exception, so they immediately welcomed the Xuanxiao Cavalry inside.","However, with Qin Shaozong having previously instructed the Cai family to suppress them, the Wei father and sons felt an inexplicable unease. This unease reached its peak when they learned that the Laimo Bookstore had been sealed off, and the shopkeeper and servants had all been imprisoned.","The Laimo Bookstore...","They did indeed have some ties to this bookstore. The other party had once sent someone to inform the Wei family:","The Marquis of Wu'an's injury was fake, and the Cai family's series of actions were all under his instruction, aimed at taking back his original promise and paving the way for him to take a wife in the future.","The Wei family was shocked and hurriedly notified the married Fifth Lady Wei. This was what led to Wei Cheng taking Wei Pingzhi to visit the Qin Manor as a test.","Well, regardless of everything that happened before.","In short, after learning that the Laimo Bookstore had been sealed, the Wei men were on pins and needles. And right at this critical juncture, the Xuanxiao Cavalry brought men to search their manor.","Feeling guilty and wanting to take precautions, they hid the trusted aide who had gone to the Laimo Bookstore to deliver messages.","However, because the Wei family did not immediately learn of the bookstore's incident, their subsequent hiding of the man was a beat too late. The aide could only hide within the manor, unable to break through the blockade formed by the Xuanxiao Cavalry outside.","Master, Wei... Wei Changsheng has been found, the servant said.","The Wei father and sons all shuddered, a loud buzz ringing in their heads.","Wei Congmu shot up from his seat. How could he be found? Was he not hidden away!","The servant looked miserable. That Garrison Commander Wei searched incredibly thoroughly, as if he had a third eye. He did not miss a single nook or cranny. Later, he even brought in a few women specifically to search the madams' rooms.","Father Wei nearly choked on a mouthful of old blood.","Where is he? Where is Wei Changsheng? Wei Congmu asked anxiously.","He... he was taken away...","The study instantly fell dead silent.","Father Wei's expression cycled through several changes before he seemed to age over a decade in an instant. Eldest, take that jade ring to the Marquis of Wu'an. Tell him that Feiniang has been gone for over fifteen years, which is long enough. If he meets the right person, there is no harm in him remarrying. He does not need to be constrained by past promises.","Father!","Father!","Wei Congmu and Wei Congsen cried out at the same time.","We cannot return the token. If we do, the Wei and Qin families will inevitably become estranged.","Yes, Father, this token cannot be returned! If we give it back now, the Marquis of Wu'an might just take a wife by next spring.","Father Wei's sagging face twisted into a cold sneer. The Marquis's estate has been undergoing renovations for a while now. Did you really think Qin Changgeng was just fixing it up for fun? Everyone in the Laimo Bookstore has been arrested. Since he could find Wei Changsheng, do you think there might be someone among the captives who recognizes him?","The two brothers looked at each other in dismay.","The person who tipped off our Wei family never revealed their true identity, but for the Marquis of Wu'an to go to such lengths to catch them, they must be extraordinary, and are very likely seen as a thorn in his side. I worry he suspects us of secretly colluding with the mastermind behind the bookstore. This was what Father Wei feared the most, and what he felt most wronged by.","He let out a long sigh, and it seemed as if most of his vitality left him with that breath. Everything Qin Changgeng has done clearly points toward him wanting to take a wife. He is not someone who gives up until his goal is achieved. Even if we dodge this time, there might well be a next time.","This token simply had to be returned.","Standing under someone else's eaves, one has no choice but to bow one's head.","Ultimately, the North belongs to the Qin family. Without military power, how could the Wei family truly go against the Qin clan?","Wei Congmu could not bear to see his father in such a dejected state and comforted him, \"Father, Qinian is your grandson. This is something that will never change no matter what.\"","Wei Congsen also said, \"Exactly, and Qinian is his only biological son. In the future, won't the Marquis of Wu'an's immense estate be handed over to Qinian? When Qinian succeeds and takes the helm, the Wei family will surely rise to a higher level.\"","These words struck a chord in Father Wei's heart. His complexion immediately improved. \"That is true. Let Yue'er and Dai'er interact more with Qinian from now on.\"","The Qin Residence.","\"My Lord, Chief Clerk Wei requests an audience. He says he has an important item to return.\"","When Hu Bao came to report, Qin Shaozong was reading the interrogation records.","The merchant surnamed Zhao from the east of the city had been brought back. It was unknown whether he had caught wind of it beforehand or simply could not endure hardship and decided to be a wise man who submits to circumstances. Before any real torture was applied, the man confessed everything like spilling beans.","He had joined the Green Lotus Sect three years ago while traveling south for business. It was not a long time, and he had previously been acting as a deputy to the fat shopkeeper. Even if the latter gritted his teeth and refused to confess, by following Merchant Zhao's lead, they could still pull up the radish and bring out the mud to uncover the whole network.","Qin Shaozong understood the underlying meaning and immediately smiled. \"Entertain Chief Clerk Wei well. My wife and I will be there shortly.\"","Dai Li, who was reading by the window, was baffled. \"The Wei family came looking for you. If you want to go, just go. Why drag me into it?\"","Qin Shaozong did not give a specific reason, only saying, \"Just this once.\"","Dai Li pursed her lips and said nothing.","He added, \"Old Mister Ding said it was a three-day treatment course. Today, by the end of the Shen hour, that boy Qin Yanzhou will finish his treatment. Until then, since you are just idling about, my lady, you might as well take a trip with me to pass the time.\"","Today was the third day of Qin Yanzhou's seclusion. If nothing unexpected happened, near dusk today, that door which had been closed for so long would finally open.","Dai Li was also certain there would be no accidents, because every day Ding Lianxi would come to report on his grandfather's orders, letting her know that everything was going smoothly.","\"Alright then.\" Dai Li put down the book in her hands.","Dai Li had specially styled her hair into a bun today, her dark hair coiled into a falling-horse chignon. Pinned to the bun was a gold-inlaid jade butterfly hairpin, and on the other side was a golden-winged phoenix holding a pearl step-shake, with hanging beads dangling from it.","The hanging beads were exceptionally round, each a beautiful bright white and almost identical in size. One glance was enough to tell that this step-shake was no ordinary item.","As Dai Li stood up, the hem of her Hunan-red skirt slid over her calves like water, like a bright ray of sunlight sweeping past.","She and Qin Shaozong left the main room together.","...","The Main Hall.","The servants served tea to Wei Congmu, but the latter had no mind to drink it at all, frequently looking toward the side corridor.","Time seemed to stretch infinitely at this moment, making him extremely anxious. It felt as if a full hour had passed, or perhaps only half an hour, before Wei Congmu heard footsteps.","Two sets of sounds, one light and one heavy.","Soon, two figures turned out from the side corridor side by side. One was burly and imposing, wearing a black robe and a military official's grand hat, with an aura as heavy as a mountain.","The other was much more petite compared to the man, but could be considered tall among ordinary young women. She had a blooming, radiant complexion and a graceful figure. Her Hunan-red long dress was dignified and elegant, yet carried a hint of restrained gorgeousness.","It was Wei Congmu's first time seeing Dai Li. He had previously heard that the Lady Dai by the Marquis of Wu'an's side was a beauty straight out of a painting, possessing the looks of a moon goddess and monopolizing all charm.","That was why the Marquis of Wu'an was so infatuated with her that he did not even live in the Marquis's estate anymore, choosing to live outside with her.","To be honest, Wei Congmu did not believe it.","What kind of person was he, Qin Changgeng? Having fought battles north and south all these years, what kind of beauty had he not seen? How could he be bewitched to the point of losing his mind? Could it be that the so-called favored concubine Lady Dai was just a front to cover up a deeper motive?","But at this moment, ninety percent of the doubts in Wei Congmu's mind vanished.","As bright as the morning sun rising through the rosy clouds, as dazzling as a lotus emerging from clear waters.","This Lady Dai was indeed a beauty in a million. No wonder...","\"Chief Clerk Wei,\" a deep voice came from above.","Wei Congmu suddenly snapped back to his senses, hurriedly lowered his head, and then looked up at Qin Shaozong, bowing deeply to him. \"This humble official pays respects to the Lord. Please forgive my abrupt visit to your residence.\"","Qin Shaozong walked down from the seat of honor and personally helped him up. \"The Chief Clerk comes visiting with a generous gift. In no way can the word abrupt apply.\"","Hearing generous gift, Wei Congmu could not help but twitch the corner of his mouth, knowing in his heart that Qin Shaozong was giving him absolutely no chance to back down.","He felt stifled in his heart, but still had to say, \"My Lord is mistaken. How can that be considered a generous gift? It is inherently an item of the Qin family, and today it is merely being returned to its rightful owner.\"","After speaking, Wei Congmu turned around and offered the brocade box he had brought with both hands.","Qin Shaozong took it, and not only did he take it, but he also opened it to look.","The gold clasp was flicked up, and this magnificent sandalwood box with carvings on all four sides was opened. Inside the box lay a piece of gorgeous red cloth, and resting quietly on the cloth was a Hetian jade ring with an exceptionally lustrous hue.","The word for ring sounds the same as the word for return, symbolizing the continuation of a relationship and implying a beautiful reunion.","This top-quality jade ring had quite a background. Counting carefully, it could be traced back to Qin Shaozong's great-great-grandfather's generation. It was a betrothal gift given by his great-great-grandfather to his great-great-grandmother, and then it was passed down to the eldest legitimate son of each generation to be given to his wife upon marriage.","Qin Shaozong was the second son in the family. Initially, this jade ring had nothing to do with him and was kept by his eldest brother and sister-in-law.","But later, the Qin family met with a disaster, and his brother and sister-in-law passed away together. This jade ring briefly came into Qin Shaozong's hands and was soon sent to the Wei family along with his promise.","After fifteen years of twisting and turning, it had finally returned to Qin Shaozong's hands.","However, it did not stay with him for too long either.","Qin Shaozong took a few glances, and after confirming there were no mistakes, he raised his hand and pulled off the pouch hanging at Dai Li's waist beside him.","Then, amidst Wei Congmu's shocked expression, he tied this Qin family token as a jade pendant to Dai Li's waist.","Dai Li: \"?\""]},{"number":123,"title":"Chapter 123","paragraphs":["Dai Li didn't know the origin of this Hetian jade ring, nor did she know what it meant.","But she wasn't blind, she could see the gorgeous box containing the treasure, and she could also see Wei Congmu's tightened, slightly trembling pupils and the unconcealable shock on his face at this time.","Dai Li looked down at the jade ring, picked up the lanyard and plucked it with her long fingers. The jade ring turned, and it could be seen that it was flawless, delicate and oily, as if it was condensed from milk fat.","It was indeed a rare treasure.","Dai Li's hand rested on the knot of the jade ring, vaguely aware that Qin Shaozong's peripheral vision was looking at her.","Not long ago, she accepted his \"Marriage Certificate\", okay, it's not much worse.","Dai Li withdrew her hand.","The curve of Qin Shaozong's lips deepened a bit, and he continued to deal with Wei Congmu in front of him.","Wei Congmu tried hard to put away the shock on his face, pulled out a stiff smile, and some polite words had to be said: \"Time flies, before I know it, Feiniang has been dead for fifteen years. The road ahead is very long, how can you be trapped in the past and live a depressed life? My father asked me to return the jade ring, hoping that you will find a beautiful woman in the future and stay with her until your hair turns white.\"","Qin Shaozong's smile became a bit more genuine, \"Thank your father for his good words for me.\"","The big stone in Wei Congmu's heart fell, the foundation was laid, and he turned to talk about other things, \"I heard that recently there are some petty thieves causing trouble in the county, and it seems that they are in cahoots with the people in Laimo Bookstore. A few days ago, under my order, my family slaves went to the bookstore a few times, and they must have talked with them. But I can swear that the Wei family is loyal to the North and has absolutely no second thoughts.\"","Qin Shaozong said \"hmm\" and didn't immediately answer.","With his attitude, the huge stone that Wei Congmu had just moved away pressed back.","What does Marquis Wu'an mean? Does he not believe him?","Dai Li glanced at Qin Shaozong, feeling that this person was probably holding back some trick.","As the in-laws of the Qin family, the Wei family couldn't possibly not know that Qin Shaozong himself deeply hated the sect. And the hotter the Qin family was, the less necessary it was for them to take risks and do things like pulling hair on a tiger's head.","\"That boy Qin San is not young anymore, it's time to start a family. Your father is also getting old, there is a saying 'People over sixty, four don't think', you go back and tell him that Qin San's marriage doesn't need his old man to worry about.\" Qin Shaozong said so.","Wei Congmu was taken aback, and then his expression changed drastically.","Marquis Wu'an not only wanted to get back the token, but also wanted to solve his son's matter together.","Wei Congmu opened his mouth to speak, but heard Qin Shaozong say: \"The Chief Clerk just said that the Wei family has no second thoughts about the North, how is this loyalty after all? I'll wait and see.\"","Speaking of the end, it was already a vague threat.","A servant of the Wei family was taken away not long ago, and his life or death is unknown now, and it is unknown whether he was forced to confess anything.","Obedience is loyalty. Disobedience is treason.","It's all in their thoughts.","...","Wei Congmu left absent-mindedly.","Dai Li sighed a lot, \"Qin Changgeng, you are really good at taking advantage of the fire.\"","Qin Shaozong had a half-smile, \"Madam, you are wrong.\"","Dai Li originally thought he would refute the unpleasant title of \"taking advantage of the fire\", but unexpectedly he said: \"I set the fire, not taking advantage of the situation. This time is to invite the Lord into the urn, an eye for an eye, and also complete a karma of the year.\"","Dai Li: \"...\"","This person is actually proud of it.","\"So Madam should know that my memory is very good.\" He changed his tone, \"Remember to give me Madam's 'Reply to Marriage Certificate' after the winter hunt.\"","With a bet ahead, Qin Shaozong always felt uneasy if he couldn't get her \"Reply to Marriage Certificate\".","Dai Li got up and walked in, \"Got it.\"","He followed, \"Madam has broken her promises too many times in the past, making me always feel that this 'got it' carries no weight.\"","\"Oh? Since you think it carries no weight, then let it go, just pretend I didn't say it.\" Dai Li didn't look back.","But as soon as she said this, her arm was clasped, an irresistible force pushed her, forcibly turning her around.","Previously facing away from Qin Shaozong, now she and he were face to face, and were blocked against the wall of the side corridor. Those slaves who served in the main hall did not enter the side corridor, and at this time there were only the two of them in the corridor.","His brown eyes were heavy, seemingly displeased, \"If Madam breaks her promise...\"","Dai Li raised her eyebrows, \"Then what?\"","In more than an hour, Zhou Zhou's treatment would be over. To put it bluntly, medicinal materials were no longer a threat, and her son could go anywhere in the world.","There was a bit of provocation in her eyes, and a bit of pride, as if that invisible fox tail was cocked up.","Qin Shaozong felt like his heart was scratched by a small paw, a bit itchy, and a bit crisp. He picked up a few uncoiled broken hairs from her temples and poked her soft cheeks, \"Madam take back that sentence just now.\"","Dai Li went against him, pursed her lips and said nothing, the provocation in her eyes became stronger.","Qin Shaozong lightly clicked his tongue when he saw this, \"Okay, since Madam insists on asking what to do, it's not impossible to tell you, of course...\"","He bent down slightly, close to Dai Li's ear, and finished the second half of the dirty talk.","Dai Li became numb.","At this time, out of the corner of her eye, she suddenly caught a glimpse of something. Dai Li subconsciously turned her head to look, only to see Qin Qinian and Shi Rongyue standing at the other end of the corridor.","The cousins both had their mouths slightly open, with a sluggish expression.","Dai Li: \"...\"","Just listening to Qin Shaozong's dirty talk, Dai Li didn't blush, after all, this person not only had many tricks on the bed, but could also say anything, she was used to it.","But now, meeting the eyes of the two juniors who seemed to have suffered some kind of impact, Dai Li instantly felt the shame of poisoning minors.","A layer of bright pink quickly appeared on her cheeks, and spread to her neck. Dai Li pressed her hands on Qin Shaozong's waist and abdomen, pushed him and said, \"No respect for the old.\"","The golden winged step shake of the phoenix holding a pearl on the woman's bun swayed, and the drooping pearl string rarely swayed out a violent arc. And putting this sentence, Dai Li turned around and walked in the other direction.","I don't know if this sentence was too lethal, or Qin Shaozong was caught off guard, he was pushed back a step.","The man's face darkened, and at this time he also noticed the two juniors not far away, he looked over expressionlessly.","In Qin Qinian's perspective, the surroundings suddenly became extremely dark, gloomy winds blew all around, a huge shadow was pulled out in front, and a pair of terrifying beast pupils shooting red light looked over from the shadow.","The young man shivered, subconsciously stepped back, moved another step to the side, and stood behind Shi Rongyue.","Shi Rongyue: \"...\"","\"Qin San.\"","This move of his undoubtedly made Qin Shaozong quite displeased, and that anger suddenly had a place to go: \"A manly man is timid, hiding behind a girl, what kind of decency is this? Roll over and follow me to the martial arts arena.\"","Qin Qinian was struck by lightning, his heart was like dead ashes.","*","Dai Li walked around the mansion, and when the golden crow was about to fall into the horizon, she came to Qin Yanzhou's pavilion.","Waiting for less than a quarter of an hour, Dai Li saw the door not far away open.","The first one to come out was Ding Luying. Having not seen him for three days, Dai Li only felt that he was a little haggard, and even his white beard seemed to have lost its luster.","Of course it is understandable. It has been highly tense these three days. Although he sleeps less when he is old, he inevitably worries a lot.","Dai Li curtsied to Ding Luying, \"I will engrave Old Mr. Ding's great kindness to Yanzhou in my heart and never forget it for the rest of my life. In the future, if you ever need any assistance, I will not refuse anything within my power.\"","Ding Luying's face wrinkled with a smile. He didn't exchange polite pleasantries with Dai Li, but accepted her gratitude, \"I hope there will never come a day when the Ding family needs to trouble Madam.\"","Smiling, Dai Li shifted her gaze to the side, only to see a tall, slender figure walking out of the room right behind Ding Luying.","Having not seen him for three days, Dai Li could tell at a glance that her son had lost a lot of weight. His face was pale, his facial bones more pronounced, and his whole being exuded a kind of frail thinness.","Yet his eyes shone brightly, as if a heavy mountain had finally been lifted from his back, or like a dust-covered sword that had been wiped completely clean, revealing a lightness and brightness distinct from the past.","Ding Luying stroked his beard and smiled. Not wanting to disturb the mother and son, he left with his grandson, Ding Lianxi.","\"Zhou Zhou...\" Dai Li was overwhelmed with mixed emotions, feeling as though her son had only truly come alive in this very moment.","\"Mother, I am fully recovered.\" The corners of Qin Yanzhou's mouth curled up slightly. He was a little shy, but also harbored an unspeakable joy. Compared to his stiff smiles in the past, he now possessed a rare touch of youthful spirit.","After saying that, the young man lowered his eyes, \"I'm sorry for making you worry.\"","Dai Li playfully patted her son's shoulder, pretending to be angry: \"What silly things are you saying, child? What is there to apologize for? Before, you were controlled by others and had no choice, but all of that is in the past now.\"","Dai Li's expression turned serious: \"Today is the beginning of winter, and more importantly, it is Zhou Zhou's rebirth. From now on, my son will surely have everything go his way, and live a life full of joy, peace, and health.\"","These words seemed to carry immense weight, enough to part the clouds and reveal the sun. The young man stood stunned for a long time before tilting his head up to gaze into the distance.","The afterglow of the setting sun covered the entire sky, spreading out like an oil painting—gorgeous and aesthetic. The warm orange light was very gentle, like a pool of warm spring water without any sharp edges.","Before long, night would fall, and darkness would swallow the light, shrouding the earth.","But Qin Yanzhou knew that every day of his future would be bright and clear, without a single shadow of a cloud.","...","\"Qin Yanzhou, you're out of seclusion!\" Seeing Qin Yanzhou, the previously dejected Qin Qinian instantly perked up. His gloominess was swept away, and he ran over happily.","The teenager circled him twice. Instead of the smell of blood, he caught a fresh scent of soap locust mixed with spices. \"Is it just my imagination, or have you lost a lot of weight? I heard earlier that your treatment required bloodletting. You must have bled buckets, otherwise why would your face be as pale as a little lady's... Ouch!\"","Qin Yanzhou slowly retracted his hand. \"You are the son of a marquis, how can you not even speak properly?\"","Clutching his stomach, Qin Qinian didn't refute this. He tilted his head and suddenly let out an \"Ah.\" \"I remember more than two months ago when you first arrived in Yuyang, you completely ignored me when I talked to you, at most giving an 'Mhm.' You're vastly different now compared to back then!\"","Qin Yanzhou ignored him and continued walking towards the main hall.","Before returning to Yuyang, he lived in the side room of the main courtyard, and at that time, he and his mother dined together in the main room.","After all, there were only three of them back then, and they couldn't be bothered to move elsewhere.","Later, after arriving in Yuyang, the number of people grew. First came the brothers Qin Yunce and Qin Qinian, and later the mother and daughter pair, Qin Hongying and Shi Rongyue.","With more people, it was no longer suitable to dine in the main room, so they moved to the main hall.","Qin Qinian was still chattering away, trying to sling an arm around his shoulders. \"Thanks a lot for that day in the passageway. If you hadn't reacted so quickly, in a few days it would be the seventh day after Rongrong and my death! Actually, you already consider me a friend, don't you? Otherwise, you wouldn't have risked your life to save me back then. Tsk, if you ask me, you just have a cold face, but your heart is quite warm.\"","\"You're covered in mud, don't touch me.\" Qin Yanzhou dodged his hand, too lazy to explain.","\"I fell in the martial arts arena just now. A real man doesn't need to be so clean.\" Qin Qinian didn't care at all. He suddenly remembered something, \"Qin Yanzhou, what do you like to eat?\"","The topic changed so abruptly that the young man tilted his head, a trace of confusion in his peach blossom eyes. \"Why do you ask?\"","Qin Qinian scratched his head, unsure of how to reply for a moment.","By this time, the two had already walked into the main hall.","They arrived neither late nor early; apart from Dai Li and Qin Shaozong, everyone else was already present.","\"Yanzhou is here. I see your spirit is much better than before. Congratulations,\" Qin Yunce smiled.","Qin Hongying, who knew all the inside details, also nodded: \"The bitterness is over and the sweetness begins. From now on, it's a new life.\"","Shi Rongyue quickly glanced at the young man, lowered her eyes, and also offered her congratulations.","In response to their words, Qin Yanzhou nodded, \"Thank you.\"","Not long after, Dai Li and Qin Shaozong arrived as well.","Seating in the hall had always followed strict etiquette. The head seat facing the door was the most honorable position, generally reserved for the master of the house.","However, Dai Li disliked individual dining portions, so she set up a large round table.","Initially, this large round table didn't have a Lazy Susan. Later, when the mother and daughter Qin Hongying and Shi Rongyue arrived, it made seven people dining together.","Without a rotating tray, the dishes were placed far away, making it inconvenient to reach for food.","Thus, Dai Li had a carpenter make a rotating tray for the table. The tray, two sizes smaller than the round table, held the dishes. Except for Qin Yanzhou, no one else had ever seen such a thing, and even Qin Shaozong found it extremely novel.","After sitting at the round table, their current seating arrangements had changed slightly, but overall remained more or less the same.","Facing the outside of the main hall sat Dai Li and Qin Shaozong. On Dai Li's other side sat Qin Hongying, and next to Qin Hongying was her daughter, Shi Rongyue.","On Qin Shaozong's other side was Qin Yunce, next to whom sat Qin Yanzhou; meanwhile, Shi Rongyue and Qin Qinian sat next to each other.","Everyone had gathered, and the food and wine on the table were ready. But the people in the head seats didn't immediately pick up their chopsticks. Instead—","\"Before we eat, I have an important matter to announce,\" Qin Shaozong said.","Dai Li's brow inexplicably twitched.","Sure enough, the next moment she heard the man beside her say: \"Madam and I plan to get married on the Beginning of Spring next year.\"","As soon as these words fell, Qin Yanzhou abruptly turned his head to look at Dai Li."]},{"number":124,"title":"Chapter 124","paragraphs":["Dai Li was stunned for a moment, not expecting Qin Shaozong to be so sudden. She noticed her son's gaze, but everyone was present, and the matter of marriage was not false. It seemed inappropriate to say anything at this time.","Not only Qin Yanzhou, but the other people also looked over, looking at Qin Shaozong and then at Dai Li.","Qin Hongying had long guessed that he was going to marry, so she smiled and said, \"Second Brother, you acted much faster than I expected. By the way, is that jade ring coming back?\"","The jade ring was the Qin family's heirloom, or more accurately, the token of every matriarch or future matriarch.","Dai Li lowered her eyes. At this moment, she only had a small purse at her waist. She had already taken off the jade ring earlier and put it back in the box in her room.","Not only because it was conspicuously large, but also because it was too heavy.","Hanging on her waist, its presence was very strong.","\"I brought it back today,\" Qin Shaozong said.","Hearing this, Qin Hongying tutted softly in her heart. He brought back the token today, and announced the marriage to the family at the dinner table that very night. Her second brother really couldn't wait a single day.","But on the surface, Qin Hongying still raised the teacup in front of her. \"What a joyous occasion, congratulations. I will substitute tea for wine to wish you and Dai Li a long life together, growing old together in harmony.\"","The smile in Qin Shaozong's eyes deepened. Qin Hongying raised a teacup; he picked up a wine goblet. \"Alright, thank you.\"","He drained it in one gulp.","With Qin Hongying leading the way, Qin Yunce also came to congratulate them. His body couldn't handle alcohol, so he also substituted tea for wine.","Qin Shaozong poured himself a full cup of wine and drank it all again.","Generally speaking, when drinking with subordinates or those of a lower generation, just touching the lips was already giving face. Drinking it all in one gulp meant he was either extremely appreciative or very happy.","Qin Hongying's mouth twitched, feeling that her second brother must be the latter.","People are in high spirits when involved in happy events. This happy event had only just begun, yet it could make him so thrilled.","After Qin Yunce, Qin Qinian, who liked to drink, also raised his cup. After Qin Qinian came Shi Rongyue.","The young girl held her tea bowl and also said auspicious words. Qin Shaozong also drank another cup, treating her equally.","Shi Rongyue put down her tea bowl and quietly raised her eyes to look at the person across from her.","The young man was currently looking down, his long, straight black eyelashes casting faint shadows under his eyes. He was much thinner than before, and his straight nose looked somewhat sharper.","As if sensing her gaze, those beautifully shaped peach blossom eyes looked up, as dark as ink.","Shi Rongyue stared blankly.","But the next moment, the other party looked away and turned to the main seat.","After Shi Rongyue put down her tea bowl, Qin Yanzhou felt a gaze from the main seat fall directly on him.","It was intense and carried other meanings.","He turned his head to meet those narrow brown eyes, expressionless.","When Dai Li saw the two of them looking at each other, she immediately felt a headache.","Her son had just come out of seclusion, not only thin but also with a face as white as paper. She originally wanted to wait until Zhouzhou's health improved a bit before telling him about this.","But she didn't expect Qin Changgeng to announce it tonight.","Qin Yanzhou's gaze only paused for a moment, then moved to Dai Li. From just now, his mother hadn't made a move.","She neither spoke nor left the table.","He saw the helplessness on Dai Li's face. The young man paused, picked up the wine goblet on the table, and gestured to Qin Shaozong.","He didn't say any auspicious words, just raised his cup.","Qin Shaozong smiled, also raised his cup, and drained it in one gulp.","Today was the Beginning of Winter.","There is a saying about eating mutton and dumplings on the Beginning of Winter.","However, the dumplings of this era were not yet called dumplings; they were called jiao'er. A famous doctor used dough to wrap some medicinal herbs to dispel the cold, such as mutton and pepper, boiled them, and distributed them to patients suffering from frostbite. Because they looked like ears, they got the name jiao'er.","Later, in many places, to commemorate the famous doctor, and also to welcome the arrival of winter, the custom of eating jiao'er on the Winter Solstice was passed down and gradually became a tradition.","The dumpling filling was mutton, which Dai Li wasn't used to eating, so she only ate one as a token gesture. The others, including Qin Yanzhou, were very good at eating mutton.","A large plate of dumplings, dipped in some mature vinegar or soy sauce, and with some minced garlic, was quite a delicacy.","This dinner was similar yet different from usual. Dai Li saw that Qin Shaozong had finished the pot of yellow rice wine next to him.","He was visibly in a good mood tonight.","After the meal, everyone dispersed.","The sky outside was already dyed black. According to the usual time, it was time to rest and sleep not long after dinner.","\"Zhouzhou, come with me,\" Dai Li said to her son.","Qin Yanzhou followed his mother without a word.","Qin Shaozong watched the backs of the mother and son leaving, turning his jade thumb ring.","...","Dai Li didn't let Nianxia and Bipo follow her. She carried a lantern herself and left the main hall with her son.","She walked towards the way back.","Not back to the main courtyard, but back to Qin Yanzhou's own courtyard, to see him off.","The mother and son didn't speak along the way, until they reached the front yard of Qin Yanzhou's pavilion, Dai Li finally spoke, \"Zhouzhou, originally I wanted to wait a few days, until your health was better, to tell you about this. It's just that just now...\"","Dai Li sighed, observing her son's expression. \"I didn't expect him to announce it so suddenly. But although what he said was hasty, it wasn't false. Qin Changgeng and I will get married in a while.\"","The last sentence was a bit quieter, somewhat muffled in the night wind.","Perhaps the silence on the way had been long enough, or perhaps various emotions had been digested a lot during the dinner just now. At this moment, Qin Yanzhou immediately asked, \"Mom, are you willing to marry him? The Gu poison in my body has been cleared now. If you're not willing, I can take you away.\"","Burning bridges after crossing the river was indeed distasteful and would be condemned by thousands. But he felt that compared to his mother's own wishes, those were not important.","Dai Li looked at her son, who was already much taller than her, and smiled gratifyingly. \"I am willing.\"","The Gu poison on Zhouzhou was cured, and the White Elephant was dead, but this absolutely didn't mean that she and the Green Lotus Sect could wipe the slate clean.","This score would eventually have to be settled with the real sect leader. But the Green Lotus Sect was a powerful force, highly likely entrenched across several provinces.","Qin Shaozong certainly hated the sect, and on his path to pacifying the world, he would most likely confront the Green Lotus Sect. But for things like revenge, it was definitely more satisfying to be involved in it, and without someone fanning the flames from the inside, who knew when they would ever face the Green Lotus Sect?","More importantly, she and Zhouzhou might not actually be able to leave smoothly.","Qin Changgeng promised not to take concubines, and there was also the winter hunt bet to fight for later.","What else could they do? Make do for now.","Of course, she couldn't tell her son about dealing with the Green Lotus Sect now, otherwise he would feel guilty again. Zhouzhou had finally been made a bit more lively by Nalan Wugong and Qin Qinian, he couldn't go back to how he was before.","Qin Yanzhou pursed his lips, and then said something Dai Li didn't expect, \"Mom, do you think the Marquis of Wu'an is better than Uncle Zhong?\"","Dai Li froze, her thoughts drifting back to the past.","In the second year after her husband passed away, she met an old flame at a high school reunion. The other party had never married, and upon learning that she was widowed, directly launched a pursuit.","Her taste in men had never been poor. Zhong Mingze had indeed gone on to achieve great success in his career, starting his own company over the years and achieving financial freedom.","Zhong Mingze had good looks, a fine character, and excellent financial standing. He pursued her passionately and frequently expressed his fondness for Zhouzhou. After testing him for a period of time, she eventually brought Zhouzhou out to let her son interact with him.","Zhouzhou did not resist at the time. As they spent more time together, the man and the boy became quite familiar with each other.","Later on, Zhong Mingze even visited her home.","But those were all things of the past, happening before the school bus plunged into the river.","Daili thought for a moment before replying tactfully, \"Both of them have their own merits. You cannot just lump them together.\"","She sounded very much like she was trying to walk a tightrope, so Qin Yanzhou pressed further, \"Do you think he treats you well?\"","When people panic, they tend to make small, nervous gestures. Daili raised her hand and scratched her cheek with one finger. \"He is alright, I suppose. He is quite generous.\"","Materially, Qin Shaozong had not mistreated her.","Eight out of ten clothing chests in the inner room of the main quarters were filled with her dresses, and her jewelry boxes were packed to the brim, mostly with items of top-tier craftsmanship.","Even in modern times, if those items did not end up in a museum for their historical value, they would still be considered rare masterpieces.","Aside from his occasional bouts of madness, his unspeakable dark hobbies, and his sharp tongue, if one set aside emotional matters, Qin Shaozong was actually a decent man.","So, yes, he was alright.","Qin Yanzhou frowned, clearly dissatisfied with this answer. \"Mom...\"","Daili pushed open the door in front of her and gently shoved her son inside. \"Rest assured, your mother knows what she is doing. You should not overthink things. Go to bed early, wake up early, and recover your lost vitality.\"","After tucking him into the room, Daili was about to leave when she suddenly remembered something else. \"By the way, Zhouzhou, I need your help with something.\"","The thick clouds in the sky were blown away by the wind, revealing the full moon. Under the moonlight, Daili's eyes glinted like jewels. \"Zhouzhou, Qin Changgeng and I made a bet regarding the upcoming winter hunt. The bet is whether he can hunt down a tiger in a single day. The loser has to promise the winner one thing. When the time comes, I need you to help me...\"","This was a secret plot that could not see the light of day. Even though there was no one else around, Daili subconsciously lowered her voice.","She lowered it more and more, until she was practically whispering into her son's ear.","Qin Yanzhou listened carefully, his handsome features shifting slightly as a similar light emerged in his eyes. \"Okay, Mom.\"","Daili smiled brightly. \"Alright, it is a deal then. Goodnight, Zhouzhou.\"","\"Mom, let me walk you back.\" Qin Yanzhou belatedly realized that her maid had not followed her here.","Daili waved her hand in refusal. \"No need, go to bed early. I have a lantern, and there are plenty of patrolling guards in the estate. I can walk back by myself with the lantern.\"","Not giving her son a chance to say anything else, Daili carried her lantern and started heading back.","...","However, just as she turned out of the moon gate of her son's courtyard, Daili was startled by a dark silhouette standing right next to it.","The figure was exceptionally tall, standing there in silence like an insurmountable peak. The light of the lantern dispelled the darkness at his feet, its warm glow casting a bright sheen over his black robes.","Near his feet, the shattered pieces of a jade thumb ring could faintly be seen.","Daili had absolutely not expected to run into Qin Shaozong here. The string in her mind instantly pulled taut, vibrating to its absolute limit, as her head filled with one thought:","When did Qin Changgeng get here?","How much had he heard? The part where Zhouzhou said he could take her away, and the plan she had just discussed with her son at the end, had he heard all of it?","Under extreme shock, Daili's hand trembled uncontrollably, and the lantern in her grasp clattered to the ground.","It fell quite hard, extinguishing the candle inside.","Qin Shaozong reached out a long arm, wrapping it around the woman's waist and pulling her tightly into his embrace. \"Madam, just who is this 'Uncle Zhong' that the boy Qin Yanzhou speaks of?\"","Daili gasped sharply.","Had he really arrived that early?","Could it be that he had followed them shortly after she and Zhouzhou had left the main hall?"]},{"number":125,"title":"Chapter 125","paragraphs":["\"Mother!\"","Hearing the commotion outside, Qin Yanzhou hurried out of his room.","Turning past the moon gate, by the faint moonlight, he saw Qin Shaozong holding Dai Li in his arms.","The black-robed man had broad shoulders and a thick back. The full moon was to his side, barely illuminating his sharply contoured face. Shrouded in darkness, he seemed to merge with the endless ink-black night, forming an imposing, menacing dark tide.","Qin Yanzhou's pupils contracted for a moment, the muscles in his back unconsciously tensing.","Dai Li turned her head slightly, her gaze sweeping over her son behind her. Her voice had calmed down, \"It is nothing, Zhou Zhou, go back to sleep.\"","Qin Yanzhou stood motionless.","Dai Li pushed Qin Shaozong. Failing to push him away the first time, she reached for a bit of his leather belt and pinched him through his clothes. \"Does the Marquis wish to feed the mosquitoes here? Even if you do, I certainly do not.\"","Winter had already arrived; where would there be mosquitoes or bugs?","Qin Shaozong stared at the woman in his arms for a moment before finally, slowly loosening his long arms. He remained silent. Dai Li reached back to grasp his wrist, pulling him along to leave together.","Qin Shaozong's bone density was greater than that of ordinary people, and he was tall, not to mention covered in smooth, well-defined muscle. Dai Li initially struggled to pull him; it was only after she looked back at him again that the man finally followed her.","\"Why did you speak of marriage so suddenly?\" Dai Li asked him.","Originally, it was just a casual topic to let her son see that she and Qin Shaozong were leaving while chatting leisurely, but bringing it up actually ended up irritating Dai Li herself.","\"You did not even discuss this matter with me, just rashly blurted it out, leaving me completely unprepared. Qin Changgeng, if you act like this next time, I will not let you off easy,\" Dai Li said with dissatisfaction.","Just speaking was not enough to vent her frustration, so she pinched him again.","\"What preparation does Madam need?\" His voice lacked emotion, and his face was entirely steeped in the night, making it impossible to see clearly.","Dai Li: \"Naturally, to let me give Zhou Zhou a heads-up first. When you brought it up directly at dinner today, you scared the child silly.\"","As they spoke, the two had already walked quite a distance.","Qin Yanzhou watched the gradually departing pair, listening to the voices carried over by the wind, and lowered his eyes thoughtfully.","The extinguished lantern had been forgotten by its owner; the young man picked it up, and after he could no longer see his mother, he turned and returned to his room.","...","Having completely left her son's courtyard, Dai Li breathed a sigh of relief and let go of the hand pulling him.","She just let it go.","The man did not speak, nor did he react in any way.","Dai Li's heart inexplicably skipped a beat. Given her understanding of Qin Shaozong, she felt this was unlike his usual behavior.","When things are abnormal, there must be a demon at work. Could this man be brewing...","On the way back to the main courtyard, Qin Shaozong said nothing else, but a certain premonition in Dai Li grew stronger and stronger.","Turning into the moon gate of the main courtyard, the main room where they usually slept was right before their eyes.","Dai Li suddenly stopped in her tracks. \"I suddenly remembered...\"","Before she could finish her sentence, Dai Li's vision suddenly spun, and her feet, which had been touching the ground, were lifted into the air.","She was picked up entirely.","No, rather than being held, it was more like being slung over a shoulder.","He scooped up her legs with one hand and wrapped his other arm up around her waist. After hoisting up the woman who wanted to run away, he strode inside.","\"Qin Changgeng!\"","Nianxia and Bipo in the side room heard the commotion and hurriedly ran out, only to be completely dumbfounded.","The man walked hastily, taking massive strides. The two women only saw the wildly swaying beads of her golden-winged hair ornament and the bright, beautiful arc of her pale pink wide sleeves fluttering in the air.","Bang. The door closed, cutting off the view from outside.","Nianxia and Bipo shuddered simultaneously at the sound.","\"This, are the Marquis and Madam having a conflict?\" Bipo said hesitantly.","They had never seen such a scene before!","Nianxia pondered for a moment. \"It should be fine. They say couples fight at the head of the bed and make up at the end of it. You and I have served the Marquis and Madam for so long; when have we ever seen them have a real conflict?\"","Bipo suddenly realized, \"You are right.\"","*","The room was unlit. The window was half open, welcoming a streak of moonlight, which became the sole light source in the room.","Qin Shaozong did not even take the time to enter the inner room. He merely placed Dai Li onto the long, soft chaise lounge by the window in the outer room, and immediately got onto it himself.","That long lounge, which had more than enough space for one person to recline, was now squeezed with two people, one high and one low.","The man positioned above was tall and burly. Kneeling on one knee against the outside of the woman's thigh, his strong, muscular arm propped up beside her like solid rock or an impenetrable iron pillar, tightly trapping the person beneath him.","The pale moonlight fell upon his deep, handsome profile, his brown eyes as dark and gloomy as a tiger in the night.","Being hoisted up and then dropped, Dai Li felt as if her brains had been thoroughly shaken. However, precisely because of this, her thoughts floated out of the mud and into an icy river, instantly calming her down significantly. \"Qin Changgeng, what crazy fit are you throwing?\"","Qin Shaozong did not understand her words; they went in one ear and out the other. He stubbornly sought an answer: \"Madam, who is that man surnamed Zhong?\"","Dai Li was blocked by him on the lounge. He was practically straddling her from above without putting his full weight down. Her back rested against the soft cushion, the wall was on one side, and his propped-up long leg and arm were on the other.","Unable to get up, Dai Li simply relaxed all her strength and lay completely flat. \"Whatever you are to me now, that is what he was to me back then.\"","The words were not particularly explicit, but they were enough.","Qin Shaozong's breathing instantly changed. Dark tides surged within his narrow brown eyes, full of hidden sharpness. \"Madam said that in the Peach Blossom Spring, it is one husband and one wife, with no such thing as concubines. And that boy Qin Yanzhou knows of the one surnamed Zhong, which means this person appeared at the latest after he could remember things. Did Madam's previous husband not care about this?\"","Although she had previously kept calling him her late husband, the late in Qin Shaozong's mouth was more of a curse. Since the other party could not find his way here from the Peach Blossom Spring, it was no different from being dead.","He did not know that the man was actually gone, but that did not stop Qin Shaozong from discovering the contradiction.","She clearly had a husband, so why did a man surnamed Zhong suddenly pop up later?","If her husband was still alive, how could he endure it?","Dai Li was stunned. She had not expected this man's focus to be here, and so logically clear at that. \"Zhou Zhou's biological father, he and I separated later on...\"","Hearing this, Qin Shaozong straightened up slightly, staring at her unblinkingly. A moment later, his thin lips curled up, and the heavy, freezing air pressure surrounding them suddenly dissipated a bit. \"So I was right before. He really has become a late husband.\"","He had always felt that if someone obtained such a smart, quick-witted, and knowledgeable beauty, they would never let her leave no matter what.","It seemed that he was not the only one with such thoughts.","Qin Shaozong locked onto the woman beneath him and said through gritted teeth, \"Madam thinks I am more generous than that man surnamed Zhong, and that is it?\"","The last few words were as if he had chewed them up and squeezed them out through his teeth, every word carrying steaming sparks.","This fox had initially said that each had their own merits, but after thinking about it later, she only came up with, He is alright, quite generous.","Alright... I guess.","What was with that tone? Why was her answer so reluctant!","He, the dignified patriarch of the Qin clan of the North, the Marquis of Wu'an personally enfeoffed by the Son of Heaven, was actually inferior to those ghosts and monsters?","How could Dai Li not see that he was burning with anger? Actually, at this moment, it was not impossible for her to patch up what she had just said.","For instance, she could say she was too embarrassed to praise him in front of their son just now, and casually throw in phrases like \"strikingly handsome\" or \"extraordinarily heroic.\"","She was confident she could gloss over it. After all, Qin Shaozong was actually quite easy to coax, but...","Why should she coax him?","There was no need for that.","Those were all facts; there was nothing to hide.","If she coaxed him this time, the next time he threw a fit and acted up, she would have to waste her time and energy again. Setting this bad precedent would make things hard to manage later, which would be even worse.","Not only should she not coax him, but she also had to thoroughly cure him of this terrible habit.","\"Qin Changgeng, there is no point in talking about this now. Those things are in the past. I will never see them again, so why must you keep asking? Besides...\"","At this point, Daili's tone grew heavier. \"I haven't badgered you about your past affairs, so why are you so obsessed with mine?\"","\"My lady may ask,\" he said, the words heavy and suppressed.","Daili's mouth twitched.","She had absolutely no interest in his past, and his words were clearly just a way to give himself the green light.","Daili turned her head away. \"The past is in the past. There's nothing to ask.\"","Qin Shaozong reached out with two fingers, pinched her chin, and forced her to face him. \"Since my lady won't ask, then I will.\"","\"What is there to ask? We are both the same, what's there to ask?\" Daili raised her hand and smacked his arm with a crisp slap. In the quiet night, the sound was quite loud.","A fierce glint appeared in Qin Shaozong's eyes. \"It's not the same!\"","\"How is it different?\" Daili shot back.","The muscles in Qin Shaozong's jaw tightened as her words from that day seemed to echo in his ears:","\"Speaking solely of arranged marriages where you have no idea what the other person is like before the wedding, living together afterward without loving each other is one thing...\"","Loving each other.","So the men she had chosen must have been very much to her liking.","She liked every single one of them.","She had thought about marrying every single one of them.","She had planned to have children with every single one of them.","Except for him...","A surge of anger rose from his chest, rushing to his head, and then morphed into an invisible heavy hammer that struck his temples fiercely.","Unbearable, complex emotions intertwined, coursing down from the top of his head, burning through his chest, lungs, and spine, spreading to his limbs and bones, causing the veins in his arms to bulge and the hairs on his body to stand on end.","Qin Shaozong's mind buzzed. \"I used to say my lady was full of wandering thoughts. It seems I wasn't wrong at all.\"","With so many hearts given away, how could she not have too many?","His words were vague, and Daili let out a questioning \"Hmm?\" with an upward inflection, not understanding what he meant.","Perhaps her confusion was too obvious, or perhaps his pent-up frustration refused to dissipate, but Qin Shaozong finished the second half of his sentence in a sarcastic tone: \"Like a butterfly enamored with flowers, moving from one to the next. My lady is no less a sly fox, abandoning one den only to dig another.\"","She didn't understand at first, but combined with the second half, Daili instantly understood everything.","She was so angry she laughed at Qin Shaozong. \"Qin Changgeng, can you be reasonable? Did you have few women in your past? Just from what I know, there were two in the Wei family, and I believe it definitely doesn't stop there. And who dictates that a woman must be faithful to one man until the end? If we get along, we stay together; if not, we part. Widows in Great Yan can remarry, and Peach Blossom Spring is far ahead of Great Yan. How could the women there not have the right to choose a suitable partner?\"","She stared right back at him, giving him a strong dose of reality. \"Let me tell you the truth. I did like a few men in the past. If you mind it so much, I don't think I need to give you my 'Response to the Marriage Proposal,' and we can just cancel the wedding next spring.\"","The brown eyes above her suddenly contracted.","\"You dare?\"","His domineering nature reared its head again, and Daili said without hesitation, \"Just watch me and see if I dare!\"","There was no response from above, only heavy, rapid breathing that felt as if it could spew fire at any moment.","Daili sneered, mimicking his sarcastic tone. \"I'm so sorry to offend Your Lordship's eyes. Why don't you return to your Marquis's mansion from now on, and I'll live outside. It's best if we stay far apart, so this promiscuous fox doesn't bring ruin upon you...\"","The rest of her words were swallowed by the man.","That fiery anger transferred over through their connection, blazing hot. Daili was already fuming, and being kissed by him now was like pouring oil on the fire.","This man was starting again.","Whenever he encountered something he didn't want to hear, he found a way not to hear it.","Daili clamped her jaw shut, biting down hard on the tip of his tongue.","The taste of blood spread, but he still didn't stop. He didn't even raise his hand to pinch her jaw and force her teeth apart like he had done before.","He let her bite him.","When bitten, he would pull back slightly, kissing and sucking at the corners of her mouth. Once she relaxed a little, he would push back in.","This half-soft, half-hard approach left Daili at a loss. Finally, she had to turn her head away, letting his kisses fall on the side of her face and her neck.","In winter, there were few insects chirping, and there was no one else in the room. At this moment, there were only two rapid breaths intertwining and merging.","Qin Shaozong wrapped his arms around her waist and, with a forceful pull, switched their positions on the upholstered chair, which was not very spacious for the two of them.","Originally, he was on top and Daili was on the bottom.","Now he lay in her previous position, his back pressing against the spot she had just leaned on. In this increasingly cold winter, he could still feel her residual warmth there.","When Qin Shaozong was on top just now, he had supported himself with his knees on the chair, merely hovering over Daili.","But Daili didn't have his excellent balance, nor could she be bothered to exert the effort. She simply used him as a human cushion.","Qin Shaozong raised his hand, stroking her back over and over, as if smoothing the fur of a small animal, or as if trying to wipe away her anger and irritability.","Daili tried to prop herself up with her hands but couldn't get up. His other hand rested on her lower back, holding her firmly in place.","She didn't speak, and neither did Qin Shaozong.","Daili's eyes gradually half-closed. Just as she was beginning to feel a bit drowsy, she heard the man beneath her say:","\"My lady, I didn't mean it like that just now.\"","When he spoke again, his voice held no trace of anger, only a hint of helplessness.","He had digested it all on his own.","The couch was near the window. The moonlight was a bit faint, but with the two of them so close, the expression of the person on the bottom could be seen with absolute clarity.","The man's thin lips were stained with blood, and the corner of his mouth was slightly torn. There was a bit of helplessness on his face, as well as a bit of... awkwardness.","Obviously, this man who had been aloof for the first half of his life and utterly dictatorial after seizing power had never bowed his head to a woman like this before.","Daili didn't expect this kind of feudal patriarch to be as proactive and considerate as a contractor at work. The fact that he could listen to reason just now, stop, and process things on his own was already an improvement.","What else could she do? She couldn't leave, so she would just have to train him slowly.","But then again, given his behavior, could it be that Qin Changgeng hadn't heard the plans she discussed with Zhou Zhou at the very end?","If he hadn't heard, that was absolutely wonderful!","Her mind raced with a thousand thoughts, even giving rise to a secret joy, but on the surface, Daili's expression remained calm. Even the \"Mhm\" she uttered in response lacked any ripple of emotion.","\"You didn't mean it like that, does that mean you won't bring it up again in the future?\" Daili struck while the iron was hot, maintaining her composure.","That large, dark hand raised again, stroking heavily down her back. This time, rather than soothing her, it seemed more like he was trying to smooth out the surge of frustration that had just flared up within himself.","Separated by a mere arm's length, their eyes met.","Qin Shaozong caught the subtle, cunning calculation in her eyes. It was as if a fluffy fox tail was wagging vigorously right in front of him, making him burn with anger yet leaving him completely helpless.","Striking a woman was not the conduct of a true man.","As for scolding her, she had an entire arsenal of words ready to counter him, each backed by her own twisted logic. And if he dared to lecture her any further, she would probably threaten to call off their marriage altogether.","He could neither hit her nor scold her.","This was the first time Qin Shaozong had ever encountered such a thorny predicament. Yet, ironically, he was the one who had personally captured this little fox from Nankang Commandery. He had brought this upon himself and had no one else to blame.","Seeing him remain silent, Daili raised the corners of her eyes slightly, the small cinnabar mole on her forehead seemingly coming alive in an instant. \"Was not the Marquis quite the talker in the beginning? Your words were full of thorns, your tongue silver and sharp. Why are you so quiet now?\"","Qin Shaozong's face darkened slightly. \"Madam is being quite unreasonable. It was clearly Madam who resorted to harsh words first today.\"","Daili was indignant. \"Qin Changgeng, do not try to turn the tables on me.\"","Qin Shaozong clenched his jaw. \"Did you or did you not call me an old man with no self-respect today?\"","Daili: \"...\"","She had only made one passing remark about him in the afternoon, and he had actually held a grudge about it until now."]},{"number":126,"title":"Chapter 126","paragraphs":["“Nianxia, do you think Madam is up yet?”","“Definitely not. They called for water several times last night. Based on past experience, Madam won't be up until at least the beginning of the Si hour. Let's keep the porridge warm first, so she can eat as soon as she wakes up.”","“Oh, it's snowing!”","...","When Dai Li woke up, she didn't know if it was her illusion, but she felt much colder.","If she had to use a metaphor, it was as if she was enveloped in a ball of cold air, and the breath she inhaled was tinged with frost, cooling her all the way from her trachea to her lungs, dispelling the few traces of drowsiness she had left.","She was alone on the bed; the space beside her had long lost its warmth. Qin Shaozong was not one to sleep in; he got up before dawn every day for morning exercises, and then went to the study.","It was a good thing he made almost no noise when he got up, otherwise Dai Li would really have a reason to sleep in a separate room from him.","She sat up holding the quilt, which slipped down a little, revealing a large expanse of snow-white skin with red marks. Dai Li lifted the quilt, looked down inside, twitched the corner of her mouth, and pulled the quilt higher, unable to bear looking.","Her belly band had slipped onto the footstool last night, and was later picked up by Qin Shaozong and hung on the wooden rack next to the bed.","The wooden rack was right next to her, not exactly close, but not far either.","Dai Li reached out to grab the belly band, only to find her whole body soft and limp, as if her bones had been taken apart and put back together again. She pulled her hand back, fell backward with a \"plop,\" and even pulled a little of the quilt over her face.","She was done for, excessive indulgence.","She hadn't expected Qin Changgeng to be so sensitive to the word \"old.\" She couldn't even say it; the moment she did, he got triggered.","Dai Li felt as if she was back to last night, with that heavy, hurried male voice close to her ear:","“I am not yet forty, in the prime of my life. I can draw a strong bow and tame a fierce horse. What does the word 'old' have to do with me?”","“It's only been once. Madam, don't pretend to be weak. Let's go again, don't sleep. Tsk, you don't even have to put in much effort, you're so delicate...”","“Put your legs up, squeeze tight.”","“If you can't finish eating today, continue eating tomorrow.”","...","Dai Li sighed heavily, “It's really killing me.”","Nianxia and Bipo, who were waiting outside, heard the sound and entered.","After washing up and putting on new clothes, Dai Li realized that her initial feeling wasn't an illusion. A cold front had indeed arrived, and not only that, it had brought a heavy snowfall.","A soft layer of white had fallen outside the window. The ground was white, the eaves were white, and the treetops were white. The sunlight reflected off it, creating a dazzling brightness, like a painting with well-arranged colors.","It truly lived up to the saying: wrapped in silver and white, exceptionally enchanting.","It was still snowing heavily at this moment. Dai Li couldn't help but push the window open to its maximum and reach out to catch the snow.","She was a Southerner. In the past, she had actually been to the North quite a few times for business trips and tourism. But it was truly rare for her to catch heavy snow during these trips.","Especially since modern industrial pollution was exceptionally severe, there was a lot of dust in the air. Much of the snow that fell on the ground was very dirty, and after the snow melted, the water was even more murky.","But it was different here.","In this era, even gunpowder hadn't appeared. The water was clean, many streams were crystal clear to the bottom, and rivers even had transparent sections of two to three meters.","Without dust pollution, one could look up at night and see the brilliant stars studding the sky. \"The dangerous tower is a hundred feet high, one can pick the stars with one's hand,\" was most concretely realized here.","Now it was snowing, and the world was a radiant white, pleasing to the eye. However, Dai Li didn't dare to look too much; the snow under the sun was too bright, and looking at it for too long would hurt her eyes.","Just as Dai Li finished her breakfast, Qin Yanzhou came over.","“Mother, good morning.” The young man cupped his hands and bowed, greeting Dai Li.","After standing up straight, he carefully observed Dai Li's complexion. Seeing that her spirit was quite good, except for the lingering redness around her eyes, he felt a little relieved.","Dai Li was also observing him, noticing that her son was wearing thin clothes. She immediately frowned in disapproval, “Why are you wearing so little? Zhouzhou, you just had blood drawn, you are in a weak period right now, you should wear more clothes.”","Qin Yanzhou lifted a bit of his collar to let Dai Li see the clothes he was wearing underneath, “I have added clothes underneath, and it's not as cold when it snows as when the snow melts.”","Over the years, he had gradually become able to endure both cold and heat, getting used to it. If it wasn't because the treatment had just ended, he wouldn't have even planned to add that inner garment.","Dai Li was worried, always feeling that the child would be cold. She got up and moved the charcoal brazier a little closer to him, and nagged him a bit more to wear more clothes when he should, and not be afraid of being laughed at.","She knew that children of this age mostly cared about style over warmth.","Qin Yanzhou helplessly agreed.","Dai Li asked him again, “Has Zhouzhou had breakfast?”","Qin Yanzhou said he had eaten.","Dai Li looked out the door. Nianxia was sweeping snow in the courtyard, and Bipo was not there, seemingly having gone to the kitchen. Needless to say, Qin Shaozong was in the study.","Dai Li withdrew her gaze in satisfaction, but still lowered her voice a bit, “Qin Changgeng didn't hear our final plan last night.”","Qin Yanzhou nodded, wanting to ask something, but feeling it was inappropriate.","“But after what happened last night, he might take the winter hunt more seriously. When the time comes, Zhouzhou, you... play it by ear,” Dai Li reminded her son.","The bet was whether a tiger could be hunted within a single day, regardless of whether anyone assisted Qin Shaozong.","Later, when Dai Li thought about this matter over and over again, she realized she had missed a spot: she hadn't specified the number of people assisting the other party!","Two people assisting was assistance, two hundred, or two thousand people assisting together was also assistance.","Qin Changgeng was a proud man. Dai Li originally thought he wouldn't dispatch many people at the same time to search the whole mountain for a tiger. But after last night's incident.","Hiss, it was really hard to say.","She could clearly see that he was holding back anger.","And the loser of the bet had to agree to one thing for the other party. This matter hadn't been clearly specified yet, the flexibility was too strong, it was hard to guarantee that Qin Changgeng wouldn't get ideas about it.","Qin Yanzhou's eyebrows moved slightly, “Mother, I have an idea...”","Dai Li leaned in curiously.","The mother and son conspired in the room, while Nianxia outside continued sweeping the snow, completely unaware.","*","“Qin Yanzhou, oh, a rare guest! It's rare for you to come looking for me.” Qin Qinian was surprised and amazed to see Qin Yanzhou.","But after saying this, he seemed to remember something and took a slight breath of cold air, “Why aren't you staying in your own courtyard, what are you running out for?”","He knew that Qin Yanzhou had taken Mr. Nalan as his teacher and had to go for guidance every other day. Originally, Old Mr. Ding treated him every other day as well, perfectly staggering the two.","Now that the treatment was over, it was equivalent to having a free day. But based on his understanding of Qin Yanzhou, if this person had free time, he would mostly just stay quiet.","Qin Yanzhou: “Naturally, I came to find you.”","Qin Qinian tilted his head, “Why are you looking for me? Could it be that you've thought it through and are willing to have a good spar with me? But not right now, you just finished your treatment. If I won now, it would be an unfair victory.”","Qin Yanzhou asked, “Why are you always thinking about sparring with me?”","“Of course, because among those around my age, none of them can fight.” Qin Qinian didn't hesitate.","His several cousins from the Wei family often came to play with him, but he always felt that he couldn't play together with them. He liked wielding swords and spears, while they liked listening to little tunes or reading books. Even if his third cousin had some martial arts skills, it was only that.","As for the playmates from other families, there were indeed some who would spar with him, but they all held back their strength, terrified of bruising or bumping him anywhere.","Boring.","Only Qin Yanzhou...","This guy truly went all out when fighting him, his martial arts were exceptionally good, and he didn't have that annoying, fawning attitude.","\"But what's the use of asking this? You won't fight me anyway,\" Qin Qinian turned his head and curled his lips.","The young man suddenly said, \"It's not entirely impossible for me to spar with you.\"","Qin Qinian spun back around in a flash. \"You agree? Not the kind where you only defend and don't attack like you're avoiding a plague god, but going all out.\"","Qin Yanzhou nodded. \"Yes, going all out.\"","Qin Qinian was just about to rejoice when he heard the other party's second half of the sentence: \"But I have a condition. I heard there will be a winter hunt in a few days. Why don't we have a small competition then? If you can beat me, I'll spar with you.\"","Winter hunts were not rare.","In Qin Qinian's memory, his father would hold winter hunts on a whim. As the third young master of the Qin family, Qin Qinian himself joined the field every time.","\"Alright, what do you want to compete in? I've even hunted wolves myself in the past,\" Qin Qinian said proudly.","This was his highest achievement. At his age, being able to ride a horse and hunt wolves alone was already remarkable. After all, wolves are pack animals; if you find one, there must be a pack nearby.","\"We won't compete in hunting fierce beasts. We'll compete in hunting rabbits,\" Qin Yanzhou said.","Qin Qinian almost thought he misheard. \"What's so good about hunting rabbits? There's no difficulty.\"","Qin Yanzhou smiled faintly. \"Not necessarily. This hunt won't purely compare the number of rabbits caught, but also the number of rabbit holes we find that have live rabbits inside.\"","Qin Qinian raised an eyebrow. \"The number of rabbit holes? And they must have live rabbits inside?\"","He still didn't understand what was so fun about hunting rabbits.","Rabbits don't need to hibernate; they always need to forage for food. Therefore, even when winter comes, there are still plenty of rabbits in the mountains. It wouldn't be an exaggeration to say they are all over the hills and plains.","Snow rabbits might not be that conspicuous. But ordinary grass rabbits are like targets on the snow; you can catch one with every attempt.","\"The difficulty of hunting rabbits is indeed not high, but precisely because of this, it tests one's skills even more,\" Qin Yanzhou said calmly.","Qin Qinian was about to ask how it tested skills, but at that moment, he saw an orange silhouette turn the corner from outside.","He and Qin Yanzhou were just inside the door, less than twenty feet away from the newcomer, able to see each other just by looking up.","The dejected Shi Rongyue froze.","Seeing this, Qin Qinian waved at her. \"Rongrong, come here.\"","\"Young Master Qin, Little Cousin.\" Shi Rongyue walked over and curtsied to the two of them. She was carrying a round wooden bucket in her hand. As she curtsied, the jade pendant on her waist clinked against the small wooden bucket with a soft sound.","Qin Yanzhou: \"Miss Shi.\"","Qin Qinian welcomed her into the room and asked, \"Rongrong, what are you holding in your hand?\"","\"S-some tea snacks.\" Shi Rongyue placed the food container on the table, opened its lid, and took out the small boxes inside.","There were three small boxes in total, holding cheese, sesame cakes, and beef jerky respectively.","\"Young Master Qin, Little Cousin, there's still some time before dinner. Why don't we have some tea snacks together?\" Shi Rongyue looked at the two of them, her gaze shifting slightly to the left.","Qin Yanzhou and Qin Qinian had originally been sitting. When Shi Rongyue arrived, they stood up to return her greeting. Now that she had taken a seat at the table, it was obviously inappropriate for the two of them to remain standing.","Their conversation wasn't finished, so he couldn't leave. Qin Yanzhou sat back down.","Just as he lowered his eyes and took his seat, a sneaky shadow appeared at the top of his vision. Soon, a small wooden box filled with beef jerky entered his sight.","He looked up. The young girl sitting opposite him pursed her lips into a smile. As she smiled, her round cheeks revealed a pair of endearing dimples. \"Young Master Qin, thanks to your quick reflexes in the passageway that day, otherwise I fear I wouldn't be here today. These small tea snacks are hardly enough to serve as a token of gratitude for saving my life, but I still hope you will kindly accept them.\""]},{"number":127,"title":"Chapter 127","paragraphs":["Qin Qinian, who was sitting nearby, didn't wait for an invitation. He grabbed a sesame cake and started eating. \"Have a bite, let's eat while we chat. Qin Yanzhou, for this rabbit hunting competition, is it purely about who hunts the most rabbits and finds the most rabbit holes? Comparing the sum of both?\"","Shi Rongyue had arrived a bit late and missed the beginning, but hearing \"rabbit hunting\" and \"competition,\" it wasn't hard to guess they were having a contest.","But, competing in hunting rabbits?","She pricked up her ears to keep listening.","Qin Yanzhou then replied, \"Yes and no. It is indeed about quantity, but it's not a one-to-one ratio. The specific rules are: hunting ten rabbits equals finding one rabbit hole with live rabbits inside, all to be completed within a single daylight period. This way, we can test not only agility and observation but also luck.\"","It was the first time Qin Qinian had heard of such a game. \"Interesting.\"","Qin Yanzhou added, \"In ordinary competitions, the winner is usually known only after a tally at the end, which inevitably leads to slacking off midway. This time, we will each bring an inspector, both to keep count and to report.\"","\"Report? How will they report?\" Qin Qinian was full of doubts. \"When hunting, we'll definitely be riding horses all over the place. It won't be easy to find people.\"","The corners of Qin Yanzhou's mouth curled up slightly. \"Indeed, so this inspector will carry gongs and cymbals. Every time a rabbit hole is found, they will beat the gong or clash the cymbals, sending a message through sound to inform the other party from a distance.\"","Qin Qinian's eyes lit up. \"Hey, that's a good idea!\"","It was equivalent to real-time reporting of the score.","In a competition, the thrill of the chase is what makes it fun!","\"Young Master Qin, Little Cousin, what are you competing to catch rabbits for?\" Shi Rongyue asked curiously.","Qin Qinian: \"I've always wanted to spar with this guy. He refused before, but today he finally relented. However, he proposed a rabbit catching competition. Only if I win will he truly agree to it.\"","Shi Rongyue suddenly said, \"Young Master Qin, I also want to join the rabbit catching competition. Can I?\"","Both of them were slightly stunned.","Shi Rongyue smiled, revealing a pair of dimples. \"How can a life-saving grace be offset merely with lip service and a small box of dried meat? Actually, I also wanted to invite Young Master Qin to a restaurant or teahouse outside. But if I just asked normally, I guess you probably wouldn't agree...\"","Qin Yanzhou wanted to say \"There's no need,\" but for some reason, the words caught in his throat.","Seeing that he was somewhat swayed, Shi Rongyue hurriedly continued, \"You just said that hunting rabbits is a test of luck, so how about we leave this matter for heaven to decide?\"","Qin Qinian thought it was fine. They could play together; the more, the merrier. \"Qin Yanzhou, let's add her. Anyway, there's no danger in hunting rabbits.\"","Two pairs of round eyes stared at him. Qin Yanzhou felt as if he were being watched by innocent little puppies.","Suddenly, he remembered his professor neighbor from many years ago. At that time, his father had already passed away, and his mother was raising him alone. The publishing house wasn't too busy, but sometimes she had to travel for business.","Whenever that happened, his mother would entrust him to the retired old professor next door, asking him to help look after him for two or three days.","The old professor had a little local dog at home, a puppy with a yellow head and a white face, as fluffy as a sponge cake.","It was a particularly smart puppy. Though tiny, it could understand human words. Its eyes were wet, not pure black, but a light brown.","Whenever it saw him, it would wag its tail, running around him and playing with him, making him want to have a puppy of his own for a very long time.","Qin Yanzhou lowered his eyes and slowly nodded in agreement.","The dimples on Shi Rongyue's face instantly deepened. She seemed genuinely happy, nodding her little head, causing a stray tuft of hair that hadn't been pinned into her bun to sway along. \"Then it's settled.\"","\"Some rules will have to be slightly changed.\"","Qin Yanzhou rearranged things. \"Your inspector will use a suona to send messages, Qin Qinian's will use a gong, and mine will use cymbals. Every time a rabbit hole is found, after the inspector makes a simple mark, they will blow or strike the instrument twice in a row to transmit the sound.\"","\"Alright!\"","\"Alright!\"","*","\"Is Rongrong back?\"","Qin Hongying saw her daughter return carrying a small round bucket, the golden wheat-ear tassels hanging from her bun swaying back and forth. Looking to be in a very good mood, she smiled and said, \"I heard from Nichang that you prepared some tea and snacks before going out. Not bad. Young men of Qinian's age have the biggest appetites, sometimes eating five times a day.\"","Nichang was Shi Rongyue's personal maid.","The young girl froze. Her mouth moved as if she wanted to say something, but she saw her mother smiling encouragingly, \"You can continue tomorrow. Anyway, that child Qinian is not a picky eater; he's very easy to feed.\"","After Qin Hongying finished speaking, she noticed her daughter's unusual expression. \"What's wrong? Did something happen just now?\"","\"Little Cousin said there will be a winter hunt in a few days. He and I, along with... Young Master Qin, have agreed to hunt rabbits together,\" Shi Rongyue said in a low voice.","\"Hunting rabbits?\" Qin Hongying raised an eyebrow, finding it novel. Along with the novelty, she felt a bit pleased. \"Good, good, good. I didn't expect that despite Qinian looking careless normally, he is still a thoughtful child deep down. Worried that you wouldn't be able to keep up hunting fierce beasts, he changed it to hunting rabbits.\"","\"Mother, it's not like that.\" Shi Rongyue shook her head. \"It was Little Cousin and Young Master Qin who originally planned to compete in hunting rabbits. I... I heard about it, got interested, and asked to join them myself.\"","Qin Hongying frowned at this. \"They originally planned to hunt rabbits?\"","What's so good about hunting rabbits?","The mountains are full of them. With a bow and arrows, and a hunting dog, there's no worry of coming back empty-handed.","Qin Hongying thought she had figured out the reason. \"Oh, could it be to take care of Qin Yanzhou? I heard his health has always been poor, so I assume his skills aren't that great either...\"","\"They aren't poor,\" Shi Rongyue couldn't help but say. Under the gaze of those long eyes that were seventy percent similar to her Second Uncle's, the young girl whispered, \"If his skills were poor, that day I... and Little Cousin would have both been buried in the tunnel.\"","Qin Hongying thought about it and realized it was true.","\"You don't need to constantly keep Qin Yanzhou's life-saving grace in mind. I, your mother, will thank Daili myself; there's no need for a junior like you to busy yourself with it.\"","Qin Hongying added, \"Your Second Uncle taking a wife is a done deal, and Qin Yanzhou will be your elder brother from now on, but he is not on the same path as you all. In the future, maintaining a superficial politeness will be enough.\"","The \"you all\" she mentioned referred to Shi Rongyue and Qin Qinian.","Shi Rongyue pursed her lips and said nothing.","Having given birth to her, Qin Hongying believed she understood her daughter. Seeing her like this, she knew she disagreed in her heart.","Her daughter had reached adulthood and grown up; some matters could be discussed with her in depth.","Thus, Qin Hongying said, \"Qin Yanzhou is not your Second Uncle's biological son, and Daili does not come from a prominent family. To put it bluntly, Qin Yanzhou's biological father is a nobody. If it weren't for his mother being capable, he would be destined to be a commoner in this life. It's hard to say if the silver he could save up in a whole year without eating or drinking would even be enough to buy a single hairpin for a noble lady. Taking a step back, even if your Second Uncle loves his mother enough to love him too, and treats him as his own son, wanting him to succeed him is almost as difficult as ascending to heaven.\"","\"Why?\" Shi Rongyue asked.","Qin Hongying said seriously, \"Because some people have already quietly chosen sides. They have secretly formed a secondary faction belonging to Qinian. For the sake of their own future interests, these people will sweep him up and push him constantly forward.\"","Shi Rongyue knitted her delicate brows. \"What if my little cousin is unwilling? I feel that with his personality, he doesn't really like fighting with his family.\"","Qin Hongying shook her head. \"There is a saying: one cannot control one's own destiny. Some things may not be Qinian's original intention, but in the end, they truly benefit him. Your second uncle is currently in his prime. He can hold on for ten years, but what about twenty or thirty years? Our generation will eventually see the day when our strength falls short of our desires. And Daili does not have a powerful maternal family. This means that besides your second uncle, there is no one behind her to back her and her son up. This will always be a fatal weakness.\"","\"Mother, are we... also going to be the ones pushing little cousin forward?\" Shi Rongyue's eyelashes trembled slightly.","Qin Hongying did not answer whether they would be those people or not. She stroked the top of her daughter's head, smoothing down a stubborn tuft of hair. \"Rongrong, you are my only daughter, and I only want your future path to be steady and secure. And Qinian is your second uncle's only biological son; on this point alone, he is miles ahead.\"","When the time comes for the Qin and Shi families to unite in marriage, it will be like adding wings to a tiger for Qin Qinian himself.","Qin Hongying suddenly remembered something. \"Your second uncle will likely make a grand affair of this year's winter hunt. Rongrong, you are going to marry into Yuyang in the future. Take advantage of this winter hunt to get familiar with the young ladies and madams of the prominent families in Yuyang. You must get to know them all in advance.\"","Shi Rongyue lowered her head and bit her lip.","...","Recently, the prominent families of Yuyang all received an invitation.","An invitation to participate in the winter hunt.","The lockdown and the dispatch of soldiers into various households to catch thieves some time ago had left some lingering effects. Now, sending this invitation to the prominent families felt very much like giving a sweet date after striking with a stick.","Living under someone else's roof, the prominent families were still quite happy to eat this sweet date.","Daili was also aware that Qin Shaozong had invited the prominent families to join the winter hunt.","\"...So it is three days and two nights in total, and we set off tomorrow?\" Daili looked at the man beside her.","Both of them were in the study. Two desks were set up side by side; Daili occupied one, and Qin Shaozong occupied the one next to it.","\"Yes, we set off early tomorrow morning.\" Qin Shaozong sat boldly behind the desk, looking at the secret reports from other states spread out on it.","He divided his attention, speaking to Daili, \"Many prominent families have been invited to this winter hunt. There are twenty-two prominent families of various sizes with recognized names. Each family will bring about thirty descendants, female relatives, and servants.\"","Not counting the Qin family members and the guards responsible for security, that was already over six hundred people.","Daili paused her wolf-hair brush from practicing calligraphy. \"That is more people than I imagined.\"","\"Aren't you happy to see this happen, Madam?\" he said meaningfully.","Qin Shaozong had seen right through her little scheme.","More people meant there would be many things to arrange, which would take up a lot of time.","It didn't matter if he saw through it. Daili smiled and said, \"Yes, I am indeed happy to see it. What is there to be ashamed of in wanting to win?\"","\"It's not shameful, it's just that Madam can only think about it,\" he said.","These words were extremely certain. Daili frowned slightly and probed, \"Qin Changgeng, you aren't planning to send all the Xuanxiao Cavalry out to hunt for tigers, are you?\"","\"Do not underestimate your husband.\" He said this with great confidence.","Daili felt relieved.","As long as the entire army wasn't deployed, it was fine.","Qin Shaozong continued, \"At that time, many noble ladies will come to converse with Madam. If you get along, chat with them for a bit. If not, then let it be. There is no need to force yourself.\"","The power and influence he had accumulated to this day were not meant for his woman to have to read other people's faces.","Daili lowered her eyes, slowly practicing writing the character for respect. Hearing his words, she replied with a hum of agreement.","...","The sun set and rose, and in the blink of an eye, a day had passed.","Today the sky was clear and bright, and the heavy snow had stopped. It wasn't snowing, but the wind had picked up. The cool breeze blew by, bringing a chill that made people involuntarily shrink their necks into their collars.","The Qin Manor became busy before dawn. Daili was dug out of her warm bed, keeping her eyes closed as she let Nianxia and Bipo help her change clothes and fuss over her hair.","By the time her complex hair bun was styled and decorated with gold hairpins and jade dangling ornaments, Daili's sleepiness had faded by eighty percent, and she slowly washed up.","At this time, the sky outside only had a faint, barely visible layer of light, paler than the white of a fish's belly, as if covered by a layer of black gauze.","By the time they finished breakfast, it was broad daylight outside.","It was time to set off.","The carriage convoy, surrounded by horses, drove out from the main gate of the manor and headed north.","The early morning market was always bustling, but today was an exception. Public notices had been issued in advance, and vendors and commoners automatically made way. Along the route, military patrols stood guard, driving away any commoners who wandered in by mistake, allowing the streets and alleys to reveal their original spacious and open appearance.","Carriages hanging wooden plaques of prominent families converged from all directions, passing through swiftly one convoy after another.","An hour later, the blockade was lifted.","Daili lifted the carriage curtain and looked at the uniform white of the world outside, feeling an inexplicable sense of emotion.","The last time she was outside the city was three months ago when she returned to Yuyang with Qin Shaozong. And it had been almost a year since she arrived in this unfamiliar era.","A year was not short, but compared to her past thirty-odd years, it really wasn't much. Yet in this short year, it was painted with rich and vibrant colors, full of ups and downs, all inseparable from one person.","Qin Shaozong rode his red horse, walking beside Daili's carriage. He knew the moment the curtain beside him was lifted. The sun had not yet risen, so the snow at this time would not hurt her eyes; it didn't matter if she looked a little longer.","But Qin Shaozong quickly noticed that her gaze had fallen upon him.","It lingered for quite a while, at least longer than usual.","The originally somewhat languid man slowly straightened up. He lightly pulled the reins, making the horse beneath him walk more steadily and closer to the carriage.","\"Madam...\"","Qin Shaozong turned his head. He had only spoken two words when he saw the carriage curtain fall right at that moment, hiding the beautiful face of the woman inside.","The cold wind blew harder at this moment, carrying some snow particles blown from who knows where, feeling prickly against his face.","Qin Shaozong: \"...\"","Pressing his tongue against his back molars, the man chuckled lightly. \"Alright then, take your time discovering it.\"","An hour later, the convoy arrived at the hunting grounds in the northern suburbs.","Before the main force officially arrived, a group of the Northern Army had come to the hunting grounds yesterday to scout ahead.","The most basic preparations had already been completed here. For example, trenches to defend against wild beasts were dug near the camping grounds, and excessively thick snow had basically been cleared away.","Now that the convoys had arrived, the servants of various families immediately began deeper cleaning work.","This area instantly became lively.","Daili stepped out of the carriage and gathered together with Qin Hongying and Shi Rongyue to chat.","Daili did not come from a prominent family, so she might not be able to relate to the squabbles and dirty deeds of those large clans. Therefore, Qin Hongying automatically avoided topics in this area.","The other party was not a northerner, and she had never been to the south, so there was no topic to discuss regarding the other's hometown either.","There were simply too few points of intersection. Qin Hongying finally placed the topic on the younger generation, first asking about Qin Yanzhou's health.","Dai Li looked at her son who was wandering around not far away. \"...Zhouzhou has recovered very well. Thank you for your medicinal herbs, Hongying. Otherwise, even if Old Mr. Ding had matchless medical skills, the cleverest housewife cannot cook without rice.\"","Qin Hongying smiled, \"No need to thank me. Yanzhou is a blessed child, and he later saved Qinian and Rongrong, which can be considered karma. When I brought Rongrong to Yuyang before, I was worried that she would have no playmates here and would be bored. I didn't expect that when Yanzhou and Qinian had a rabbit-hunting competition, they were actually willing to bring her along.\"","Approving of her daughter and little nephew spending time together before marriage was one thing, but the two of them being alone would be too conspicuous. Adding Qin Yanzhou made it perfect; to outsiders, it was just a cousin taking his younger sister out to play.","A trace of surprise flashed across Dai Li's eyes, \"Rongrong is going too?\"","The little girl nodded and said yes. After speaking, she felt that Dai Li's question was unusual and looked at her cautiously.","Dai Li smiled: \"Let her go, it's actually for the best.\"","As for what was for the best, Dai Li didn't say.","The morning of the first day of the winter hunt was mainly for setting up camp and socializing. Except for the young gentlemen who rode their horses out, everyone else basically stayed at the base camp.","Visiting this one, making connections with that one.","Wei Cheng was also here, coming to the winter hunt with her husband's family, the Zous. She seemed to have lost a piece of her memory. The person who had previously spoken with veiled barbs was now coming with several of her sisters-in-law from the Wei family to pay their respects to Dai Li, showing her the utmost humility.","The second signal spread silently.","Soon, Dai Li was surrounded by a group of noble ladies, and words of compliment and flattery filled her ears. Even the smallest details about her could be praised to the skies. She was getting dizzy from seeing so many smiling faces.","Her eyes were filled with swaying phoenix hairpins, swaying willow waists, and fragrant breezes.","The young ladies followed their mothers, lining up to pay their respects to Dai Li.","Dai Li only felt that one delicate flower passed by, and another came over, softly introducing themselves.","The myriad of flowers gradually dazzled her eyes, and she couldn't remember any of the names.","Dai Li: \"...\"","Finally managing to extricate herself from the group of noble ladies, Dai Li sat in the already pitched tent, feeling as if she had finally come back to life.","She wasn't socially awkward, nor did she dislike socializing, but she really couldn't handle crowds and lines of people swarming her like an assembly line.","Qin Hongying looked at her sitting quietly holding a cup of hot tea, her eyes vacant, and immediately smiled, \"My second brother's achievements will absolutely not end here. You will have to face much more in the future.\"","Dai Li rubbed the space between her eyebrows.","In the morning, the various families set up their camps and established connections. After noon, Dai Li, who was resting in the tent, received a message from Qin Shaozong.","He had Hu Bao bring a verbal message, asking if she wanted to go watch the ceremony.","The ceremony, the small ceremony marking the official start of the winter hunt.","At that time, Dai Li had just finished lunch and was overwhelmed by sleepiness. The tent was warm, and she didn't want to move. Moreover, Qin Shaozong had asked if she wanted to, rather than directly telling her to come over, so she declined Hu Bao.","Shortly after, Dai Li heard the sound of horns.","Following that was the neighing of horses trampling the snow, and a group of people set off.","Dai Li took a short nap in the tent and woke up to find that Qin Shaozong had returned at some point.","\"Madam wakes up right on time.\" He was boiling tea.","Dai Li supported her hair bun, from which the hair ornaments had already been removed, and sat up. \"Isn't My Lord going hunting?\"","Qin Shaozong remained calm and composed. \"If I set off at noon and returned empty-handed in the evening, would Madam tell me that the outcome has been decided?\"","Dai Li paused for a moment and smiled, saying she would.","A day is a day, regardless of when he sets off, as long as he sets off, the timer starts.","\"There you have it. I will set off early tomorrow morning to hunt a tiger.\" Qin Shaozong changed the subject, \"How did Madam chat with the young ladies from various families this morning? Are there any young ladies that caught your eye?\"","Doubt appeared in Dai Li's eyes, \"Young ladies that caught my eye?\"","\"Qin Yanzhou has just reached adulthood. A grown man should marry, and a grown woman should be wed... Madam, please do not look at me with such eyes. I didn't say he should get married immediately, just that this major life event can begin to be planned. The young ladies showing their faces at this winter hunt are basically unbetrothed and all come from prominent families, so their backgrounds won't be too bad. If there are any that catch Madam's eye, it wouldn't hurt to call them over for a few words and then let Qin Yanzhou meet them.\" Qin Shaozong's voice was calm.","Compared to his initial strong rhetoric insisting on \"the orders of parents and the words of matchmakers,\" Dai Li knew that Qin Shaozong's willingness to let Zhouzhou meet them was already a huge improvement.","So she didn't give him a cold shoulder, but only said gently, \"In my eyes, they are all about the same. The winter hunt has just begun. Let the child play for now, and I'll ask him later.\"","Qin Shaozong lowered his eyes, \"So there are none that Madam fancies.\"","Dai Li caught a whiff of something unusual, \"Qin Changgeng, what are you trying to do?\"","\"What could I do?\" Qin Shaozong asked with a smile.","Dai Li looked him up and down suspiciously.","He","spoke of other things, \"The two older boys are of similar age. After the winter hunt, we can prepare for their capping ceremonies together. Have you thought of a courtesy name for Qin Yanzhou? Will you choose it yourself, Madam, or will you let Nalan Wugong choose it?\"","A man is capped at twenty and given a courtesy name. The capping ceremony marks adulthood, meaning he can stand on his own.","Dai Li's attention was diverted, \"Let me think about it.\"","...","The first day of the winter hunt ended amidst the hustle and bustle. Those who rode horses out to hunt today were mostly young men in their teens and twenties, with fewer older men.","It wasn't that they didn't want to go, but upon hearing that Qin Shaozong would only set off tomorrow, they involuntarily pushed their schedules back.","There were very few military generals among them. They were used to living in luxury. One day of high-intensity exercise might be fine, but two consecutive days would inevitably be strenuous.","The night slowly passed amidst the occasional howling of wolves in the surroundings. The weather the next day was just as good. The sun hid behind the clouds, the sky was a clear blue, and the snow was not glaring.","Perhaps because she had something on her mind, when Dai Li noticed movement beside her today, she woke up immediately.","Opening her eyes to a small slit, she roughly took in the situation, then accurately grabbed the arm of the man beside her and pulled him back, \"Won't you sleep a little longer?\"","Caught off guard, Qin Shaozong actually fell towards her a bit. But it was only a bit. Before he pressed down on her, he relied on his core strength to straighten up again.","He turned his head to look into the bed. The woman in the cherry-red inner garment was sunk in the brocade quilt, with skin like snow, hair like satin, a face like flawless jade, and that spot of dark red between her eyebrows perfectly matching the cherry red of her clothes.","She slowly opened her eyes, her beautifully shaped peach-blossom eyes rippling with water. Nestled in the soft bed looking at him, she appeared even more alluring.","The veins on the side of Qin Shaozong's neck tightened, and a wisp of dark fire emerged in his brown eyes. \"Madam.\"","Dai Li slowly sat up. Her black hair slid past her snow-white neck and the open collar of her inner garment, faintly revealing her moving plumpness.","\"My Lord, keep me company and sleep a little longer.\" she pressed against him from behind and to the side, her soft arms wrapping around his neck, hooking him towards the soft bed.","A rich fragrance floated at the tip of his nose, that warm, fragrant, and soft jade pressed against his back shoulder, and her fair fingers affectionately stroked his cheek.","The dark fire in Qin Shaozong's eyes surged, and his mountainous desire clamored for him to devour this annoying fox.","But, it was daylight.","From now on, every quarter of an hour was extremely precious.","\"Husband.\" she breathed out like orchids, and finally, her red lips kissed the corner of his mouth.","Qin Shaozong's tall frame stiffened. He turned around and fiercely pinned the woman back down into the soft bed. \"Seducing me? Fine!\"","The heat inside the main tent steadily rose.","...","By the time Qin Shaozong had tidied himself up and stepped out of the tent, it was already eight in the morning.","\"My Lord, your breakfast...\" Before Nianxia could finish her sentence, she watched the man casually grab some dry rations and stride off without a backward glance.","Nianxia looked at the steaming bowl of noodle soup in her hands and muttered in confusion, \"What could be so urgent that the Lord won't even stop for his noodles?\"","Inside the tent, Dai Li nonchalantly put on her clothes.","Qin Shaozong had kept his plans to hunt a tiger today a secret. The main reason was that if the news spread, a bunch of dead weight would inevitably swarm around him.","He mounted his horse and led a squad of men hurriedly toward the mountains. However, just as they entered the woods, two loud clangs echoed from deep within the forest, sounding exactly like a struck gong.","Qin Shaozong and his entourage were all momentarily stunned.","\"Who is beating a gong?\"","The moment the words left his mouth, a few more clattering sounds rang out from another direction.","It was like a chaotic musical performance—clanging over here, cymbals crashing over there, and surprisingly, someone was even blowing a suona horn.","The entire forest was filled with a cacophony of noises, rising and falling, ringing endlessly in their ears.","Qin Shaozong's face instantly turned pitch black."]},{"number":128,"title":"Chapter 128","paragraphs":["The young man, dressed in a black and red patchwork martial arts suit, squatted on the ground, staring unblinkingly at the pitch-black hole. For a moment, a small black shadow darted out of the hole with a \"whoosh\".","The young man was quick-witted, grabbed the rabbit's two ears and lifted it up. He smiled to reveal a row of white teeth, \"Found another one, hahaha, quick, strike the gong!\"","\"Clang, clang——\"","The follower neatly struck the gong, took out a small notebook, and meticulously wrote the first horizontal stroke of the character \"Zheng\".","Qin Qinian stood up with the rabbit, \"It's still faster to find rabbit holes. Just hunting rabbits is too inefficient.\"","Ten rabbits are only worth one rabbit hole with live rabbits, so of course they should put their effort into the latter.","\"Xuenu, quick, let's go find the next rabbit hole,\" Qin Qinian shouted into the hole.","Soon, another small creature, entirely snow-white, ran out of the pitch-black hole. The animal had a slender body, short limbs, a triangular head, large ears, and a fluffy tail. It was clearly a sable.","The snow sable climbed up the young man's shoulder along his lowered hand with a \"whoosh\". Qin Qinian was in high spirits, \"Let's go, let's continue to other places. We can't let them get ahead...\"","As soon as he finished speaking, he heard the sound of cymbals and suonas. He let out an \"ouch\" and said, \"Qin Yanzhou and Rongrong are close behind, so I can't fall behind even more!\"","He hurriedly led his people to find the next rabbit hole. Along the way, he unexpectedly saw a wild rabbit. Qin Qinian didn't miss this opportunity to score points.","The young man drew his bow and shot an arrow, never missing his target.","\"Clang, clang——\"","Two more gong sounds.","Anxious in his heart, Qin Qinian acted quickly. He lifted the rabbit and hurried to other places, not stopping for a moment.","He didn't know that shortly after he left, a group of people followed the sound to the place he had just been.","As a result, they missed him.","Looking at the traces on the ground, Qin Shaozong had already guessed what the other party was hunting. Just as he was about to order his subordinates to pass on an order, he heard two \"clang clang\" sounds again.","His five senses were sharper than others, and he was holding back anger in his heart. Now the sound of gongs and cymbals followed one after another, making Qin Shaozong's temples throb, and he even felt a little headache.","He dismissed the idea of sending someone over and went over personally again.","...","Qin Qinian was \"clang clang clang clang\" all the way. He had a fruitful harvest and was satisfied. Just as he was about to mount his horse and continue forward, he heard the sound of approaching horse hooves from behind.","The snow-covered twigs trembled slightly, and the snow fell rustling down.","There was definitely more than one rider.","Qin Qinian looked back curiously. From a distance, he saw a burly man in a black robe riding towards him.","The horse's hooves stepped on the snow, moving at lightning speed. The other party's momentum was majestic, and his clothes were blown into sharp arcs by the wind.","Winter was cold, and if the wind blew, it would be even colder. But the young man was hot-blooded. Qin Qinian hadn't felt cold since he woke up this morning, except for this moment——","A cold wind blew from nowhere, making Qin Qinian's back feel chilly.","Especially after meeting those narrow eyes, Qin Qinian wondered if it was an illusion, but he seemed to see rolling flames and lightning flashing with purple light in the sky.","Qin Qinian's scalp tingled slightly, and his hair stood on end inexplicably. He immediately stood to the side, making way, and motioned for his attendants to stand aside so as not to block the way.","After everything was ready, Qin Qinian kept his eyes and nose focused, waiting for his father to completely pass by.","But the red dragon stopped in front of him.","\"Qin San.\" Two heavy words fell.","This ominous tone made the young man subconsciously shrink his neck, but his mind quickly thought it over.","No, what was he afraid of? He hadn't done anything bad!","Thinking of this, Qin Qinian instantly stood up straight and even took the initiative to talk to Qin Shaozong: \"Father, I heard wolves howling everywhere last night. There must be a pack of wolves nearby. Are you going to hunt wolves?\"","Qin Shaozong sneered, \"With you around, your father won't be able to hunt a single hair.\"","Feng Feng, who was following Qin Shaozong, kept winking at Qin Qinian, motioning him to look at the guard holding the gong.","But at this moment, Qin Qinian couldn't see anything else. He was shocked by his father's words and said without hesitation, \"How could that be? Your son is hunting rabbits, not competing with you.\"","Feng Feng's mouth twitched.","Qin Shaozong's face darkened a degree.","Did this kid really not understand, or was he pretending?","Truly enraged, Qin Shaozong whipped the young man in front of him with his horsewhip, \"You bastard!\"","Qin Qinian dodged subconsciously, but the tip of the whip still brushed his arm. He had thick skin and was used to being beaten. At this moment, compared to the pain, he felt more wronged, \"I don't hunt wild beasts, why did you hit me, Father?\"","\"Who told you to beat gongs and drums everywhere? You take a broken gong and go clang clang clang everywhere. The wild beasts run away when they hear the sound. How are others supposed to hunt?\" Qin Shaozong gritted his teeth.","Qin Qinian choked, realizing belatedly that the problem was the gong.","\"I was doing it because...\"","\"Clash clash——\"","At this time, the cymbals not far away started ringing again. After this side finished ringing, there were suonas playing.","Qin Shaozong got a headache from hearing it and called Feng Feng's name, \"Feng Feng, go and confiscate all those broken cymbals and broken suonas for me.\"","Feng Feng took the order and quickly led his men into the forest.","After Feng Feng left, Qin Shaozong looked at his youngest son again, \"What did you just say?\"","Qin Qinian swallowed his saliva, \"Father, there's a reason I was beating the gong. Qin Yanzhou, Rongrong, and I are competing to see who can hunt more rabbits and find more rabbit holes. Beating the gong is for communication, so we can inform each other of our progress.\"","\"Clash clash——\"","The cymbals not far away were still ringing.","The veins on Qin Shaozong's forehead throbbed twice more.","No need to ask, he had already guessed which little bastard came up with this idea.","No, maybe it wasn't a little bastard, it was a bad fox.","\"Father, I won't continue beating the gong. Can I go now?\" Qin Qinian was still thinking about the competition.","The gong was confiscated, but it didn't mean the competition was over.","He had to hurry up.","\"Get lost. If you cause trouble for your father everywhere again, see how I deal with you.\" Qin Shaozong ordered someone to confiscate Qin Qinian's gong and led his people to continue inward.","But after walking a long way, the harsh \"clash clash\" sound lingered in his ears, making Qin Shaozong furious.","This sound kept ringing. Not to mention tigers, bears, and other beasts, even larger herbivores like deer completely disappeared.","\"Did Feng Feng not eat breakfast today? Qiao Wangfei, you lead your men over there too.\"","...","Feng Feng didn't know that his superior had grown disgusted with him. If he knew, he would definitely be extremely depressed.","It wasn't that he wasn't doing his best, it was that he really couldn't catch the person.","For some reason, the other party seemed to know he was coming to catch them. They would knock for a while, stop for a while, and run very fast. When they had run enough, there would be two more \"clash clash\" sounds, which was no different from a provocation.","Feng Feng was so depressed that he almost vomited blood, and once doubted whether the other party was playing him.","However, not finding the cymbals didn't mean he had no harvest. He found the source of the suona sound, but the owner surprised him extremely.","“Young Lady Shi?”","Shi Rongyue was just holding a little white rabbit when she turned her head at the sound. She had met Feng Feng before and knew that he was the Platoon Commander of the Black Brave Cavalry.","However, she didn’t remember having any interactions with him.","At this time, Shi Rongyue didn’t pay too much attention to it. She merely gave Feng Feng a slight nod and then said to the person beside her, “Blow it.”","Feng Feng: “...”","“No, no, no!” Feng Feng hurriedly tried to stop it, but he was a step too late and could only watch helplessly as the suona blared “ba ba”.","In the Great Yan Dynasty, the suona was basically used as the musical accompaniment for folk weddings, funerals, and festive ceremonies. Now that the suona sounded, Feng Feng felt that his soul had been sent away along with it.","While the “ba ba” sound continued vigorously over there, Feng Feng wiped his face in despair.","“Platoon Commander Feng, what are you looking for me for?” Shi Rongyue asked.","Feng Feng dismounted from his horse. He didn’t answer Shi Rongyue’s question immediately, but walked silently toward the soldier. Snatching the suona from the soldier’s hand, Feng Feng couldn’t help but kick him in the butt, “Did you grow ears for nothing? Step aside.”","Seeing this, Shi Rongyue frowned, “Platoon Commander Feng, what is the meaning of this?”","“The Marquis has ordered that no musical instruments be used in the hunting ground.” Feng Feng coughed lightly and explained, “Once the instruments sound, the fierce beasts are scared away, making it difficult to hunt. I hope Young Lady Shi can forgive us.”","Shi Rongyue pursed her lips.","Since it was an order from Second Uncle, there was really nothing to be done.","“Young Lady Shi, I have to go find the person with the cymbals. I will take my leave first.” Feng Feng cupped his hands to her.","Shi Rongyue curtsied in return. While looking down, she seemed to think of something. After the other party got on his horse, the young girl also climbed onto horseback and followed behind Feng Feng.","Feng Feng glanced back but didn’t say anything more.","The “cha cha” sound of the cymbals was still ringing.","Qiao Wangfei and Feng Feng followed the sound and attacked from both sides, finally catching the last source of the noise.","“Young Master Qin, musical instruments are not allowed in the hunting ground. Please hand over the cymbals to us.” Feng Feng looked as if he was facing a formidable enemy.","Along the way here, a smart person like Feng Feng had already figured out some clues on his own.","When had the Marquis ever been so low-key when hunting tigers in the past? Moreover, he had clearly seen the Marquis eating dry rations earlier, quickly and casually. No matter how you looked at it, it seemed like he was in a hurry.","Now that there was a case of playing music in the hunting ground, the leaders were actually Young Master Qin and the Third Young Master.","Something was wrong!","Could it be that Young Master Qin was secretly...","But what surprised both Feng Feng and Qiao Wangfei was that the young man who was stopped not only obediently handed over the cymbals but also handed over the accompanying attendants around him.","He was extremely cooperative, looking as if he clearly realized his mistake.","Holding the cold cymbals in his hands, Feng Feng was in a daze for a moment, feeling that it was somewhat unreal. However, completing the task was a good thing. He cupped his hands to Qin Yanzhou, “The matter is settled. We will go back and report first.”","Feng Feng and Qiao Wangfei left with their men.","Shi Rongyue had observed the whole way and felt quite strange in her heart, vaguely noticing something. She dismounted and stepped forward, “Young Master Qin, my suona was also confiscated. How about we just don’t use musical instruments for the rest of the competition and just count the numbers?”","Qin Yanzhou looked at the retreating figures of Feng Feng and the others and smiled almost imperceptibly, “No, we still have to use them.”","Shi Rongyue was stunned, “Still use them? But the instruments were taken away, and Second Uncle won’t let us use them either.”","Qin Yanzhou said, “You don’t have to use them, but I will still use them.”","Shi Rongyue’s eyebrows twitched slightly: “Young Master Qin, actually, is it...”","She choked for a moment, and her subsequent words turned into, “Then, then I’ll use them with you.”","Qin Yanzhou looked at the little girl who only reached his lips. She was currently looking up at him slightly, her light brown eyes like pomelo konpeito hidden in glass.","The young man shook his head, “You clearly realized it, so why take the risk with me?”","Shi Rongyue had indeed realized it. When she followed Feng Feng over just now, she had been pondering it along the way. The strange feeling reached its peak when Qin Yanzhou said “still have to use them”.","He was doing it on purpose.","“We agreed on it at the time.” Shi Rongyue smiled, “Besides, the law does not punish the masses.”","Qin Yanzhou: “...Two people don’t count as the masses.”","“I heard that Second Uncle has never raised a hand against young ladies, and my mother will definitely help me. You don’t need to worry, Young Master Qin.” The dimples on Shi Rongyue’s face deepened.","Qin Yanzhou pondered for a moment, “Follow me first.”","Qin Yanzhou’s attendants had all been dismissed, while those following Shi Rongyue were the people Qin Hongying had brought from the Shi family in Nanyu.","Strictly speaking, they were Shi Rongyue’s own people.","They rode their horses for a distance. Qin Yanzhou stopped his horse in front of a crooked neck tree. He looked around and finally selected a spot to dig. Before long, a new gong and cymbals were dug out of the snow pile.","Shi Rongyue: “!”","*","“Marquis, the cymbals and suona have all been retrieved.” Feng Feng returned with the items and reported, “The cymbals were used by Young Master Qin, and the suona was blown by someone ordered by Young Lady Shi.”","Qin Shaozong remained expressionless and was not surprised.","Although that brat Qin San was noisy, he definitely couldn’t come up with such a wicked idea.","Qin Shaozong: “Since it has been resolved, let’s go.”","Tigers generally wouldn’t appear on the outskirts of the forest. More than half an hour later, just as this imposing tiger hunting team attempted to drive straight in—","“Dang dang dang!”","The familiar sound of the gong drifted over again.","After the gong sounded, there was also the sound of cymbals. It was like singing an opera; one would sing and the other would rest.","Qin Shaozong flew into a rage, “Didn’t you say they had all been confiscated?”","Feng Feng and Qiao Wangfei were both dumbfounded.","Feng Feng hurriedly said, “Marquis, at that time Young Master Qin only had one pair of cymbals. This subordinate indeed took them away, Old Qiao can testify.”","Qiao Wangfei nodded, “He carried very few things.”","Hunting emphasizes being light and agile, so the items carried are generally not too many, usually a bow and arrows, a knife, a water skin, and a net for catching prey.","Absolutely no one would carry a large backpack, so whether they hid anything was truly obvious at a glance.","Qin Shaozong took a deep breath, “That little brat must have hidden the things elsewhere. You two lead people to keep an eye on him and don’t let him continue to make trouble.”","The two cupped their hands in acknowledgement and immediately led their men to follow the sound.","...","Qin Qinian also heard the sound of cymbals and... gongs.","Gongs?","The young man pricked up his ears and listened again. It was indeed the sound of a gong.","But what was going on? Wasn’t it agreed that Qin Yanzhou would use the cymbals, Rongrong would use the suona, and he would beat the gong? But now his gong had been taken away by his father, so where did this gong sound come from?","However, this doubt only circled in his mind for a moment before Qin Qinian cast it aside.","Who cares why, hunting rabbits is more important.","As a result, Qin Qinian had just walked a short distance with high morale when he was stopped by Feng Feng, who he bumped into.","“Third Young Master, can you stop for a while?” Feng Feng urged earnestly, “The Marquis’s mood seems unclear today, so please don’t add fuel to the fire.”","“What nonsense are you talking about? How am I not stopping?” Qin Qinian was confused, and then he belatedly became angry, “It wasn’t me beating the gong just now!”","Feng Feng's eyes filled with suspicion, but after glancing around, he indeed saw no sign of a gong.","No?","Then who was bold enough to do this?","It was indeed not him, for the gong sounded once more.","\"Clang, clang, clang—\"","Instead of striking twice, it was hit three times in a row.","Qin Qinian let out a breath of frustration. \"See? It really wasn't me!\"","Looking embarrassed, Feng Feng cupped his hands and apologized. \"My apologies, Third Young Master. I still have a mission to attend to, so I shall not disturb your leisure any longer.\"","With that, he hurriedly led his men away.","Qin Qinian watched his retreating back and muttered, \"Something isn't right. Only the three of us knew about using sounds to signal the rabbit hunt. Where did these other gongs come from? Is it Qin Yanzhou? It must be him, but why would he act like this? Could it be that hunting rabbits and looking for rabbit holes was just a decoy...\"","CR","Qin Yanzhou led Shi Rongyue further in, narrowly avoiding two groups of people.","When they heard the sound of approaching hoofbeats for the third time, he turned to Shi Rongyue and said, \"Miss Shi, stay here for now. We must part ways temporarily.\"","At first glance, his words sounded unfeeling, but Shi Rongyue caught the underlying meaning. \"You want to face them alone?\"","This time, the people coming to catch them had brought a massive force. Just from the sound of the galloping hooves and the dust and shadows rising in the distance, it was clear there were many of them.","\"Young Master Qin, do you still plan to continue with your plans after this?\" Shi Rongyue asked.","Qin Yanzhou nodded. Not entirely sure what compelled him to explain, he added, \"What happens during daylight today is of the utmost importance.\"","Shi Rongyue suddenly asked, \"Do you have things hidden in other places? If you do, could you tell me? I can... help you.\"","Qin Yanzhou remained silent, simply looking at her.","His dark eyes were incredibly deep and quiet, like a still, mirror-like black pool that could reflect a person's innermost thoughts.","The young girl looked down at her toes, kicking at a little mound of snow with her white boots as she whispered, \"Once they find you, they will definitely keep a close eye on you. But I am different. I am a young lady, so I won't easily draw suspicion. Even if they see through my act, it wouldn't be appropriate for them to lay a hand on me. Young Master Qin, you saved my life. It is only right that I help you.\"","Qin Yanzhou's gaze shifted past her, sweeping over the several guards accompanying her.","These were the Shi family's personal guards. It was evident that Qin Hongying cared deeply for her daughter's safety; every guard assigned to her was robust and powerful. If they worked together, they would even stand a chance against a small pack of wolves.","\"You have my thanks, Miss Shi.\"","Shi Rongyue looked up in pleasant surprise, her amber eyes shining brightly. \"Don't worry, I will definitely get this done for you.\"","Dai Li remained at the main camp. Ever since Qin Shaozong set out, she would occasionally peek outside. Unfortunately, the sun hadn't come out today, making it difficult to judge the time by the height of the golden crow.","When the first sound of the gong drifted over, a satisfied smile touched the corners of her lips, and she began to leisurely eat her noodle soup.","The sounds of gongs, cymbals, and suonas started and stopped, echoing intermittently until they finally ceased entirely right at the hour of Wei.","In winter, the days were short and the nights were long; by the end of the hour of Shen, the sky would be completely dark. And the time between the hour of Wei and the end of the hour of Shen was little more than two hours.","\"How strange. Just who is out there beating gongs and drums all over the hunting grounds?\" Qin Hongying wondered aloud.","Dai Li was in an exceedingly good mood. \"Perhaps it is someone offering congratulations.\"","Qin Hongying misunderstood her meaning. \"Carrying a gong and drum around to strike in celebration upon hunting a fierce beast—that is quite a novel idea.\"","Dai Li smiled but said nothing.","...","Two hours later, the daylight gradually faded, and the firmament was draped in a thin veil of black. Ever since dusk fell, the sunlight was swallowed up at an increasingly rapid pace, until in the blink of an eye, only a faint sliver remained.","Just as the last ray of sunlight in the sky was extinguished and the main camp lit its torches, Qin Shaozong returned.","Hearing the successive calls of \"The Marquis has returned,\" Dai Li eagerly went out to greet him.","Not far away, the man sat astride a crimson steed. Dressed in a black robe and carrying a longbow on his back, his posture was heroic and extraordinary. Flanked by a throng of attendants, his imposing aura felt as vast as the mountains and seas.","However, that was all there was to it.","Let alone fierce beasts like tigers and bears, he had not even brought back secondary prey like wolves and deer.","Dai Li instantly bloomed with joy, her eyes curving into happy crescents.","And just as Dai Li saw Qin Shaozong, he saw her as well. He watched her rush out in a flurry, take one look at him, and then beam with a smile as beautiful as a flower.","That smile was genuinely radiant, even brighter and more brilliant than the clear moon that had already revealed itself in the sky.","Qin Shaozong ground his back teeth, his expression turning even fouler.","In his thirty-odd years, he had gone on countless hunts. He had hunted tigers, beaten black bears, shot down packs of wolves, and even harvested the white deer that symbolized auspiciousness.","The only thing he had never done was return empty-handed.","But it couldn't be helped; there was absolutely nothing along his path. He hadn't encountered a single large animal. As for the smaller prey, Qin Shaozong disdained the thought of bringing them back.","Bringing a mere rabbit back to see her would be worse than not returning at all...","The people gathering around, who had originally intended to flatter and congratulate him, looked at one another in dismay, momentarily at a loss for words.","It was truly a sight rarely seen in a lifetime—the Marquis of Wu'an had actually returned empty-handed?","\"You have worked hard, My Lord,\" Dai Li said with a smile, walking up to his crimson steed.","Qin Shaozong gritted his teeth. \"You look exceedingly cheerful, Madam.\"","\"Of course. I am happier than anyone else that you have returned safely from the tiger's jaws, My Lord. Whether you caught any prey or not does not matter. If there is nothing this time, we can simply wait for the next.\" Dai Li smiled brightly, even reaching out to steady his reins.","Qin Shaozong vaulted off his horse. \"Today cannot be considered a failure.\"","Dai Li looked at him in confusion. Meeting those narrow eyes surging with dark fire, her brow twitched.","\"I indeed failed to hunt a tiger, but I did catch a wicked fox. Later tonight, I will most certainly strip this fox bare and spread it out for you to take a very good look at, Madam.\" His final sentence sounded as though it had been squeezed out through his teeth."]},{"number":129,"title":"Chapter 129","paragraphs":["Daili couldn't care less about being stripped bare.","He was just talking tough, let him.","Qin Changgeng didn't hunt a tiger within the specified time, so no matter what, she won this bet.","If it was just about talking, anyone could do it. Daili deliberately raised her voice and said, \"What fox? Did the Marquis hunt a fox on this trip? Is it a white fox or a red fox, alive or dead? Don't hide it, bring it out quickly and let me see.\"","Qin Shaozong: \"...\"","Feng Feng, who accompanied him, knew exactly what prey they had brought back, and quickly smoothed things over: \"We did hunt a red fox, but later we found out that the mother fox was pregnant. The Marquis couldn't bear to kill it, so he let it go.\"","Daili praised: \"The Marquis is benevolent and loves all creatures. He is a noble person who abides by the hunting rules.\"","She deliberately emphasized the word \"abides\".","Qin Shaozong was really amused by her anger, \"Madam has an excellent memory. It's a pity you're not an accountant.\"","\"Thank you for your guidance, Marquis.\" Daili took it as a compliment.","The impact of the gongs and cymbals was not small. Not only did Qin Shaozong return empty-handed, but the other people who went hunting today also got nothing.","It wasn't that no one was angry, but when they learned that the \"instigators\" were Qin Qinian and Qin Yanzhou, they all fell silent.","So it was the boys being mischievous. Fine, let the Marquis of Wu'an teach them a lesson himself.","Although everyone returned empty-handed today, the evening bonfire banquet was held as usual.","The meat was hunted by those young men yesterday. Part of it was eaten at the banquet last night, but it wasn't completely finished. The deer and roe deer with broken legs were kept. They were originally intended to be brought back as trophies, but unexpectedly became a reserve food supply.","The bonfire was lit, and the wooden spears skewered with meat were placed over the fire. As the meat gradually turned golden brown, oil slowly dripped out.","The butter dripped down after a short while, and the flames shot up like snakes, making the aroma instantly richer.","However, tonight, few people focused their attention on the food. For no other reason, as long as one wasn't blind, anyone could see that Qin Shaozong was not in a good mood.","Invisible dark clouds covered the sky and blocked the sun. Faint rumbling thunder could be heard, but it remained hidden and unreleased.","Everyone sat upright, being cautious in their words and actions.","The man beside her had a gloomy air pressure, and the surrounding atmosphere was also very strange. But Daili didn't care about that. She ate heartily, her appetite much better than last night.","After eating this skewer of meat, she reached out to get a frozen persimmon. Her snow-white cheeks bulged a little, and her red lips were shiny with oil, as if coated with a layer of honey.","Qin Shaozong looked at Daili a few times, but he didn't know if she didn't notice or was too lazy to pay attention to him. She didn't turn her head once.","Qin Shaozong sneered coldly and reached out to take a skewer of meat.","Daili was sitting right beside him. She saw his movement clearly, and her chewing paused.","What he just took seemed to be... venison.","Daili couldn't help but turn her head, just in time to see this man eating meat in big mouthfuls. His sharp white canine teeth bit hard into the meat, and his light brown eyes locked tightly onto her. The dark fire in his eyes was even more intense than the blazing bonfire in front of them.","Daili's heart skipped a beat.","In no time, Qin Shaozong finished a skewer of venison, and then went to get a new one.","This time he still took venison.","He still looked at her while eating meat in big mouthfuls, as if the meat he was biting was her. In a few bites, a large skewer of venison was completely devoured by him.","Qin Shaozong reached out again, wanting to take a third skewer.","Daili's alarm bells rang instantly. She quickly reached out and pressed his arm, \"A balanced diet of meat and vegetables is the right way. The Marquis has already eaten enough meat. How about having some frozen persimmons?\"","While asking \"how about\", Daili forcefully snatched the skewer of venison from his hand and stuffed two frozen persimmons into it.","Venison is known as the \"fruit of the kidneys\". Qin Changgeng was passionate about matters of the bed, and once he started, he would go on endlessly. He also had a powerful engine himself. If she let him continue eating, he would probably stay up all night making a fuss.","Having his venison snatched away, Qin Shaozong didn't say anything. He took the frozen persimmon and bit into it.","The bite mark was very deep. The bright red inside of the frozen persimmon looked like some kind of open meat, making Daili's spine tense up.","The bonfire banquet ended in a strange atmosphere. Dinner was over, and it was time to rest.","Daili's eyebrows moved slightly. Just as she was about to tell Qin Shaozong that she was going to find Qin Hongying, she suddenly felt her wrist being grabbed. Then an irresistible force pulled her up.","\"Madam, it's late. Let's go back.\" He stared at her intently.","Daili: \"...\"","*","Inside the main tent.","The heavy curtain in front of the tent door hung down, completely separating the inside from the outside. The winter chill and piercing wind vanished without a trace with the fall of the curtain.","The temperature inside the tent quietly rose.","Qin Shaozong took off his cloak and casually draped it over the coat rack. He approached Daili, his eyes brewing with heavy dark fire, \"Madam was very impressive today, strategizing and playing me like a fiddle.\"","His aura was overwhelming, a head taller than Daili. Even without his cloak, he was still as burly as a mountain.","\"Qin Changgeng, when we made the bet, we didn't specify that tricks couldn't be used.\" As he advanced, Daili unconsciously retreated.","Qin Shaozong stepped forward step by step, trapping her near the corner of the soft bed. His tone was unclear: \"This move of beating the grass to scare the snake was very ingenious. Whose idea was it? Madam's, or that boy Qin Yanzhou's?\"","Daili wanted to retreat further, but unexpectedly there was a soft bed behind her. She accidentally tripped and lost her balance, falling onto the soft bed. She was already not as tall as him, and now that she had fallen, she was almost completely enveloped by his shadow.","She sat there, looking up at him.","\"If it was Madam's idea, tonight I will definitely make Madam dry up like a river and sea. If that boy Qin Yanzhou thought of it himself...\"","Qin Shaozong suddenly smiled. Daili couldn't understand this smile. It wasn't sarcasm, anger, or annoyance, but another kind of emotion. What exactly it was, she couldn't say at this moment, but she acutely sensed that it was positive.","Daili had always trusted her intuition.","Whether it was when she climbed a tree in the Jiang mansion and felt something was wrong, or later when she felt faintly uneasy in the teahouse in Taiping County, it was her sixth sense helping her.","At this moment, she inexplicably felt that perhaps she could tell the truth. He might really not cause trouble for Zhou Zhou.","\"If it was Zhou Zhou's idea, then what will you do?\" Daili couldn't help asking.","\"I won't pursue the matter with him, and I will deal with Madam leniently.\" This man said \"deal with leniently\", but his hand was actually resting on the beast-head belt around his waist. His long fingers with thick calluses unfastened the buckle.","Daili's mouth twitched.","She didn't speak, and Qin Shaozong didn't urge her. After unfastening the belt, he pounced like a hungry tiger, pressing Daili down amidst her exclamations.","Qin Shaozong wrapped one arm around her waist, and his other large hand spread out to cup her jaw. Two fingers pinched her lips open through her soft cheeks, and then skillfully pried them open and entered.","The pent-up anger from the whole day finally flared up. He enveloped her in his shadow, sucking and biting her trembling lips, and then swept recklessly inside, like the most strict and cautious patrol, not letting go of a single corner.","Dai Li was already accustomed to his ways. Seeing him coming on so aggressively and setting such a high tone now, she inwardly cried out in dismay, hoping this night wouldn't truly last until dawn.","She raised her hand to press down on his hand, which had somehow hooked onto her waistband. Unable to speak, she wrapped her fingers around the belt twice and tugged it back, while trying her best to turn her head away.","\"Does My Lord not want to know the answer?\" her breath was already erratic.","The man propped himself up, actually managing to hold back and retreat a little. His gaze was like a torch, his brown eyes seemingly glowing in the dim light. \"Confess the truth.\"","\"Most of it was Zhou Zhou, I only helped him fill in the gaps,\" Dai Li said hesitantly.","Qin Changgeng had very good credit with her. He always did what he promised and had never broken his word once. Since he said he wouldn't pursue the matter with Zhou Zhou, then he truly wouldn't.","Just as these words fell, she did not know if it was her illusion, but she seemed to see him smile again, the same kind of smile as before.","Before Dai Li could carefully ponder it, the waistband that had been wrapped around her fingers was untied and swiftly pulled away. Once the entire strip was separated from her outer robe, it was wrapped around her wrists.","\"Madam's waistband is quite unique, lend it to me for a bit.\"","Dai Li was just about to struggle when his voice suddenly became strict and solemn. \"The guilty woman, Dai Li, has committed the crime of teasing her husband. This official now sentences her to three hundred lashes and to be stripped of her fox skin for the night, as a warning to others.\"","Dai Li was speechless.","Dai Li was greatly shocked. She was just about to retort when her mouth was blocked again.","...","Time passed, and the full moon in the sky gradually slanted westward.","The cold wind of the Northland howled loudly. In the night, pairs of faint green little lanterns flickered with a cold, sharp light. There were wolves howling all around, masking many sounds.","The night was deep, but there were still people who had not fallen into a sound sleep.","In the large tent, the door curtain had been lowered. The curtains on the opposite sides were rolled up a little to facilitate air circulation.","Inside the tent, it was blazing hot, and the fierce battle was at its peak.","Dai Li lay on her stomach on the soft bed, her hands tightly gripping the brocade quilt beneath her. She bit her red lips tightly, trying hard to suppress the sounds in her throat.","The temperature inside the tent was much higher than outside. A thin layer of sweat appeared on her temples, neck, and body. Her snow-white skin was steamed into a light pink hue, as if she had just been scooped out of a hot spring.","He was full of interest and relished the experience, using that bamboo-red waistband to measure many places.","\"Rest, let's rest for a moment...\" Dai Li had just finished a round, her eyes lacking focus.","\"The three hundred lashes are not even halfway done, how can we rest?\" Not only did he not listen, but he also conveniently took back the waistband that was currently tied directly around the woman's waist and tied it around her wrists again.","Dai Li laughed out of anger. \"Not halfway? You are lying through your teeth. I refuse to accept this, have your superior come speak with me.\"","He smiled wickedly, and also moved wickedly. \"Who in the hall is suing this official?\"","Dai Li was speechless again.","\"Qin Changgeng, you are shameless.\" Dai Li kicked her legs.","His large, vein-bulging hand reached over, fingers spread wide, tightly gripping that section of her pale thigh, with some tender white flesh spilling out between his fingers. \"To think you would hurl insults at an imperial court official. I punish you to start over from the beginning.\"","Dai Li was speechless.","\"However, this official is benevolent and can give you a chance for a pardon.\" He retreated a little, maintaining a half-withdrawn state as he flipped Dai Li over, making her face upwards.","He stared into her eyes, pointing out something implicitly. \"If Madam asks me to stop now, I will definitely obey the order.\"","Dai Li understood his underlying meaning.","He and she had made a bet, and the loser had to promise the winner one thing. This man clearly wanted her to use the prize on such an insignificant trivial matter.","Dai Li turned her head away. \"Standing firm through countless grinds and blows, letting the winds blow from all directions.\"","Qin Shaozong gave a fake smile. \"Not only do you not agree, you actually dare to compose a poem to mock this official. You deserve to be punished. The three hundred lashes are doubled, you are sentenced to take six hundred.\"","\"Qin Changgeng, I beg you to have some shame...\"","The winter night was long and endless. The two large skewers of venison Qin Shaozong had eaten all turned into firewood and dry grass this night, stewing the fox in the pot until she was completely disoriented.","Waking and sleeping throughout the night, Dai Li unsurprisingly woke up late the next day.","When she woke up, she noticed that there seemed to be quite a few people missing from the camp. Upon asking, she found out that some people had gone out hunting in the morning. And among these people were Qin Shaozong, as well as Qin Yanzhou and Qin Qinian.","...","After a night of recovery, a portion of the prey that had been scared away originally returned.","Last night, Qin Shaozong could not encounter any prey and had no chance to make a move, but this morning he ran into some.","They discovered a large roe deer.","\"Qin San, you go catch the roe deer,\" Qin Shaozong said.","Yesterday, while hunting rabbits, Qin Qinian was distracted by other things, which caused him to lose the competition. The young man was holding in a surge of energy with nowhere to use it. Now, hearing his father's words, he took two people and plunged headfirst into the forest.","Besides the roe deer, they had also encountered deer on the road just now, and Qin Shaozong similarly assigned tasks out. At this time, the number of people following by his side could be counted on one hand, and among these few people was Qin Yanzhou.","The young man rode his horse forward and dismounted when he reached Qin Shaozong's side. He cupped his hands to Qin Shaozong. \"One person takes responsibility for their own actions. They were merely acting on my orders. The source is me, and I can bear the consequences myself. I ask the Marquis of Wu'an to release them, and please do not make things difficult for Young Lady Shi.\"","The they Qin Yanzhou spoke of referred to those few personal guards brought over from the Shi family.","Yesterday, after Qin Yanzhou fell into the net, Shi Rongyue ran around with her personal guards. Midway, she specifically separated a group of people to go look for gongs and cymbals respectively. Two quarters of an hour after one fell into the net, another would strike, thereby dragging out the time that the cymbals and gongs could be struck as much as possible.","Afterwards, this group of people, including Shi Rongyue, were all arrested. And because Shi Rongyue's own status was special, she was released.","She was the only one released. The other personal guards of the Shi family were still being locked up by Qin Shaozong at this moment.","Qin Shaozong was still riding on the Red Dragon. At this time, he looked down at the person from a high position, but his tone was very calm. \"Why would the Shi family's personal guards listen to your orders?\"","Qin Yanzhou: \"It was I who requested Young Lady Shi to lend me a helping hand.\"","Qin Shaozong's long fingers tapped the horse whip rhythmically. \"You requested, and she agreed? Did she know the inside story?\"","Qin Yanzhou shook his head and said she did not know.","Qin Shaozong suddenly chuckled.","Whether she knew or not, after Shi Rongyue had her suona confiscated, she definitely knew that music was forbidden in the hunting grounds.","\"This little Shi Rongrong is quite audacious.\" He suddenly changed the subject, \"But last night I heard my Madam say that beating gongs and drums everywhere and dispersing the guards to act was all her idea...\"","\"No, it has nothing to do with Mother! I arranged this matter single-handedly. It was because I heard she had a bet with you, and the contents of this bet had no rule restrictions, that I had other thoughts.\" Qin Yanzhou could not help but interrupt.","Qin Shaozong's gaze patrolled his face, and after a moment, he replied, \"Alright, then let those people go.\"","He agreed too readily. He didn't even say anything else, made no demands, and didn't mention any follow-up.","Qin Yanzhou was slightly stunned.","Qin Shaozong understood his confusion. \"The art of war is of deception. In the past, during the Battle of Hongshui, Duke Xiang of Song rigidly adhered to ancient rules, stubbornly waiting for the Chu army to cross the river and form their ranks before attacking, and ultimately suffered a crushing defeat. Duke Xiang himself was also severely injured and fled in defeat. From then on, the hegemony of the Central Plains had nothing to do with him.\"","Qin Shaozong's eyes held a hint of mockery, clearly looking down upon such blockheaded behavior. \"On the battlefield, there isn't so much of 'can or cannot,' 'should or should not.' Once the horn blows, a battle only has two outcomes: success or failure.\"","Qin Yanzhou looked thoughtful.","\"Besides, come next spring, your mother will marry me and become my wife. By then, you will have to call me father. Why would I bicker with my own son?\" Qin Shaozong laughed.","Qin Yanzhou: \"...\"","After the hunting party returned and everyone had another round of meat, the various families began to break camp.","Today was the third day, the day this winter hunt concluded, and everyone was preparing to return to Yuyang.","The northern winds were piercingly cold. Daili had come in a carriage, and she would return in one as well. However, unlike before, there was an extra person in her carriage for the return trip.","The man dressed in a black robe leaned lazily against the soft seat. With his long arms and legs, he stretched out in an unrestrained posture, taking up a large portion of the space.","This carriage also had seating on only one side; the small table inside was pushed all the way to the front of the cabin, leaving only the long bench in the back for sitting.","When Daili arrived, she had worn a cloak, sinking into the warm lotus-green mink fur. Now, on the way back to the city, the cloak was set aside.","It simply wasn't needed.","Qin Shaozong was essentially a giant furnace himself; sitting next to him was incredibly warm.","\"Qin Changgeng, you went hunting with Zhou Zhou this morning. Did you say something to him?\" Daili suddenly asked.","When her son returned from the hunt this morning, although he didn't say anything and his expression remained as usual, Daili noticed some of his little habits.","He glanced at Qin Shaozong twice, seemingly curious.","Later, she overheard Qin Qinian mention that his father still hadn't hunted anything himself this morning, and her intuition told her something was off. If Qin Changgeng went out for a spin without hunting any prey, what was he doing out there?","Qin Shaozong picked up one of her hands, gently rubbing from the base of her palm all the way to her fingertips. \"That boy came to confess to me. He said he would take sole responsibility for his actions, and asked me to let Shi Rongrong and her guards go.\"","Daili couldn't help but sit up straight.","When they returned last night, she had been so caught up in her amusement that she forgot to ask for the details. It turned out this matter not only involved Zhou Zhou's handiwork but also implicated Shi Rongyue.","Before Daili could ask, Qin Shaozong continued, \"Since I already promised you last night, my lady, I naturally won't hold it against the younger generation.\"","Daili's spine relaxed, and she casually flattered him, \"The Marquis truly is a man of his word.\"","He brought up the previous matter again. \"Having lost to you this time, what is your request, my lady?\"","Worried that she would keep dragging it out and focus entirely on tampering with the Marriage Agreement, Qin Shaozong deliberately added, \"You must make your request today or tomorrow, my lady. Otherwise, the offer will expire.\"","Daili replied, \"Rest assured, I will tell you once we get back.\"","Qin Shaozong raised a long eyebrow. \"You can't do it now?\"","Daili still insisted, \"I'm missing a few things right now. Let's talk about it when we get back.\"","He did not press the issue further.","There were activities during the day, and both breaking camp and the journey back to the city took time. Therefore, by the time they returned to Yuyang, it was already dusk.","The brilliant afterglow covered the sky, dyeing the heavens into a beautiful oil painting. The main gates of the Qin Manor were wide open, with Qin Yunce, who had stayed behind to guard the residence, leading the welcoming party for their return.","\"The winter winds are harsh; Yunce, you didn't need to wait here.\" The carriage curtain was lifted, and Qin Shaozong frowned as he spoke.","Qin Yunce offered a deep bow. \"Thank you for your concern, Father. I have been feeling quite well lately; it is no trouble at all.\"","Qin Shaozong said, \"Let's go inside.\"","The carriage drove straight to the main courtyard. Qin Shaozong stepped down first, then raised his hand to help Daili out of the carriage.","After Daili entered the main room, she heard footsteps behind her and knew that Qin Shaozong had followed her in, instead of heading to his study as he usually did.","Daili turned to look at him.","Meeting her gaze, the man curled his lips into a smile. \"Now that we are home, feel free to state your request, my lady. Your husband will certainly grant your wish.\"","Daili suddenly asked, \"Did the Marquis bring his personal seal?\"","Qin Shaozong said he had.","Officials had official seals, and prominent families had their own personal seals. A personal seal was a form of credential, carrying the same legal weight as a signature. In some prestigious families, seeing the personal seal was akin to seeing the person themselves.","Daili went into the inner room and emerged a moment later holding two letters.","Qin Shaozong was already seated at the desk. His eyesight was excellent, and he clearly saw that one of the envelopes had Marriage Agreement written on it.","The curve of the man's lips instantly deepened.","Daili first placed the Marriage Agreement on the desk, sliding it forward until it was right in front of him. \"This is the Marriage Agreement I promised you earlier.\"","Almost the very second the letter came to a stop, he snatched it up.","\"However, I suggest the Marquis take a look at this one first,\" Daili suddenly added.","Qin Shaozong paused in his motion of opening the letter. Ultimately humoring her, he picked up the other envelope she had pushed over.","Nothing was written on this envelope, making it seem rather mysterious compared to the Marriage Agreement beside it.","Qin Shaozong tore it open, unfolding the mulberry paper inside.","But when his gaze touched the central title at the very top, his pupils suddenly shrank. His face turned ashen, and the smile on his lips quickly vanished.","The central title at the very top of the paper clearly read:","Divorce Agreement"]},{"number":130,"title":"Chapter 130","paragraphs":["In the Great Yan Dynasty, the concept of a mutual separation did not exist. The more modern term \"divorce,\" therefore, was even less likely to appear here.","However, the literal meaning of the two characters for \"divorce\" was self-evident. In this time and place, anyone who could read would understand their implication.","Li meant to leave.","Hun meant marriage.","Thus, after merely glancing at the title centered on the page, Qin Shaozong could read no further.","He only felt a surge of fury rise from the bottom of his heart, spreading through his limbs and bones with the force of a sweeping army, rushing straight to the top of his head. It made the veins on his neck bulge and twitch, and his vision went dark.","The Qin family was a prominent and aristocratic clan in the region. Although he was not the eldest legitimate son, he still bore the title of a legitimate heir. Since childhood, apart from his elders and older brothers of the same generation, who hadn't treated him with the utmost respect and profound humility?","When he came of age and took over the heavy burdens of the family, and was later conferred a title by the imperial court, the Qin clan directly honored him as their patriarch, following his every command.","Later, he continued to wage wars across the land, bringing the Ji and Bing provinces under his control and firmly grasping the entire North in the palm of his hand. It could be said that the entire situation in the North was at his fingertips.","His elders had passed away, and the Emperor of Han was far away in Chang'an. There was no longer anyone in the North who could make him bow his head, nor anyone who dared to show him even the slightest disrespect.","He had set his heart on taking her as his wife. They were not even married yet, but she had already handed him some sort of \"Divorce Agreement.\"","When had he ever suffered such an insult?","\"Absurd!\" He slammed the table and stood up.","Everything on the desk jumped, including the personal seal Qin Shaozong had taken out and the inkstick resting on the inkstone. The latter was jolted so hard it slid down the edge. The wet tip of the inkstick smacked onto the table, leaving a streak of ink.","Slapping the desk was not enough for him; he reached out, crumpled the \"Divorce Agreement\" into a ball, and threw it out the door with a swoosh.","Dai Li: \"...\"","Anyone else facing Qin Shaozong's thunderous rage would surely turn pale and tremble in fear, but this was not the first time Dai Li had provoked his anger, and she had anticipated this reaction.","\"It's not absurd.\"","Dai Li did not rush to pick up the agreement. Instead, she walked around the long desk to stand on the same side as Qin Shaozong. She took the initiative to hold his large, rough hand, trying to pull him back down to his seat.","On her first attempt, she couldn't move him.","The man stood as immovable as a mountain. He stared straight ahead, not even turning his head in the slightest. Were it not for his violently heaving chest and rapid breathing, Qin Shaozong would have looked more like a majestic and cold stone statue.","\"My Lord, do not be angry. There is a reason for this. Listen to me and I will explain it slowly,\" Dai Li said, raising a hand to gently stroke his chest.","Her voice was a soothing, gentle tone, like a flowing spring or the silent, nourishing spring rain.","Qin Shaozong turned his head to cast a sidelong glance at her. He didn't speak, but that heavy look clearly said: I don't want to hear it.","Seeing that he had at least reacted, Dai Li pulled his hand a second time, trying to get him to sit back down.","And this time, she still couldn't move him.","Dai Li said softly, \"In my homeland, there is no such thing as a 'Betrothal Reply Letter.' But since you wanted one, I granted your wish and learned how to write one, even though I had never written such a letter to any man before.\"","Qin Shaozong's expression remained ugly, but the terrifying pressure radiating from him dissipated slightly.","Dai Li began to spin a lie to deceive him. \"It's not that I'm deliberately making things difficult for you. It's just that where I come from, all men and women who are about to marry must sign a 'Divorce Agreement.' The purpose is so that in the future, if they grow to despise each other and can no longer live together, they can separate quickly.\"","Following his exclamation of \"Absurd,\" he finally spoke his second sentence:","\"Impossible,\" he said, his voice ice-cold.","Dai Li knew he wasn't exposing her lie; he was simply refuting the word \"separate.\"","She continued, \"Actually, not many people end up using this prenuptial agreement. Many loving couples leave it buried at the bottom of a chest for their entire lives, until it is mostly eaten by moths or naturally rots away, never seeing the light of day again. After all, the conditions in the agreement are not easily met. Or rather, if they are met, such a couple is basically estranged and there is no longer any need for them to be together...\"","Pausing for a moment, Dai Li's tone took on a hint of melancholy. \"I was willing to adapt to local customs for you, My Lord, and write a 'Betrothal Reply Letter' that I had never written before. Are you not willing to change even the slightest bit for me? Even if this agreement were taken to court, according to the laws of the Great Yan, it likely wouldn't be recognized anyway.\"","Hearing the last sentence, Qin Shaozong's expression softened slightly.","At this moment, Dai Li reached out to pull him for the third time. He finally moved, following her gentle force to sit back down.","Only then did Dai Li go to retrieve the crumpled ball of paper.","The mulberry paper had quite a bit of weight to it when crumpled. Moreover, since the man had been furious, his throw had not only sent it flying out the door but almost into the middle of the courtyard.","When Dai Li returned, she saw Qin Shaozong looking at the \"Betrothal Reply Letter.\" His expression was even better than before she went out.","Dai Li secretly curled the corners of her lips, quickly composing her expression before he looked up. But she soon noticed that the personal seal previously placed on the desk was gone.","Dai Li: \"...\"","She walked around behind the desk to sit beside Qin Shaozong and smoothed out the crumpled \"Divorce Agreement.\"","The displeasing title was glaringly obvious. The veins on Qin Shaozong's forehead twitched again, but this time he didn't immediately look away.","He forced himself to read on with patience.","The beginning was very brief, without much elaboration. It simply stated that if the married couple met any of the following conditions, they could separate.","Qin Shaozong took a deep breath, his gaze shifting imperceptibly to the side for a moment before he continued reading.","There were not many conditions; she had only listed three scenarios.","1. If either party in the marriage takes a new lover, the marriage shall be considered broken.","2. If the two parties have disagreements in their values, including but not limited to views on childbearing, and cannot reach a consensus, the marriage shall be considered broken.","3. If conflicts arise involving the children of either party, and the conflicts are irreconcilable, the marriage shall be considered broken.","After reading the first clause, Qin Shaozong simply skipped past it.","Her taking a new lover?","If she actually did, he could make this so-called new lover immediately reincarnate, turning a reality into nothingness.","He paused slightly upon reading the second clause, then skipped it as well. But when he saw the third clause, his gaze froze.","The man's fingers, resting on his thigh, tapped rapidly a few times. \"Madam, what exactly does 'conflicts' refer to in this third clause?\"","\"There are no specifics; it is a general term.\" Seeing him frown, Dai Li said gently, \"Although it's a general term, I don't believe either of us is the type to just have a mouth but not know how to communicate.\"","Dai Li's tone remained gentle, but there was a hint of probing in her words. \"Could it be, My Lord, that you believe we would have irreconcilable conflicts when it comes to raising children?\"","Qin Shaozong fell silent. He did not respond to Dai Li's words and continued reading.","[After the marriage is broken, both parties shall take their respective children and live separately. From then on, they shall part amicably and have nothing to do with each other. They must absolutely not inquire about or interfere with each other's futures.]","Every word in this paragraph seemed to grow legs, running wild across Qin Shaozong's minefield. The fury he had just barely suppressed threatened to surge wildly once more.","Dai Li knew what he was displeased about; it was nothing more than his objection to the \"verdict\" in the final line.","But on this bottom line, she absolutely could not compromise.","The laws of this era were highly flexible. The saying that a prince who breaks the law commits the same crime as a commoner was often just empty talk.","A man like Qin Shaozong, who was arrogant yet exceptionally strict with himself in certain aspects, tended to take his promises very seriously. Even if these matters were not explicitly stipulated by the law, he would still abide by them.","As long as Qin Changgeng signed and stamped his seal, the matter would be ninety percent settled.","Thus, Dai Li pretended not to notice his displeasure. She took the box of sealing clay, thoughtfully unscrewed the lid, and placed it in front of him. Without asking what he was dissatisfied with, she said directly, My Lord, please.","Qin Shaozong did not move.","My Lord? Dai Li called out.","Qin Shaozong did not respond.","Dai Li's mouth twitched.","Fine, if he wanted to stay silent, let him stay silent.","It was useless for him to hide his personal seal; she would just find it herself.","The two were sitting close to each other anyway, so it was very convenient for Dai Li to search for things. She simply reached over and rummaged through his sleeve pocket.","Qin Shaozong noticed her movements. He didn't move his hands or feet, but merely lowered his eyes, watching her dig through his pocket.","The garments of the high officials and nobles of this era featured wide sleeves with pockets designed to slant upwards, preventing small items from falling out easily. The wider sleeves could even reach half a meter in width.","As Dai Li reached her hand inside, her body naturally leaned toward Qin Shaozong. There wasn't much in his sleeve, and she quickly felt his personal seal.","Qin Shaozong's personal seal was rather bizarre. No, calling it a personal seal wasn't entirely accurate.","The man held many official positions, which meant he had many corresponding seals. Finding it cumbersome and annoying, he specifically took another piece of jade and carved it into a multi-faceted seal.","Each face was a different seal; turning it to the side revealed yet another. Several seals were all encompassed within a single piece of jade.","Dai Li placed the seal by his hand. I must trouble you.","In the fading daylight, the man's light brown eyes increasingly resembled those of a tiger lurking in the forest, staring at its prey, exuding a hint of ferocity.","One glance told Dai Li that he was unwilling, but she said nothing more. She merely took the unfolded Marriage Agreement, folded it, and then reached for an envelope.","She looked as if she were about to put the Marriage Agreement away.","Qin Shaozong finally moved. He first picked up the wolf-hair brush, casually dipped it in some ink, and then signed his name on the paper. The signature was much messier than usual; someone with poor eyesight might not even be able to read it.","After signing, he waited quite a while before picking up his personal seal. He sluggishly dipped it into the red paste and then smacked it down on the designated stamping area at the bottom.","Dai Li tried to push her luck. There are other faces too.","Qin Shaozong tossed the jade block aside, his face dark and gloomy, refusing to do any more.","If he wouldn't do it, Dai Li would.","She immediately took his personal seal, dipped it in the ink paste herself, and with several loud smacks, stamped every remaining face onto the paper.","Once the stamping was done, Dai Li also signed her own name.","With that, the task was successfully completed.","After letting the hard-won agreement air dry and folding it up, Dai Li belatedly realized that the Marriage Agreement had somehow ended up back in his hands.","Her goal was achieved; the rest didn't matter.","Dai Li tucked the letter into her own sleeve pocket and stood up to head outside.","Where is Madam going? asked the man who had been treating his words like gold just moments ago.","Dai Li replied, Earlier, I was worried about the carriage ride and didn't dare to eat much. Now I am a bit hungry, so I am going to have someone cook a bowl of noodle soup.","Qin Shaozong said, It is a trivial matter. Just have a maidservant handle it.","Dai Li reasoned smoothly, After sitting in the carriage for so long, my bones are about to fall apart. I still need to go out for a walk.","In reality, however, after leaving the main courtyard, Dai Li did not go to the kitchen herself. Instead, she casually passed the task off to a servant she bumped into, while she headed toward Qin Yanzhou's courtyard.","The winter sky darkened quickly. By the time Dai Li arrived at her son's courtyard, only a faint layer of light remained in the sky.","Mother? Qin Yanzhou was surprised by her arrival at this hour.","Dai Li didn't waste words. She pulled the agreement from her sleeve pocket. Zhou Zhou, help me keep something safe. I just signed a divorce agreement with Qin Changgeng regarding our marriage next year. Although the government offices of this era do not recognize a divorce initiated by a woman, Qin Changgeng generally keeps his word. Plus, this has many official seals stamped on it, so I think it should be enough to fool others.","Qin Yanzhou looked down at the letter in his hand. His face was shrouded in the dim light, making it impossible to read his emotions. Mother, do you... not want to marry the Marquis of Wu'an at all?","Dai Li lowered her eyes. Of course not. Writing this agreement is purely a precaution. After all, the civil affairs bureaus of this era don't process divorces, so I have to arrange a way out for myself.","Qin Yanzhou looked up, facing the gradually clearing moonlight. His eyes were as deep as pools. Mother, may I take a look at this agreement?","Dai Li was momentarily stunned. Ah? Sure, go ahead and look.","The letter hadn't been sealed yet, so it could be taken out directly. As soon as the mulberry paper inside was pulled out, Qin Yanzhou immediately noticed that it was severely wrinkled, as if someone had forcefully crumpled it into a ball and thrown it away.","The young man unfolded the letter and read it very carefully, word by word. It wasn't a long letter, but Qin Yanzhou looked at it for a very, very long time."]},{"number":131,"title":"Chapter 131","paragraphs":["Qin Yanzhou finished reading the letter. \"Mom, rest assured, I will definitely keep this agreement safe and sound. I won't give the Marquis of Wu'an any chance to exploit it. If the day ever comes when the Marquis betrays you, not only will I take you away, but I will also make him regret it bitterly.\"","\"I will do this at any cost.\" A shocking coldness flickered in the young man's dark eyes.","Dai Li smiled and patted her son's shoulder. \"That's a long way off. Perhaps such a terrible situation will never happen.\"","Looking at her son in front of her, a memory suddenly popped into Dai Li's mind.","\"Qin Yanzhou is about to reach adulthood. It is natural for young men and women to marry when they come of age... I'm not saying he needs to get married immediately, but I think we can start planning for this major life event...\"","Qin Changgeng's words still echoed in her ears.","Dai Li suddenly asked, \"Zhouzhou, what did you think of the winter hunt this time?\"","The topic shifted so quickly that the young man clearly hadn't grasped Dai Li's underlying meaning. He nodded and said, \"It was quite good.\"","Then Qin Yanzhou added, \"Very smooth.\"","Obtaining the Divorce Agreement meant his mother had not only won the bet but also struck while the iron was hot to exchange the prize. As for the rest, Miss Shi and Qin San were not held accountable, and all the personal guards of the Shi family were released.","So, in summary, everything went smoothly.","Dai Li knew her son had misunderstood. She coughed lightly, \"I didn't mean in that regard. Mom just wanted to ask you, Zhouzhou, did you meet any girls who caught your eye during this winter hunt?\"","Qin Yanzhou was slightly taken aback, a hint of confusion in his eyes, and then he shook his head.","Dai Li wasn't surprised. She chose her words carefully, \"Mom isn't asking this to pressure you into marriage. It's just that it's normal to have crushes at your age. In the modern world, Zhouzhou, you would be in college by now, and perhaps, like many other boys, you would have already started dating. But here...\"","Dai Li sighed, her helplessness and sorrow hard to put into words.","Worried about putting pressure on her son, Dai Li added, \"It's different here from modern times. They emphasize 'the orders of parents and the words of matchmakers,' and it's not customary for young people to date on their own. If you have a favorable impression of a certain girl, I would probably need to step forward and invite her and her elders to our home as guests.\"","\"Mom, there's no need.\" The young man shook his head again. \"I don't have any intentions like that.\"","Dai Li sighed again in her heart.","That meant he hadn't met any girl he liked at the winter hunt. Well, Zhouzhou was still young. He wouldn't turn twenty until his birthday in the winter, so there was no rush.","\"If you ever find someone you like in the future, just tell Mom, and Mom will help you arrange everything,\" Dai Li instructed.","Although he didn't really think he would need it, Qin Yanzhou still nodded and thanked his mother.","By the time Dai Li returned from her son's place, the noodle soup she had ordered earlier had been delivered to the main courtyard.","Just earlier, Qin Shaozong had unilaterally flown into a thunderous rage. Now that Dai Li was back, she acted as if she completely forgot they had a conflict, her expression gentle as she took the initiative to chat with him:","\"A timely snow promises a good harvest; it looks like next year will definitely be a prosperous one. Wheat has a short growth cycle and its yield is much higher than millet. Everything about it is good, except it requires more water. Since the trend of using square-pallet chain pumps has now spread all over the North, my Lord, you might as well have the farmers plant more wheat next year.\"","If she had talked about anything else, Qin Shaozong might have sulked for a while and ignored her, but when it came to food...","\"What you said, Madam, is exactly what I am planning. We absolutely cannot lack provisions for marching and fighting. Next year, I plan to issue an order in the North for the farmers to change their crop seeds,\" Qin Shaozong said.","There was nothing more direct than issuing an order.","Once a decree was handed down, supervised layer by layer by local officials with both rewards and punishments, it would yield results very quickly.","Dai Li immediately flattered him, \"My Lord is truly far-sighted. Paired with the curved-shaft plow, you will get twice the result with half the effort. I imagine that in just two or three years, the North will become a massive granary that the whole world will envy. By then, who in the world could compete with you, my Lord?\"","Seeing her smiling like a flower, Qin Shaozong felt the anger suppressed in his chest was stuck—he couldn't dispel it, nor could he hold it in, and it rampaged inside him like a disobedient beast.","He simply reached out a long arm, pulling her directly into his embrace. With his other hand, he supported and pinched her chin, forcing her to look up, and then kissed her heavily.","Dai Li wrapped her arms around his sturdy waist and back, beginning to accommodate him.","The unspoken anger transferred over like a burning fire through their lips and tongues. Dai Li could sense all of his fury, displeasure, and faint frustration as he bit and sucked on the tip of her tongue.","Her goal had been achieved, so now she needed to stroke his ego.","Thus, Dai Li catered to him to the utmost. Unfortunately, she still underestimated his anger. Later on, the tip of her tongue ached from his sucking, yet the man had no intention of letting her go.","Dai Li tried hard to turn her head away, pretending to be dizzy.","Qin Shaozong pinched her soft cheeks, causing those moist, glossy lips to pop open slightly. \"Madam's mouth is truly formidable. It can ignite a raging wildfire in a paddy field, and it can also summon rain clouds over parched land for a heavenly downpour.\"","With her cheeks pinched by him, it was inconvenient for Dai Li to speak, so she merely blinked at him innocently.","Qin Shaozong suddenly thought of something and released her cheeks. \"When you were abducted by the Green Lotus Cult, did they threaten you into doing anything else?\"","A glimmer of light flashed in Dai Li's eyes.","For Qin Changgeng to ask this meant that the matter of the Divorce Agreement from earlier was officially over.","The noodle soup was already set on the table, so Dai Li simply sat down first. \"No. I told them about the curved-shaft plow purely to gain their trust and prepare for my subsequent escape. Even if they had plans, they didn't have time to implement them.\"","Because she had run away during the festival.","Qin Shaozong twisted his jade thumb ring.","It was pretty much as he had guessed. When he had found her and brought her back, she had no injuries on her body.","He suddenly changed the subject. \"Madam, you personally chose Qin Yanzhou's courtesy name. How about letting Nalan Wugong perform his capping ceremony? On the day the two boys come of age, the prominent families of Yuyang will all come to observe the ceremony. Nalan Wugong is renowned far and wide; having him personally cap the boy will bring him many benefits in the future.\"","Dai Li thought for a moment and nodded in agreement.","Qin Shaozong sat beside her, watching her eat the noodles, his eyes a deep, dark green. When Dai Li set down her jade chopsticks, he scooped her up with his long arm again. \"The wildfire is not yet extinguished. Please, Madam, do not be stingy with the heavenly downpour.\"","Dai Li: \"...\"","The sun set and rose, and a new day arrived as promised.","Early this morning, an express dispatch from the south crossed thousands of miles and was delivered to the Qin Manor.","Qin Manor, Study.","Qin Shaozong looked at the secret report on his desk, his face expressionless, the atmosphere around him heavy and oppressive.","Several strategists residing in the Qin Manor exchanged glances, all seeing solemnity in each other's eyes.","\"...My Lord, this Liu of Jingzhou rose to power relying on his wife's family. His brother-in-law later died inexplicably. Regardless of whether there was foul play, just looking at how Liu Zhanguo subsequently became the leader of his wife's Sun family, and then defeated numerous competitors to become the Governor of Jingzhou, one can tell that this man is ruthless and extremely calculating. Now that he has taken Yi Province into his pocket, and also recruited the venomous strategist Shi Wuji, formerly under Fan Tianshi's command, it is no exaggeration to say that Liu Zhanguo, Liu of Jingzhou, is unmatched in prominence in the south,\" Sheng Ran said in a deep voice.","Cui Shengping nodded. \"Indeed. Not to mention that Governor Ye of Yangzhou also has intentions of forming a marriage alliance with Liu Zhanguo. Once the Liu and Ye families are united in marriage, the south... will likely become the Liu family's domain.\"","The three provinces of Jingzhou, Yizhou, and Yangzhou covered a vast expanse of land. If they were to connect into a single territory, their sheer size would be unmatched by any three random provinces in the north.","Qin Shaozong held a tiger-shaped brush rest, absently stroking the tiger's back. \"The situation of the realm is now largely clear.\"","Emperor Han was young. The imperial court was currently controlled jointly by Prime Minister Dong Zhou and Empress Dowager Wang, who were subtly standing in opposition to each other.","Regardless of how fiercely they clashed in the shadows, and regardless of whether the surrounding provinces harbored disloyal intentions or alternate plans, at least on the surface, the neighboring Liangzhou, Sizhou, and Yuzhou still deferred to the imperial court. Their level of obedience was much higher than that of the other provinces.","A year ago, he had swallowed up Bingzhou, and from then on, the northern lands were entirely under the surname Qin. And now, the power dynamics in the south were also becoming clear.","The imperial court, situated in Chang'an of Yongzhou, connected with the surrounding Sizhou, Yuzhou, and others to form a long east-west belt, which perfectly separated the north from the south.","Whether he wanted to march his army south or Liu Zhanguo wanted to push north, they would inevitably have to pass through this buffer zone in the middle.","\"My Lord, the imperial court is now facing enemies on both fronts. Prime Minister Dong and the Empress Dowager must be struggling to eat and sleep in peace. I personally believe this situation will not last much longer.\" Cui Shengping stroked his long beard.","The reason he said it would not last long was because the current Emperor Han was young and sickly. Word had it that he had fallen severely ill just last winter.","With a weak ruler and strong ministers, the surrounding provincial governors definitely had their own ambitions, even if they feigned submission on the surface. The imperial court's buffer zone was teetering on the edge of collapse, and once it fell, both the north and the south would likely make their moves simultaneously.","After all, it was easier to fish in troubled waters. The more chaotic the situation, the better. As for how much meat one could ultimately secure, that would depend entirely on their own abilities.","Nalan Zhi remained silent for a moment. \"My Lord, what are your thoughts on Governor Nangong's proposal for a marriage alliance?\"","The letter from Qingzhou had been delivered the day before yesterday, but Qin Shaozong had set it aside on his desk at the time, and it had not been mentioned since.","\"Let us wait and see,\" Qin Shaozong said in a calm tone.","With the marriage letter previously shelved and this phrase let us wait and see, the men could all tell that he was not very enthusiastic about the proposal.","As strategists, they could not merely plan for themselves; they also had to plan for others. And others in this context specifically referred to their superior.","Often, they had to swim against the current. Thus, Cui Shengping said, \"My Lord, you and Governor Nangong took Yanzhou together, splitting it in two, which means Governor Nangong is no longer the governor of just one province. If the northern lands form an alliance with Qingzhou, not only will it strengthen our side, but we can also use Qingzhou as a boundary to form another buffer zone. I personally believe this marriage should be arranged. May I be so bold as to ask what concerns you have, My Lord?\"","If the marriage truly went through, the layout from north to south would be the northern lands, Qingzhou, the imperial court, and the southern factions.","Sheng Ran nodded in agreement. \"Governor Nangong's legitimate daughter has a noble status and is fit to be the primary wife of the Third Young Master. Should there be other noble ladies in the future...\"","He thought about it for a moment. There did not seem to be many who had yet to clearly choose a side, and even if there were, they could not rival Nangong Xiong's power.","\"...they could serve as concubines for the Third Young Master,\" Sheng Ran finished.","Nowadays, the inner courtyards of noble young masters were filled with women at most, and had at least a few at the bare minimum. This was not solely due to personal lust, but also a result of political alliances.","Especially for a regional overlord, their children were either marrying into one family or forming an alliance with another faction. Ranked in order of importance, those from a powerful maternal clan who arrived early became primary wives, while those who were less powerful or married later became concubines.","Someone like Qin Shaozong, whose two sons were both still unmarried, was incredibly rare.","But Qin Shaozong suddenly said, \"Yunce is not yet married and is older than Qin San. Why did Haiqing and Zhongliang coincidentally bypass him to suggest Qin San?\"","Both Cui Shengping and Sheng Ran were taken aback.","Their Lord's tone remained calm, and at first glance, the words did not sound harsh, but the implications within them made their hearts skip a beat.","It was a difficult statement to respond to. Cui Shengping chose his words carefully, \"My Lord, the Eldest Young Master's capping ceremony is approaching in a few days. Has he ever revealed to you... any intentions of acknowledging his biological father?\"","Qin Shaozong replied that he had not.","Cui Shengping's mind raced.","He had not?","If the Eldest Young Master did not acknowledge his biological father, then he would remain under their Lord's name. Following the order of seniority, since the Eldest Young Master was not yet married, it would indeed be inappropriate for the Third Young Master to marry first.","But the Eldest Young Master...","\"My Lord, do you wish for the Eldest Young Master to marry Governor Nangong's legitimate daughter?\" Sheng Ran asked hesitantly.","Qin Shaozong cherished his words like gold. \"We shall see.\"","None of them could figure out what their superior meant.","To say he wanted to support the Eldest Young Master, he had not agreed to let him marry Governor Nangong's legitimate daughter. To say he did not want to support him did not make sense either, because he had clearly just interrupted Sheng Ran's words.","However, one thing was certain. It seemed their Lord—","Was not too keen on the Third Young Master having an overly powerful wife's family.","Qin Shaozong suddenly called out Cui Shengping's courtesy name. \"Haiqing, for Yunce's capping ceremony, could I trouble you to crown him?\"","Cui Shengping quickly sat up straight. \"It would be my utmost honor.\"","There was more than one young man coming of age this winter, so Cui Shengping asked again, \"My Lord, for young Master Qin's capping ceremony...\"","Qin Shaozong said, \"I will entrust Qin Yanzhou to Wugong. What do you think, Wugong?\"","Nalan Zhi cupped his hands and bowed, accepting the task as well.","After a few more words, the men finally bowed and took their leave, but Qin Shaozong spoke up at that moment. \"Wugong, please stay for a moment.\"","Nalan Zhi remained behind.","Cui Shengping and Sheng Ran paused briefly before exiting the study together. Once they had walked a distance away, Sheng Ran asked in a low voice, \"Haiqing, what do you think our Lord means by this?\"","Cui Shengping was older than Sheng Ran, and also older than Qin Shaozong. But at this moment, he stroked his beard repeatedly before finally shaking his head. \"Our Lord's thoughts have always been as deep as the ocean abyss, impossible to fathom. We might as well wait until after the capping ceremonies to see; everything will become clear then.\"","\"You make a good point...\"","*","Inside the study.","The door closed once more. Qin Shaozong looked at Nalan Zhi standing nearby and gestured to a seat beside him with an open palm. \"Wugong, sit.\"","\"I wonder what instructions you have for me, My Lord,\" Nalan Zhi said, confusion in his eyes.","Qin Shaozong said in a deep voice, \"Haiqing comes from the Cui clan of Hedong. Let us leave Zhongliang aside for now, but both of them have already been overtly and covertly plotting and calculating for Qin San. Wugong, this boy Qin Yanzhou is an uncut jade. Since he has taken you as his master, I hope you will carve this jade in the future and help him plan more.\"","Nalan Zhi's pupils contracted slightly."]},{"number":132,"title":"Chapter 132","paragraphs":["Nalan Zhi stepped out of the study and looked up at the sky above.","Today was sunny and pleasant, with a cloudless sky. The sunlight shone on the white snow on the ground, reflecting a brilliant glow.","The snow scenery was as beautiful as a painting, but Nalan Zhi could faintly see a storm brewing.","He paused for a moment, his expression complex, feeling that there were many things he could not see through. The only clear thing was that from today onwards, he would be Qin Yanzhou's master.","Not the kind of confidant from before who only enlightened him and kept the boy from getting stuck in a dead end, but a true master who would teach him everything, guide him, push him, and take care of his future path.","He did not know where this path arranged for him by his lord would lead. Whether it would open up to a bright future, or be fraught with danger only to end in peace, or be a long and arduous journey leading to a dead end, he could not fathom. He only knew that once he set foot on this path, there would likely be no turning back.","Nalan Zhi let out a long breath and strode away.","The invitation letters for the coming-of-age capping ceremonies of the two young masters of the Qin family spread rapidly among the prominent families as if they had grown wings. Not only in Yuyang Commandery, but prominent families in other regions also received invitations to attend the ceremony.","Overjoyed, the prominent families from out of town hurriedly had their servants prepare heavy gifts and set off early.","Time flew by, and in the blink of an eye, the day of the capping ceremony arrived.","Winters in the north rarely saw rain; it was usually snow. Today, Daili woke up very early. When she got up, light snow was falling outside the window. By the time she finished washing up and getting dressed, the snow had stopped.","A thin layer of white covered the ground, spread out like a delicate sheet of dough.","Servants were sweeping with brooms, making rhythmic swishing sounds. The moderate and regular noise was rather interesting in its own way.","Daili was dressed up for the occasion today, wearing a rattan-green dress with wide sleeves and a crossed collar. Above the crossed collar that folded just below her collarbones, a ruby necklace hung. The translucent, water-like red was particularly striking against her snow-white skin.","Her flowing, cloud-like dark hair was carefully put up by Nianxia. Silver-gilt phoenix hairpins were inserted on both sides of her temples, and the specially made kingfisher feather dangling ornaments were bright and dazzling in the sunlight.","It was currently popular to apply huadian, sticking patterns of flowers, birds, or butterflies on a lady's forehead to enhance her beauty. However, Bipo held the floral applique and stared at it for a moment, hesitating to apply it.","Qin Shaozong returned as if he had timed it perfectly. Seeing that Daili had finished dressing up, he stared at her for quite a while and suddenly quoted, \"There is a beautiful lady in her chamber; her room is near, but she seems far, tormenting my heart.\"","Daili replied, \"...The Marquis has such elegant taste.\"","Qin Shaozong saw the applique in Bipo's hand. \"There is no need to apply the huadian. It would be entirely superfluous.\"","Without the applique, her makeup was complete. Daili slowly stood up. \"Have the guests entered the manor?\"","Qin Shaozong nodded in affirmation. \"I have already let Hongying and a few boys welcome the guests on our behalf. Madam, Yunce is a month older than that boy Qin Yanzhou. For today's capping ceremony, I plan to have Yunce go first and be capped before him.\"","Daili agreed.","The two walked out of the main courtyard arm in arm. The snow in the courtyard had already been swept to the side by the servants. When the cool breeze blew past, it occasionally carried some snow dust with it.","Qin Shaozong said, \"Today, Yunce's younger sister, Yunshu, will also return. When she does, I will have her come to pay her respects to you...\"","Daili's footsteps suddenly stopped as a memory abruptly surfaced.","That was when she first arrived in Yuyang. Hearing of Qin Changgeng's return, the chief administrator of the Wei family had blocked the doorway, claiming he had urgent matters to discuss with him. At that time, Qin Changgeng had sent the man away. Later, he told her that the Wei family was his late wife's maternal family.","He had once said, \"...The Qin and Wei families were once related by marriage. I married the legitimate daughter of the Wei family, but she was frail. She passed away from illness less than two years after giving birth to a son.\"","The Wei family daughter married him and died of illness after giving birth to a son. Later, when Wei Cheng visited, Qin Qinian called her aunt, so he must be that child.","Then were Qin Yunce and the Yunshu he mentioned children born of concubines?","But Daili felt something was not quite right. Not only was Qin Qinian's attitude towards Qin Yunce highly respectful, but there was also Qin Changgeng's recent phrase, \"Yunce's younger sister, Yunshu.\"","Putting herself in his shoes, if it were her own daughter, Daili would definitely say \"my daughter.\" Why would there be a need to beat around the bush like this?","But when she first met Qin Yunce, the young man had indeed called Qin Changgeng \"father.\"","Qin Shaozong watched Daili with interest as she frowned one moment and relaxed her brows the next. Her expression was peculiar, as if she were trapped by some difficult puzzle.","A moment later, he saw her slowly raise her eyes and ask him, \"Qin Changgeng, exactly how many children do you have?\"","Qin Shaozong raised his long eyebrows slightly. \"I have waited from the time I returned to Yuyang until now, and I have finally waited for Madam to have the time to ask about family matters.\"","Daili was speechless.","This remark was hard to follow up on, so Daili simply coughed. \"Things happened one after another before. First it was detoxifying Zhouzhou, then the winter hunt, and later I was thinking about the capping ceremony. It was all so hectic that I couldn't attend to it for a while.\"","After explaining this, Daili quickly added, \"Qin Changgeng, so exactly how many children do you have?\"","Every time she called him by his full name and courtesy name together, it was either because she had serious business to discuss with him or she was somewhat annoyed. The man smiled and put his hands behind his back. \"It could be one, it could be two, or it could be three.\"","Daili was bewildered.","How could the number of children change back and forth like this?","Once they are born, they are born. Could they be stuffed back in?","Daili found it hard to describe her feelings. \"Are the Marquis's children like gourds on a vine, able to change according to the seasons?\"","Qin Shaozong explained, \"Yunce and Yunshu are my older brother's children. Years ago, after my brother was killed in battle on the front lines, my sister-in-law committed suicide for love, leaving behind a pair of young children. At that time, some people within the Qin clan were quite restless, so I decided to adopt Yunce and Yunshu as my own. That year, Yunce was five years old, and Yunshu was two.\"","Daili suddenly understood.","No wonder those two brothers did not have the slightest discord; it turned out they were cousins.","Qin Shaozong walked forward with her. \"Yunce remembered things early. He had a deep affection for my brother and initially did not want to acknowledge me. I then told him that after his capping ceremony, if he wanted to acknowledge my brother as his father again, I would have no objections.\"","Only then did Daili understand where that variable came from. \"So when you just said it could be one, that is under the circumstance that both Yunce and Yunshu change back to acknowledging your brother as their father?\"","Qin Shaozong nodded.","Daili looked at his expression. \"If a child who has called you 'father' for over ten years suddenly changes to calling you 'uncle,' what are your thoughts?\"","Qin Shaozong looked at the boundless blue sky, a look of nostalgia in his eyes. \"My brother was a very good father. In my memory, he would even let Yunce ride on his shoulders, carrying the child around everywhere, and he would personally teach him how to read and write. Every time he traveled, he would definitely bring back gifts for his wife and children. Even some of Yunce's childhood toys were made by my brother's own hands.\"","In all these things, Qin Shaozong felt inferior.","Compared to his brother, he always had much less patience with children. As long as the child wasn't missing an arm or a leg, it was fine. They needed to take a few tumbles to grow tough; there was no need to raise them so delicately.","Daili nodded in agreement. \"He truly was a good father.\"","\"So even if he acknowledges my brother again, it is only human nature.\" Qin Shaozong's tone did not fluctuate much. \"However, regardless of whether he changes his acknowledgment or not, he is older than Qin Yanzhou. In the future, Qin Yanzhou will rank second in the family alongside Yunshu.\"","Qin Yunce was the oldest. Next was Qin Yunshu, who was the same age as Qin Qinian but slightly older, and finally, Qin Qinian, the third child.","In some families, the young masters and young ladies were arranged together, males and females in a single line. Before Qin Yunshu was married, others called her the Second Young Lady of the Qin family.","In other families, they were arranged separately, males and females each in their own line. This was usually the case for families with many offspring. If there were too many children and they were arranged together, the line could wind like a long snake.","As they spoke, the two arrived at the main hall.","Dai Li had not yet married Qin Shaozong, but the news that they would wed next spring had already spread throughout Yuyang. She assumed the duties of the main wife, returning the guests' greetings, and no one around dared to show the slightest dissatisfaction.","Are you kidding? The Marquis of Wu'an came with her, a smile on his lips, clearly showing no objection.","Since the host saw no problem, how could these guests, who were subordinates trying to curry favor with the Marquis of Wu'an, dare to show any disdain?","Among the guests, Dai Li spotted Qin Yunshu. She bore a five-point resemblance to Qin Yunce, especially in the lower half of her face, and both siblings had a gentle temperament.","The young woman, whose hair was already done up in a married woman's bun, took the initiative to step forward, curtsied, and greeted Qin Shaozong and Dai Li, \"Father, Madam Dai.\"","Qin Shaozong asked, \"How have you been in the Tang family?\"","This question made Tang Wenjin, who had accompanied his wife, tense his scalp.","Qin Yunshu smiled, \"Everything is fine. Thank you for your concern, Father.\"","Qin Yunshu was married outside the commandery, but it wasn't too far from Yuyang. Qin Shaozong said, \"Since you've returned to Yuyang, why not stay in the mansion for a few days with your husband and reunite with the family?\"","Qin Yunshu nodded obediently.","There were many guests, so they couldn't just focus on one. Therefore, after a short conversation with Qin Yunshu, Dai Li went to deal with other guests.","Amidst the busyness, time passed unknowingly, and soon it was the auspicious hour.","Today's auspicious hour was exactly noon. As the gong sounded, the seated guests all fell silent.","The capping ceremony had an opening ritual, which was overseen by Qin Shaozong. After the ritual, the core figures of the capping ceremony, the two boys, stepped forward.","Both had their hair down. At this moment, each knelt on a previously prepared kneeling pad, while an elder of the Qin family helped comb their hair.","The guests below already knew that the two were being capped together today. But seeing them step forward together at this moment, their eyes held varying degrees of surprise.","After the combing was finished, Qin Yanzhou stood up and temporarily stepped aside. The strategist Cui Shengping took the stage and adjusted the collar of Qin Yunce, who remained in the center.","At this moment, the sponsor sang: \"On this auspicious day of this good month, we first place the capping garment upon you. Cast aside your childish aspirations, and follow your adult virtues. May you live a long and happy life, and be blessed with great fortune.\" 1","The capping ceremony was quite complicated, requiring three cappings and three bowings. The \"three cappings and three bowings\" referred to the capping three times, with each capping using a \"black cloth cap\", a \"leather cap\", and a \"sparrow cap\", each representing a different meaning, and each cap corresponding to a set of clothes.","This meant that after a capping, one had to return to the room to change clothes before coming out to bow to the guests again.","\"A man is capped and given a courtesy name at twenty. Time flies, and twenty years have passed. Yunce, today you will receive a courtesy name.\" Cui Shengping's face was flushed with excitement.","Qin Yunce said, \"Please tell me, sir.\"","Cui Shengping said, \"Born anew and growing upwards, thriving in the future, it is called 'Changsheng'. This is one of the courtesy names Boyang thought of for you many years ago, even before you were born. I think it is the most suitable one now, so I chose it.\"","Qin Yunce was stunned, his eyes instantly reddening. He bowed deeply, \"Thank you, sir.\"","Suddenly, a wet mark spread on the ground.","Qin Yunce straightened up, walked to the side corridor to return to his room to change clothes, and when he came out to bow to the guests again, his capping ceremony would basically be over.","Next was Qin Yanzhou, repeating the three cappings and three bowings. Nalan Zhi was the one capping him.","After the capping came the granting of the courtesy name. Nalan Zhi said seriously, \"Yanzhou, the past is gone with the wind. After the capping is a new beginning. I grant you the word 'Chongle', wishing you smiles year after year and peace year after year.\"","The last sentence lacked a subject and was too gentle, slightly different from Nalan Zhi's past style, more like...","The young man couldn't help but turn his head slightly to look at his mother sitting not far away. He saw her smiling, and when she noticed him looking over, her smile obviously deepened.","A warm current surged in his chest. As Qin Yanzhou bowed his head again, he silently repeated in his heart: Qin Chongle.","Chong meant both anew and double.","It was wonderful. He liked this name too.","The two boys successfully completed the ceremony one after another. At this point, the capping ceremony for the guests was basically over.","If it were young masters of other families, they would need to visit local prestigious figures after the ceremony, such as the local top official or the township official, before returning to pay respects to their ancestors.","In the Qin family, that intermediate step was directly omitted.","Dai Li and Qin Hongying went together to see off the guests. The guests came with generous gifts, and now that they were leaving, it would be unreasonable to let them leave empty-handed.","After seeing off the guests, it was time to go to the Qin family's ancestral hall to pay respects to the ancestors.","The Qin family's ancestral hall was inside the Marquis's mansion, requiring a carriage ride.","Riding in the carriage, listening to the rumbling sound of the wheels, Dai Li felt a somewhat indescribable complexity in her heart.","They were going to pay respects to the ancestors, and they specifically asked Zhouzhou to go together. She hadn't married Qin Changgeng yet, and Zhouzhou's biological father and grandfather had nothing to do with Qin Changgeng's family.","It just felt a bit off, strange.","Qin Hongying and Dai Li rode in the same carriage, sitting face to face.","Dai Li's expression changed back and forth. Qin Hongying somewhat guessed her thoughts and couldn't help but smile, \"You mother and son will be part of the Qin family sooner or later. It doesn't matter if you go and pay respects early. Besides, my second brother personally asked for this. He knows what he's doing.\"","Dai Li smiled but didn't speak.","Before long, the carriage arrived at the Marquis's mansion.","Dai Li had never been to the Marquis's mansion. Now, looking out through the curtain, she only felt that this mansion was astonishingly large.","Looking from afar, the carved beams and painted rafters, the flying eaves and soaring corners each had their own characteristics. The pavilions, terraces, and waterside pavilions were quiet and elegant, and the green tiles and red ridges were unspeakably magnificent.","Dai Li suddenly remembered something.","The palaces of various dynasties were actually built smaller and smaller. Take the Forbidden City of the Ming and Qing dynasties for example; its area was only about a quarter of the Daming Palace of the Tang dynasty.","There were many reasons, one of which was that giant timber became increasingly scarce. The further back in time, the more giant timber there was. By the Ming and Qing dynasties, many timbers had to be sought in deep mountains and old forests.","The carriage drove straight in until it stopped at the ancestral hall.","Dai Li didn't really want to go in, so Qin Hongying accompanied her outside, while the two boys followed Qin Shaozong inside.","Qin Hongying took the initiative to ask Dai Li, \"Dai Li, do you know about Yunce's matter?\"","\"Huh?\" Dai Li realized later, \"Are you talking about whether Yunce should acknowledge his biological father? I just learned about this.\"","\"What's the result?\" Qin Hongying asked.","Dai Li laughed, \"You, as his aunt, don't know, how would I know?\"","Qin Hongying looked suspicious, \"My second brother didn't tell you?\"","Dai Li shook her head and said no.","Qin Hongying murmured, \"Second Brother feels guilty toward Eldest Brother, and has always brooded over what happened back then. If Yunce continues to acknowledge Second Brother as his father, it's not impossible that in the future...\"","Her voice grew softer and softer. Daili didn't catch the rest of her words, but it wasn't hard to guess.","Daili's brow twitched slightly.","Didn't Qin Changgeng say his elder brother died in battle? Swords and spears on the battlefield have no eyes; going there means putting one's life on the line, so casualties are to be expected.","Generally speaking, no one else could be blamed. Could there be some hidden secret behind what happened back then?","Qin Hongying snapped back to reality. Perhaps feeling that the topic was a bit sensitive, she immediately changed the subject.","The two of them chatted casually outside.","About fifteen minutes later, someone came out.","It was Qin Yanzhou.","Qin Hongying, who had been leaning somewhat lazily, straightened up. \"Why are you the only one? Where are my brother and Yunce?\"","Qin Yanzhou replied, \"The ancestral worship is finished. The Marquis of Wu'an asked me to come out first.\"","Qin Hongying turned to look at the ancestral hall, deep in thought.","*","After Qin Yanzhou left, Qin Yunce dropped to his knees before Qin Shaozong with a thud.","He didn't use a kneeling cushion, but knelt directly on the ground. In front of the array of Qin family spirit tablets, he solemnly kowtowed three times to Qin Shaozong. \"Your grace in raising me, Changsheng will never forget and will forever engrave in my heart.\"","He referred to himself as \"Changsheng.\"","Qin Shaozong lowered his eyes, his gaze dark and unreadable. \"Have you truly thought this through? Do you know what changing it back represents?\"","Qin Yunce, whose forehead had been touching the ground, slowly straightened up. He had kowtowed solidly those three times, and now his forehead was red, as were the rims of his eyes.","\"I know. But fourteen years have passed, and I still cannot forget the bits and pieces of the past. Moreover, those things are not what I seek, and this body of mine... does not allow me to do otherwise.\"","A line of hot tears flowed from his eyes. \"Uncle, I am sorry. I have disappointed you and failed to live up to your cultivation of me all these years.\"","Qin Shaozong closed his eyes.","...","Qin Yunce left, leaving only Qin Shaozong in the ancestral hall.","The light of the setting sun slanted in through the door, falling on the burly man and casting a long shadow to his side.","In the empty room, that back, which was like a heavy sword and seemed as if it would never bend, now revealed a touch of unknown loneliness and desolation.","A moment later, someone sighed softly, \"Brother, you were much more successful as a father than I am.\""]},{"number":133,"title":"Chapter 133","paragraphs":["The carriage traveled swiftly, draped in the afterglow of dusk, and returned to the Qin Manor stepping on the last ray of daylight.","After a busy day, Qin Hongying and Shi Rongyue both looked tired. They exchanged greetings and returned to their rooms.","Dai Li was doing alright, but she felt the hair ornaments on her head growing heavier and heavier. She wanted nothing more than to hurry back and take off all the pearl hairpins and jade ornaments.","However...","\"Mom, I'll go back with you,\" Qin Yanzhou said in a low voice.","Dai Li looked at her son, inexplicably feeling that there was more to his words. Usually, if they were going back, they would just go; Zhouzhou wouldn't add this extra sentence.","She briefly told Qin Shaozong that she would take another path. The man nodded, his face shrouded in the already dim shadows, making it hard to see clearly.","For some reason, Dai Li felt that his mood right now was rather gloomy.","The group left, and Dai Li didn't delay for too long before heading back with Qin Yanzhou.","Night had fallen, and the long corridor was dark. Dai Li declined Nianxia and Bipo's offers to carry the lantern for her, asking them to go back first to prepare the bathwater. She held the lantern herself and walked slowly with her son.","With no one else around, Dai Li spoke without hesitation. \"Has something happened recently, Zhouzhou?\"","Qin Yanzhou replied, \"Mom, Mr. Nalan has been a bit strange lately. In the past, when I went to see him, we would talk about everything under the sun, mostly interesting anecdotes from the past. But recently, he has completely changed his style and started teaching me the Book of Changes, the Great Learning, and the Book of Rites...\"","Dai Li paused her steps.","The contents of these books varied, but if one were to summarize them, it would be: cultivate one's moral character, manage the household, govern the state, and bring peace to the world.","\"Zhouzhou, did you ask Nalan why he suddenly started talking to you about this?\" Dai Li asked.","Qin Yanzhou nodded and said he had. \"Mr. Nalan said that all the other boys have to read these books. I wasn't in a good state before, so he didn't teach me. Now that I've changed so much compared to the past, I have to make up for what I missed.\"","The lantern in Dai Li's hand swayed gently in the wind, much like her wavering heart at this moment.","A trace of hidden worry quietly crept out from the bottom of her heart.","But this wisp of worry was too faint, like the smallest tender shoot in spring, so much so that Dai Li was more focused on other things right now. She asked her son, \"Zhouzhou, do you want to learn these things?\"","\"Mom, I want to study,\" Qin Yanzhou said softly.","Dai Li's thoughts were instantly pulled back to the past.","In the past, many of her colleagues envied her for having an angel baby. And indeed, Zhouzhou had been easy to raise since he was little. Even when he was a baby, he would sleep after eating and wouldn't fuss when he woke up. He would only cry a little when he was hungry; the rest of the time, he would just roll his big eyes and observe his surroundings.","When it was time for kindergarten, he only cried that very first time. After coming back, he told her that kindergarten was fun, and from then on, he happily carried his backpack with a little water bottle and handkerchief to school.","When he started elementary school, she never had to worry about his homework.","The first thing Zhouzhou always did when he came home from school was finish his homework. He wrote quickly and could often finish everything before dinner. And after eating, he would read the children's storybooks she bought for him by himself.","Dai Li suddenly realized that those precious, sparkling things like seashells had not been worn away by those ten bitter years; they had only been temporarily buried by the wind and sand, waiting for the right moment to break through the soil again.","\"Zhouzhou, during the first two years you spent in the Green Lotus Sect, what else did they teach you besides how to read?\" Dai Li asked.","Qin Yanzhou shook his head. \"I just learned some basic characters, and later it was mainly martial arts training.\"","They didn't teach him much reading either, only the most commonly used characters needed for communication. He slowly learned the rest by himself in every spare moment.","Dai Li smiled and said, \"Then study with Nalan. No matter what era it is, reading more is always good. If it weren't for the coincidence of coming here, Zhouzhou would be in college by now.\"","Some parents saved up enough wealth for their descendants and felt that it didn't matter whether they studied or not. After all, they would just end up working like dogs after graduating anyway, so it was better not to let their children suffer the hardships of studying.","Dai Li did not support the theory that studying was useless.","Regardless of whether the final outcome was the same, there was no denying that the process in between was different. Every school was a macro-environment, and the higher you went, the better the environment.","Living with good people is like entering a room full of orchids; after a long time, you won't notice the fragrance. Living with evil people is like entering a fish market; after a long time, you won't notice the stench.","Dai Li deeply agreed with this.","She continued, \"If there's anything else you're interested in, you can tell Nalan. He's a very good teacher, and I believe he will definitely teach you well.\"","Ever since Zhouzhou took Nalan Zhi as his teacher, her son had become much more energetic than before. It was like a withered little tree being moved to moist soil, carefully watered and cleared of pests, so that slowly, the withered tree grew tender green branches and leaves.","Dai Li felt relieved and happy from the bottom of her heart.","The two didn't walk fast, but the path eventually came to an end.","Before long, the main courtyard was right in front of them. Dai Li said to the young man beside her, \"You've been busy all day today, too. Go back and get some rest early.\"","Qin Yanzhou: \"Okay, good night, Mom.\"","Dai Li carried the lantern and went inside alone.","Inside the room, Nianxia and Bipo had already prepared the water. Dai Li took off all her golden hairpins and took a comfortable bath, washing away all her fatigue. But when she came out of the side room and completely dried her long hair, Qin Shaozong had still not returned.","Dai Li glanced at the door.","From what she had observed so far, unless there was an urgent confidential report or a small meeting to hold, Qin Changgeng would definitely return before the Hour of Hai.","\"Nianxia, did the Marquis mention that he wouldn't return to the main courtyard tonight?\" Dai Li called Nianxia over.","Nianxia shook her head. \"No one came to pass on a message.\"","Sitting on the soft chair, Dai Li's thoughts wandered, and for some reason, she thought of what happened at the Marquis Manor's ancestral hall today.","Following Zhouzhou, Qin Yunce came out alone afterward. The young man, who had just reached adulthood, had a red forehead and red rims around his eyes. She could tell that he had shed tears.","About half a quarter of an hour later, Qin Changgeng finally exited the ancestral hall.","Dai Li tried to recall that moment, but he had been standing under the eaves of the ancestral hall. The setting sun wasn't very bright, and coupled with the dark shadows cast by the eaves, he seemed to blend into the darkness.","She couldn't clearly remember his expression at that time; she only remembered that after closing the doors of the ancestral hall, he mounted his horse without saying a word and didn't speak to anyone the entire way.","Dai Li stood up from her seat and walked toward the door.","Nianxia and Bipo, who had finished serving her and were preparing to leave, were both startled to see this. \"Madam, where are you going?\"","\"I'm going out for a bit,\" Dai Li said.","Perhaps it was Qin Shaozong's rare abnormality, or perhaps it was what Zhouzhou had just told her about Nalan Zhi's change. The nerve that belonged to her sixth sense was tingling, telling her that something was happening.","\"It's cold late at night; Madam, please put on your cloak.\" Nianxia hurriedly brought the garment over.","Bipo also said, \"Wherever Madam wishes to go, your servant will carry the lantern for you.\"","Dai Li refused once more. \"There's no need. I can go out by myself.\"","Wearing her cloak, Dai Li went out carrying the lantern.","She first went to the study. Surprisingly yet unsurprisingly, there was no one inside. However, although it was empty inside, there were guards on duty at the door. Dai Li asked, \"Did the Marquis come by earlier?\"","Guard: \"To answer Madam, no.\"","Dai Li nodded. \"Thank you for your hard work.\"","She turned and walked away slowly. This residence could not compare to the Marquis's Manor, but it was certainly not small. There were over twenty courtyards alone, not counting other areas such as the dedicated martial arts training grounds.","Daili naturally could not search them one by one, so she directly asked a patrolling guard she encountered.","The guard indeed knew. Madam, the Marquis went to the martial arts courtyard in the southwest.","Having lived here for several months, Daili was completely familiar with every part of the estate. Hearing the guard mention the martial arts courtyard, she immediately knew it was the place where weapons were stored.","But what was Qin Changgeng doing over there?","Carrying a lantern, Daili walked slowly to the martial arts courtyard.","A bright moon hung high tonight, its light reflecting off the snow in the courtyard and making it sparkle as if sprinkled with glowing powder. This area was not frequently occupied, and servants only came to sweep the snow every two days. At this moment, a line of footprints extended inward across the moderate layer of snow on the ground.","The footprints were large, clearly left by a man's black boots.","Looking further in, faint light seeped from the rather large building. The glow was extremely weak, suggesting the person inside had lit no more than a single candlestand.","Daili followed the footprints inside.","The door was not closed. As soon as Daili reached the entrance, a strong stench of alcohol assaulted her senses. It was rich and pungent, as if a brocade handkerchief had been dropped into a wine jar, fished out, and placed wet over her nose.","The man sitting in the middle of the room turned his head at the sound. Seeing it was Daili, his hand holding the wine jar paused slightly. You are here, Madam.","The candlelight on the floor flickered, casting shifting shadows over the man's sharply defined features. His light brown eyes lacked their usual unstoppable sharpness.","Daili pursed her lips, feeling that the scene before her was very incongruous.","The dim room, the various weapons placed on wooden racks all around, the wine jars scattered across the floor, and the man sitting on the ground surrounded by them.","There were many weapons in the room. Halberds were propped up, longbows hung on the walls, short swords lay quietly on wooden rests, and there were even complete sets of armor.","The only exception was a silver helmet, which sat right beside Qin Shaozong's hand along with a wine jar.","That helmet was likely quite old; most of its silver coating had faded, giving way to dark red rust. Even with the candle placed nearby, it reflected little light.","Qin Shaozong casually swept aside a few wine jars, clearing an empty space. Come sit, Madam.","Daili walked over and sat down, using her cloak as a cushion. Why is the Marquis here drinking alone to get drunk?","If only I could get drunk. Sometimes having a high tolerance is not a good thing. He twitched the corners of his mouth but failed to form a smile.","Daili opened her lantern and took out the wick to make the surroundings brighter. Even if you cannot get drunk, you should drink less. Heavy drinking is never good.","Qin Shaozong still held a wine jar in one hand. He had just raised it, but upon hearing Daili's words, he set it back down.","He spoke of other things. This residence originally belonged to my grandmother. When my older brother and I were young and got into trouble, we were afraid to go home and would hide here. Later, when we reached the age to go to the battlefield, whenever we were injured out there, my brother and I would mostly come here to recover, to save our grandmother and mother at home from worrying when they saw us.","Daili's brow twitched slightly.","Given Qin Changgeng's current domineering personality, he was probably a fearless and stubborn troublemaker in his youth. And his older brother, who would personally make toys for his son, likely had a gentler temperament and might have been a scholarly general.","She could roughly imagine the scene back then.","Two youths, one older and one younger, covered in injuries, sitting face to face helping each other bandage their wounds. The older one would be giving gentle advice, while the younger one wore a look of defiance.","So all these weapons were brought over little by little by the two of you back then? Accumulating to such a large amount over time. Daili looked around again.","Otherwise, it was hard to explain why, when there was already a Marquis's Manor, so many weapons would be kept in an outside residence.","Qin Shaozong nodded and said yes.","A period of silence followed.","Yun Ce... did he acknowledge his biological father? Daili asked tentatively.","It is human nature, he replied in a calm tone.","Daili could not help but turn to look at him.","This morning, this man had said: So even if he acknowledges my brother, it is human nature.","Now he used the exact same words; it seemed her guess was correct.","Yun Ce said he was sorry to me, that he disappointed me and failed to live up to my cultivation of him all these years. There was self-mockery in Qin Shaozong's eyes. But if he knew that my brother died because of me back then, he would not have said those words.","Daili was startled. Did you not say your brother sacrificed himself on the battlefield? Could it be that he died taking a blade for you?","She could only think of this reason, otherwise why would Qin Changgeng say he died because of him?","But the man shook his head. Perhaps because he had been drinking, the dusty past from many years ago was rarely brought up again under the influence of alcohol. Back then, the Wuhuan had not yet been beaten into submission. They constantly came south to pillage villages, committing all sorts of atrocities like burning, killing, and looting. After the Wuhuan army invaded again and slaughtered a village, my father decided to teach them a lesson, so they would learn the meaning of knowing their place. However, the timing was not very good, because relations between the Northern Territory and the Imperial Court were very tense at the time.","Daili calculated in her mind.","He had said Yun Ce lost his biological father at the age of five, which was nearly fifteen years ago. Fifteen years ago, the Northern Territory and the Imperial Court might have been in the early or middle stages of intensifying conflict.","Why were relations tense? Daili asked.","The expression on Qin Shaozong's face slowly faded. The Han Emperor at the time, that is, the late Emperor, wanted the sons of the provincial governors to go to the capital to accompany the Crown Prince in his studies.","Go to the capital as hostages? Daili was surprised.","Qin Shaozong finally lifted the wine jar and took another gulp. The intention was so blatant that almost everyone knew it. My father only had two sons, my brother and me. My brother was the heir, so there was absolutely no possibility of him leaving the Northern Territory. If anyone was to go to the capital, it could only be me. But my father knew perfectly well that Chang'an was a dragon's pool and a tiger's den, and he was unwilling to send me into such a cage.","But if you did not go, it would be defying an imperial decree, giving them an excuse to do whatever they wanted. Daili asked curiously, How did your father handle it later?","Qin Shaozong: By dragging it out.","Daili nodded unconsciously; it was indeed a good method.","It was not that they were refusing to go to Chang'an, just that they would go later. It could not strictly be considered defying the decree.","Just as the Wuhuan invaded, my father simply rallied the army to crusade against them, planning to ambush and flank them when they came south again. At the time, I was appointed as the vanguard general, responsible for the charge; my brother was the left general, responsible for the flank. But right before going into battle, an old injury of mine flared up. After my brother noticed, he told my father he would swap with me. I became the left general, and he became the vanguard general, saying that since we had led the army together for so long and were quite familiar with the soldiers, changing commanders would not matter. Qin Shaozong set down the wine jar with a thud.","A gust of wind blew in at that moment, surging like a black tide, and extinguished the lamp in front of Qin Shaozong with a whoosh.","The light in the room instantly halved, leaving only the wick in front of Daili glowing faintly, like a lonely living soul.","Daili froze, then blurted out, So your brother sacrificed himself in that battle?","The veins on Qin Shaozong's forehead bulged. His face was half-hidden in the dim light, exuding an indescribable ruthlessness. \"At that time, there was a spy from the imperial court in the army. That spy sabotaged our operations during the battle, which not only led to my elder brother's death but also caused the entire vanguard unit to be almost completely wiped out. It was only later that I figured it out. The Wuhuan invasion at that time was also unusual. Someone in the imperial court secretly colluded with the higher-ups of Wuhuan to set up this trap.\"","Dai Li drew a sharp breath.","Colluding with foreigners to set a trap for their own people? This was clearly treason!","She could roughly guess the reason. His merits were so great that they threatened the ruler. The Emperor, far away in Chang'an, felt that his throne was not secure.","Coupled with Father Qin's delaying tactics, which added fuel to the fire, someone simply colluded with Wuhuan to chop off one of the North's arms.","As for the Great Yan border soldiers and innocent villagers involved in this...","No, none of it mattered.","In the face of politics, those things were of no consequence.","\"But in the end, it was still because of the change of commanders with me...\" Qin Shaozong suddenly fell backward, covering his eyes with the back of his hand, the knuckle of his index finger brushing against his broken eyebrow.","It was as if a solemn voice drifted from afar: \"Prefect Qin of Youzhou, this child has brown pupils and long eyes, born with a broken eyebrow. He is destined to harm his father and mother, bringing misfortune to his relatives, and is doomed to have shallow ties with his kin.\"","\"I don't think you're right,\" someone suddenly said.","Her voice was gentle, not particularly loud or forceful, but it was like a spring breeze blowing away the black mist in front of him.","Qin Shaozong paused slightly and moved the hand resting on his eyes away a little.","Dai Li understood the unspoken meaning behind his words.","If the commanders hadn't been switched, his elder brother wouldn't have been murdered by treacherous people, his sister-in-law wouldn't have committed suicide for love, and the siblings Yun Ce and Yun Shu wouldn't have lost their parents at such a young age.","She didn't know the details of that year and couldn't easily judge the change of commanders, but she was somewhat certain about another matter. \"Those involved are often blind to the truth. Actually, I think Yun Ce might know about what happened back then. He admires his biological father so much that he wants to acknowledge him even after more than ten years, which proves that those memories and feelings have never faded. Such a child would definitely do his utmost to collect everything related to his father, let alone the fact that the incident was of such vital importance.\"","Qin Shaozong's pupils contracted slightly.","\"I cannot see what happened in the past, but over these past few months, I have observed that Yun Ce treats you with great respect and holds no resentment. Even if you two are not meant to be father and son in the future, he will definitely treat you as his most respected uncle.\" Dai Li could roughly understand Qin Shaozong's unusual behavior today.","Qin Yunce had reached his coming-of-age ceremony; he was an adult now.","On such a memorable day, he should have received the blessings of his parents as they watched the ceremony. Yet, because of the change of commanders back then, he was separated from his parents by life and death at an early age.","Even though the change of commanders was not proposed by Qin Shaozong himself, just as Qin Hongying had said, her second brother felt guilty and took it to heart.","However, to say how much Qin Changgeng wanted Qin Yunce to be his son, Dai Li felt that wasn't entirely the case either.","Perhaps it was more about the sense of loss from the change in status, or the helplessness of his efforts in cultivating him falling through.","\"The Northern Kingdom has been subdued by you, and the great vengeance of the past has been avenged. I think your elder brother would be very happy if he knew in the netherworld.\" Dai Li took the wick and lit the extinguished candlestick.","The light suddenly flared up, warm and comforting.","Dai Li put the wick away, turned to look at the man still lying on the floor, and suddenly smiled. \"Actually, it's not necessarily knowing in the netherworld. Your brother and sister-in-law might have gone to the Peach Blossom Spring to live a better life... Hey, Qin Changgeng, don't pull my robe.\"","The hem of her clothes stirred up a gentle breeze, and the two candle flames swayed with it, the warm light flickering.","She fell into his arms and was caught steadily by him. The man smiled and sighed, \"You are right, Madam. They have all gone to a better place.\"","\"Right, I have something to ask you.\" Dai Li tried to get up.","The long arm wrapped around her waist did not loosen. \"What is it? Please feel free to say it, Madam.\"","Since he wouldn't let go, Dai Li shifted slightly, sitting on him and looking down at him from above. \"Zhouzhou told me that Nalan recently started teaching him to read other books, learning the ways of cultivating moral character, managing the family, and governing the state. Qin Changgeng, did you instruct Nalan to do this?\"","With the two small lamps behind her, Dai Li's shadow enveloped the face of the man beneath her.","But his eyes gleamed with a hint of brightness in the dark, and she saw him curl his thin lips. \"Madam's guess is correct.\"","Without waiting for Dai Li to ask, Qin Shaozong said leisurely, \"Even if that boy Qin Yanzhou had read books before, he was only nine years old when he left the Peach Blossom Spring. The Green Lotus Cult picked him up to use as a blade, not to make him the reincarnated God of Literature. Knowing a few words was enough; they wouldn't teach him other literature.\"","He suddenly clicked his tongue lightly, his following words carrying a hint of disdain. \"As the dignified patriarch of the Qin clan and the Marquis of Wu'an decreed by the imperial court, how can my son know fewer words than he has fingers on his own hands?\"","Dai Li: \"...\""]},{"number":134,"title":"Chapter 134","paragraphs":["After the coming-of-age ceremony, the entire Qin residence fully entered a busy state of wedding preparations. The wedding date was set for the beginning of spring next year, at which time Daili would marry out from the Qin residence into the Marquis's mansion.","The servants in the residence bustled about, and Qin Shaozong would sometimes spend the entire day at the Marquis's mansion to inspect the progress of the renovations.","The younger ones had to study. Qin Hongying frequently took Shi Rongyue out to meet her old close friends in Yuyang Commandery, paving the way for her daughter to thrive like a fish in water in the future.","The most idle person in the residence was actually Daili.","After staying indoors for another two days, Daili really could not sit still anymore. She took Nianxia and Bipo out of the residence to stroll through the markets. She left at the hour of Chen and was gone for the whole day, finally returning as the last light of the setting sun faded.","Winter days were short and nights were long. Barely the time it takes an incense stick to burn had passed since her return, and the sky, which had just been painted as beautifully as an oil painting, turned completely pitch black.","Lamps were lit in the room. The glowing candlelight was bright and warm, as if it could dispel all gloom.","\"Madam has returned?\" Today, Qin Shaozong had surprisingly returned earlier than Daili. \"Did you have a pleasant time out?\"","Daili casually replied that it was alright, then took off her cloak and sat on a soft chair in a daze. She did not even immediately remove the gold and jade hair ornaments that she usually complained were too heavy.","Having served Daili for some time, Nianxia knew well that her mistress did not like wearing heavy gold and jade temple ornaments when not going out. She was about to walk toward Daili when she saw the master wave his hand at her, indicating that she was not needed here.","Nianxia understood, curtsied, and withdrew.","Qin Shaozong sat beside Daili and raised his hand to help her remove the gold temple ornament inlaid with colored glaze and carved with cloud and phoenix patterns. \"Madam's expression does not look like the 'alright' you just claimed.\"","He had hardly ever done such a thing. When the gold hairpin was pulled from her dark, cloud-like hair, it accidentally caught a strand. Daili felt a sharp pain on her scalp, followed by a faint snap.","It sounded like something had broken.","Daili turned to look at the gold temple ornament tangled with her black hair, and then looked at the man in front of her.","Qin Shaozong: \"...\"","Qin Shaozong coughed lightly. \"Practice makes perfect. Next time, I promise it will return empty-handed.\"","\"The Marquis should just stand aside.\" Daili swatted away his hand that was reaching out again and took off the hair ornaments herself.","\"Madam seems to be in low spirits today,\" he asked from the side.","Daili paused her movements slightly and said something completely unrelated, \"Qin Changgeng, is there any place in Yuyang, led by the local government, that is responsible for taking in beggars?\"","He said, \"Is Madam talking about beggars? No, there isn't. The beggars in the commandery find their own places to stay. In winter, they mostly live in dilapidated houses, and in summer, they rest in the piled-up fish ponds at the market until the fishmongers drive them away early in the morning to do business. There are many recruitment jobs initiated by the government in the commandery. They are mostly manual labor. Although the pay is not much, those who do them will not fail to save enough copper coins to at least live in a thatched hut.\"","Excluding those who are too old or too sick to work, nine out of ten of the others who continue to beg are just suffering from a bout of laziness.","Yuyang Commandery has a population of over four hundred thousand. The same kind of rice feeds a hundred different kinds of people; naturally, it is impossible for there to be not a single beggar.","\"Could it be that Madam saw beggars when you went out today? The winters in the north are bitterly cold. If those beggars sleep outside, it's hard to say how many will be left after a winter.\" His tone was flat.","From the corner of her eye, Daili caught sight of the man bringing his hands together and then slightly apart, constantly moving, not knowing what he was doing.","She turned her head to look and happened to see him twisting a long, fine strand of black hair in his hand. As the final knot was pulled tight, two strands of long hair folded several times were tied together.","Daili: \"...What are you doing?\"","He replied as a matter of course, \"Tying hair. It's rare for the temple ornament to deliver a treasure today, so it shouldn't go to waste. Your husband is just using it for practice.\"","\"I did see beggars,\" Daili answered his initial question, and added, \"Today, as I was wandering around the commandery, I saw many pigsties, some built by wealthy farmers.\"","The so-called pigsty was a pigpen with a latrine attached.","This kind of pigsty with a latrine was generally divided into upper and lower parts. The upper part was a place specifically for using the toilet, elevated by wooden steps, while the lower part was used for raising pigs.","Human feces would drop down for the pigs to eat, and the pig feces would be collected to make fertilizer for the crops.","Daili: \"As far as I know, manure from stables is used the most here, followed by river mud, bean stalks, and silkworm excrement.\"","Qin Shaozong had never farmed, but there were plenty of military farmers in the north. When there were no wars, the soldiers were farmers and had to take their hoes to the fields.","In the past, he had often gone on inspections with his subordinates, so Qin Shaozong was not completely ignorant about farming. \"Madam is right. However, the rivers in the north are not as abundant as those in the south, so river mud is used even less here.\"","Qin Shaozong thought about how she had seemed to have lost her soul since returning to the residence, and then suddenly brought up pigsties. \"Does Madam have any brilliant ideas?\"","\"In terms of crop varieties alone, the yield of wheat is higher than that of millet. Has the Marquis ever thought that if fertilizers are used well, perhaps the yield difference between one wheat field and another could be as vast as the gap between heaven and earth.\" This was what Daili had been thinking about just now.","At that time, she had asked White Elephant whether they had picked up Zhouzhou ten years ago or after the great famine. The latter didn't say explicitly, but looking at his demeanor at the time, she guessed it must have been after the great famine occurred.","That is to say, before this, Zhouzhou had either wandered around, eaten whatever meals he could get from various families, or was adopted by an unknown family for a year before going to the Green Lotus Sect.","Perhaps because she was gradually settling down, her son was by her side, and things were getting better and better, Daili had a different thought for the first time:","In poverty, one should perfect one's own virtues; in success, one should benefit the whole world.","The agricultural history manuscripts she used to review at the publishing house contained many things that could be put to use.","In the earliest times, people adopted the farming methods of plowing with fire and weeding with water and slash-and-burn. The former involved first burning the weeds with fire and then diverting water into the fields. This method was mostly used in the Jiangnan region, which was rich in mountain, forest, and wetland resources. The latter involved cutting down mountain trees in early spring, setting them on fire before the spring rains arrived, and then using the ashes of the trees and grass as fertilizer to plant seeds while the soil was still warm.","This was the initial way to increase the fertility of farmland.","The long river of time flowed slowly until the Spring and Autumn and Warring States periods. At this time, manure seeding, which involved mixing seeds with human and animal feces for planting, appeared.","Human and animal feces are rich in elements such as nitrogen, phosphorus, and potassium. Although people at that time did not recognize these elements, it did not prevent them from knowing that crops grew very well this way.","Later in the Han Dynasty, people turned their attention to green manure. The so-called green manure refers to the use of green plants as fertilizer, such as vetch and alfalfa. Both can fix nitrogen and improve soil fertility.","Further on, people worked hard on the combination of fertilizers, as well as the timing and methods of fertilization, to further increase grain yields.","Qin Shaozong, who had been sitting lazily by the side, straightened up upon hearing this. \"A gap like heaven and earth? How much is that?\"","Daili asked him in return, \"How many shi of wheat can one mu of land yield here?\"","Qin Shaozong: \"About one shi per mu.\"","One shi was equivalent to one hundred and twenty jin.","Daili looked thoughtful. \"If everything goes smoothly, it should be able to increase by half.\"","Even having experienced many great storms, Qin Shaozong couldn't help but show astonishment at this moment. \"That much?\"","Increasing it by half meant that with the same manpower, animal labor, and land area, it was like being gifted half as much land for free. The extra half of the grain was no different from falling from the sky.","\"That's not even considered a lot. Where I come from...\" Daili paused. \"Forget it, I'd better not say.\"","\"Why can't you say?\" Qin Shaozong's curiosity was itching fiercely. He took the initiative to ask, \"How much wheat can one mu of land produce in the Peach Blossom Spring?\"","Daili shook her head and sighed. \"Trust me, it's better if you don't know. Otherwise, I'm afraid if I tell you, you'll be tossing and turning all night, wide awake until dawn.\"","\"Impossible,\" Qin Shaozong flatly denied.","Daili changed her phrasing. \"Sometimes setting expectations too high isn't a good thing. For example, just now when I said I could increase the yield of one mu by half, you already thought it was a lot. However, if you knew the yield in the Peach Blossom Spring, you definitely wouldn't be satisfied with just a fifty percent increase. Because after comparing them, it really would seem pitifully small.\"","Her fair fingers grasped the end of a gold hairpin, slowly pulling it from her hair. Daili continued, \"But that's something I have no way to solve, because wheat yield is related to the wheat seeds, soil moisture, temperature, soil fertility, and so on. And among these, the wheat seeds are absolutely crucial.\"","Qin Shaozong nodded. \"I understand everything Madam says. It's just like how fine steeds from Fergana can endure pain and run fast, unmatched by other horse breeds.\"","If the horse breed wasn't important, he wouldn't have taken away eighty percent of the Northern Kingdom's tens of thousands of excellent horse breeds after conquering them back then.","Daili cast a sidelong glance at him.","Qin Shaozong smiled and said, \"Therefore, Madam might as well speak freely. A fifty percent increase in grain yield means we can feed half of the Northern region's population, and even the common people of the world will benefit in the future. If this matter can be accomplished, perhaps in future times of severe drought, there won't be corpses of the starved littering the fields, and people won't have to resort to exchanging children to eat. Madam's merit would be boundless. As for the rest, just consider it as opening my eyes.\"","He had always been extremely interested in her homeland. Seeing that Daili still didn't speak, he guessed himself, \"Could it be three shi per mu?\"","Here it was one shi, so three shi would be three times as much.","A fifty percent increase was enough to greatly astonish him; three times was already Qin Shaozong guessing as high as he possibly could.","Daili shook her head. \"No.\"","Qin Shaozong asked, \"Could it be five shi?\"","Daili removed all her hair ornaments and stood up feeling completely relaxed, preparing to go to the main hall for dinner.","Qin Shaozong followed behind her. \"Madam...\"","Seeing that he wouldn't give up until he got an answer, Daili said as she walked, \"In the Peach Blossom Spring, the average for one mu of land is around eight shi. With the highest quality soil and wheat seeds, the yield can even reach over fourteen shi.\"","The footsteps following behind her suddenly stopped.","Daili turned her head, not at all surprised to see him frozen in place, the shock in his brown eyes practically overflowing.","Daili chuckled softly, ignoring him, and continued walking forward on her own.","During this dinner, everyone present could see that Qin Shaozong was distracted. The man, who usually drank a little millet wine with every meal, completely ignored his wine cup today. He just kept staring at the millet rice in his bowl, lost in thought, not even paying attention when Qin Hongying spoke to him.","After the meal, as soon as Daili stood up to leave, he also stood up and followed.","The two left the main hall one after the other.","Qin Qinian watched their retreating backs. \"Father was very quiet just now. Could it be that he's tired from running around everywhere today?\"","As soon as he finished speaking, Qin Hongying laughed. \"If your father hears you saying that, he'll inevitably drag you off to the training grounds to discipline you personally.\"","Qin Qinian immediately shrank his neck.","Qin Yunce smiled and said, \"Every day that passes is one day less. We are getting closer and closer to next spring. I guess Uncle might be preoccupied with tomorrow's progress. By the way, the teacher isn't holding class tomorrow. If you're curious, why not go back with Uncle?\"","\"No can do, we already have plans for tomorrow, we're busy,\" Qin Qinian said without a second thought.","He said \"we\". If the other person wasn't present, he would usually use \"they\".","\"Who do you have plans with? Is it Yanzhou?\" Qin Hongying ruled out Qin Yunce, who had just asked the question, and could only think of Qin Yanzhou.","Qin Qinian: \"Yes, and also...\"","He suddenly paused, forcefully steering his words in another direction. \"And Xuenu is going out with us to wander around the markets, to take a stroll in the commandery.\"","Shi Rongyue breathed a sigh of relief in her heart. She took a tiny step forward, moving out of her mother's blind spot, and stood back by her mother's side.","Qin Hongying seemed to sense something and turned to look at her daughter, only to see the little girl looking perfectly well-behaved, still the picture of gentle quietness.","She couldn't see it, but Qin Yanzhou and Qin Yunce had seen it clearly. Just a moment ago, Shi Rongyue had been waving her little hands so rapidly they were almost a blur.","\"It's good for young people to go out and walk around more.\" Qin Hongying suddenly changed her tune. \"How about you take Rongrong out with you too?\"","Qin Qinian: \"Huh?\"","Qin Hongying thought he was unwilling. \"Rongrong was taken out by me a few days ago to meet some old friends. She hasn't known the young ladies of her age for very long, so it's inevitably a bit awkward for them to hang out together. But you and Rongrong are different; you grew up together. Others can't compare. She'll be much more at ease going out with you.\"","Qin Qinian immediately said, \"Aunt is right.\"","Having received a satisfactory answer, Qin Hongying left contentedly.","As soon as she left, Qin Qinian said, \"Does this count as that saying... two different paths that eventually lead to the same destination?\"","\"Different paths, same destination.\" Qin Yanzhou couldn't bear listening anymore.","Qin Qinian slapped his forehead. \"Ah, right, different paths, same destination.\"","\"What are you guys secretly plotting?\" Qin Yunce looked at one, then the other.","\"Uh, well, the matter has to start from the winter hunt...\"","*","Back in the main courtyard, Daili planned to go to sleep after digesting her food. The production of organic fertilizer would be put on the agenda starting tomorrow, so she needed to go to bed early tonight.","The winter was cold, so Daili had specially asked someone to make a copper bed warmer to heat her blankets. The copper bed warmer was wrapped in a layer of velvet fabric to slow down the heat loss, and placing it in the bed could keep it warm all night.","The bed was warmed up to be incredibly cozy. Daili sighed contentedly, then rolled herself up in the blankets, ready to sleep.","As for Qin Shaozong, he could do as he pleased.","This man sometimes still had to write one or two urgent letters before bed to be dispatched first thing the next morning.","However, tonight, the man merely sat at his desk with a profound expression, not touching the writing brush, ink, paper, or inkstone temporarily set up in the outer room.","After sitting for about a quarter of an hour, he got up, returned to the room, took off his clothes, and got into bed.","Daili had good sleep quality. By the time he came back, she was already deeply drowsy, half a step out the door ready to meet the Duke of Zhou in her dreams.","By the time he lay down completely, she had already fallen fast asleep.","Daili was asleep, but Qin Shaozong had absolutely no desire to sleep.","One mu of land could produce up to fourteen shi of wheat, with an average of eight shi. This meant that under the same conditions of human and animal labor, that place yielded fourteen times as much as here.","No wonder she once said that every household in the Peach Blossom Spring had surplus grain. This was far more than just a normal surplus; it was clearly a reserve capable of bursting granaries.","Qin Shaozong thought of that famine from nine years ago.","At that time, the entire Great Yan was shrouded in the dark clouds of famine, and the northern lands were naturally no exception. Yuyang had a population of over four hundred thousand, and the north could not compare to the fertile lands of Jiangnan. Unable to even fend for themselves, they could only distribute grain within the city.","As for the refugees blocked outside the city gates, relief was provided at most only once after a considerable period of time.","Some refugees were in rags and all alone; some were emaciated and dragging their families along; others were on the verge of death. They chased after and begged passing carriages, hoping to plead for a mouthful of food from the occupants.","However, as carriages passed by, they usually could not give out food casually. Once the starving refugees received a signal, they would swarm forward like they had lost their minds. If the travelers were weak in numbers, they could easily be devoured clean.","During that period, corpses littered the wilderness outside the city, piling up like swamps. Children's heads were severed from their necks, and bellies and intestines trampled by horse hooves trailed out sparsely across the ground.","Qin Shaozong seemed to hear the endless wailing and crying again. He stretched out his long arm and pulled the woman beside him into his embrace.","In the darkness, the brown eyes watching the person in his arms seemed to gleam with light.","If Great Yan could also have barns full of grain, then whether encountering severe droughts or the flooding of the two rivers, the common people would still not have to worry about food and drink, and could live and work in peace and contentment.","As Dai Li slept, she suddenly noticed an uncomfortable sense of constriction holding her tightly. She broke free from that feeling, rolled herself up in the quilt, stepped on her hot water bottle, and continued to sleep.","But as she slept, her feet suddenly stepped into empty space.","The perfectly good heat source was suddenly gone. Still asleep, Dai Li instinctively stretched out her feet to feel around.","She didn't find the hot water bottle, but she kicked a solid wall.","It was equally hot and toasty.","Dai Li tucked both her feet in, even stepping on the self-heating footrest underneath.","Mhm, comfortable.","Dai Li had a dreamless and restful night. But beside her, someone kept his eyes open until dawn.","...","When Dai Li woke up the next day, she found that her hot water bottle had somehow rolled to the corner of the bed and plunged into the covers, leaving only its round bottom exposed.","Holding the quilt, she stared at the hot water bottle for a moment, inexplicably feeling that it shouldn't be there. However, this doubt only flashed by and didn't occupy too much of her attention.","After finishing breakfast, Dai Li called for Hu Bao. Captain Hu, I would like two shi of plant ash, two shi of bone meal, and half a shi of limestone. Please take your men to prepare them.","Hu Bao asked in confusion, Madam Dai, does the bone meal you mentioned refer to anything specific?","Dai Li said there wasn't. Just lead your men to the meat market and collect a batch of large bones. After calcining them, they can easily be crushed into powder.","Poultry bones were bones, and cattle and sheep bones were also bones, but catching an entire family of the former probably wouldn't even equal a single leg of the latter.","Wood ash is rich in potassium, bone meal is rich in phosphorus, and a small amount of lime can adjust the pH of the soil.","Of course, apart from these auxiliary inorganic materials, the most important ones were the organic materials.","Besides these three items, you... never mind, Captain, just gather these for now, Dai Li changed her mind mid-sentence.","Hu Bao accepted his orders and left first.","Before Dai Li could speak, Qin Shaozong, who had been observing from the side, took the initiative to ask, Does Madam have any concerns?","Great Yan currently still mostly uses stable manure, but one must know that the core principle remains the same; other materials also cannot do without various types of manure. But this stuff isn't suitable to be piled directly in the manor. It affects the living environment and makes subsequent fertilizing inconvenient. Dai Li wrinkled her nose as if she could already smell the odor.","Qin Shaozong chuckled, I thought it was some earth-shattering problem, but it's only this. If it can't be placed in the manor, then pile it in the fields. I have tens of thousands of hectares of fertile land, why worry about not having room for a few piles of manure?","Dai Li: ...","Having said that, Qin Shaozong raised his voice and called for Feng Feng, who was on duty today. Feng Feng, take some men to buy a few carts of cow dung and pig dung, and then deliver them to the fields in the south near the Wangqun Mountains.","Feng Feng's expression remained unchanged.","With orders from his superior, let alone just buying pig and cow dung, even if he were told to carry the dung himself, he would have to go.","We also need some straw, Dai Li added from the side.","Feng Feng was different from the other three garrison commanders of the Xuanxiao Cavalry. His father was a farmer, and he had to help farm when he was young. Now, hearing that they needed both manure and straw, Feng Feng realized, My Lord, are you trying to compost?","It is not I who wishes to, but Madam. Qin Shaozong then looked at Dai Li. Madam, can this matter be spoken of?","Some matters must be accomplished in secret. While others, the more high-profile they were, the better.","Feng Feng was slightly taken aback.","Dai Li didn't care either way. Sure, they'll find out sooner or later anyway.","She spoke casually, but Qin Shaozong heard another layer of meaning: she was absolutely certain that it wouldn't fail.","Qin Shaozong curled his thin lips. Madam has a brand-new method of composting that can increase crop yields by half.","It was as if a clap of thunder exploded in Feng Feng's mind, causing his entire body to tremble uncontrollably. In a rare breach of etiquette, he questioned his superior for the first time, Is what you say true?","His father had died during a drought when heaven was uncooperative; more accurately, his father was crushed to death by the exorbitant cost of grain.","If at that time...","Qin Shaozong: Naturally it is true. Go and handle this first; you will understand this matter later.","Feng Feng couldn't wait to cup his hands and accept the order.","Cow dung and pig dung were not difficult to collect, especially for the son of a tenant farmer; he knew all too well where to quickly get these things. Although he set off later than Hu Bao, Feng Feng was the first to complete his task.","When he returned in the afternoon, he ran into Qin Yanzhou, Qin Qinian, and Shi Rongyue.","Commander Feng, aren't you today... what is that smell? Qin Qinian originally wanted to go up and chat for a bit, but after taking two steps, he abruptly stopped.","Feng Feng showed no embarrassment. I just followed the Lord's orders to collect a few carts of cow and pig dung. It is said that Madam Dai has a unique composting method that can make crop yields far exceed those of the past, even increasing them by about half.","The few of them suddenly saw the light.","And these words, as if growing wings, spread throughout the entire Qin manor in just a single day."]},{"number":135,"title":"Chapter 135","paragraphs":["\"Increase the yield by half? How is that possible?!\" Sheng Ran's eyes widened.","\"Madam Dai does not appear to be of peasant origins, so how could she understand composting, let alone speak of some exclusive method? And this claim of a fifty percent increase is far too exaggerated,\" Cui Shengping said, his tone filled with suspicion and gravity.","Sheng Ran understood his suspicion, but the gravity that followed...","The two exchanged a glance.","No one who served as a strategist was foolish. In that brief exchange of looks, Sheng Ran suddenly understood something. \"Haiqing, do you think all of this is our Lord's doing?\"","The messenger had already retreated, and with no one else around, Sheng Ran finished the second half of his thought. \"Are you suspecting that our Lord is currently building up momentum for Young Master Qin?\"","\"Is that not the case? Increasing crop yields by half is easy to say, just a slip of the tongue, but how easy is it to actually achieve? If it could be done, the number of people who starved to death during the floods in the Two Rivers and the great droughts of the past would have been reduced by fifty or sixty percent. In terms of political achievements and merit, what could be greater? Taking a step back, even if such a method existed, it should be in the hands of an experienced farmer. How could a delicately raised lady know of it?\" Cui Shengping said, his brows tightly furrowed by the end of his speech.","\"But the dragon bone water wheel clearly...\" Sheng Ran paused. \"At that time, you and I were both in Bingzhou handling Lord Rong's subsequent affairs and had no time to go to Ying Commandery. Only Nalan Wugong knows the true details of that matter.\"","But Nalan Zhi was Qin Yanzhou's master, and he himself was an extremely sharp person.","If they inquired about the dragon bone water wheel at this critical juncture, the other party would definitely guess that not only were they half-believing at first, but they were now holding an attitude of doubt.","Cui Shengping stopped stroking his long beard. \"It is not appropriate to discuss this matter with Nalan Wugong.\"","Sheng Ran originally disagreed, but now he nodded.","\"Previously, we suggested that the Third Young Master marry the legitimate daughter of Governor Nangong, but this proposal was rejected by our Lord. Now, with such news spreading, a son's status rises with his mother's. Our Lord is so deeply in love with Madam Dai that it makes one worry he is paving the way for Young Master Qin...\" Cui Shengping said.","The grand wedding next spring was already set in stone.","Let alone them, even the prominent Wei family had been dealt with by their Lord when they tried to interfere. They could not hinder, nor did they have the power to stop their Lord's wedding.","Both men felt a terrible headache coming on.","\"What should we do about this?\"","\"Our Lord has always ruled with an iron fist. If we try our best to dissuade him halfway, it might backfire. It is better to wait and see. Anyway, this fifty percent increase...\" Cui Shengping shook his head. \"Unless our Lord secretly opens his private treasury to make up the difference for her, it is absolutely impossible.\"","He spoke the last four words with resounding force.","\"You are right. When the time comes, we will keep a close eye on our Lord and join forces with the other garrison commanders to stop it in time, so that we can end this farce early...\"","After dinner, the sky was gray, as if covered by a heavy black veil. And at this time when they should have been resting, a group of military officers gathered in the courtyard, whispering among themselves.","\"...Increasing the yield by half is a bit exaggerated.\" This was the tactful Bai Jianping.","\"I really want to believe Madam Dai, but my reason tells me that if I believe her, then all those granary officials, the Grand Minister of Agriculture, and the Chief Commandant of Waterways are all uselessly occupying their positions and deserve to die!\" This was the serious Mo Yanyun.","Did they not deserve to die? So many people had studied this back and forth, yet none of them had the extensive knowledge of a single lady like Madam Dai.","\"Since Madam Dai dared to make such a claim, I think she must know what she is doing.\" This was the steadfast Qiao Wangfei.","\"So how much material was prepared today?\" This was Wei Qing, who had been absent during the day.","Feng Feng answered truthfully, \"I was in charge of buying three carts of cow and pig manure, and Hu Bao was responsible for buying bone meal, lime, and plant ash.\"","\"Bone meal? What is this used for?\" asked the usually taciturn Yan San.","Feng Feng rolled his eyes. \"I do not know. But since Madam Dai has already started preparing the materials, she will probably start composting soon. Why do we not all go outside the main courtyard tomorrow and await her orders?\"","\"You always have the best ideas, Old Feng!\"","...","The sun set and rose, and the eastern sky turned white.","Dai Li woke up from her sleep and heard Nian Xia say that a group of military officers was waiting for her outside. Having just woken up, Dai Li thought she had misheard. \"Waiting for me? Why?\"","\"Is it not because you mentioned composting yesterday? They are all extremely curious and are now competing to serve you, Madam.\" Nian Xia pursed her lips and smiled.","Dai Li rubbed her eyes. \"How long have they been here?\"","\"About two quarters of an hour. Hearing that you were not awake, they all said there was no rush and to wait until you had slept enough. They have already drank several pots of tea.\" Nian Xia looked extremely proud.","In the past, she had also been a slave and a maid, but the masters she served were extremely subservient in front of the male master, and by extension, they were evasive and accommodating when facing the male master's subordinates.","Let alone having a group of people wait for her to wake up, even getting a word of praise from the subordinates was impossible.","No, not necessarily.","It was just that after receiving praise, the male master was very likely to give away his favored concubine as a gift.","Dai Li said to Nian Xia, \"I am going to the fields today, so keep my hair accessories and clothes simple.\"","After she washed up, finished breakfast, and came out of the main courtyard, the group of military officers who heard her footsteps turned their heads in unison.","From Dai Li's perspective, there were several wooden stakes standing at the entrance of the main courtyard. Some were leaning against the wall, some were squatting, and others were simply sitting on the ground.","Now that they saw her, their eyes lit up. If they changed out of their martial attire, they would look exactly like a group of workers demanding unpaid wages.","Dai Li was speechless.","But before Dai Li could speak, a tall figure turned the corner at the other end of the corridor.","It was Qin Shaozong, who had returned right on time.","After the news was released yesterday, he was not surprised that a circle of military officers surrounded the front of the main courtyard early this morning. However, knowing about it was one thing; seeing it with his own eyes and feeling displeased was another.","His beloved generals from the past now looked like wooden splinters stuck in the ground, the ones squatting were an eyesore, and the ones standing were in the way. Qin Shaozong's gaze swept over them, and as soon as he opened his mouth, his tone was unwelcoming. \"What, are you all very free?\"","The scalps of all the military officers tightened.","Just a moment ago, they were sitting and standing without any proper posture, but now they quickly stood up straight.","\"My Lord.\"","After the group paid their respects, they looked down at their noses and their noses at their hearts, lowering their heads like quails.","Since no one spoke, Dai Li said, \"Are you all planning to go to the fields with me?\"","The frozen atmosphere instantly boiled over.","\"We are willing to offer our meager strength to you.\"","The military officers had loud voices, and this unanimous shout carried far away. Qin Yanzhou and Qin Qinian, who had just finished their morning exercises in the distance, were both taken aback.","The young man asked in surprise, \"What happened over there?\"","Qin Yanzhou thought of yesterday. \"Garrison Commander Feng prepared the materials yesterday. They must have gone to look for my mother today.\"","Qin Qinian loved to join in the fun. \"Then let us go too!\"","...","In front of the main courtyard.","\"...Right, we also need a lot of straw. I'll have to trouble you to go and collect some.\" Dai Li nodded.","Temperature directly affects composting. In spring and autumn, the temperature is suitable, and the microorganisms in the soil are active, which can quickly decompose waste.","In summer and winter, it is either too hot or too cold. Especially in the winter in the north, the temperature can easily drop below ten degrees, so it is necessary to keep the soil warm.","In modern times, plastic film can be used for insulation. A large piece of black plastic film is pulled over the ground and pressed down to form a relatively heat-absorbing area. But in this era, there is no such thing as plastic film, so straw can only be used as a substitute for insulation.","Don't underestimate straw. There is an ancient saying, \"Before the troops and horses move, the provisions and fodder go first.\" The \"fodder\" here not only refers to horse feed, but also straw.","Before the Song Dynasty, when cotton was not yet widely used, soldiers marching and fighting used straw to keep warm at night. Dried straw was covered over their bodies, smelling good and keeping them warm.","And now, Dai Li needed to use straw for insulation.","Feng Feng and Qiao Wangfei took the task of collecting straw and left first. The others were still in place, rubbing their hands in anticipation, waiting for Dai Li to assign tasks.","Dai Li rubbed her forehead helplessly. \"Food is the most important thing for the people, and grain is the foundation of the country. I can understand your anxiety, but composting is not something that can be achieved overnight. Just the pre-process of fermentation and decomposition of feces can take several months.\"","Normally, the fermentation and decomposition of feces takes a month and a half to two months. And the microorganisms in it are affected by temperature, and the time will be shortened or extended accordingly.","If it is summer, the fermentation and decomposition can be completed in about a month; but if it is winter, the time will be much longer, and it will take three to four months to complete the fermentation.","Of course, this is the most traditional composting method.","In modern times, fermentation bacteria are usually added artificially to efficiently complete the decomposition process. But there is no way here, and everything can only be left to time.","\"Several months? So long?\" Mo Yanyun was dumbfounded.","Not only him, but the others also looked astonished.","Except for Feng Feng, who was ordered to collect straw, none of the other generals had ever farmed. Now hearing Dai Li say this, besides their shock, they also felt a sense of frustration of having a lot of strength but nowhere to use it.","\"But if you don't mind, there is still work to do.\" Dai Li suddenly smiled. The corners of her eyes curled up a little, adding a bit of rare slyness.","Qin Shaozong could tell at a glance that her next words would be unusual. He raised his eyebrows slightly, but said nothing.","All the generals were very enthusiastic:","\"Madam Dai, just say it. As long as I can do it, I will not refuse.\"","\"Even if it is a mountain of swords and a sea of fire, I will go and brave it!\"","Hearing them speak more and more exaggeratedly, Dai Li couldn't help laughing and waving her hands. \"You don't need to climb a mountain of swords. It's just that the compost needs to be turned from time to time, about every four or five days, to change the position of the feces and grass, so as to dissipate the exhaust gas in the pile and help the growth of small creatures inside.\"","As soon as these words came out, the surroundings became quiet.","Some people didn't understand the latter sentence about small creatures, but it didn't prevent them from understanding the former.","Turn, turn the feces and dirt?","The generals' eyes widened.","Letting them go to the battlefield to kill the enemy and fight a bloody battle, they would never blink an eye, but turning this feces and dirt...","The atmosphere froze again.","Just then, a highly recognizable drake voice came over: \"Father, are you and Madam Dai going out of the mansion? Can you take me and Qin Yanzhou with you?\"","Swish, swish, the figures in front of Qin Qinian and Qin Yanzhou all flashed away.","The young man's eyebrows moved slightly, and his gaze swept over everyone, finally landing on Dai Li. Today, Dai Li was dressed in all black, and her long hair was tied into a high ponytail. She looked quite valiant and heroic, and it was obvious that she was not going for an ordinary outing.","\"Mother, I want to go with you,\" Qin Yanzhou said.","Dai Li suspected that these two didn't know anything and purely wanted to join in the fun, so she asked him directly: \"Zhou Zhou, do you know where I'm going and what I'm going to do?\"","Qin Yanzhou nodded and said he knew, \"You are going to the fields outside the city to compost.\"","Dai Li said again: \"Yesterday I had someone collect a few carts of cow dung and pig dung. According to the plan, we have to go pile it up today. Are you sure you want to come?\"","Qin Yanzhou: \"I want to come.\"","He had seen streets full of rice shops side by side, and barns full of rice and flour. He was also a person who had truly suffered from hunger and even eaten grass roots and tree bark. If he could help, stepping on cow dung a few times was really nothing.","The other generals suddenly felt their faces burning hotly.","As the son of Madam Dai, Young Master Qin would soon be a young master recorded in the Qin family's genealogy. He didn't mind the dirt and mess, so what face did they have to keep quiet.","Having watched enough of the show, Qin Shaozong spoke, \"You can stay or leave as you please. Madam, let's go.\"","The group rode out of the city.","In winter, it doesn't snow every day. After it snows, as long as the sun comes out, the snow will slowly melt. In a word, it snows for a day or two, and then the snow melts for a long time.","It hadn't snowed for the past few days, and the snow on the ground had mostly melted. The silver clothing that the earth had previously put on gradually faded away.","The Qin family was originally a prominent family. Even if Qin Shaozong wasn't the top official of Yuyang Commandery, he also had a lot of land. These fertile fields would be rented to tenant farmers for cultivation, and as the owner of the farmland, he only needed to collect rent regularly.","The sky was broad and blue, occasionally with sparse birds gliding by, and majestic green mountains in the distance. Looking at the flat fields in the suburbs, they were like neat patches, connected to each other, end to end, as if they were going to reach the horizon.","Winter is the slack season in farming, and Dai Li didn't see many farmers along the way.","\"We're here.\" Qin Shaozong reined in Chi Jiao.","Dai Li dismounted, and then rubbed her face. She was in a hurry when she went out and forgot to wear a veiled hat. Having just been blown by the cold wind all the way, her face was numb from the cold.","Seeing this, Qin Shaozong also reached over. \"Fair-skinned and tender, frostbitten? Let me see.\"","\"Don't trouble yourself.\" Dai Li disliked the thick calluses on his hands and turned her head to avoid him.","Behind them, the generals were either looking down to study the mud under their feet, looking far away at the green mountains, or seriously adjusting their saddles.","Everyone was very busy.","Dai Li was also busy. After hurriedly ending a banter, she asked Hu Bao: \"Have the bone meal and plant ash collected yesterday been transported here?\"","\"Yes, they have all been packed in gunny sacks.\" Hu Bao went down to the field first.","\"We don't need them urgently for now, we can leave them for a while.\" Dai Li also went down to the field area.","She gestured the height. \"Mix those few piles of cow dung and pig dung together, try to pile it into a round mound. The compost mound should be about nine feet high, and it should be as large as possible so that the heat dissipates as slowly as possible. Oh, right, before piling, a layer of weeds should be laid at the bottom, preferably a four-to-six ratio of dry leaves and green grass. A total of ten gunny sacks are needed.\"","They didn't have people collect weeds yesterday, but this field of Qin Shaozong's was close to the mountain, so taking a trip would be quite fast.","Yan San and the others immediately grabbed the sacks and rode over on their horses. Not long after, they returned with bulging sacks.","\"Scatter it all here.\" Dai Li had just ordered someone to dig a pit. \"Lay the dry leaves first, then the green grass. Don't use it all, just a third is enough. Where is the water I asked for just now? Zhou Zhou, pour some water in.\"","The young man lifted the wooden bucket, holding the wooden handle with one hand and supporting the bottom of the bucket with the other, splashing water into the pit with a loud splash.","Dai Li instructed, \"Now lay down the cow dung and pig manure, alternating layers with the dry leaves and green grass. Zhou Zhou, water it.\"","Everyone followed her instructions.","After a flurry of activity, six carts of manure mixed with dry leaves and green grass were piled into two large compost heaps.","Dai Li clapped her hands. \"Cover the top with straw and we're done. Let's call it a day here. Tomorrow, go collect some more cow and pig manure, and repeat the process to make more compost heaps. As for these finished piles, My Lord, arrange a duty roster and have someone come turn them every five days.\"","There were so many fields in the North; just a little bit of organic fertilizer would never be enough. Since it was currently the agricultural off-season, they might as well make more.","The crowd acknowledged the order.","Rumble—","Dai Li faintly heard the sound of wheels. She looked towards Yuyang following the sound, and unexpectedly saw a carriage driving this way.","She froze slightly, subconsciously turning her head to look at Qin Shaozong beside her. The man met her eyes, a touch of gentle warmth filling his brown eyes.","\"My lady, come home with me,\" he smiled.","A cold wind blew against her face, so icy that it even made her skin feel slightly numb.","But that carriage was like a torch. It was clearly not luxurious or eye-catching, yet it exuded a comforting warmth.","Dai Li lowered her eyes.","*","From that day on, every few days, several fast horses would leave the Qin Manor together, heading straight for the outskirts of the city.","Fast horses came and went, the sun rose and set, and time slowly flowed by.","Before they knew it, three months had passed. And at the tail end of deep winter, Dai Li's first batch of mature compost completed its fermentation amidst everyone's eager anticipation.","-----------------------"]},{"number":136,"title":"Chapter 136","paragraphs":["Madam, three months have passed. That fermentation process you mentioned should be complete by now.","It wasn't just Feng Feng and the others; Qin Shaozong had also kept the composting matter in mind at all times.","When he said this, Dai Li was eating breakfast.","The steaming noodle soup gave off a mist that clung to the woman's long, dark eyelashes, as if coating them in a layer of moisture. As she slowly raised her eyes, that bright glint seemed to fall into her pitch-black pupils, accompanied by the radiant ripples that spread as she curled her lips into a smile.","You only asked about the composting date once before. I thought you weren't in a hurry, Dai Li teased him with a smile.","It involves the granaries and the livelihood of the people. As the governing official of the North, I am naturally anxious. Though Qin Shaozong spoke of being anxious, his expression was remarkably peaceful. He picked up the teapot and refilled Dai Li's half-empty cup. But I have complete faith in you, Madam, which is why I haven't asked much about it.","As he poured her tea, Dai Li subconsciously brought her index and middle fingers together and tapped the table twice lightly.","Qin Shaozong paused. After setting down the teapot, he mimicked her gesture, tapping twice. What does this mean?","Dai Li: ...It means thank you.","Qin Shaozong tapped again. Is this popular where you come from?","It's derived from an old story passed down through the generations. Seeing his keen interest, Dai Li knew without guessing that he would ask, so she simply explained, In the past, there was an emperor known as Qianlong who went on an incognito inspection tour. While chatting with his ministers in a teahouse, he casually poured tea for a subordinate. Because the teahouse was bustling with people, the minister couldn't kneel to thank him for his imperial grace. In a moment of desperation, he used two fingers as legs, bending them to show gratitude. Later, this story spread, and over time, the bent fingers evolved into a simple finger-tapping gesture, meaning a silent thank you.","Qin Shaozong sighed in admiration, How interesting. If there's ever a chance, I'd truly like to accompany you to see your Peach Blossom Spring.","Forget it, you wouldn't get used to it there, Dai Li said without a second thought.","Qin Shaozong frowned in confusion. Why? I have always had an infinite fondness for your homeland.","You now control several states in the North. Do you know what this kind of behavior is called in my homeland? Dai Li's expression turned solemn. Amassing troops to build personal power—that's warlord behavior! In a place where the people are the masters, you'd be overthrown and executed on the spot.","Qin Shaozong: ...","It was rare to see such a conflicted and speechless expression on this man's face. Feeling quite pleased, Dai Li picked up her jade chopsticks, scooped into her bowl, and quickly finished the rest of her noodles.","They did indeed need to visit the fields today. After breakfast, Dai Li and Qin Shaozong led their people and rode out of the city.","A heavy snow had fallen last night, leaving deep drifts along the road to the farmlands. Under normal circumstances, recklessly riding a horse through it could easily result in a broken horse leg.","However, before the two arrived, Mo Yanyun and the others had roughly cleared the path, so Dai Li and Qin Shaozong enjoyed an unimpeded journey.","Three months had passed. The original two round compost heaps had multiplied like rabbits breeding madly. In what seemed like the blink of an eye, the fields were covered with mounds.","Dai Li arrived at the very first farmland—Field Number One.","Mother. Qin Yanzhou had also arrived early.","Not only him, but Qin Qinian and Shi Rongyue were also there.","Qin Hongying was, after all, married into the Shi family and had more children than just Shi Rongyue. Shortly after her nephew's coming-of-age ceremony, she returned to Nanyu Commandery, leaving only her daughter in Yuyang. Before leaving, she specifically pulled Dai Li aside for a long chat, asking her to look after Shi Rongyue.","Dai Li had never raised a daughter. Aside from occasionally calling Shi Rongyue over to chat with the little girl, she mostly just let her play with the three young masters of the estate.","A sixteen-year-old child would only be in their first year of high school in modern times. They were bound to be playful, and she couldn't just keep her locked up.","As the composting project gradually unfolded, Shi Rongyue also frequently tagged along to the outskirts.","The young girl was born into a prominent family but was not spoiled. Right now, wearing a pair of brown deerskin boots, she was stepping into mud puddles as she followed behind Qin Yanzhou. After Qin Yanzhou greeted them, she also bowed to Dai Li. Madam Dai.","Dai Li dismounted her horse. How long have you all been here?","Qin Yanzhou knew she usually slept until she naturally woke up, so he said, Only about half an hour. Mother, what should we do next?","Dai Li: Spread the compost heaps open so we can take a look.","A group of military officers received the order and began working vigorously with large shovels.","In the early stages of composting, every time the heaps were turned, Dai Li would have people add bone meal and other materials. Later, when these materials ran out, several empty sacks were left sitting there.","It was fortunate that it was the agricultural off-season, otherwise the sacks would definitely have been scavenged.","The nine-foot-tall mounds were quickly leveled. Dark brown, sand-like fertile soil poured out and was spread over a large area.","It's truly magical. It was clearly reeking before, but now it hardly smells at all, Qin Qinian said in surprise.","He and Qin Yanzhou had previously volunteered to turn the compost heaps a few times. The mixed stench of cow and pig manure was enough to blow the top off a person's skull, but now there was barely any odor.","Dai Li smiled. Once fermentation is complete, it naturally doesn't stink. Let them dry out a bit more in the daylight today, and then we can bag them up when the sun is about to set.","Bag them? Madam, why not just leave this fertile soil directly in the fields? Qin Shaozong asked.","Whether it was slash-and-burn or fire-tillage and water-weeding, the fertilizer was always left in place; there had never been a step to extract it.","Before sowing, one mu of land uses at most one shi. Dai Li looked at the spread-out manure heaps. This single mu of land had four large compost heaps piled on it, and each heap weighed at least a few tons.","Only one shi is needed before sowing, and later topdressing requires diluting the fertile soil. From any angle, it's impossible to just leave it directly in the field, Dai Li explained.","Qin Shaozong's pupils contracted slightly. Only one shi?","A single compost heap was about several dozen shi, which meant it could cover several dozen mu of land.","He gazed out over the fields. Mound after mound stood on the farmland. At first glance, they looked completely ordinary, and many of them had not yet finished fermenting, still carrying a stench that ordinary people would find unbearable.","But Qin Shaozong knew that these mounds of dung and dirt, which ordinary people found repulsive, would turn into soft gold in the fields after the coming spring, vigorously supporting the growth of the crops.","If there were no severe droughts or insect plagues, by next autumn, this endless stretch of farmland would yield a vast, brilliant expanse of gold. Whenever the wind blew, the scent of wheat would drift, and golden waves would flutter and ripple outward, seemingly without end.","Qin Shaozong felt as if he could hear the swaying of the wheat ears and smell the rich fragrance of the wheat.","Invisible scrolls of scenery unrolled before his eyes.","Farmers harvesting wheat in the fields grinning from ear to ear; ox carts traveling endlessly through the countryside, each piled high with mountains of wheat.","The large granaries in the commandery stuffed to the brim, with agricultural commandants and field-protecting officers coming one after another to report that there was insufficient granary space, requesting the construction of new ones.","When spring comes next year, we will distribute this organic fertilizer to the farmers. Plant a single seed in spring, harvest ten thousand grains in autumn. Next autumn is bound to be a golden season of abundant harvest. Seeing her son pick up a shovel, Dai Li also joined the ranks of those bagging the fertilizer.","\"When the wind rises, the crops thrive, and the carts are filled with bountiful harvests. If that day truly comes, the people of Yuyang, the North, and even the whole world should thank you, Madam,\" Qin Shaozong said solemnly.","\"It's just organic fertilizer. Being able to improve the seeds is what's truly remarkable...\" Dai Li looked at the distant sky, her tone full of nostalgia.","In the sky, it was as if vast fields of rice ears, taller than a person, appeared. An old man wearing a straw hat leaned against a rice stalk, smiling as he enjoyed the shade beneath the heavy ears of grain.","\"Qin Yanzhou, come compete with me and see who can pack more!\" a young boy's voice rang out, full of fighting spirit.","The young man's voice wasn't as loud as his, and it was unclear what he said. The two of them quickly went their separate ways, each holding a shovel, and then began shoveling the fertile soil with all their might.","Dai Li could not help but smile.","Winter passed and spring arrived. When the frozen rivers slowly began to flow and the earth gradually revealed its original colors, the tail end of the bitter winter finally slipped away.","Lichun, the Beginning of Spring, had arrived.","Lichun is the first of the twenty-four solar terms, marking the start of spring. All things come back to life in spring, and there is no farmer who does not look forward to its arrival.","And this year's Lichun was undoubtedly special. In the vast lands of Yuyang, if you grabbed any old person, weakling, woman, or child at random, who wouldn't know that their Marquis of Wu'an was getting married?","As early as seven days ago, during the meal times of morning and late afternoon, all the major eateries in Yuyang Commandery opened up endless banquets.","Whether one was a commoner, a merchant, or a noble, as long as they came to dine at the eateries, they did not need to spend a single silver coin. All expenses were covered entirely by the Marquis's estate.","In addition to the endless banquets, at a side gate of the Marquis's estate, sweet treats were specially distributed to children under the age of ten. As long as a child sang a festive limerick while taking a stroll around the city, they could return to claim a handful of snacks.","Furthermore, there was a piece of news that the farmers of Yuyang found hard to believe: it was said that this Madam Dai, whom their Marquis was about to marry, had developed a type of fertilizer. Using it could significantly increase crop yields, up to fifty percent. Every farming household could go to the local government office to receive a bag of fertilizer for free.","This fertilizer was considered a celebratory gift from her to the farmers of Yuyang for her wedding.","There was no need to mention the farmers' astonishment, ecstasy, and skepticism. In short, after this event, the discussions about Dai Li in Yuyang Commandery reached a whole new level.","Seven days before Lichun, cart after cart of betrothal gifts and dowry were simultaneously pulled into the Qin estate by horse-drawn carriages.","Dai Li's identity was no secret. She did not come from a prominent family, and even her parents were no longer alive. Anyone with a discerning eye could tell that those boxes of eye-catching and magnificent treasures were not prepared by Dai Li herself at all.","The carriages formed a long, winding line like a dragon, stretching out for a great distance and appearing in the city day after day. The onlookers went from initial surprise and shock to becoming numb and accustomed to it, until finally, only sighs of admiration and envy remained.","As for the prominent families in Yuyang, the astute ones who noticed the carriages entering the Qin estate on the first day immediately ordered their servants to prepare a generous gift and send it over.","They used the pretext of congratulating Dai Li, without mentioning Qin Shaozong.","The Qin estate, which usually did not accept gifts, gladly accepted them this time. Seeing this, the other prominent families quickly followed suit. For a time, brocade box after brocade box and chest after chest of treasures flowed into the Qin estate like water, all becoming part of Dai Li's dowry.","In the Great Yan Dynasty, the bride and groom were not allowed to see each other for seven days before the wedding. During these seven days, Dai Li was initially unaccustomed to not having someone act as her bed warmer at night, but she got used to it after two days.","It was a rare moment of peace and quiet.","Obviously, this peace did not last long, because Lichun arrived in the blink of an eye.","The auspicious time for the wedding was around noon. The Qin estate and the Marquis's estate were both in Yuyang Commandery and not far apart. Therefore, Dai Li only woke up slightly earlier than usual today, avoiding being dragged out of bed before dawn to put on her makeup.","The Great Yan Dynasty was similar to the Qin and Han eras; important occasions emphasized solemnity and dignity, thus favoring the colors black and red.","Dai Li's wedding dress was black and red. The shoulders and sleeves were carefully outlined with gold and silver threads to create gorgeous auspicious cloud patterns. Amidst the clouds, dark golden phoenixes spread their wings, soaring through the mist and clouds, looking incredibly lifelike.","It was a long robe with wide sleeves. The waist ornaments changed from their previous casual style, using multiple jade pendants spliced together into a long set of jade hangings to weigh down the hem of the skirt.","After changing clothes, her hair had to be styled and her makeup applied.","In this era, there was no tradition of wearing a phoenix coronet for weddings; ladies mostly wore dangling hairpins. The hairpin on Dai Li's head featured gold as the base, strung with white pearls, and intertwined like osmanthus branches, made exactly to the highest specifications.","Sunlight shone in through the window, making the entire inner chamber extremely bright. The lady sitting in front of the vanity had already finished her makeup. She looked as radiant as the spring sun, her cloud-like hair thick and lustrous. Her black and red wedding dress was as passionate as fire, yet carried a solemn and majestic aura.","As she slightly lowered her head, the back of her neck was as white and smooth as congealed fat, seemingly enveloped in a hazy, soft glow. It complemented the white jade on her hairpin perfectly, making her exceptionally beautiful.","Dai Li looked at herself in the mirror and felt very unfamiliar. She frowned, and the beautiful woman in the mirror, dressed in splendid attire, also frowned. She turned her head, and the person in the mirror followed suit.","The old woman doing her hair and makeup saw Dai Li frown and felt a jolt of fear, thinking she was dissatisfied with something. \"Madam is as beautiful as a heavenly flower; you should smile more. Looking across the entire North, and even the whole world, one cannot find a lady more gorgeous and enviable than you, Madam.\"","Another old woman quickly chimed in, \"Yes, a few days ago, cart after cart of large chests flowed into your honorable estate like water. Who in the world doesn't know that the Marquis treats you as preciously as his own eyeballs?\"","A match between families of equal social status was never just an empty saying.","Even in a powerful alliance between prominent families, there would not be such a grand display as Qin Shaozong's, where he seemed to want to announce to the whole world that he was taking a wife.","Dai Li sighed, \"We'll see.\"","The old women were astonished, not understanding where her melancholy came from, but the affairs of nobles were not something they could comment on.","Dai Li had no elders present, so the tradition of bidding farewell to her parents before marriage was omitted.","She sat quietly in the room holding a round fan. The ice-cold golden handle of the fan, after being held for so long, had absorbed some warmth. Listening to the approaching sounds of commotion outside, Dai Li's state of mind—which had remained undisturbed since the wedding preparations began and throughout the past seven days—suddenly experienced a slight shift in this moment.","The sounds of the commotion were like tiny pebbles thrown into a lake, stirring up ripples that spread from near to far.","\"Mother, he's coming soon,\" Qin Yanzhou came in from outside. Today, he wore a sapphire blue robe, his ink-black hair tied high within a jade crown. His handsome features were slightly less aloof than usual.","Before today, Qin Yanzhou had referred to Qin Shaozong as the Marquis of Wu'an, calling him directly by his title. But today, he used the word \"he.\"","Dai Li acutely sensed a difference in her son's tone. She patted the seat next to her, \"Zhou Zhou, sit.\"","Only Nianxia and Bipo were in the room, so they couldn't be considered outsiders. However, Qin Yanzhou looked at Dai Li's spread-out skirt, shook his head, and simply knelt down by her feet.","Nianxia and Bipo exchanged a glance and quietly exited the room.","With only mother and son left in the room, Qin Yanzhou said awkwardly, \"Mom, I'm a bit unaccustomed to the idea of becoming a family with him in the future.\"","Dai Li guessed that her son had been hiding these words for a long time and truly couldn't hold them in any longer. She raised her hand and touched the jade crown on the young man's head. \"Qin Changgeng may not be the easiest person to get along with, but he is definitely not a petty man. Zhou Zhou, you can just treat him as an ordinary elder.\"","On the streets of Yuyang City.","Qin Shaozong rode upon the Crimson Wyrm, looking absolutely radiant. Today, he was dressed in a long robe of black and red, wearing a brand-new headdress. The Crimson Wyrm beneath him had been specially washed the day before, and every strand of its mane shimmered in the sunlight.","He rode at the very forefront. Behind him followed a host of robust cavalrymen, all equally dressed in new attire, along with a horse-drawn carriage adorned with red silk on all sides.","The corners of Qin Shaozong's lips curled upward. Riding forward into the brilliant, warm sunlight, he carried an invincible, triumphant aura, even though he had been entirely stripped of his weapons.","\"The Marquis of Wu'an looks exceptionally spirited today!\" The commoners in the crowd craned their necks to watch.","\"Ha, he is taking a wife, after all. You would be just as spirited in his shoes. By the way, I heard that later on, the Marquis's estate will be tossing out wedding favors. We absolutely cannot miss that.\"","\"What an extravagant display. Counting today, it has been eight days, hasn't it? The expenses of these eight days could probably bankrupt a minor noble family entirely. Rumor has it that Lady Dai has a soul of snow and the spirit of a flower, possessing the beauty of the Moon Goddess herself. It seems nine out of ten of those rumors are true.\"","\"You have heard about the fertilizer matter too, right? If those things truly can increase grain production by a large margin, then I would say these betrothal gifts are nothing at all. Abundant harvests and surplus grain for every household—that is a merit worthy of having temples built in her honor!\"","\"That is true.\"","...","The whispers drifted over. Qin Shaozong casually glanced over and met the man's eyes.","Their eye contact lasted but a fleeting moment, exceptionally brief, breaking away in the blink of an eye without a single bystander noticing. Qin Shaozong continued to ride forward, while the man from moments before went on talking about the fertilizer amidst the dense crowd.","Before long, the bridal procession arrived at the main gates of the Qin estate.","Dai Li had no other relatives. The main gates of the estate were surrounded by ring upon ring of commoners, but they merely watched; no one dared to block Qin Shaozong's path.","With his black and red robes fluttering in a crisp arc, the man dismounted his horse with practiced agility. He led his men straight inside, advancing completely unhindered, until—","He hit a wall right in front of her room.","A tall, elegant young man stood at the doorway, striking a pose that clearly said, \"If one man holds the pass, ten thousand cannot breach it.\"","Qin Shaozong raised an eyebrow, but before he could speak, Qin Qinian, who had accompanied him, excitedly stepped out of the ranks and quickly rushed forward.","\"Father, let me do it! Let me take him on!\"","The moment the boy's words fell, Qin Yanzhou spoke: \"Compose a poem to invite my mother out.\"","Qin Qinian immediately slammed on the brakes. He retreated just as quickly as he had advanced. \"Sorry, Father, I am no good at poetry. I cannot do this one. You will have to invite her yourself.\"","Qin Shaozong: \"...\""]},{"number":137,"title":"Chapter 137","paragraphs":["Qin Shaozong was a military general. Although he had read some books, he certainly could not compare to the civil officials who could effortlessly compose essays and poems.","Hearing the mention of composing a poem, not only Qin Qinian but also the other military officers who had accompanied Qin Shaozong to receive the bride all felt their scalps tighten.","Just a moment ago, their eyes were bright and they were full of energy, but now they all turned their heads away in unison, terrified of meeting their superior's gaze.","Qin Shaozong fell silent.","The surroundings were deathly still, and some people did not even dare to breathe loudly.","After a long time, Qin Shaozong finally said, \"Then I shall compose a short poem titled 'Inviting Madam'.\"","He had not even started and had only announced the title, but the group of military officers behind him completely abandoned their previous dead silence. They immediately clapped and cheered, filled with the relief of \"thank goodness it's not me,\" and unanimously shouted out their support for Qin Shaozong.","Among them, Qin Qinian cheered the loudest.","The young man's mouth twitched.","Qin Shaozong coughed lightly. \"Spring mountains serve as dark eyebrows on a face like jade, red beans convey affection and draw out longing. Do not hide the bright moon behind the clouds, I ask Madam to return with me.\"","It was quite rough. There were no majestic phrases or gorgeous words, but it was straightforward enough. It was so straightforward that anyone present, whether they had read books or not, could understand it.","The military officers all paused for a moment, then erupted into a burst of applause even louder than before.","\"Amazing, the Marquis is the reincarnation of the God of Literature!\"","\"With the pen he can secure the state and pacify the world, with the sword on horseback he can settle the universe. The Marquis is truly a great man!\" Wei Qing cheered.","As soon as he finished speaking, someone nudged his chest with an elbow. \"Good on you, Old Wei, aren't you quite eloquent yourself.\"","Wei Qing backhanded Mo Yanyun in return. \"Today is the Marquis's wedding, how could I steal his thunder?\"","Today there were no taboos, and some people were countless times bolder than usual, deliberately raising their voices to say, \"The Marquis has already sent his longing, when will the mistress return it?\"","As soon as this was said, the others immediately echoed:","\"Yes, when will the mistress return it?\"","\"It must be returned right now!\"","Amidst the chaotic noise, the room door creaked open. The clamor abruptly stopped, and everyone looked over in unison.","A tall and graceful figure came into view. She was dressed in a trailing long skirt of black and red, wearing a magnificent dangling hairpin on her head. With the phoenix hairpin slightly swaying and her delicate steps gracefully moving, the young woman slowly walked out of the room, holding a circular fan to cover her face.","Reflected in the sunlight, the young woman's fair fingers holding the fan and the gold and jade on her head seemed to emit a faint glow together. The golden phoenix on her shoulder also seemed to come alive. Even without seeing her face, there was an indescribable, resplendent beauty about her.","Silence spread.","\"Why are you still blocking the way?\" Qin Yanzhou frowned.","The crowd awakened as if from a dream and scattered like birds and beasts, making way for a path.","Covering the face with a circular fan provided a much wider field of vision than a red veil. Although she could not see too much ahead, walking steadily was not a problem.","Surrounded by the crowd, Dai Li walked out of the Qin residence and, under the eager gazes of the surrounding commoners craning their necks, sat inside the brand-new, festive carriage.","\"Hey, I saw the side profile of the Marquis's wife. She looks just like an immortal from a painting, so incredibly beautiful.\"","\"Coming from a humble background, marrying for the second time with a son, marrying up into the Marquis's estate, and even becoming the primary wife... I wouldn't even dare to dream this big.\"","\"Take a few more looks and remember it. Go back and dream about this tonight.\"","...","In the Book of Rites, the Meaning of Marriage, it is said: \"When she descends and goes out, she mounts the bride's carriage, and the groom hands her the strap, driving the carriage for three revolutions.\"","This meant that after the bride was received outside, the groom had to personally drive the carriage for her, making the wheels turn three times. This symbolized the completion of the odd and even numbers of yin and yang, ensuring future marital harmony and a stable marriage.","After helping Dai Li into the carriage, Qin Shaozong sat in the driver's seat at the front and gently tapped the horse ahead with his whip.","The wheels rolled slowly and stopped after three revolutions.","The wedding ceremony was also called the \"dusk ceremony,\" as it had to be held right at dusk. Therefore, after Qin Shaozong received his bride, he did not rush back to the Marquis's estate but instead led the procession on a detour around the city.","However long they walked, the spectating commoners followed, trailing along to watch the excitement.","The long procession wandered through the city, and wherever they passed, sounds of congratulations were endless. Qin Shaozong rode his horse at the front, occasionally turning his head to look back at the carriage behind him. Whether it was because the sunlight was too intense or something else, the depths of his eyes seemed to be paved with a layer of crushed diamonds, shining much brighter than usual.","When the golden sun gradually slanted westward, just about to sink below the horizon, the convoy returned to the Marquis's estate.","The main gates of the residence were wide open, and the carriage stopped in front of them.","\"Mistress, please disembark.\"","Dai Li picked up the circular fan from the side again. Out of the corner of her eye, she saw that the carriage door had been opened, and a footstool was placed below. She stood up and slowly stepped out of the carriage using the footstool.","The guests were all in their seats; one group sat in the main hall, and another in the front courtyard. Long tables laden with delicious delicacies were lined up neatly row by row, packed so tightly that for the first time, the spacious Marquis's estate felt crowded.","The moment Dai Li stepped into the front courtyard, she felt countless gazes fall upon her. Appraising, amazed, curious, scrutinizing...","\"A match made in heaven, surely a blissful union,\" someone said first, though it was unclear who.","With someone starting it, a wave of blessings swept through.","\"Created by heaven and set by earth, truly a perfect match.\"","Amidst the chorus of congratulations, Dai Li did not stop her steps. Continuing to hold her fan, she walked forward into the main hall together with Qin Shaozong. The hall had clearly been redecorated and was equally festive.","Qin Shaozong's parents had passed away, so the step of kneeling to the parents and listening to their instructions was omitted. After the mutual bowing ceremony was completed, the bride entered the inner chambers while Qin Shaozong temporarily remained outside to entertain the guests.","The Marquis's estate covered a much larger area than the Qin residence. As Dai Li walked along, she saw pavilions and halls situated one after another in the distance, with winding corridors and high-peaked eaves. After entering the main courtyard, there was even a rockery and a fish pond, looking just like a miniature backyard garden placed within.","\"Madam, the Marquis will not return this quickly. Please eat something to pad your stomach first.\" Nianxia brought over some pastries.","Dai Li was indeed a little hungry, but right after finishing a small piece of pastry, she heard Bipo, who was waiting outside, say, \"The Marquis has arrived.\"","\"This fast?\" Nianxia asked in astonishment.","Dai Li unhurriedly took a few sips of tea and wiped her mouth clean with a brocade handkerchief before raising her circular fan once again.","Qin Shaozong turned into the inner room. A pair of red candles burned quietly in the room, which contained many exquisite ornaments.","A sandalwood incense table stood to the side, upon which rested a black-lacquered, gold-painted makeup box. Not far away was a three-fold carved screen depicting flying birds, and the gauze curtains hanging over the bed swayed gently in the breeze, half-revealing their cloud patterns.","But at this moment, Qin Shaozong could not see any of that at all. He stared unblinkingly at the young woman on the bed. The woman held a fan to cover her face, her skirts spreading out to the sides like a blazing red lotus.","She was in his bedroom, and after today, they would be husband and wife.","From now on, they would share the same bed in life and the same tomb in death.","\"Marquis, please compose a poem to ask the bride to remove her fan,\" the master of ceremonies who had come with Qin Shaozong said with a smile.","Qin Shaozong stiffened for a moment.","Dai Li blocked her face with the fan and could not see, but after hearing the master of ceremonies' words, there was a long, enduring silence in the room.","The fan-removing ceremony; the word for \"remove\" here also meant \"to take away.\"","The groom needed to compose a poem to move the bride, and only then would she \"remove the fan.\" Everyone knew this procedure, and generally speaking, the groom would prepare a poem in advance.","But if this poem had been used ahead of time due to some accident...","Behind the circular fan, Dai Li secretly curled her lips.","Don't tell me Qin Changgeng has been thinking all afternoon and still hasn't come up with one.","Seeing the atmosphere suddenly freeze, the master of ceremonies was greatly alarmed. He could not help but look at Qin Shaozong, only to see his jawline pulled taut as a bowstring, as if he were facing a formidable enemy.","\"Did Your Grace perhaps spend too much breath entertaining the guests outside just now? Why not have a cup of tea first to soothe your throat?\" The master of ceremonies hurriedly asked a maid to serve tea.","Qin Shaozong brought a fist to his lips and coughed softly. \"That works.\"","The smile on Dai Li's lips deepened.","After finishing the tea, Qin Shaozong spoke, \"It is still 'Inviting the Madam'. Snowy skin, silken hair, and a golden swaying hairpin; a round fan hides half your painted face. My beloved, from now on you are my wife, there is no need to shyly conceal your jade-like visage.\"","Dai Li could not help but chuckle.","This was even more careless and straightforward than the first poem.","However, she could tell that as a military general, he had truly tried his best. If he were asked to compose another one, he probably would not be able to come up with anything even if he thought until tomorrow morning...","The round fan blocking her front was slowly moved away.","At this moment, it was as if a vibrant painting had been unrolled. Under the lamplight, the red mole between the woman's brows was bright and beautiful, her cloud-like hair thick and lustrous. As her red lips curved into a slight smile, it was like a peony blooming to its absolute peak on a high terrace swaying gently, bringing forth a dizzying, mature, and gorgeous allure.","Qin Shaozong's Adam's apple bobbed.","With the fan-removal ceremony complete, the hand-washing ceremony followed. Simply put, it was cleansing the hands, symbolizing the start of a new life with a pure heart.","Dai Li rose from the couch and went to wash her hands together with Qin Shaozong. After they wiped away the water droplets on their hands, Nianxia stepped forward carrying a tray of beef.","The meat-sharing ceremony, to share joys and sorrows.","Dai Li picked up the jade chopsticks and took a small, thinly sliced piece of beef.","Qin Shaozong also picked up his chopsticks, but unlike Dai Li, who was careful while eating the meat to avoid ruining her lip rouge, he kept his eyes on her from beginning to end. His brown eyes, illuminated by the firelight, were completely filled with her reflection.","That gaze was too scorching, as if kerosene had been poured over her body and then completely melted into her blood and bones, making it impossible to ignore.","Dai Li's eyelashes trembled slightly, and she did not raise her eyes to look at him.","After they put down their jade chopsticks, Bipo brought over a silver tray, upon which lay a bitter gourd that had been split into two halves.","Drinking from the nuptial cups, from now on, husband and wife are one.","Clear wine flowed into the gourd halves. Standing facing each other, the two raised their cups and drank at the same time. He and she stood very close; when they raised their hands, the ends of their wide sleeves fluttered and gently brushed against each other.","The gourds were emptied, and the millet wine slid down their throats.","The nuptial cup ceremony was complete.","Dai Li set down her half of the gourd. The hard bottom of the gourd struck the silver tray with a soft clack, sounding like the settling of dust.","That passionate, brazenly greedy gaze from before looked over once again. Dai Li sighed inwardly and finally met his eyes. \"May I share one heart and one mind with you, my lord, and may we treat each other with mutual respect.\"","Qin Shaozong's long eyebrows furrowed imperceptibly.","He was somewhat satisfied, yet somewhat displeased.","But that slight hint of displeasure was quickly dispelled by the two locks of long hair presented to them. These locks of hair were naturally not cut right then, otherwise Dai Li's intricate hairstyle would definitely be ruined.","The hair had been taken yesterday, to be used for the hair-tying ceremony today.","Qin Shaozong waved the others away and personally picked up the two locks of long hair to tie them together. His movements were skilled, and he actually tied them neatly.","Dai Li's brow arched slightly. Recalling the time he had accidentally pulled out her hair before, she suspected he had practiced in private more than just once.","With the hair tied, the wedding ceremonies were thus concluded, and what followed was the consummation in the bridal chamber.","However, since Qin Shaozong's parents had already passed away, the situation was special. The guests outside required him to personally go out and entertain them. \"Madam, will you go with me?\"","Dai Li thought for a moment and nodded in agreement.","Entertaining guests inevitably involved drinking. Not only did Qin Shaozong have to drink, but a few of the younger generation could not escape it either. She did not know how Zhou Zhou's alcohol tolerance was, so she had to go and see.","The two walked out hand in hand.","Earlier, Dai Li had walked all the way with the round fan covering her face. Many guests had only seen her side profile and not her full face, but now they all saw it.","Glorious as the autumn chrysanthemum, lush as the spring pine.","Her eyes and brows were exceptionally beautiful. The slightly upturned outer corners of her eyes looked as if they had been painted with fine brushwork. She was distinctly alluring, yet due to her aura, she appeared incredibly dignified, without the slightest hint of vulgarity.","Dai Li followed Qin Shaozong to entertain the guests, occasionally glancing at Qin Yanzhou. Seeing that he had not drunk too much wine, she finally felt relieved.","The wedding was held at dusk. By the time the guests enjoyed themselves to the fullest and returned home, the sky had long since darkened.","There was only one last item left for today's wedding."]},{"number":138,"title":"Chapter 138","paragraphs":["All the guests had left, and the massive estate instantly fell quiet. The servants deftly cleared away the leftovers, striving to quickly restore the front courtyard and main hall to their usual tidiness.","A bright moon hung high in the sky, its lustrous light spilling over the upturned eaves and neatly paved blue bricks, as if draping them in a layer of soft white gauze.","Dai Li had come out with Qin Shaozong tonight to entertain the guests, originally just wanting to keep an eye on her son so he wouldn't get drunk.","Although distilled liquor had not yet appeared in this era, and the alcohol content of brewed wine was limited, drinking too much would still leave one intoxicated.","In the end, while chatting and laughing with the guests, she had unknowingly drunk quite a bit herself. The tipsiness was like a mischievous kitten, diving headfirst into her thoughts and tangling the threads of her mind into a messy ball of yarn.","When Qin Shaozong returned from seeing off the last batch of guests, he saw Dai Li sitting in a chair in a daze. \"Is my wife drunk?\"","\"I'm not drunk,\" Dai Li flatly denied.","Seeing her misty, rippling eyes and the bright pink flush on her cheeks, Qin Shaozong thought she looked very much like some exceptionally soft and white steamed pastry, making one's appetite stir.","Staring at her intently for a couple of breaths, Qin Shaozong ultimately couldn't resist reaching out to pinch Dai Li's cheek.","It was indeed incredibly soft.","With just a little pressure, his fingertips sank into the smooth, white flesh. It felt even better than he had imagined.","Smack—","Qin Shaozong's hand was swatted.","The sound was crisp and loud. Whether it was Qin Qinian and Qin Yunce not far away, or the surrounding servants of the Marquis's mansion who were cleaning up, everyone heard it clearly.","Someone visibly shrank their neck back.","Qin Shaozong nonchalantly withdrew his hand.","\"Where is Zhouzhou?\" Dai Li looked around.","Qin Shaozong swept his gaze around and indeed did not see Qin Yanzhou. \"Where is Qin the Second?\"","Qin Yunce, standing to the side, said at this moment, \"He seems to have gone to the side corridor with Rongrong?\"","\"Oh, it should be about going out to play in a few days,\" Qin Qinian burped from the alcohol.","\"Yunce, go and call Qin the Second back,\" Qin Shaozong ordered.","Qin Yunce went as ordered.","Shortly after, he returned with Qin Yanzhou, followed by Shi Rongyue, whose hair bobbed up and down on her head.","The young man had inherited his mother's fair skin and was similarly prone to blushing when drinking. At this moment, his cheeks were flushed red, and his brow had lost its usual coldness, appearing exceptionally lazy and casual under the influence of alcohol. Coupled with his brightly colored, wide-sleeved robe, he looked like a romantic noble young master who had never experienced hardship.","Qin Shaozong was concise: \"Greet us.\"","Qin Yanzhou stood in front of the two. It was unknown whether the alcohol had clouded his thoughts and he didn't understand the words, or if he was simply unwilling, but regardless, he did not move.","Seeing this, Qin Yunce hurriedly stepped forward and bowed with cupped hands to the two seated above, \"Congratulations to Uncle and Aunt on your newlywed.\"","Qin Shaozong gave an \"Mm,\" and his gaze shifted back to Qin Yanzhou. \"Qin the Second.\"","Qin Yanzhou's eyes shifted, and finally, just like Qin Yunce a moment ago, he slowly cupped his hands and said, \"Congratulations to Father and Mother on your newlywed.\"","Qin Shaozong smiled in satisfaction.","Not wanting to fall behind, Qin Qinian also came over to pay his respects. Shi Rongyue lined up behind him.","After the younger generation had all paid their respects, Qin Shaozong stood up from his seat, conveniently scooping up Dai Li next to him. \"Madam, let's return to our room to rest.\"","Qin Qinian watched the two figures leaving together, then looked at the young man beside him, suddenly realizing, \"Qin Yanzhou, so Father waited here for so long just for you to call him that!\"","As soon as the words fell, the youth's forehead was flicked.","Qin Yunce calmly withdrew his hand. \"Don't be unruly. From now on, you must call Chongle your second brother.\"","Qin Qinian clutched his head and muttered, \"I've been calling him that for half a year, how can I just change it like that... Hey, hey, eldest brother, stop hitting me, I didn't say I wouldn't change it.\"","*","Before walking out of the long corridor and completely leaving the sight of the younger generation, Dai Li walked slowly, her steps unsteady, holding onto Qin Shaozong's hand.","The moment they turned out of the corridor, Qin Shaozong wrapped one arm around Dai Li's waist and swept the other under her knees, lifting her completely off the ground.","Carrying her, Qin Shaozong strode back to the main courtyard.","Dai Li had drunk quite a bit of wine, and now that she had left the main hall and was blown by the wind, her head felt dizzy. \"Qin Changgeng, put me down, I'll walk by myself.\"","\"You called me the wrong thing,\" he said only these words.","Dai Li sluggishly asked, \"Called what wrong?\"","He got straight to the point, \"You should call me Husband.\"","Dai Li: \"...\"","Seeing her play deaf and dumb, a dark fire flared in the depths of Qin Shaozong's eyes. \"I'll deal with you when we get back.\"","Dai Li was too familiar with this look of his. Every time he revealed such a gaze, a wild and passionate session was inevitable, and he wouldn't stop until he was fully satisfied.","Dai Li narrowed her eyes, deep in thought.","...","Inside the master bedroom.","The pair of festive red candles had long burned out and had been replaced with a new pair by Nianxia right on time. The incense burner in the corner silently gave off a faint fragrance, and the lamplight cast a long shadow from the carved folding screen.","At some point, a dark silhouette approached from the outside, merging with the shadow of the screen, as if forming a greedy Taotie beast.","\"Not back here,\" Dai Li suddenly said.","\"My wife has dined with me and performed the wedding cup ritual, having already married me as my wife. If not back here, where else do you want to go?\" Qin Shaozong chuckled, setting her down by the bed, and then beckoned Bipo over to help remove her head ornaments.","Dai Li, however, answered irrelevantly, raising her hand to point not far away. \"There needs to be a soft chair over there.\"","Qin Shaozong followed her gaze and glanced over, then turned back to look at her, knowing she was referring to the chair that used to be in the inner room of the master bedroom at the Qin residence. \"Tomorrow I'll have someone add a long chair.\"","Dai Li: \"I want to drink water.\"","Bipo was just about to call Nianxia, but saw that Qin Shaozong had already stood up and personally went to the outer room. When he returned, he heard Dai Li say that the spring chill was biting, and she needed a hot water bottle stuffed into the blankets.","After tossing and turning back and forth several times, just as Dai Li wanted to speak again, Qin Shaozong sat beside her, pulled a small object out of his sleeve pocket, and slipped it directly around Dai Li's neck. \"Stop making a fuss, and you're not allowed to take it off.\"","Dai Li looked down nonchalantly.","Previously, Qin Changgeng had also given her many things, mostly jewelry given by his own hands: bracelets, necklaces, rings, and various earrings. He would give them to her that night, and the next day the jewelry would be left in her dressing case; this kind of thing was very common.","However, at the first glance when she looked down, Dai Li almost thought her eyes were playing tricks on her.","It was a piece of suet white jade strung on a black cord. It was as solid as white fat and incredibly delicate. The entire piece was carved into the shape of a tiger, with its mouth slightly open, its front and hind legs drawn together, front low and back high, with a slightly curled long tail.","On the tiger's body, there were slightly sunken patterns colored with either black ink or some other special pigment. These patterns formed individual characters, covering the tiger's back like a garment.","She had seen something of the exact same shape in a museum before, and the plaque hanging next to it at the time was called a \"Tiger Tally.\"","However, Tiger Tallies were made of bronze and could be split and joined using an internal mortise and tenon structure. The piece of jade currently hanging around Dai Li's neck was a single, solid piece and could not be taken apart.","\"It wouldn't be very good if others saw this,\" Dai Li flicked the white jade with her finger.","\"What does the business between you and me have to do with anyone else?\" He was unconcerned.","The last hairpin was removed, Dai Li's hair bun and jeweled pins were all taken out, and the heat of the gaze that had been fixed on her all along rose to another level.","\"All of you, step down,\" his voice was hoarse.","The two servants obeyed the order and withdrew.","“Creak.” The door outside closed.","The massive shadow drew near, first climbing onto the footstool, then ascending the bed to envelop her. The scorching breath cascaded downwards, licking at her straight, long eyelashes like a snake's tongue.","Not only his breath, but his initial kiss also truly landed on her eyelids. He first kissed her eyes, deliberately making her long eyelashes wet.","Stimulated, Dai Li's eyes trembled, and a few meaningless physiological tears were forced out from the corners of her eyes, only to be swallowed by him as well.","Only when the spark-like burning sensation moved away from her eyes did Dai Li open them. The close-range eye contact allowed her to clearly see the turbulent waves surging in those brown eyes.","The surging waves seemed to transform into a terrifying whirlpool capable of sweeping up and swallowing a person whole. Before she could look further, he leaned over, pinning her to the bed like a hungry tiger pouncing on its prey.","He bit her red lips, his slightly pointed canine teeth sinking into the soft flesh, bringing Dai Li a slight, itchy pain akin to an electric shock.","In an instant, he released her and drove straight in.","Dai Li slightly tilted her head back, always feeling that every part of her was forcefully patronized by him. He nibbled and bit, making loud smacking sounds. A strand of silver thread, sparkling in the candlelight, fell from the corners of their mouths. It was extremely vivid at this moment, yet failed to attract anyone's attention.","The belt loosened, the collar opened a sliver, and that dark color with thick calluses took the opportunity to enter, first patrolling in circles, then wreaking havoc.","Dai Li's breath grew heavier, like duckweed tossing in the wind and rain at sea. With her back pressed against the brocade quilt and her field of vision mostly occupied, she closed her eyes for a moment, then opened them again.","As Qin Shaozong gradually shifted his position, Dai Li hooked her arms around his neck, taking the initiative to lean forward and kiss his thin lips. \"Husband, could you promise to let me take the lead tonight?\"","That voice was as sweet as honey, as if it had turned into invisible long threads, wrapping around his heart circle by circle.","Just as the first two words fell, the breath above seemed to stagnate for a moment.","By the time he heard the rest, Dai Li clearly saw the dark fire in his eyes burning ever more vigorously, like a pot of boiling water, ready to steam and eat her at any moment.","Dai Li tried to reach out and push him.","The man full of muscles was pushed away by a force that wasn't considered heavy.","A gleam of light flashed past the bottom of Dai Li's eyes. As soon as he retreated, she sat up. Seeing that Qin Shaozong was still sitting, she raised her hand to push him down.","He raised his long eyebrows, not resisting, and fell down following her force. Dai Li smiled at him, leaned over to kiss him again as a reward, and conveniently sat on his lower abdomen.","Almost at the same time, his long arm reached over to clamp around her waist. The apricot-colored silk inner garment was very light and thin, clinging to the woman's waistline, faintly revealing a bit of flesh color in the candlelight.","He clamped onto her, secretly rolling her and shifting backward.","Dai Li just pretended not to know. She took the belt that Qin Shaozong had previously torn off, first grabbed his left hand, and tied the belt around his wrist.","\"What is the meaning of this, Madam?\" he asked.","Dai Li didn't look at him, busy with her own affairs. \"Based on the Lord's poor credit on the bed, I have no choice but to resort to this bad plan.\"","The beds of this era all had bedframes. Dai Li passed the other end of the belt through the hollowed-out carved bedframe, and then tied two knots.","After tying his left hand, Dai Li went to get Qin Shaozong's belt, and then took down his right hand that was circling her waist.","When she tugged the first time, she couldn't move it. Dai Li looked down at him from a commanding height, but her tone was extremely gentle. \"Is Husband going to break his promise?\"","Qin Shaozong's Adam's apple rolled up and down. \"Madam, leave me one hand...\"","Dai Li didn't say yes or no, continuing to pry his right hand. This time she moved it, and she used his own belt to tie him to the bedframe.","When both of his hands were fully tied, Dai Li curled her lips in satisfaction. \"I am the Northern Inspector specially appointed by the current Emperor, bearing the duty of supervising local officials. After my undercover investigation, I found that the Marquis of Wu'an in the North bullies men and oppresses women, committing many evil deeds. Now his official position is temporarily dismissed, and his right to ask 'Who in the hall is suing this official' is stripped.\"","This phrase \"Who in the hall is suing this official\" was said by Qin Shaozong on the night of the winter hunt, and now Dai Li brought it out exactly as it was.","Qin Shaozong revealed a bit of sharp canine teeth. \"Oh? Then what does Inspector Dai want? How about punishing me to be a little jailer, working hard every day to administer the whip.\"","He was quite obedient in his words, but his hipbone pointed upward, approaching boldly and presumptuously.","Both of their belts were removed, Dai Li's inner garment was open, and the peony bellyband inside had been pulled loosely by Qin Shaozong earlier, the thin strap wrapping around her fair neck, on the verge of falling off.","Dai Li raised her hand to hook the thin strap, and under the man's burning gaze, pulled the bellyband down another section.","The length of the rope for the tiger-shaped mutton-fat jade had not yet been adjusted. The tiger jade dragged the overly long black rope, hanging heavily and stopping on the undulating fullness.","Dai Li picked up the black rope, and under the gaze of those brown eyes that seemed about to burn out sparks, she leisurely hid the tiger jade into the snow-white depths. \"This is a treasure given to me by my husband. How could I let a nameless pawn like you see it?\"","The muscles at his waist and abdomen instantly tightened severely, urging, \"Madam, hurry up...\"","The more he urged, the less Dai Li hurried.","She slowly shifted backward, only softly pressing against him. \"I am an official appointed by the imperial court. Who is your madam? Don't shout nonsense.\"","Veins popped on Qin Shaozong's forehead. \"Then I ask Inspector Dai not to delay, hurry up and interrogate me.\"","Dai Li smiled. Her beautiful face was extremely bright under the candlelight, carrying an indescribable charm, as if there were several invisible fox tails wagging behind her.","Her slender fingers stroked the man's neck, teasing that dark Adam's apple to roll up and down incessantly. \"Since you took the initiative to mention the word 'interrogate', then tell me yourself, what other crimes have you committed besides bullying men and oppressing women? Speak well, and this official has a reward.\"","Her fingers moved down, as if curious about every part. Whenever she touched something she found interesting, she would stop and study it seriously.","That fire burned so much that the veins on the side of Qin Shaozong's neck stood up, and the bottoms of his eyes turned red. \"Madam!\"","Dai Li glanced at him, not speaking.","She did what she had to do, continuing to set her fires.","He took a deep breath. \"I intend to commit insubordination.\"","This sentence had more than one meaning if listened to closely, but leaving those aside, Dai Li sitting on him right now was indeed \"above.\"","He really wanted to \"commit insubordination.\"","\"Mhm, what else?\"","Dai Li removed the barriers between them one by one, observed the position, and then carefully sat down.","His pupils contracted for a moment.","\"Hey, why are you sweating? Although you are now a prisoner, I am a reasonable and good official. I will find a handkerchief for you.\" With that, Dai Li propped herself up a little with her knees, slowly getting up.","Not only did she get up, but she also specifically went to get the handkerchief placed by the pillow.","Seeming unable to reach it, Dai Li leaned over.","The two flaps of the inner garment opened wider with her movements. The mutton-fat jade-like skin glowed white and moist. A bundle of long hair split into several strands, like the open claws and teeth of some beast, spreading open to cover that secret place.","A rich fragrance lingered around the tip of the nose. Qin Shaozong only felt that the white was white, the fragrant was fragrant, like a piece of fragrant meat dangling in front of him.","His canines itched, his mouth watered; he could see her but could not touch her. The man instinctively tried to raise his hand. The sashes binding his wrists stretched to their absolute limit, letting out a sharp snapping sound.","Dai Li was startled. She carefully inspected the two sashes and only relaxed when she saw they were perfectly intact.","Not bad at all; the fabric used for wedding garments was indeed sturdy.","Taking a handkerchief, Dai Li casually wiped the sweat from his brow, then sat back down. Speak. That is not your only crime.","Seeing him remain silent, merely staring at her with predatory, wolfish eyes, Dai Li lightly scratched his chest. Little soldier of the Qin clan, have you ever forcefully taken another man's wife?","It was as if the downy feathers of a baby bird had brushed against him. An agonizing itch exploded from his heart. Qin Shaozong's throat was as dry as a scorching fire. ...I have.","Dai Li looked down at him from her vantage point. Do you plead guilty?","I do not. He answered without a moment's hesitation.","Dai Li gave a soft snort.","After that, she moved entirely at her own pace, taking her time, drawing it out like a slow-flowing stream. When she was tired, she rested for a bit; when she felt like it, she rested even longer. Whether he exhausted every sweet word or spouted shameless obscenities, she ignored him completely.","She was so comfortable that the corners of her eyes curled up in a tiny, pleased arc, but it tormented Qin Shaozong as if he were burning in roaring flames.","It was not just missing the edge by a little, but by a massive margin, leaving him scratching his heart and clawing his lungs in frustration, his eyes red-hot with desire.","That inferno rolled and roared through his limbs and bones. Before it could be extinguished even a fraction, a large bucket of oil was poured over it, making the flames surge even more violently.","A faint tearing sound echoed.","Dai Li paused, looking suspiciously at the sashes binding Qin Shaozong's arms.","The quality of these sashes was truly excellent, and the knots she had tied were no ordinary knots. Logically speaking, it should be impossible for Qin Changgeng to break free. And looking at it now, his hands indeed showed no signs of escaping.","Dai Li resumed her enjoyment.","Qin Shaozong gnashed his teeth. Madam, if you untie me within half a quarter of an hour, we can end things early tonight. Otherwise...","Dai Li chuckled. Just a moment ago you said within a quarter of an hour, and in the blink of an eye you have actually cut the time in half. Not only are you not treating me with honesty, but you actually dare to threaten me. That is an added crime!","Madam, be careful not to play with fire and get burned. The last few words seemed to be squeezed out from between his teeth.","You talk too much for a little soldier. I should gag your mouth. Dai Li paid his warning no mind. She even grabbed her own silk bellyband, casually crumpled it into a ball, and stuffed it into his mouth.","Qin Shaozong not only did not resist, but he actively bit down on it. His slightly pointed canines dampened the peony-embroidered silk with a trace of moisture.","Dai Li was just about to feel satisfied when she suddenly heard a loud crack.","It was a massive bang, completely incomparable to the sound from earlier. She stared dumbfounded as the openwork carved edge of the bed frame, where the sashes were originally tied, suffered a complete decapitation, it had actually been ripped off entirely by Qin Shaozong.","When Dai Li was grabbed by the waist and flipped from the top to the bottom, her mind buzzed. Her first reaction was that she was doomed. Her second reaction was...","The bed was broken on their wedding night. If word of this got out, she would never be able to show her face in public again."]},{"number":139,"title":"Chapter 139","paragraphs":["\"What was that sound? Nianxia, did you just hear a loud crash?\" Bipo turned her head to look at Nianxia.","She didn't need an answer; just by looking at Nianxia's expression, Bipo knew that the sound wasn't her imagination.","On a wedding night, a sudden loud crash coming from the bedchamber was highly unusual no matter how you thought about it.","Could something have happened?","\"I should go ask.\" Nianxia felt uneasy. She took small steps forward until she reached the front of the main chamber. \"My Lord, Madam, do you require your servant's assistance?\"","\"Step back,\" a hoarse male voice commanded from inside the room.","Nianxia lowered her head and was just about to retreat when she suddenly heard another loud bang from inside.","The sound was exceptionally loud, like some heavy wooden frame smashing onto the floor. It could be heard clearly even through the doors, making Nianxia shudder in fright.","Bipo tugged at Nianxia, signaling her to leave first.","Once they had walked a distance away, Bipo finally said, \"The Lord has spoken. No matter what, we must not disturb them tonight.\"","Nianxia's face was full of worry. \"But two such loud noises in a row sound terribly frightening. Could the Lord and Madam... have gotten into a fight?\"","\"Impossible!\" Bipo immediately denied it. \"We have followed Madam for nearly a year, and we have both seen everything that has happened during this time. If Madam wanted the stars in the sky, the Lord would probably pluck them down for her. They finally married and became husband and wife, and tonight is their wedding night. The Lord is too overjoyed to even think about fighting her!\"","The worry on Nianxia's face turned into confusion. \"Then what was that just now? It can't be that the Lord and Madam got so carried away that they knocked over the ornaments in the room.\"","Bipo blinked. \"That's not impossible.\"","Nianxia coughed lightly. \"We might find out the details when the Lord calls for water.\"","The two girls gradually blushed as they looked at each other.","Inside the main courtyard's bedchamber.","As Dai Li was pinned by the waist and lying on the bed, she still couldn't help but turn her head to stare at the carved wooden bed rail on the floor.","That pitiful carved bed rail had first been yanked down, then deemed a nuisance by its master, and finally took a kick, being unhesitatingly booted to the floor.","\"It's over, it's over...\" Dai Li's mind was buzzing.","Her chin was caught by long, rough fingers and turned back around. This time, it was Qin Shaozong's turn to look down at her from above. From his angle, he could see the white waves parting, slowly revealing the tiger-shaped jade carving originally hidden deep within the peaks.","The belt had been removed, and the two lapels of her inner garment were opened wider. The edge of the clothes, embroidered with auspicious clouds, pressed perfectly against her vivid beauty, half-hidden and half-exposed.","The man stared unblinkingly, the fiery lust in his eyes almost overflowing, but his tone was quite serious. \"Inspector Dai despises the court's rules, abuses illegal punishments, and acts recklessly as an envoy. According to our dynasty's new laws, those who trample on propriety and law shall receive five hundred lashes.\"","Dai Li's heart and eyes were entirely focused on the broken bed rail; she had no mind to listen to his nonsense. She immediately kicked her legs. \"Qin Changgeng, get up first.\"","But he swiftly raised his right hand, firmly gripping that fair, long leg, and said to himself, \"The guilty official, Dai, shows no repentance. She shall first be punished with one strike.\"","A strike originally meant beating with a wooden board. But as Qin Shaozong's words fell, he simply raised his hand and gave a light smack.","White waves fluttered, and the half-covered inner garment slipped down completely, unable to conceal the trembling crimson, a sight of breathtaking beauty.","Dai Li, eyes wide open: \"...\"","\"Confess truthfully at once, who taught you to abuse illegal punishments?\" he scolded.","Seeing her just looking at him, Qin Shaozong raised his hand and picked out the tiger jade carving tied with a black string, a wicked smile on his face. \"A nobody like me loves to take away what others love most. Since you cherish this gift from your husband so much, I insist on snatching it away.\"","Dai Li: \"...\"","With that said, he reached out with three fingers to grab, but he didn't grab the tiger-shaped mutton-fat jade; instead, he took hold of something else.","Dai Li had known he wanted to act wickedly and intended to guard against him. She hurriedly raised her hand to cover herself, but she was a step too late, only managing to cover the back of his hand.","The curve of Qin Shaozong's lips deepened. His palms were full of thick calluses, and at this moment, he rubbed and squeezed with the pads of his fingers, thoroughly enjoying himself. \"Inspector Dai, still won't confess?\"","Dai Li's entire body trembled uncontrollably. She let out a soft moan, her cheeks flushing red, her peach-blossom eyes shimmering with tears, as if the moisture would fall with just a blink.","Her hand suddenly tightened in response, her fingernails scratching a few red marks on the back of his dark hand.","Qin Shaozong feigned dissatisfaction. \"I still can't get it out. Inspector Dai truly keeps her treasures tightly hidden. Very well, I shall just find another path.\"","He lowered his head.","Dai Li opened her mouth and gasped. Her thoughts were forced to drift away from the damaged bed rail and focus entirely on the present. \"You unruly nobody indeed harbor treacherous intentions. I will definitely bring you to justice today.\"","His voice was muffled, as if he was eating something. \"How dare you, Inspector Dai, turn the tables on me. Hiss, so you are a snake spirit in disguise, otherwise how could you entangle a person so tightly...\"","The bright moon in the sky was covered by dark clouds, only to be slowly blown open by a belated wind. Nianxia and Bipo waited outside for an unknown amount of time before they finally heard the call for water from inside.","Both sides of the main chamber were connected to side rooms. Usually, one was used for bathing, and the other was for servants to rest so they could come to serve at any time.","But Dai Li didn't like having no private space, so at her request, Nianxia and Bipo lived in the side chambers further away, and they would be called from outside if needed.","However, that was before. Tonight was the grand wedding, naturally incomparable to ordinary times, so Nianxia and Bipo were on standby at all times.","When they heard the call for water, they hurried inside to prepare.","Two buckets of boiling water had already been prepared in the side room earlier. After being boiled, no cold water was added; they were simply covered with wooden lids.","Although quite some time had passed, given the large volume of water and the good insulation measures, the water was still very hot and difficult to use without adding cold water.","The two girls efficiently mixed in cold water to make it warm. Just as they were about to enter the inner chamber to do a simple tidying up as usual, they heard the male master say in a deep voice, \"There is no need to enter the inner chamber.\"","Nianxia subconsciously looked toward the voice and saw the burly man standing at the connection between the inner and outer chambers, almost blocking most of the archway with his robust body.","At this moment, he merely draped a long robe over himself. The belt was tied very casually and loosely, revealing a large expanse of his firm chest. On his dark skin, there were a few faint scratch marks.","Even though his attire was informal, the majesty accumulated over the years was not diminished in the slightest. He possessed a powerful aura that high-spirited, impetuous young men could never match.","Nianxia didn't dare to look further and hurriedly lowered her head to comply.","Lying on the bed, Dai Li listened to Bipo and Nianxia enter and then leave. Panting softly, her attention drifted back to the broken carved bed rail on the floor.","Bipo and Nianxia hadn't entered the inner chamber this time, but what about next time? They couldn't be kept out forever, could they?","Beds of this era were mostly assembled using mortise and tenon joints. Now that the carved wooden rail of the bed edge was broken, repairing it would require completely dismantling the entire bed to replace that specific part.","Completely dismantling it meant the process would inevitably involve a lot of clinking and clanking. The noise would not be small, and as word spread from one to ten, and ten to a hundred, wouldn't the whole estate know about it very soon?","Dai Li shuddered, her face burning fiercely.","Qin Shaozong returned at some unknown point. He reached out and scooped up the soft and limp Dai Li from the couch, carrying her to the side room. Seeing her distracted and flushed, he took the initiative to interpret it with a hundred percent subjectivity, \"Is my wife still unsatisfied? Just in time, so am I. Why don't we have another round where we each lead an army and engage in a naval battle on the Huai River to see who is the victor?\"","Dai Li: \"... You've had enough.\"","But clearly, Qin Shaozong had not had enough. After the door to a new world was opened, he was extremely excited and successively gave Dai Li several different identities.","From a postal inspector to a commander, and then from a ruthless female spy to an innocent and romantic princess, he changed them one by one.","By the time Dai Li finally reverted to being herself, she let out a sigh of satisfaction and exhaustion, closed her eyes, and fell asleep.","...","As the saying goes, \"the spring chill can freeze the young,\" and the early spring mornings were indeed very cold. But the cold had its benefits, such as being perfect for sleeping.","Both of Qin Shaozong's parents had passed away, leaving no elders in the family. Therefore, Dai Li didn't have to get up early on the second day of her marriage to pay respects to her parents-in-law with her husband, like ordinary new brides.","With no one to rush her, she slept until she naturally woke up, completely free of any psychological burden.","Except...","Dai Li sat on the couch hugging the quilt, her scalp tingling as she looked at the carved wooden bed rail still lying on the floor.","And the other culprit was nowhere to be seen!","\"Madam, are you awake?\" Nianxia's voice came from outside. But strangely, the other party didn't immediately come in.","\"Nianxia, you and Bipo stay outside for now. Don't come in,\" Dai Li had to speak up.","She hadn't used servants for the past thirty-plus years. She had done everything personally that machines couldn't replace, so she wasn't out of practice when cleaning up now. She first put on her clothes and combed her hair, then put the dirty quilt and pillows into the wooden basket.","Once everything was neatly arranged, Dai Li finally looked directly at the carved bed edge that she had intentionally or unintentionally ignored just now.","This thing certainly couldn't be left here indefinitely.","Just as she tried to pick it up, Dai Li heard footsteps.","Steady and unhurried, as if he had a well-thought-out plan for everything.","Dai Li knew without looking that it was Qin Shaozong returning. And indeed, she didn't turn around, focusing entirely on picking up the carved sandalwood rail from the floor.","Sandalwood has a tight and hard texture, with a higher density than ordinary wood. Even though it had a hollowed-out design, such a large piece was still quite heavy.","A strong arm reached over from behind and easily took the carved wooden rail from Dai Li's hand. \"Throw this away for now. I'll have someone come and fix the bed this afternoon.\"","It was a rather short sentence, but it trampled all over several of Dai Li's landmines.","\"What do you mean throw it away? It cannot be thrown away.\" Dai Li firmly grasped the other end of the carved wooden rail to prevent him from taking it out.","Qin Shaozong raised an eyebrow. \"Madam, the bed rail is broken and useless to keep. Why shouldn't we throw it away?\"","The tips of Dai Li's ears kept turning red. \"Throwing away a bed frame on the second day of our marriage? What would others think if they saw it?\"","The Marquis's mansion had just been renovated, so this bed couldn't possibly have been faulty before. If it broke, it could only have broken on their wedding night.","She and Qin Shaozong were no longer young kids. Their children had come of age, married, or were running around everywhere.","To break the bed on the night these parents got married, just thinking about word getting out was embarrassing.","\"Who cares what they think?\" Qin Shaozong didn't mind at all. Seeing the red from the tips of Dai Li's ears spread to her face, he couldn't help but chuckle softly. \"It is a good thing that the lord and the lady have a good relationship. Why hide it?\"","He meant that he had absolutely no intention of hiding it.","Dai Li didn't have his thick skin. By now, her face was completely red, but this man was simply wicked, adding one last remark, \"Inspector Dai, am I wrong?\"","A rush of heat shot straight to the top of Dai Li's head, steaming her lotus-like jade face bright red. She endured and endured, but finally couldn't hold back and nudged him with her elbow. \"I don't care. In short, outsiders cannot know about this. Qin Changgeng, put this carved bed edge back.\"","Qin Shaozong was puzzled. \"Put it back? Madam, this item is broken. Putting it back is of no use.\"","\"Just take a few ropes and tie it up to make do for now. We don't need to replace it with a new one yet.\" This was the most appropriate solution Dai Li could come up with.","If it's broken, let it be. Just leave it for a few months and figure out a way after the storm has passed.","Dai Li felt her method was very sound, but unexpectedly, he flatly denied it, \"We cannot do that.\"","Firm, unquestionable, and at the same time, resonant.","Dai Li frowned. Just as she was about to ask why, she heard him continue, \"Keeping a broken bed is unlucky and will affect our future marital relationship.\"","Dai Li was truly amused by his reasoning. \"Keeping a broken bed is unlucky, but you breaking the bed last night was lucky? What kind of logic is that?\"","He had a well-founded argument. \"Last night was out of uncontrollable passion. Now that we've found something wrong and have the chance to correct it, why shouldn't we?\"","Dai Li: \"...\"","She put on a stern face and called him by his surname and courtesy name again. \"Qin Changgeng, you might not want face, but I do. I don't care; anyway, others cannot know about this, and you cannot let anyone come to fix it.\"","When she was expressionless, that sense of distance, like an unreachable peony on a high terrace, immediately emerged. It had absolutely no connection to her myriad of charms when she was teasing him last night.","The atmosphere seemed to freeze for a moment, as if the cold spring breeze had blown into the inner room.","The two looked at each other for a moment, and Qin Shaozong clicked his tongue softly. \"Fine, we won't let others know. Madam, your skin is really thinner than paper; you're afraid of it being pierced by the slightest rustle of leaves in the wind. Besides, their discussions would only be out of envy for us. What is there to worry about?\"","Seeing him agree, Dai Li treated his latter words as wind past her ears. \"Then put it back.\"","\"Why put it back when it's broken? We'll replace it.\" Qin Shaozong took the section of the carved bed edge, grasping one end with one hand. The veins on his arm suddenly bulged, and with a loud snap, the carved sandalwood was forcibly broken in half by his brute strength.","\"Hey, wait...\"","Snapping it once wasn't enough for Qin Shaozong. A few more snaps followed, and the carved wooden rail that had quite an artistic conception just moments ago was now a pile of scrap wood.","\"This can be taken out now, right?\" He looked up at her, teasing in his eyes.","Dai Li: \"...\"","Dai Li kept a wooden face. \"Who told you to break it? Nianxia and the others will notice if a piece is missing.\"","\"If a piece is missing, I'll just install one back.\" Seeing her open her mouth to speak, Qin Shaozong added, \"If we don't let others install it, I'll fix it myself. Will that do?\"","Dai Li looked at him suspiciously.","Every profession has its specialty. She believed he had the talent of a military commander and could lead thousands of troops, but as a carpenter...","He had never done that before, right!","Dai Li was deeply suspicious and felt an unspeakable sense of unease.","Qin Shaozong: \"I already found a carpenter this morning. I originally planned to have him repair the bed after you woke up. Since Madam does not want others to know, I have no choice but to have the carpenter teach me a few tricks and then order him to keep his mouth shut.\"","Dai Li pursed her lips and soon revealed a smile. \"My husband is mighty! As long as you step up, this trivial matter of fixing a bed will surely be easily accomplished.\"","Regardless of whether he could do it or not, she would praise him first to give him the motivation to work, preferably fixing the bed before tonight.","Qin Shaozong went to find the carpenter in high spirits.","After lunch, Dai Li took Nianxia and Bipo for a stroll around the Marquis's estate, giving Qin Shaozong space to fix the bed.","The Marquis's estate covered a vast area. Dai Li had only just married yesterday; before that, she had only visited once during the capping ceremony. However, she had taken a carriage directly to the ancestral hall back then and never had the chance to look around properly.","The estate possessed both the majestic grandeur of winding corridors and soaring eaves, as well as the gentle elegance of winding paths, small bridges, and flowing water.","It was now early spring. In the back garden, clusters of flowers were budding among the scattered rocks, as beautiful as a richly colored painting.","Dai Li spent the entire afternoon outside, thoroughly enjoying the sights. It wasn't until the sun began to set in the west that she reluctantly led her servants back.","However, they did not return to the main courtyard, but went to the main hall instead.","It was time for dinner. Normally, she and Qin Shaozong would dine with the younger generation. Only after the meal would they return to their respective courtyards.","When Dai Li arrived at the main hall, all the juniors, including Shi Rongyue, were present. The seat she usually occupied was still empty, and Qin Shaozong was nowhere to be seen.","Just as Dai Li took her seat, footsteps echoed from the side corridor. She turned her head, but the newcomer was not Qin Shaozong.","A guard bowed to Dai Li with cupped hands. Madam, the Marquis asked me to pass on a message. He says you and the young masters and misses should go ahead and eat dinner without waiting for him.","Dai Li's heart skipped a beat, but she maintained a normal expression, nodding and saying she understood.","Was an entire afternoon not enough for Qin Changgeng to fix the bed? Please, please let nothing have gone wrong...","Dai Li was absent-minded, barely hearing what the juniors said to her. After rushing through her meal, she set down her bowl and chopsticks and hurried back to the main courtyard.","However, upon reaching the entrance to the courtyard, Dai Li told Nianxia and Bipo, You two wait here for now, no need to come in, before walking in alone.","The lamps in the main room were lit, illuminating everything clearly in the darkening twilight.","Because of this, Dai Li could see that the spot where the bed used to be was now replaced by a floor covered in sandalwood. There were many wooden planks; some were fitted together with mortise and tenon joints, while others were not.","And amidst this scattered pile of wood that looked nothing like a bed, the tall, broad-shouldered man stood with a dark, displeased expression on his face.","Dai Li's vision went black.","It was over. Indeed, there was a specialization for every profession; she never should have trusted Qin Changgeng. This man had dismantled the bed, but looking at it now, he couldn't put it back together at all!","Dai Li could almost hear people whispering behind her back:","Hey, hey, did you hear about the Marquis of Wu'an's wedding? Oh, you haven't? Then you are really out of the loop! Let me tell you, I heard that the Marquis of Wu'an and his new bride were so incredibly passionate on their wedding night that they actually shattered the entire bed!"]},{"number":140,"title":"Chapter 140","paragraphs":["No one spoke. Daili looked at the scattered wood on the floor, exchanged a glance with Qin Shaozong who was standing among the pile of wood, and then turned to walk out without a word.","When she was touring the gardens this afternoon, she saw many courtyards in the manor. If the main courtyard was uninhabitable, there were plenty of other places to stay. She would move out for now.","However, before Daili could take a few steps, or even leave the outer room, her arm was firmly grasped by a large, dark hand.","Where are you going, Madam? he asked, pulling her back.","Daili was not as strong as him and was pulled back two steps. She had to turn her head to look at Qin Shaozong, her expression wooden. You and I had a disagreement over something, had a massive argument in the room, and parted on bad terms. I went to sleep alone in a separate courtyard of the manor, and the Marquis, burning with anger, took his frustration out on the bed. The conflict lasted for a few days, and only then...","No, he interrupted coldly.","As he said this, Qin Shaozong was still holding a piece of wood with mortise and tenon joints that had not yet been assembled.","He threw the piece of wood aside with a cold face. What kind of decency is it to sleep in separate rooms right after getting married? Besides, the massive argument you mentioned is purely fabricated. The bed is broken, and that's that. Why deceive ourselves?","This culprit actually dared to say she was deceiving herself. Daili choked on a breath.","But before Daili could say anything else, he guided her outside with his arm around her, speaking without any hesitation, You and I will sleep in the separate courtyard for tonight, and we will come back tomorrow morning when the bed is fixed.","You're going to fix it? Daili's tone was full of suspicion.","Qin Shaozong fell silent for a moment. I am busy with military affairs and probably won't have the time. I'll have two carpenters come to fix it.","Daili: ...","Qin Shaozong added, Rest assured, Madam. I will issue a gag order to ensure they don't say a word. I expect mere carpenters wouldn't dare disobey.","Since he refused to cooperate and wouldn't sleep in separate rooms, Daili had no choice. As things stood, she could only make do in the separate courtyard for one night. As for Nianxia and Bipo, Daili brought them along as well.","However, whether it was because she was not used to the bed or because that ominous premonition lingered, even with Qin Shaozong's repeated reassurances that everything was fine, Daili still didn't sleep soundly that night.","A dark cloud loomed over her heart; she felt that something was bound to happen.","...","The sun set and rose, and in the blink of an eye, a day passed.","The guard duty at the Marquis's manor operated on a shift system. Whether it was the personal guards or the core military generals, everyone had to take turns. The former had more frequent shifts, while the latter's were more spaced out.","And the shift change every day took place at noon.","Mo Yanyun came on duty at noon yesterday, and upon arriving, he happened to see a carpenter being called into the manor. It was rare for such outsiders to visit the manor, so Mo Yanyun immediately asked him why he was there.","The carpenter shook his head and said he didn't know, only mentioning that he was summoned by the Marquis and that the nobleman hadn't specified the details.","After checking the man's belongings, Mo Yanyun let him through.","Coincidentally, after finishing his patrol of the area, he ran into the carpenter leaving with his toolbox on his back. Mo Yanyun did a quick calculation and realized the man had only stayed in the manor for about thirty minutes.","Something wasn't right!","So he stopped the man and questioned him again.","However, the previously very cooperative carpenter now seemed to have been struck dumb. He just shook his head, saying the Marquis had issued a gag order, and refused to say another word.","Mo Yanyun immediately grew suspicious, but then he figured the man had only been in the manor for thirty minutes and the items he brought were standard, so he probably couldn't cause any trouble.","Let him go, then.","But the next morning, Mo Yanyun ran into the carpenter again. This time, the man did not come alone; he was accompanied by a fellow carpenter.","Mo Yanyun's suspicions arose once more. Just as he was about to question them carefully, Hu Bao, who was leading them, blocked all his words with a simple, The Marquis has given orders.","Watching their retreating figures, Mo Yanyun instinctively followed. By the time he snapped back to reality, he saw from a distance that they had entered the main courtyard, while Hu Bao stood guard at the entrance, surprisingly not following them in.","Mo Yanyun turned pale with shock. He darted forward, intending to rush in, but was swiftly stopped by Hu Bao.","Hu Bao, what are you doing? Didn't you see the two of them go in? How can outsiders be allowed to casually enter an important place like the main courtyard? The Madam has so much precious jewelry. If anything is lost, who can bear the responsibility? Even if we take a step back and don't talk about jewelry, there are clothes. What if they have sticky fingers... Mo Yanyun said anxiously.","He loved to drink and visit brothels, so to some extent, he was well-acquainted with the baser instincts of men.","Mo Yanyun didn't specify what he meant by sticky fingers. But as a fellow man, how could Hu Bao not understand after the hint was dropped.","Hu Bao hesitated, his tone no longer as firm as before. But this is an order directly from the Marquis. He told me to escort the two carpenters to the main courtyard, wait outside for them to come out, and then escort them out of the manor. I am not allowed to enter the main room at any point and must only wait outside.","Mo Yanyun: Is there anyone else in the room?","Hu Bao shook his head, saying he didn't know, adding that the Marquis hadn't mentioned it. He truly hadn't gone inside, obediently stopping in front of the courtyard, so naturally, he didn't know.","Mo Yanyun had a sudden flash of inspiration. The Marquis only told you to wait in the front yard, but he didn't forbid me from entering. I'll call out from the door or take a quick peek inside. If there's a reliable overseer in the room, I'll come right out.","Hu Bao's brows knotted.","But in terms of military rank, Mo Yanyun was higher than him. So, after dropping those words, he strode inside.","Hey, Lao Mo, wait...","Just as he reached the door of the main room, Mo Yanyun heard a few clanging sounds coming from inside.","It was normal for carpenters to make noise while repairing things, so he didn't think much of it. Convinced that the Madam wasn't inside, Mo Yanyun called out casually, Is there anyone else in the room besides the carpenters?","But there was no answer.","Mo Yanyun called out again, but still, no one answered.","This was strange!","Could it be that only the carpenters were inside?","He stepped inside, unsurprisingly finding the outer room with its open doors completely empty. Upon passing through the moon gate into the inner room, Mo Yanyun saw the two carpenters, as well as Bipo standing not far from them.","Bipo was covering her ears with her hands to block out the annoying banging sounds. Her eyes were fixed on the two men nearby, dutifully acting as the overseer.","Suddenly, from the corner of her eye, she caught a glimpse of a tall, dark shadow. Bipo quickly turned her head, the words My Lord barely escaping her lips before getting stuck in her throat.","She looked at Mo Yanyun in astonishment, while the latter stared in shock at the bed that was smashed to pieces on the floor.","No one spoke, but Mo Yanyun, as if poked in the backside by a needle, suddenly turned and left.","He came in a hurry and left in a hurry, not leaving a single word behind.","Outside, Hu Bao saw Mo Yanyun rushing out less than a moment after going in, his expression extremely bizarre. Driven by curiosity, he asked, What happened?","As if finding an outlet to vent, Mo Yanyun first drew in a sharp breath with a hiss, then gestured with both hands. Hu Bao, can you even imagine? Such a massive bed, completely shattered into pieces! I heard the Marquis and the Madam slept in the separate courtyard last night. It seems this bed was broken on their very wedding night...","Hu Bao's expression gradually synchronized with Mo Yanyun's.","Mo Yanyun drew in another sharp breath. Everyone knows the Marquis keeps a close eye on the Madam, but I didn't expect him to be so... well, eager. As soon as he made her a woman of the Qin family, he couldn't wait to ignite that dry wood with a blazing fire.","\"No, I can't hold it in anymore. I have to talk to Old Bai and the others, tighten their skins a bit, so they show a hundred and twenty percent respect from now on.\" Mo Yanyun turned and left.","Hu Bao's sluggish brain took a long time to slowly turn over. Remembering the solemnity when their superiors assigned the task, he suddenly shuddered. \"Oh no!\"","But Mo Yanyun was tall and walked fast, disappearing in the blink of an eye.","*","Dai Li and Qin Shaozong were in the study, each at a long desk piled high with documents. The former's desk held information on fertilizers, while the latter's held confidential reports from various provinces.","The matter of the fertile soil was solely Dai Li's responsibility, which included not only composting but also the subsequent distribution of the fertilizer.","Yuyang Commandery had nine counties under its jurisdiction, with a total population of over four hundred thousand. Even though Dai Li had led people to collect materials and compost without a day's rest last winter, producing several bags of fertilizer almost daily.","A single fertilizer bag weighed at least several tons, enough for dozens of acres of farmland. But spread across the nine counties of Yuyang, the fertilizer was still far from enough.","Therefore, how to allocate it was a matter that allowed for no carelessness.","However, at this moment, Dai Li's attention was not on the desk. She looked at the two people Qin Shaozong had called into the study.","One tall and one short. The taller young man wore a jade crown and a white robe. His features were handsome and refined, his gaze restrained, and he stood as straight as a pine tree.","The slightly shorter youth beside him had not yet come of age. His long hair was half-tied with a red ribbon, complementing his black and red martial attire and slightly relaxed stance. His rebellious aura was impossible to suppress.","Qin Shaozong sat behind the desk, looking at the tall and short pair. His expression was not particularly gentle; it even carried an undeniable, commanding majesty. \"Your mother and I are now married, and from now on we are husband and wife. Since you two have paid your respects and changed how you address her, we are a family from now on.\"","His gaze swept over the two. \"In the future, you are brothers, branches of the same tree, and both my sons. I will treat you equally. If you earn merit, you will be rewarded; if you make mistakes, you will be punished. There will be no exceptions.\"","Dai Li lowered her eyes, listening to Qin Shaozong beside her shift the topic to inquire about their studies.","He first had them speak for themselves, and then he asked questions.","Staring at the open document on the desk, Dai Li didn't take in a single word. It took a long while before she looked up again, just in time to see Qin Qinian saying with a bitter face, \"Father, it's really not that I'm not working hard. It's just that those words seem to dance...\"","\"Bastard!\" Qin Shaozong slammed the table. \"You don't even know how to change your excuse. Every time it's that they're dancing. Let's see if you look like you're dancing when I whip you in a moment!\"","The tiger-shaped brush rest on the desk jumped at the impact, then fell over on its side with a clatter.","Qin Qinian wilted. \"Father, I'm really not lying. Those words really don't sit still.\"","Seeing his lack of repentance, Qin Shaozong burned with anger. \"How difficult is it for a child from a poor family to seek a famous teacher? You boy, you don't know how blessed you are. Not to mention the young masters of other families in the commandery at your age, even those ten years younger wouldn't make so many typos.\"","Dark clouds gathered over Qin Qinian's head, and he wilted even more, like a little cabbage rotting in the field.","Seeing him merely wallow in dejection without the slightest sign of rousing himself, the veins on Qin Shaozong's forehead bulged. He was about to scold him again when he suddenly felt his arm being patted twice.","Dai Li spoke gently to the man who turned his head to look at her: \"Let me ask Qinian a few questions.\"","Qin Shaozong said nothing, only leaning back with a cold face.","Dai Li looked at Qin Qinian. \"Qinian, since when did you start feeling that words dance?\"","Qin Qinian was still dejected, but since Dai Li asked, he answered honestly: \"A long time ago. Probably since I first started learning to read.\"","\"When you say 'words dance,' does it mean that in your eyes, certain word shapes are inverted or reversed? If you don't point at them with your finger, do they easily skip lines? And when you pick up a pen to write, do you always have to think for a long time before you faintly remember the full appearance of some words?\" Dai Li asked.","With every sentence she spoke, the youth perked up a little more.","Finally, Qin Qinian was astonished. \"Mother, how did you know this? Could it be that you, like me, feel that words dance?\"","Before today, he had never told her this, and presumably, his father's subordinates wouldn't speak ill of him outside. Unless she herself was the same and could empathize, how could she understand as soon as he spoke?","He had been saying this for over ten years, and neither his father nor his teachers understood.","Qin Shaozong turned his head to look at Dai Li, surprise in his eyes.","But he knew she didn't have those issues. She read books very smoothly; when she rummaged through books in his study in the past, she could finish one in two or three days.","\"This condition of Qinian's has a specific term in my homeland. It's called dyslexia,\" Dai Li said, looking at Qin Shaozong. \"You can simply understand it as a lack of coordination in a certain area of the brain that processes auditory and visual information, which triggers this disorder.\"","\"A problem with the brain? Doesn't that mean he's an idiot?\" Qin Shaozong said.","Qin Qinian choked.","Dai Li was exasperated. \"How can you speak like that as a father? This is just a disorder; it doesn't mean there's a problem with his intelligence. On the contrary, many such people are very smart and have unique talents in other fields.\"","Qin Shaozong raised his long eyebrows.","Qin Qinian's eyes grew brighter and brighter. If he had a big tail behind him, he would definitely be wagging it hard enough to fan up a breeze.","Dai Li gave them an analogy. \"It's like a wooden barrel. At first glance, a certain plank might be shorter, but in places you don't know, the missing wood from this short plank has been added to another plank, making other areas into long planks.\"","Qin Shaozong remained silent, reaching out to set the tiger-shaped brush rest upright, his long fingers stroking the tiger's back.","If someone else had said these words, he would have definitely thought they were spouting nonsense, making excuses for Qin San's foolishness.","But it happened to be her who said it personally.","Qin Shaozong asked, \"Madam, is there a cure for this disorder you mentioned?\"","Dai Li hesitated. Since he asked for a \"cure,\" she could only say, \"It is best to intervene in this disorder from childhood. The later the intervention, the weaker the effect. For someone of Qinian's age, it will be a protracted battle, and it might not be completely cured.\"","Qin Shaozong frowned.","Qin Qinian wasn't too disappointed; he was used to it after all these years.","He could eat, drink, run, and jump. He was thick-skinned and much sturdier than others. And now that someone understood him and didn't think he was lying, he was too happy to care.","\"However, it's not impossible to alleviate. Practice more usually. While reading by yourself, have someone slowly read the contents of the book to you. Combine the two for training, and after a period of time, add writing to the mix. A three-pronged approach,\" Dai Li said.","Qin Qinian's expression changed slightly. \"Mother, actually, I'm doing quite well right now...\"","Qin Shaozong's anger flared up again. \"You miss strokes and parts when you write, what's so good about that? Do as your mother says and have the teacher try this method.\"","Qin Qinian dawdled and agreed.","Qin Shaozong couldn't stand his unmotivated appearance; it made his eyes hurt to look at him, so he simply waved his hand to dismiss the two juniors.","After they left, Dai Li finally said, \"With a father as domineering as you, and Qinian losing his mother at such a young age, it is a miracle his personality didn't turn out crooked.\"","Qin Shaozong did not like hearing this. \"I am domineering?\"","\"Are you not?\" Dai Li countered. \"Your word is law, and you brook no defiance once you have made a decision. Tell me, if that isn't domineering, what is?\"","Qin Shaozong looked away. \"That boy Qin San was mostly raised by my parents in the past, and Hongying would also come back to see him from time to time. Yunce has a gentle temperament and is very protective of his younger siblings, and I also chose a tutor for his early education early on.\"","Dai Li roughly understood.","Despite his biological mother's early passing, Qin Qinian did not lack love.","He had kind grandparents, a doting aunt, gentle older siblings, a tutor to accompany and guide him, and moreover, Qin Shaozong, a father who had always been watching over him from behind.","\"Tomorrow I will have Mi Yifan come over, and you, Madam, can talk to him about the ways to alleviate that disorder,\" Qin Shaozong said.","Dai Li agreed.","After finishing their affairs in the study, it unknowingly became time to eat.","The two left the study and headed to the main hall for their meal. On the way, Dai Li ran into Mo Yanyun.","The man bowed in greeting and stepped aside, all in one smooth motion.","Dai Li did not know if it was just her imagination, but she felt his gaze was slightly different from before; there seemed to be an indescribable sense of admiration and respect.","Dai Li: \"?\"","\"Madam?\" Qin Shaozong noticed she had suddenly stopped.","Dai Li's mind raced. \"It is Commandant Mo on duty today. Could he have seen those two carpenters?\"","Otherwise, why would Mo Yanyun have such an attitude?","\"Absolutely impossible. I already sent Hu Bao to guard the entrance of the main courtyard. Besides, why would he go to the main courtyard for no reason?\" Qin Shaozong saw she was still frowning. \"Didn't you leave a maid in the room? If you are still worried, just ask her when we get back.\"","Dai Li thought about it and agreed.","However, after lunch, Dai Li was not able to return to the main courtyard right away. She and Qin Shaozong had their plans for the rest of the day disrupted by an express dispatch.","No, it was not just them. It would be more accurate to say that the entire core leadership of the Northern Territory was severely shaken by it.","This dispatch had gold-plated jade rollers on both sides, and the middle was made of the finest silk brocade. It came from the south, or more accurately, from the capital in Chang'an, an imperial decree issued personally by the young Emperor.","First, it highly praised Qin Shaozong's achievements in guarding the border, then commended Dai Li for promoting the keel waterwheel, and congratulated the two on their recent marriage. Finally, the imperial decree summoned Dai Li and Qin Yanzhou to Chang'an to receive their titles."]},{"number":141,"title":"Chapter 141","paragraphs":["\"Is the imperial court trying to stage a repeat of what happened all those years ago?\"","Many years ago, when the late emperor still presided over the court, an imperial decree was issued summoning the sons of Qin, the Governor of Youzhou, to the capital to serve as reading companions. Later, Father Qin employed stalling tactics. As it happened, the Northern Kingdom invaded, and Father Qin led his two sons into battle.","In that battle, where they were attacked from both front and rear, Qin Shaozong tragically lost his elder brother—a loss he had brooded over for more than a decade. Now, after all these years, the same trick was being played again, and this time, the spearhead was pointed directly at his wife and child.","Anyone could see that this was a trap, and even more so, a naked provocation.","Sitting behind the long desk, Qin Shaozong's face was exceptionally grim, his entire being exuding a heavy, oppressive aura. \"Reckless fools seeking death.\"","Nalan Zhi frowned. \"My Lord, although the imperial edict only mentions the keel waterwheel, I personally suspect that the matter of the Madam creating compost bags last winter has also become known to the court.\"","Composting had to be done out in the fields; there was no way to hide it. Moreover, the process spanned the entire winter. As long as someone was paying attention, it really wouldn't be hard to discover.","In the vast Yuyang Commandery, it was impossible to say there wasn't a single spy from another province.","\"Going to Chang'an to receive a title sounds nice, but I fear this is a Hongmen Banquet—a trap with no return. How about we stall a bit longer?\"","\"With what excuse? The edict has a set time limit, and that team of envoys is still here, watching with their own eyes. We can't exactly... kill them all, can we?\"","As this softly spoken sentence fell, it was like piercing through an outer layer of disguise. The atmosphere in the study noticeably shifted.","Qin Shaozong spun the jade archer's ring on his thumb.","\"We cannot do that. It's not just one or two people; this is a full envoy team of twenty. How can we just kill them on a whim? Besides, that might only be their overt number. How many are in the shadows, or whether there is another group of escorts waiting for a reply in another county—all of this is still unknown,\" Cui Shengping shook his head.","\"This time, entering the capital to receive a title is presented as an imperial grace. If we rashly kill the envoys, in the eyes of the world, we would appear far too arrogant and unappreciative of favors...\"","Sheng Ran sighed. \"Even if you are at the height of your power in the North, My Lord, at the end of the day, you are still a subject of Great Yan. We cannot let others find a pretext to crusade against the disloyal. We cannot be the bird that sticks its head out to be shot.\"","No matter how young or incompetent the child emperor was, as long as he wore the dragon robes and sat upon the imperial throne, he was the legitimate ruler.","All the royalists in the world, true or false, would support him. Not to mention the blood oath the founding emperor made with his officials in the past, establishing the covenant: \"If anyone other than the Han clan takes the throne, the whole world shall unite to strike them down.\"","Dai Li was also in the study. After the imperial edict had come down, Qin Shaozong hadn't avoided her, and he allowed her to sit in on the subsequent discussions.","Now, listening to the advisors and generals exchanging words, Dai Li was deep in thought.","She had to admit, everything they said was correct.","It was a fact that the dynasty had reached its twilight years, and it was a fact that the world was about to descend into chaos. But it was even more of a fact that the nail that sticks out gets hammered down. Looking throughout the long river of history, those who jumped the highest at the very beginning generally didn't meet a good end.","However, Qin Shaozong was by no means a docile master; he was rebellious to his very core. Dai Li felt that he wouldn't obediently follow orders.","They stayed in the study for an entire afternoon. It wasn't until the sun sank in the west and a layer of dim light veiled the sky that everyone left the study, though they didn't immediately head to their respective homes.","It was mealtime, and the Marquis's estate had prepared food for them. After eating, everyone returned to their homes before the curfew.","After being well-fed, Dai Li and Qin Shaozong returned to the main courtyard together.","In the afternoon, there had been quite a few people in the study. She had only listened, without asking questions or offering opinions. Now that there was no one else around, Dai Li asked him, \"Qin Changgeng, what are your thoughts on this matter?\"","Qin Shaozong looked up at the sky. Dusk had passed, and scattered stars were faintly visible against the pitch-black firmament. \"About ten years ago, Nalan Wugong told me that the Emperor Star was hidden and unclear, and that Great Yan's destiny only had a little bit left. He said that in another ten years, there might be a massive upheaval.\"","He suddenly let out a light chuckle. \"At the time, I just thought he was speaking casually. Looking at it now, perhaps this is the time.\"","He didn't say it explicitly, but these words were fraught with murderous intent. Dai Li guessed, \"So you plan to head south? But regional governors and border generals are not allowed to enter the capital without an imperial edict.\"","Qin Shaozong: \"There will be an edict. Several explosions will occur in Chang'an, suspected to be the work of rebels causing chaos in the shadows. Consequently, His Majesty will urgently dispatch another edict to the North. I will enter the capital by imperial decree, but while passing through Yanzhou, I will encounter a band of bandits, and during the bandit extermination, I will accidentally lose the other edict.\"","These words left Dai Li completely stunned.","Explosions in Chang'an? Where would explosions come from? Wait, could he be talking about dust explosions?! This man wanted to imitate the Green Lotus Cult and trigger a few dust explosions in Chang'an?!","Thinking this, she asked him directly.","\"Why not?\" Qin Shaozong didn't deny it. \"Desperate times call for desperate measures. When the time comes, we'll avoid the commoners and have our hidden agents blow up a few houses. Then, we'll leave behind some 'divine oracles' on the ground about the birth of a new king. I'm not worried about Chang'an not falling into chaos.\"","He wasn't just going to blow up houses; he was going to frame someone else while he was at it. And the scapegoat would naturally be chosen from among the governors of the Si, Yu, and Xu provinces, who still ostensibly maintained a high degree of obedience to the imperial court.","By linking someone from there with the Commandant of the Capital Guards, who was responsible for the capital's security, he didn't believe Empress Dowager Wang and Chancellor Dong Zhou would still be able to sit still.","The muddier the waters in Chang'an, the better!","With the capital in great chaos, it would be perfectly reasonable for him, a regional border general, to be ordered to enter the capital to protect the emperor, wouldn't it?","Dai Li sighed in admiration, \"So, after listening to them discuss for an entire afternoon, you already had a plan in mind all along.\"","Qin Shaozong spoke truthfully, \"I didn't exactly have a plan all along; the method came to me while listening to their discussions this afternoon. Actually, now is not a good time to march, because spring is the most important farming season. I originally wanted to wait until autumn to make a move. With the help of the fertilizer developed by my Madam, this golden autumn would surely yield an abundant harvest, and the army wouldn't have to worry about provisions. What a pity...\"","What a pity that they couldn't wait until autumn.","Dai Li walked forward alongside him. \"Regarding the dust explosions, you must execute it flawlessly. Otherwise, you'll be actively handing leverage to the imperial court.\"","Qin Shaozong smiled. \"If it weren't for Madam's guidance back then, I wouldn't have known the inner workings of dust explosions either. That bunch of parasites in Chang'an are short-sighted; they definitely won't know. However, as for the specific execution, I still need to discuss it carefully with the gentlemen to ensure that this matter is absolutely foolproof.\"","Dai Li expressed her concern, \"The Green Lotus Cult is widely distributed, and there are bound to be their followers in Chang'an as well. After the houses collapse, it won't be long before they figure out the true cause.\"","Qin Shaozong was silent for a moment. \"Knowing is one thing, but having evidence is another. Words without proof mean nothing. I certainly won't accept this basin of dirty water being poured on me, and by that time, I will probably have already entered the capital.\"","The two chatted as they walked, and before they knew it, they had returned to the main courtyard.","Night fell. Candles were embedded in the white jade lamps situated on both sides of the main house's front yard, casting a soft halo of light into the surroundings. At a certain moment, two silhouettes stepped into the halo together—one tall, one short—moving forward in unison, gradually settling into a synchronized rhythm that no outsider could intrude upon.","Having finished her after-dinner stroll to digest her food, Dai Li, who hadn't taken a nap today, let out a yawn, planning to wash up and go to sleep.","Right, the bed!","Dai Li quickly walked into the inner chamber. Sure enough, the large bed that had previously been reduced to splintered wood by Qin Shaozong's tossing and turning had its broken carved edge replaced without anyone noticing.","It was as good as new, as if everything that had happened before was just a bizarre dream.","Dai Li smiled with satisfaction.","Fine, there was no \"as if\" about it—that incident was simply an absurd, bizarre dream! Anyway, apart from Bipo, who had been supervising, no one else would ever know.","\"Madam, today when the carpenter came to repair the couch, Commandant Mo came in...\" Bipo's voice was very quiet.","Daili looked as though she had been struck by lightning. She stood frozen like a wooden chicken, and it took her a long while before she slowly turned her head like an old, rusty machine. \"What... what did you just say?\"","Qin Shaozong was also stunned.","Bipo braced herself and repeated it, also explaining the entire sequence of events she had later learned from Hu Bao.","Thinking back to Mo Yanyun's strange behavior that morning, Daili closed her eyes in despair. Keeping her eyes shut, she walked toward the bed, collapsed onto it with a soft thud, and pulled the nearby quilt over herself, wrapping her entire body and head up like a silkworm cocoon.","After his initial surprise, Qin Shaozong actually laughed.","He stepped forward and grabbed a corner of the brocade quilt, tugging at it gently. \"Madam, since the matter is already set in stone, why not treat it as a passing breeze? Let it go, and do not take it to heart.\"","The person wrapped up like a cocoon did not speak, but there was a distinct pulling force trying to yank the quilt back from his grasp.","Qin Shaozong turned his head to Bipo, who was standing to the side, and said, \"There is no need for you to serve here. You may leave.\"","Once the maid had left, Qin Shaozong directly peeled Daili out of the quilt and made her sit on his lap. \"It was that fellow Mo Yanyun who disregarded the rules first. The fault is entirely his. Why should you punish yourself for someone else's mistake?\"","Daili looked at Qin Shaozong in astonishment. Seeing that this chief culprit felt not a shred of guilt and had pinned all the blame on Mo Yanyun in just a few words, she could not help but ask, \"Qin Changgeng, are you missing a piece of your memory?\"","Qin Shaozong knew perfectly well what she was talking about, but he did not take the bait. \"Trespassing into a superior's residence—where are his manners and respect for the law? Tomorrow, I will definitely punish that fellow Mo Yanyun severely.\"","Daili was speechless.","Daili sighed in sheer amazement. \"Truly a brilliant talent who could come up with a countermeasure in just one short afternoon. If you ever fail as the Lord of the North in the future, you could go become a traveling persuader. With your silver-tongued talent for sophistry, you would surely become renowned throughout the world.\"","He suddenly raised an eyebrow. \"Why wait for the future? I shall be a traveling persuader tonight.\"","With those words, he pounced like a starving tiger and pinned her down.","Daili's eyes widened for a moment, then she reached back and grabbed his belt. \"A traveling persuader, are you? Then I am the assassin who specializes in slaying such persuaders.\"","The imperial envoy's procession naturally took up residence in the Marquis's manor. The day after the edict was issued, they received their reply.","The Marchioness and her son would answer the summons and enter the capital. However, as the journey would be long and arduous, they needed some time to pack their belongings.","The leader of the envoy procession was named Shen Tianming, a General of Agile Cavalry personally appointed by the young Emperor. The second-in-command of the group was Guo Nai, a man who held the high rank of Palace Attendant.","An envoy procession comprising both civil and military officials, featuring a great general whose status rivaled the Three Ducal Ministers, as well as a close attendant to the young Emperor—the arrangement could only be described as grand.","They were absolutely determined to invite them to Chang'an.","Upon learning that Qin Shaozong had agreed to let his newlywed wife and his son enter the capital, both Shen Tianming and Guo Nai breathed a sigh of relief.","\"As long as he is willing to accept the decree, that is good. I was afraid he might try to pull some tricks.\" Guo Nai swallowed the rest of his words.","Shen Tianming sneered coldly. \"Having his wife enter the capital to receive a title is a gracious reward. How could he dare refuse? Besides, as long as Qin Shaozong remains a subject of the Great Yan, he must obey orders. But saying they need time to pack... tsk, I just hope no unexpected complications arise.\"","Guo Nai replied, \"Let us wait and see. In any case, the deadline stipulated in the edict has not yet arrived.\"","Qin Shaozong spent two days plotting the dust explosion incident in Chang'an with his group of advisors. At the end of the hour of Shen on the second day, a squad of fast horses carrying secret orders galloped swiftly out of the south gate of Yuyang.","They headed all the way south, making straight for Chang'an.","...","Qin Yanzhou answered the summons and went to the study.","When he arrived, the study door was half open. Peering inside through the gap, he saw no one else, so he stepped in.","There was indeed no one else in the study. A burly man sat behind the desk, toying with a tiger-shaped brush rest. Hearing his footsteps, the man looked up.","It was already dusk, and no lamps had been lit in the room. There was only a single beam of light shining in through the lattice window, making the room appear rather dim.","Qin Yanzhou cupped his hands and bowed. \"Father.\"","\"The imperial court has issued an edict summoning Madam and you to the capital to receive titles. I have already agreed to this. Once Madam has roughly finished dealing with the fertilizer matter, we will head south to Chang'an,\" Qin Shaozong said.","Over the past two days, Qin Shaozong had been holding private meetings with his advisors, which Qin Yanzhou had not participated in. Therefore, he only knew that they would be going to Chang'an in a few days; he was completely ignorant of any other details.","Now, hearing Qin Shaozong bring it up on his own initiative, Qin Yanzhou knew that what the other man was about to say would concern both their journey south and himself.","\"Local officials are not allowed to enter the capital without an edict. However, when the time comes, certain things will happen in the capital, and I will enter the capital under the pretext of answering a summons to protect His Majesty.\" Qin Shaozong twirled the brush rest in his hand. \"Bandits have been appearing at the border of Yan and Ji provinces. My edict to enter the capital will be 'lost' there. When the time comes, whether it is to recover the edict or to eliminate a menace for the people, there will be a bandit-suppression operation.\"","Qin Shaozong's gaze burned like a torch. \"Qin the Second, do you wish to establish your merits and build a career?\""]},{"number":142,"title":"Chapter 142","paragraphs":["To build a legacy.","These words undoubtedly held an immense allure for any ambitious man.","\"I do,\" Qin Yanzhou said without hesitation.","It was not a lie; he truly wanted to.","In every possible aspect.","The past could not be chased, he could not return to the modern era, and reeking of blood, he was completely out of place in that beautiful time. It was better to focus on the future right in front of him.","The past ten years had certainly been arduous, but his martial arts skills were undeniable. He did not want to waste the sole harvest of those ten years, nor did he want others to refer to him simply as the son of the Marquis of Wu'an when speaking of him in the future.","Furthermore, in the eyes of outsiders who did not know the truth, his mother's marriage to the Marquis of Wu'an was seen as a lone orphan girl climbing the social ladder, lucky to marry into a wealthy family.","His mother indeed lacked a prominent family background and had no backing to rely on. But that was in the past. From now on, he could be her safe harbor, letting everyone know that even if the Marquis of Wu'an proved unreliable one day, he could still hold up the sky for his mother.","This legacy had to be built!","Qin Shaozong said lightly, \"Having ambition is a good thing. But you must know that hiding in a cushy position at the rear of the army will not earn you much military merit.\"","The four great military merits of this era were: being the first to scale the enemy walls, breaking the enemy formation, slaying an enemy general, and capturing the enemy flag.","The danger level for each of these was extremely high, but high risk also meant high reward. Any one of those four merits was enough to equal over a decade of hard work in a rear-echelon idle post.","Qin Shaozong did not speak too explicitly, but with the previous mention of bandit suppression and the subsequent mention of idle posts, Qin Yanzhou understood. He cupped his hands again and said solemnly, \"Father, your son requests to go to the front lines.\"","Qin Shaozong's tone was calm. \"Shedding blood on the front lines builds merit quickly, but it is indeed not as safe as the rear. Although you are my son, once you are truly on the battlefield, I cannot possibly assign a squad of men to do nothing but protect you.\"","The Qin family had guarded the borders for generations. Not only Qin Shaozong himself, but his father, his grandfather, and even the currently seventeen-year-old Qin Qinian had all been to the battlefield and engaged in close combat with the Northern Kingdom.","Bleeding and getting injured were unavoidable.","\"I understand.\" Qin Yanzhou's words still carried no hesitation. \"Going into battle is to kill the enemy; one cannot put the cart before the horse.\"","The man sitting behind the desk imperceptibly curled his lips. In the dimming twilight, this slight smile vanished in a flash, making it hard to see clearly.","\"Madam's Divorce Agreement is with you, isn't it?\" Qin Shaozong suddenly said.","This remark had nothing to do with what they were just discussing. Qin Yanzhou froze, a hint of suspicion entering his gaze.","When the young man did not speak, Qin Shaozong tapped his fingertips lightly on the desk twice. \"Most likely it is. Have you read that agreement, boy?\"","He asked if he had read it, but his tone was just like the previous declarative sentence, without the slightest doubt.","He was certain that Qin Yanzhou had already read it.","\"I have,\" Qin Yanzhou answered truthfully.","The agreement had three clauses in total, two of which were related to him, both being his mother's plans for his future.","Qin Shaozong gave an affirmative sound in response.","When she handed over this agreement, she must have solemnly instructed her son, and since it involved his mother, this boy could not possibly sit still.","\"The third clause involves conflicts regarding children, and conflicts that cannot be mediated...\" Qin Shaozong's fingertips tapped quickly on the desk a few times. \"Qin the Second, if I were the one to take the initiative and propose sending you to the front lines, Madam would definitely turn the world upside down arguing with me.\"","\"I will volunteer for battle, and I will speak to Mother about this myself.\" Qin Yanzhou understood his meaning.","Pausing for a moment, the young man added, \"When I discuss it in detail with Mother, I will not mention you from beginning to end. Father, you only need to nod and agree at the very end.\"","Qin Shaozong chuckled. \"You do have some wit about you. Alright, handle this matter as you see fit.\"","As they were about to set off for Chang'an, the matter of the fertilizer had to be expedited. Dai Li thought it over and finally overturned her previous plans, deciding to concentrate their efforts on a single district.","First, they would establish a base and make this area an experimental field. This would not only facilitate the subsequent transportation of fertilizer but also help with future comparisons.","After all, scattering fertilizer everywhere like a fairy scattering flowers would yield far less obvious results than targeted application. Having a model in the first year would mean that when the composting method was announced in the winter after the golden autumn, the farmers' enthusiasm would surely run high.","Dai Li was about to head south, so the subsequent fertilizer matters had to be handed over, and the person taking charge was Yan San.","The Yan clan had been personally supported by Qin Shaozong. As the current leader of the Yan clan, Yan San was not only efficient but also had relatively few conflicting interests.","Qin Shaozong had been very at ease entrusting the previous salt stone matter to him, and the same was true for the fertilizer issue now.","On this side, Dai Li completed the handover, while on the other side, Nianxia and Bipo had also packed the luggage for the journey south. Dai Li's various belongings alone filled three entire carriages.","Everything was ready, waiting only for tomorrow's departure.","In the main room of the primary courtyard.","\"...What? Rongrong is also going south with us? This journey isn't very safe; it's inappropriate to bring her. What if she gets hurt? How will we explain it to Hongying?\" Dai Li looked at Qin Shaozong in astonishment.","\"Who told you it wasn't safe?\" Qin Shaozong pulled her in front of him and flicked the golden hairpin on her head, watching the gold tassels sway back and forth. \"Marching life is dull, and the ranks are filled with men, each with their own duties, so they probably won't have time to chat with you, Madam. But Shi Rongrong is different. She is a girl and doesn't have to work, so she can keep you entertained.\"","\"I came to Yuyang just like that in the beginning, so why can't I leave the same way now?\" Dai Li still felt it was inappropriate.","Putting herself in the other's shoes, if she were Qin Hongying, she wouldn't want her daughter to travel with the army either. Why give up a comfortable life to suffer with the troops, all just to keep someone entertained?","Qin Shaozong replied, \"We didn't have the conditions back then, but it's different now. Besides, I've already spoken to Shi Rongrong about this beforehand, and she is very willing.\"","Dai Li choked on her words.","She truly hadn't expected the young girl to agree.","Qin Shaozong continued, \"Madam, this trip south will be undertaken alongside Shen Tianming's group of imperial messengers, and I will initially accompany them under the banner of an escort. The escorting party shouldn't look too formidable, or it will definitely arouse their suspicion. If those people send a letter to Chang'an, when the incident in Chang'an occurs, it will be inevitable that someone in the imperial court will connect it to the North. Whether or not they receive a hint to seek the true culprit makes a world of difference.\"","Bringing a niece along with several carriages of a lady's luggage gave a very different impression than having Madam travel light with barely any baggage, accompanied instead by thousands of armored cavalry.","The former looked like going to the capital to receive a title while enjoying the scenery along the way; the latter looked exactly like marching to war.","But the destination was Chang'an; against whom could they be rebelling?","Dai Li furrowed her brows, then relaxed them, repeating this several times. \"I'll go write a letter to Hongying.\"","Qin Shaozong let the golden tassels slip from his palm, smiling without saying a word.","The ink-black color of the sky faded from dark to light, until finally, a sliver of pale white dawned on the horizon.","The night passed in the blink of an eye.","As they were to depart today, Shen Tianming and his party woke up the moment the first rays of morning light touched the earth.","They got up, had breakfast, and tidied up a bit.","Fully equipped and ready to go.","As a result, when they had everything ready and sent someone to ask when they would set off, the reply they received was—","\"What? The Marquis's Madam hasn't gotten out of bed yet?\" Guo Nai was dumbfounded.","\"She is still not up?\" Shen Tianming turned his head to look at the sundial, his expression turning rather ugly. \"It is already the beginning of the hour of Chen, how is she still not awake?\"","The imperial soldier looked miserable. \"That is indeed what the maidservant said. She said her mistress always wakes at the end of the hour of Chen every day, so it is still quite early right now.\"","\"How can today be the same as any other day?\" Shen Tianming said in dissatisfaction. \"There are priorities. Today is the day of departure, how can she be so negligent?\"","Seeing the soldier hesitating to speak, Guo Nai said, \"If you have something to say, just say it.\"","The soldier swallowed hard. \"General Shen, Attendant Guo, the Marquis of Wuan was right there in the room. He said that this trip to Chang'an is to receive a title, not to rush to reincarnate, so what is the hurry.\"","Shen Tianming: ...","Guo Nai: ...","Shen Tianming's face twisted, and he finally squeezed out two words: \"How arrogant.\"","Guo Nai signaled for the soldier to step down. \"The Marquis of Wuan has always been arrogant, so it is not surprising that he would say such a thing. Forget it, there is no need to argue with him over such trivial matters. Let us just wait. It is a good thing that he is willing to let his wife and children depart at all.\"","This wait lasted until nearly noon.","A convoy of carriages finally slowly emerged from the Marquis's estate. Qin Shaozong, riding his horse Red Dragon, rode parallel at the front with Shen Tianming, the General of Agile Cavalry.","\"General Shen is indeed fit to be a commander; your patience is much better than those lowly soldiers,\" Qin Shaozong said with a smile.","Shen Tianming's mouth twitched.","The soldier only dared to rush them because he was ordered to do so by him, right? This man surnamed Qin was insulting him in a roundabout way.","Shen Tianming smiled without the smile reaching his eyes. \"Actually, departing earlier means your esteemed wife could receive His Majesty's reward sooner, which is not a bad thing. You should know that the number of living titled ladies in the court today can be counted on one hand.\"","Women in the imperial family or the wives and daughters of important ministers could hold the title of a Lady. For example, Empress Dowager Wang was titled Lady Xiangyu.","Once titled, they would have their own fiefdom, and the recipient would enjoy rights such as taxation and conscription within their territory. It could be said that they were like a minor feudal lord.","Of course, the title of Lady was not bestowed casually. It depended not only on the husband's status and identity but also on the woman's own abilities.","Shen Tianming was not lying; counting Dai Li, who had not yet been officially titled, there were only five living titled ladies in the current dynasty.","Because of this, this grace was clear and plain; at least in the eyes of the people, it was completely genuine.","Qin Shaozong and Shen Tianming rode side by side, chatting as they went.","After leaving Yuyang Commandery and traveling another twenty miles, Shen Tianming turned to Qin Shaozong and said, \"Even if you escort someone for a thousand miles, there must eventually be a parting. My Lord Marquis, you may stop your escort here. Rest assured, I will definitely escort your esteemed wife and son to the capital without a single scratch.\"","Guo Nai chimed in from the side, \"Even if the Marquis does not trust our twenty elite soldiers, you should at least have confidence in the three-hundred-strong guard detail you are leaving behind.\"","Qin Shaozong, however, replied, \"The journey is long, over mountains and waters. A round trip will take at least several months. I finally managed to marry a wife, and we are deeply in love. A single day apart feels like three years. Escorting her a mere twenty miles is still too little.\"","Guo and Shen both choked on their words, their expressions turning strange.","A grown, manly man acting so overly affectionate in front of outsiders—what kind of propriety was this?","Did he not feel embarrassed?","\"Furthermore, my niece is also traveling with my wife, so no matter how you look at it, twenty miles is still too short,\" Qin Shaozong said leisurely.","Guo and Shen were speechless.","And so, this escort lasted until dusk.","Two fine steeds pulled the carriage together. The horses were not only extremely sturdy but also an excellent breed from the North, boasting outstanding endurance and speed. Therefore, despite the slightly late departure, the group still arrived at a small county south of Yuyang before the curfew.","With a wave of his hand, Qin Shaozong directly booked several inns to settle the soldiers, and he had the renowned chef traveling with their entourage take over the inn's kitchen, putting on a grand display.","Shen Tianming and Guo Nai exchanged a glance.","It was also at this time that they finally saw Dai Li, who had remained hidden inside the carriage all along.","The beautiful woman dressed in mountain-green took off her veiled hat. The afterglow of the setting sun shone in from outside, completely enveloping her gorgeous face. She looked like a glowing pearl radiating a soft halo, indescribably captivating.","As the two men stared in a daze, they also felt a sudden flash of realization.","So that was it. No wonder the Marquis of Wuan was so reluctant to leave.","Dinner was served in the main hall. The inn was not as particular as noble households, so they did not use individual dining tables for each person.","Everyone sat around large tables, though men and women were separated.","Qin Shaozong and Guo Nai shared a table. Dai Li sat with Shi Rongyue, while Qin Yanzhou and Qin Qinian sat at another table.","After the meal, just as Dai Li put down her chopsticks, the young man at the next table also set his chopsticks down.","\"Mother, I have something to discuss with you,\" Qin Yanzhou said in a low voice.","Dai Li's gaze swept over Guo Nai and the others not far away, and she stood up to head upstairs with Qin Yanzhou.","The second and third floors were entirely their rooms. At this moment, the stairs were empty, so Dai Li asked, \"Zhou Zhou, what is it?\"","Qin Yanzhou: \"Mom, let's talk when we get back to the room.\"","Dai Li raised an eyebrow. \"Being all mysterious and keeping me in suspense, are we?\"","Once they reached the third floor and she followed her son into his room, before Dai Li could even ask, Qin Yanzhou said, \"Mom, I want to beg you to promise me something.\""]},{"number":143,"title":"Chapter 143","paragraphs":["Dai Li froze. Her son's tone was much more solemn than usual; Zhou Zhou rarely spoke to her like this.","Along with her curiosity, a sudden, inexplicable sense of unease crept into her heart.","Dai Li didn't agree immediately. Instead, she raised a hand to tuck a stray strand of hair behind her ear. After a brief moment of thought, she asked with a smile, \"What is it that has made you so serious? Let me state beforehand, if it's something major, I can't just agree to it right away.\"","Qin Yanzhou lowered his eyes. \"Mom, I heard that on our journey south, we will lose the other imperial edict due to a bandit attack.\"","Dai Li wasn't surprised that he knew about this; there were simply too many channels of information. Qin Changgeng himself was one, Nalan Zhi, who was Zhou Zhou's master, was another, not to mention the gossip among the military officers.","\"Yes, that's the plan,\" Dai Li nodded.","\"They say there really is a group of bandits in the Yan and Ji provinces, it's not a fabrication,\" Qin Yanzhou finished the rest in one breath. \"After encountering the mountain bandits, there will inevitably be an operation to eradicate them. Mom, I want to join the soldiers in the troops to wipe out the bandits.\"","Dai Li's heart suddenly trembled. The words \"wipe out the bandits\" seemed to be infinitely magnified, echoing so loudly that her mind went blank for a moment.","And after that blankness, she seemed to envision a scene of flashing swords, glinting steel, and flying blood and flesh.","\"No!\" Dai Li refused immediately. \"The mountain bandits are familiar with the terrain. They know exactly where every ravine and steep slope is. It's too dangerous!\"","\"The three hundred soldiers of the Qin clan are all elites. In terms of skill, they outmatch those outlaws by an unknown measure; the enemy only has a geographical advantage at best. But I figure that before launching an attack, scouts will definitely be sent out to assess the situation, so their geographical advantage isn't actually that absolute,\" Qin Yanzhou stated firmly.","As he continued, his tone softened slightly. \"Mom, the Qin clan has helped me a lot along the way, and I remember all of it. Now, it's just a small bandit suppression operation. If the other soldiers can go, why can't I? I am just like them.\"","\"It's not the same!\" Dai Li stared fixedly at the young man in front of her, repeating, \"Zhou Zhou, you are not like them. Whatever we owe the Qin clan, whatever we owe Qin Changgeng, I can pay it back—with grain or anything else. There's no need for you to risk your life.\"","\"But Mom, I've grown up. I can be your backing now. I shouldn't and cannot continue hiding behind you like a coward.\" Qin Yanzhou twitched the corners of his mouth, revealing a forced smile.","Dai Li lowered her eyelashes, her gaze falling on his heavily scarred hands. Her eyes grew hot. \"Zhou Zhou, making a name for yourself, going down in history... those are not what Mom expects of you. You've suffered enough in the past ten years. I just want my son to be healthy, safe, and happy from now on. Nothing else matters.\"","In the era of cold weapons, there were no antibiotics. Once an infection occurred, it basically meant having one foot in the grave.","If a wound wasn't cleaned properly, localized tissue necrosis could occur, and in more severe cases, amputation wasn't impossible.","Noticing her gaze, Qin Yanzhou subconsciously hid his hands in his sleeves and said with feigned lightness, \"You have more than one son now. If Qin Qinian can go, I want to go too.\"","Dai Li's tears were dried up by her anger at him. She turned her head away. \"No. In short, I do not agree to you going to the front lines.\"","\"Mom...\"","A gentle tug came from her sleeve, and this single action instantly dragged Dai Li back to the past.","For Qin Yanzhou, the events of the modern world were ten years ago and had become very distant. But for Dai Li, it wasn't so. Those scenes were just over a year ago, and the figure of that little boy had not yet faded away.","In the past, whenever her son had a request—whether he wanted to buy an extracurricular book, eat a certain snack, or go to the old professor's house next door to pet the dog—he would gently pull on the corner of her clothes and look at her with eager eyes.","This trick worked very well; it was almost foolproof.","Dai Li's eyelashes fluttered slightly. She didn't turn her head, trying hard to restrain herself from looking and from softening her heart. \"No means no. There is no room for discussion on this!\"","As soon as she finished speaking, her sleeve was gently tugged again.","\"Mom, I have martial arts skills. I managed to survive perfectly fine fighting alone in the past. Now that I have three hundred comrades by my side, for what is merely an insignificant bandit suppression, how could anything go wrong? Please believe in me.\"","These words were spoken very solemnly. Even though Dai Li didn't turn her head, she could imagine the seriousness on her son's face.","Dai Li put her hands behind her back, withdrawing the corner of her clothes that was being tugged, and only then did she look back at Qin Yanzhou. \"Zhou Zhou, the medical care in this era is very primitive. The weapons used by those bandits are unclean, and it's hard to guarantee they aren't covered in dangerous bacteria. What if you get hurt somewhere and end up dying from an infection, or lose an arm or a leg...\"","The tears she had just barely held back filled her eyes once again. Dai Li grew more emotional as she spoke. \"I finally found you. If... if something like that really happens, it means I would lose my son again in less than a year. Have you ever thought about how I would feel? What would you have Mom do then?\"","Qin Yanzhou was stunned by her tearful eyes. He opened his mouth but couldn't utter a single word.","Dai Li's expression suddenly shifted, revealing a hint of fierceness. \"Did Qin Changgeng put you up to this? Did he give you some kind of hint? Is that why you want to join the army?!\"","\"No,\" Qin Yanzhou shook his head.","Dai Li wanted to say more, but she saw the young man in front of her, who had already grown much taller than her, suddenly lift his robes and kneel down.","Her dark pupils abruptly contracted.","\"I've had the thought of joining the army for a long time, even before you married him.\" The young man looked up at Dai Li, his height completely reverting to what it was ten years ago.","There was pleading in his eyes. \"I want you to be proud of me. I want those ignorant outsiders to know that you have more to rely on than just the Marquis of Wu'an, and I want to prove that I am not useless. A lifetime is so long; I cannot spend it living incompetently under your protection forever. That is not what I desire...\"","With that, he bent his spine, and his forehead heavily struck the ground.","Dai Li felt as if she had been bitten by a snake, stumbling back a step unsteadily. And that venomous snake that bit her slyly slithered into her head, roaming wildly inside, giving her a splitting headache. \"Qin Yanzhou, get up!\"","Qin Yanzhou merely lifted his head, but did not rise.","Dai Li heard footsteps outside the corridor; it must be the others returning after having their evening meal.","Dai Li cast a tearful glance at her son, who was still kneeling on the floor, before silently opening the door and leaving.","Only when Dai Li's footsteps faded away did Qin Yanzhou rise from the ground. This was his guest room. Now that dinner was over, he could normally stay in his room for the rest of the evening.","However, Qin Yanzhou went out.","The entire third floor consisted of guest rooms for the people of the Northern Lands. Qin Yanzhou had just stepped out and barely walked a few steps when he saw Shi Rongyue turning the corner from the stairs.","The two walked toward each other.","\"Brother Chongle,\" Shi Rongyue smiled and greeted Qin Yanzhou.","Ever since Dai Li and Qin Shaozong had married, she had dropped her previous address of \"Young Master Qin\" and started calling him Brother Chongle.","Qin Yanzhou stopped in his tracks. \"Rongrong, I have a favor to ask of you.\"","The young girl's light brown, round eyes blinked, a bright gleam rising from the depths of her gaze. \"No problem!\"","Qin Yanzhou was slightly taken aback. \"I haven't even told you what it is yet.\"","Shi Rongyue realized this belatedly. Her gaze drifted to the side in a guilty conscience, while she reached out a slender finger to gently scratch her cheek. \"I... I just think that since it's a rare occasion for Brother Chongle to ask me for a favor, given our friendship, I absolutely cannot refuse. So just tell me what it is.\"","Qin Yanzhou shook his head. \"This matter is of great importance, and you must consider it seriously. This is not the place to talk. Come with me.\"","Qin Yanzhou originally wanted to take Shi Rongyue downstairs to the courtyard of the inn. This inn was designed in a square shape, with the guest rooms on all sides facing outward. Looking down from the current corridor, one could see the central courtyard below.","He had good eyesight and saw a few imperial soldiers chatting idly down there.","The young man stopped in his tracks.","\"Brother Chongle?\" Shi Rongyue was confused.","Qin Yanzhou turned to look at her. \"There are quite a few imperial people in the courtyard below, so it is inconvenient to talk. Rongrong, would you mind coming to my room?\"","Shi Rongyue hurriedly shook her head. \"I don't mind.\"","Qin Yanzhou nodded and walked back. In a place he couldn't see, the young girl behind him couldn't help but reveal a big smile, and then happily followed him.","Several rooms in a row on the third floor were the highest-grade guest rooms, and their layouts were exactly the same. But after coming in, Shi Rongyue still couldn't help but secretly look around.","Before dinner, the owner of the room must have stayed in the room briefly, as some traces could be seen left inside.","A sheathed long sword was placed on the desk; his clothes box was placed at the end of the bed, and a dark blue robe was folded a few times into a rough square before being placed on top.","Shi Rongyue had two full brothers, and she had been to their rooms before. The only feeling she had then was that it was a mess, and she despised their inability to take care of themselves without servants.","She withdrew her gaze and curled her lips slightly in an imperceptible manner.","Since the visitor was a guest, Qin Yanzhou used a fire starter to ignite the small stove, heating the warm water inside slightly for later tea brewing.","Shi Rongyue sat down opposite the desk, placed her hands on her knees, kept her back straight, and said very seriously, \"Brother Chongle, generally speaking, I would directly agree to you. But if it really is as you said before that 'this matter is of great importance' and requires a great deal of effort from me, I will still agree to you, but after it is done, please do me a small favor, brother.\"","The water soon boiled, and the teapot steamed with heat. Qin Yanzhou took a handful of tea leaves and put them into the clay bowl. The tightly furled tea leaves slowly unfurled in the hot water, tinting the water with the color of tea.","Through the rising hot mist, the young man's handsome features seemed to be coated with a layer of soft water color, making him less aloof than usual, like ice and snow melting and spring returning to the earth.","As if sensing her gaze, or perhaps intending to ask her anyway, he looked up. His eyes were like black agate soaked in a mountain spring, dark and shiny, with their brilliance restrained in the fading twilight of the dusk.","Shi Rongyue's hands on her knees subconsciously tightened, crumpling her dress.","He asked, \"What favor?\"","Shi Rongyue stuttered a bit, \"I... I just want to keep a puppy. That time we went to the market and passed by a stall selling dogs, I saw you, Brother Chongle, glancing at it several times, so I guessed that you must know how to pick a puppy. So I want you to help me pick one after we return to Yuyang.\"","As she spoke, Shi Rongyue swayed slightly from side to side in delight, and her stray lock of hair swayed with the little girl's movements. \"Oh, right, I want a white dog, preferably with dark eyes, as beautiful as jade.\"","Qin Yanzhou fell silent for a moment.","\"I actually don't know much about picking, but I can ask others.\"","\"That's my only request, nothing else. Brother Chongle, what do you want to ask of me?\"","The two voices overlapped, one slow and the other fast. The former was hoarse with hesitation, and the latter was soft and full of vitality.","The tea water boiled. Qin Yanzhou took a cup and poured tea, first for Shi Rongyue, and then said, \"In a while, there will be a bandit suppression operation. I want to join the other soldiers in eliminating the harm for the people, but my mother is worried that I might get hurt and won't let me go into battle. Rongrong, you ride in the same carriage with my mother during the day, and she mentioned to me before that she gets along quite well with you, so I want to ask you to try and persuade her.\"","Shi Rongyue held the teacup in both hands, her mouth slightly open in surprise.","Seeing her completely stunned, Qin Yanzhou lowered his eyes. \"Is it very difficult? If...\"","\"Did Second Aunt really tell you that she feels a connection with me?\" Shi Rongyue's eyes were bright, as if an invisible tail was wagging behind her. \"That's wonderful!\"","This time it was Qin Yanzhou's turn to be stunned.","Realizing that she was being too expressive, Shi Rongyue coughed lightly. \"No problem, I will talk to her. But I can't guarantee the result.\"","Her voice lowered towards the end, because Shi Rongyue had realized by now that perhaps he had already mentioned this matter to Dai Li beforehand, but failed, which was why he resorted to a roundabout tactic.","\"That is natural. No matter the result, I will give you a little white dog after we return to Yuyang,\" Qin Yanzhou promised.","Shi Rongyue suddenly raised her hands to cover her face.","\"Rongrong?\" Qin Yanzhou was confused.","The little girl's hands moved down a little, revealing only a pair of big eyes smiling like crescents. \"It's nothing, I'm just so happy, hehe.\"","Qin Yanzhou instructed further, \"The matter regarding the bandits must not be known to the imperial people.\"","Shi Rongyue nodded profusely. \"I understand.\"","*","Shi Rongyue walked out of Qin Yanzhou's room with brisk steps. Before she could unabashedly reveal a smile, she suddenly saw Qin Shaozong approaching from not far away.","The two were not far apart, only a few steps away.","Shi Rongyue was caught right as she came out, and even her expression was completely seen by Qin Shaozong.","The little girl stiffened and hurriedly put on a serious face. \"Second Uncle.\"","Qin Shaozong's gaze glanced at the tightly closed door behind her, and he said meaningfully, \"What happy event has made Rongrong so delighted?\"","Shi Rongyue kept her eyes lowered and said, \"It's my first time traveling far from home, so it's very novel.\"","Qin Shaozong chuckled softly but said nothing else, passing by her and heading straight to his room.","Shi Rongyue turned slightly to steal a glance at the tall figure walking away, doubt in her eyes.","Was it her illusion? She felt that Second Uncle seemed to be in a quite good mood.","...","\"Creak.\" The door was pushed open.","The last ray of twilight had faded just now. There were no lights in the room, and the tide-like dimness stretched endlessly, inexplicably giving rise to a sense of oppression.","Qin Shaozong swept his gaze and accurately caught the beautiful silhouette from the dark tide.","She stood by the window, facing outward with her back to the inside, her expression unseen.","\"Why hasn't my wife lit the lamps?\" Qin Shaozong took out a fire starter and lit the lamps in the room one by one.","As the firelight grew brighter, the room was filled with warm brightness, and her emerald cross-collared dress lost a bit of its unapproachable solemnity.","However, when the woman by the window turned her head, the coldness that had just melted away once again covered her beautiful profile. \"Qin Changgeng, would you lie to me?\"","This voice was extremely gentle, carrying an indescribable dependence, like being coated in a circle of charming honey.","Qin Shaozong's footsteps stopped abruptly. For some inexplicable reason, his back subconsciously tensed up at this moment."]},{"number":144,"title":"Chapter 144","paragraphs":["Qin Shaozong quickly thought of the scene downstairs just now.","After his wife finished her dinner and set down her bowls and chopsticks, the young man had taken the initiative to approach her. The tables weren't set very far apart at the time, and coupled with his excellent hearing, he clearly heard the kid tell her he had something to discuss.","Connecting this to her current strange behavior, he felt that the kid, Qin the Second, had nine times out of ten told her about his desire to join the army.","To report this on the very first day out of the city, Qin Shaozong was somewhat surprised by Qin Yanzhou's impatience, but thinking about it carefully, it wasn't incomprehensible. It meant that his wife was firmly against it, which was why Qin the Second needed more time to persuade her.","However, for her to catch him and interrogate him the moment he returned was indeed beyond his expectations.","But this fox had always been full of schemes; perhaps she had figured something out on her own...","His thoughts took a few turns, but Qin Shaozong's face remained impassive. He didn't directly answer Dai Li's question, but asked in return, \"My lady, that is a strange question. We have known each other for so long; when have I ever lied to you in the past?\"","Dai Li, standing by the window, turned completely around. The candlelight fell upon her face, giving it a jade-like coldness and aloofness. She looked at the man a few steps away, scrutiny in her eyes.","The man, on the other hand, was calm and composed, as if he knew nothing.","Dai Li scoffed coldly. \"Just now, Zhou Zhou told me he wants to join the army and go exterminate bandits with the other soldiers. Qin Changgeng, did you secretly push for this?\"","\"It might have something to do with me, or it might not,\" Qin Shaozong said.","Dai Li laughed out of anger at his words. \"If you did, you did; if you didn't, you didn't. Stop playing games with me here. Being so vague, it seems...\"","\"My lady, there are some things I haven't told you. Actually, before coming south, Qin the Second told me he wanted to establish himself and requested to go to the front lines.\" Qin Shaozong stepped forward and reached out to pull her into his arms, but just as he moved, his hand was slapped away.","The man helplessly retracted his hand. \"I asked the kid at the time whether the agreement you and I signed was with him.\"","Hearing him take the initiative to mention the Divorce Agreement, Dai Li shot him a sideways glance, remaining silent to listen to what he had to say next.","Qin Shaozong continued, \"After signing the agreement back then, you immediately went out with it. I thought it over and felt that you would most likely give it to Qin the Second for safekeeping. Later, exactly as I expected, the kid admitted to it. I then asked if he had read the agreement, and he said he had.\"","Dai Li pursed her lips.","\"Although my Qin family has guarded the borders for generations, and aside from those with weak constitutions like Yunce, most in the clan start going into battle in their early teens. Qin Yanzhou is now my son, and to tell you the truth, my lady, I do hope he can make a name for himself on the battlefield and become a true, indomitable man, rather than a useless dandy who can only rely on his mother for the rest of his life.\"","Qin Shaozong sighed. \"But how could I forget the agreement we signed earlier? I knew in my heart that you definitely wouldn't be happy about it, so at the time, I specifically brought up the third clause of the agreement with Qin the Second, and upon hearing it, the kid said he would persuade you himself.\"","Having mentioned it a few times, he always vaguely referred to it as the agreement, avoiding the first two words.","Dai Li looked at Qin Shaozong suspiciously.","What this man said sounded quite plausible. Could it be that she had guessed wrong? Could it be that in this matter, Qin Changgeng was merely a triggered participant from start to finish?","If that was truly the case, then what he said earlier wasn't false, and the main responsibility couldn't be pinned on him.","But she still felt like something wasn't quite right.","\"I guarantee upon my title as Marquis that there is absolutely not a single lie in what I just said,\" Qin Shaozong finally added.","Dai Li's expression shifted slightly. She still didn't speak, but the coldness between her brows faded considerably.","Qin Shaozong reached out to embrace her, and this time, his hand wasn't slapped away. He smiled and guided Dai Li toward the bed. \"Today's journey was exhausting, and we have to continue traveling tomorrow. My lady, let's rest early.\"","This was the best suite in the inn, much larger than the ordinary rooms. There was some distance from the window to the bed, and they had to pass by a desk holding a candlestick.","The candlelight cast two overlapping dark shadows. As the movers' robes fluttered, the edges of the shadows became erratic. For a moment, they looked like agile flowing water, or perhaps a black sack that could be pulled in any direction.","Dai Li suddenly stopped in her tracks.","\"My lady?\" Qin Shaozong turned his head.","Dai Li stared at him. \"You just said that Zhou Zhou told you he wanted to make a name for himself. Where did he say this?\"","Qin Shaozong: \"The study.\"","\"Did he go looking for you himself, or did you have someone call him over?\" Dai Li asked again.","Qin Shaozong paused, realizing she wasn't just asking casually. And it was this exact pause that allowed the little seed of doubt that had been making Dai Li feel uneasy to quickly take root and sprout.","\"You had someone look for Zhou Zhou, didn't you?\" She looked at him.","It was a question, and her tone carried heavy doubt, but there wasn't much uncertainty in those perfectly shaped peach-blossom eyes.","Qin Shaozong just opened his mouth to speak, but she was a beat faster than him.","\"You can deny it and say no right now, but as long as something has been done, it will inevitably leave traces. For example, the soldier who ran the errand to pass on your message, or the guards stationed at the door of the study, they can all testify. I think a few soldiers in the convoy look quite familiar; they are probably the guards from around the study earlier. It's not particularly late right now, and asking a few questions won't take much time. Why don't we call them up and ask them one by one, what do you think, husband?\" Dai Li said with a smile.","Her voice was extremely soft, like the murmuring flow of a warm hot spring. At this moment, a cool breeze blew in from the open window, making the candle flame on the desk sway slightly.","The flickering candlelight reflected on her smiling face, possessing a dizzying, magnificent beauty like a peony blooming to its absolute peak.","A current of electricity seemed to rise from Qin Shaozong's tailbone, stirring up waves of numbness wherever it passed. Without saying whether it was a good idea or not, his expression remained very calm: \"My lady doesn't believe what I just said? Even though I told you I guaranteed it with my title as Marquis.\"","Dai Li, however, said, \"Qin Changgeng, let me tell you a story first. A home invasion murder occurred in a certain place. When the patrol arrived, they ran into a man in front of the residence and asked if he had seen the killer. The man said he heard the killer and the homeowner arguing over a debt, and claimed that the perpetrator was wearing brown short clothes and a white headband. However, because his position was wrong, he didn't see the killer's face clearly. At the time, that man raised his hand and swore, vowing confidently that he absolutely wasn't lying, or else he would never strike it rich in this life and everything would go wrong for him.\"","The electric current climbing up his spine seemed to instantly intensify. The muscles beneath his robes tightened uncontrollably, trembling with irrepressible excitement.","\"After multiple verifications, this person indeed did not lie, but standing in front of the house, he, the most suspicious one, is also indeed the murderer. Everything he described is correct, only he blurred out the key parts or inverted the information. He said he heard the argument between the murderer and the homeowner; as one of the main parties in the argument, of course he could hear it. His claim that 'because the position was wrong, he did not see the murderer's face clearly' was naturally not a lie either. After all, eyes grow on the face, and since he wasn't standing in front of a bronze mirror, how could he see his own full appearance?\" Dai Li said.","In later generations, this kind of lie had a specific name, called a montage lie.","The word \"montage\" was originally a film term. And turning truth into falsehood through editing and blurring the sequence is called a montage lie.","\"Just now, you never answered me directly whether you were the one who sent people to look for Zhou Zhou. I think it's highly likely, and later you said he wanted to establish merits and build a career, requesting to go into battle...\" Dai Li sneered, the gentleness on her face like a spring breeze instantly dissipating without a trace. \"Before this, you must have guided Zhou Zhou, right? You started this, didn't you?\"","Qin Shaozong did not speak, only looking unblinkingly at Dai Li. The flickering candlelight gathered in the depths of his eyes, seemingly condensing into a dazzlingly bright color.","As bright as glazed amber, and as scorching as fire.","\"As for what you said at the beginning, mentioning the agreement when you were talking with Zhou Zhou, it was absolutely not to reassure me, but to hint to him at that time, making him come to find me on his own.\" The fire in Dai Li's heart flared up wildly.","Seeing the man in front of her remain silent, especially with this unrepentant look in his eyes, Dai Li was so angry that her fingertips were trembling. \"Qin Changgeng, you treat my words like wind past your ears, don't you? Since you broke the contract first, there is no need to continue living this life together. I won't be your Marquis's wife, and I won't go to Chang'an to receive the conferment...\"","Before she could finish her words, she was suddenly enveloped in an embrace.","An extremely aggressive wave of hormones rushed over her, like the weapons of a long-fought battlefield, and also like boiling wine. Dai Li was a head shorter than Qin Shaozong, and her skeletal frame was far less robust than his. Now held by him, she couldn't move at all.","Qin Shaozong raised his hand and stroked Dai Li's back, again and again, as if soothing a bristling little animal. \"Madam, there is a reason for this.\"","\"Still trying to quibble? Let go of me!\" Dai Li didn't want to listen to his nonsense.","Qin Shaozong carried her to the bed, letting Dai Li be on the inside and him on the outside, blocking her way out. \"Madam, Qin the Second wants to establish merits and build a career, there is no need to doubt this. If he didn't want to go into battle himself, could I point a silver spear at his back and force him up?\"","Dai Li was still wearing her curved-toe shoes. The shoes were new, and she had spent most of the day in the carriage. The dirtiest path she had walked was just from the carriage into this posthouse, so the soles didn't have much dust on them.","Even so, when she was carried onto the bed, Dai Li still subconsciously lifted her feet to avoid dirtying the bedding.","Qin Shaozong's words fell on her ears like pouring oil on a fire. Originally having nowhere to put her feet, coupled with the fire raging high in her heart, in a fit of anger, Dai Li pressed her foot against his hand and kicked him outward. \"Utter nonsense!\"","Qin Shaozong opened his palm, cupping the sole of her shoe, then slightly tightened his grip, making the curved-toe shoe narrower and longer, and then took the opportunity to take it off.","\"Madam, Qin the Second has now reached adulthood and is a grown man. He has his own ambitions and plans for the future. As parents, we cannot always keep our children confined by our sides. If a young eagle doesn't spread its wings on its own for a day, it will never be able to shake off the word 'young'.\" He directly threw her shoe to a place she couldn't reach.","Dai Li was so angry at his action of throwing the shoe that her brain buzzed. He threw away the left one, so she used her right foot to step on him.","The curved-toe shoe stomped on the man's arm, leaving a shallow footprint on his black robe. Dai Li angrily rebuked, \"Nonsense! Qin Changgeng, stop secretly swapping concepts here. When did I confine him by my side? I just don't want him to go take other people's blades.\"","After taking a kick, Qin Shaozong remained completely unmoved and continued to help Dai Li take off the other shoe. \"Madam, Qin Yanzhou's skills are not weak. That time he sneaked into the mansion alone to find you, he even fought back and forth with Bai Jianping. He has reached adulthood; he is no longer that nine-year-old child. You should believe in him.\"","Dai Li didn't listen. She wanted to get off the bed to pick up her shoes, but just as she moved to the edge of the bed, Qin Shaozong scooped her back by the waist.","\"Qin Changgeng, you bastard! Not only did you break the contract, but you also tried to deceive me with a mouth full of nonsense. I can't live like this anymore. I want to divorce you.\" Dai Li pinched the flesh on his arm.","Whether it was from her pinching or stung by the last sentence, the man's arm suddenly tensed, his muscles as hard as a rock.","He couldn't stand hearing those two words. His fairly stable emotions were instantly shattered. \"What divorce? Which clause on it did I violate? Madam, take out the agreement and point it out to me.\"","Dai Li's eyes widened slightly. This man actually had the nerve to ask her for the agreement! Being away from home, how could she possibly carry such an important document with her?","\"You are at least a Marquis officially conferred by the imperial court. How do you have the nerve to act like a rogue?\" Dai Li gritted her teeth.","Qin Shaozong curled his thin lips. \"A lifetime is so long, one can't always stick to just one identity.\"","\"Move away, I want to go out.\" Dai Li raised her hand and pushed him.","Qin Shaozong took the opportunity to hold her hand. \"It's getting late, and everyone else has already gone to sleep. There is no one outside to listen to your orders. Where are you going, Madam?\"","Dai Li was expressionless. \"I won't trouble anyone else. I'll walk back to Yuyang myself to get the 'Divorce Agreement'.\"","The curve on Qin Shaozong's lips gradually disappeared: \"...\"","The two looked at each other. Qin Shaozong saw raging flames in her eyes, while Dai Li saw his unyielding determination.","\"Qin Changgeng, you are really a jerk.\" Dai Li withdrew the hand he was holding, grabbed a brocade pillow, and smashed it over. \"Only one person can stay in this room tonight. Either you go out or I go out!\"","Qin Shaozong caught the pillow in one fell swoop. Seeing her face covered in frost, he said helplessly, \"Madam, the guest rooms on the third floor are already full, and there are people from the imperial court staying on the second floor. You and I are currently in our honeymoon period. If I go out at this time, it will inevitably arouse suspicion from others.\"","Hearing him say \"in our honeymoon period,\" Dai Li couldn't help but sneer coldly. Daring to pull this kind of stunt right after their wedding, did he think she was easy to bully?","\"If you can't go down to the second floor, then I'll trouble the Marquis to squeeze in with the other military generals on the third floor. Anyway, you are their superior. If you tell them to open the door, would they dare to disobey your order? As for your pride, didn't the Marquis just say that changing identities to play the rogue isn't bad?\" Dai Li suggested coldly.","Qin Shaozong: \"...\"","He raised his hand, wanting to hold that soft hand again, but she avoided it. Just now Dai Li couldn't get off the bed, so now she simply didn't try. Hugging another brocade pillow, she shrank inward, refusing to let him touch her.","Dai Li retreated to the inside, clearing a space on the outer part of the bed.","Qin Shaozong glanced at it, itching to move; in the past, this was where he slept. But before he could take advantage of the situation and sit on it, a quilt flew out from the inside. If Qin Shaozong hadn't been quick-eyed and deft-handed to roll it up, his head would likely have been covered by it.","\"Get out,\" Dai Li glared at him.","Qin Shaozong held a pillow in one hand and a blanket in the other. \"Madam...\"","Dai Li simply lay down and rolled over, turning her back to him to cut off any further communication.","Qin Shaozong stared at the empty space beside her on the bed. After a long moment of internal struggle, he finally let out a soft click of his tongue and refrained from climbing in.","However, the man didn't leave the guest room with his blanket and pillow, either. He scanned the room and eventually walked over to the only daybed available.","The small daybed was originally designed for guests to recline and relax on, but now it had to serve as Qin Shaozong's bed.","When the tall, broadly built man lay down on it, the piece of furniture looked pitifully small. It wasn't even as long as he was tall, leaving his lower legs dangling over the edge.","Lying on the cramped daybed, Qin Shaozong stared up at the ceiling. With his arms completely empty, he felt thoroughly uncomfortable.","Tsk, that brat Qin Yanzhou really was useless at getting things done."]},{"number":145,"title":"Chapter 145","paragraphs":["\"Hey Lao Feng, don't you think the Lord's mood is quite bad today?\"","\"More than just bad, it's absolutely terrible. I just saw Lao Mo get scolded. Even though Lao Mo was a bit reckless just now, given the Lord's usual demeanor, he would at most glare at him. He wouldn't have a tongue dipped in poison like he did just now.\"","\"So what exactly happened to make the Lord's mood plummet from the mountain peak to the gutter in just one night? Could it be those two court officials causing trouble?\"","\"Impossible, mere bookworms aren't worth mentioning.\"","...","Lao Feng and Bai Jianping huddled together, muttering to each other, but despite their long discussion, they couldn't figure out the reason.","After breakfast, the group set off again.","During this time, Dai Li didn't say a single word to Qin Shaozong, nor did she look him in the eye. Once she was full, she boarded the carriage with Shi Rongyue.","Qin Shaozong, on the other hand, glanced at Dai Li several times. Once, he even tried to step forward to speak with her, but Dai Li noticed and pulled Shi Rongyue away to avoid him.","Lao Feng and the others, observing secretly, suddenly realized the truth: the Lord and the Mistress were having a conflict.","No, or rather, it seemed the Lord had angered the Mistress.","Shi Rongyue had also picked up on this signal.","The young girl followed Dai Li into the carriage. When Dai Li wasn't looking, she tugged at her skirt with a worried expression.","Second Aunt is in a bad mood; now is not a good time. I don't know when the bandit suppression operation will take place, but I hope it won't be too soon...","\"Rongrong?\"","Shi Rongyue shivered and subconsciously straightened her back, calling out, \"Here!\" Realizing she had overreacted, her earlobes turned red with a mix of guilt and shyness.","Dai Li, who had been in a foul mood this morning after being overtly and covertly bothered by Qin Shaozong, now smiled. \"What were you thinking about just now? Did Rongrong have a sweet dream last night and was just reminiscing?\"","Shi Rongyue said dryly, \"I guess so. But I don't remember the details, I just vaguely feel it was wonderful.\"","\"Dreams really aren't easy to remember clearly,\" Dai Li agreed deeply.","The carriage began to move, passing through the small county town's morning market. The shouts of vendors and the haggling of pedestrians drifted in from outside the curtains, full of the lively atmosphere of everyday life.","Dai Li lifted a corner of the curtain. The spring morning breeze blew in, carrying a refreshing coolness that swept away the rest of her irritation.","Shi Rongyue sighed in admiration, \"How wonderful!\"","Hearing her, Dai Li turned her head. In the sunlight streaming into the carriage, the fine peach fuzz on the young girl's cheeks was clearly visible, and the orange hair ribbon on her head curled slightly in the wind. At this moment, her large eyes crinkled contentedly, looking like a melted orange cat pancake basking in the sun.","\"Rongrong, is this your first time traveling far from home?\" Dai Li asked with a smile.","\"The furthest place I've been to before is Yuyang. If we don't count Yuyang, then yes!\" Shi Rongyue answered honestly.","\"This trip to Chang'an will take at least two or three months round trip. Plus, you arrived in Yuyang in the autumn, so you'll be away from home for at least half a year. Will Rongrong be homesick?\" Dai Li teased her on purpose. \"If you secretly cry in bed at night, I'll have no choice but to send someone to rush you back to Hongying on horseback.\"","Shi Rongyue's words, \"I do miss it a little bit,\" got stuck in her throat. She hurriedly said, \"I won't cry. I've had my coming-of-age ceremony, and after that, a young lady can leave home. I can't always cling to my mother, otherwise, I wouldn't feel right about it either.\"","Dai Li was dazed for a moment. \"How could that be?\"","Shi Rongyue suddenly realized something. Pretending to tuck her hair behind her ear, she pinched her earlobe, striving to calm herself. \"Growing up means having the tasks and responsibilities of an adult; I can't let my parents toil for me my whole life.\"","Dai Li snapped back to reality, slowly lowered her eyes, and didn't reply to that.","Shi Rongyue was anxious on the inside, but since Dai Li didn't speak, she couldn't rashly continue.","She could only wait helplessly.","However, until the carriage drove out of the county town, Shi Rongyue couldn't find another opportunity. The little torch in her heart grew dimmer and dimmer, until it finally went out with a poof.","Shi Rongyue: \"...\" Boohoo.","*","Over the next six days, the group's itinerary was managed exceptionally well. They departed in the morning and accurately settled in a township or village when the sun set in the west.","The turning point occurred on the seventh day.","After leaving a certain small village, the next county town to the south was very far away. Even though the group was equipped with fine steeds, it was difficult to reach the destination in a single daylight period. Therefore, at dusk, the group halted in the wilderness.","Setting up camp always requires being near water, and large river channels in the north are much scarcer than in the south. Since great rivers were hard to find, they located a small river about ten feet wide and set up camp not far from it.","This expedition used an especially large number of carriages. In addition to ordinary luggage, there was a batch of carriages specifically used to transport the tents.","The tents were mostly made of leather and cloth brushed with tung oil to block the wind and rain. In rainy and humid seasons, wooden boards even needed to be laid underneath to prevent dampness.","However, spring rain is as precious as oil, so the step of laying wooden boards was skipped.","The soldiers were nimble, and soon tents were pitched one after another, forming a square. Shen Tianming, Guo Nai, and their men occupied one side of the square, while the others from the North occupied the other three sides.","Dai Li and Qin Shaozong slept in the same tent, with the main tent situated right in the center. Next door was the small tent of the brothers Qin Yanzhou and Qin Qinian, and on the other side was Shi Rongyue.","After dinner, Dai Li entered the tent to rest.","Over the past few days, she had spoken very little to Qin Shaozong, not saying a single extra word to him unless necessary. As for this necessity, there was only one situation: when the people from the imperial court happened to come over.","\"It's been several days, is Madam still angry?\" Qin Shaozong followed Dai Li into the tent.","Dai Li ignored him.","Qin Shaozong said helplessly, \"I was wrong before. I won't say those things to Qin the Second in the future, alright?\"","Dai Li couldn't hold back and scolded him, \"You've already said everything you shouldn't have. What's the use of promising me now?\"","Qin Shaozong suppressed the upward curve of his lips and didn't speak. Instead, he suddenly reached out and pinched Dai Li's waist. She completely hadn't expected this move.","Her waist was incredibly ticklish. Being pinched by him so unexpectedly, she couldn't maintain her serious expression and let out a laugh.","Dai Li: \"...\"","Qin Shaozong forcefully pulled her into his arms, rubbing his jaw against her cheek. \"How much anger is still left in Madam's stomach? Let me pinch again and see if you'll smile some more.\"","\"Qin Changgeng, you are so annoying.\" Dai Li swatted his hand.","They had set up a small tent, which couldn't compare to a private room in a relay station. The space was very small, only big enough for a soft cot. Thus, Qin Shaozong, who had slept on a small cot for six days, was finally able to sleep in a bed together.","Well, although this bed was very crude, Qin Shaozong didn't care at all.","As soon as he lay down, he closed his eyes and reached out his hand to the side. Once he scooped up that soft lump, he rolled her into his embrace, embedding her firmly in his arms, and then, not surprisingly, received a kick to his calf.","Qin Shaozong didn't even open his eyes. \"How does the old saying go? Couples fight at the head of the bed and make up at the foot of the bed. Since Madam is still burning with such anger, why don't we have a fight?\"","As he spoke, the large hand gripping her waist slid downwards suggestively.","Dai Li grabbed his rough palm. \"Stop messing around.\"","A small tent was even less soundproof than a room; if they made too much noise, the people next door would probably hear them. If she were to have a tryst with him in the tent tonight, Dai Li felt she would end up smothering Qin Changgeng to death with a pillow in the middle of the night, and then throw him into the river to destroy the evidence.","His well-defined fingers spread open and intertwined with hers. At the same time, his kisses fell on the tip of her ear one after another. \"It's been six days, Madam. We've already left Youzhou. Could you please let your anger go?\"","\"Go to sleep.\" Dai Li pulled the blanket up and covered his head.","...","Tonight, there were neither stars nor a bright moon. The sky above seemed to be covered by a heavy black veil. Crows flapped their wings and flew past, their ghost-like shadows completely blending into the darkness, leaving only their cawing to be heard without a trace of them to be seen.","The square campsite set up by the river was lit with fire pits and torches, resembling precious, glittering pearls in the dark night.","On the low eastern hills not far from the camp, there was a rustling movement.","\"The Marquis of Wu'an and his men have made camp. Looking at their formation, they have about three hundred men, more than twice our number.\"","\"Our main objective this time is to kill the imperial messengers. If the situation turns sour, retreat immediately. Do not drag out the fight.\"","\"Commander, there are only twenty or so imperial men. I'm afraid they will be difficult to distinguish...\"","\"It won't be hard. The imperial mole just sent word that they are stationed on the north side. As long as the imperial court suffers heavy casualties this time and most of their men die on the way back to Chang'an, it will be hard for the Marquis of Wu'an to avoid suspicion. After all, the North is his territory.\" The man sneered. \"Pass down the order: we move at the Yin hour. If anyone is captured alive, they must insist that they are greenwood outlaws and do not serve anyone.\"","The rustling sound slithered through the grass like a snake and quickly faded away.","Deng Qianfeng looked at the distant fires, his gaze dark and unreadable.","This was Jizhou territory, Qin Shaozong's domain. They couldn't mobilize too many soldiers here. No, more accurately, the men could come, but not their weapons.","Every city gate had patrols that inspected travelers' luggage. Weapons, especially fine swords and sabers that were obviously meant for combat, could not be brought through.","If discovered without the proper paperwork, not only would the weapons be confiscated, but the carrier would likely be thrown in prison.","Of course, bypassing the cities to avoid the gate inspections wasn't impossible. But when traveling, one always needed to eat, drink, and rest, and those supplies could only be found within the cities.","If they carried their own baggage and supplies, they could bypass the gates and penetrate deep into the North, but traveling with so many heavy bags carried a certain risk of being discovered by city patrols or real mountain bandits.","Therefore, even after planning this for a long time, they had only managed to bring in a little over a hundred men.","A cool breeze swept by, and the dark clouds in the sky shifted. The full moon briefly peeked out, only to hide back into the clouds at the end of the Chou hour.","Right at the Yin hour, the night was pitch black and the wind blew high.","A group of dark figures holding blades hunched over, lowering their bodies to hide in the grass as they advanced, rapidly closing the distance.","A bird whistle chirped twice, and a row of archers took their positions.","The bowstrings were pulled taut, emitting a creaking sound. With another drawn-out bird whistle, arrows rained down.","\"Ah—\"","...","Inside the tent.","Qin Yanzhou's eyes snapped open. He quickly grabbed the longsword resting by his pillow and flipped to his feet in a single bound.","At this moment, Qin Qinian, who was beside him, also woke up. \"What was that sound just now?\"","Almost as soon as his words fell, a loud shout came from outside:","\"Enemy attack! We're under attack!\"","\"Preposterous! To dare attack us while we're still in the North, they really don't know the meaning of death! Just you wait, brats, your daddy is coming to teach you a lesson right now.\" The furious youth didn't even bother tying up his hair before grabbing his sword and rushing out.","When Qin Qinian went out, the tent flap flew up, and Qin Yanzhou saw a steady stream of soldiers wielding weapons stepping out of their tents, clearly preparing to meet the enemy in battle.","Four words suddenly flashed through his mind: Execute first, report later."]},{"number":146,"title":"Chapter 146","paragraphs":["Dai Li jolted awake from her deep sleep. The clamor rushed into her ears like a tide. She heard someone shouting \"Enemy attack!\" followed by the continuous beating of gongs and drums. The silence of the night was like a shattered bronze mirror, every piece sharp enough to pierce the eardrums.","She instinctively hugged the quilt and sat up, turning her head toward the door curtain.","The tent was unlit. The curtains rolled up on both sides for ventilation let in a bit of firelight, though it wasn't bright, only illuminating the inside just enough to see beyond one's fingers. Thus, Dai Li saw a tall silhouette who had also sat up.","Qin Shaozong touched Dai Li's forehead. Finding no cold sweat, he still asked, Were you frightened, Madam?","There's an enemy attack. Could we have run into mountain bandits? Dai Li frowned, guessing.","It wasn't impossible. After all, they had many carriages, and at first glance, it indeed looked like the travel procession of wealthy merchants. In the eyes of bandits, wasn't this a guaranteed fat sheep?","Qin Shaozong got up unhurriedly. Mere bandits, what is there to fear? If we meet them, we meet them.","Dai Li's sleepiness completely vanished, and she also got up to dress. I don't know why, but I feel a bit uneasy.","Uneasy? With your husband here, how could petty thieves snatch you away? Qin Shaozong seemed to suddenly think of something, his eyes flashing. Why doesn't Madam stay in the tent and wait for good news.","Dai Li didn't stop dressing. I'd rather not. I'll go out with you to take a look.","Qin Shaozong paused slightly but said nothing.","After dressing neatly, the two stepped out of the tent together. Outside, the firelight blazed, illuminating the area as bright as day. Earlier in the tent, they had heard the clanging of gongs and drums, along with faint screams, but once they truly came out, the surroundings were not as chaotic as Dai Li had imagined.","The soldiers had poured out in full force, each holding a sharp blade, like wolves baring their sharp fangs, just waiting for the alpha's order to swarm forward.","The sound of clashing weapons came continuously from the north side of the square camp. Qin Shaozong took one look over there and laughed. A sneak attack from the north? They sure know how to pick a spot. Feng Feng, what's the situation now?","Qiao Wangfei and Wei Qing had already gone to assist. Bai Jianping stayed behind to guard the south, while Feng Feng waited outside the main tent for instructions.","Now called upon by his superior, he immediately replied, Visually, the attackers number no more than a hundred. They're likely some blind mounted bandits who learned a bit of amateur martial arts and came out to make trouble.","Qin Shaozong turned his thumb ring. A hundred or so men can be considered a fairly sizable bandit gang. Surprisingly, no news of them reached us beforehand. Leave a few alive, and try to save those useless sacks of wine and rice from the imperial court.","Feng Feng: Understood.","Hearing the north, Dai Li also looked over and, sure enough, saw that the north had fallen into chaos. People were raising their swords to hack and kill, the shiny blades reflecting a chilling light.","Second Uncle, Second Aunt...","Dai Li turned her head and saw Shi Rongyue with her hair down.","The little girl's face was pale. It was her first time encountering such a thing, and being young, she was still in shock.","It's cold at night. Why didn't Rongrong put on more clothes before coming out? Their tents were close to each other, so Dai Li simply ushered the girl back to where she came from. Don't worry. The enemy's numbers are far fewer than ours. Your Second Uncle will handle it.","Shi Rongyue was coaxed back inside by Dai Li.","Emerging from the little girl's tent, Dai Li suddenly shuddered.","With such a big commotion tonight, even Rongrong ran out. Why had there been no movement from Zhou Zhou and Qinian's side? Could it be...","Dai Li quickened her pace, bypassing the main tent and Qin Shaozong, who stood in front of it, and headed straight for the brothers' tent.","The door curtain of that tent fluttered slightly in the wind, obviously unfastened from the inside. Dai Li's heart skipped a beat. Restraining the urge to lift the curtain directly, she first called out, Zhou Zhou, Qinian.","No one answered from inside.","Her heart sank to the bottom. Dai Li abruptly lifted the curtain. The firelight shone in from both sides of her, climbing onto the empty soft couch inside.","No one!","Both brothers were gone.","The distant sounds of killing seemed to magnify infinitely at this moment, as if shaking the earth along with it. Otherwise, why would she feel so dizzy that she couldn't even stand steady?","An iron arm reached out from behind her side, scooping up Dai Li, who was about to collapse onto the ground. She heard a low, slightly surprised male voice close to her ear ask, Where did those two boys go?","...","Where do you petty thieves come from? Hand your lives over to your daddy! Qin Qinian raised his sword and hacked.","The man was startled. He hadn't expected someone to suddenly pop out while he was engaged in combat, coming at him so fiercely as if carrying the momentum of thousands of troops.","However, the opponent's self-cheering roar actually did him some good, serving at least as a warning.","The man quickly pulled another short sword from his lower back, turning the blade horizontally to block. Just as he was about to mock the young upstart for being too impulsive, his expression changed the moment the blades actually clashed.","It felt as if a tremendous weight had been added to his wrist. He was already fighting one-handed, and now defending with his left hand, he couldn't bear the force.","The blades crossed for merely two breaths before his short sword was sent flying by Qin Qinian.","Li Wu, I'm coming to help you! Seeing the situation turn grim, his companion, muscles bulging, cleanly dispatched a wounded imperial soldier and prepared to step forward.","Yet before he could take two steps, a chilling, scalp-numbing murderous intent wrapped around him like a snake, making the hairs on his back stand on end.","The man instinctively turned his head and raised his blade at the same time, but unfortunately, he was a beat too late. The viper's fangs had silently approached his throat. As the blade sliced cleanly through, a line of blood sprayed out like a fountain.","A heavy body fell straight down.","Qin Yanzhou's handsome face was as cold as ice, completely devoid of emotion. He didn't even spare a glance at the fallen corpse, nor did he flick the blood off his blade, before plunging into another fray like a wild beast.","While finishing off the burly man whose short sword he had knocked away, Qin Qinian kept a portion of his attention on Qin Yanzhou. Seeing this, his eyes lit up, and he chased after him with his blade. Qin... Second Brother, how about we compete? Let's see who claims the most heads in the end.","Qin Yanzhou shifted his gaze over there for a moment, said nothing, and continued reaping lives with his blade.","The young man's inner garments were black, blending into the night as if melting into an inconspicuous pool of ink. Stabbing, thrusting, hacking, retreating, and dodging were all done in one smooth motion, flowing like water. Wherever he passed, rolling objects continuously fell to the ground.","Toward the end of the slaughter, the circle of people around Qin Yanzhou, whether they were mountain bandits or from the imperial court, unconsciously avoided him.","Deng Qianfeng had previously given orders to mainly attack the imperial soldiers and kill them if possible. The first wave of the night raid was a rain of arrows, taking down the outermost soldiers. By the time they reacted, the attackers had already penetrated a good distance under the cover of night.","But this fierce offensive didn't last long. With the arrival of reinforcements from the northern territory, the situation quickly reversed.","It's not a merchant caravan, retreat first! someone roared out of nowhere.","The attackers fought as they retreated, attempting to flee. But having suffered a silent loss, the imperial forces, seeing the northern reinforcements, couldn't swallow this insult. They immediately called out to their companions to give relentless chase.","After taking down several people in a row, Qin Yanzhou paused upon hearing the order to pursue the enemy. He finally lowered the blade in his hand and did not follow the others.","Qin Qinian originally wanted to follow Qiao Wangfei and the others in pursuit, but out of the corner of his eye, he caught sight of Qin Yanzhou stopping. He abruptly changed direction and stood before the young man. \"Right now, we are strong and the enemy is weak. The situation is greatly in our favor. Why aren't you pursuing them?\"","Qin Yanzhou shook his head. \"No, this is enough.\"","Qin Qinian didn't understand. The youth frowned. \"The invading enemies haven't even been annihilated, how can you say it's enough? Let's go. Brothers fight together on the battlefield, come with me to kill the enemy.\"","Qin Yanzhou, however, simply sheathed his blade and turned around without a word.","\"Second Brother, what are you doing?\" Qin Qinian was dumbfounded. He watched as the other man walked toward a nearby tent and picked up a bundle from a corner of the small tent.","Qin Qinian: \"?\"","He watched the young man, whose sword was sheathed, first lower his head and spread his arms as if inspecting himself. Only after confirming everything was fine did he open the bundle and take out a white robe he usually wore.","He shook out the white robe and slowly put it on, tying the waist sash and gathering his long hair up into a simple, high ponytail.","In just a moment, the man who had just been wielding a blade to slaughter enemies, as cold and sharp as a night demon, transformed into an elegant young lord.","Qin Qinian's eyes widened in shock. \"You, you...\"","\"I'll give you my sword. If you're going to kill the enemy, you can bring it back for me when you're done.\" Qin Yanzhou shoved his sword into Qin Qinian's arms.","Qin Qinian instinctively hugged it. \"No, you gave me your sword, so where are you going?\"","\"Going back. If Mother doesn't see me, she'll be worried.\" Qin Yanzhou turned and headed toward the main tent.","Qin Qinian looked down at the sword, then at Qin Yanzhou who was gradually walking away. He stepped forward to follow him. \"You are a grown man with extraordinary martial arts skills, what is there for Mother to worry about? If you ask me, we should just follow Uncle Qiao and the others to pursue the enemy first. To think there are bandits of this scale in the North; if we don't deal with them promptly, I'm afraid they'll snowball and grow bigger and bigger...\"","Although his mouth didn't stop talking, Qin Qinian's footsteps following Qin Yanzhou didn't stop either.","\"Second Brother, Qin the Second, say something! If you're going to make up a lie, at least make it believable. It's just going to the battlefield to kill enemies, not putting away your sword to offer up your head. What's there to worry about?\"","Qin Yanzhou suddenly stopped.","Qin Qinian thought he had changed his mind, but turning his head, he saw their parents and Feng Feng standing not far away. The people nearby noticed their gazes and looked over.","He didn't know if it was his imagination, but in the flickering firelight, his mother's eyes were much brighter than usual, as if a pool of tears was welling up in them.","Seeing the two brothers' attire, Qin Shaozong couldn't help but twitch the corner of his mouth.","The taller one was neatly dressed in a clean and tidy white robe, looking completely spotless. The shorter one was holding a sword, his hair disheveled, wearing black inner garments, with a drop of blood splattered on his face from who knows where.","One white and one black, a stark contrast.","When Dai Li saw Qin Yanzhou return, her pupils suddenly contracted. She hurriedly looked him up and down. Seeing him in snow-white, with not much dirt or dust on him, let alone bloodstains, the heart that had been in her throat finally settled down.","With people coming and going around them, it wasn't a place to talk. Dai Li pursed her lips and looked away, not looking at Qin Yanzhou again.","Seeing that his mother had no intention of speaking and wasn't even looking at him anymore, Qin Yanzhou's eyelashes couldn't help but tremble.","As gazes gathered from all around, he had no intention of putting Dai Li on the spot, so he only said to Qin Shaozong, \"Father, Garrison Chief Qiao and Garrison Chief Wei have led men to pursue the enemy.\"","Qin Shaozong took in his micro-expressions. \"Then leave it to them. You two go back and rest. They are just some petty thieves anyway, no need to make a big fuss.\"","With that said, there was nothing left for the two brothers to do tonight.","The atmosphere stagnated slightly. At this moment, Dai Li finally spoke, \"Qin Yanzhou, come with me.\"","Qin Qinian watched Dai Li and Qin Yanzhou walk further and further away, scratching his head in confusion. \"What's wrong with Mother and Second Brother?\"","\"You want to know?\" Qin Shaozong suddenly asked.","Qin Qinian belatedly realized he had spoken his thoughts aloud. He hesitantly nodded and said he did, but saw that his father didn't say anything, only lifting his chin in the direction the two had left.","Qin Qinian said uncertainly, \"But Mother didn't call me just now.\"","Qin Shaozong clicked his tongue in distaste.","...","Dai Li led the person directly to a tent used for storing supplies. There was no one else here, making it a good place to talk.","Qin Yanzhou followed Dai Li inside. Seeing a rolling pin resting on a stack of wooden crates nearby, he picked it up without hesitation, then lifted his robe and knelt down, holding the rolling pin high with both hands. \"Your son has gone against Mother's expectations, I beg for your punishment.\"","Dai Li hadn't been able to find him earlier and was both shocked and terrified, afraid something had happened to him. When she saw Qin Yanzhou return in one piece, the panic in her heart quickly morphed into anger.","Now seeing him voluntarily asking for punishment, the flames of her anger surged even higher. Dai Li snatched the rolling pin, pointed it at him, and scolded angrily, \"Qin Yanzhou, what did I tell you before? It just goes in one ear and out the other, doesn't it? Do you really think I can't bear to hit you?!\"","\"Master said, 'Learn the arts of literature and martial combat to serve the imperial family.' However, the world is like this now. Your son has received the grace of the Qin family and is in the Qin army, how could I sit by and ignore a night attack by scoundrels?\" The young man lowered his eyes.","Hearing his plausible arguments, Dai Li's fury reached its peak. Unable to hold back, she struck his arm with the rolling pin. \"It seems you haven't listened to a single word I said before.\"","The young man kowtowed. There were no wooden boards underneath, so this kowtow wasn't as loud as the first, but his attitude was firmer than before. \"Mom, going to the front lines is not a difficult thing. You see, I went, and I came back safely.\"","Dai Li was trembling with anger. \"Qin Yanzhou, you are dead set on doing this, aren't you?\"","He slowly straightened up. \"I have already come of age. Please give me your permission.\"","Dai Li was so angry her head was buzzing. Just as she was about to strike again, she suddenly saw a pair of dark eyes peeking through the gap in the wind-blown tent curtain.","The other party didn't seem to expect to be discovered, and those somewhat round eyes blinked. Soon, the curtain was lifted, and the youth, who was still growing, cautiously stepped inside.","\"Mother...\" Qin Qinian felt the atmosphere was a bit strange.","He had just arrived and heard the gist of it; it seemed Mother didn't agree to let Qin the Second go to the front lines.","Dai Li took a deep breath, trying hard to restrain her anger. But before she could say anything, she unexpectedly saw Qin Qinian kneel down beside Qin Yanzhou.","Dai Li paused.","\"Mother, I also went to the front lines just now.\" Qin Qinian glanced at the rolling pin in Dai Li's hand.","For some reason, Dai Li inexplicably felt a hint of eager anticipation from him.","She had only raised one child before, but she had heard from colleagues with a second child that the most important thing in raising children is to treat them equally—people do not worry about scarcity, but rather about uneven distribution.","You can't give love and good things to only one, nor can you punish one and not the other.","In the past, Dai Li just listened to it for fun, after all, Zhou Zhou was an only child, but now there was another one...","Holding the rolling pin, Dai Li hesitated for a couple of breaths before finally striking Qin Qinian's arm as well. \"There are so many soldiers in the army, do the two of you need to keep rushing to the front?\"","Receiving this light tap, Qin Qinian's previous caution vanished in a poof, replaced by the comfort of a large dog being scratched in just the right spot.","Dai Li: \"...\"","Dai Li was both angry and amused, and after all this commotion, the burning anger in her heart had finally subsided a little. \"You are both young men now, in your late teens and twenties. Be more careful with your actions from now on.\"","The two of them nodded in unison.","Dai Li glanced at the brothers, said nothing more, and turned to leave.","\"My Lord, the enemy's remnant forces have retreated into the mountains. They are familiar with the terrain and used the cover of night to escape,\" Qiao Wangfei reported, his face flush with shame.","Qin Shaozong asked, \"Were any kept alive?\"","\"We struck down forty-two men this time and captured five alive.\" Wei Qing looked troubled. \"My Lord, the casualties on the imperial court's side are rather heavy. Out of their twenty men, ten have died. Beyond that, Attendant Guo is the most severely injured.\"","Qin Shaozong raised an eyebrow slightly. \"How severe? Half-dead?\"","The brazier to the side flickered wildly in the wind, casting a gloomy shadow over Wei Qing's expression. \"The man lost an arm. I don't know if he lost his mind from the shock or if he harbors ulterior motives, but at the very beginning, he actually yelled, 'The North goes too far in bullying others!'\"","Right at this moment, Qin Yanzhou and Qin Qinian returned.","Hearing this, Qin Qinian found it utterly baffling. \"He is as fragile as a twig and got his own hand chopped off. What does that have to do with our North? He can't just shove all the blame onto us simply because he was traveling with our group.\"","Qin Shaozong narrowed his long, slender eyes and suddenly ordered Wei Qing, \"Keep a close watch on those five captives. Gag their mouths tightly right away. You absolutely must not let them commit suicide.\""]},{"number":147,"title":"Chapter 147","paragraphs":["\"Gently, you clumsy fool! I told you to be gentle, are you deaf?\"","When Qin Shaozong arrived with his men, he heard Guo Nai roaring in anger.","The imperial court's envoy team consisted of only twenty men. Excluding the leaders Shen Tianming and Guo Nai, there were only eighteen. Such a small squad was made up of elite soldiers. Aside from the Palace Attendant Guo Nai, every one of them was robust and strong, striving to travel north at top speed to deliver the imperial decree.","With this setup, they obviously wouldn't bring along a frail military doctor. Besides, there was one town after another along the route; if anyone fell ill, they could seek local treatment.","Therefore, the Northern military doctors being yelled at were Ding Lianxi and his assistant.","Qin Shaozong said lightly, \"Attendant Guo has such a strong voice, I suppose there is no serious harm. Cong Jian, Qiao Wangfei was also injured just now, go take a look at him.\"","Ding Lianxi had long since lost the desire to serve this man.","This imperial Palace Attendant surnamed Guo had poor martial arts skills but was first in throwing his weight around. While helping him bandage his severed arm, the man kept complaining and finding fault. If he was so capable, he shouldn't have come.","Now hearing Qin Shaozong speak, Ding Lianxi moved swiftly. With a sharp snap, he closed the wooden medicine box beside him, grabbed it, and walked away. He moved so fast that Guo Nai couldn't even react.","Qiao Wangfei had followed Qin Shaozong here. Seeing Ding Lianxi walking toward him, he looked completely bewildered.","He wasn't injured!","As if remembering something, Qiao Wangfei suddenly looked down at his own hand. During the battle earlier, he had deflected a scimitar. When the blade spun away, its tip had grazed the back of his hand.","It was insignificant, just a scrape that oozed a line of crimson. Later, he casually wiped his hand, and the bleeding stopped.","This must have been noticed by the Marquis when he cupped his hands to report just now.","It was just a minor flesh wound. If discovered any later, it would have already healed. How could he trouble Mr. Ding with this?","\"Platoon Leader Qiao, you are so heavily injured, how can you move around on your own? Come, come, let me take you back for treatment.\" Ding Lianxi grabbed Qiao Wangfei's arm, half-dragging him away.","Qiao Wangfei: \"...\"","How could Guo Nai fail to see that Qin Shaozong was doing this on purpose? That military officer clearly had a ruddy complexion, how could he suddenly be severely injured? His eyes widened with fury. \"Marquis of Wu'an, do you really think the sky above is surnamed 'Qin'?\"","These words were too heavy and too sensitive, causing the surroundings to fall dead silent. No one dared to chime in.","Qin Shaozong suddenly chuckled softly. \"Why is Attendant Guo so furious? You lost an arm to bandits during your mission to deliver the decree. When you return to Chang'an and His Majesty sees your unwavering dedication despite your disability, he will surely be deeply moved. He will likely promote you and reward you with fertile lands and beautiful maidens. Let alone losing one arm, even if you lost both, you wouldn't have to worry about the rest of your life. So, by all accounts, you should be thanking me. Why are you hurling insults instead of shedding tears of gratitude?\"","Guo Nai nearly choked on a mouthful of blood.","He had lost an arm, and this man actually wanted him to thank him?","If this was a blessing, would he want it?!","He was so angry that his blood rushed up, and the severed arm that had just barely stopped bleeding began to seep crimson again.","Seeing the situation turning sour, Shen Tianming hurriedly advised, \"Attendant Guo, please do not get angry, mind your wound. The ambush was unpredictable, it's all the fault of those blind bandits. Besides, what's done is done, why don't we...\"","\"Who says it was unpredictable!\" Guo Nai's eyes were bloodshot as he glared fiercely at Qin Shaozong. \"I heard it! Tonight's incident was clearly orchestrated by the North!\"","Feng Feng and the others' expressions changed drastically.","\"Attendant Guo, watch your words! You can eat whatever you want, but you cannot speak nonsense!\"","\"Exactly! Without proof or evidence, on what grounds do you claim the North did this? Assassinating an imperial official—do you have a death wish?\"","Qin Shaozong's face also turned cold. Under the firelight, his brown eyes were as icy as the pupils of a large predatory beast. \"Where did Attendant Guo hear this, and who was the one speaking?\"","Intimidated by his imposing aura, Guo Nai was momentarily speechless.","\"My Qin family has guarded the borders for generations. The number of casualties we've suffered to secure the peace of Great Yan's frontiers is countless. I never expected to be baselessly slandered in the end. Until this dirty water is washed clean and the truth of the matter is brought to light, I don't think there is any need to rush to the capital. General Shen, wouldn't you agree?\" At the end of his speech, Qin Shaozong looked at Shen Tianming beside him.","Shen Tianming stiffened, but this matter indeed needed to be clarified. \"Attendant Guo, this is no trivial matter. Please explain in detail.\"","\"When those so-called bandits attacked just now, I heard them say things like 'The Marquis said to finish this quickly,' 'If caught, absolutely do not confess,' and 'Martyrdom.' The situation was chaotic then, so I couldn't remember every face of those who spoke, but I do remember one of them had a black mole on the left side of his mouth,\" Guo Nai recalled.","Qin Shaozong glanced at Feng Feng, who quickly left the ranks.","Mo Yanyun then said angrily, \"This is utterly absurd. What is wrong with the Marquis saying to finish things quickly? Encountering such petty thieves disturbing our sleep in the middle of the night, if we don't finish it quickly, are we supposed to dawdle until dawn and let them enjoy tomorrow's sunrise before dealing with them?\"","Shen Tianming's mouth twitched.","The words were crude but made sense; encountering such an event indeed required a swift resolution.","Guo Nai choked on his words, but immediately followed up, \"Even if the first part makes sense, what about the rest? Who knows if you did this on purpose? Otherwise, why has the Marquis of Wu'an been following us for so long after leaving Yuyang? His Majesty did not summon you to the capital for an audience, and entering the capital without an imperial edict is tantamount to rebellion.\"","The last word dropped with particular weight.","Qin Shaozong said expressionlessly, \"If I wanted to rebel, I could simply kill all of you right now, pin the blame on the bandits, and finally enter the capital to personally report to His Majesty under the pretext that the imperial envoys were attacked and entirely wiped out.\"","The expressions of Shen and Guo changed drastically.","Guo Nai instantly lost most of his bravado. They had lost nearly half their men in the ambush and now only had a scattered ten or so left. In terms of numbers, they were not even a fraction of the opposing side.","\"My Lord, the man with the black mole under his mouth that Attendant Guo just mentioned has been found,\" Feng Feng returned at this moment.","The surroundings quieted down as everyone looked at him.","Feng Feng's expression was grave. \"However, this person is one of the slain enemies and is already dead.\"","*","Not long after Dai Li returned to the main tent, she heard the sounds of clashing weapons outside cease, turning instead into shouting that sounded like an argument. They seemed to be disputing something, but it didn't last long before the voices sank slowly, like a boat overturned by the tide.","Dai Li lay back on the soft couch, completely devoid of sleepiness.","One moment she thought of Qin Yanzhou's resolute face, and the next she thought of the blood splattered from nowhere on Qin Qinian's face. All sorts of complicated thoughts crowded her mind, making her completely unable to sleep.","Perhaps fifteen minutes passed, or perhaps a very long time. Hugging her quilt with her back facing the door flap, Dai Li heard the soft rustle of the curtain being lifted.","The newcomer moved very lightly. Dai Li heard the sound of a sash being untied, followed by the rustling of robes. He must have taken off his outer garment and set it aside.","Dai Li did not move.","The space beside her dipped.","Hot breath fell upon the back of her neck, somewhat like a large carnivore sniffing before a meal.","Before Dai Li could use the motion of rolling over to avoid it, a sturdy long arm reached over from behind. It clamped around her waist and pulled her back slightly, pressing her against his broad chest.","\"Why is Madam not asleep yet?\"","Dai Li was slightly taken aback, unsure of how he had managed to sense her mood. She was currently troubled by her stubborn, disobedient son, so she had no patience for the instigator lying behind her.","Dai Li said, \"I am asleep. Do not bother me.\"","A low chuckle came from behind, and then Qin Shaozong took the initiative to bring up the events of the night. \"Madam, Attendant Guo lost an arm and is claiming that this whole affair was directed and staged by our Northern Territory.\"","Surprised, Dai Li could not help but blurt out, \"Have you not even started yet?\"","Qin Changgeng indeed wanted to stage a scenario where the imperial edict was lost, but that was something planned for later, when they reached the border of Yan and Ji provinces. After all, the dust explosion in Chang'an required time to set up, and extending the timeline was also necessary to avoid suspicion.","Qin Shaozong replied, \"Indeed, I have not started. Someone else acted ahead of time, wanting to muddy the waters.\"","Dai Li rolled over in his arms to lie flat on her back. \"Did you capture any alive? Were you able to interrogate them to find out who is behind this?\"","\"We caught five alive, but strangely, they all withstood the interrogation without confessing. They insisted they were just commoners who could no longer make a living and were forced into banditry.\" Qin Shaozong's gaze was heavy. \"And then, all five of them died from poison.\"","Dai Li was stunned. \"Did they know beforehand that the poison would act up? Otherwise, why would they all refuse to confess so fiercely?\"","Qin Shaozong said calmly, \"Most likely.\"","\"How did Attendant Guo react when he found out?\" Dai Li asked.","Qin Shaozong answered, \"He lost an arm, so naturally he harbors extreme hatred in his heart. After all, with his appearance marred, he will never be allowed to serve by the young emperor's side again. His official career is effectively over for the rest of his life. But so what if he hates it? The imperial court's envoy only has a few scattered men left. As the saying goes, a person standing under someone else's roof has no choice but to bow their head. No matter how dissatisfied he is, he has to swallow it.\"","Hearing his last remark, Dai Li's brow twitched. She suspected that this man had likely spoken some arrogant words to them.","Qin Shaozong continued, \"Half of the 'bandits' escaped, and they might mount a comeback later to kill more people from the imperial court.\"","If at first he only had a mindset of watching a good show, feeling that Shen, Guo, and the others were simply unlucky, how could he not know that the other party was specifically targeting the imperial court's troops after the captives all died at the same time?","Dai Li pondered, \"Let them stay in the center of the formation from now on. Do not place them on the edges.\"","Qin Shaozong gave a murmur of agreement and pulled Dai Li, who was facing the ceiling, over so that she was face-to-face with him.","The two were very close, their noses almost touching, their exhaled breaths intertwining. \"I heard from the others that the kid, Qin the Second, performed quite well tonight. Furthermore, when he came back earlier, his clothes were neat, so he likely was not injured. After this experience, Madam should finally be able to rest a little easier.\"","\"Rest easier about what?\" Dai Li reached out and pressed her hands against his chest, trying to push him away. \"Tonight we had the advantage of numbers. The enemy was weak and we were strong; it was a favorable situation and we had good luck. But who can guarantee that every time in the future will be just like tonight?\"","\"Qin the Second is quite stubborn in his bones,\" Qin Shaozong said.","The subtext was that Qin Yanzhou would not give up.","Dai Li was already worried sick. She knew these things well enough, but she did not appreciate someone else repeating them to her.","Her fair hand, which had been pressing against the man's chest, moved up to cover his mouth. Dai Li said unhappily, \"You still have the nerve to speak? Is it not because you were fanning the flames? This is all your fault.\"","As soon as the words left her mouth, Dai Li withdrew her hand as if she had been electrocuted, her expression shifting rapidly.","This man had actually licked her palm. How shameless.","\"I have a method that might solve Madam's urgent problem. Would Madam care to listen?\" Qin Shaozong asked at that moment.","Dai Li looked at him suspiciously.","He had a suggestion?","He was the one fanning the flames earlier, and now he was the one claiming to have a solution. Could this guy be secretly plotting some wicked trick?","Qin Shaozong added, \"Just listen to it. As for whether you adopt it later, the decision is entirely up to Madam.\"","Dai Li hesitated but could not overcome her curiosity. \"Alright, tell me.\"","Qin Shaozong curled his thin lips, though his tone remained very serious. \"Madam once signed a written agreement with me in black and white. I believe that this time, we can refer to the past and have Qin the Second make a pact with you.\"","Dai Li's eyebrows moved slightly. \"Make a pact?\"","Qin Shaozong replied, \"Exactly. That kid is entirely focused on going into battle right now; most likely, a team of nine oxen could not pull him back. Why does Madam not temporarily take a step back, retreating in order to advance? It would also save your mother-son relationship from becoming too strained.\"","\"Are you saying you still want him to participate in suppressing the bandits?\" Dai Li's tone gradually turned hostile.","Qin Shaozong explained, \"He ran off on his own to fight the enemy tonight. When the time actually comes for bandit suppression, who is to say he will not repeat his old tricks? Madam might as well make a pact with him early on. If he sustains a severe injury next time—for example, if his back is sliced open or his limbs are broken—then...\"","Before he could finish his sentence, Qin Shaozong's calf received a swift rabbit kick.","Dai Li's anger flared. \"Qin Changgeng, although Zhou Zhou is not your biological son, you do not need to harbor such malice when speculating about him.\"","\"Madam, it is not malice. These are all things I have experienced myself.\" Qin Shaozong pulled back the blanket she had kicked askew. \"However, today is different from the past. The Northern Kingdom has been subdued, and many of the armies in the Central Plains are far less ferocious than the Northern Kingdom was back then. Besides, with the Northern Territory as our backing, and with the help of Madam's fertilizer, we certainly will not have to worry about provisions in the future.\"","It was not like Youzhou in the past, which was restricted by the imperial court. While their military pay was repeatedly delayed, they also had to face the arrogant and aggressive tribes of the Northern Kingdom.","Dai Li suddenly thought of the scars all over his body.","Those scars were long and short, the new and the old crisscrossing over one another. In some places, they even formed a grid pattern. If those injuries had been sustained all at once, a massive chunk of flesh would undoubtedly have been carved right off.","Dai Li opened her mouth, but she could not bring herself to say a single word.","\"So Madam does not need to worry too much.\" In truth, what Qin Shaozong did not mention was that he was not the only one; Qin San had also gone through such experiences.","During the battle with the Northern Kingdom back then, that boy had nearly reported to the King of Hell for reincarnation. It was precisely for this reason that when he went south to deal with the salt smugglers, he had not brought Qin San along.","However, Qin the Second and Qin San were both of the younger generation. If she knew about this, she might project her fears onto her son and become entirely consumed by fright, so he decided it was best to simply say nothing.","Dai Li lowered her eyes, hugged the blanket, and rolled over, muttering a muffled, \"Let us sleep.\"","In the darkness, the man smiled silently.","*","After staying out in the wilderness for a night, the caravan resumed its journey early the next morning, heading toward their next destination, Manjiang County.","Because there were quite a few injured individuals on the imperial court's side—especially Guo Nai, one of the leading commanders, who had lost an arm—their marching speed was much slower than usual. They had originally planned to arrive at Manjiang County at noon, but it dragged on until the late afternoon before they finally entered the city.","As soon as they entered the city, Guo Nai impatiently led his people to a medical clinic to seek treatment.","Clearly, he did not trust the physicians of the Northern Territory.","Qin Shaozong let him be and took Dai Li to check into a guest house. Manjiang County was not particularly large, but it was a crucial transit point for those traveling from the Western Regions to Ji Province, so there were quite a few people from the Western Regions present in the town.","This was Shi Rongyue's first time seeing such blonde-haired, hook-nosed foreigners. Sitting by the carriage window, she leaned further and further out, until finally, both of her hands were resting on the windowsill, much like a curious cat peeking its head out.","\"Second Aunt, they are so unique. Some have blue eyes, and some have green eyes. I suppose most of the foreigners from the Western Regions look like this.\" There was a trace of subtle envy in the little girl's tone.","If not for her second uncle's prominent status and immense power, she would certainly have faced much more criticism in the past for sharing his eye color.","Dai Li was absent-minded, her attention divided. Different environments nurture different kinds of people. On the other side of the distant world, some people even have black skin, the kind that practically blends into the dark of night.","Shi Rongyue marveled, Second Aunt, you are truly amazing to know even this.","Dai Li just smiled and said nothing.","Not long after, they arrived at the relay station.","Just as before, Qin Shaozong waved his hand and booked the entire relay station. Dai Li and the other core members of the Northern Territory stayed on the highest floor, the third floor.","It was the Shen hour, not yet time for dinner. Dai Li watched Nianxia and Bipo as they tidied up the guest room, eventually saying, Nianxia, take out the brush, ink, paper, and inkstone from the chest. Oh, and the inkpad too.","Nianxia didn't understand why, but she briskly complied.","The mulberry paper was rolled out. Dai Li ground the ink, picked up her brush, and slowly began to write on the paper. She didn't write fast, but she was very serious and didn't pause at all.","After finishing one page, Dai Li slightly lifted her wolf-hair brush, looking at another brand-new sheet of paper with some hesitation. After hesitating for a long time, she finally pulled that sheet over as well and began to ink it again.","This time, her writing was far less fluid than before. Dai Li paused many times halfway through, and even crossed out what she had written, scrapping the paper to start over.","By the time she finished writing on the mulberry paper, nearly half an hour had passed.","Bipo, go and have Yanzhou and Qinian come here, Dai Li instructed.","Bipo received the order and took her leave.","Shortly after, two figures, one tall and one short, arrived side by side.","The room door was not closed, but both stopped at the threshold. Qin Yanzhou knocked on the doorframe. Mother, you were looking for us?","Dai Li said, Come in.","Only then did the two enter.","Without avoiding Qin Qinian, Dai Li looked at the young man and said in a cold tone, Zhou Zhou, I will ask you one last time. Are you absolutely determined to go bandit hunting?","Qin Yanzhou lowered his head in a submissive posture, yet he said, I beg Mother's permission.","The expected scolding did not come. He only heard the woman ask, What about you, Qinian? You as well?","Qin Qinian was momentarily stunned. He had thought Dai Li called him over to act as a persuader, never expecting her to ask him too.","Of course, Qin Qinian said without hesitation.","Dai Li waved for the two to step forward. When they reached the table, she handed the brothers each a sheet of mulberry paper. Since you want to go to the front lines, sign this. If you don't sign, don't even think about going to hunt bandits. Let me make this clear in advance: Qin Changgeng has agreed to let me have full authority over this matter. Even if you try to find another way by going to him, it will be useless.","Compared to Qin Qinian, who was frowning in distress and struggling to read word by word, Qin Yanzhou read very quickly.","He finished reading first and looked up in astonishment, his eyes full of joy. Mother, I can do this. I promise you!","The agreement in his hand was very concise. Dai Li agreed to let him go bandit hunting, but on two conditions. First, he had to obey commands unconditionally. Second, if he got injured during this expedition, even if it was just a superficial flesh wound, he would never be allowed on the front lines again.","Dai Li remained cold. If you agree, sign it, and then stamp your fingerprint at the end.","On this side, Qin Yanzhou had already finished signing his name and stamping his fingerprint.","On the other side, Qin Qinian's face was scrunched up into a ball, wearing a miserable expression as if he had been struck by lightning. Mother, can you change the condition? Finishing four books in half a month and writing a twenty-thousand-word reflection is impossible for me. A beating would be much more pleasant.","Dai Li: ...No, it has to be this."]},{"number":148,"title":"Chapter 148","paragraphs":["Without exaggeration, as Qin Qinian looked at the mulberry paper in his hands, he felt as if the sky was falling. \"Mother, reading four books in half a month and then writing twenty thousand words... I, I can't do it...\"","Dai Li corrected him, \"Look closely. It's reading four books in the first half of the month, and writing a twenty-thousand-word reflection in the second half. It adds up to a whole month.\"","Qin Qinian's eyes widened as he looked.","It really was.","However, this made little difference to him. Let alone four books, even one was enough to give him a headache, not to mention the twenty-thousand-word book report that followed.","Not two hundred, not two thousand, but twenty thousand! What was the difference between this and asking him to ascend to the heavens on the spot?","Seeing him looking as if he had eaten a whole basket of bitter melons, Dai Li revealed her first smile since they entered the room. \"Of course it's difficult. Otherwise, did you think I had you sign this just for fun? Qinian, if you don't want to write those twenty thousand words, then protect yourself well during the bandit suppression.\"","The first half of both their agreements was the same: neither of them was allowed to get hurt. The only difference lay in the conditions that followed; one was forbidden from going to the front lines in the future, while the other was forced to read and write.","It had to be said that each had their own version of the sky falling. This was also the result of Dai Li's long consideration to balance the scales evenly between the two.","However, as someone who was merely implicated, Dai Li finally gave him a chance to back out. \"Of course, if you feel you can't do it, Qinian, you don't have to sign.\"","\"There's no way I can't do it!\" The young man, full of youthful vigor, couldn't stand being provoked.","Dai Li nodded in satisfaction. \"Alright, since you think there's no problem, come over here, sign your name, and press your fingerprint.\"","Once the signing and thumbprints were done, Dai Li couldn't be bothered to look at them anymore and sent the two away. \"It's almost time for dinner. Go downstairs.\"","The two brothers left the room and walked toward the stairs. Halfway there, the youth scratched his head in belated realization. \"Second Brother, why do I feel like I just went to Mother's room and ended up signing an agreement in a daze?\"","Qin Yanzhou remembered his unhesitating kneel from the previous night, and his gaze softened. \"For you, that is indeed the case. I'm sorry, I dragged you into this.\"","\"Hey, hey, why are you saying this to me? I didn't mean to blame you at all.\" Qin Qinian reacted strongly. \"Just like Mother said just now, since I dared to sign the agreement, I will definitely make sure to come out of the bandit suppression completely unscathed.\"","\"Creak.\" The door to the guest room beside them opened.","Shi Rongyue, who also wanted to go downstairs for dinner, looked at the two outside the door. Thinking of the snippets she had just heard, her eyes lit up faintly. The little girl first glanced in the direction of Dai Li's room before suppressing her joyful voice to ask, \"Brother Chongle, Second Aunt agreed to let you go suppress the bandits?\"","Qin Yanzhou nodded. \"She agreed.\"","Qin Qinian was surprised. \"Rongrong, how did you know about this?\"","Shi Rongyue smiled, revealing two small dimples. \"I heard it by accident. I wish you both a victorious start when the time comes.\"","Qin Yanzhou: \"Thank you.\"","\"What was the agreement you were just talking about?\" Shi Rongyue looked at Qin Yanzhou curiously.","\"It's a long story...\"","Dai Li put the two agreements away properly before going downstairs. The first floor of the inn was already prepared for dining. Today's dinner was the first time the Northern Territory and the imperial court factions gathered for a meal since the bandit disaster.","The atmosphere was incredibly stiff.","Although the two sides were not well-acquainted previously, for the sake of face, exchanging pleasantries back and forth shouldn't have been a problem.","Playing along on the official stage, who didn't know how to do that?","However, for tonight's meal, they simply split into separate tables. Shen Tianming and Guo Nai sat together, while Qin Shaozong sat with the generals of the Northern Territory. The two sides were clearly divided, with zero communication throughout the entire process.","When the meal was over, Dai Li set down her bowl and chopsticks. Seeing that Shi Rongyue across from her was also full, she simply went upstairs with her. But Dai Li did not know that as soon as she and Shi Rongyue left, the atmosphere on the first floor immediately turned sour.","\"Marquis Qin, we can't just let last night's matter go like this, can we?\" Shen Tianming gave a fake smile.","Guo Nai, who was beside him, didn't speak, but his gaze was fierce.","Qin Shaozong said calmly, \"Then according to General Shen, are we to pause our journey to the capital and put all our efforts into hunting down the remnants of the bandits?\"","Guo Nai's face twisted. \"Qin Shaozong, so you mean we should just drop this matter? The dozen or so people killed on my side and my lost arm are just gone for nothing?\"","As soon as the name Qin Shaozong came out, the surrounding atmosphere grew even more tense.","He didn't use a courtesy name, but directly addressed the other party by his full name. Such a situation was usually from a superior to a subordinate; otherwise, it was considered a provocation.","Obviously, if one really got down to it, a Palace Attendant was not as high-ranking as a top-tier Marquis.","Mo Yanyun was instantly enraged and returned the favor by calling him by his full name. \"Guo Nai, you insolent fool! Wasn't the Marquis asking you what you want to do? He was clearly asking for your opinion. Which word of his mentioned dropping it?\"","Bai Jianping quickly followed up, \"Exactly! Always thinking about dropping it, I reckon the person who wants to drop it is you.\"","\"Tsk, tsk, someone is a thief crying stop thief!\" Feng Feng sighed.","The veins on Guo Nai's forehead throbbed. \"You lot are simply lawless. Just wait until we return to the capital...\"","His shoulder was suddenly pressed down by Shen Tianming, intending to make him calm down. The former paused, took a deep breath, and fiercely looked away.","Only then did Shen Tianming say to Qin Shaozong, \"Then, in the Marquis's opinion, how should this group of bandits who assassinated imperial officials be dealt with?\"","This was clearly kicking the problem back to Qin Shaozong.","Qin Shaozong: \"Naturally, we notify the local government office to arrest them.\"","Guo Nai snorted heavily. \"That's it?!\"","\"Otherwise, what does Attendant Guo think we should do? Stop in our tracks and focus on searching for the bandits alongside the local government? Or do you want to send a letter back to the capital, asking His Majesty to send people from a thousand miles away to suppress the remaining few dozen bandits?\" Qin Shaozong retorted.","Guo Nai just glared at him, unable to open his mouth for a long time.","Upstairs, a half-hour after Dai Li returned to her room, Qin Shaozong also came back. As soon as he entered, he said to Dai Li, \"Madam, I'm afraid we will have to stay in this small county for a few more days.\"","Dai Li pondered, \"Is it because Attendant Guo needs to heal his wounds here?\"","\"Exactly. This person still believes that everything last night was a trap set by our Northern Territory. Why would he be willing to let Ding Congjian treat him now? He went to find a doctor in the city himself.\" Qin Shaozong sneered. \"Whatever, it's good to stop for a bit. It gives Chang'an more time to prepare.\"","Hearing that he already had everything planned out in his words, Dai Li didn't say much more.","Instead, he suddenly changed the subject. \"Just now during dinner, I saw that Qin the Second had a huge appetite, eating a bowl of rice more than usual. Did Madam agree to his request?\"","The early evening had arrived. Outside the window, the setting sun was gradually fading in layers, leaving only a barely visible trace. A lamp was lit in the room, its bright and harmonious light spreading a warm color all around.","The man's sharply defined face was enveloped in the warm colors, fading his usual heavy and intimidating pressure. Although there were shallow traces of time at the corners of his eyes, they did not diminish his mature aura in the slightest.","Dai Li knew at a glance that he was in a quite good mood at the moment, and deliberately said, \"I did agree, but Zhou Zhou wasn't the only one who signed the agreement.\"","His eyebrows twitched slightly. \"Oh? Who else?\"","Dai Li only replied with two words: \"You guess.\"","\"Since Madam is unwilling to tell me, I can only rely on my own hands to find the answer.\" Qin Shaozong walked over to the desk and began searching for the answer.","The items were not hard to find. The couple had two small wooden boxes for important letters, and Qin Shaozong saw them as soon as he opened the first one.","He took out the mulberry paper and unfolded it. Daili did not know which one he read first, but she saw him raise his long eyebrows in apparent surprise before breaking into a bright, clear smile. You did very well, Madam. This is exactly how it should be done.","Daili guessed that he had probably seen Qin Qinian's copy first. I told them that you would not intervene in this matter. No matter how the situation develops, it would be useless to seek you out.","Naturally.","Chang'an.","As the capital of the nation, even if other regions were littered with the starved dead or filled with ruined walls, Chang'an still maintained its bustling scene of crowded vendors and an endless stream of fragrant carriages and fine horses.","On this day, the young ladies of the city's prominent families arranged to go on a spring outing. Spring had arrived, and a myriad of flowers competed in beauty, making it the perfect time to enjoy the season.","Just as a long line of carriages passed through the busy market and was about to head toward the east city gate, a sudden, deafening roar echoed from the other direction. The sound was so immense that it felt as if a giant dragon were tossing about in displeasure underground, causing the earth itself to seemingly tremble for a moment.","The earth dragon is turning! Get out of the houses! someone roared first.","The endlessly flowing market instantly descended into chaos. The horses pulling the carriages were spooked, neighing loudly as they dashed forward with the carts.","What is going on? Quick, get the horses under control!","Was it an earthquake?","Huh, it only sounded once with no follow-up. It doesn't look like the earth dragon turning; it sounds more like a house collapsing.","That direction seems to be the Jiang Manor. Let's go take a look.","...","By the time the busybodies from the market rushed over, quite a few people had already gathered at the site of the collapse.","A man with a broad forehead and a pale complexion stepped forward. With a shrewd glint in his eyes, he raised his voice, This house looks quite grand. The master of the household must have deep pockets. If we rescue them, we might be able to get some reward money. Who wants to help me save them?","Then let's dig and see.","People tend to follow the crowd. Once one or two started, many others joined the rescue team.","When the capital guards of Chang'an arrived, they heard people saying from afar:","A white fox is considered an auspicious sign, right? How could there be a white fox here? And it's lying on the ground vomiting blood endlessly?","There are words written in blood here. Could they have been written by the fox vomiting blood? Is there anyone who can read? Someone come and see what the white fox wrote!","Uh, it seems to be Han-Yan falls in Chang'an, the golden dragon emerges by the nest. Han-Yan? Doesn't that mean the ones above...","The leading guard's expression changed drastically, and he immediately scolded, Cease this nonsense at once!","Seeing the capital guards arriving on horseback, the commoners all quieted down, not daring to speak further.","However, such a bizarre incident as a white fox writing a blood letter appearing out of nowhere, and happening right in the bustling market where a perfectly fine house suddenly collapsed, looked incredibly strange no matter how one looked at it.","That phrase, Han-Yan falls in Chang'an, the golden dragon emerges by the nest, quietly spread throughout Chang'an.","The current dynasty's official title was Yan, and the current emperor's surname was Han. What this Han-Yan referred to was self-evident. The word falls closely following it was a direct offense to those in power.","...","The emperor was young, so the court affairs were jointly controlled by Empress Dowager Wang and Prime Minister Dong Zhou. Backed by the Wang clan, the Empress Dowager held half the empire, making the Wang clan incredibly powerful and sought-after in Chang'an.","However, the Wang residence, usually filled with esteemed guests, had recently rejected a large number of visiting cards and kept its main gates tightly shut.","Inside the study of the Wang Manor.","The young emperor's uncle, Wang Tianchuan, wore an ugly expression. Have you found anything out?","The two men in front of him lowered their heads and hunched their backs, looking utterly ashamed. Please forgive us, Master. There is no news as of yet...","Bang!","A top-quality mutton-fat jade paperweight smashed near the feet of the two men, and the flying jade shards cut one of their cheeks.","Blinding bright red blood immediately flowed down, but the man only lowered his head even further, not daring to utter a word.","Useless trash! It's not like I asked you to recapture the Northern Territories or Jingzhou. You can't even handle this little matter. What use do I have for you? Wang Tianchuan slammed the table and stood up, his fat belly jiggling continuously with the movement.","The eldest young master of the Wang family, sitting to the side, advised, Father, please calm your anger. Since the other party dared to act in such a way, they must have made ample preparations. It is normal that we cannot root out the culprit right away. However, this land of Chang'an is ultimately in your grasp. The source will be dug up sooner or later. I believe that besides searching for the mastermind from the root, we can also approach this from another angle.","With his proudest legitimate son speaking, Wang Tianchuan's anger subsided slightly. My son, what are your thoughts?","The one who orchestrated this is undoubtedly the beneficiary. 'The golden dragon emerges by the nest'—could this second half of the phrase, which has caused such an uproar in the city, be the beneficiary building momentum for themselves and directly related to them? he speculated.","Since the previous dynasty, the dragon had been endowed with a special meaning. People believed it possessed the power to predict the future and turn the tides of the world.","Although it was not yet directly linked to imperial power as it would be in later generations, there was no doubt that at this time, the dragon absolutely represented a great hero.","Wang Tianchuan's expression turned somewhat peculiar.","The current dynasty favored the colors profound black and red; black and red were used for all major occasions.","Gold, on the contrary, was rarely used.","Gold... could it be the Capital Guards?","The golden dragon emerges by the nest.","If the imperial city was compared to a nest, then the Capital Guards who patrolled the capital were indeed right by the nest.","However, before the Wang father and son, along with other prominent families, could make sense of things, eerie roaring sounds began to appear one after another within Chang'an city, occurring during both the day and night.","And after every tremor, a blood-written letter that resembled a prophetic omen was left at the scene."]},{"number":149,"title":"Chapter 149","paragraphs":["The procession heading to the capital stayed in the small county for several days. During these few days, Dai Li only went out once to visit the market. The atmosphere in the county was very tense. Military patrols hurried back and forth, seemingly busy organizing a bandit eradication campaign.","However, this tense atmosphere automatically dissipated after Dai Li returned to the guest house. The men from the North seemed very casual about the bandit eradication, not caring about it at all.","Dai Li had asked Qin Shaozong about it, and he merely replied, \"No rush.\"","Alright then, it seemed he already had a plan.","After resting and reorganizing in the small county, the procession set off once again.","Chang'an was located in Yongzhou, and Yongzhou was to the west of Yanzhou. If they were heading to the capital, logically they should travel directly southwest from Yuyang to reach Chang'an as quickly as possible.","But now, Qin Shaozong was heading south first before turning west, which was equivalent to taking a detour and traveling a longer route.","Shen Tianming realized this belatedly and said with a displeased expression, \"Marquis Qin, we are going the wrong way.\"","\"We are not going the wrong way.\" Qin Shaozong curled his thin lips into a smile. \"Last year, Fan of Yanzhou colluded with the Green Lotus Sect to cause chaos and harm the common people. I was invited by Governor Nangong to head south and eliminate this threat for the people. Later, I beheaded that Yanzhou leader and parasite, causing Yanzhou to lose its ruler and turn into scattered sand. Ultimately, this matter started because of me, so how could I just ignore it? I had no choice but to take on the hardship and jointly assume the position of Yanzhou Governor alongside Nangong.\"","Shen Tianming's face twitched fiercely.","He had clearly killed Fan of Yanzhou and seized his territory, yet he could still speak in such a high-sounding and righteous manner.","How utterly shameless!","How could Qin Shaozong not see what he was thinking? But that didn't stop him from continuing to smile. \"Since we happen to be traveling far from home, and Chang'an is not too far from Yanzhou, I thought we could drop by Yanzhou on the way to see how much vitality has been restored to this land after the parasite was eradicated. General Shen, could it be that you are not happy to see the common people living and working in peace?\"","With such a huge accusation pressed upon him, Shen Tianming naturally denied it immediately. \"Not at all. A harmonious government and peaceful people is naturally a good thing. It's just that heading to the capital cannot be delayed. Why don't we part ways here? I will escort your esteemed wife and young son to the capital to receive their titles, and you, Marquis, can continue to Yanzhou to handle your official business.\"","Qin Shaozong coldly rejected the idea. \"The imperial edict only specified the deadline for setting off to the capital, but there is no time limit for arrival. Moreover, I have already sent someone to report this matter to the higher-ups. If they lay blame, I will bear it all myself. General Shen need not worry.\"","Beside them, Guo Nai was entirely focused on hurrying to the capital. Hearing that Qin Shaozong wanted to take a detour, he naturally disagreed. But just as he opened his mouth to speak, Shen Tianming held him down and gave a slight shake of his head.","Shen Tianming thought it over and felt that this situation truly could not go in the direction he hoped.","A man accustomed to summoning the wind and rain in the North could not tolerate repeated provocations. If they really angered this Northern tiger, it was hard to say whether they would ultimately arrive safely in the capital.","There was nothing to be done. Who told their side to have fewer than ten men left!","Shen Tianming gritted his teeth and said, \"Fine. Since Marquis Qin has already submitted a memorial to the imperial court, we will walk a few extra steps and visit Yanzhou first.\"","The procession continued south.","Time flew by like a white horse passing a crevice, with the sun rising and setting. After traveling for about ten days, Dai Li and the group arrived at the border between Yanzhou and Jizhou. Traveling a bit further south would bring them into Yanzhou.","Approaching dusk, the procession arrived at a mountain village at the border of the two provinces. There were no towns nearby, only rural villages, so they settled in the village for the night.","The village was not small, containing about a thousand households. When Qin Shaozong's three hundred men arrived, their numbers were less than a third of the villagers, but their imposing aura was overwhelming.","Seeing them armed with swords and sabers, wearing armor, and riding fine horses, the villagers were momentarily terrified.","\"Village Chief, have the bandits come?\"","Hearing this, Shen Tianming immediately glared at the speaker with his tiger-like eyes. \"Nonsense! I am the grand General of Agile Cavalry appointed personally by His Majesty. When did I ever degenerate into a bandit?\"","This shout echoed far and wide, causing many villagers to look at each other in dismay.","\"Not bandits?\"","\"He said he is a general of the imperial court. Could it be that the court has learned about the bandit menace around Spring Sprout Mountain and finally sent people to eradicate them?\"","\"That must be it. Thank the heavens and the earth! Thank His Majesty for his great grace!\" Someone took the lead to kneel.","With this one kneeling, a whole crowd fell to their knees in a sweeping motion.","Shen Tianming was dumbfounded, feeling as if he had instantly been put on a pedestal.","But bandits? Were there bandits here too?","Qin Shaozong rode his horse forward and told the person who had kneeled first that they needed a place to stay for the night.","The man agreed to everything without hesitation, but at the very end, he said, \"Noble sir, the bandits of Spring Sprout Mountain are extremely cunning. Please be very careful when eradicating them. The military officers from the local government office who went previously all returned in defeat.\"","Qin Shaozong did not reply immediately. Instead, he cast a sidelong glance at Shen Tianming, whose face had turned stiff.","The procession proceeded to settle in and make themselves at home.","When Dai Li heard the word bandits, she knew the time had come. At the earliest, it would be tomorrow night; there would definitely be action within five days.","Indeed, just as she expected, after the meal, Shen Tianming took the initiative to seek out Qin Shaozong.","\"Marquis Qin, what are your thoughts on the matter of the Spring Sprout Mountain bandits?\" Shen Tianming asked.","He had always been brooding over the previous attack, but strangely enough, after that incident, the remaining dozens of bandits had completely vanished. It was unknown whether they had fled after completing their mission or hidden away waiting for an opportunity to strike.","\"If there is a bandit menace, it naturally must be eliminated. Besides, General Shen has already revealed his identity just now, and the common people have knelt to thank the heavens for its grace. If we just ignore it, wouldn't that ruin His Majesty's prestige?\" Qin Shaozong said.","Shen Tianming choked for a moment. He had made up his mind not to get involved. \"If you want to eradicate the bandits, go ahead. But ultimately, this matter is not part of my mission. Forgive me, but I cannot accompany you.\"","\"As you wish.\" Qin Shaozong was surprisingly easy to talk to.","Then, right in front of Shen Tianming, he summoned Feng Feng. \"Feng Feng, pick a few sharp scouts to go and scout the terrain of Spring Sprout Mountain tonight.\"","Feng Feng: \"Yes, sir.\"","In just a few short sentences, the bandit eradication matter was set in stone.","Shen Tianming said in a cryptic tone, \"Then I wish Marquis Qin victory upon the first unfurling of your banner.\"","Qin Shaozong accepted it entirely. \"You are too kind.\"","The houses in the village were mostly single-story. As they spoke outside, Dai Li could hear them clearly from inside the room. They talked about their matters, while she busied herself with hers.","Shen Tianming left after finishing his important business. Dai Li, who was busy in the room, heard the creaking sound of the wooden door's hinges. A man's footsteps approached, but she did not look up, remaining focused on her work.","The woman sitting on the wooden chair had delicate eyebrows like dark ink, and her face was gorgeously beautiful, resembling a peony in full, stunning bloom.","At this moment, she had her eyes cast down, looking at the small pouch gradually taking shape in her hands. Her dark eyes were steeped in a faint smile, and her whole being seemed enveloped in a soft, peaceful halo that made it impossible for anyone to look away.","Qin Shaozong's footsteps suddenly stopped, and he narrowed his long, narrow brown eyes.","These past few days of traveling, he rode a horse while she rode in the carriage. The only time they spent together for a slightly longer period was at night. He had previously thought she was just embroidering handkerchiefs out of boredom, but looking at it now, that was not the case...","\"What is Madame embroidering?\" he asked, despite already knowing the answer.","Dai Li didn't hide it. \"Embroidering a small pouch. Earlier, when I was visiting the market in the small county, I saw an old man selling peace amulets. He said the peace amulet was brought back from a distant temple, and the paper used to fold it had been steeped in the chanting of eminent monks for over half a year, and it was only meant for those destined for it.\"","Speaking of this, Daili could not help but smile. \"Actually, I also know that his words were somewhat exaggerated. Strictly speaking, a peace amulet is just a piece of paper. But at the thought of Zhou Zhou and Qinian going to wipe out the bandits, I still couldn't resist buying it.\"","He stared unblinkingly at the item in her hands and offered a very sincere suggestion. \"Since the peace amulets were bought, why should you, Madam, exhaust yourself with needle and thread? Wouldn't it be just as well to casually buy two pouches outside?\"","Daili disagreed. \"How is that the same? The temple is too far, and I have no way to go there, but embroidering small pouches is not something I am incapable of doing.\"","In truth, her embroidery skills were not very good either. After all, she had only learned needlework on a whim from Nianxia and the others last winter.","Qin Shaozong asked again, \"Barring any accidents, the bandit suppression operation is set for the day after tomorrow. Do you plan to rush and finish the small pouches before then, Madam?\"","\"That is natural. When the time comes, the two brothers will each wear one.\" Daili calculated in her heart, thinking that she would definitely be in time by the day after tomorrow.","She had started making the pouches ten days ago. At first, she had even ruined one. Fortunately, the pouches only needed to hold the peace amulets, so it did not matter if they were made small. Otherwise, she really would not have made it in time.","\"Does everyone going to suppress the bandits get one?\" he continued to ask.","Daili was not a slow-witted person. He rarely dwelled on a single matter, asking about it over and over again like this. She paused her movements and finally looked up at him.","With this glance, Daili met his amber-brown eyes. Those mirror-like eyes gazed at her, a rarely seen darkness surging in their depths.","Daili coughed lightly. \"Yes, but you are not going to suppress the bandits...\"","\"Who says I am not going?\" he cut her off.","Daili parted her red lips slightly, but in the end, she said nothing.","Why would this man go? During the previous night attack, half of the imperial court's men were killed, and that attendant surnamed Guo had an arm chopped off, yet he had not personally set out to pursue the culprits.","Now, these were just ordinary mountain bandits, and he had already thoroughly scouted the vicinity beforehand. What difficulty could there possibly be in this bandit suppression?","Qin Shaozong sat down beside her, took one of the small pouches, and examined it.","The pouch was dark blue and plain, with nothing embroidered on it. It was already small to begin with, and in the man's large, dark palm, it looked even more petite and exquisite. Let alone half, it probably only took up about a quarter of his hand.","After looking it over, Qin Shaozong said, \"This is that boy Qin Yanzhou's first time going into battle. As his father, I ought to be by his side to look after him a bit.\"","Daili: \"...\"","\"Do the words you just said still count, Madam?\" Qin Shaozong asked again.","Seeing him turning her ninety-percent-finished pouch over and over in his hands, his intentions couldn't be more obvious. Daili had no choice but to say, \"...They count.\"","Qin Shaozong smiled. \"Then I will quietly await the good news from you, Madam.\"","...","A night passed in the blink of an eye.","After waking up, Daili continued to finish her small pouches. The two pouches were mostly completed yesterday, so the finishing touches were quick. They were completely done exactly at the hour of Si.","After finishing the two, Daili hesitated for a moment before finally taking another small pouch out of a small wooden box.","This pouch was the one she had first started sewing, the very one she had ruined initially. At the time, she was using scissors to cut a thread inside the carriage when the carriage wheel happened to get stuck in a small pit. In the jolt, the scissors slipped and accidentally snipped the surface of the pouch.","With a piece of the surface fabric missing, it could no longer be used. She simply set it aside and took new fabric to sew it all over again.","Of course, apart from the ruined surface, the stitches on this first pouch were also understandably crude.","Daili stared at the little thing in her hand and suddenly chuckled softly. \"New for three years, old for three years, patched and mended for another three years. Don't even think about making me embroider a new one.\"","...","Time unknowingly reached the hour of Shen, and the scouts sent out earlier returned.","The scouts gave a detailed report on the situation around Chunmiao Mountain, including the location of the bandit camp, the number of enemies, the main paths up the mountain, the frequency of their shift changes, and some simple defensive equipment around the bandit stronghold. They didn't even leave out the locations of the streams in the mountains.","Simply put, one side of Chunmiao Mountain was a sheer cliff. There were only three viable paths up the mountain: the main eastern and western roads, plus a small trail on the back mountain.","After listening to the report, Qin Shaozong began to assign tasks. \"We move at the end of the Yin hour tonight. We will divide our forces into three routes. Feng Feng, you will lead forty men to ambush the rear trail. There is no need for a forced attack; just wait for them to fall into the trap. Qin the Second, you and Bai Jianping will lead eighty men up from the east. Qin San, you and Wei Qing will lead another eighty men to attack the west. You two must act according to orders and not be reckless.\"","The end of the Yin hour, converted to modern time, would be 5:00 AM.","The Yin hour was the darkest time before dawn. By the time the first wave of sneak attacks was over, the sky would be light. It would be just right for daytime combat, minimizing the bandits' terrain advantage.","The few men cupped their hands in obedience, and the two Black Cavalry platoon leaders quickly went to prepare. Qin Yanzhou and Qin Qinian were also about to follow them out but were stopped by Daili, who was coming out of the room.","The two turned around simultaneously and, seeing Daili waving at them, both obediently walked over.","Daili handed the small pouches to the two brothers, one for each. \"I made you small pouches, and there is a peace amulet inside. Take it with you when you go into battle. Go happily, and return safely.\"","Both of them were stunned for a moment.","Qin Yanzhou looked at the small pouch and couldn't help but murmur, \"Mother...\"","\"Thank you, Mother!\" Qin Qinian acted as if he had found a precious treasure. He held it in his hand, turning it over and over to look at it, and then opened the pouch to peek inside. The corners of his mouth rose higher and higher until he finally smiled, revealing a row of white teeth. \"Rest assured, Mother. I will definitely come back exactly as I left.\"","Qin Shaozong stood to the side, watching the two youngsters constantly fiddling with the pouches. No matter how he looked at it, it was an eyesore. He clicked his tongue lightly. \"Alright, you two hurry up and go scout the terrain.\"","After the older and younger boys were chased away, Qin Shaozong looked at Daili. \"Madam.\"","Daili knew what he meant and slowly took another small pouch out of her sleeve. \"This one is for you.\"","Qin Shaozong's original intention was just to remind her not to forget his. Because he also knew that she had only recently learned needlework and was not yet skilled, but he didn't expect her to immediately pull out a small pouch.","He took it and couldn't resist asking, \"Did you really embroider this yourself, Madam, without asking anyone else to do it for you?\"","Daili got angry out of nowhere. It was already good enough that she had made one for him in passing, yet this man actually dared to doubt this and that. She immediately reached out to snatch it back. \"It wasn't embroidered by me, so don't take it.\"","\"How can there be a reason to take back what has been given?\" Qin Shaozong raised his long arm, making her grab at empty air. The man held the pouch and looked at it again and again. The item in his palm was made of the same material as the ones she had just given to the two boys, and the size was identical.","The difference was that the brothers' pouches were plain, with nothing embroidered on either side, whereas his had a small flower embroidered on one side.","Qin Shaozong paused.","Looking closely, it really was a small flower, even smaller than his pinky fingernail, and it inexplicably had a somewhat cute feel to it.","Seeing him staring at the patch, Daili quickly said, \"I only bought two peace amulets back then, so there's nothing inside this one.\"","Qin Shaozong replied with an \"Mm,\" not minding at all, as he was still looking at the pouch.","Daili glanced at his expression and said tentatively, \"Husband, since you said earlier that you were going into battle, please help me look after Zhou Zhou a bit. It is his first time on the battlefield, after all, and he has no experience.\"","He finally looked over, his tone unreadable. \"So, is Madam trying to bribe me?\"","Dai Li said nothing.","He snorted. \"Qin Yanzhou is my son too. You have no need to worry, Madam.\"","Since there was an operation that night, everyone spent the day catching up on sleep. When night fell and the hour slowly crept toward Hai, the soldiers, led by Qin Shaozong, set out for Chunmiao Mountain.","Two hundred men were deployed for this mission, leaving the remaining one hundred to guard the base camp.","Chunmiao Mountain was not too far from the village. However, considering that horses would be useless going up the mountain and riding at night might alert the bandits, Qin Shaozong and his men abandoned their mounts and proceeded on foot.","The night was thick, and a bright moon hung high in the sky, shedding a graceful, silvery glow.","After traversing the initial stretch and nearing Chunmiao Mountain, Feng Feng, who was tasked with guarding the back mountain trail, was the first to lead his men away from the main group.","After walking another distance, it was time to split up toward the east and west.","Bai Jianping was in charge of the east. He looked at Qin Shaozong, awaiting his orders.","Although the Marquis had previously ordered him to take the east and let Old Wei take the west, that was when the Marquis himself had not yet arrived. Now...","And Bai Jianping was not the only one waiting for orders; Wei Qing was too.","Qin Shaozong said calmly, \"I will be on the eastern side tonight.\"","Wei Qing understood. He cupped his hands to his superior and continued leading his men forward.","It was exactly the Zi hour, not yet the agreed time. The men silently climbed a short distance up the mountain and then found the cover the scouts had previously discovered to rest temporarily.","Qin Shaozong sat on the ground, and beside him was Qin Yanzhou.","In this night of mounting tension, Qin Shaozong spoke as if making idle chatter: \"I have seen the agreement you signed with Madam.\"","The young man turned his head, his dark eyes calm.","\"As they say, the first step is always the hardest. If you can pass the first hurdle smoothly, everything else will be easy,\" Qin Shaozong said suddenly. \"Qin the Second, how about you stay right here and wait tonight?\"","Qin Yanzhou froze.","According to the agreement, he could not suffer even the slightest injury. If he just came along but stayed at the foot of the mountain without advancing, he would indeed be one hundred percent safe from harm.","This was exploiting a loophole in the agreement.","The young man remained silent for a moment before finally shaking his head. His eyes sparkled like gemstones under the moonlight. \"No, I will follow you up the mountain. I can hide for a while, but not for a lifetime.\"","Qin Shaozong chuckled softly. \"You're quite resolute, kid.\"","Time flew by in a flash. Soon it was the Yin hour, slowly shifting from the beginning of Yin to the end of Yin.","Qin Shaozong looked up at the sky. Seeing that the time was right, he blew a bird whistle.","\"Tweet—\"","The surrounding grass rustled into action. The rustling sound moved all the way up, reaching the wooden palisade made of stakes and spikes halfway up the mountain.","More than two zhang behind the palisade, two figures were dozing with their arms crossed.","Qin Yanzhou picked up a longbow and, along with Bai Jianping, nocked an arrow, drew the bowstring, and aimed at the targets.","The two released their grips almost simultaneously.","With two swooshing sounds tearing through the wind, both arrows struck their targets right in the heart. Two streams of crimson blood spurted out, splashing successively onto the grassy earth.","Seeing this, a Northern soldier in front of the palisade took the lead, raising his saber and hacking down. With a loud crack, he chopped the wooden stakes into pieces, and the Northern army behind him flooded in like a tide.","After passing two checkpoints in succession, the sleeping bandits finally realized what was happening.","Gongs and drums clanged, echoing across the mountaintop.","The mountainside, which had previously been cloaked in darkness, seemed to instantly summon a fiery dragon. The bright, fiery dragon quickly climbed the enclosure, forming a small circle and illuminating the area as bright as day.","\"Enemy attack! Get up quickly, enemy attack!\" someone shouted at the top of their lungs.","\"Hurry, wake everyone up.\"","\"Damn it, is it the government officials again? They just suffered a loss last time, how could they forget their lesson so quickly?\"","Amidst the clamor, the pale white of a fish's belly slowly rose in the east, and the night gradually faded away.","The bandit lair was in complete chaos. Some bandits hadn't even dressed properly, rushing out bare-chested with their sabers and slashing at anyone they saw.","Clad in a black robe and wielding a scimitar, Qin Yanzhou attacked a house from which bandits continuously poured out, accompanied by several Northern soldiers.","Iron blades clashed and scraped against each other, producing a grating sound that gave one goosebumps.","The young man's scimitar moved like a dragon, wiping a streak of blood red wherever the blade passed. His slashing motions never ceased, the crimson flashing out vague afterimages. The growing light fell upon his handsome, icy features, giving him the ruthless air of a jade-faced Asura.","\"Thud, roll...\"","Heavy objects continuously rolled and fell; with every landing thud, someone's expression was frozen forever.","Crimson quietly pooled together. Some seeped into the soil, softening the mud; some fell to the roots of the vegetation, silently absorbed while no one was watching.","\"Not good, there are people on both the east and west sides. We can't go west either.\"","\"Something's wrong. Why are the government troops this time different from the last?\"","Bai Jianping grinned, \"Could your granddaddy be the same as those spineless weaklings from Yanzhou?!\"","Wang Hu hadn't expected that in just one night, their past glory would be completely shattered. Holding a longbow, he hid in a pile of tall trees, his eyes wide and bloodshot as he watched his comrades fall one by one. \"You all deserve to die!\"","The enemy had launched a night raid, attacking simultaneously from the east and west. Their numbers were about the same as the bandits', but they were several times more ferocious.","\"I have to take one down with me.\" Wang Hu drew his bow, first aiming at the black-robed young man below.","But after pausing for a moment, he deliberately shifted his arrowhead away.","This person was incredibly agile; it was hard to say whether this rare shot would hit.","He aimed at someone else.","Releasing his fingers, the long arrow flew out with a swish.","For a split second, Qin Yanzhou felt a chilling killing intent, but in the next instant, the intent vanished without a trace.","He dispatched a man with a backhand strike, only to suddenly see a long arrow hurtling toward him from not far away, aimed straight at a Northern soldier two steps away. At this moment, the soldier was fighting one against two, holding off a pair of bandits.","Qin Yanzhou's pupils shrank abruptly. On the other side, a bandit saw him distracted and raised his saber to slash at him.","In this instant, many things flashed through Qin Yanzhou's mind.","He remembered this soldier's name; the man was called Xun He, loved his wine, and was a very hearty fellow. Just yesterday, Xun He had told Mo Yanyun that after this battle, he would exchange his accumulated military merits for silver to buy new clothes for his wife and children back home.","He also thought of that agreement, and his mother's worried eyes...","The myriad thoughts swept by rapidly; in just a fraction of a second, he had made his decision.","The young man swiftly stepped forward, using his scimitar to knock away the deadly long arrow, and then quickly pulled his blade back to block. However, due to the extra movement he had just made, the bandit's saber was slightly faster, and the tip of the blade pressed into Qin Yanzhou's arm.","His robe was sliced open, and he felt a trace of pain in his arm."]},{"number":150,"title":"Chapter 150","paragraphs":["The young man's eyes turned cold. Just as he reversed his grip on the scimitar resting against his arm and was about to exert force, he heard the sound of something piercing the wind, followed by a spray of bright red blood.","The bandit, who had been grinning with a face full of smugness from his successful sneak attack, suddenly widened his eyes. He stiffly lowered his head, looking in disbelief at the arrowhead protruding from his chest.","Not far away, after firing an arrow, Qin Shaozong expressionlessly drew his bow again. The second arrow aimed at Wang Hu, who was hiding in the tall vegetation.","Wang Hu had just shot an arrow, and a small half of his body was currently exposed. Seeing that his shot had failed, he hurriedly hid into the dense grass.","Nocking the arrow and drawing the bow in one smooth motion, the man's long, thick-knuckled fingers released the tiger-sinew string.","Another arrow flew out like a shooting star.","This arrow carried even more force than the previous one. When it first entered the grass, it swept through like a sickle, slicing off a handful of emerald leaves before fiercely plunging into it, drawing out a miserable scream.","Qin Yanzhou glanced at the stalwart man not far away. He didn't say anything and turned to help Xun He, who was fighting two enemies at once behind him.","The two bandits fell one after another.","Xun He was not unaware of the danger just now, but he truly had no way to free up his hands. After surviving the perilous situation, he broke out in a cold sweat and hurriedly thanked Qin Yanzhou, \"Thank you, Second Young Master, for saving my life.\"","Qin Yanzhou only gave a slight nod, similarly saying nothing. His black eyelashes lowered slightly as his gaze fell on his right arm.","Coming to exterminate the bandits today, everyone's attire was different from their loose everyday clothes. Including him and Qin Qinian, they all wore black armor. However, to make it easier to climb the mountain and pursue the enemy on foot, they did not wear heavy armor that covered them from head to toe.","Black armor was black iron armor. Its defense was superior to cloth and leather armor, but because it contained iron, it was much heavier than the latter two.","Like the other Northern Army soldiers, Qin Yanzhou's black armor only covered his upper body, plus a piece of fauld armor to protect his lower body. On his upper half, besides the breastplate protecting vital areas like his chest, there were only shoulder guards protecting his upper arms.","The shoulder guards barely reached the middle of his upper arms, and underneath was Qin Yanzhou's black robe. At this moment, the black robe on the side of his elbow had a tear about a finger's length long.","The dark-colored robe concealed everything, making it impossible to tell whether he was bleeding or not.","The young man dejectedly lowered his hand, and it took a long while before he lifted his sword to continue forward. A few paces away, Qin Shaozong took in his expression completely.","Attacked from both the east and west, the bandits were like driven sheep, only able to flee through the rear path. After the Northern Army initially converged, their offensive grew even fiercer.","Seeing Qin Yanzhou, Qin Qinian happily trotted over. \"Second Brother, how many bandit heads did you take?\"","Qin Yanzhou said he didn't remember.","\"How can you not remember such an important matter?\" Qin Qinian frowned. Seeing the other looking him over as if searching for something, he smiled and patted his chest. \"I'm not injured. The peace amulet Mother gave me works perfectly.\"","Of course, another reason was that he was worried about accidentally scraping his skin this time, which would mean he'd have to bury his head in reading and writing when he got back, so he was especially careful.","\"How are things on your end?\" the youth asked.","Qin Yanzhou casually flicked the blood off his blade. \"Not bad.\"","The bandit lair held not only bandits but also some women abducted from elsewhere, including young ones as well as older ones specifically responsible for cooking.","When the sounds of fighting first started, the women had heard it, but no one dared to come out. Now that the battle was basically over, people gradually began to peek out.","After seeing the ground covered in bandit corpses, some wept tears of joy, while others were numb and bewildered. It wasn't until someone unknown shouted, \"It seems the government has come to exterminate the bandits,\" that the women erupted in excitement and swarmed outside.","Qin Shaozong called upon Wei Qing, having him lead a few soldiers to temporarily settle these women, while he led the rest to continue pursuing the remaining bandits.","The Qin brothers went along with Qin Shaozong.","They pursued for a distance when suddenly they heard shouts of killing coming from ahead.","\"Oh, it looks like Uncle Feng and the others have made their move.\" Qin Qinian rubbed his fists and wiped his palms, then said to Qin Shaozong, \"Father, let's hurry over. A pincer attack from front and back will beat them to a pulp!\"","Qin Shaozong: \"Qin San, you and Bai Jianping lead the men and go quickly first. Qin the Second and I will come shortly.\"","The few who were called out didn't understand why, but they complied anyway. A group of people rushed forward to chase the enemy. Soon, only Qin Shaozong and Qin Yanzhou were left on this small path leading to the back mountain.","After the murderous troops left, the birds that had been startled away earlier landed back on the treetops, tilting their heads to observe the remaining father and son walking side by side.","Qin Shaozong walked on the young man's right side. Lowering his head slightly, he could see the torn sleeve. \"Were you injured just now? Is it serious?\"","Qin Yanzhou stiffened, only shaking his head without speaking. It was as if a heavy dark cloud enveloped his head, and his mood was much lower than before.","\"Qin the Second, putting the agreement aside, do you still want to go to the battlefield after this?\" Qin Shaozong asked again.","\"I do.\" Qin Yanzhou did not hesitate. He twitched the corners of his mouth, as if wanting to say something else, but in the end, he only revealed a bitter and helpless smile.","The agreement couldn't be put aside. Mother was so sharp; once he returned, she would definitely know everything. So what was the use of just wanting it?","He could no longer...","\"As long as you want to, that's enough. I see you've only suffered a minor injury. Since that's the case, secretly sew up this tear in your sleeve, and then you can pretend nothing happened,\" Qin Shaozong laughed.","Qin Yanzhou stopped in his tracks, utterly astonished.","\"Why so surprised? Is what I said not feasible? Although Madam dotes on you, you are already an adult. A grown son avoids his mother; she definitely won't order you to strip naked for her to inspect. When she asks, just insist that you weren't injured,\" the curve of Qin Shaozong's mouth deepened.","Qin Yanzhou's eyes widened slightly. \"But...\"","\"I'll teach you a lesson today: the wise adapt to circumstances, the foolish stick to the rules, and those who achieve great things do not sweat the small stuff.\" Qin Shaozong pulled out a small pouch embroidered with flowers from who knows where.","He didn't look at the young man beside him again, his gaze falling on the pouch. \"You want to establish merit and build a career. Aside from realizing your ambitions, I think Madam is also a significant reason for this. Her not wanting you to risk your life on the battlefield is purely out of a loving mother's heart, which is completely understandable. After all, something lost and found is far more precious than something that has always been by one's side. But are you really willing to live a mediocre life forever, unable to repay your mother's grace?\"","Qin Yanzhou unconsciously pressed his lips tightly together.","Hearing no response, Qin Shaozong didn't rush him.","The man's long, heavily callused fingers brushed over the small flowers on the pouch. There was no peace amulet inside, but it wasn't flat and empty either; it bulged with a noticeable curve.","His fingers squeezed open the mouth of the pouch, faintly revealing a small piece of jade inside. It had a long and narrow shape, looking like a brush rest.","\"I've said all I have to say. You can consider the rest yourself.\" Qin Shaozong suddenly tightened his large hand, firmly grasping the small pouch.","As if remembering something, he smiled and added one more sentence, \"If you are willing to do as I say, find a trustworthy woman and have her quickly sew up your outer robe for you.\"","With that said, Qin Shaozong no longer walked leisurely and picked up his pace to catch up with the main force ahead.","Qin Yanzhou followed.","\"Achoo!\" Dai Li suddenly sneezed.","Nianxia said nervously, \"Madam, let this servant add a layer of clothing for you. As the saying goes, bundle up in spring and stay cool in autumn; you mustn't catch a cold.\"","Dai Li rubbed her nose. \"I don't feel cold.\"","But Nianxia still went back to fetch a piece of clothing.","Dai Li looked in the direction of Mount Chunmiao and murmured, \"It's already the end of the Mao hour. They should be in the latter half of their operation over there. I hope everything goes smoothly.\"","Whether it was an illusion or not, Dai Li thought she heard the clashing of weapons. Just as she was about to listen more closely, she saw a man rushing in from outside the courtyard.","\"Madam, the end of the village has been attacked by bandits. Please stay together with Lady Shi and do not wander around.\" The newcomer was Hu Bao.","Dai Li was greatly astonished. \"Bandits attacking the end of the village? But the village end and Mount Chunmiao are in two opposite directions and aren't close to each other. How could those bandits...\"","She suddenly paused, recalling the attack from half a month ago.","Since that night attack, the \"bandits\" had not appeared again. Now it seemed they hadn't fled, but had been hiding and waiting for an opportunity to strike.","And Qin Shaozong leading his men to wipe out the bandits was exactly that \"opportunity.\"","After her initial shock, she quickly calmed down. \"It's fine. I heard that the initial night attack involved no more than a hundred men, and over half of them were slain by your blades. If it is the same group this time, they likely have less than fifty men left. Meanwhile, we have over a hundred men, giving us the numerical advantage. However, their purpose for this attack should be the same as before. Hu Bao, the imperial court officials must be kept safe; we cannot let them be killed.\"","Hu Bao said solemnly, \"Please rest assured, Madam. We will definitely not let those scoundrels succeed.\"","Dai Li smiled faintly. \"Thank you for your hard work.\"","After Hu Bao left, Shi Rongyue and her personal maid quickly arrived at the courtyard where Dai Li was staying, gathering together.","At that time, Dai Li was speaking with the owner of the courtyard. She and Qin Shaozong were staying at the village chief's house, and the person conversing with her right now was the old village chief's daughter-in-law.","\"...Yes, there is only one den of bandits nearby, and speaking of which, they only appeared the year before last. At first, there were only about a dozen of them. I heard they were fugitives from somewhere who fled to Mount Chunmiao to become outlaws. They often robbed passing merchants. Later, news spread that there were bandits here, and somehow, more and more people came here to become outlaws,\" the village woman said.","Dai Li looked thoughtful. \"Only one den of bandits. So, it really is them.\"","The village woman didn't understand who \"they\" referred to and was extremely worried. \"Noble lady, there are bandits in the east and bandits in the west. With us unable to defend both ends, could it be that...\"","If they couldn't hold them off and the bandits truly entered the village, the first to bear the brunt would definitely be defenseless villagers like them.","Dai Li looked up at the sky.","The end of the Mao hour. It had barely been one shichen since the end of the Yin hour. One shichen, two hours.","For completely eradicating a bandit den, it was still too early.","Dai Li massaged the space between her eyebrows.","She had appeared very calm in front of Hu Bao just now, but only Dai Li herself knew that she was still somewhat worried.","Her previous assurance that it was \"fine\" was entirely based on her assumption that the enemy had only fifty men. If they had more than fifty...","Dai Li looked at the village woman and asked, \"Do you have a drum here?\"","*","On Mount Chunmiao.","In large-scale wars, if the defeated side surrendered in time, they most likely wouldn't lose their heads.","Prisoners of war, representing human resources, were undoubtedly valuable assets. Just like the battle in Yanzhou last year, the defeated Yanzhou army was reorganized by Qin Shaozong and entirely converted into a labor force for farming.","However, this time was an exception.","The bandits' numerous evil deeds were one reason; Qin Shaozong harboring certain ulterior motives was another. In short, he did not give the order to leave any survivors.","By the time the father and son arrived, this one-sided, crushing skirmish was almost over.","The corpses of the bandits lay scattered haphazardly. Blood flowed continuously from their severed necks or chests, gathering into small puddle-like shallow pits on the ground, only to be splashed in all directions when stepped on by latecomers.","Seeing Qin Shaozong arrive, Bai Jianping reported, \"Marquis, the bandits have been entirely eradicated. The number of bandits who attempted to flee down the mountain totals fifty-two.\"","\"Fifty-two, plus the corpses up on the mountain, this bandit den must have had over a hundred people.\" Qin Qinian clicked his tongue. \"I didn't expect it to be such a large den.\"","Qin Shaozong was just about to speak when he suddenly heard the continuous beating of a drum from afar. The man's face instantly turned cold as he turned to look in the direction of the village.","Among many instruments, the penetrating power of a drum is second to none, which is why drums are often used in marches and sacrifices to transmit messages or boost morale.","The others were all stunned in disbelief.","\"Was that a drum just now? Who is beating the drum?\"","\"Wait, that's not an ordinary drumbeat. It's a military march signal!\"","\"It seems to be coming from the direction of the village. How could this be? We launched a night attack on the bandit den. Logically speaking, the bandits should all be fast asleep during the Yin hour. How could they have gone down the mountain?\"","Qin Shaozong ordered, \"Bai Jianping and Qin San, you two lead twenty men to clear the battlefield. The rest of you, follow me back.\"","Being called out, Qin Qinian instinctively responded. After answering, he looked over at Qin Yanzhou.","Father hadn't called out his second brother's name, which meant his second brother would also be going back with Father to kill the enemy? If it were normally, he would have definitely fought for the chance, but today...","Cough, never mind. Better obey orders first.","Qin Qinian, whose sleeve had just been sliced open by a bandit's blade tip—though without breaking the skin—still felt a lingering fear.","*","The small mountain village.","Deng Qianfeng's eyes were bloodshot from the killing. After a fierce back-and-forth struggle with Hu Bao, he belatedly realized that his battle line hadn't advanced inward much at all.","\"Thump, thump, thump—\"","The sound of a drum abruptly erupted within the village.","Being a military man himself, Deng Qianfeng knew instantly upon hearing it that this was a military march signal. His expression immediately turned quite ugly. While blocking Hu Bao's attacks, he roared, \"We don't have much time! Scatter and enter the village!\"","A village is different from a walled city. The former is built in an accessible area with roads leading everywhere, while the latter is protected by city walls. To enter the village, besides the front and back mountain roads suitable for carriages and horses, one could also slip in through the tall grass or the woods.","Hearing the order, the others immediately scattered in all directions.","The veins on Hu Bao's forehead throbbed.","The Marquis had left a hundred men to protect the Madam. A hundred men was a third of their total force, which was already quite a lot. However, for a hundred men to protect an entire village of a thousand people while also trying their best to kill \"bandits\" who were slithering around everywhere like loaches, it was undeniably a strenuous task.","Especially since the troops stationed at the Madam's courtyard were fixed and absolutely could not be moved.","With the village in chaos, how could Guo Nai and Shen Tianming, who were staying in another location, not hear the commotion?","Guo Nai could not conceal his astonishment. \"Didn't the Marquis of Wu'an lead his men to wipe out the bandits? How could bandits enter the village? Could it be that the remnants were forced down the mountain and stumbled into the village?\"","As a military general, Shen Tianming had more experience in this area than Guo Nai. He frowned and shook his head. \"It doesn't look like it to me. Mount Chunmiao is to the east, but those sounds are coming from the west. Furthermore, if the remnant bandits wanted to flee, why would they escape toward a crowded place?\"","Guo Nai's expression looked grim. \"Could it be that again...\"","At this moment, a soldier from the Northern lands arrived outside.","The newcomer cupped his hands in greeting and got straight to the point: \"General Shen, Attendant Guo, the village is under attack. The bandits are coming in fiercely, and our forces are limited. I hope you two and the other imperial soldiers will not leave the courtyard.\"","He was purely there to pass on a message, and having said his piece, the man promptly left.","After Guo Nai's expression shifted several times, he suddenly looked at Shen Tianming beside him. \"General Shen, do you think this bandit disaster is a self-directed act?\"","Shen Tianming stroked his chin. \"It's hard to say.\"","Guo Nai gave a sinister chuckle. \"General Shen, the safest place in this village right now is not where we are standing.\"","Hearing the hidden meaning in his words, Shen Tianming asked, \"What do you mean?\"","\"How about we go find the Marquis's wife?\" A ruthless glint flashed in Guo Nai's eyes. \"If this bandit attack is just a front put up by the Marquis of Wu'an, we'll take his wife and niece as hostages. If I'm wrong, that's fine too—we can just use the guards around her to protect ourselves.\"","\"Excellent!\"","*","When Qin Shaozong hurriedly led his men back to the village, the main road was already stained with blood, and the clashing of blades echoed from afar.","The imposing man coldly raised his hand and pressed it forward. Without a word, the Northern soldiers behind him surged like tigers released from their cages, swiftly charging into the scattered skirmishes in all directions.","Qin Shaozong headed straight for the village chief's house, effortlessly dispatching any bandits who crossed his path along the way.","The closer he got, the more casualties he saw on both sides. The thick stench of blood carried by the wind made it feel as though a wet, bloody towel had been pressed over one's nose.","\"My Lord!\" The guards stationed outside the courtyard were thrilled to see Qin Shaozong return.","The wooden courtyard gate was mostly destroyed, leaving only half of it hanging askew and creaking slightly in the wind.","His gaze pierced through the entrance, and only when he saw the woman in the smoky-purple ruqun standing in the courtyard did the taut string in his mind finally snap loose.","Qin Shaozong let out a heavy breath.","Only then did he spare attention for the rest of the scene. Seeing Dai Li and Shi Rongrong both in the courtyard rather than inside, he asked, \"Why aren't you and Rongrong inside the house?\"","Seeing him return with a contingent of Northern soldiers waiting outside, Dai Li honestly felt a wave of relief. \"General Shen and Attendant Guo are inside. The situation is... a bit peculiar.\"","Qin Shaozong frowned. \"Why aren't they staying in their own quarters? Why take over ours like cuckoos in a magpie's nest?\"","Dai Li explained, \"Attendant Guo said he was worried I might be harmed by the bandits, so he rushed over to help. But on his way here, he was ambushed by hidden thieves and had an arm chopped off. Mr. Ding and General Shen are inside looking after him now.\"","Everyone was astonished.","Qin Shaozong let out an undisguised laugh of mockery. \"Tsk, it seems the heavens couldn't stand how uncoordinated he was, so they sent someone to chop off his other arm to match.\"","Dai Li: \"...Keep your voice down.\"","As if suddenly remembering something, Qin Shaozong turned his head to Qin Yanzhou beside him. \"Qin the Second, this place is filthy. Take Shi Rongrong next door.\""]},{"number":151,"title":"Chapter 151","paragraphs":["Take Rongrong to the next door?","Qin Yanzhou's back could not help but tense up. He subconsciously looked at Dai Li, but saw that his mother was turning her head to look into the room at the moment, seemingly worried that her father's words just now had been heard by the people in the room.","Mother didn't notice...","Qin Yanzhou then looked at Shi Rongyue, who happened to be looking at him too. After their eyes met, the little girl took the initiative to walk two steps toward the courtyard entrance.","Scene after scene flashed through Qin Yanzhou's mind, including when he was in kindergarten, when he was eating grass roots while fleeing from famine, when he was in the Qinglian Sect, and when he was reunited with his mother.","He lowered his eyes for a moment, and when he raised them again, the waves in his dark eyes had leveled out, \"Rongrong, come with me.\"","After walking out of the village chief's courtyard, Shi Rongyue, remembering the agreement, asked, \"Brother Zhongle, did your bandit suppression go smoothly this time?\"","Qin Yanzhou knew what she meant, \"It was generally smooth, but there was a little problem...\"","\"What problem?\" Shi Rongyue asked hurriedly before he could finish, \"Brother Zhongle, are you hurt?\"","Her small face, which had just regained some color, turned pale with fright, and she sized him up nervously. But because she was walking on Qin Yanzhou's left side, she couldn't see anything.","Qin Yanzhou didn't expect her to react like this, and his footsteps paused for a moment. The young man shook his head and simply said, \"Rongrong, can you do me a favor?\"","She was still looking him up and down. Hearing that, she nodded without hesitation, \"Yes! Tell me, Brother Zhongle.\"","The amplitude of her nod was a bit large, which caused the tuft of ahoge on Shi Rongyue's head to sway violently.","Qin Yanzhou suddenly had an illusion that the cute little puppy from the old professor next door seemed to have returned.","Its light brown fur puffed up like a fluffy cotton candy, and its eyes shone with a honey-like luster in the sunlight. Usually, it liked to play with him very much. Whether it was the ball he threw or some small instructions, it would receive them happily.","In a puppy's world, there is no haze.","Two pairs of equally clear eyes seemed to slowly overlap across time and space. Qin Yanzhou couldn't help but curl his lips into a slight smile, \"Rongrong, do you know needlework?\"","The topic changed so quickly that Shi Rongyue nodded blankly and honestly.","In this world, there were very few women who didn't know needlework. The daughters of commoners would rely on embroidery to help their families reduce the burden, while the young ladies of prominent families would embroider their own wedding dresses.","This was also why, when Dai Li first asked Nianxia and Bipo to teach her needlework, the two girls' eyes almost popped out.","While they were talking, the two arrived at Shi Rongyue's residence from last night.","She stayed at Widow Wang's house next to the village chief's, which was about a dozen steps away. And when the bandits attacked the village earlier, the defense line with Dai Li at the core was drawn all the way to this house.","Widow Wang stayed behind closed doors. Shi Rongyue took Qin Yanzhou into the side room and asked the maid to guard outside.","Most of the houses in the village were simple and crude, and this place was no exception, with only a bed, a cabinet, and a table. However, the room was cleaned very neatly, and there was a delicate and small incense burner placed in the corner.","A faint fragrance permeated the air, very fresh, like orchids blooming.","Qin Yanzhou took a seat next to the table. He raised his right arm and pointed to the tear on his right sleeve with his left hand, \"Rongrong, please help me sew up this tear.\"","Shi Rongyue only then saw that his sleeve was torn, and her pupils constricted, \"Brother Zhongle, are you really hurt?\"","\"It's nothing, just a minor injury.\" Qin Yanzhou urged, \"There isn't much time, Rongrong, sew it up first.\"","Shi Rongyue rummaged out a needle and thread from a small box and went back to kneel and sit beside him. Her small hands were chubby, but unexpectedly flexible, and she threaded the silver needle with a swish.","Qin Yanzhou went to battle today. In addition to wearing black armor and a shoulder cape, he also wore sleeve bindings on his forearms. The sleeve bindings bound up the wide sleeves, which also tightened the tear at the elbow.","He neatly removed the sleeve bindings and loosened the wide sleeves.","There was enough space, and there was no need to take off his clothes.","Shi Rongyue grabbed a corner of his sleeve, her eyelashes trembling a few times, trying her best to focus her attention on the tear of the sleeve, but she still couldn't stop a wisp of thought from diverging crazily.","She smelled a mixture of vegetation and blood.","The bloody smell that used to make her nauseous seemed to have become another smell after being mixed with the fragrance of grass, as if it had transformed into some kind of wine, making people tipsy after smelling it.","Shi Rongyue lowered her head even further, afraid that the person beside her would see the abnormality on her face.","The little girl held the needle in one hand and pulled the young man's hem with the other, continuing to pierce the robe with the silver needle.","No one spoke in the room, and there was only the slight sound of the needle and thread passing through the clothes.","Shi Rongyue's head dropped lower and lower, but the loud thumping sound intensified.","Qin Yanzhou was thinking about the follow-up. When he came back to his senses, he found a small head almost buried in the crook of his arm.","\"Rongrong?\" Qin Yanzhou was puzzled, \"Are you nearsighted?\"","\"...Ah!\"","*","The junior was intensely sewing clothes, and Dai Li was still in the main courtyard. At first, she also wanted to leave with her son, but was told by Qin Shaozong that the boy was fine and that she was needed here.","And later, something did happen.","The remaining arm of Guo Nai was chopped off by the bandits when he came to find her, and it was originally enough to do a good job of stopping the bleeding.","As long as the person is still there and alive, it's fine.","As a result, just after Ding Lianxi bandaged him, in less than a quarter of an hour, Guo Nai's lips suddenly turned black, and he actually vomited a mouthful of blood. He rolled his eyes and died.","This change was too fast, so fast that Ding Lianxi had no time to respond, and could only watch the person fall.","Shen Tianming was dumbfounded, and his questioning blurted out, \"What did you add to his wound?\"","\"You're making false accusations!\" Ding Lianxi was so angry that he lost the elegance of a doctor. \"I only stopped his bleeding and never did anything else.\"","\"Attendant Guo's lips were black, which is undoubtedly poisoning. And he was fine just now, so why did he die suddenly only after you touched him?\" Shen Tianming asked back.","Ding Lianxi felt very wronged, \"Naturally, he was poisoned before he came.\"","Shen Tianming sneered, \"You are a doctor. If he was poisoned earlier, how could you not tell? But you didn't mention a word. You clearly did it on purpose.\"","Ding Lianxi gritted his teeth and said, \"Stopping the bleeding of a severed arm cannot be delayed. How could there be so much time to observe, smell, ask, and feel the pulse?\"","\"You have a glib tongue,\" Shen Tianming only said.","\"General Shen,\" a cold and deep voice fell, carrying an undisguised sharp edge.","Shen Tianming's face became a bit uglier.","Qin Shaozong said lightly, \"General Shen, don't forget that the captive caught in the night attack also died of poisoning. The other party is good at using poison, and when they first attacked the camp, they came straight for you. Has General Shen ever thought that the imperial court's troops and horses were their target?\"","Shen Tianming retorted, \"When we camped that day, we didn't encounter any so-called passers-by. If the other party is a real bandit, how could they know the location of our camp?\"","After all that talk, he still suspected that the North was manipulating everything.","Qin Shaozong clicked his tongue lightly, unwilling to waste his breath with such a stupid person.","\"Lord Marquis, the bandit leader has been captured!\" At this time, Feng Feng's voice came from outside.","The few people in the room heard this and went out.","Dai Li didn't enter the room just now, but only stood outside and listened to their dispute. Now seeing Feng Feng and Hu Bao coming together, they were also holding down a man tied up.","The man had an ordinary appearance, his skin tanned dark, looking no different from a peasant. However, upon seeing Shen Tianming walking out alongside Qin Shaozong, he suddenly blurted out, \"I hope you will not break your promise, My Lord.\"","The expressions of everyone present changed drastically.","\"Cease your nonsense, you scoundrel! When did the Lord ever promise you anything!\" Feng Feng scolded.","Hu Bao was equally furious, \"You bastard, you clearly know you are at a dead end, so you're just biting at anyone you can.\"","Dai Li looked at Deng Qianfeng, then observed Shen Tianming. The latter's face was as dark as deep water, veins faintly pulsing on his forehead, clearly on the verge of explosive rage.","\"Mister Ding, quickly check his pulse to see if he has been poisoned,\" Dai Li reminded.","Feng and Hu awakened as if from a dream. Ignoring their verbal sparring with Deng Qianfeng, they hurriedly pressed the man down before Ding Lianxi for a pulse check.","Upon checking, sure enough, Deng Qianfeng had also been poisoned.","The subsequent rush to detoxify him goes without saying. In short, Qin Qinian, who had returned with Bai Jianping and the others, found the atmosphere in the village quite heavy upon his arrival.","After understanding the whole story, Qin Qinian trembled with anger, \"Absurd! If my father wanted to kill him, why would he need to use poison?\"","Qin Yanzhou held back the youth who was about to turn and leave, \"Wait until the bandit leader is cured of the poison. Do not cause any trouble at this moment.\"","One of the imperial court's leaders had already died; if something happened to the other, it would be truly difficult to explain.","Bai Jianping was still reporting, \"...My Lord, I interrogated a few survivors. Their confessions unanimously stated that there were one hundred and nineteen members in the stronghold. But I counted the corpses and the remaining captives, and the total is only one hundred and ten.\"","Nine people were missing.","The stronghold was located halfway up the mountain; these nine likely fled into the mountains during the chaos.","Qin Shaozong turned his thumb ring. \"It's normal, there are always some who are particularly clever. But it doesn't matter; these people won't dare to return, so they certainly won't interfere with our subsequent plans.\"","Bai Jianping nodded, but then hesitated slightly.","\"Is there something else?\" Qin Shaozong asked.","Since his superior asked, Bai Jianping had to reply, \"My Lord, among the rescued women, one claims to be from Qingzhou, a maid of the legitimate daughter of Governor Nangong. She said she was ordered by her master to come to Yanzhou to serve the young lady Nangong, but unexpectedly the journey was treacherous. While purchasing goods in a small county on the border of Qing and Yan provinces, she was accidentally abducted. Later, she found an opportunity to escape, but unfortunately, her luck was poor, and she jumped from the wolf's den straight into the tiger's lair. I asked her about Governor Nangong's appearance and the names of his family members, and she could answer them all. Her identity is likely genuine.\"","Qin Shaozong slightly raised his long eyebrows, his focus elsewhere. \"Nangong Xiong brought his daughter to Yanzhou?\"","Yanzhou was conquered through an alliance between the Northern Territory and Qingzhou. The Northern Territory was vast with many affairs to handle, and he had been in a hurry to return to Yuyang for his wedding. After leaving behind his trusted aides and a group of Xuanxiao Cavalry, he led his army north.","He wasn't surprised that Nangong Xiong was in Yanzhou, but he was surprised that the man had brought his daughter along.","Qin Shaozong said, \"Bring that maid here.\"","Bai Jianping received the order, and soon, a dirt-streaked young woman was led before Qin Shaozong.","Wenxin already knew who she was going to meet when she arrived. She immediately bowed down in fear and trepidation, \"This servant pays respects to the Marquis of Wu'an and the Marchioness.\"","Qin Shaozong got straight to the point, \"You previously said you were ordered by your master to come to Yanzhou to serve your young mistress. When did your young lady go to Yanzhou?\"","Wenxin did not dare to hide anything. \"At the end of winter last year.\"","Dai Li pondered for a moment in her heart.","Winter of last year...","She remembered that last winter, Qin Changgeng had mentioned in passing that the southern war had settled, and Liu of Jingzhou had annexed Yizhou, leaping to become the overlord of the south.","For Nangong Xiong to take his daughter away from Qingzhou at this time, could he be thinking of a marriage alliance with the southern forces?","But Dai Li felt it was unlikely. Qingzhou bordered Ji and Yan to the east, and Xuzhou to the south. Leaving the former aside, the latter meant there was a whole group of provincial governors who nominally belonged to the imperial court in between. He was separated from Liu of Jingzhou in the south by thousands of miles. There was no reason to stretch his hand so far to extend an olive branch; wasn't he afraid of having his hand broken off?","Dai Li couldn't figure it out.","Qin Shaozong fell silent for a moment, then waved the two of them away.","The Nangong family was not the main point right now. The main point was the upcoming imperial edict...","\"Things in Chang'an have brewed just about enough. Bring me that half-piece of the golden jade scroll,\" Qin Shaozong looked at Feng Feng, whose eyes suddenly lit up as he agreed heartily.","Hearing about the golden jade scroll, the corner of Dai Li's mouth twitched.","Qin Shaozong had sharp eyes. \"What is that expression, Madam?\"","\"I just admire your ability to find new uses for old things,\" Dai Li looked away.","Taking advantage of the empty courtyard, Qin Shaozong reached out and turned her head back. \"Since you admire your husband, why aren't you looking at him?\"","Dai Li: \"...I'm afraid he might get so puffed up he'd float away with the wind.\"","Qin Shaozong chuckled.","\"Impossible! Why would His Majesty summon you to the capital?\" Shen Tianming looked at Qin Shaozong as if he had seen a ghost. \"Where is the edict? Where is His Majesty's edict?\"","Qin Shaozong slowly took out a section of a golden jade scroll. The golden jade scroll was not alone; attached to its side was a small, tattered piece of silk damask.","In terms of material alone, this was indeed an edict used by the Son of Heaven.","Qin Shaozong said, \"The messenger carrying the edict originally headed north, probably learning later that I had changed my route to Yanzhou, and pursued me here. However, likely due to traveling day and night without rest, the messenger was exhausted. Therefore, when they subsequently encountered fleeing bandit remnants, they were unable to resist and were almost entirely wiped out.\"","Shen Tianming was dumbfounded but still insisted, \"Impossible.\"","\"What is impossible? As one of the leaders delivering edicts, General Shen, can you not recognize the material of this edict?\" Qin Shaozong added.","Shen Tianming certainly recognized it. He evaded the question and only said, \"You just said the messengers were almost entirely wiped out. Since it's 'almost,' that means they weren't. Where are the people? Let them come see me!\"","Qin Shaozong's expression was calm. \"He only has one breath left and is currently undergoing emergency rescue, so I'm afraid he cannot come to see you. General Shen, Chang'an has already fallen into chaos. What exactly is your purpose in stopping me from entering the capital? If the current Emperor is murdered by treacherous villains, can you bear the charge of conspiring against the Han royal family?\"","Shen Tianming was left speechless. It took him a long time to choke out a sentence, \"Why has Chang'an fallen into chaos?\"","Qin Shaozong replied, \"The edict messenger only said that a prophecy has emerged in Chang'an, and it seems there are traitors in the city colluding with outsiders, but the specific details of the prophecy are still unknown.\""]},{"number":152,"title":"Chapter 152","paragraphs":["Carved carriages compete to park on the heavenly streets, while precious horses race along the imperial roads. Dazzling gold and jade catch the eye, and the fragrance of fine silks fills the air. This dreamlike sentence is equally fitting to describe Chang'an. (1)","Chang'an, the imperial city at the foot of the Son of Heaven, possessed a prosperity and splendor that other places could never hope to match.","In this wealthy land, events big and small played out every day. The big ones could affect all the high officials and nobles inside and outside the imperial city, while the small ones only happened within families of three, vanishing without a trace in the blink of an eye.","Recently, however, hidden currents surged in Chang'an, and the folk teahouses were occupied by a crowd of storytellers.","Smack! The sharp sound of a wooden gavel pierced the air.","The tea drinkers in the hall felt a jolt in their hearts and focused their attention.","\"Today, let us briefly talk about the Marquis of Wu'an from the North. This man is truly the reincarnation of the Star of Military Arts. At the age of eleven, he followed his father into battle, and brought back the head of a Wuhuan soldier on his very first try. Right after his coming-of-age ceremony, he dared to take the head of Prince Langye from amidst an army of ten thousand, severely crippling the Wuhuan's vitality and securing another ten years of peace for the borders of our Great Yan!\"","The tea drinkers cheered in unison.","The storyteller in green robes stroked his goatee. \"Since ancient times, heroes have been matched with beauties. Lady Dai, the Marquis of Wu'an's second wife, not only possesses a face like a flower and the moon, but is also compassionate. The highly acclaimed dragon-bone water wheel from last year spread rapidly from the North to the Central Plains precisely because of her promotion. As the saying goes, agriculture is the foundation of the people, and when the foundation is solid, the country is secure. The Marchioness's entry into the capital this time is precisely for the matter of being granted a noble title.\"","\"It is said that the Marquis of Wu'an treats his wife like a precious pearl. He escorted her again and again, actually accompanying her all the way from Yuyang to Yanzhou, where he had just quelled a rebellion, unable to bear parting with his wife and children. Coincidentally, this happened right as the golden flood dragon appeared, committing all sorts of evil in Chang'an, causing a huge uproar and leaving the people with no peace.\"","At the mention of the evil flood dragon, all the tea drinkers in the hall nodded.","Previously, there had been a series of minor earthquakes in Chang'an City, and every time, a prophecy would be unearthed.","The rumor that \"Han Yan is about to perish\" spread until everyone in Chang'an knew it.","The Empress Dowager was furious and bypassed the Bearer of the Gilded Mace, instead dispatching the Feathered Forest Guard to investigate thoroughly. However, for more than two consecutive months, they failed to find even the slightest clue.","Someone in the hall whispered, \"Isn't it bizarre? Among the collapsed houses, there were newly built ones as well as those built only five or six years ago. There is no such thing as them being in disrepair due to age.\"","\"They investigated for months and still found nothing. Instead, the more they investigated, the more mysterious it became.\"","\"Could it really be that the evil flood dragon bit the white fox to death, which triggered all the subsequent events?\"","\"I think it most likely is. If not for such anomalies, how could it attract the governors of various provinces to all come to the capital and gather together? Just from what I've heard, there's Governor Xie of Sizhou, Governor Nangong, Governor Jiang of Yuzhou...\"","Smack! Another strike of the wooden gavel sounded.","The green-robed storyteller silenced the discussions in the hall before saying, \"Provincial governors guard their respective regions and cannot enter the capital without an imperial edict. But now that evil demons are harming Chang'an, those who eat the ruler's salary must share the ruler's worries. Heroes from all over have flocked to the capital to slay the evil flood dragon. Our Chang'an hasn't had such a gathering of distinguished guests in a long time. But speaking of yesterday, when the Marquis of Wu'an and his wife arrived in Chang'an, many noble families were so moved that their tears flowed freely...\"","Someone below couldn't help but whisper, \"I'm afraid it wasn't out of emotion. The daughter of the brother of the distant cousin of my third cousin's great-uncle married a gatekeeper of the Yuan family. I heard that yesterday, many masters of the Yuan family were so worried that they didn't eat all day.\"","\"The Yuan family and the Empress Dowager's maternal family, the Wangs, are related by marriage, so it's normal for them to be worried. With heroes gathered together, if the helm of this ship isn't steered well, the capital will likely undergo a massive upheaval. After all, the troops and horses of the various families are all stationed thirty miles outside the city.\"","\"Shh, don't be so direct!\"","One of the heroes being discussed both openly and covertly by the commoners was currently in the most prestigious eatery in the capital.","\"Madam, this lotus seed calabash duck is quite good, you should try it.\" Qin Shaozong recommended it to Dai Li, and then sighed, \"Chang'an truly is the top golden nest under heaven. They can even make a single duck in such an elaborate way.\"","The customs of the North were rugged, and their meals were correspondingly much bolder. For example, the noodle soup Dai Li had eaten earlier came in a bowl that was larger than her face.","However, the lotus seed calabash duck that had been praised as \"quite good\" was served on a carved white porcelain plate less than seven inches long, and the calabash duck on the plate was even more ingenious.","The entire duck had been deboned, yet its skin remained perfectly intact. It had been specially shaped into an auspicious calabash, and the inside was stuffed with ingredients such as lotus seeds, sea cucumbers, and mushrooms. The duck meat had been infused with the flavors of the various ingredients for a long time, giving it a unique taste.","Dai Li picked up a piece with her chopsticks, chewed it slowly and carefully, and after saying, \"It is indeed quite good,\" she went back to eating the white jade Buddha's hand that she had already taken a few bites of earlier.","This dish had a good name and a beautiful presentation. It was as crystal clear as carved jade, resembling a pale hand with its palm facing upwards. Paired with the dark sauce underneath, it was a feast for the eyes.","\"Why are you only eating that white radish? You barely eat any meat in a meal, no wonder a simple cold previously kept you bedridden for days.\" Qin Shaozong took a small porcelain bowl, picked out a few pieces of the calabash duck, and placed it next to Dai Li's hand. \"Finish it.\"","\"I just indulged in too much cold food at the time, and I was a bit unaccustomed to the climate when we first arrived in Yongzhou.\" Dai Li refused to admit that her health was poor.","\"Anyway, you have to finish it.\" His tone was forceful.","Dai Li pursed her lips and whispered, \"Zhou Zhou and Qinian aren't here right now, you don't need to keep acting like a father.\"","\"No acting spoiled.\" Qin Shaozong added another piece of fish to her bowl.","Dai Li: \"...\"","Qin Shaozong picked up the teacup beside him and took a sip.","Setting out from Yuyang in Youzhou, passing through Jizhou, stopping in Yanzhou to handle some affairs, and finally crossing through Sizhou to arrive here, they had taken their time and traveled for an entire spring.","They arrived in the capital right when the appearance of the golden dragon in Chang'an was causing the greatest panic among the people, and following several provincial governors who harbored certain unspoken intentions.","Today was their second day in the capital. Yesterday, when they first arrived in Chang'an, officials had welcomed them early on and led them to a large mansion in the southern part of the city.","Later, Dai Li found out that the neighbors of that mansion were the other provincial governors. Everyone had been housed together in one cluster.","And the Northern faction was placed right in the center.","\"Could it be that General Shen filed a complaint, so the imperial court put us right in the middle?\" Dai Li suspected.","Qin Shaozong: \"It's entirely possible. Who told them that the final bandit leader couldn't be saved in the end?\"","\"It's like raising Gu poison,\" Dai Li suddenly blurted out.","She spoke without context, but Qin Shaozong understood. \"The matter of the prophecies is causing a huge uproar, and yet at this very moment, the wolves and tigers bordering the nest are jumping in one after another to muddy the waters. If I were the mastermind behind the scenes, I would also gather them all together, sit on the mountain and watch the tigers fight, and be the relaxed fisherman who reaps the benefits.\"","The Chang'an dust explosion was an opportunity to enter the capital. Obviously, the North wasn't the only one to spot and seize this chance.","Dai Li looked thoughtful. \"In that case, the matter of me being granted a noble title might not be put on the agenda immediately.\"","\"Let's wait and see.\" Seeing her chopsticks absentmindedly poking at the fish in her bowl without actually eating it, Qin Shaozong lightly tapped the edge of her bowl with his wooden chopsticks. \"Madam, stop torturing that poor piece of fish and quickly send it to its next life.\"","Dai Li muttered, \"It would have been better to let Zhou Zhou and the others come along too.\"","With the younger generation present, he would restrain himself somewhat, unlike now where he even micromanaged her when she didn't want to eat.","\"They aren't babbling toddlers anymore, how can they stick to their parents all day?\" Qin Shaozong had intentionally left the juniors behind when they went out today.","The Hewei Pavilion where the two were dining was the most famous large eatery in Chang'an. The private rooms from the second floor upwards did not accept walk-ins and required advance reservations.","Dining in a private room required paying a hefty fee for the room itself, and each dish cost twenty percent more than it did in the main hall. Yet despite this, wealthy and noble families came in an endless stream, ensuring the private rooms at Hewei Pavilion were fully booked every single day.","The reason was simple: pushing open the window on one side of the room revealed a nearby river winding like a ribbon of jade. Painted pleasure boats drifted upon it, with snatches of song floating up from time to time. Along the banks, willow trees formed a continuous wave of green, swaying in the wind beneath the azure sky.","It was a picturesque scene, painting a corner of Chang'an's prosperity.","\"My lord, this private room is already occupied. Please come this way.\"","\"It's fine, I know the people inside.\" This was a rough, hearty male voice.","Qin Shaozong slightly raised his long eyebrows.","Dai Li was a little stunned.","Did Qin Changgeng still have such open and aboveboard friends in Chang'an? Could it be...","The next moment, the door to the private room was pushed open, and a burly man with the back of a tiger and the waist of a bear strode in. He was eight feet tall, with a square face, tiger-like eyes, and a dark shadow of stubble on his jaw.","Who else could the newcomer be but Nangong Xiong?","Nangong Xiong knew Qin Shaozong was inside, and he also knew he was definitely not alone in the room.","Last year, Quanjie suddenly became Qin Yanzhou, and the Madame Dai beside him later leaped to become the matriarch of the North, not to mention he suddenly had an extra son to his name.","Knowing quite a bit of the inside story, how could Nangong Xiong not understand? Back then, Qin Changgeng had repeatedly claimed that Qin Yanzhou was the son of an old friend. That was clearly a trick.","Although he had some expectations before coming, Nangong Xiong was still incredibly amazed when he actually saw Dai Li.","The young woman wore a pale pink satin ruqun dress, her dark hair swept up in a flowing cloud chignon. Her skin was white as snow, with a dot of crimson between her brows, and her radiant eyes seemed to gather the brilliant glow of the horizon's sunset.","She did not act like other noble ladies, who would consciously retreat to the connecting small tea room next door when an outside male visited. She merely looked him over with curiosity.","Previously, when the North and Qingzhou cooperated, Dai Li had only heard of Governor Nangong but had never met him. Now that she saw him...","How to put it? He completely matched her impression of a military general.","Qin Shaozong opened his mouth and said, \"Nangong, your wife hasn't been granted a title, so why are you joining the fun in Chang'an?\"","Nangong Xiong's mouth twitched. \"Although my wife has not received an imperial title from His Majesty, it doesn't stop me from caring about Chang'an. Didn't I hear there was an evil dragon stirring up trouble, so I hurried over to protect the emperor?\"","\"Come on, there is no one else here. Why do you need to put on an act in front of me, Nangong?\" Qin Shaozong sneered.","Dai Li subconsciously looked at Nangong Xiong's waist. The man had traveled with a saber, and looking at its length, it was about five feet long. She silently tapped the black boot of the man opposite her under the table, signaling him to restrain his words.","The other party was, after all, a provincial governor and a former partner. Now they were all in Chang'an, and the place they were staying was even surrounded.","Restrain yourself!","Qin Shaozong picked up his chopsticks and put another piece of meat in Dai Li's bowl. \"Finish this piece too.\"","Dai Li: \"...\"","Nangong Xiong's eyes flickered slightly. He reached back and closed the door to the private room, shutting out the restaurant attendants and Feng Feng and the others who had hurried over from the next room.","He took a few steps forward and sat down beside the table. \"Alright, since you, Qin Changgeng, say there is no one else here, let me ask you a question. I hope you will tell me the truth.\"","Without waiting for Qin Shaozong to respond, Nangong Xiong lowered his voice and said, \"Those baffling prophecies in Chang'an, are they your doing?\"","A trace of surprise flashed in Dai Li's eyes.","Qin Shaozong smiled faintly. \"Why do you say that?\"","\"Although the prophecies point directly to the Bearer of the Golden Mace and Governor Xie of Sizhou, I actually feel it isn't them. Governor Xie of Sizhou has been in power for less than half a year, and he was heavily damaged by you last year. His foundation is still shallow, and Sizhou itself is not yet stable. How could he have the energy to mess around outside?\" Nangong Xiong rubbed his chin. He knew more of the inside story than most. \"The Emperor summoned your esteemed wife to the capital to receive her title first, and then the golden dragon appeared in Chang'an later. And I always felt you wouldn't let your esteemed wife enter the capital alone.\"","If he hadn't witnessed all those previous events, Nangong Xiong would have unhesitatingly dismissed such talk from others as absurd.","But it just so happened that he had received three hundred fine horses and other compensations from the North. First there was the comment that it really is better to die quickly, then there was the matter of Quanjie being written off, and that fellow immediately getting married in early spring...","Not feeling at ease letting his newlywed wife go to the capital alone, and thus secretly causing trouble to stir up the whole city—that was indeed something Qin Changgeng would do.","Nangong Xiong stared unblinkingly at the man in front of him, wanting an answer, when suddenly he saw the other man curl his lips into a smile.","\"What if it is? What if it isn't?\" Qin Shaozong asked in return.","Nangong Xiong gasped inwardly, doubts popping up one after another.","\"The collapsed houses were all brand new. How did you make them turn into a pile of ruins without anyone noticing?\" Nangong Xiong pressed.","Qin Shaozong was about to open his mouth when he suddenly heard:","\"Boom!\"","A loud crash came from outside the window. Dai Li turned her head in shock, only to see what looked like billowing dust and smoke not far away.","Nangong Xiong's pupils contracted for a moment, and he subconsciously looked at Qin Shaozong. \"You're doing it again?\"","Unexpectedly, there was another loud crash at this moment. The direction was similar but not exactly the same. Dai Li stared into the distance. They were on the third floor, and Hewei Pavilion was grandly built; the third floor offered a wide view, allowing them to see far away.","\"No, that looks like the place we are staying.\" Dai Li's expression changed.","South District, Minhe Street.","When Dai Li returned, she saw that the collapsed houses were right next to the mansion they were staying in.","One house on the left and one on the right had collapsed. Their Qin Manor stood tall in the middle, completely unharmed.","If she remembered correctly, the mansion on the left temporarily belonged to Qingzhou, and the one on the right belonged to Sizhou.","\"Father!\" Nangong Zijin, escorted by a group of soldiers, didn't dare stay in the house anymore. Seeing Nangong Xiong return, the young girl who had just been keeping a brave face immediately got red eyes.","Nangong Xiong's heart ached terribly. \"Was my little girl frightened? Were you hurt just now?\"","Nangong Zijin slowly shook her head and said no.","After looking his youngest daughter over, Nangong Xiong finally breathed a sigh of relief. But as he turned his head, he glared unkindly at Qin Shaozong. \"Qin Changgeng, you need to give me an explanation for this!\"","Qin Shaozong said coldly, \"It wasn't me who blew up your house. Why are you yelling at me in broad daylight?\"","Nangong Xiong paused, then changed his tune. \"Since we parted last year, we haven't had a proper catch-up. You were only halfway through your dinner just now, so you must not be full yet. It just so happens I haven't eaten either. How about inviting me and my child into your manor for a meal?\"","Qin Shaozong: \"Fine.\"","Dai Li looked at the young lady of the Nangong family.","Nangong Xiong's daughter didn't look like him at all. She was like a delicate and vibrant begonia flower, dazzling and radiant. She wore a water-red round-collar ruqun with cloud and swallow patterns, and a pure gold buyao hairpin inlaid with pearls on her head, which made her already bright and beautiful features look even more elegant.","Noticing Dai Li's gaze, Nangong Zijin slightly tucked her chin and bowed to her. \"Marchioness, I am the sixth child in my family. You may call me Nangong Xiaoliu. I apologize for the intrusion.\"","Dai Li smiled.","The young girl's teary expression from just a moment ago was still vivid in her mind, yet seeing her now bowing and introducing herself so methodically, Dai Li inexplicably felt as if she were looking at a reserved little kitten.","\"Come in. Speaking of which, I have three boys and girls about your age at home. You might find you have a lot to talk about,\" Dai Li said.","Just as she led the group into the front courtyard, she saw Qin Yanzhou hurrying out from the side corridor. Noticing the guests, the young man spoke in veiled terms, \"Mother, he has sent me a letter.\"","The mother and son locked eyes. Even though Qin Yanzhou left the details unspoken, in that fleeting moment, Dai Li inexplicably knew exactly who \"he\" was.","A letter had arrived from the Green Lotus Cult."]},{"number":153,"title":"Chapter 153","paragraphs":["White Elephant died in Yuyang, and Dai Li anticipated that the Green Lotus Sect would absolutely not let it go. But she hadn't expected them to act so quickly. On the second day after the Northern Army arrived in Chang'an, the opposing side delivered a preemptive warning.","Dai Li opened the mulberry paper. The signature at the bottom right corner was a lotus drawn in traditional ink. The ink on the paper had dried, leaving only a brief line of text:","[The past accounts are complicated; wait for them to be settled in detail.]","Dai Li's eyes darkened.","Obviously, this was a declaration of war. Not only the governors of the surrounding provinces, but even the Green Lotus Sect was determined to wade into these muddy waters.","Fishing in troubled waters, it was still unknown which fish would ultimately be caught and become the meat carved up on the chopping block.","Dai Li asked, \"Zhouzhou, where did this letter come from?\"","\"When the cooks went out to purchase supplies, the letter was slipped into the goods and brought in,\" Qin Yanzhou said.","Dai Li slowly folded the mulberry paper. Chang'an was not the North; there was no way to make a big show of tracking down the true messenger. She asked about another matter, \"Zhouzhou, have you, Qi Nian, and Rongrong had dinner yet?\"","This afternoon, she and Qin Changgeng went out to tour Chang'an. Before leaving, she told the three youngsters at home to figure out dinner themselves, but she returned earlier than expected.","Qin Yanzhou shook his head. \"Not yet.\"","Dai Li thought it was perfect timing. \"Governor Nangong and his daughter have come to visit the manor. The Marquis and the Sixth Miss's father have matters to discuss. Zhouzhou, you take her to have dinner later.\"","Then Dai Li turned slightly to introduce Qin Yanzhou to Nangong Ziqin. \"This is my eldest son, Qin Yanzhou.\"","Nangong Ziqin had been observing him from the start. It wasn't that she was overly curious, but it was the first time she had seen such a handsome young master.","The golden sun set in the west, and the brilliant afterglow reflected on the young man's profile. With his high-bridged nose as a dividing line, it cast a soft interplay of light and shadow on half his face.","He was extremely good-looking, with eyes as black as ink and eyelids layered like peach petals. However, his aura was cold and sharp, forcefully suppressing any hint of romantic charm.","Nangong Ziqin curtsied in greeting.","Qin Yanzhou returned the courtesy.","...","\"Second Brother, you were gone for so long, how...\" Qin Qinian suddenly stopped. It was because he saw that Qin Yanzhou had not returned alone; a beautiful young lady was following behind him.","The youth, who had been lazily sprawling on the table waiting for dinner, immediately sat up straight and adopted proper etiquette.","Shi Rongyue also looked at the guest in surprise. \"Brother Zhongle, who is this young lady?\"","\"This is the Nangong family's Sixth Miss. She came to the manor with her father as a guest. The elders have important matters to discuss, so Mother asked us to entertain her.\" Qin Yanzhou introduced Nangong Ziqin to Shi Rongyue and Qin Qinian, and then ordered the servants to add a set of bowls and chopsticks.","The few of them exchanged greetings.","Although there was no strict custom at this time forbidding unmarried young ladies from seeing outside men, they were ultimately unfamiliar with each other, and there was a distinction between men and women. Therefore, after the greetings, the brothers didn't speak.","The atmosphere was unsurprisingly awkward.","\"Ah, we should have people bring up a few separate tables!\" Shi Rongyue realized belatedly.","They usually used a round table, but with a distinguished guest present, to show respect, they should dine at separate tables.","Qin Qinian was about to go arrange it when he heard Nangong Ziqin say, \"There's no need for the trouble; a guest should follow the host's convenience. I heard that last year my father and the Marquis formed an alliance to jointly attack the Green Lotus. Now that they meet again in Chang'an, who knows, they might continue their previous connection in the future. Since that's the case, why be so formal?\"","Nangong Ziqin had always known clearly why she was able to accompany her father to the capital. Born to enjoy the prosperity of the Nangong clan, it was common for marriage to serve the family.","Since Fan of Yanzhou was defeated and the male members of the Fan clan were slaughtered, her past engagement was naturally void. This time entering the capital, it was highly likely her father would choose a new husband for her.","With the prior alliance to jointly attack the North, and now visiting the manor as guests, Nangong Ziqin privately felt the chances of her future husband coming from the North were quite high.","She looked again at the two young masters of the Qin family.","The older one, though the Marquis's stepson, stood tall and straight like a pine. He had a cool demeanor, a saber at his waist, and picturesque features. He was a top-tier handsome young master.","The younger one's face was not as handsome as his brother's, but his eyes were clear, and he looked easy to get along with, plus he was the biological son of Marquis Wu'an.","Nangong Ziqin nodded in her heart.","Shi Rongyue had attended many gatherings in Nanyu and was very popular among her peers. Now she smiled and said to Nangong Ziqin, \"Alright then, we'll sit at the round table, side by side.\"","*","In the main hall.","Qin Shaozong had just eaten a round and was now only holding a wine goblet, barely touching his chopsticks. \"...So it's not some supernatural force, purely the mischief of flour. If you're worried about a next time, just send people to search the houses carefully.\"","Nangong Xiong hadn't eaten tonight. Now, with a table full of delicacies in front of him, he completely ignored them, listening in a daze.","Mere wheat flour could produce such great power? It was truly unbelievable!","Nangong Xiong hurriedly called in the Qingzhou soldiers waiting outside and instructed his subordinate, \"Ba Guang, quickly lead a squad to thoroughly search the houses, leaving no corner unexamined. If you find flour spread on the ground, clean it up and report back.\"","This order seemed baffling, but the lieutenant clasped his hands in acknowledgment and immediately went to carry it out.","\"Marquis Wu'an, to be honest, I have doubts about the house collapse in Yuyang you mentioned earlier. You wouldn't mind if I send a squad to Yuyang right now to verify it, would you?\" Nangong Xiong spoke frankly.","Those who could claim a share of power in the current situation of warlord fragmentation were no fools. And Nangong Xiong only half-believed what the man in front of him said.","Verification was also easy; just send someone to Yuyang to check the details.","Qin Shaozong readily agreed, \"Sure. But given the several assassinations I encountered on my way south, I will send another squad to accompany yours.\"","Nangong Xiong had no objections.","Having people from the North accompany them, with tokens in hand, would indeed make travel much more convenient.","However...","Nangong Xiong leaned forward slightly and said curiously, \"It doesn't make sense. They say you pick the softest persimmon to squeeze. Even if the Green Lotus Sect hates us for ruining their plans, they have no reason to strike directly at Yuyang.\"","That was Yuyang, the core of the North. What was the difference between that and entering a tiger's den?","\"It's just that human greed is like a snake trying to swallow an elephant,\" Qin Shaozong said, not mentioning that the other side had lost a core member.","Nangong Xiong, however, felt this matter was not simple. But seeing Qin Changgeng's demeanor, he knew the man was unwilling to tell him the inside story. He simply didn't ask and changed the subject. \"Aside from Liu of Jingzhou, all the other warlords have come to the capital. Do you think he'll eventually get involved too?\"","\"Very likely. Liu Zhan is no fool, why wouldn't he come? The reason he's late is probably that his newly acquired Yizhou still needs more consolidation, plus he's avoiding suspicion.\" Qin Shaozong drained the wine in his goblet in one gulp.","The golden dragon emerges from near its nest.","The province adjacent to Yongzhou was not just Sizhou, but also Yizhou. Yizhou had changed hands, and Liu Zhan, who had leaped to become the overlord of the south, could also be that golden dragon.","Nangong Xiong picked up the wine jug and poured wine for Qin Shaozong with a face full of smiles. \"We formed an alliance last year, so we can be considered to have a life-and-death friendship. Now Chang'an is treacherous and full of dangers. Going it alone makes it easy to be attacked from front and back. I wonder if you, Marquis Wu'an, have the intention to swear a blood oath and continue to be good brothers who share each other's burdens with me?\"","Actually, Nangong Xiong initially had no intention of allying with the North.","His previous requests for marriage alliances had been repeatedly rejected. As a dignified provincial governor, he wasn't so lacking in integrity. Whoever won in the end would rely on their own abilities; why did he have to depend on Qin Changgeng?","However, the two explosions from earlier seemed to ring like a great bell in Nangong Xiong's ears, shearing away half of the verdant bamboo forest in his heart.","The Qinglian Cult had always been wicked, skilled at manipulating people's hearts and playing the devil. Their filthy tricks were endless. Today, they could engineer the collapse of two houses to sow seeds of doubt among the provincial governors; tomorrow, who knew what other methods they might use.","If he were to capsize in the gutter due to a moment of carelessness, wouldn't this trip to Chang'an just be making a wedding dress for someone else? The Northern Region had fought many battles with the Qinglian Cult, so they must be the most familiar with their tricks...","Thus, after a brief moment of thought, Nangong Xiong shamelessly spoke up again.","Qin Shaozong allowed him to fill his wine cup. \"Oh? That troop hasn't even set off for Yuyang yet, and you are already so eager to be brothers with me, Nangong. Aren't you afraid of being stabbed in the back by your good brother when the time comes?\"","Nangong Xiong smiled, showing his ability to yield and adapt. \"If it were anyone else, I absolutely wouldn't trust them. But Marquis Wu'an, you are an indomitable man. Once you give your word, a team of horses cannot chase it back. What do I have to fear?\"","Qin Shaozong did not accept this flattery, replying leisurely, \"Not necessarily. In the past, I once declared that if I were to remarry, I must marry a woman from the Wei family, but I haven't done that either.\"","Nangong Xiong: \"...\"","Fabric shops were as common as clouds in Chang'an. The Wennan Fabric Shop, situated on the edge of the bustling market, could only be considered below average and could not catch the eyes of the dignitaries.","However, it was within this very ordinary fabric shop that the third floor held a hidden universe. The top floor used sandalwood for its beams and featured a gold inlaid jade screen carved with landscapes. Beside the window sat an agarwood desk, and along the edges of the room stood treasure racks displaying exquisite and precious ornaments.","But the most special feature had to be the desk in the center of the room, which resembled a sand table. At this moment, two people stood facing each other before it.","The two shared somewhat similar facial features, with only a clear difference in their ages.","The handsome man dressed in a green robe was clearly past thirty. There were two shallow lines of age at the corners of his eyes, and a string of gold-patterned Buddhist prayer beads wrapped around his right wrist, making him look like a man of religion.","The sand table in front of him was like a gluttonous beast, containing a miniature version of Chang'an City. Within the city, there were small cloth pouches, each with a small flag planted on top.","Han, Liu, Xie, Jiang, Li, Nangong, Qin, and... Dai.","Among them, the flag for Han, representing the Emperor, was the most unique. The cloth pouch beneath it was black, while the rest were all white.","\"Uncle, after the flour explosion, Marquis Wu'an invited Nangong into his residence. These two collaborated last year, and I'm afraid they are going to collude again now.\" Diting picked up the Nangong flag and placed it next to Qin.","He was somewhat puzzled. \"Why would you let these two get on the same boat? Wouldn't it be easier to defeat them one by one?\"","\"Those who can form an alliance can also part ways. Moreover, even you feel the threat is intensifying, let alone the impatient Chancellor Dong; he definitely won't be able to sit still. Before Liu of Jingzhou enters the capital, let them fight it out,\" Liudao said lightly.","Diting suddenly understood.","His uncle was trying to accelerate the development of the current situation while simultaneously using another's knife to kill.","The small cloth pouch with the Dai flag planted in the sand table was suddenly picked up by a pair of slender hands. Liudao traced the character on it with his finger. \"How is Concubine Du doing now?\"","Diting smiled and said, \"She has some intelligence and cannot let go of Marquis Wu'an herself. Therefore, knowing that doing as we say might help her regain her past glory, she is actually quite obedient.\"","Liudao put Dai down again, but not in its original position close to Qin; instead, he placed it far away. \"Let her go and test the waters first. Combining internal and external efforts will yield results.\"","Qin Residence.","\"A wine-tasting banquet?\" Dai Li looked at the delivered invitation, her brows slowly furrowing.","The gold-stamped invitation was exceptionally exquisite. Using gold powder as ink, the invitation details were written in beautiful clerical script, inviting her and Qin Shaozong to attend the wine-tasting banquet together.","The host of the banquet was Chancellor Dong Zhou, who held immense power in the court, and the location was arrogantly set at a royal villa in the suburbs.","Qin Shaozong was beside Dai Li. He was much taller than her, and only needed to lower his head slightly to read the words on the invitation. \"There has been no movement regarding the conferring of titles, yet a wine-tasting event comes first.\"","\"Qin Changgeng, are we going to attend this banquet?\" Dai Li asked.","Qin Shaozong waved his hand to summon Hu Bao. \"The Dong family sent an invitation. Go and investigate who else they have invited.\"","Hu Bao received the order and left. He returned shortly after and reported, \"My Lord, the Dong family's attendants have visited several surrounding residences without missing any.\"","\"Everyone has received an invitation, so it seems inappropriate if we don't go,\" Dai Li said hesitantly.","\"Not we, just me,\" Qin Shaozong corrected her. Meeting the woman's confused eyes, he explained in a low voice, \"There will likely be drinking contests during the banquet, and possibly spontaneous martial arts matches. Swords and blades have no eyes, so it is best for you to stay in the residence, Madam.\"","Since Dong Zhou had also invited others, the Northern Region certainly could not be absent. Otherwise, if they did not even dare to attend a wine-tasting banquet, how could they compete for anything else?","Hearing him mention a martial arts match, Dai Li immediately thought of Xiang Zhuang's sword dance from the past. It was only natural that Dong Zhou could not hold back at this wine-tasting banquet.","\"Madam, you don't need to worry. The wine-tasting banquet is held at Changle Villa in the southern suburbs. I will dispatch a team to stand by at the foot of the mountain. If there is any unusual activity on the mountain, we will use a beacon fire as a signal, and the Black Valiant Cavalry will charge up to attack. Besides, I personally believe that Dong Zhou will not easily break the balance.\" Qin Shaozong guessed that this wine-tasting banquet was meant to test their true strength.","After the dust explosion, Nangong Xiong had questioned him in public, and there were at least dozens, if not a hundred, pairs of eyes in the area. It was not surprising that the phrase \"You need to give me an explanation for this\" had spread.","\"Anyway, just be careful,\" Dai Li lowered her eyes.","The man, who had just been so imposing and serious, suddenly smiled, revealing a bit of inherent wickedness. He abruptly reached out and pulled her into his arms, bending slightly to rub his slightly stubbled jaw against her soft cheek. \"Oh, Madam is worried about me.\"","The short stubble was prickly, giving Dai Li the illusion of being licked by the barbed tongue of a giant tiger. She leaned to the other side as he rubbed against her, but the iron arm around her waist held her firmly in place.","\"Madam is deeply in love with me.\" The corners of his mouth curled up high.","Dai Li's mouth twitched, and she reached out to push him. \"...Qin Changgeng, don't you really think remarrying is troublesome?\"","Those words stung his nerves, making them jump. \"It is indeed troublesome, so I must ask Madam to remain the wife of the Qin family for the rest of your life.\"","He paused and added, \"And in the next life as well.\""]},{"number":154,"title":"Chapter 154","paragraphs":["Changle Yuan was half a day's journey from the imperial city. It was built by the late emperor for the then most beautiful woman in the harem, Consort He. Although this villa had the title of \"Yuan\", it could completely be called a temporary palace.","It covered an unusually large area, almost encompassing the entire mountain. It was luxurious yet elegant, with winding paths leading to secluded spots, waterside pavilions overlooking lakes, as well as bracket sets, flying eaves, and high-raised ridge beasts, making people feel pleased and sigh in admiration.","From the outside, this temporary palace built on the mountain looked like a giant beast occupying a majestic peak.","Qin Shaozong and Nangong Xiong set off together and arrived at Changle Yuan on the mountain at the end of the Wei hour.","The attendants from the North and Qingzhou dismounted respectively.","The gate of Changle Yuan was wide open. From the entrance, there was a guard every three steps and a sentry every five steps. The guards wore armor and carried swords, with helmets on their heads, fully armed. In the distance, archers on standby could faintly be seen on the high platform.","Seeing this, Qin Shaozong actually laughed, \"After all, he has controlled the government for about twenty years. Why is he still so timid and fearful? What's the difference between his courage and that of a large rat?\"","Nangong Xiong, who was beside him, was so shocked by his arrogance that his eyebrows twitched. \"Disaster comes from the mouth. Speak cautiously!\"","\"Disaster and fortune depend on each other. Sometimes disaster is not a bad thing.\" Qin Shaozong's eyes swept over the surroundings, his light brown eyes calm and waveless.","Nangong Xiong understood the meaning of his words and gasped in his heart. \"There are at least a thousand troops stationed in this Changle Yuan, and whether there are troops hidden in the mountains is unknown. You, Qin Changgeng, have a large family business and strong soldiers and horses. I can't compare with you. If you want to rebel at this banquet, at least let me know in advance.\"","Qin Shaozong: \"The enemy outnumbers us; it is better to avoid their sharp edge.\"","That meant no action.","Nangong Xiong felt relieved. \"I also think it's more appropriate to hold off. I received news that Liu of Jingzhou has already set off and will arrive in Chang'an within a few days. This big play cannot start singing until everyone is here.\"","During their low-voiced conversation, the two were led into the main hall by a maid in front. As soon as they entered, they saw that someone was already seated by the table in the hall.","There were three people seated.","One was a man around thirty-five or thirty-six years old. He had pale skin, was slightly thin, and had a graceful bearing. Rather than a military general, he looked more like a literati.","Nangong Xiong recognized him. This was the Governor of Yuzhou, Jiang Shi, Governor Jiang.","Beside Jiang Shi sat a man with the body of a tiger and the arms of an ape. He was over forty years old and had a pair of leopard eyes shooting lightning. The moment Qin Shaozong stepped into the hall, fierce cold light burst from his eyes, as if wishing to turn into a snow blade to cut off the newcomer's neck.","It was clearly Governor Xie of Sizhou, Xie Yuanyue, whose residence had also been blown up like Nangong Xiong's.","Another person was like an old monk in meditation, but his small mung bean eyes constantly swept around. This person was Governor Li of Xuzhou, Li Lishen, who had been guarding one side in recent years.","Receiving Xie Yuanyue's angry glare, Qin Shaozong smiled and replied, \"Isn't this Governor Xie of Sizhou? You looking at me like this, could it be that you want to thank me but are too embarrassed to say it?\"","Xie Yuanyue smiled without mirth. \"Where does the word 'thank' come from? I didn't expect that besides being good at fighting, Marquis Wu'an's skill in putting gold on his own face is also top-notch.\"","His tone was unkind, like a needle pointing at a wheat awn, and his hostility towards Qin Shaozong was not without reason.","Coincidentally, Xie Yuanyue happened to stroll to the front of the collapsed house at that time. When the secret room below exploded, bricks and tiles flew, and beams and pillars broke and collapsed, almost hitting Xie Yuanyue.","Before he could recover from the shock and investigate the cause, he heard a report from the door...","Then Nangong Xiong's words reached his ears. Xie Yuanyue immediately became suspicious. His chest felt as if it had been dug open, and a cold wind blew through, making his hair stand on end.","If Qin Shaozong didn't know the inside story of the house collapsing, why did Nangong Xiong say those words? Why did Nangong Xiong change his face after they entered and exited the mansion together?","He, Qin Shaozong, must know the mystery inside!","And the collapse of the house brought out the Golden Dragon prophecy, which pointed directly to the Zhi Jinwu and the provincial governors neighboring Chang'an.","The hidden thoughts were suddenly cut open, completely disrupting the plan, making all parties vigilant and the world pay attention; it also made Xie Yuanyue, who was heavily damaged last year and had not yet recovered his vitality, extremely annoyed.","How could he not hate this?","Qin Shaozong only answered the first half of his sentence. \"Last year, your younger brother was mischievous and silently brought thousands of people to Yanzhou to bully men and women. I couldn't stand it and escorted him back to Sizhou. It hasn't been a year since this happened. Governor Xie of Sizhou shouldn't be so old that he can't remember things, right? I think you should remember, after all, people call you Governor Xie of Sizhou every day, rather than your third brother.\"","The old governor of Sizhou died suddenly, and his three sons fought for power. The second son was the first to be defeated and fled. The eldest and the third fought fiercely, and finally, Xie Yuanxiu successfully ascended to power with the help of the Green Lotus Sect. If it weren't for what happened later, the current Governor of Sizhou would indeed not be named Xie Yuanyue.","The burly man immediately widened his leopard eyes, like a hissing snake being pinched at its seven inches, unable to make another sound.","\"Governor Xie of Sizhou was just confused just now. Why do you have to be so aggressive, Marquis Wu'an?\" Jiang Shi spoke up.","\"It's rare for Prime Minister Dong to hold a banquet. We should get along peacefully. Marquis Wu'an, be forgiving when possible,\" Li Lishen also said, but he didn't mention Xie Yuanyue at all.","The states near Chang'an explicitly showed a high degree of obedience to the imperial court.","And this kind of grouping together was completely exposed at this time.","Qin Shaozong turned his eyes to look at them and said with a half-smile, \"Probably because I'm used to fighting the Northern Kingdom in the past, the motto 'If others offend me, I will definitely offend them' is carved into my bones.\"","Nangong Xiong thought to himself, not only that, you offend people even if they don't offend you.","Jiang Shi picked up the white jade ivory carved fan on the table and waved it gently, smiling warmly. \"The past is the past, and the present is the present. How can they be generalized? In this world, feng shui takes turns. The heroes who once dominated an area, such as the awe-inspiring Hegemon-King of Chu, ultimately committed suicide by the river. People shouldn't be too proud.\"","Qin Shaozong chuckled softly. \"That's true. Being too proud will attract the jealousy of some villains who have never been proud.\"","The hand holding the fan paused.","Qin Shaozong stopped looking at him and turned to look around. A long sandalwood table was placed at the head of the main hall. The wine vessels on the table were ready, but it was still empty and no one was seated.","Below were two rows of desks. Xie, Jiang, and Li had already taken their seats. They arrived early, so they chose their seats early. Xie Yuanyue was seated at the first seat on the lower left, with Jiang Shi behind him in the same row; Li Lishen sat at the first seat on the lower right.","The first seats on both sides were taken.","Qin Shaozong walked to the right side and lifted his robe to sit down at the second seat. Nangong Xiong followed him and sat on the same side.","This time, Qin, Nangong, Xie, Jiang, and Li were mainly invited. The remaining seats were filled by their attendants in a staggered manner.","A quarter of an hour after the latecomers sat down, Dong Zhou arrived late.","The prime minister who had held power in the imperial court for many years ate the fattest fat of Great Yan and had grown to have a waist circumference of ten spans. He wore a Jinxian crown and a black robe with wide sleeves. Python patterns were embroidered on the robe, and a string of gold and jade pendants hung around his fat waist. As he walked, he looked like a dazzling mountain of meat moving.","As soon as Dong Zhou entered, the few people stood up, cupped their hands, and said they were greeting Prime Minister Dong.","Dong Zhou raised his hand casually and pressed it down. \"You are all important ministers, dedicating yourselves to the country. You are no different from my own family, so there's no need to be overly polite. Inviting you all to gather at Changle Yuan today is not only to enhance our feelings but also to plan for the subsequent elimination of treacherous officials.\"","While speaking, Dong Zhou's gaze seemingly casually swept towards the second seat on the lower right.","The man was extremely tall, wearing a martial cap with a tall crown and a black robe, his face stern and cold. Though seated in a lower position, his presence was imposing. Looking at him, one felt the heavy majesty of a mountain and the unfathomable depths of an ocean, as if no matter how the lightning flashed or thunder rolled outside, nothing could cause him the slightest harm.","Dong Zhou was secretly alarmed. Having not seen him for many years, this man surnamed Qin was actually even more formidable than before.","Xie Yuanyue chimed in at this moment, \"With treacherous evildoers causing trouble, the common people cannot eat or sleep in peace. We indeed ought to dig them out of the dark ditches early and expose them to the sunlight, so that their souls may scatter and perish.\"","As he said this, he stared unblinkingly at Qin Shaozong opposite him.","Qin Shaozong smiled, \"It is only right. It seems that when it comes to catching thieves, Governor Xie of Sizhou has great experience and determination. Perhaps later you can be the first to lend Prime Minister Dong a helping hand.\"","The veins at Xie Yuanyue's temples throbbed twice, and he merely sneered, saying that it was naturally so.","The banquet had barely begun, yet the air was already thick with the smoke of gunpowder.","After a few more pleasantries, Dong Zhou clapped his hands. \"Since this is a wine appreciation banquet, how can we lack wine? Men, bring the wine!\"","Beautiful maidservants filed in, each holding a small wine jar in her hands.","Han wine came in many varieties: some named after their raw materials, some after their ingredients, and others after their regions. Millet wine, Yicheng wine, kumiss, grape wine, chrysanthemum wine...","There were those whose names could be called out and those that could not, too many to list. The young women holding the wine jars stood in a row behind the several men, ready to pour wine for the esteemed guests at any moment.","\"The fine vintages of Great Yan are all here. Gentlemen, please!\" Dong Zhou was the first to raise his cup.","Everyone drank together.","Since it was a wine appreciation banquet, naturally they would not drink only one kind of wine. A few cups of this, a few cups of that, drinking a mixture, and with every type they tasted, they would offer a few earnest words of critique.","After three rounds of wine, Dong Zhou, seated at the head, spoke again: \"With such fine wine, how can we lack song and dance? Let the dancers enter.\"","A breeze swept in, bringing a waft of fragrance into the hall that was already lingering with the scent of wine.","The crisp, melodious chiming of silver bells rang out as graceful dancers stepped to the rhythm and entered. Their flowing water sleeves fluttered, revealing glimpses of fair arms and slender waists.","The dancers all wore sheer veils, their beautiful faces half-hidden, captivating the eyes like flowers vying to bloom in the light morning mist.","Among the troupe of dancers, a young woman dressed in vermilion was the most striking. She had a tall and lithe figure, and her eyes were extremely beautiful, with large, dark irises that seemed to speak. The vermilion sheer fabric draped over her snow-white skin exuded an indescribable charm as she twirled and leaped.","Many present were watching her.","Qin Shaozong held his wine goblet in one hand, resting the other on the desk, lightly tapping his long fingers off and on. He seemed to be looking forward, yet also seemed not to be.","When the dance concluded, Dong Zhou at the head said, \"Do not just stand there. Go and pour wine for our heroes.\"","A fragrant breeze drifted as the young women, who had just been in the center of the hall, scattered like blooming petals to the sides, settling beside the seated guests.","The most eye-catching dancer floated over gracefully. After taking a wine jar from a maidservant's hands, she took a seat to Qin Shaozong's right.","\"My Lord Marquis,\" she called softly.","Qin Shaozong did not react, only noting the faint, drifting gazes coming from the crowd opposite him.","\"Qin Lang,\" the young woman changed her address.","And this time, the sharp gaze of the man beside her finally swept over.","Du Manxiang's heart surged with excitement, but suddenly seeing his brown eyes devoid of emotion, she realized he likely had not recognized her. She immediately pulled down the sheer veil from her face. \"Qin Lang, it is me. Save me.\"","Qin Shaozong remained expressionless. \"Why are you here? Who arranged for you to come?\"","\"It is a long story. After I left the Marquis's estate last year...\"","\"Marquis of Wu'an,\" someone opposite suddenly called out loudly.","The cheerful laughter and chatter at the banquet abruptly stopped, and everyone looked at Xie Yuanyue. The latter grinned and said, \"The dancer beside you is not bad. Could you let her come serve me?\"","Du Manxiang trembled in fright, instinctively trying to shrink into the arms of the man beside her, but she was blocked by his long arm as he placed his goblet on the desk.","\"They all say the Marquis of Wu'an from the North is generous and magnanimous. Could it be that your reputation exceeds the reality?\" Xie Yuanyue said.","Qin Shaozong said nothing.","Jiang Shi smiled at this moment, \"You, Xie Tengyun, are being quite unreasonable. If you want her to come over, wouldn't that leave the Marquis of Wu'an with an empty seat beside him? He surely won't agree to it. You should offer the beauty beside you in exchange.\"","\"Makes sense. I was inconsiderate just now,\" Xie Yuanyue laughed heartily, then pushed the dancer in his arms forward, signaling for her to go over.","The pushed dancer was very panicked. She first looked back at Xie Yuanyue, and seeing that the latter didn't even glance at her and clearly wouldn't change his mind, she could only walk towards Qin Shaozong.","Nangong Xiong took a sip of wine, happy to watch the show.","A mere dancer—if this were an ordinary gathering of friends, she could be given away casually. But in this setting, one could not yield an inch.","However...","Nangong Xiong stroked his chin.","He had heard that before Qin Changgeng married last year, he had completely cleared out his backyard of concubines, living only with Lady Dai.","Under the watchful eyes of the crowd, Qin Shaozong asked the person beside him, \"Governor Xie of Sizhou wants you to go over and serve him. Are you willing?\"","Du Manxiang lowered her head and shook it, leaning closer to his side.","Qin Shaozong frowned imperceptibly. \"Governor Xie of Sizhou, she is not willing. Let us drop the matter.\"","\"And what if I insist?\" Xie Yuanyue slammed his wine goblet heavily onto the desk. Fine cracks spread from the bottom of the white jade goblet, and soon it shattered into a pile of broken jade with a sharp crack.","Dong Zhou, seated at the head, seemed to finally notice the heavy atmosphere and stepped in to smooth things over. \"Since ancient times, heroes have been matched with beauties. Why don't you, Wu'an, and Tengyun decide the victor through martial arts? If Tengyun wins, Wu'an, you let her go serve Tengyun.\"","\"The Prime Minister's suggestion is excellent. The Marquis's prestigious name resounds like thunder in my ears, and I, Xie, have heard of it for a long time. It's a pity I never had the chance to spar with you before. I hope I can get my wish today.\" Xie Yuanyue stood up.","He was eight feet tall with a thick neck. As he spoke, veins occasionally bulged on the sides of his neck, and when his hands clenched into fists, they were as large as bushels, exuding an immense sense of power.","Feng Feng and others sitting in the back rows of the lower seats frowned upon hearing this.","Naturally, this match could not be lost, otherwise it would surely make the opponent's arrogance soar to the heavens. But winning didn't seem to be a good thing either...","Qin Shaozong likewise let go of his wine goblet and slowly stood up. \"Fists and kicks have no eyes. If I accidentally injure Governor Xie of Sizhou later, I hope you won't go crying to Prime Minister Dong.\""]},{"number":155,"title":"Chapter 155","paragraphs":["\"Do you want to disarm or not?\" Although he asked whether to take off the swords, Qin Shaozong had already removed his sword slide and taken off the ring-pommel sword at his waist.","Xie Yuanyue immediately felt despised and was about to say it was unnecessary when Dong Zhou, seated at the head, spoke first. \"Disarm. After all, today is a wine-tasting banquet, not a life-and-death struggle on the battlefield. You two don't need to fight with weapons; bare hands will do.\"","Nangong Xiong picked up his white jade goblet to drink, hiding the sneer at the corner of his mouth.","He was the one who hosted the banquet, and he was also the one who had a strong man standing on either side of him. How could Dong Zhou be so timid...","The two men took off their swords and stood face to face in the hall. Xie Yuanyue moved his neck left and right, and every time he twisted, his bones cracked. He was indeed heavily built, and with his dark skin, at first glance, he looked like a black bear standing upright.","\"Marquis Wu'an, pardon my offense.\" Xie Yuanyue's smile did not reach his eyes.","After this sound fell, it was as if he had already informed the other party, so there was no need to wait any longer. Xie Yuanyue lunged forward, shortening the distance between them.","A fist as big as a bowl swung towards him. If it had hit a wooden board, those present had no doubt that the poor wooden board would have been shattered into splinters.","His punch was as fast as lightning, but Qin Shaozong was already prepared. While dodging sideways, he raised his hand to grab Xie Yuanyue's wrist. If it were an ordinary person, let alone grabbing and twisting, just holding it would not be able to stop the momentum of the fist.","But Qin Shaozong was also a military general. He had experienced many battles and was in his prime, possessing experience and strength that young people could not match. His thick fingers opened and bent, like a tiger's claw with all its sharp claws extended.","With a solid muffled sound, he blocked and then deflected the force. At the same time, Qin Shaozong raised his leg and kicked fiercely at Xie Yuanyue's calf.","Xie Yuanyue stood his ground firmly, taking the kick head-on, buying time to attack Qin Shaozong's vital points again.","In the spacious hall, the two exchanged blows back and forth. Bare-handed, hand-to-hand combat, blocking and attacking hit the flesh with muffled thuds.","The military generals accompanying the several provincial governors were all capable fighters. As the saying goes, the layman watches the excitement, while the expert watches the technique. Many could see that in this fierce battle, Qin Shaozong was slightly superior.","The advantage was not much; it could barely be called a draw.","Nangong Xiong sipped his wine and sighed, \"This Qin Changgeng has more schemes than a rabbit hole on the Qinghe Plain.\"","However, just as he finished sighing, before he even had time to take another sip of wine, he saw a small object fly out of Qin Shaozong's arms.","Nangong Xiong had excellent eyesight and saw that it was a very delicate pouch, with a pattern seemingly embroidered on it.","After the small pouch flew out, the black-robed man in the hall immediately noticed it and reached out to catch it. The burly man opposite him, however, mistakenly thought he was going to punch a vital point, and hurriedly chopped at Qin Shaozong's wrist-guarded forearm with his hand as a blade.","Qin Shaozong's extended hand was forced to deviate, missing the small pouch flying towards Xie Yuanyue.","The two exchanged a few blows in an instant, and in the blink of an eye, the small pouch fell to the ground.","Before Qin Shaozong could take any other action, Xie Yuanyue, who had just suffered a flurry of attacks, wanted to readjust his state and took a step sideways.","And this step happened to land on the small pouch.","The brown pupils suddenly contracted.","Bai Jianping, Kuang Ye, and the others sat in the back. In terms of viewing position, they were far inferior to Nangong Xiong in the front row, so they only saw the draw broken in an instant.","Qin Shaozong changed his previous style. He used both hands and feet, attacking the opponent's throat above and Xie Yuanyue's base below. This set of attacks was not only as fast as lightning but also carried the force of a thunderbolt, as heavy as a mountain pressing down, unstoppable.","Xie Yuanyue retreated repeatedly in a moment of inattention. Finally, seeing the opponent suddenly launch a heavy flying kick, he was powerless to stop it. He took a kick to the chest, spat out a mouthful of blood, and was actually sent flying.","Jiang Shi was originally watching the show, but when he suddenly saw the situation on the field reverse, he was shocked. Before he could figure out why, he saw Xie Yuanyue flying straight towards him.","Jiang Shi's expression changed drastically as he tried to dodge, but he was sitting down, so how could he retreat in time?","Xie Yuanyue crashed directly onto his desk and was carried backward by the residual force, knocking Jiang Shi dizzy.","Amidst cries of \"Ouch,\" the desk overturned, jade plates shattered into pieces, and even the young woman carrying a wine jar behind was affected, spilling wine all over the floor.","Qin Shaozong didn't look over there. He bent down, picked up the small pouch from the ground, carefully patted the dust off it, pinched the opening of the bag to glance at the tiger-shaped brush rest inside, and then put it back into his arms.","Dong Zhou and Governor Liu of Xu Province, seated at the head, were both dumbfounded.","In the large hall, there were only the groans of pain from Xie Yuanyue and Jiang Shi.","Qin Shaozong said coldly, \"I yield.\"","Hearing this, Xie Yuanyue, whether out of severe injury or extreme anger, vomited another mouthful of blood.","Kuang Ye and Feng Feng exchanged a glance, both showing solemn expressions.","Dong Zhou barely recovered his senses and hurriedly called for the physician waiting secretly to treat Xie Yuanyue: \"It's just a martial arts sparring. Tengyun has no enmity or grudge against you. Marquis Wu'an, why did you strike so heavily?\"","These words carried a reprimand.","However, whether it was because Dong Zhou had drunk too much and his tone was strange, or for some other reason, Qin Shaozong inexplicably heard a trace of excitement in it.","\"Since ancient times, heroes have had difficulty passing the beauty test. It's normal for Marquis Wu'an to be furious for a beautiful woman. Since he likes her so much, Tengyun, you shouldn't fight with him over that dancer,\" Governor Liu of Xu Province smoothed things over with a smile, calling Xie Yuanyue by his courtesy name.","Qin Shaozong turned and returned to his seat without saying a word.","Du Manxiang was still in her original seat. Looking at the burly man walking towards her, her heart thumped, making her cheeks flush and her eyes blurry.","After nearly a year of separation, he was still as strong and imposing as in her memory, like an eternally standing mountain, always reliable.","\"Qin Lang, I knew you wouldn't lose.\" Seeing him sit down, Du Manxiang instinctively leaned towards him.","Qin Shaozong suddenly picked up the wine jug on the desk. As he poured the wine, he bent his elbow outward, blocking the woman who wanted to get closer. He turned his head slightly, his narrow eyes like amber soaked in a cold spring, devoid of much warmth. \"Can't straighten your bones?\"","Du Manxiang knew he always meant what he said. At this moment, he was somewhat displeased. She paused and could only slowly straighten up.","The sparring just now seemed to have given Dong Zhou some inspiration. His interest suddenly rose. \"The great affairs of the state lie in sacrifice and military affairs. Although the world is at peace now, martial arts cannot be neglected. It's rare for a gathering of heroes today, and with Marquis Wu'an and Tengyun competing as a start, why not carry it through to the end? Everyone, send your subordinates to the field to spar. The winner will receive a prize. What do you all think?\"","Li Lishen was the first to agree, \"The Prime Minister's proposal is excellent.\"","Where there is one, there is two. Nangong Xiong thought about it and also agreed.","\"Marquis Wu'an, what about you?\" Dong Zhou specifically asked Qin Shaozong.","Qin Shaozong: \"Since it is the Prime Minister's word, we should obey.\"","Dong Zhou clapped his hands and laughed, praising it. He took the lead in pointing out the subordinates of Jiang Shi and Li Lishen.","The two groups of people walked to the center, gave a hasty salute, and began to fight.","Qin Shaozong's gaze fell on the center of the hall, but he said, \"Who arranged for you to come here?\"","There were only two people seated at this desk. How could Du Manxiang not know he was asking her? \"Qin Lang...\"","\"Call me Lord Marquis,\" he corrected.","Du Manxiang looked at his profile with hidden bitterness. \"It is a long story, full of twists and strange turns. There are maids behind us; would you allow me to explain it to you in detail later?\"","Qin Shaozong took a sip of wine, noncommittal.","Du Manxiang knew in her heart that he had agreed.","Most of the guests had arrived at the Changle Manor around the hour of Wei, but by the time the wine-tasting banquet truly began, it was already the hour of Shen. The event flowed seamlessly into the evening banquet. As they drank and dined, the sky outside unknowingly darkened layer by layer.","Changle Manor was quite a distance from Chang'an, and it was now too late to rush back even on fast horses.","Besides, the invitations sent to the various families had originally noted that they would stay overnight at the manor. Therefore, the setting sun had no impact on the grand feast; it merely added a touch of radiant afterglow.","The spacious hall was filled with the scent of alcohol as wine jars were brought out one after another.","The entourages of the various warlords had all drunk heavily. Some had seen battle, while others had not, but right now, as they held wine jars in one hand and embraced dancing girls with the other in wild abandon, one could hardly tell the difference.","At the very least, they were not like Xie Yuanyue, whose face was currently deathly pale, clearly suffering from internal injuries.","The evening banquet lasted until the end of the hour of You before it finally dispersed.","The courtyards and pavilions of Changle Manor were as numerous as carp in a river; there was plenty of room for everyone to stay.","Dong Zhou arranged for Qin Shaozong and Xie Yuanyue to stay in the same large courtyard, while Li Lishen and Jiang Shi shared another.","As for himself, he announced that he would be staying in the same courtyard area as Nangong Xiong.","However, this was only on the surface. After entering the courtyard area known as Jiangnan Garden with Nangong Xiong and the others, Dong Zhou quickly slipped away through the back door.","He arrived at another courtyard.","Jiang Shi had been waiting respectfully for him there for quite some time. Seeing Dong Zhou walking over slowly, he hurried forward to greet him.","Dong Zhou let out a drunken hiccup and did not stop the other man from supporting him. However, he was so obese and round that he resembled a mountain of flesh, while Jiang Shi had a slender build. Even if the latter gritted his teeth, it was a struggle to hold him up alone.","The two of them swayed precariously together until Dong Zhou finally stood up straight on his own and took a seat by a nearby desk.","\"How is Xie Tengyun's condition?\" Dong Zhou asked.","Jiang Shi said, \"He is a martial artist after all. Even after spitting out two mouthfuls of blood, he was still able to answer with a clear mind. I am afraid... he won't be easily confused.\"","The last few words were spoken vaguely.","Dong Zhou sneered, \"What is there to fear? There are many helping you tonight. Besides, Yu Teng, Yang Tong, and Min Zhongtian are already nine parts drunk; they had to be carried back by others. I imagine they won't wake up until the golden crow rises into the sky tomorrow.\"","The \"Yu Teng and Yang Tong\" he mentioned were both subordinates of Xie Yuanyue.","Jiang Shi had also drunk a lot of wine tonight. At this moment, he felt as if rivers were surging through his veins, causing his heart to jump up and down. He lowered his voice to make one final confirmation, \"Chancellor Dong, are you certain that apart from Yang Tong and his ilk, the rest are all Second Brother Xie's men?\"","A massive, palm-leaf-fan-like hand reached out and patted Jiang Shi heavily on the shoulder. Dong Zhou smiled and said, \"Rest assured. This matter also concerns my safety and the future shifts in power. If I were not absolutely certain, I would never ask you to take such a risk.\"","Xie Yuanyue was the eldest in his family. He had two younger brothers: Xie Yuanqi was the second, and Xie Yuanxiu was the third.","Initially, it was Xie Yuanxiu who had risen to power.","Later, Xie Yuanxiu was defeated in battle and captured. He suffered greatly at the hands of Qin Shaozong, and his defeat was like a landslide. His faction was naturally swallowed up completely by his two older brothers.","Then came the struggle between the eldest and Second Brother Xie, which ended with Xie Yuanqi's defeat. After Second Brother Xie lost, he fled Si Province in a panic. It was said that he later encountered bandits on the road and tragically perished. There were also rumors that he was successfully assassinated by Xie Yuanyue's subordinates.","Opinions varied, and there was no definitive conclusion. To the outside world, it was only claimed that Xie Yuanqi had fled.","Yet only a very few knew that the defeated fugitive was still living safely and soundly; he had merely gone elsewhere.","He transitioned from the light into the shadows, becoming a hidden chess piece.","Jiang Shi still hesitated. Tonight was of grave importance; the slightest mistake, and the meal on the chopping block would instantly change from the Tiger of the North to himself.","The smile on Dong Zhou's face widened, his fat squeezing his eyes into tiny slits. \"If this succeeds, half of Si Province will be yours.\"","On the surface, Li Lishen and Jiang Shi showed a higher degree of obedience to the imperial court than those in other regions. Dong Zhou's relationship with both men was decent, but the former was far less useful than the latter.","Xu Province's terrain was excellent, easy to defend and hard to attack, and it was further from Chang'an than Yu Province. Li Lishen had a broader avenue of retreat than Jiang Shi, which was why the latter was the most suitable pawn for tonight's operation.","The look in Jiang Shi's eyes shifted unpredictably, but ultimately, ambition gained the upper hand. He rose from his seat, cupped his hands, and bowed to Dong Zhou. \"Then I shall follow Chancellor Dong's words. However, I am not a man of steadfast fortitude or tight lips. I can only hope that everything goes smoothly tonight.\"","His final words carried a distinct undertone of threat.","Dong Zhou's smile did not wane. After watching him leave, he leisurely picked up a cup and poured himself some tea.","To win a game of chess, how could one be unwilling to sacrifice a single piece?","*","The door to the main room of the courtyard was pushed open, and the gradually brightening moonlight spilled inside. A burly man entered first, followed by a graceful figure.","Qin Shaozong pulled out a fire starter. Just as he was about to blow on it to light the lamp, he suddenly furrowed his long brows and stepped aside.","It was exactly this step that caused the woman coming up from behind, intending to embrace his waist, to catch nothing but air.","Du Manxiang had not expected him to move so suddenly. Unable to stop her momentum, she stumbled and fell to the floor.","Qin Shaozong didn't look at her, continuing what he had been about to do.","Soon, light filled the pitch-black room.","Kuang Ye, Feng Feng, and their group had also drunk quite a bit tonight. The military officers of the North had excellent tolerance for alcohol, but they were slightly inferior to their superior, hence their footsteps were a few beats slower now.","The first to step into the doorway of the main room was Feng Feng.","He was just about to speak to Qin Shaozong regarding tonight's guard duty. However, the moment he looked up, Feng Feng shuddered, his drunkenness instantly dissipating by a few degrees, and he hurriedly stepped back.","Yet the scene he had just witnessed still flashed before his eyes.","Lady Du, dressed in a thin, crimson gauze robe, was slumped on the floor. Whether she had accidentally torn her clothes when she fell or for some other reason, a large expanse of her chest was exposed, and a pair of snow-white mounds were just a fraction away from spilling out.","She seemed entirely oblivious to it, only gazing at the man beside her with tear-blurred eyes.","She was, after all, his superior's woman. Even if she was a dismissed concubine, Feng Feng instinctively pulled the door shut and backed out.","Qin Shaozong walked over to a chair and sat down with an imposing, wide-legged stance. Tonight, Dong Zhou and the others had deliberately urged him to drink, and he had consumed a great deal. However, aside from an imperceptible flush on his dark skin, he showed no signs of intoxication.","Du Manxiang did not stand up. She crawled over on her knees, crying softly, \"Lord Qin...\"","Qin Shaozong finally spoke, but his first sentence was not directed at the person in the room. \"Why did you close the door? Feng Feng, open the door and roll back in here.\""]},{"number":156,"title":"Chapter 156","paragraphs":["Feng Feng outside was shouted at, and his drunkenness dissipated a bit. He hurriedly pushed the door open with a creak and entered.","The shallow moonlight slipped into the room again. The person in the room still felt it was not enough and said, \"Everyone outside, come in.\"","Kuang Ye and Bai Jianping looked at each other, not daring to disobey.","So in just a moment, the scene in the room was completely different. A row of tall and sturdy generals lined up in front of Qin Shaozong, as if forming a hard and high wall.","Du Manxiang faced Qin Shaozong, and behind her were a group of drunken and masculine generals. Caught in the middle, she was like a petal blown by the wind in the wild yellow sand, quickly eroding and withering in the dust.","Feeling like she had thorns on her back, Du Manxiang froze, feeling completely uncomfortable. She couldn't help but quietly lift up her deliberately slipped outer garment a little.","Only then did Qin Shaozong speak, \"Tell me, who arranged for you to come to Chang'an?\"","Before his wedding, he gave each of the concubines in the backyard a sum of money and the deeds to houses and shops, and then sent them all out of the mansion. As for what happened after they left, whether they were taken back by their maiden families or married someone else, it had nothing to do with him.","Except, if it involved a conspiracy against the North.","From Yuyang to Chang'an, it was more than a thousand miles away. If Du Ji had no one to help her, how could she safely arrive at the imperial city?","Dong Zhou was fond of women, and it was normal for him to take a fancy to Du Ji. But he didn't take her into his backyard, but sent her to Changle Garden as a dancer...","When things go wrong, there must be a demon!","*","In the next courtyard.","\"Knock, knock.\" Someone knocked on the door.","Xie Yuanyue, who had already laid down in the room, vaguely asked who it was upon hearing the sound.","\"Governor Xie of Sizhou, I am Xinglin of Changle Garden. I have been ordered by Prime Minister Dong to treat you,\" the person replied.","Xie Yuanyue's chaotic brain cleared up a bit, remembering that when he left the banquet, Dong Zhou casually mentioned that he would send a Xinglin to see him after he returned to his room.","He had been kicked by Qin Changgeng at the banquet. Although he immediately summoned a doctor, in order not to show weakness in front of others, he only briefly checked it and waved him away.","Now, he really felt uncomfortable.","Xie Yuanyue took a breath and stood up to open the door. A man carrying a wooden box stood at the door. Just as he was about to let the other party in, he suddenly saw a familiar figure pass through the guarded courtyard gate and come alone.","Who else could the visitor be but Jiang Shi?","\"Brother Xie, I have something important to find you for.\" Jiang Shi seemed drunk, his steps heavy.","Xie Yuanyue welcomed him at the door, \"What is it that makes you come in the middle of the night?\"","Jiang Shi seemed to realize later that there was a third person present. He burped and said with a thick tongue, \"Brother Xie, you treat your injury first. After the doctor finishes seeing you, I will tell you in detail how to deal with that arrogant Marquis of Wu'an. This time, we must cut him into a thousand pieces!\"","Xie Yuanyue originally wanted to refuse Jiang Shi and tell him to talk about it tomorrow, as it wouldn't make a difference. But when he heard his astonishing words, he hurriedly covered his mouth and dragged him into the room.","\"Speak carefully!\" Xie Yuanyue said in a deep voice.","He and the people from the North lived in the same area, separated by only a few walls.","Walls have ears, so one cannot speak carelessly.","Once the door was closed, the three of them were in the same room.","Jiang Shi mumbled, his words so vague that Xie Yuanyue couldn't hear what he was saying. The latter simply threw him aside and took off his clothes for Xinglin to check his bones and dispel the bruises. \"Governor Jiang of Yuzhou, you sober up first.\"","After a long while, Xinglin withdrew his hand and said, \"Governor Xie of Sizhou, I have ordered a maid to brew a bruise-dispelling medicine. The medicine will be delivered shortly. Please drink it while it's hot. The medicine also has a sleep-inducing effect. It is normal to feel sleepy after taking it.\"","Xie Yuanyue nodded, \"I know. You can go out first.\"","It was indeed \"delivered shortly.\" As soon as Xinglin left, the maid carrying the medicine arrived.","\"Put it down and step back,\" Xie Yuanyue waved his hand.","The door closed again.","\"Has brother sobered up?\" Xie Yuanyue sat cross-legged next to the desk.","Jiang Shi pressed his temples, \"I really drank too much tonight. I made a fool of myself in front of brother.\"","\"Since you've sobered up, go back and rest early. We have to return to the city tomorrow.\" Xie Yuanyue picked up the medicine bowl. The temperature was just right, and he drank it all in one gulp.","Jiang Shi watched him drink the medicine in the bowl cleanly, a strange dark light flashing in his eyes. \"Does brother think I was just talking nonsense when I said I had a way? No, I really have a brilliant plan that will make Qin Changgeng overwhelmed, become the target of public criticism, and have to bear a bad name and be at the mercy of others.\"","He spoke so firmly that Xie Yuanyue heard this, and his loose spine slowly straightened. \"What brilliant plan does brother have?\"","Jiang Shi stood up and walked to him. \"Prime Minister Dong declared at the banquet that our gathering at Changle Garden was not only to connect our feelings but also to plan for the subsequent elimination of treacherous officials. In fact, you and I both know well that this trip is only to eliminate treacherous officials. But the treacherous thief is cunning and hides in his shell, refusing to come out. If left alone, when the golden crow rises tomorrow and the gates of Chang'an City open, it will only be a waste of effort.\"","Xie Yuanyue hesitated and guessed, \"Brother, do you want to lure the snake out of its hole?\"","\"No.\" Jiang Shi smiled and shook his head. \"Qin Changgeng has made up his mind to be a shrinking turtle, so how could he not endure this short night? Luring the snake out of its hole will not work. Only by stepping on the snake hole and smashing his turtle shell to pieces can we subdue him.\"","Xie Yuanyue didn't understand. \"How to smash?\"","\"Naturally, use a sharp weapon to break the situation,\" Jiang Shi smiled even deeper.","The light and shadow in front of Xie Yuanyue suddenly separated and merged. He felt dizzy, as if the jars of wine he had drunk earlier rushed to his head together.","Oh, it might be the bruise-dispelling medicine prescribed by Xinglin earlier taking effect. It indeed made people sleepy, but Governor Jiang of Yuzhou was still there, so he couldn't fall asleep.","Xie Yuanyue shook his head, but the symptoms only increased. Unwilling to drop the ball at such an important juncture, he forced himself to ask, \"Where does the sharp weapon come from?\"","\"Sharp weapon...\" Jiang Shi stared closely at Xie Yuanyue. Taking advantage of the moment when the other party lowered his head and dozed off, he suddenly pulled out the short knife at his waist and stabbed it hard into the other party's chest. \"Naturally, take it from in front of you!\"","A faint line of blood shot out with a \"hiss.\"","Xie Yuanyue's pupils contracted and dilated, and he stiffly raised his head: \"You...\"","The Prime Minister held a banquet, and it was inconvenient for everyone present to wear armor, which naturally included Xie Yuanyue.","Jiang Shi was thin. In terms of strength alone, even three of him couldn't beat Xie Yuanyue. But his advantage was that the other party was drugged and not as good as before, that Xie Yuanyue was already injured, and even more so, his surprise attack and ruthlessness.","The wrist holding the knife handle turned fiercely, and then pulled out forcefully. Jiang Shi watched coldly as the other party fell.","The person was dead, but he didn't leave immediately. Jiang Shi picked up the bedding on the couch, wrapped a tea set in it, and threw it heavily on the ground.","The movement was not loud. The high-quality tea set was completely destroyed, pretending that a dispute had occurred on the scene.","The quilt was put back on the couch. Jiang Shi turned and walked out. Midway, he seemed to remember something, paused slightly, took out a dark-colored purse he had temporarily asked for from his arms, and threw it casually on the ground.","*","In the next courtyard.","There was a bit of fear in Du Manxiang's eyes. \"After leaving the Marquis's mansion, I originally wanted to seek refuge with my cousin in Jizhou. But not long after leaving Yuyang, I unluckily met some bad people. The other party had evil thoughts and wanted to take both my money and my body...\"","When she said this, Du Manxiang quietly observed Qin Shaozong in front of her.","He sat by the desk. On the desk was a bright lamp, its light falling on his profile, illuminating his full forehead and straight nose. The man's deep brown eyes remained like a frozen pool in winter, perfectly still, without the slightest ripple.","She lowered her eyes in disappointment. \"Perhaps the heavens took pity on me; I was saved by a group of traveling merchants. They claimed I owed them my life and could not leave until I repaid their kindness. They took me all the way south, finally arriving in Chang'an.\"","She said she was so terrified later on that she accidentally revealed she came from the Marquis's estate in the North. This made the merchant, who originally intended to give her to a minor official in Chang'an, change his mind. He handed her over to Dong Zhou instead, explaining her origins.","\"...My Lord, I only want to survive. Coming to Chang'an was not my wish, nor was dancing at the banquet my true intention. I was forced into all of this. Could you, for the sake of our past years together, save me from this tiger's den?\" Du Manxiang said, her eyes brimming with tears.","She was undoubtedly beautiful. Seeing a beauty weep, many would sigh with pity.","But this clearly did not include Qin Shaozong. The candlelight could not add even a fraction of softness to his face. Expressionless, he asked, \"What is the name of the key figure in that merchant caravan, and what does he look like? Also, where did you stay when you first arrived in Chang'an, and who did you contact before Dong Zhou? Tell me everything.\"","Du Manxiang choked slightly, almost imperceptibly, before speaking slowly.","Qin Shaozong rested his hand on his knee, his long fingers tapping against his kneecap rhythmically as he listened to Du Manxiang's description.","Qin Shaozong did not fully believe her words, but the basic framework of her information seemed true.","Her appearance at Changle Estate was deliberate. This person—or rather, the leader of these merchants—had known long ago that the imperial court was going to confer a title upon his wife. He had the means to reach Dong Zhou and viewed the North as an enemy...","There were truly very few candidates left.","Concubine Du was a \"brick.\" The other party had calculated that his guard and curiosity would be aroused simultaneously, and he would definitely seek her out to ask for the truth. Therefore, the subsequent sparring match was inevitable.","That match was the \"jade\"—casting a brick to attract jade.","But why do this? What could a mere sparring match decide?","Qin Shaozong had drunk quite a bit tonight. He wasn't drunk, but the alcohol had made his thoughts much more sluggish. The doubts lingering in his mind yielded no answers.","He raised his hand to pinch the bridge of his nose and said, dividing his attention, \"You and I have long severed our ties. It is useless for you to seek me out for this. If you want to leave Changle Estate, go find Governor Nangong.\"","Anxious, Du Manxiang moved forward on her knees a couple of steps. \"Lord Qin! I do not know Governor Nangong at all; he certainly won't agree to my request. Are you worried that taking me back will displease the Marchioness? I promise that when I see her, I will kowtow and pay my deepest respects. I will put her first in everything and serve her tea every morning. If Madam dislikes seeing me, I can...\"","\"You are mistaken.\" Qin Shaozong lowered the hand pinching his brow, his brown eyes as cold as ever. \"I am the one who does not wish to keep you; it has nothing to do with my wife.\"","The so-called jealousy of women was merely an excuse for men's own restless desires. Qin Shaozong knew this perfectly well. In the past, he hadn't cared, so he didn't point it out, didn't interfere, and didn't waste the slightest energy paying attention to it. But things were different now.","The bright moon already hung high in the sky; why would it need to compete with the stars for radiance?","Du Manxiang's lips parted, but she was too stunned to speak.","Qin Shaozong, however, stopped looking at her and directly called out a name. \"Feng Feng, see our guest out.\"","Feng Feng had no choice but to step forward. He didn't speak, only gesturing with his hand for her to leave.","Looking at the rough palm before her, Du Manxiang's heart trembled repeatedly. She had the feeling that if she didn't cooperate, the man would just drag her out. She turned to look at Qin Shaozong, but before the words \"Lord Qin\" could leave her mouth, Feng Feng forcefully hauled her away.","After the two left, Qin Shaozong looked at his gathered military officers.","Kuang Ye and the others all wore solemn expressions. Just as they thought their superior was going to discuss the follow-up plans with them, they heard a light cough, followed by him saying:","\"Do not tell my wife about what happened today, nor mention it in front of the two boys. If, by some misfortune, Madam finds out, you must tell her everything truthfully. Do not fabricate anything.\"","Everyone: \"...\"","Deathly silence.","Pretending not to notice their strange expressions, Qin Shaozong said, \"Tell me, what was the other party's intention in provoking the sparring match?\"","Everyone had drunk wine tonight, so their words were a bit wild and imaginative, covering all sorts of theories. Qin Shaozong listened for a moment but still couldn't find a clue, so he simply sent them back to sleep.","He also went to bed himself, closing his eyes to rest.","Scene after scene flashed through his mind. His thoughts slowly sank into the deep sea. Just as Qin Shaozong was about to fall asleep, a flash of lightning suddenly struck his mind.","Like crashing waves and a shattering sky.","Qin Shaozong abruptly opened his eyes.","He had been thinking in the wrong direction earlier. He shouldn't have looked for clues within the Green Lotus Sect, nor from Dong Zhou, who hosted the banquet.","Xie Yuanyue, he should be looking at Governor Xie of Sizhou, who had sparred with him! They were only staying at Changle Estate for one night. After tonight, they would all return to their respective estates, and it would be difficult to meet again in the future.","The incident was meant to happen tonight...","Qin Shaozong quickly got up and dressed. He had just fastened his belt and equipped his ring-pommel sword when he heard a commotion outside.","The noise spread like an incoming tide, rolling in from far to near.","\"My Lord!\"","\"My Lord!\"","Kuang Ye and the others also hurried out upon hearing the noise.","All of them were half-dressed, the only similarity being that they all held swords in their hands.","Qin Shaozong's narrow eyes swept over them, finally stopping on Bai Jianping, who had a special talent for mimicking the sounds of birds and beasts. \"Bai Jianping, there is a mutiny tonight. You and Mo Yanyun will secretly leave Changle Estate and immediately notify Wei Qing at the foot of the mountain. Tell him to split the troops in two: one unit will come up the mountain, and the other must quickly return to the military camp outside Chang'an.\"","Bai Jianping and Mo Yanyun froze.","Qin Shaozong quickly estimated the time. \"At the earliest, the soldiers from the suburban camp will reach Chang'an by tomorrow morning. When the city gates open at dawn, have them enter the city with my token. If the city guards block them, do not hesitate—force your way in. You must escort Madam back to the military camp. Go quickly!\"","The two men shuddered, cupped their fists in salute, and quickly vanished into the darkness.","Kuang Ye said with concern, \"My Lord, the reinforcements will arrive in Chang'an tomorrow at the earliest. If Chancellor Dong decides to rebel tonight, our Mistress will likely face enemies tonight.\"","Qin Shaozong looked toward Chang'an. As if answering Kuang Ye's question, or perhaps speaking to himself, he said, \"Before leaving, I left two hundred elite soldiers for Madam, and I warned her that things might change tonight. She should understand, and she will definitely be able to wait until I return...\""]},{"number":157,"title":"Chapter 157","paragraphs":["\"Bullshit! What does Governor Xie of Sizhou's death have to do with our lord? You can't just say we killed him because he and our Northern forces live in the same compound. By that logic, I could say he was harsh to his subordinates, causing them to harbor malicious intent and kill him while he was drunk.\"","\"Their Sizhou soldiers were guarding the courtyard entrance, how could they not have heard the commotion inside? Logically, they should have rushed in the moment the dispute began. But the Sizhou soldiers did nothing, so the culprit must definitely be from among them!\"","\"Exactly, stop framing our lord.\"","...","With Qin Shaozong at the center, the military officers on his sides spread out like wings.","Opposite them, Dong Zhou, Jiang Shi, and Li Lishen, along with their subordinates, also formed a wing-like formation. Compared to the Northern forces, their wings were larger and exuded a greater sense of power.","On the side of the two opposing factions, the Qingzhou forces led by Nangong Xiong sat like hyenas watching from the sidelines, hiding their intentions.","The dead Xie Yuanyue was in the nearby courtyard, the room brightly lit and the doors wide open.","Li Lishen said at this time, \"You make a good point. If there were guards at the courtyard entrance, they should have known. However, everyone drank wine tonight and returned in high spirits. It's perfectly normal for the guards to be negligent. Furthermore...\"","He pointed to the wall separating the two courtyards. Inner walls were never as high as outer walls. \"Who doesn't know the martial prowess of Marquis Wu'an? A low wall is nothing to you, Qin Changgeng. Just a lift of your foot and you're over. If you didn't take the usual path, it's highly likely the guards wouldn't have spotted you.\"","Jiang Shi chimed in opportunely, \"Among everyone present, only you had a grudge against Xie Tengyun. You defeated him in the banquet's competition and took the dancer he fancied. After the banquet, you both live in the same compound, so you were bound to meet again. Given Tengyun's temper, he probably provoked you. Marquis Wu'an, if you could strike him heavily at the banquet over a mere dancer, it makes sense that you would sneak into his room and kill him after being enraged.\"","\"Absurd! All of this is just your speculation. To pin the crime on our lord based on this alone, I think it's you, Governor Jiang of Yuzhou, who has an ulterior motive,\" Feng Feng said angrily.","Two people had clearly proposed the speculation, but Feng Feng only singled out Jiang Shi, acting as if he was only attacking him.","Jiang Shi's brow twitched, but he quickly calmed down. He took out an object and tossed it in his hand. \"This is not baseless speculation. I have a little trinket to prove it.\"","Qin Shaozong barely noticeably glanced sideways, quickly looking at the full moon in the sky.","Unaware, Jiang Shi continued, \"You all saw it in the room just now. There's a pouch next to the fallen Tengyun. Marquis Wu'an, are you familiar with this?\"","He suddenly sneered, \"Heh, even if you intentionally or unintentionally ignored it just now, you can't change the fact that it fell from you earlier. After all, I saw it clearly at the banquet.\"","Qin Shaozong scoffed, \"What kind of physical evidence is this? My pouch is still on me. If you just find a random pouch and claim it's mine, then I could say the knife stuck in Governor Xie of Sizhou's chest belongs to you, Governor Jiang of Yuzhou.\"","Jiang Shi's face changed drastically. \"Nonsense!\"","Nangong Xiong, who had been a bystander nearby, began to sense something amiss.","This trap was clumsy, ridiculous, and crude to the extreme. It was just a torn fig leaf thrown over it in a vain attempt to frame someone.","But it had to be said that Chancellor Dong, who held the power of the imperial court, really had the ability to mobilize several provincial governors near Chang'an to point at a deer and call it a horse.","It seemed the other party wanted to take down Qin Changgeng before Liu of Jingzhou arrived in the capital.","He wasn't surprised that the Chancellor set a trap; this wine tasting banquet was never pure from the start. Now that the two sides were purely fighting with words, he could understand Chancellor Dong's urgency to pin the crime of \"murdering Governor Xie of Sizhou\" on Marquis Wu'an, but he couldn't understand Qin Changgeng's attitude.","Based on his understanding of the man, he wasn't the type to enjoy verbal sparring or surrender without a fight.","But strangely...","Nangong Xiong quietly looked at the walls in the courtyard. On the dark, low walls, it seemed as if mountain peaks had risen from the ground, with \"small hilltops\" appearing continuously.","But those weren't small hilltops; they were clearly heads wearing helmets. Under the moonlight, the arrowheads in the soldiers' hands reflected a cold, sinister gleam, like the bared fangs of venomous snakes.","Nangong Xiong gasped inwardly.","It seemed there was indeed no other way but to clear his suspicion through verbal sparring. But what use was mere verbal sparring? Since Dong had decided to capture him tonight, sooner or later would be the same; they would end up at the same destination.","Unless Qin Changgeng had known everything in advance and sent people down the mountain ahead of time, which was why he needed to stall...","But Marquis Wu'an wasn't an immortal; how could he foresee everything?","While thinking this, Nangong Xiong suddenly saw Dong Zhou frown nearby, as if pondering something.","Qin Shaozong's ears suddenly twitched, and then he said, \"Although there are signs of a struggle in the room, Governor Xie of Sizhou was quite skilled in martial arts. If he really died in combat, there couldn't possibly be only such a small amount of struggle marks in the room. The specifics need to be carefully investigated further.\"","With that, he took the lead and walked inside.","As soon as he stepped forward, the group of Northern military officers followed closely behind. They were all tall, and with their long legs taking large strides, the group flowed into the room like water in the blink of an eye, completely retreating.","Jiang Shi and Li Lishen were both stunned.","Almost as soon as Qin Shaozong and the others entered the room, someone hurried over from the courtyard entrance. \"Chancellor! A group of soldiers has arrived outside the garden and is forcing their way in. Their attack is extremely fierce. It looks like... the attackers are from the North.\"","Dong Zhou's expression changed instantly. In that moment, the faint, spiderweb-like anomalies in his mind all found their answers.","\"Marquis Wu'an murdered Governor Xie of Sizhou and even attempted to destroy the corpse and silence witnesses. This is truly despicable. Men, capture all the Northerners!\" Dong Zhou shouted.","As soon as he finished speaking, the soldiers who had been climbing the walls all jumped down, while another group of guards surged in from outside the courtyard.","Nangong Xiong's pupils shrank to pinpricks, a myriad of thoughts flashing through his mind in an instant.","To advance meant joining Qin Shaozong; to retreat meant automatically joining Dong Zhou's camp. He had already formed an alliance with Qin Changgeng to jointly attack the Qinglian Faction. Even if he submitted to Dong Zhou now, the latter might not truly trust him.","In this life-and-death struggle, there was no neutrality.","Nangong Xiong couldn't help but curse, gritted his teeth, and said to his subordinates, \"Follow!\"","The Qingzhou group immediately rushed forward. The room door was closed, so they took a side path to the backyard, intending to exit through the side door.","A fierce glint flashed in Dong Zhou's eyes. \"Marquis Wu'an is colluding with Governor Nangong. Capture them all! Kill anyone who resists on the spot!\"","...","Inside the room.","Feng Feng, the last to enter, swiftly locked the door.","Without Qin Shaozong's order, Kuang Ye drew his sword and swung it fiercely at the long desk. With a \"bang,\" it was split in two, turning the desk into shields.","The others followed suit.","In addition to the main door, windows in various parts of the room were also opened. The group passed through the house and retreated from the other side.","There were also soldiers stationed at the rear, though fewer than at the front. Seeing them jump out of the window, the leader immediately raised his voice, They are out! Fire the arrows!","Swish, swish, swish!","Arrows rained down.","Meanwhile, in Chang'an. Spring Day.","On the night Qin Shaozong left, Dai Li did not sleep soundly. His words, There might be changes tonight, seemed to become an ebbing and flowing tide, echoing in her ears from time to time.","The Sword of Damocles hanging over her head finally fell when the silence of the late night was broken.","My Lady! There were hurried footsteps, followed by Qiao Wangfei's voice. A large group of military patrols has arrived outside the estate. The leader claims that a petty thief they are pursuing has slipped into our manor, and they are demanding that we open the gates for a search.","Dai Li sat up in shock, clutching her quilt. Her first words were that the gates must not be opened.","Qiao Wangfei quickly replied, Of course we didn't open them. But they are coming on strong and look as if they won't give up until they achieve their goal. I ordered men to climb the trees and go up to several pavilions in the estate to look out. We found that not only the main gate but also several side gates are surrounded by patrols. At a rough estimate, there are no less than a thousand men.","Dai Li's heart sank to the bottom.","She had two hundred elite soldiers on hand, but there were no less than a thousand men surrounding the estate alone. What about those ambushing in the dark?","In the massive city of Chang'an, it was common for the patrol guards to number in the tens of thousands. Two hundred against tens of thousands—even the strongest soldiers would be worn to death.","Dai Li quickly got out of bed and dressed, saying at the same time, It seems a fierce battle is inevitable tonight. Order them to make sure their armor is properly worn. Only by preserving our combat strength as much as possible will we have a chance of survival. By the way, which gate is the leader at?","Qiao Wangfei said he was at the main gate.","Dai Li: Send someone to tell the patrol leader to wait a moment. I will speak with him personally.","You must not, My Lady, Qiao Wangfei said anxiously. They came while the Lord is away, harboring unpredictable motives. You must not fall for their tricks.","I must go. As the saying goes, courtesy before force. If we want to stall for time, we can only do so through courtesy. Dai Li fastened her belt and then tucked a short sword left by Qin Shaozong into her waist. Don't dawdle, do as I say!","Dai Li's voice had always been gentle, having nothing to do with heroism. At this moment, speaking with her voice slightly lowered, that spring-breeze-like voice actually revealed a bit of majesty.","Qiao Wangfei unconsciously stiffened his spine. The muscles on his cheeks bulged and then smoothed out. Finally, he raised his voice and called a guard outside the main courtyard, telling him to pass on the message.","The message was passed, but other things still needed to be said.","Qiao Wangfei reminded her, My Lady, Changle Garden is a full half-day's journey from Chang'an. Even if the Lord knows about the changes in the estate now, the fastest he can rush back is tomorrow morning.","No matter how much they delayed, it was impossible for the other party to spend the whole night outside with them.","There was not enough time.","Creak. The door was suddenly pulled open.","There was a moon tonight. The moonlight fell on the woman's cold and glamorous jade face, which was like a peony on a high terrace, as if covering her in a layer of holy gauze. Her face was soft, but her eyes were as bright as snow blades, shining like firelight, hiding sharpness and a piercing spirit.","Who said we have to wait for Qin Changgeng to come back? Dai Li walked briskly out of the courtyard. Distant water cannot put out a nearby fire. Tonight, we can only save ourselves.","Qiao Wangfei subconsciously followed her. Just as he was about to ask how to save themselves, he heard Dai Li continue: You just said that several gates of the estate are surrounded by military patrols. Which gate has the fewest soldiers?","This really stumped Qiao Wangfei.","As the garrison commander of the Xuanxiao Cavalry, he had hundreds of soldiers under him and didn't need to do everything himself. The fact that several side gates were blocked by military patrols was told to him by his subordinates.","Seeing his pause, Dai Li understood that he didn't know either. Send someone to investigate immediately. Once it's clear, organize a hundred men around that small gate and open it to welcome them in.","Qiao Wangfei's expression changed drastically. My Lady, how can this gate be opened? Once the gate is open, the guards outside will definitely swarm in. Moreover, if we directly transfer a hundred men away, that means only a hundred men will be left elsewhere. This estate is very wide, and the outer wall defense consumes a lot of troops. In this way, there will be even fewer people left by your side.","I didn't tell you to keep the gate open all the time. Lure a batch of military patrols in and then close it. Dai Li turned to look at Qiao Wangfei, the light in her eyes seeming to grow brighter. I need the clothes on the military patrols. This is the key, and we must get them!","Qiao Wangfei was stunned.","He was able to sit in the position of garrison commander absolutely not just by brute force without wisdom. Now hearing Dai Li mention the clothes of the military patrols, he immediately thought—","My Lady, are you trying to take advantage of the dark night and muddy waters to escape in the chaos? After stating this guess, Qiao Wangfei quickly weighed the success and failure, and finally had to shake his head: It's not very feasible. The soldiers surrounding the estate are only the first line of defense; the city gates are the second.","Saying not very feasible was already a euphemism.","Even with the cover of night, precisely because night had fallen, the curfew in the city kept the commoners indoors, which ironically reduced many unnecessary obstacles for the enemy.","This cat-and-mouse hunt might not last the night. In the end, two hundred men were simply too few.","I know everything you're saying. I have a way to get reinforcements. Dai Li did not stop walking.","Qiao Wangfei froze for a breath.","Reinforcements? Where would reinforcements come from?!","The main force of the Xuanxiao Cavalry was thirty miles outside the city. Now the city gates were tightly closed, and no news could be sent out of the city. How could reinforcements arrive?","Qiao Wangfei's mind spun, even guessing whether the Lord had secretly left an unknown guard squad for the Lady before he left.","The situation was urgent. The two talked as they walked. Just as they walked out of the courtyard, they met three juniors who had come after hearing the news.","Dai Li could not be in two places at once, so she could only speak concisely to her son: Zhou Zhou, there is an incident tonight. You and your younger siblings follow Hu Bao and do not run around.","After instructing the juniors, Dai Li, without stopping her steps, continued to Qiao Wangfei, Our residence is surrounded by the dwellings of people from several other provinces. Tonight the military patrols are aggressive. I don't believe they are unaware of this. Since it's a blockade, who says they can only hunt the Northern Territory?","Qiao Wangfei's breath hitched. After understanding the meaning of Dai Li's words, he was so excited that his arm hairs stood on end. You want to use the clothes of the military patrols to let us pretend to be Chang'an soldiers, and then attack the residences of Sizhou, Yuzhou, and Xuzhou?","Yes!","Dai Li gave an affirmative answer. I don't believe they are of one mind with that man surnamed Dong. As long as they are not a monolithic block, as long as there is still suspicion among them, we can use it. It just so happens that those provincial governors are away tonight, and everyone's military camps are set up in the suburbs. There are only a mere two or three hundred people left in their estates, or even fewer. Suddenly attacked late at night, they will definitely be full of doubts, guessing that Chancellor Dong wants to wipe them all out in one fell swoop.","These were not countermeasures that Dai Li had thought up in a few moments, but the train of thought she had sorted out after tossing and turning before falling asleep tonight, and waking up in shock from her dreams several times.","Dai Li: It's true that we only have two hundred men, but if we can trick the various families over in the chaos and twist everyone together into a single rope, we'll have a force of at least nearly a thousand men, and all of them elite soldiers. It's not impossible to open the city gates from the inside and get out of the city.","One must know that when Dong Zhuo attacked Luoyang back then, he also relied on merely an elite force of three thousand men. One can imagine that the power of elite soldiers is far beyond compare with a ragtag bunch.","\"However, to simultaneously attack the other provincial governors' estates, a hundred or so men are far from enough. It would be best to secure the assistance of neighboring Qingzhou.\" Dai Li paused. \"Right, Governor Nangong has already gone to the banquet, so his daughter must have stayed behind in the estate. We need to send a team over there, not only to act as persuaders but also to bring her out.\"","She remembered that Nangong Xiong had always intended to cooperate with Qin Changgeng.","With the sudden upheaval in the Changle Garden tonight, everything depended on the other party's choice. Optimistically, her action would be saving an ally's daughter; pessimistically, it would be taking a crucial enemy hostage.","Qin Yanzhou glanced at Qin Qinian. The latter's mind worked like lightning, and the two brothers found themselves on a rare, identical wavelength.","\"Mother, leave this matter to Qinian and me.\"","\"Mother, leave this matter to Second Brother and me.\""]},{"number":158,"title":"Chapter 158","paragraphs":["When the two juniors volunteered at the same time, Dai Li's lips trembled, and at first, she couldn't speak.","Tonight was different from that bandit suppression. In the bandit suppression, the enemy was outnumbered by her side, and the sheer numbers largely guaranteed safety, plus Qin Changgeng was with them at the time.","But tonight...","It was true that they lived next door to the Qingzhou party, but it was not as if they could reach the opposite residence just by climbing over a wall.","There was a not-so-narrow alley between the two mansions. If the city patrol surrounded this mansion entirely, there would definitely be people in that alley too.","Just the thought of gleaming swords and arrows that seemed coated in poison raining down on her children made Dai Li's heart feel as if it were being dragged down into an ice cellar.","Seeing Dai Li remain silent, Qin Qinian grew anxious. \"Mother, Miss Nangong has seen Second Brother and me. She even promised to go out with Rongrong later, so we are not complete strangers. Going to find her now, the Qingzhou soldiers shouldn't draw their swords against us, so it couldn't be more appropriate to leave this to us.\"","Qin Yanzhou understood her worries. \"Mother, Qinian and I can act during the chaos. Once a gap in the mansion's defenses opens, the patrol will definitely rush there upon hearing the noise. This way, the soldiers guarding other areas will be much fewer.\"","Luring the tiger away from the mountain, they would use this chance to leave the mansion.","Dai Li opened her mouth, but the word \"Okay\" felt like it was covered in thorns; she just couldn't spit it out.","There was a stagnation in the air for a few breaths.","Qin Yanzhou suddenly cupped his hands to Dai Li. After a deep bow, the young man turned and walked quickly toward the Qingzhou mansion.","Qin Qinian was stunned. When he reacted, he followed suit, cupped his hands, and immediately went after his older brother.","Dai Li watched the two figures, one tall and one short, gradually fade away. Her eyes, facing the moonlight, slowly filled with moisture. But until the brothers disappeared around the corner, she did not call them to stop.","\"Madam, there are guards following them. The young masters will be fine,\" Qiao Wangfei comforted her.","Time was pressing, and there was no room for delay. Dai Li slowly exhaled a breath. As she turned and closed her eyes, a barely visible crystal tear fell from the corner of her eye.","\"Let's go. Tonight allows for no mistakes,\" she said in a cold, deep tone, showing no sign of abnormality.","This mansion used for hosting guests covered a very wide area, and every part of it was built grandly, naturally including the main gate connected to the front courtyard.","At this moment, rows of torches stood inside and outside the main gate, the flames soaring to the sky, illuminating the area as bright as day.","Just outside the door, the sounds were mixed and chaotic. There were footsteps of boots, muffled whispers, and the light clashing of weapons.","Inside the wall, the armored Northern soldiers had already drawn their swords. Their eyes were like torches, ready to strike, like wolves waiting for the wolf king's command.","\"Madam, please wait a moment,\" Qiao Wangfei called out to Dai Li at this time.","It turned out to be a foot soldier carrying armor. Qiao Wangfei said, \"The situation tonight is ever-changing, and swords have no eyes. Everything must be done with the utmost caution. This is new armor; please put it on, Madam.\"","Dai Li did not refuse. She put on the armor, which was much too large for her.","When she arrived at the main gate, it just so happened that someone outside was shouting, \"Has the Marchioness arrived yet? If not, then don't trouble her to make the trip. I will personally enter the mansion to find her.\"","As soon as these words fell, a burst of laughter erupted outside, and someone immediately chimed in:","\"The Lieutenant is right! But in the middle of the night, how can we make a beauty go through so much trouble? Why don't we just march straight in, talk to the Marchioness, and take a look at her fragrant boudoir while we're at it.\"","\"The beauty is married. The room has been tainted by the foul air of a man; it's not as good as it used to be.\"","\"What does that matter? Anyway, the Marquis of Wu'an and the Marchioness will be separated in the future and will never see each other again. If we go find the Marchioness for a chat and a meeting, the Marquis of Wu'an can't control it.\"","\"Hahahaha, exactly!\"","They not only laughed out loud but also started banging on the door, making the rather thick mansion gate rattle loudly.","Inside the gate.","Qiao Wangfei and the group of Northern soldiers were gnashing their teeth, their eyes red with hatred.","\"Bastards! How can you casually discuss the wife of a Marquis appointed by the imperial court!\" Qiao Wangfei couldn't help but shout angrily.","As a result, the laughter outside became even more presumptuous.","Dai Li shook her head at Qiao Wangfei and said in a low voice, \"It's just a provocation. Commander Qiao, don't fall for it.\"","Qiao Wangfei also knew it was a provocation, but the anger in his chest was like boiling water, churning uncontrollably. To him, Dai Li was far more than just his superior's lover; she was his savior.","Seeing that he was still extremely angry, Dai Li thought of a way to send him away. \"Once the side door is broken, their morale will definitely soar, and we will likely face the first wave of a strong attack. Commander Qiao, go arrange the archers first.\"","Qiao Wangfei took a deep breath, accepted the order, and left.","Dai Li walked to the door, pretending not to hear their malicious discussions and loud laughter, and directly asked in a raised voice, \"Where is the leader of the city patrol?\"","Amidst the rough laughter, this female voice was so abrupt and clear, like a gentle spring breeze suddenly blowing across a wilderness piled with yellow sand.","Thus, the howling of the jackals became even more arrogant.","After a good while, it seemed that the person outside suppressed the voices of his subordinates, and the surroundings quieted down again.","\"Marchioness, I am Zhong Zhuo, Lieutenant of the Northern Army. I have taken the liberty of visiting your mansion with my subordinates tonight because a petty thief stole a palace treasure, and we followed the trail, finally discovering that the thief is very likely hiding in your mansion.\" Zhong Zhuo stared intently at the tightly closed gate, as if piercing through this obstacle to see the beautiful woman behind the door.","At this moment, his canine teeth seemed to continuously elongate and sharpen, turning into the fangs of a hyena stained with foul-smelling drool.","Zhong Zhuo suppressed the smile at the corner of his mouth. \"That treasure was a tribute to His Majesty from the provinces during last year's Lantern Festival. His Majesty loves it very much, so I hope the Marchioness will open the door and cooperate with our search.\"","Dai Li said coldly, \"There are non-stop patrols in my mansion twenty-four hours a day. The soldiers of my mansion have never seen the petty thief Lieutenant Zhong speaks of. Moreover, this mansion was carefully arranged by Chancellor Dong, and the several doors and walls are impregnable. Even if Lieutenant Zhong doesn't trust the soldiers of my mansion, can it be that he also doesn't trust Chancellor Dong's judgment?\"","Bringing up Dong Zhou at the end of her words made Zhong Zhuo choke for a moment.","The adjutant beside him said, \"It's just opening the mansion gate, a matter of a single word from you. You don't have to catch the thief and recover the stolen goods yourself. Why is the Marchioness making so many excuses? Could it be that the thief who stole the rare treasure is really in your mansion?\"","As his words fell, there was a chorus of agreement all around.","Dai Li silently calculated in her heart.","Investigating which of the side doors had the least troops took time, assembling a hundred men took time, and passing orders to coordinate the subsequent actions also took time...","She had to delay a bit longer.","\"Wait. You just claimed to be a Lieutenant of the Northern Army, but words are no proof. Throw your token over for me to see,\" Dai Li suddenly said.","Zhong Zhuo was astonished. \"Why do you need a token for this? It's currently curfew. The only ones who can walk so openly in the city are our city defense patrols.\"","Dai Li retorted, \"That's not necessarily true. The little thief you mentioned can even steal treasures from the palace and retreat unscathed after the theft. How could he do that without the assistance of an accomplice? Moreover, the Marquis has conflicts with several neighboring provincial governors. How do we know if you are really the Chang'an military patrol?\"","Zhong Zhuo frowned. After whispering a few words to the adjutant beside him, he finally dug out a token from his pocket. \"Madam Marquis, please open the door. The token is here.\"","Dai Li said, \"Throw it over from above.\"","Zhong Zhuo's mouth twitched, thinking that this Marquis's wife was really not easily fooled. After a moment of stalemate, he finally tossed the token up.","Dai Li saw an object falling from above. Not waiting for it to land before picking it up, she directly raised her hand to catch it. The bronze token was not light, and it hurt her hand when it hit. Dai Li gasped.","Ignoring the pain in her hand, she stuffed the token into the hands of the soldier beside her and whispered two instructions. The latter's pupils trembled slightly, and without hesitation, he took the token and ran wildly.","\"Madam Marquis, the token has been inspected. You can open the door now,\" Zhong Zhuo shouted from outside.","Dai Li replied, \"I am just a woman and don't recognize this token. Please wait a moment. I'll call my husband's adjutant.\"","Laughter started outside again.","\"Madam Marquis, why go through so much trouble? Open the door, and I will teach you hand-in-hand how to recognize the token.\"","\"It is rumored that Madam is as beautiful as a peach or plum, with the appearance of the Moon Goddess. If we see Madam Marquis later, the lieutenant might be distracted.\"","\"Hahahaha!\"","The large hand of Qiao Wangfei holding the knife gripped so hard that his knuckles turned white, wishing he could tear them apart for firewood and cut their flesh for cooking.","Dai Li gave a reassuring look.","These words were nothing to her. The most important thing was to buy more time. As long as they could successfully exit the city tonight and rendezvous with the Xuanxiao Cavalry outside the city, it was hard to say whose head would fall in the future...","After a round of laughter over there, they urged Dai Li again.","Just as Dai Li was about to find another excuse to stall, a sudden uproar came from the west side. It was like a depth charge exploding, stirring up a thousand-layer wave, completely shattering the precarious peace that had been maintained.","A bright light flashed in Dai Li's eyes.","Here it comes!","Qiao Wangfei hurriedly said, \"Mistress, this place is dangerous. Please take shelter first.\"","Dai Li was not good at martial arts and naturally would not stay on the front line. She nodded and turned away neatly, the corner of her fluttering clothes looking like the sharp claws of a lioness in the moonlight.","...","Outside the main gate.","Zhong Zhuo looked to the west in astonishment. \"Why is it so noisy over there? What exactly happened?\"","The sound of galloping hooves came. The military patrol who came to report shouted, \"Lieutenant, the west gate of the Qin Mansion has opened. Our brothers are in a standoff with the Northern Army over there, but the other side has a large number of people and is resisting vigorously. We are temporarily at a disadvantage. Please send reinforcements, Lieutenant!\"","Zhong Zhuo abruptly turned his head to look at the tightly closed main gate. The arc of his mouth widened a bit, like a hyena celebrating before a meal. \"Madam Marquis, since your mansion has already opened the west gate, I assume you won't mind if someone enters through the other gates. Men, climb over the wall!\"","The prepared military patrols heard the order and moved forward with ladders.","*","North side gate direction.","The Qin brothers, who were waiting, heard the commotion on the west side and looked at each other simultaneously. Qin Yanzhou whispered, \"Wait ten more breaths.\"","There were hurried footsteps outside the door, sounding like they were split into two, half heading west and the other half surging towards the main gate.","After counting ten breaths, the north gate creaked open.","Qin Yanzhou and Qin Qinian led ten Northern soldiers to charge out. The group held a knife in one hand and a grappling hook in the other, with a long rope connected to the hard iron grappling hook wound around their arms.","A batch of military patrols outside had left, but they hadn't completely dispersed. Seeing someone come out now, they shouted and came over with knives.","But before they could shout a few more times, a bright red spurted out abruptly. Someone was stunned, realizing belatedly that his vision was completely upside down, and his neck hurt terribly.","\"Gulu, gulu,\" something rolled to the ground.","After dealing with a few people in succession, the brothers crossed the alley, threw their iron grappling hooks onto the wall of the opposite mansion together, and climbed up neatly.","However, just as they climbed onto the wall of the Qingzhou Mansion, everyone paused. In the cold moonlight, rows of arrowheads below were aimed at them.","\"Don't shoot arrows, I'm Qin San from next door, here to play with Nangong Xiaoliu!\" Qin Qinian sat on the wall.","Qin Yanzhou couldn't help but glance sideways at the young man; the latter noticed it and spread his hands helplessly towards his brother.","If they didn't act familiar now, they probably wouldn't be able to get down. Moreover, they had already shared a meal with everyone, so how could they not be considered familiar?","Qin Qinian unilaterally thought they were.","It was not safe to stay on the wall for a long time, as they would easily become targets. Seeing this, the military patrols outside also raised their arrows one after another.","\"Get down first.\" Qin Yanzhou jumped down.","The crowd followed closely.","The Qin brothers spent some effort and finally met Nangong Zijin. At the same time, the chaos at the west gate of the Qin Mansion came to an end.","Initially, a hundred people were stationed at the west side gate.","The strong and sturdy Northern soldiers cooperated tacitly, like the bloody mouth of a giant wolf, easily breaking up the Chang'an military patrols pouring inside.","Corpses fell one by one, and the victors removed their upper garments. These garments were roughly divided into three portions.","\"I'll lead people to the Sizhou Mansion. Xun He, you lead a team to the Xuzhou Mansion. Zhou Jinyuan, you are responsible for Yuzhou.\" The tasks were quickly assigned.","Xun He walked at the end. Just as he led his people to leave, he was suddenly stopped by a soldier running towards him.","The young soldier had probably run to many places and was out of breath, but he still neatly handed a bronze token to him, while speaking intermittently, \"Mistress, the lieutenant's token... take it...\"","Xun He's heart trembled. \"Okay!\"","*","Xuzhou Mansion.","\"The military patrols outside have completely surrounded the Qin Mansion. There will probably be a fierce battle tonight. Oh, there's commotion outside. It seems there aren't many people left from the North in the mansion. Let's see how long they can hold out.\"","\"I guess at most two hours.\"","\"Why bother with them? Before the Lord went to Changle Garden, he said that there would likely be changes tonight, and we just need to watch from the sidelines.\"","\"The Marquis of Wu'an has been majestic for decades, and it's time...\"","Before these words were finished, the noise in the distance was like dead leaves flowing downstream, suddenly pulling closer several times, as if close to the ear.","\"Commander, something bad has happened! A group of military patrols suddenly snuck in near the east gate. They killed several guards in succession and then opened the east gate.\"","A sturdy man stood up in anger and shock. \"Are you sure they are Chang'an military patrols?\"","\"I'm sure. They are indeed wearing the uniforms of the military patrols, and...\" The man gritted his teeth and said, \"The small front courtyard is brightly lit. After they attacked there, subordinates saw someone call a person in the team lieutenant, and the latter clearly had the token of the Northern Army hanging on his waist.\"","The faces of everyone present changed drastically.","You could hear a pin drop in the hall, and even rapid breathing could not be hidden. The sound of weapons outside seemed closer, and the sounds of killing intertwined, forming an unfolding net.","Inside the net were suspicious and uncertain hearts.","Someone softly broke the silence. \"Didn't the Lord say that their target tonight is the North?\"","\"It is true that it was said, but looking at it now, our lord has likely been deceived by those vermin. That fat-bellied Chancellor Dong is probably not content with swallowing just one Tiger of the North; he wants to catch us all in one fell swoop,\" someone sneered coldly.","\"Commander, since they have acted without honor, we need not show them righteousness. We cannot just sit here and wait for death. Our lord is still at the Changle Pavilion waiting for us to rescue him!\"","Commander Lei exhaled two heavy streams of air from his nose. His tiger-like eyes gazed toward the direction of the Xuzhou military camp outside the city, and his voice boomed, \"Follow me, we fight our way out!\"","...","Almost identical scenes were unfolding one after another at the Sizhou and Yuzhou estates.","Similar to the situation at the Xuzhou estate, everyone inside was greatly alarmed. After their initial shock came an unquenchable rage. They slammed the tables and rose to their feet, drawing their blades to fend off the enemies. They fought the so-called Chang'an Patrols until the guards were forced to retreat and eventually driven out of the estate entirely.","But looking around, there were still many patrols on the surrounding streets. Each of them held a long halberd, exuding a murderous aura.","\"That brat Dong Zhou has gone back on his word! He is lower than a beast! Follow me, kill!\"","The area had descended into utter chaos, like a pot of boiling porridge tossed with every kind of mixed grain—the only word for it was pandemonium.","Amidst the surrounding turmoil, Dai Li, having changed into plain clothes, took Shi Rongyue and followed Qiao Wangfei. Taking advantage of the chaotic crowds, they headed together toward the East City Gate.","Coincidentally, they ran into the Qin brothers along the way.","Looking at a scene unfolding not far away, Shi Rongyue subconsciously stopped in her tracks, her lips pressing tightly together without her realizing it.","A few steps away, Nangong Zijin, who was also fleeing, was walking in a hurry and tripped over something on the ground. Seeing this, the young man beside her lent a hand to steady her.","Under the moonlight, the illuminated space between their two figures was reduced to a tiny sliver.","Her personal maid looked at her in confusion, \"My lady?\"","Shi Rongyue raised a hand to press against her chest, murmuring, \"It suddenly feels a little sour here.\"","As if sensing something, the tall and slender young man suddenly looked over. Without a moment's hesitation, he let go of the other girl's arm and started walking toward her.","Shi Rongyue pressed her chest again, a stray tuft of hair on her head perking straight up. \"I think I'm all better now!\""]},{"number":159,"title":"Chapter 159","paragraphs":["Qin Yanzhou approached and first glanced at Dai Li. She was neatly dressed, her clothes undamaged, and it was obvious she wasn't injured. So he shifted his gaze to Shi Rongyue.","The young girl, like Dai Li, wore a black leather armor and a black hooded cloak over it. At this moment, the hood was on her head, and when she slightly lowered her head, the brim cast a dark shadow.","However, compared to Dai Li's neatness, she was much more casual. The hood was crooked. The left brim was flatter than the right, making the slightly upturned right side look like a little horn.","Dai Li was also observing her son, \"Zhou Zhou, did everything go smoothly?\"","\"Everything went smoothly,\" Qin Yanzhou replied, turning his head to look at Shi Rongyue's hood.","He looked once, then looked again.","\"As long as it's smooth, let's leave the city.\" The heavy stone in Dai Li's heart finally fell. She turned and continued walking forward, not seeing the young man behind her raise his hand at that exact moment to slightly lift the left brim of Shi Rongyue's hood.","Left and right were at the same height, finally symmetrical.","From the moment he raised his hand, Shi Rongyue stood frozen in place. Her amber-like brown eyes were as clear as a mirror, clearly reflecting the person in front of her.","First was his hand reaching over, appearing much larger as a result, and then that handsome face, as cold and clear as a high mountain ink painting.","The hood on her head was gently lifted a little. It was clearly a very light movement, but it seemed to bring a gentle spring breeze. Clothes couldn't block the breeze, and it seemed skin couldn't either. It blew through the skin into the bones, making them feel soft and crisp.","\"Little Lady! We're setting off, we need to keep up,\" the maid urged anxiously, while muttering in confusion in her heart why the Little Lady suddenly looked as if she were drunk.","Shi Rongyue responded with an \"Mhm,\" floating forward.","The maid was stunned.","Did she see wrong? The Little Lady's face, facing the moonlight, seemed red.","Even though all families were rushing out of the city at the same time and in the same direction, the journey out of the city was not easy.","For a moment, Dai Li felt like a wildebeest migrating in the African savanna, crossing a wide river full of Nile crocodiles.","Beside her were zebras and gazelles gathered together, trying to band together while keeping their guard up. And the giant crocodiles with sharp teeth attacked from both sides, opening their bloody mouths, dragging the prey away from the herd.","The air was filled with a strong, nauseating smell of blood.","\"Clang—!\"","A deafening sound of a blade beside her brought back Dai Li's wandering thoughts. She subconsciously turned her head and saw Qin Yanzhou standing beside Shi Rongyue, blocking a sneak attack.","The young man who had climbed out of piles of dead bodies did not have the burly physique of a strong man, but he was battle-hardened.","His black eyes were cold and sharp, and the hand holding the knife was as steady as Mount Tai. After intercepting the attack, he pressed the knife forward and then cleanly withdrew. Taking advantage of the opponent's inability to keep up, he swung the long knife horizontally and quickly slashed forward.","The sharp blade that had drunk its fill of blood was first wiped clean of its redness by the fierce wind, and then quickly coated with a dazzling color.","Dai Li quickly lowered her eyes.","No, the opponents were not terrifying Nile crocodiles, and they were not prey without the power to resist in the water.","Dai Li was a distance away from them. After seeing that her son clearly had the upper hand, she looked away.","But Shi Rongyue, who was close at hand, did not. She watched the attacker with spraying blood fall, her face paling a little. However, what occupied her eyes more was the slender figure under the moonlit night.","The young man turned his head to look, his face reflecting the moonlight seemingly softening a bit, \"Don't worry.\"","Shi Rongyue's soul immediately returned, and she nodded heavily: \"Mhm!\"","One side of the hood brim that had just been adjusted a short while ago collapsed again.","Qin Yanzhou took another look, his long fingers holding the knife moving slightly.","...","\"Stop them quickly! Damn it, quickly ride a horse to notify the guards at the East Gate, absolutely do not let them out of the city!\"","The patrol received the order, and just as he was about to ride his horse to detour to the East Gate to pass the order, a long arrow flew out of the dark with a \"whoosh,\" hitting the patrol directly in the back of the heart.","It was unknown whether the person was shot through, but the person fell straight down.","The Northern Army Lieutenant Zhong Zhuo's eyes were splitting, and the increasingly out-of-control situation was like a sharp saw, cutting his nerves again and again.","\"Lieutenant, we can't, we can't stop them!\" The adjutant was full of difficulties.","As the saying goes, an army burning with righteous indignation is bound to win. Tonight, these people knew that only by leaving the city could they survive, so how could they not hold their breath and rush out? Moreover, those who could enter the city with the provincial governors were all carefully selected good seedlings.","Zhong Zhuo grabbed the adjutant's collar, his face ferocious and twisted, \"Even if you can't stop them, you have to! If they leave the city, tomorrow will be the day of your death and mine. Now, immediately, send someone to ride a fast horse to detour to the East City Gate to report!\"","On this night with dim stars, if one looked down at the entire Chang'an City from high up, one could see a fire dragon moving from the south to the east.","The fire dragon was starving, very thin, and even quite short in size. It plunged into the black tide, wandering in the black water, its firelight flickering intermittently. The light was sometimes bright at the dragon's head, sometimes at the dragon's tail.","But no matter what, its goal was clear, and it never stopped.","The fast horse arrived at the East City Gate first. The city gate guards were already very curious about the noise in the city. Now, hearing the reason, their faces all changed drastically.","\"The Lieutenant has ordered, defend the city gate to the death! Men, set up wooden fences, lay out two lines here, one in front and one behind. Shields behind the second obstacle, be sure to build a low wall.\"","\"Where are the bows and arrows? Bring out all the bows and arrows, tonight we must shoot them into sieves...\"","The patrol who rode ahead to arrive at the East City Gate quickly laid out the plan. Although the orders were passed down quickly, the one giving the orders was still uneasy.","For no other reason, the difficulty of opening the gate from different directions was completely incomparable.","If people were outside the city, they could only open the city gate with battering rams or scaling ladders, mostly using flesh and blood as steps to siege the city; but if they were inside the city, the biggest problem disappeared.","\"Speed up, they are almost here.\"","*","Chang'an City, outskirts.","A bright moon hung in the mid-sky, shining its glowing light. The moonlight sprinkled on the roofs of thousands of households, fell on the boundless fields, and also fell on the heavily wooded mountains.","Changle Mountain, named after Changle Garden, was widely bathed in moonlight. The tree canopy was gently blown by the wind, looking like a leisurely old man in the afternoon waving a feather fan out of boredom, but under the tree canopy, it was far from as peaceful as it appeared.","A bloody pursuit began in the mountains. Blades flashed and swords shadowed, murderous intent boiling. Even the birds and beasts in the mountains were silent like cicadas in winter in this majestic sharpness.","After Qin Shaozong and Bai Jianping met up with the others, they rushed straight down the mountain.","\"The Marquis predicted things like a god, there really are many ambushers in this mountain. Heh, fortunately we were prepared early, otherwise tonight we might have lost a layer of skin.\"","\"Look at what you're saying, losing a layer of skin is an exaggeration. In the past, the Marquis was chased alone by the Wu family. He just turned around in the mountain then and killed all the pursuers cleanly. Now the Marquis is not single-handed, what is there to fear?\"","\"If the situation allowed, we could immediately kill our way back.\"","Feng Feng followed behind and to the side of Qin Shaozong. He did not talk and laugh with his comrades. Because he noticed that, apart from giving necessary orders and Governor Nangong taking the initiative to strike up a conversation, the superior hardly spoke.","Occasionally, when a few blind people jumped out to block the way, they were directly shot and killed by the superior drawing an arrow.","One arrow per person, never missing a target.","The force behind each arrow was extremely heavy, capable of flipping a man over. If he had used a heavy bow, it would have surely pierced through and pinned the person to a tree trunk.","The Marquis was in a bad mood.","\"Marquis Wu'an, why are you so irritable?\" Nangong Xiong's state of mind had calmed down significantly. Sooner or later, a choice had to be made, and taking advantage of the current situation wasn't a bad idea.","Fleeing together with Qin Changgeng and looking out for each other made for a much more stable relationship than an ordinary alliance. Hmm, if they could form a marriage alliance later, that would be even better.","Qin Shaozong did not speak, nor did he even look at Nangong Xiong.","Nangong Xiong continued, \"Tonight Dong Zhou set a trap to kill you, so I imagine there will be similar disturbances within Chang'an City. But no matter how bad the situation gets, I don't think your wife and children will be in mortal danger.\"","Qin Shaozong shot him a cold sidelong glance.","Fine fragments of moonlight fell through the gaps in the forest leaves, casting constantly shifting, mottled shadows as they rode without a moment's pause. The man's brown eyes were dark and unreadable, like a snow blade with its sharp edge concealed.","Nangong Xiong immediately said, \"Hey, what's with that look? Am I wrong? In the past, when the Supreme Emperor and the Hegemon-King faced off at Guangwu, the Supreme Emperor's family was captured by the Hegemon-King. The latter placed the Supreme Emperor's father on a chopping block, boiled water in a pot nearby, and declared that if he did not surrender, he would boil the old man alive...\"","Nangong Xiong coughed lightly. \"Regardless of how it ultimately ended, the point is that the old man's life was initially not in danger.\"","Because a living person's value is greater than a dead one's.","As long as Qin Changgeng's wife and children were captured alive, they could be used as bargaining chips for negotiation or even threats, which had many uses.","\"Noisy,\" Qin Shaozong said expressionlessly.","Nangong Xiong's face darkened slightly. \"You really don't know what's good for you. I'm trying to comfort you. My darling daughter is also in Chang'an City. When news comes back tomorrow, who knows, she might be staying in the same room as your wife.\"","Why would they stay together? Naturally, because they were all hostages.","Nangong Xiong continued, \"Liu of Jingzhou has not yet arrived in the capital. I guess that if Dong Zhou captures our families, he will likely use them to command us to deal with Liu Zhan. When the snipe and the clam grapple, the fisherman profits. Prime Minister Dong wants to be the fisherman behind the scenes...\"","Saying this, he suddenly sighed bitterly, \"My darling daughter is as beautiful as a flower. I hope she isn't unlucky enough to run into some idiots who think with their lower halves.\"","\"Whoa.\" The horse was suddenly reined to a halt.","Seeing Qin Shaozong stop, Nangong Xiong called out to him in confusion, only to see the man silently pull the reins, actually looking as if he were about to turn back.","\"Marquis Wu'an, what are you doing?\" Nangong Xiong was greatly alarmed.","He was not the only one shocked; Kuang Ye and the others accompanying them were all horrified.","Having followed his superior for many years, Feng Feng instantly understood that he wanted to execute a sudden counterattack and go back to capture Dong Zhou. He immediately urged, \"My Lord, you must not! Prime Minister Dong has numerous troops, and furthermore, he has the guards of Xu, Yan, and Si provinces. Turning back now is no different from walking right into a trap. The Madam is still waiting for you to rescue her. If you put yourself in danger again, I fear no one will be able to save her.\"","Kuang Ye also hastily said, \"My Lord, Dong Zhou can die, but absolutely not now! If he dies by your hands, on this mountain, it will be very easy for people with ulterior motives to make an issue out of it, which will be greatly detrimental to your reputation.\"","They had been invited to a wine-tasting banquet.","No matter what the reality of this treacherous feast was, in the eyes of the general public, it was the powerful Prime Minister being hospitable, widely inviting the provincial governors, who rarely visited the capital, up the mountain for entertainment.","If the outcome was that the host was killed by a guest, the perpetrator would inevitably bear a bad name.","\"My Lord, the Madam has shown great kindness to Qiao Wangfei; he will definitely protect her.\" Mo Yanyun lacked confidence; as a military general, refusing to surrender made one very likely to be killed. But he still had to advise, \"The most urgent task right now is to hurry back to the military camp, assemble our troops, and then make further plans.\"","Nangong Xiong hissed, drawing in a sharp breath of cold air. Realizing belatedly that he had misspoken, he quickly advised, \"Since the negotiations haven't concluded, they definitely won't touch a single hair on your esteemed wife's head. Don't be anxious.\"","Chang'an East City.","The wooden barricades previously set up at the east city gate had long been turned into powder and sawdust, and corpses lay strewn all over the place. Fresh blood meandered and converged on the bluestone bricks, looking like red snakes mating in the breeding season under the moonlit night.","The city gates were wide open. The corpses hanging upside down from the city walls swayed slightly in the night wind, as if bidding farewell to the travelers who had already galloped far away.","Daili and Shi Rongyue rode on the same horse, galloping toward the Xuanxiao Cavalry camp under the escort of Qiao Wangfei and the others.","They had not brought many military horses into the city, especially since Qin Shaozong had taken a batch away when he went to the banquet yesterday, so there were very few horses left tonight.","Some were their own horses, some were snatched from the city patrols, and others were borrowed from the Xu, Si, and Yan provinces.","They had managed to gather quite a few from outside, but even so, there were not enough horses for everyone to have their own, so two people sharing a horse was a common sight.","The Xuanxiao Cavalry camp was thirty miles outside the city.","Generally speaking, a horse's speed is about forty kilometers per hour. A fine steed can reach fifty or sixty kilometers, or even higher.","And for cavalry, this mere thirty miles could be covered in less than half an hour.","The military camp coiled in the suburbs was like a slumbering behemoth. At the hour of Yin, the giant beast suddenly awakened. It was as if a ladle of hot water had been poured into a pan of hot oil, crackling and exploding all over.","The one left to guard the military camp was the marching instructor, Jin Duole. Hearing the commotion, he got up in the night and rushed out without even having time to put on his outer coat.","Upon seeing Daili, Jin Duole's expression changed drastically. \"Madam, what happened in the city? Why have you returned to the camp in the middle of the night?\"","Daili reined in the horse. Shi Rongyue was sitting in front of her, making it easier for her to dismount from the back, so she got down first. \"There was an incident in the city. The Chang'an patrols tried to enter our residence at night under the pretext of catching thieves. The intruders harbored unpredictable intentions, and the Marquis had gone to the banquet. After thinking it over, I decided it was best to bring our people back first.\"","She said this lightly, but stormy waves surged in Jin Duole's heart.","How could leaving the city at night be easy?","Not to mention that since the other party had a plan, they must have made quite a few preparations...","\"Many soldiers were injured tonight. Arrange for medical treatment first.\" After Daili finished speaking to him, she wanted to help Shi Rongyue, who was still on the horse, get down.","But when she turned her head, she found that the young girl had already dismounted, and Qin Yanzhou, who was holding the reins, was by her side. After dismounting, Shi Rongyue looked at the person in front of her, her large eyes brighter than the moon in the sky.","Daili paused, inexplicably feeling a trace of strangeness, but she was too tired tonight.","First, she hadn't slept soundly, then she was jolted awake halfway through her sleep, then she had to deal with the patrol leader, and finally break out of the city. Her nerves had been taut the whole time, terrified that one wrong step would ruin everything.","Now that she was back at the military camp, Daili, finally relaxing, only wanted to sink into her fluffy quilt and get a good night's sleep.","Daili composed herself and briefly told Jin Duole about the temporary alliance with Qingzhou. Then she tilted her head and looked at Nangong Zijin, whom she had conveniently brought back with her. \"...The young lady of the Nangong family is here as a guest this time. Sir, please do not neglect her.\"","Jin Duole nodded solemnly. \"I will remember.\"","Having instructed everything, the cooks had just finished setting up her small tent. Daili immediately entered the tent, pulled off her cloak, removed her outer garments, threw herself onto the soft couch, and closed her eyes to sleep.","Her sleep had not been particularly restful. Toward the end of it, she seemed to hear cheering, as though someone was being triumphantly welcomed back. The sound was like the rising tide, surging against her eardrums in overlapping waves, yet it remained muffled and indistinct.","Then, in a single moment, like a wave crashing heavily against the rocks, it suddenly swelled over her, wrapping her up so tightly she could barely breathe, binding her, pulling her in.","And in that very instant, all those formless sounds suddenly took on a physical sensation. Accompanied by a rush of hot breath, it landed on the tip of her ear, brushing against her skin again and again, before finally melting into a single murmur:","\"My lady.\""]},{"number":160,"title":"Chapter 160","paragraphs":["At first, Dai Li thought she was dreaming, but the heat and touch on her ear were so real, and the voice that seemed to float across the vast wilderness shed its blurred outer garment.","She finally broke free from her slumber and slowly opened her eyes.","It must be early morning; the rolled window of the small tent was framed with a bright band of light. Occasionally, a breeze brushed by, and the inside of the tent instantly became a bit brighter.","The realization that it was morning flashed by and vanished without a trace. Dai Li looked at the man in front of her, whose palms were pressing and holding her face, and blinked somewhat sluggishly: \"Qin Changgeng, you're back...\"","After running around outside for a long time, Qin Shaozong was covered in dust.","A short, bluish stubble had sprouted on his jaw, and he hadn't yet taken off his weighty black armor. It was clear that he had been awake for a day and a night without rest, but far from being tired, he was quite excited.","This excitement was similar to, yet distinct from, his past victories over enemy forces on the battlefield. It was as passionate as fire, making the blood in his veins howl and boil; it was also as sharp as a halberd or a cavalry lance, invincible, able to reach the deepest part of the heart.","Qin Shaozong was of a burly stature, with broad hands; normally, he could cover her face with just one hand. But now, using both hands, Dai Li's face appeared pitifully small.","His rough, long fingers brushed over the red mole on her forehead, her thick, long eyelashes, her black eyes that looked like ink pearls, her delicate nose, and her rather vibrant red lips.","Every part was exactly as he liked it best.","In his ears, he seemed to hear Qiao Wangfei's excited report again—","He said that at first, the mistress decided to save herself without hesitation, for which she allied with other provinces, truly or falsely, tying several provinces to the same boat, and then using the power of the masses to break out of Chang'an City.","How she dealt with the military patrol leaders, how she tricked them out of the tokens, and how she subsequently commanded the soldiers to charge the city gates...","All were vividly laid out in his subordinate's account.","Qin Shaozong took a deep breath, his emotions remaining the same. His chest felt as if it held a bottomless sea, and on that sea, a beautiful little boat was riding the wind and waves.","The waves were heavy, the difficulties and obstacles were many. Just when he thought the ship was about to be swallowed, she was able to steady herself above the huge waves with a beautiful posture.","He was happy and proud of her, but at the same time, he felt an unspeakable lingering fear. The times were dangerous, and if she wasn't careful, she would be torn to pieces.","Several complex and slightly contradictory emotions blended together, and for a moment, Qin Shaozong felt as if he had been struck by a tiny bolt of lightning. The muscles on his back tightened and shivered, and every hair on his body trembled uncontrollably.","He traced her features with satisfaction, confirming whether she was warm and intact, \"Yes, I'm back.\"","Perhaps it was an illusion caused by the light, but Dai Li felt that the brown eyes of the man in front of her were like a pool of boiling honey gold.","Scorching, impassioned, and at the same time, as thick as ink that couldn't be melted.","Dai Li had just woken up, her thoughts were chaotic. Being looked at by these eyes, she suddenly forgot what she wanted to say.","Seeing her dazed, with the light red flush of sound sleep still on her face, Qin Shaozong's eyes darkened, and he finally couldn't help but lean down and kiss those red lips.","The elite vanguard, still in a state of combat readiness, was excited and brave, easily slaughtering the unequipped troops until they retreated steadily. After breaking the city, the former was still dissatisfied, not only entering the city to plunder wantonly but also setting fires everywhere in the morning when the sunlight was getting stronger.","The large hands that had been holding her soft cheeks moved downwards, as if to check whether she had any wounds, exploring every part with particular care.","From the neck to the chest, then to the waist and abdomen, and even the two arms were not spared. He almost stroked the whole fox from head to toe, and finally had to lift the big tail to take a look.","When he finally confirmed that she was flawless and that she hadn't suffered any hidden losses last night, the last stone in Qin Shaozong's heart fell to the ground.","His enthusiastic and careful inspection made Dai Li tremble uncontrollably. An invisible fire spread everywhere, first rolling back and forth in her lower abdomen and then churning downwards. After burning everything to ashes, an emptiness swept over her like a tide, making her subconsciously clamp her legs together.","A deep laugh came from above, \"Madam worked hard last night, let me comfort Madam.\"","Qin Shaozong quickly took off his belt and black iron, throwing the two heavy objects aside casually, and then was about to roll onto the soft couch.","When he rolled up, Dai Li accidentally touched his elbow. The overly moist sensation made her slightly stunned. Instinctively feeling that something was wrong, she withdrew her hand to look, only to see a smear of dark red on her fingertips.","The remaining traces of sleepiness and everything else flew far away at this moment. Dai Li sat up in astonishment, \"You're injured?\"","The man being questioned didn't care at all, just muttered \"Hmm\" and spat out the ambiguous word \"maybe,\" and then wanted to continue pressing down.","\"Go find Ding Lianxi right away.\" Dai Li forcefully pushed him away and then got off the end of the couch.","\"Madam.\" His voice was hoarse, and he wasn't very willing.","Dai Li didn't look at him, turning her back to him and dressing herself, \"Times are different now, a great battle is imminent, My Lord must take good care of yourself.\"","If this boat in the North capsized, everyone on board, including her and Zhouzhou, Qinian and Rongrong, etc., would not be able to escape.","As soon as the words \"My Lord\" came out, the man frowned, but it quickly relaxed.","Dai Li's belt was draped over her waist, not yet tightened, when two sturdy long arms reached out from her waist, first embracing her and pulling her into his arms.","The height difference between the two was nearly twenty centimeters, and the top of Dai Li's head just reached his jaw.","Qin Shaozong hugged her, rubbing his chin against the top of her head, \"Madam's care is like a spring breeze brushing the face, refreshing the heart and making one linger. I just don't know if this spring breeze will come often in the future?\"","This man's jaw still had stiff stubble. When he rubbed against her, Dai Li always felt like there was a wire brush grinding against her head.","A weird feeling.","Dai Li tried to remove the large hands from her waist, \"I don't know if it will come often, I only know that you should go out.\"","Qin Shaozong loosened his grip slightly following her strength, but didn't completely let go of her. Instead, he took the two loose belts on her waist and, maintaining the posture of embracing her from behind, carefully tied them for her.","When the two came out of the tent, Dai Li looked up at the sun, guessing that it was probably early Chen hour, which is seven o'clock in the morning.","It was still early.","Dai Li and Qin Shaozong went to find Ding Lianxi first. When the latter heard that he was injured, his expression immediately changed, but seeing that Qin Shaozong acted as if nothing had happened, he calmed down a bit.","Qin Shaozong directly took off his outer robe and inner clothes.","The military general, who hadn't slacked off for a day, was covered in muscles. His chest muscles bulged, and the smooth and powerful lines tightened downwards, outlining a strong and vigorous waist. The muscles on his abdomen were distinct. After taking off his clothes, he raised his hand to hang them on the wooden rack. As he stretched his arms, the veins and vessels faintly appeared, and a thick sense of masculine power rushed towards her face.","This was a robust male body at its prime, like a sword that had been tempered for a long time, not comparable to a callow youth.","However, this dark-skinned body was now like a palette. Apart from the old scars, there were also some bruises and three or four knife wounds of varying depths.","Dai Li only gave a rough glance before hurriedly looking away, but the slightly turned-up flesh still lingered in her mind, terrifyingly tight, \"You, didn't you wear black armor?\"","\"I put them on later,\" Qin Shaozong said.","His expression remained normal. He didn't even frown when Ding Lianxi bandaged him, and he even had the leisure to continue talking to Dai Li. \"Madam, I'm afraid your title of Lady will have to be delayed a bit.\"","Dai Li wanted to turn her head, but she forcefully restrained herself. She really couldn't stand the sight of blood, and even felt a little faint from it. \"Delayed? Are you sure it's not canceled?\"","\"What belongs to Madam, no one can take away,\" Qin Shaozong said in a deep voice.","Dai Li's mind raced.","Listening to his words, it meant he still wanted to enter the capital. But since he came back covered in injuries, he must have fallen out with Dong Zhou last night. How could he enter Chang'an after such a fallout?","Could it be...","\"Prime Minister Dong didn't die at your hands yesterday, did he?\" Dai Li asked him.","A cold glint appeared in Qin Shaozong's eyes. \"The timing wasn't right. Let him live a while longer.\"","Dai Li was thoughtful, but after a moment, she couldn't think anymore.","It was now early Chen hour (7-9 AM). She had only arrived at the military camp at Mao hour (5-7 AM) last night. She had only slept for a few hours before getting up, and after the initial rush, a wave of sleepiness overwhelmed her.","Dai Li couldn't help but cover her mouth and yawn.","She didn't look at Qin Shaozong, but the latter's gaze had been on her the whole time. Seeing this, he said to Ding Lianxi, \"Congjian, for such minor scratches, just treat them casually.\"","Ding Lianxi knew that his lord had always lacked patience for medical treatment. The fact that he was still strong today was all thanks to his super-strong physique that far surpassed ordinary people.","In the past, he had advised him again and again, but his lord didn't pay much attention. Now...","Ding Lianxi looked at Dai Li, but his words were addressed to Qin Shaozong: \"My Lord, a gentleman in times of peace does not forget danger, in times of survival does not forget ruin, and in times of order does not forget chaos. Thus, his person is secure and the state can be preserved.\"1","The original meaning of this saying was to be prepared for danger in times of peace, so that both individuals and the governance of the state could be secure. Now Ding Lianxi was using it as a subtle reminder.","Dai Li noticed Ding Lianxi looking at her. Her sluggish brain struggled to turn again, and then she looked at Qin Shaozong, her words laced with the irritability of lack of sleep. \"The gentleman is bandaging you properly. Just sit there and wait for the treatment. Why do you have so much to say? What are you muttering and protesting about?\"","Qin Shaozong: \"...\"","Ding Lianxi coughed lightly, suppressing the smile that was about to spill from his lips.","Since ancient times, there has been the saying of giving a slap and then a sweet date. Now that the mistress's \"slap\" had fallen, it was time for him to offer his earnest \"sweet date.\"","However, someone spoke faster than Ding Lianxi. It was Dai Li, who hadn't finished her words: \"In my hometown, there was a survey. Combining various indicators, under normal circumstances, a man's lifespan is slightly shorter than a woman's.\"","Ding Lianxi gasped inwardly, but Dai Li wasn't finished.","She continued, \"As for those who don't listen to advice, don't listen to reason, and act recklessly relying on their good health, they will leave even earlier when they get old. The Marquis will be busy with myriad affairs every day in the future, and there will be plenty of times for hard work. Don't you think I should plan ahead for myself?\"","Qin Shaozong's face turned completely black, and he scolded sternly, \"Absurd!\"","It wasn't clear whether he was saying the survey results from her hometown were absurd or that Dai Li's plans were absurd.","The man who usually commanded thousands of troops and horses was very authoritative, and this shout made Ding Lianxi tremble violently.","Dai Li remained expressionless and suddenly turned and walked out without a word.","As soon as she left, Qin Shaozong, who had been sitting, instinctively stood up to follow her, but he was still wrapped in unfastened cloth strips, the other end of which was in Ding Lianxi's hands.","\"Ah, My Lord, you can't leave yet!\" Ding Lianxi didn't know whether to hold tight to the cloth strip or let it go. Suddenly, he had a bright idea and said, \"Your wounds haven't been bandaged yet. If you go back now, the mistress might be displeased when she sees it.\"","The man stopped in his tracks, the veins on his forehead throbbing a few times, and finally sat back down. \"Be quick.\"","*","Dai Li returned to the small tent, slowly took off her clothes, and got back into bed. It was summer now, and there was still some residual heat on the soft couch. She pulled a corner of the quilt over her stomach, closed her eyes, and went to sleep.","However, before Dai Li could return to see the Duke of Zhou (fall asleep), the sound of the tent flap rustling came, followed by footsteps.","Dai Li's eyelashes didn't even flutter.","Qin Shaozong looked at her lying straight, like an old monk in meditation, and his footsteps hesitated for a moment.","With her eyes closed, Dai Li heard the sound of clothes rubbing. It seemed he had also taken off his outer garment and hung it on the rack.","A moment later, the outer side of the soft couch sank.","That familiar aura swept over and enveloped her. She fell into a solid, fiery embrace. He kissed her cheek and the tip of her ear again and again, pressing against her temples, rubbing affectionately. \"Madam...\"","Dai Li still didn't open her eyes, only raised her hand to push him. When she couldn't push him, she simply put her hand over her face to fend off the intrusion.","Qin Shaozong's kisses then fell on the back of her hand. As if he couldn't see her block, he continued to kiss a few more times before saying slowly, \"Madam, I didn't mean to blame you just now. I just feel that we still have many decades ahead, so it's hard for me to accept you planning a future without me.\"","This was the truth in his heart, and he felt there was nothing that couldn't be said.","Dai Li kept her eyes closed. \"Be quiet, I'm going to sleep.\"","Instead of being quiet, he chuckled softly and kissed her a few more times affectionately. \"Actually, after calming down just now, I was very happy. Madam's words meant you want to grow old with me.\"","Dai Li: \"...\"","Qin Shaozong smiled and sighed, \"I share the same wish as you, to grow old together with one heart through the cold years.\"","\"It's really impossible to reason with you.\" Dai Li bent her elbow and nudged him, trying to create some distance between them.","Unexpectedly, a muffled groan came from next to her ear. She froze, remembering the knife wound on him, and ultimately didn't give him a second nudge. \"Qin Changgeng, let go of me and sleep on your own side.\"","\"I'm already married, why should I do what lonely people do?\" The curve of Qin Shaozong's lips deepened.","Dai Li scolded him a few more times, but it went in one ear and out the other for him, treating it entirely as a spring breeze brushing past his ear.","Already exhausted, Dai Li grew even more tired. Her voice grew softer and softer, until finally only shallow breathing remained.","Embracing her, Qin Shaozong also closed his eyes. After a day and a night of rushing about, now truly relaxed, he quickly fell into a deep sleep.","A good sleep.","...","When Dai Li opened her eyes again, the light outside the rolled-up window seemed a bit brighter. Very rarely, the man beside her was still there when she woke up.","Qin Shaozong didn't have the habit of taking afternoon naps, and he got up at dawn every day for morning exercises, so Dai Li usually didn't see him.","The burly man slept behind her, his breathing falling rhythmically on the back of her neck like a goose feather brushing past, a bit ticklish. Dai Li tried to get up, but as soon as she moved, Qin Shaozong woke up.","Having slept for less than two shichen (four hours), he was already full of vigor and vitality, the exhaustion in his eyes completely swept away. \"Is Madam hungry?\"","It was about time for lunch now.","Dai Li murmured an \"mm,\" and at this moment vaguely heard someone speaking in a low voice outside:","\"Governor Nangong has come to visit with his subordinates. By rights, we should inform the Marquis...\"","\"But the Marquis only returned at Chen hour. I heard Commander Bai say there were fierce battles last night. The Marquis is probably resting right now.\"","Dai Li turned to look at Qin Shaozong. \"I conveniently brought the Nangong young lady back last night. Her father has come to ask for his daughter now.\"","Qin Shaozong sneered, \"He returned early this morning, yet he only comes to ask for her now. His fatherly love is as thin as paper; he harbors ulterior motives.\"","Dai Li's mouth twitched, but she ignored him.","The two of them walked out of the tent together.","When Dai Li saw Nangong Xiong, he was speaking with Nangong Zijin. The father and daughter wore differing expressions, and Governor Nangong was stroking his chin, seemingly deep in thought.","Seeing Dai Li and Qin Shaozong arriving together, a glint flashed in Nangong Xiong's eyes. He suddenly said, \"Marquis Wu'an, Chancellor Dong unexpectedly struck last night. I had no time to look after the young woman you sent over, the one who claimed to be a concubine from your estate. She is most likely still in the Changle Courtyard. I am truly sorry; I have failed the task you entrusted to me.\"","Qin Shaozong subconsciously glanced at Dai Li."]},{"number":161,"title":"Chapter 161","paragraphs":["Pairs of eyes instantly looked over. Feng Feng and the others' expressions changed again and again, seemingly fearful and surprised, with complex and indescribable emotions.","Dai Li's expression remained the same. Seeing Qin Shaozong looking at her, she even calmly said, \"Why are you looking at me?\"","A very faint tone, indistinguishable from emotions.","Her attitude made Qin Shaozong's eyes darken. \"Madam, I have not given any instructions to Nangong. Bai Jianping and the others can testify. Do not listen to this fellow's nonsense.\"","The named squad leaders echoed repeatedly.","\"Exactly! When the Marquis found out the situation, he drove the person out without stopping for a moment. And we were all present during that questioning, and it ended in less than half a quarter of an hour.\"","\"I was the one who led Concubine Du there at the beginning. Why don't I remember any Marquis's instructions? Could it be that Governor Nangong fled in the mountains in fear all night and messed up his memory?\"","...","Dai Li didn't speak.","Qin Shaozong looked at Nangong Xiong, his gaze sharp and dark, making the other party's back tighten, but the latter had no thought of dodging.","Nangong Xiong was deliberately finding fault.","Last night they said they would retreat together, but in the end, his dear girl was abducted to the Northern army camp. Some words could fool the younger generation, but everyone was a thousand-year-old fox, and they all knew it clearly in their hearts.","This was catching his dear girl as a hostage!","If he were an idler unrelated to this incident, then he would quite appreciate the neat style of this Marquis's wife; unfortunately, he was the father of the \"hostage\", how could he be happy? Ha!","It was only because Qingzhou and the North had formed an alliance now, and they had to act with moderation, so he could only say a few words to make people unhappy.","The echoing voices of the generals gradually weakened, the surroundings quieted down, and the atmosphere solidified and stalemated.","Zhang Mingdian, a Qingzhou strategist who came to the Northern army camp with his lord, saw that the situation was not good and was about to speak out to smooth things over. At this time, a cook came and said that lunch was ready.","Nangong Xiong laughed loudly, as if he had completely forgotten the previous unhappiness. \"Marquis Wu'an, Quanshu and I came in a hurry and haven't had a meal yet. It seems we'll have to eat your meal today.\"","He wasn't asking if he could stay, but directly wanted to stay for dinner.","Qin Shaozong smiled without mirth. \"It's just a lunch, I won't be reluctant.\"","Nangong Xiong's eyelids suddenly twitched wildly, and he felt inexplicably uneasy. But on second thought, he heard that Qin Changgeng was generous. After successively taking over Bing and Ji provinces, he treated the surrendered generals politely and was never stingy with money to his subordinates. Such a person shouldn't mind a few jokes from his allies...","He looked at his strategist Zhang Mingdian, who shook his head imperceptibly.","The worries in his heart could not be told to outsiders. Nangong Xiong looked happy on the surface and sat down with Qin Shaozong.","The wine and food were served, but Nangong Xiong only took a small sip and casually moved a few chopsticks, and then he was so worried that he couldn't swallow. \"Now that we have fallen out with Dong Zhou, the gates of Chang'an City are closed, and we can only attack by force if we want to enter the city. But if we really do that, we will probably bear the name of rebellious subjects and thieves. However, it is not appropriate to stay in the suburbs for a long time. The suburbs are flat and wide, easy to attack but hard to defend, and food is also a big problem.\"","Dong Zhou certainly wouldn't provide food for these uninvited heroes. Everyone ate their own food.","And in marching and fighting, the most taboo thing was the food supply being cut off. As long as the army had no food, the other party could win without a single soldier.","Chang'an was in Yongzhou. Yongzhou connected to Sizhou in the east, Yi and Jing provinces in the south, and the former Northern Kingdom in the north. In terms of geographical location, Qingzhou was the farthest from the base camp.","Nangong Xiong sighed deeply. \"After the Changle Garden incident, Dong Zhou will use the power of Si, Yu, and Xu provinces, and will definitely respond to their requests. Food, Li Lishen and others will certainly not lack. Xie Yuanyue's death will mostly be pushed to you, which is equivalent to having the title of an army of justice. Not good!\"","Qin Shaozong and Dai Li sat at the same table. While his ally was sighing, he held wooden chopsticks, picked up a piece of dried meat and put it into the small bowl in front of Dai Li, composed and calm. \"A blessing in disguise, it's a good thing to break the deadlock early.\"","Nangong Xiong didn't see what was good about it.","\"I have already sent people to occupy Wugang County in the morning, and will strike camp and head north in the afternoon. After that, we will block the soldiers with generals and cover the water with earth.\" Qin Shaozong said lightly.","Wugang County was north of Chang'an, a small county with relatively high terrain. The road leading south to Chang'an was open and flat; but heading north, it directly faced a high peak.","The main road ahead split into two, winding around the mountain one to the east and one to the west.","Zhang Mingdian immediately smiled and chimed in, \"Wugang County is indeed a good place. My lord, why don't we go with Marquis Qin.\"","The strategist offered a step down at the right time, and Nangong Xiong was waiting for this sentence. Wugang County was a good place, and he hadn't not thought about it, just...","A step too late.","When he had settled the army a little and remembered to plan for the future, so he sent a team of people to occupy the \"mountain top\", he was shocked to find that someone had already beaten him to it.","The North entered the city faster than them and closed the city gates. No matter how they shouted and proved their identity under the city, the soldiers on the city tower didn't respond, as if their ears had been bitten off by wolves.","Nangong Xiong laughed heartily again and said it was just right. \"When Li Lishen and the others come to their senses, maybe they will launch a sneak attack to resolve the battle quickly. Marquis Wu'an, how about we go to Wugang together? Two armies merged into one, if we are attacked, we can still counter-encircle.\"","Qin Shaozong made a \"hmm\" sound, not saying yes or no, his attitude vague.","Nangong Xiong's heart skipped a beat, and he simply asked, \"What do you mean by this? Last night Xie Yuanyue died, and Dong Zhou suddenly attacked you. At that time, all arrows were on the string. When you fled into the room and used it as a cover to escape, I didn't hesitate at all and chased after you. Now I just want to borrow Wugang County, which you occupied first, is this not allowed?\"","Actually, there was hesitation, but the hesitation time was extremely short, and Nangong Xiong automatically ignored it.","Since Qin Shaozong returned, Dai Li hadn't had time to ask about last night. Now Nangong Xiong was talking about last night in a few words. Although she didn't experience it personally, she also felt it was quite dangerous.","No wonder he brought back a few knife wounds.","Dai Li looked at the man beside her, but the latter lightly tapped the small bowl with meat in front of her with wooden chopsticks, motioning her to finish eating.","\"Wugang can let you in, but I have a condition.\" Qin Shaozong was still unhurried.","\"You say.\"","Qin Shaozong said in a deep voice, \"As long as your Qingzhou is still allied with my North for one day, how the subsequent battles are fought and how the army moves must be under my command.\"","Nangong Xiong and Zhang Mingdian's expressions changed slightly.","The other party wanted to separate the primary and secondary.","Qin Shaozong no longer looked at them, and poured wine for himself. \"I only have this one condition, nothing else. This matter stresses mutual willingness. Nangong, you can consider it more. I will strike camp at the beginning of the Wei hour.\"","Nangong Xiong sneered in his heart.","It sounded nice to say \"only\" strike camp at the beginning of the Wei hour, but it was already noon, and there was less than an hour left before the beginning of the Wei hour.","...","The space in the main tent was limited. After the Northern generals sat down, the Qingzhou people were added, and there was not enough space. Qin Shaozong simply let the younger generation go to the next tent to eat.","After the meal, Nangong Xiong lifted the curtain and went out of the tent, and saw his daughter waiting outside the tent who had finished eating a step earlier.","Nangong Zijin saw her father's displeased expression and asked in a low voice, \"Father, did my coming here last night cause trouble for you?\"","Last night, Chang'an City was in utter chaos, with every faction rushing to break through the gates. It was chaotic before leaving the city, and not much better afterwards. The relentless pursuit by the Chang'an military patrols was one thing, but the dark, windy night also emboldened those with malicious intent to fish in troubled waters.","Nangong Zijin, who had been traveling with the Northern troops from the beginning, only belatedly realized after traveling a distance from the city that she was completely surrounded by Northern soldiers. The forces from Qingzhou had either been deliberately separated or had gotten lost, leaving only a handful of men behind.","Nangong Xiong's expression softened. He told her it had nothing to do with her and that he was merely worried about the future political situation.","As the father and daughter walked out of the Northern military camp together, Nangong Xiong changed the subject and asked, \"My dear girl, you have already met the two sons of the Marquis of Wu'an. What do you think of them?\"","Nangong Zijin was slightly taken aback. \"The second young master has a cool temperament and acts steadily. As for the third young master...\"","She visibly paused. Even though that person was not by her side, she felt as if she could still hear his incessant, tide-like chatter.","Time seemed to instantly pull back to last night.","Amidst the flickering torches and the flashing of swords and shadows, the youth dressed in a black and red martial outfit looked her up and down.","\"This outfit of yours won't do at all. You're dressed like a golden pheasant. The moment you step out, you'll draw everyone's attention. Who would even look at anyone else? Wouldn't you just become a walking target?\"","\"You also need to smear some ash on your face. Here, just rub some of that charcoal on. It would be best if even Governor Nangong couldn't recognize you. That's the only way to be safe.\"","...","A long arrow flew straight toward her, only to be deflected away by him with a sharp clang.","Still reeling from the shock, a trace of gratitude had just begun to sprout in her heart when she saw the youth turn around. He glanced at her a couple of times and muttered, \"You're already as gray and drab as a little sparrow, yet someone still shot an arrow at you. It seems your luck today is quite terrible, Nangong Xiaoliu.\"","Her gratitude vanished into thin air, instantly replaced by a surge of anger that rushed to her head, making her ears ring.","As the legitimate daughter of a provincial governor, Nangong Zijin had always maintained her dignity and prided herself on her composure, but at that moment, she truly could not hold back.","She could not help but step forward and stomp viciously on his foot. As the youth let out a surprised howl, she fiercely rewarded him with a \"Shut up.\"","\"My dear girl?\"","Nangong Zijin snapped back to reality. Meeting her father's probing gaze, she turned her head away. \"This Qin San is incredibly annoying!\"","Nangong Xiong raised his thick eyebrows. \"How is he annoying?\"","But Nangong Zijin said no more.","Qin Shaozong's declaration to break camp at the beginning of the Wei hour was not just to fool Nangong Xiong. After their meal, the military generals swiftly exited the main tent to take charge of their respective areas.","Daili also left the tent, walking slowly to digest her food. However, after walking for a while, she noticed soldiers constantly casting reverent glances behind her. She turned around to look and, sure enough, Qin Shaozong was following her.","Seeing that he had been exposed, the man simply quickened his pace to walk side by side with her. \"Madam...\"","\"Is there something you need?\" Daili maintained her indifferent expression.","Qin Shaozong coughed lightly. \"Forced by the current situation, Nangong will likely lower himself to secure a place in Wugang City. But this man is full of lies and is by no means a good person. You should not get too close to him, Madam.\"","\"Qin Changgeng, if that matter of yours hadn't been exposed by Governor Nangong, would you have told me?\" Daili asked suddenly.","\"Of course I...\"","\"Tell the truth.\"","Qin Shaozong paused. Looking into those eyes that resembled ink-wash pearls, he suddenly let out a soft chuckle. The arrogant streak he had just suppressed flared up again. \"No. Just an irrelevant person, why should they consume your thoughts, Madam? It's just like if I went out and met some unremarkable old oil peddler or a mediocre butcher's daughter. I wouldn't mention them to you when I got back either, because there's nothing worth saying.\"","With soldiers coming and going around them, Qin Shaozong refrained from any intimate gestures like putting his arm around her shoulders or waist, but his brown eyes seemed to hold a fire capable of completely enveloping a person.","Daili averted her gaze from his.","...","The dense cluster of tents was quickly dismantled. Horses neighed as the entire army marched north.","This place was not far from Wugang County. Daili and her party arrived at the small county town before sunset. Swift scouts had already relayed the message ahead of time, so unlike before, the city gates were wide open to welcome the Northern army inside.","Just as Daili entered the city on this side, the rumbling of hooves echoed from the other. Billowing dust rose in the distance, and the military banner bearing the character for Qing fluttered in the wind.","Qin Shaozong stood on the city tower, gazing out at the galloping Qingzhou army against the backdrop of the setting sun. His eyesight was excellent, and among the crowd, he spotted Nangong Xiong wearing golden armor.","When the opposing forces reached the base of the city walls, Qin Shaozong rested his hands on the solid, uneven battlements. Leaning forward slightly, he looked down at Nangong Xiong, who had arrived before the tightly shut city gates, and smiled. \"Governor Nangong, I trust you have been well since we last met.\"","They had been separated for less than half a day, yet the other man spoke as if they hadn't seen each other in half a lifetime. Furthermore, he made no move to open the gates, causing the veins on Nangong Xiong's forehead to throb.","This scoundrel was doing it on purpose. He was waiting for him to speak first!","\"I agree to what you proposed earlier,\" Nangong Xiong gritted his teeth.","It wasn't that he lacked backbone, but the current situation left him no choice. Now that Dong Zhou and the three provinces had banded together, if he distanced himself too much from the Northern forces, there was no guarantee the enemy wouldn't adopt a strategy to defeat them one by one.","In terms of foundation and resources, he was weaker than Qin Changgeng.","Qin Shaozong raised his voice, \"Are you saying that you, Nangong Xiong, agree to follow my orders throughout this entire journey south?\"","As a military general, his voice was booming, and Qin Shaozong's shout carried far into the distance.","Nangong Xiong nearly choked on a mouthful of blood, highly suspecting that this man surnamed Qin was retaliating against him for exposing the matter with the dancer.","Seeing that he was on the verge of flying into a rage, Zhang Mingdian hurriedly advised, \"My Lord, a great man must act like a dragon or a snake, able to bend and stretch. In the past, the Marquis of Huaiyin could endure the humiliation of crawling between another's legs. What harm is there in us enduring this for a moment?\"","Nangong Xiong took a deep breath. \"Quanshu is right. I will endure him for now.\" He then raised his voice in return and said, \"A promise is not lightly made. Since I agreed earlier, I absolutely have no intention of breaking it. You can rest assured, Marquis Wu'an.\"","With those few short words, he barely managed to claw back a fraction of his dignity in the exchange.","Having achieved his goal, Qin Shaozong didn't mind his attempt to save face. \"Open the gates!\"","The heavy city gates slowly opened.","...","Sun Tzu's Art of War states: In war, victory is prized, not prolonged campaigns.","Thus, much as Qin Shaozong had anticipated, on his second day in Wugang, a manifesto issued by Chancellor Dong Zhou was proclaimed to the world:","We observe Qin Changgeng; originally a Marquis guarding the borders of Yuyang, yet his nature is cruel and he forsakes righteousness for profit. Rather than seeking to serve the state, he harbors the vicious heart of an owl or a beast. This man has committed grave injustices, brutally murdering Xie Yuanyue, the Governor of Sizhou. Bereft of all benevolence and righteousness, he is intolerable to Heaven and Earth.","...His actions are despicable, and his crimes warrant death. We hope the heroes of the four seas will jointly raise the banner of righteousness to eradicate this treacherous villain and restore order to the universe!"]},{"number":162,"title":"Chapter 162","paragraphs":["\"The villain complains first, this is outrageous!\"","\"With the manifesto already started, there will definitely be a battle within seven days.\"","\"As expected.\" The one speaking was Cui Shengping, who had just rushed to Wugang County not long ago.","When Dai Li and Qin Shaozong went south, they initially did not bring a group of advisors. Entering the capital was to receive titles, bringing military generals could be justified as escort, but bringing advisors would be unjustifiable.","Moreover, the promotion of fertilizer was listed as the top priority this year, so Qin Shaozong simply left all the advisors in Yuyang, and he leisurely went south with Dai Li, inspecting Jizhou, Yanzhou and other places successively, and finally slowly went to the capital.","As for the several advisors, after the matters on hand temporarily came to an end, they all had their own places to go.","Nalan Zhi and Cui Shengping rode fast horses south, and happened to join the lord on the second day after the manifesto was issued.","In the tent, there were not only people from the North, but also people from Qingzhou. Nangong Xiong looked at the spread sheepskin map with a solemn face.","If Wugang was the center, to the southeast was Chang'an City, to the north was Xiongfeng; to the west was the Loess Plateau, while the east was somewhat flatter, and not far away was a small county called Liuzhangping.","If they wanted to encircle and suppress the allied forces of the North and Qingzhou, they could dispatch troops from Chang'an and Liuzhangping in the east at the same time. Once Wugang fell, the allied forces could only flee north. If they set up an ambush on the paths on both sides of Xiongfeng, it would be like catching turtles in a jar.","\"I personally think that how to face the battle is not the point now, the point is that manifesto.\" Zhang Mingdian said.","Nalan Zhi and Cui Shengping both nodded.","Nalan Zhi said sternly: \"The highest is to establish virtue, the second is to establish merit, and the third is to establish words. Although it takes a long time, it will not be abolished, this is called immortality. If we wait for the people of the world to believe the false words, thinking that you, my lord, are lacking in virtue, and deeply rooted in this, it will take hundreds and thousands of times the effort to make them change their views.\"","This meant that the battle still had to be fought, but before that, the manifesto needed to be properly handled, and the weight of the manifesto was even above the war.","Qin Shaozong asked: \"Then according to Wugong's opinion, how should we deal with this manifesto?\"","Everyone looked at Nalan Zhi, including Qin Yanzhou and Qin Qinian who were summoned into the room to listen.","Nalan Zhi smiled and stroked his long beard. He did not answer directly, but first kept them in suspense, \"Everyone might as well think about it. If you unfortunately encounter a gang fight alone, under the premise that you cannot escape, how should you stop this fight?\"","Qin Qinian clenched his fist, and his knuckles cracked softly. He thought to himself, isn't this simple? Subdue them all, and this fight will naturally stop.","As a result, just as he was about to open his mouth, he saw that his teacher Cui Shengping seemed to have guessed what he wanted to say, and shook his head at him.","Qin Qinian got stuck.","Qin Shaozong turned his jade thumb ring, raised his eyebrows with a bit of a smile.","Nangong Xiong pondered slightly, and suddenly became cheerful, \"Very good! A manifesto is nothing, who can't write it? Yuzhou's strength is inferior to Xuzhou, taking Jiang Yuzhou as the first target is the most suitable.\"","Qin Qinian listened to them, first frowned into a ball, and then suddenly realized.","It was him who previously judged others by himself, taking it too much for granted. Not everyone practiced martial arts since childhood like him, nor was everyone born with greater strength than others like him.","So when ordinary people are beaten by a group, if they want to get out of trouble, apart from holding their heads and letting the other party beat them up, the only way is——","Pick the weakest one on the opposite side to beat!","Beat hard, only beat that one. After dealing with the weakest one, then pretend to look at the second to last.","Similarly, in this multi-party encirclement and suppression, if you want to pick, pick the one with the weakest strength to attack.","That is, Jiang Shi, the governor of Yuzhou.","*","\"Madam.\" Qin Shaozong pushed the door and came in.","Dai Li didn't participate in the meeting just now, she was looking at data in another room. Nalan Zhi and Cui Shengping not only came, but also brought a batch of fertilizer materials.","The batch of fertilizer bags in the winter of last year had all been distributed to the fields. And which family had how much land, how many stones they got; how the crops with fertilizer grew, and how the ones without fertilizer grew, as well as the subsequent production of fertilizer, etc., all had records.","Hearing him come back now, Dai Li didn't even lift her head, \"You finished the meeting so quickly? It seems you have a countermeasure.\"","Qin Shaozong sat down beside her. Seeing Dai Li didn't look up, he didn't take the other books on the table, but insisted on snatching the one she was looking at, \"Well, indeed there is a countermeasure.\"","With empty hands, Dai Li had to turn her head to look at him, \"There are so many on the table you don't want, why do you insist on taking mine?\"","This person came out of the council hall, hid the majesty in front of outsiders, and added some lazy frivolity, \"Madam's is good-looking.\"","Dai Li originally wanted to take another book, but felt uncomfortable not finishing reading half of it, and felt why she should give it to him, so she simply snatched the book back from his hand, \"What countermeasure?\"","Qin Shaozong: \"Issue a manifesto claiming that the murderer of Xie Sizhou is someone else, the real culprit Jiang Yuzhou harbors evil intentions, deceives the monarch and ministers, and we swear to die to clear the monarch's side.\"","Dai Li smiled: \"So cunning.\"","Just as the words fell, she was scooped over by Qin Shaozong, \"There is a more cruel one, does madam want to experience it?\"","\"In broad daylight, behave yourself.\"","\"There is only you and me in the room, as long as madam doesn't say, who can know?\"","*","\"...The current emperor is young, Prime Minister Dong Zhou is simple and dull, the treacherous minister Jiang Shi uses His Majesty's authority to act unlawfully, his crimes are obvious, too numerous to record:","First, deceiving the Holy listening, murdering dukes and important ministers. Causing the loyal and good to retreat, villains to run rampant, the court is full of smoke and miasma, dark and gloomy.","Second, harboring evil intentions, confusing the public with demonic words. This person has designed so-called earth dragons turning over several times to justify himself and build momentum, causing houses to collapse and people to panic.","Third, murdering officials, planting evidence to frame others. Jiang murdered Xie Yuanyue, the governor of Sizhou, and framed his colleagues, which is treachery and deviation from the norm.","...","There are no upright ministers in the court, and there are traitors and evils inside. How can such national thieves and enemies of the people occupy a high position for a long time? Today I raise troops to punish the treacherous and evil, the blade is pointed only at the chief culprit, not daring to offend the palace...\"","\"Absolutely absurd!!\"","The desk was slapped with a \"bang\", the things on the desk jumped hard, Dong Zhou breathed heavily and stared at the mulberry paper in front of him.","Prime Minister Dong Zhou is simple and dull? Damn it, this is attacking Jiang Shi while not forgetting to scold him.","Li Lishen didn't speak, his eyes were obscure.","And Jiang Shi beside him was as dark as ink, also silent, but his whole person didn't know whether it was anger or something else, actually trembling a little.","No wonder Jiang Shi looked bad, this manifesto pointed directly at him.","To put it unpleasantly, if Dong Zhou's side lost in the end, then as long as his, Jiang's, head was offered, the \"treacherous sycophant\" would be eliminated, and everything could return to peace.","To him, Prime Minister Dong, what he lost was just an ally who might rebel in the future.","No, not even an ally, but a chess piece.","Taking the expressions of Jiang and Li into his eyes, Dong Zhou's heart skipped a beat, and hurriedly said: \"What a poisonous stratagem of sowing discord, this manifesto is extremely sinister! But please rest assured, you two, I, Dong Zhou, am absolutely not that insidious person like Qin Changgeng, and the North and Qingzhou have now formed an alliance. If I cut off my own hands and feet, it would be tantamount to playing with fire and burning myself, I still understand the principle that if the lips are gone, the teeth will be cold.\"","Hearing this, Jiang and Li's expressions softened slightly.","\"According to what the Prime Minister said, what should we do now?\" Jiang Shi asked.","\"The call to arms has been issued, so naturally we must press on and attack the rebels in one vigorous stroke.\" But Dong Zhou was merely a minister who manipulated power; he knew nothing of leading troops in battle. Therefore, he turned to Qiu Tong, the General of the Flying Cavalry beside him, and asked, \"General Qiu, what is your brilliant opinion on our crusade against the Qin rebels?\"","Qiu Tong was tall and robust, but his position as General of the Flying Cavalry was not earned through his own blood and sweat. Rather, he had ridden the coattails of his ancestors, walking the path they had paved for him and constantly claiming the military merits of others to reach his current status.","Qiu Tong's eyes flickered slightly. \"This matter is of great importance. It would be far too reckless for me to make a decision alone. Men, please invite Libationer Zheng and Libationer Wu in.\"","Zheng Yizhi and Wu Shuda were both military libationers. They hailed from prominent families in Chang'an, but as middling sons within their clans, they had been stuffed into these idle positions.","Of course, \"idle positions\" only applied during times of peace. Now, military libationers were figures of crucial importance.","At this moment, Wu Shuda's heart was pounding wildly, and a thin layer of sweat broke out on his back. He knew very well that this battle was no trifling matter. If a strategic error led to defeat, it was entirely possible that Prime Minister Dong would push the \"instigator\" out to be executed as a sacrifice to the battle flag.","Wu Shuda stole a glance at Zheng Yizhi, only to be shocked by how composed the other man appeared, seemingly having a well-thought-out plan in mind.","Zheng Yizhi actually smiled. \"Prime Minister Dong, General Qiu, the enemy's call to arms is employing a strategy to sow discord among us. Since that is the case, why don't we beat them at their own game?\"","The expressions of the men in the room varied.","Zheng Yizhi's finger first pointed to Chang'an City, then moved east. \"We can leak word that you, Prime Minister Dong, had a fierce argument with Governor Li of Xuzhou, and that Governor Li has led his troops east, leaving Chang'an. When the Marquis of Wu'an hears this news, he will definitely send scouts to investigate the truth. We don't need to bother with the scouts, let alone kill them. Just let them follow...\"","His finger circled a small county on the east side of Liuzhangping. \"Jiangkou. After passing this small town of Jiangkou, just as we are about to reach Luoyang, we will pull out the vast majority of our forces to travel light over the Zhongtiao Mountains, taking a shortcut to sneak up behind Wugang. As for the small portion of troops left near Jiangkou, they will cook meals according to the daily numbers of the main army to confuse the enemy scouts. We absolutely must not let the enemy realize what is happening.\"","\"At the same time, we will send the Sizhou army to blatantly circle behind Wugang and choke off the main roads on both sides of the majestic peaks north of Wugang. This will form a pincer movement, and the enemy's attention on the Xuzhou troops will be greatly reduced...\"","\"...Once Wugang is breached, as long as we capture Lady Dai and her son alive, the Marquis of Wu'an will surely be thrown into utter chaos.\"","...","It was not until the sun set in the west that the doors to the room finally reopened.","Dong Zhou's face was beaming with a wide smile. His large, fan-like hands repeatedly patted Zheng Yizhi on the shoulder. \"Libationer Zheng is truly a son of the Zheng family. You possess heaven-spanning talents and strategies that are nothing short of miraculous. You are far superior to Minister Zheng.\"","The advisors from Xuzhou and Yuzhou also chimed in, \"Brother Zheng has the talent to assist a king. It is a pity that you had nowhere to showcase it before, which is why you were buried in obscurity until now.\"","Zheng Yizhi felt as if he were floating on air from all the flattery.","However, this elated Libationer Zheng did not immediately return to his manor after leaving the military headquarters. Instead, he went to a small residence within Chang'an City.","Unlike the casual nature of their previous chance encounter as kindred spirits, this time Zheng Yizhi came bearing heavy gifts.","Upon seeing the handsome young man dressed in white, Zheng Yizhi was so polite that he almost seemed sycophantic. He ignored the age difference between them, repeatedly calling him virtuous younger brother. Only after a great deal of preamble did he relay word for word what had been said in the council room today.","\"...Virtuous younger brother, I never imagined that the joking words you casually spoke back then would give your foolish older brother such tremendous help, saving me from a crisis. The first hurdle has been passed, but what should be done next?\" Zheng Yizhi asked eagerly.","Diting smiled and said, \"Do not be anxious, virtuous older brother. The tides of war are ever-changing and cannot be generalized. Let us wait and see what happens next.\"","Wugang County.","\"My Lord, the enemy has made a move,\" Feng Feng reported. \"According to our scouts, it seems Governor Li of Xuzhou had a dispute with Prime Minister Dong. Governor Li has led his army out of Chang'an City and is heading east. It looks as though he is returning to Xuzhou.\"","\"Could it be that the call to arms worked, making Li Lishen realize that Dong Zhou is untrustworthy, so he changed his mind and no longer wants to wade into these muddy waters?\"","\"Dong Zhou has always been a treacherous rat who hides a knife behind his smile and acts with venom. Back then, he was willing to sacrifice Governor Xie of Sizhou just to frame you, My Lord. Now, he might very well sacrifice Li Lishen. It is not surprising that Governor Li of Xuzhou refuses to become the second Xie Yuanyue.\"","\"It is still too early to draw conclusions. We need to send scouts to investigate the exact situation.\"","Everyone talked over one another, but in the end, they all agreed on sending scouts to verify the truth.","Qin Shaozong nodded. \"Then let us send the swift scouts first. Kuang Ye, you...\"","Before he could finish his sentence, a tall, slender figure stepped forward. The man cupped his hands and requested, \"Father, your son asks to lead a team of scouts to investigate the truth.\"","The surroundings fell silent, and the rest of Qin Shaozong's unfinished sentence faded away.","Qin Yanzhou raised his eyes at this moment. His dark eyes were like a lake after the first melting of winter snow, shimmering with rippling light. \"I ask for Father's permission.\"","Qin Shaozong did not answer immediately. He simply looked at Qin Yanzhou, whose gaze did not waver in the slightest.","In that single exchange of glances, many messages were silently communicated, along with many instructions that were difficult to speak aloud at this moment.","After a moment, Qin Shaozong took a deep breath. \"Granted.\"","\"Thank you, Father.\"","This matter brooked no delay. After receiving his orders, Qin Yanzhou did not participate in the rest of the meeting and immediately strode out the door.","Qin Qinian watched his older brother leave, itching to follow along and act as a scout as well. However, bringing it up now would make him seem immature, so he remained silent.","After the meeting adjourned and he had eaten his meal, Qin Shaozong paced outside for several rounds, simply unable to bring himself to return to his room.","Bai Jianping was on guard duty tonight. When he saw Qin Shaozong walk past for the third time, he finally could not help but step forward. \"My Lord, do you have any orders?\"","Qin Shaozong waved his hand. \"None. Go back to your duties.\"","Bai Jianping did not leave. Seeing a look of worry between his superior's brows, he assumed the man was concerned about the upcoming battle, so he said, \"My Lord, your subordinate believes that no matter how difficult this battle may be, it cannot be harder than when we fought the Wuhuan in the northern lands. Why must you worry so much?\"","Back then, they had no grain when they needed it, their numbers were few, and their horses were not as sturdy as those of the Wuhuan, yet didn't they still conquer the northern kingdom?","Qin Shaozong could not be bothered to explain it to him. He touched the small pouch in his robes and returned to his room without a word.","Bai Jianping stood frozen in place, faintly seeming to understand something.","...","\"Creak.\" The door was pushed open.","Dai Li, who was not yet asleep, looked over at the sound. \"Qin Changgeng, have you seen Zhou Zhou? Why didn't I see him at dinner tonight?\""]},{"number":163,"title":"Chapter 163","paragraphs":["Qin Shaozong closed the door as if nothing had happened, saying, \"Qin the Second has been sent out by me to scout the way.\"","Dai Li thought of the rear.","Qin Changgeng's supply line came from the north, which meant it had to pass through the main road beside the northern peaks. The supply route was especially crucial; once intercepted, there was a risk of falling into a desperate situation. Therefore, when the war started, it was unavoidable to send scattered troops back and forth to clear the way and ensure there were no ambushers around the supply route.","Dai Li naturally assumed her son had gone to the rear. She knew this task was relatively safe, but she still asked one more question, \"How many people went with him?\"","Qin Shaozong replied, \"Twenty men.\"","After speaking, the man took the book from Dai Li's hands. \"Madam, there is no need to worry. Qin the Second has learned his martial arts well, and nothing will happen on this trip. It is getting late, we should rest early.\"","The curtains beside the bed were lowered, and soon, the lights in the room were extinguished.","With the lights out, Dai Li felt no sleepiness. She was well aware of why. Unlike the bandit suppression at Chunmiao Mountain, and unlike the previous late-night departure from the city, this time Zhou Zhou was very likely the leader.","He did not need to listen to others' orders; he led the team himself and made his own decisions. Correspondingly, he had to bear all the responsibilities himself, with no one else to rely on.","\"About when will Zhou Zhou be able to return?\" Dai Li asked.","Qin Shaozong only said a few days, without giving a specific timeframe.","Dai Li wanted to ask more, but the man beside her seemed to know what she wanted to say. He simply rolled over and pressed down on her, then lowered his head, his voice becoming much more muffled. \"The war will start in a few days. During wartime, military orders are like mountains. I am afraid I will not be able to comfort you then, Madam, so it is better to fill the gap now.\"","A section of moonlight was drawn into the room through an open window. In the dimly lit room, a thin shirt could be faintly seen slipping off her shoulders. Below the young woman's fair neck was snow-white skin as bright as the bright moon and rising round hills.","The intimate affair was hearty and dripping with sweat, but this time, when she returned to her pillow, Dai Li did not fall asleep as quickly as usual.","A faint sense of anxiety lingered around her.","And that seed named unease, which had been planted long ago, grew longer roots on this night.","At the same time.","In the pitch-black night, a group of men and horses coming from the direction of Wugang quietly sneaked to the west side of Liuzhangping County.","Qin Yanzhou looked into the distance and saw that the western suburbs of Liuzhangping were empty, with no troops stationed there.","A trace of doubt flashed through the young man's eyes.","\"Commandant, the Xuzhou army is not in the western suburbs. Could they be in the eastern suburbs?\" Xun He, who was in the same team, whispered.","Qin Yanzhou, who had been temporarily appointed as Commandant, said, \"Let's go to the eastern suburbs and take a look.\"","The group sneaked to the eastern suburbs and indeed saw a continuous stretch of military tents set up there. Fire basins were placed in the camp for illumination, spaced orderly, reflecting the entire military camp in the night like a colorful tiger resting in a coiled position.","Xun He said in surprise, \"They are actually here. I didn't expect Governor Li of Xuzhou to really withdraw his troops. He is actually willing to pack up and go home just like that.\"","Although there was only a one-word difference between the eastern suburbs and the western suburbs, the actual locations were very different.","Liuzhangping was originally on the east side of Wugang County. If the military camp was pitched in the western suburbs, they could quickly march to respond as soon as the war started. However, pitching the camp in the eastern suburbs, which was farther from the battlefield but closer to Xuzhou, looked like they really wanted to go home.","Qin Yanzhou fell silent for a moment, then shook his head. \"It's too early to draw a conclusion now. Let's keep watching.\"","The round moon in the sky gradually sank to the west, and before they knew it, a night had passed.","After dawn, the Xuzhou military camp was like a giant beast waking up from a deep sleep. After getting up and shaking its fur, it dragged its food reserves and continued eastward.","Whether it was because they carried too much grain or for some other reason, the Xuzhou army, which consisted of more than half infantry, did not march fast. It was not until sunset on the second day that they barely reached the small county town of Jiangkou on the east side of Liuzhangping.","This time, they also came to the eastern suburbs of Jiangkou County and set up camp there.","The terrain of the eastern suburbs of Jiangkou was relatively high, which could be described as a small low hill. With the military camp pitched on high ground, it was not as easy to spy on as Liuzhangping. Moreover, the other side had sent out scouts several times along the way. To be on the safe side, Qin Yanzhou did not follow too closely.","Another night passed in the blink of an eye.","When the golden sun rose again, the distant behemoth reorganized its troops and set off once more, still continuing its eastward march.","Viewed from a distance, the rolling dust and magnificent momentum completely indicated a large army on the move.","Qin Yanzhou waited for them to walk a long distance before leading his men to the area where the Xuzhou army had previously camped. The method of cooking meals during a march had always been to bury pots and make food, which meant digging a pit in the ground as a temporary stove and then placing a pot in it.","Qin Yanzhou looked at the pits all over the ground and said, \"Count them.\"","After dividing the areas, the group quickly counted them.","After dawn, the gates of Jiangkou City welcomed those coming and going, and merchant caravans continued to pass through. Qin Yanzhou heard the merchants passing by not far away discussing:","\"I heard that fighting has broken out in Wugang. Fortunately, we heard the rumors yesterday and didn't go to Wugang, otherwise losing our goods would be a small matter, but losing our lives would be a big deal.\"","\"Brother Gao is right. Sigh, who knows when the war will end? By the way, both the one in Chang'an and the one in the north have issued proclamations. Who do you believe?\"","\"Probably the one in the north. For the past few decades, our Great Yan has been guarded by the Qin family on the borders. That person even beat the foreign tribes into submission. It's much better than the one in Chang'an who only indulges his relatives in extorting money everywhere.\"","\"True, I heard from a distant cousin of mine in the north that the Marquis and his wife seem to be tinkering with something that can increase grain production. Regardless of whether it's true or false, having this heart to benefit the people is always good.\"","\"But let's hope the war ends quickly. To be honest, as long as it allows us to live a good life, it doesn't matter who sits on that throne above.\"","\"Shh, do you have a death wish? Is that something you can say casually?\"","Qin Yanzhou listened to the drifting discussions and watched the merchant caravan go far away. At this time, the soldiers who went to count the pot pits also returned, and everyone combined the numbers of their respective pits.","\"The number of these pot pits matches the initial number of the Xuzhou army. It seems that the proclamation issued by the Marquis has worked, completely causing their already unstable alliance to fall apart,\" Xun He said excitedly.","A scout smiled and said, \"Without Governor Li of Xuzhou, that treacherous prime minister is like having lost an arm. Governor Xie of Sizhou is dead, and changing commanders right before a battle is not secure, so the Sizhou army is far worse than before. In this way, there is only one Yuzhou army left, along with those useless drunkards from the Chang'an military patrols. What is there to fear in this battle?\"","The others smiled and agreed.","Xun He asked Qin Yanzhou, \"Commandant, I just heard that the war has already started in Wugang. It must be that the Marquis has taken action. If the Xuzhou army continues to march east, it means they are completely withdrawing from the battlefield. When should we go back and inform the Marquis of this matter?\"","Everyone looked at Qin Yanzhou, while the young man looked in the direction the Xuzhou army was leaving.","After a moment, he shook his head. \"It's too early to draw a conclusion now. Keep following.\"","The others looked at each other in dismay.","Xun He originally wanted to suggest sending a few people back to deliver a message to Qin Shaozong first. However, seeing Qin Yanzhou's resolute expression and remembering that the other party had saved his life during the bandit suppression at Chunmiao Mountain, he ultimately did not become the first to jump out and sing a different tune after this Qin Second Young Master was parachuted in as Commandant.","Qin Yanzhou led his men and continued to trail behind the Xuzhou army.","Continuing east from Jiangkou, they could not reach the next town within a day, so tonight the Xuzhou army camped in the wilderness.","The canopy of the sky spread out in pitch black, and the summer cicadas chirped incessantly, making people feel annoyed and restless.","Unlike Jiangkou County, which was situated on a low hill and thus had higher surrounding terrain, the Xuzhou army's campsite today was merely near water and close to the mountains, a rather ordinary location.","Qin Yanzhou looked at the distant military camp, then at the nearby mountains, and suddenly said, \"We cannot see anything just by looking from afar. Tonight, we will climb the mountain.\"","\"Commandant, it is dark now. I fear there may be bears and tigers roaming the mountains at this hour.\"","Someone chimed in, \"If I die under an enemy's blade, it means my skills were inferior, and I would have no complaints or regrets. But if I die in the jaws of a wild beast, how could I have the face to tell our former brothers in the underworld...\"","One after another, they voiced their objections.","It was not just that they thought entering the mountains at this moment was unsafe; it was also because Qin Yanzhou was too unfamiliar to them.","The son of the Lord had been parachuted into the scout squad, becoming their leader right from the start. Prior to this, he was a nobody with no achievements, which clearly failed to convince the masses. Not to mention, this Commandant was too young and too handsome, looking like a mere decorative vase. It also seemed very much like the Lord, out of deep love for his son, had stuffed him in here to secure a safe and steady job.","Since it was meant to be a safe job, how could they let the Second Young Master take risks?","\"We do not need to go deep into the forest. We just need to climb high enough to get a general view of the Xuzhou army camp,\" Qin Yanzhou said resolutely.","He had a feeling that the Xuzhou army would not leave so easily.","He had stayed in the Green Lotus Cult for a long time and was very clear about Liudao's ambitions. He also knew exactly how extensive the cult's roots and claws were. Now that the waters in Chang'an were extremely muddy, given Liudao's personality, he would never let this golden opportunity slip by.","If Li Lishen was really allowed to retreat to Xuzhou, then just as the soldier had said earlier, \"the treacherous prime minister cutting off his own arm,\" it would be beneficial to the North. Qin Yanzhou felt that Liudao would not allow such a thing to happen.","At this moment, Qin Yanzhou actually did not see anything unusual about the Xuzhou army. He decided to climb the mountain purely out of his understanding of his former adoptive father and an indescribable intuition.","The group looked at each other, none of them fully agreeing with Qin Yanzhou's decision.","But after all, Qin Yanzhou was the Commandant, and military orders were like mountains. They could advise him, but the final decision-making power remained in his hands.","Qin Yanzhou's gaze swept over the crowd. He said nothing and walked straight into the mountains.","Xun He whispered, \"Let's follow him first. No matter what, we cannot let anything happen to the Commandant.\"","Starting their climb at dusk, by the time the moon was nearly at its zenith, Qin Yanzhou and his group finally reached a sufficient height. Pushing aside the branches and leaves to look out, they took in the entire view of the Xuzhou army camp not far away.","At this sight, Qin Yanzhou's gaze froze.","The scale of the military camp remained the same, occupying just as much land. However, the distribution of the military tents was quite strange. The outer circle was densely packed, while the inside was empty, planted with many banners and flags.","If one observed from the outside at eye level, they would only see military flags fluttering in the wind and could not see the interior, naturally failing to notice anything odd about the tents.","But now, Qin Yanzhou and the others were on high ground.","\"Something is wrong. Why does it seem like there are fewer military tents?\"","\"It doesn't just seem like it, there are fewer! The very center looks like a granary, which is no different from usual. But think about it, when we normally set up camp to rest, would we ever leave such a large empty space in the middle? This makes no sense at all.\"","\"But we clearly counted earlier, and the cooking pits in the outskirts matched the numbers. Could it be that they deliberately left the cooking pits, and this is all a smokescreen by Xuzhou?\"","\"A smokescreen? What are they trying to hide? Could it be that the main force of the Xuzhou army is no longer here...\"","As they spoke, everyone unanimously hushed, because at this moment, they all realized in hindsight—","Thank goodness they climbed the mountain to take a look!","Everyone looked at Qin Yanzhou. Their eyes were no longer lifeless with suppressed gloom as before, but instead gleamed with a dark light like that of fierce wolves.","\"Commandant, Governor Li of Xuzhou is hiding something. He must be trying to conceal the movements of his main force...\" Xun He took a deep breath, extreme excitement making his hairs stand on end. \"They definitely want to take a shortcut to launch a surprise attack on Wugang County!\"","They had followed the Xuzhou army all the way and had not noticed anything unusual before. There was only one explanation:","The enemy had left the camp under the cover of night, and to avoid detection, they most likely did not ride horses.","No, they definitely did not ride horses!","To detour from here to the rear of Wugang County, crossing the mountains was the fastest route, and horses could not climb mountains.","\"Commandant, let us quickly return and inform the Lord of this news!\"","\"Haha, now that we have this foresight, we absolutely cannot let their scheme succeed.\"","Everyone rubbed their hands together in eager anticipation.","Qin Yanzhou did not speak, and the group descended the mountain. They had come on horseback, so naturally, they would return on horseback. However, while passing the East River of Jiangkou, the young man leading them pulled his horse to a halt.","\"Commandant?\" Xun He was puzzled.","Qin Yanzhou said, \"Based solely on the distribution of the military tents, I do not believe we can definitively conclude whether the main force of the Xuzhou army has slipped away. We still need to look at other things.\"","Someone froze. \"Look at what?\"","Qin Yanzhou looked toward the Xuzhou army's campsite from last night. \"The terrain in Jiangkou is relatively high. If they did not take the main road, their only option would be to abandon their horses and flee lightly into the mountains and forests. Over a thousand people passing through would definitely leave traces.\"","What he wanted to check were exactly those traces in the forest.","Whether the main force of the Xuzhou army had left was a matter of grave importance. It involved whether the allied forces of the North and Qingzhou would need to divert a portion of their troops to deal with an ambush later on.","If their reconnaissance was wrong and they were misled by this information, a batch of troops would be wasted for nothing.","The others came back to their senses and all praised him, \"You are truly meticulous, Commandant.\"","They dismounted and entered the forest.","They had climbed the mountain at night, descended back to their original spot at the beginning of the chou hour, and then rode back to Jiangkou without a moment's rest. By the time they returned to the eastern suburbs of Jiangkou, the golden sun was hanging high in the middle of the sky.","In broad daylight with ample light, the minute details in the forest could be seen quite clearly. Thus, everyone saw that branches and leaves were obviously broken in some places, and the grass and leaves on the ground were trampled so solidly that a path had almost been trodden out.","Seeing this, the light in the eyes of the few men grew even brighter.","\"We definitely cannot be wrong this time, it's a near certainty!\"","\"That Governor Li of Xuzhou, to think he is this cunning! If the Commandant hadn't insisted on climbing the mountain, wouldn't we have been fooled? If they really managed to become an ambush force, what face would we have left to return and see the Lord?\"","\"They must have set off the night before last. Although infantry marches are not as fast as riding horses, they must be traveling day and night to make up for lost time. Commandant, let's hurry back and tell the Lord about this!\"","Unlike the excitement of the others, Qin Yanzhou had remained silent from the moment he saw the traces in the forest, seemingly pondering something.","When the others finished their discussion and looked at him, the young man finally called out three names and then ordered, \"You three, ride as fast as you can back to Wugang to deliver the message.\"","The named soldiers accepted the order.","Xun He guessed, \"Commandant, do you wish to continue observing the Xuzhou army?\"","Qin Yanzhou, cherishing his words like gold, simply said yes. After speaking, he turned around to lead his horse.","The group spent another half day, and just as the sky was about to be shrouded in darkness, they returned from the eastern suburbs of Jiangkou to the side of the Xuzhou army's campsite.","\"Let's rest first,\" Qin Yanzhou said.","They had been rushing about intensely these past two days. They had climbed the mountain all night last night, not to mention tracking the Xuzhou army during the day yesterday. Counting it all up, they had not closed their eyes for a day and a night.","Qin Yanzhou leaned against the tree trunk, staring intently in the direction of the Xuzhou army camp, his elongated eyes as dark as ink.","\"Captain, aren't you going to rest?\" Xun He asked, seeing the surrounding soldiers sleeping haphazardly while Qin Yanzhou kept his eyes wide open.","\"I have an idea,\" the young man suddenly said. \"The main force of Xuzhou has already left. Right now, not only are their troops depleted, but they are also unguarded. After all, they could never imagine that we already know they are weak on the inside despite their strong facade. If we launch a surprise attack now, we might just be able to burn down the Xuzhou army's granary in one fell swoop.\"","Since Li Lishen made a show of withdrawing his troops, he naturally had to put on a full act, returning to Xuzhou with bags big and small. Therefore, their grain was carried with them.","If they could really burn down the granary...","Xun He's pupils contracted for a moment, feeling both excited and horrified by this exceptionally bold idea. But he quickly calmed down and shook his head dejectedly. \"Captain, we don't have enough men.\"","A standard scout squad usually consisted of ten men, typically splitting into pairs to investigate in different directions.","The number of people dispatched this time was more than ever before, totaling twenty. Xun He secretly guessed that the Marquis must have been worried about his son leaving the main force for the first time, so he doubled the numbers.","But even so, twenty was far too few. Xun He didn't believe the enemy soldiers left guarding the camp would number less than two hundred. Not to mention, they had just sent three men back to deliver a message, leaving them with only seventeen...","Xun He punched the tree trunk fiercely and said indignantly, \"So this is what it feels like to be castrated and then see the beauty of your dreams!\"","Qin Yanzhou: \"...\"","\"Captain, if only we had two hundred men, we wouldn't be as helpless as we are now.\" Xun He was frustrated to the point of tearing his hair out.","But it was obviously too late to go back and report the news now. No... not just now, it was already too late back at the river mouth.","To return to Wugang County, they had to pass through Liuzhangping and then change course to the north. Not to mention the time it would take for a round trip, leading an army south would inevitably attract attention.","If they could be scouts, so could others.","Qin Yanzhou looked toward the Xuzhou army camp again. The distant camp was brightly lit by fires, looking in the night like a piece of roasting meat sizzling with oil over a fire pit.","It was incredibly appetizing.","Qin Yanzhou's Adam's apple bobbed up and down. After a long, long time, so long that Xun He thought he had finally given up and couldn't resist going to sleep—","\"We still have to try.\"","Xun He's sleepiness vanished without a trace in an instant. \"Captain, you...\"","\"It's true we only have seventeen men, but the enemy doesn't know our numbers. I plan to leave four men behind, two in the eastern woods and two in the western woods, to act as decoys and create a false impression of strength. At first, the eastern decoys will make their move, while the rest of you will follow me to charge into the camp, overturn the fire braziers, extinguish the torches, kill some of them in the chaos, steal their uniforms, and finally retreat back into the woods.\" In front of Qin Yanzhou's eyes, a vision of flashing blades and soaring flames seemed to appear.","\"After retreating, we will immediately change into the Xuzhou soldiers' clothes. At this time, the western decoys will make their move. The Xuzhou army will have just suffered an attack and will inevitably be in a state of panic. It will be the perfect time for us to infiltrate the enemy camp in the chaos, head straight for the granary, and burn it down!\" Qin Yanzhou didn't speak fast, but every word was firm and resolute.","Xun He's heart pounded with fear. When he spoke again, his voice was extremely dry. \"Captain, we have less than twenty men. This operation is too dangerous. If anything happens to you, I...\"","Qin Yanzhou gave an almost imperceptible smile. \"How can you catch tiger cubs without entering the tiger's den? I used to make a living licking blood from the edge of a blade. Whether this plan is launched or not depends entirely on whether you are willing to risk your lives with me.\"","*","The night was as thick and black as ink. After working for two consecutive nights, the moon hid behind the clouds to slack off, refusing to show its face again. The dark canopy of the sky was terrifyingly heavy, as if it might collapse at any moment.","At the beginning of the Yin hour, rustling sounds came from the forests on the east and west sides of the Xuzhou army camp.","A stationed soldier turned his head to look, yawned lazily, and didn't take it seriously. It was common to have wild beasts in the forest; it was probably just some animals scurrying around inside.","He didn't guess wrong; there were indeed animals inside, but these animals were extraordinary.","\"...We don't have enough vines, get a few more. Damn it, I really wish I could grow another pair of hands, then I'd have ten more fingers.\"","\"Can you be a bit more ambitious? If you're going to dream, dream bigger. At least wish for three heads and six arms!\"","\"You're right.\"","\"Are they tied securely? Why don't you try pulling them.\"","The person standing in the very middle had his ten fingers and arms wrapped with small vines. These small vines extended outward, tied to thicker vines, which in turn extended further out to the next level.","Advancing layer by layer like this, the sturdy vines were ultimately tied to various tree branches.","Hearing the prompt, the man moved his hands. A large swath of forest leaves moved in unison, genuinely creating the imposing aura of thousands of troops hidden in the woods.","\"Good, good, good. Just like that.\"","...","Half an hour passed, and the time quietly reached the middle of the Yin hour.","Qin Yanzhou hid behind the bushes closest to the barracks. He stared unblinkingly at the guard not far away. When the guard let out his third yawn, the young man blew a bird whistle.","The group charged out like lightning.","\"What's going on?\"","\"Enemy atta...\" Before the final syllable could be uttered, a sword's shadow flashed by, severing head from body.","The raised fire braziers were knocked down, some landing upside down, instantly dimming the light in this area by a degree.","And as Qin Yanzhou led his men to pierce the Xuzhou army camp like a sharp knife, the vast expanse of forest branches and leaves behind him shook violently, as if a massive army of soldiers was about to charge out from the woods, causing the faces of a group of Xuzhou soldiers to change drastically.","\"Quick, bring in reinforcements! Damn it, how could they launch a sneak attack at this time? Were the scouts we sent out earlier all useless trash? They didn't bring back a single piece of intel!\"","Qin Yanzhou harvested several heads in quick succession while rapidly approaching a military tent. He was ambidextrous with a blade, and during the melee, he used his left hand to slice open the tent flap with his sword.","Surprisingly yet unsurprisingly, inside the relatively large tent, there were only three people. And unlike ordinary days when neat communal beds were laid out on the ground, there were only three quilts in the tent; the rest of the space was completely empty.","Qin Yanzhou concealed the sharp glint in his eyes.","Their group had come fast and fierce. At first, they indeed caught the Xuzhou army off guard, taking many lives in a row. But after all, they were few in number, and soon the Xuzhou army reacted.","\"Wait, there are only a dozen or so of them.\"","At this moment, Qin Yanzhou shouted loudly, \"Retreat!\"","This had been discussed well in advance, so there was absolutely no hesitation. They retreated the moment the order was given, demonstrating an exceptionally high level of obedience.","The assassination squad that had been tearing into the Xuzhou army like a pack of vicious wolves just moments ago retreated with their meat in their mouths in the blink of an eye.","A foot soldier wanted to pursue them, but saw his superior raise a hand to stop him. He immediately asked in confusion, \"Colonel, why aren't we chasing them?\"","The Colonel sneered, \"How do you know the enemy hasn't set an ambush in the woods? If that was just bait, wouldn't chasing them now play right into their hands? Besides, our army already has few men left, numbering only four hundred, and we cannot afford to leave the granary unguarded.\"","The soldier suddenly understood.","The surrounding people also nodded in agreement.","As a result, just as these words were spoken, the leaves in the western forest suddenly rustled loudly, startling everyone and sending a shock through their hearts.","\"There is movement over there! Go check it out quickly and stay on high alert. Hah, I knew that earlier commotion was just a diversion to lure us away! It is a good thing we didn't give chase, or we would have fallen right into their trap!\"","As the Xuzhou army's forces surged toward the west, they failed to notice a few \"comrades\" emerging from the eastern woods.","These men swiftly \"rejoined the ranks,\" swaggering straight toward the granary at the heart of the camp.","Following the earlier skirmish, the camp was in utter disarray. Braziers had been overturned and half the torches extinguished, leaving the area bathed in dim shadows. With everyone's attention fixated on the west, remarkably no one noticed this rather unusual squad.","Qin Yanzhou crept up to the edge of the granary. Ever cautious, he didn't immediately hurl a brazier inside. Instead, he peered in first. Only after confirming his target did he shout at the top of his lungs, \"Watch out! Another enemy attack from the east!\"","His words were like a boulder crashing into a lake. Countless heads snapped around in unison, and sure enough, the foliage in the eastern woods was rustling wildly once again.","Seizing the distraction, Qin Yanzhou and his men snatched up torches and braziers, hurling them forcefully into the granary.","\"Fire!\"","\"Who set the fire? Damn it, there are spies in the ranks!\"","Turning a deaf ear to the panic, Qin Yanzhou continued to ignite the granary.","Because grain would mold if exposed to moisture, the interior of the granary was kept bone-dry. Consequently, the flames caught and spread with terrifying speed. The raging inferno surged upward, resembling an arrogant, fiery dragon ascending straight into the heavens.","Qin Yanzhou cast one last, profound look at the sky-piercing flames before turning on his heel to leave. The blazing light stretched his silhouette across the ground, giving his retreating figure the majestic aura of a fire dragon itself."]},{"number":164,"title":"Chapter 164","paragraphs":["Wugang County.","\"Waiting at the Changping intersection, we really waited for the defeated Xuzhou army. Father, your son has successfully completed the mission, and most of those fleeing ambushing soldiers have been executed!\" Qin Qinian came back panting, still holding a head in his hand.","He was bathed in blood, and his armor was broken in many places. The whole person seemed to have walked through a pool of blood, and the clothes inside the armor had become dark red, with his own blood and the blood of others.","Although bloody, Qin Qinian did not look weak after the fierce battle, but rather extremely excited.","He was not the only one excited, but also the others in the hall. Since the scouts came back from the eastern suburbs of Jiangkou, everyone has been rubbing their fists and wiping their palms, wishing to open their bloody mouths and swallow the enemy completely.","The withdrawal of Xuzhou troops is a cover. Connecting with the direction of the other party's advance, it is not difficult for them to guess Li Lishen's intention.","Especially when it is known that the Sizhou army has \"secretly\" detoured behind Wugang, trying to be the oriole in \"the mantis stalks the cicada, unaware of the oriole behind\", the other party's intention is even more obvious -","The real \"oriole\" is not the Sizhou army, but the Xuzhou ambush led by Li Lishen.","If the North side really believed that Governor Li of Xuzhou and Dong Zhou had broken up, and turned to send troops to the back of the Sizhou army, trying to stab them in the back, there would be only one ending:","Surrounded by the Xuzhou army and Sizhou army ambush hidden further behind, flanking from front and back.","However, that is an assumption that will no longer appear.","Everyone looked at the head in Qin Qinian's hand, some shouted loudly, some clapped and laughed, and some clenched their fists and hit the air.","And that round head impressively belonged to Governor Li of Xuzhou, Li Lishen.","\"After this battle, the main force of Sizhou surrounded by our side lost nine out of ten, and the Xuzhou army had a way out, and half of them escaped. The remaining Governor Jiang of Yuzhou must be unable to support it alone, and it is just around the corner for us to take the head of that treacherous minister!\"","\"Although many Xuzhou soldiers escaped, Li Lishen is dead. Now the Xuzhou army is leaderless, and they can't make any waves in a short time.\"","\"Hahaha, since Dong and Li like to form an alliance, let's put their heads together another day.\"","Cui Shengping laughed and said: \"There is a saying that those who lead the whole army with the courage of one person are brave generals; and those who lead the whole army with the strategy of one person are wise generals. The third son is both brave and wise, and is truly a tiger cub from a general's family, perfectly inheriting the Lord's wisdom and martial arts.\"","Everyone echoed, \"A tiger father has no dog son, nothing more than this!\"","Nalan Zhi interjected at this time, \"This time, thanks to the scout team for exploring the opportunity, otherwise, at best, we would lose troops and generals, and at worst, the Yanzhou we captured earlier might have to be handed over.\"","Why hand it over?","Naturally, it is defeat, and we have to retreat.","Everyone also nodded in agreement, \"Yes, thanks to the second son's meticulousness, otherwise others would be laughing happily today.\"","Qin Shaozong glanced at Nalan Zhi and Cui Shengping, turned the jade thumb ring in his hand, and said nothing.","At this time, there were hurried footsteps outside, but it seemed to encounter something near the door and paused. Qin Shaozong looked at the door and was about to ask someone to come in. Before he could speak, a soldier strode in.","It was a travel-stained man, exactly the scout who went to investigate with Qin Yanzhou. Xun He arched his hands and reported excitedly, \"Lord, the Xuzhou granary has been burned!\"","One sentence shocked the four seats, and everyone was in an uproar.","\"Burned? Who burned it? Did the treacherous minister and the others have internal strife?\" This was the first reaction of many people.","Qin Shaozong didn't think so, because Xun He's eyes were very bright at the moment. Even though his eyes were covered with bloodshot, obviously he had not slept for a long time, it still could not cover the light in his eyes.","\"The captain led us to burn it together.\" Xun He answered loudly.","The hall fell silent again, and everyone was extremely shocked and speechless for a time. Cui Shengping's long beard trembled, and he asked with a complex expression: \"How many people did the second son take to investigate?\"","Xun He first said twenty, and later changed it to seventeen, and then described the whole process of investigating the military camp in detail.","He probably has some talent for storytelling. He started from when Qin Yanzhou insisted on going up the mountain, suffered minor obstacles in the middle, and then said that Qin Yanzhou proposed a sneak attack on the granary and was dissuaded by him, and a series of dangerous situations followed.","Everyone was fascinated, and their hearts could not help but rise and fall.","After Xun He finished speaking, many people let out a long breath, praised Qin Yanzhou highly, and asked where he was.","Xun He said truthfully: \"The captain was injured, and he and other brothers went to find the gentleman for treatment first.\"","They only had seventeen people, and they were extremely short of hands. Even the soldiers who were responsible for shaking branches before participated in the subsequent cover retreat.","Xun He was arranged to shake branches in the west. Compared with others, he had fewer chances to fight with Xuzhou soldiers. He was the least injured among the crowd, so Qin Yanzhou specially sent him to report.","Qin Shaozong immediately looked at his youngest son who was still holding the head, \"Qin San, there is nothing for you here, you go find Ding Congjian to see your injuries immediately.\"","The sudden concern of the father made the young man light-headed. He scratched the back of his head embarrassedly and wanted to say that he was fine, \"Father, I can still...\"","\"Go quickly!\" The two unquestionable words fell.","Qin Qinian was scolded and confused, and subconsciously went to the door, but was soon stopped by Qin Shaozong: \"Put down the head.\"","Qin Qinian came out of the room and walked slowly. He had no goal. After thinking about it, he simply went to see a military doctor as his father said.","Just on the way there...","\"Mother?\" He saw Dai Li. The other party was walking in front of him, not facing him, but with her back to him, looking as if she was also going to the room where Mr. Ding was.","It's just that the second brother just came back, how did the mother know that he was at Mr. Ding's? Could it be that she just went to the main hall?","This thought flashed through Qin Qinian's mind.","Dai Li heard his voice and didn't stop at first, but walked two steps forward before realizing it and turning around, \"Qinian is back...\"","Qin Qinian saw that there was an imperceptible trance on her face, and asked worriedly: \"Mother, are you feeling unwell?\"","Dai Li calmed down, shook her head and said no, and then realized that the armor on his body was broken, and the clothes inside were rotten, like a rag, and the smell of blood was overwhelming.","\"Why are you hurt like this, child? Don't delay, go find Mr. Ding quickly.\" Dai Li changed her face, seeing that he was still standing, wanted to pull him, but didn't know if he had injuries on his arm, and finally didn't dare to move randomly, only urging him repeatedly.","The two came to the medical area together.","After two rounds of battles, many wounded gathered here. Dai Li was a little dizzy with blood. She usually wouldn't come here, but hearing that Qin Yanzhou was injured, she couldn't care so much.","In the room, the medical soldiers led by Ding Lianxi were busy helping the soldiers stitch up their wounds.","Last year, on Dai Li's suggestion, Ding Lianxi replaced silk threads with mulberry bark threads, and the results were surprisingly good. Marveling at the outcome, he had continued to use them ever since.","When Dai Li arrived, Qin Yanzhou's wounds had already been treated, and he had put his clothes back on, though his belt was still loosely tied around his lean waist.","It was unknown where he had procured a new set of clothes, but he looked perfectly clean now. Aside from his pale complexion, there was no sign he had been injured. Anyone unaware of the truth would assume he was merely bringing his subordinate soldiers to see the military doctor.","\"Mother?\" Qin Yanzhou stiffened upon seeing Dai Li. \"Why are you here?\"","\"To see you, and to bring Qinian for treatment,\" Dai Li said, looking him up and down. However, her son was dressed so neatly that she couldn't tell where he had been hurt.","Since she couldn't see anything for now, Dai Li first addressed the young man beside her. \"Qinian, take off your armor and let the doctor treat your wounds.\"","Qin Qinian obediently followed her instructions.","He moved quickly, his equipment clattering to the floor. In just a moment, he was down to his inner garments. However, as he was about to remove his final top, the young man paused, looked back at Dai Li, and shyly called out to her.","Not only was it a matter of a grown son avoiding his mother, but he had never been so \"uninhibited\" in front of other women before.","Dai Li understood, but she didn't leave. She simply turned around, her back to Qin Qinian and facing Qin Yanzhou, and began to interrogate her eldest son. \"Zhou Zhou, where are you hurt?\"","Qin Yanzhou hesitated.","Dai Li's face grew cold. \"Tell the truth.\"","\"My arm and my back.\" After reporting the two locations, he quickly added, \"The wounds aren't deep. They'll heal with some rest. Don't worry.\"","As if that weren't enough, Qin Yanzhou swiftly tied his belt, seemingly afraid she would ask to see the wounds.","Dai Li's head throbbed. The murmurs she had heard at the door seemed to rush at her from all directions, a tangled web of emotions that made her heart race and her head split. She remembered that there were many wounded soldiers here, and it wasn't the place to talk, so she remained silent.","Qin Yanzhou lowered his eyes, avoiding Dai Li's gaze.","The atmosphere grew tense for a moment.","Ding Lianxi worked swiftly, taking little time to bandage Qin Qinian's wounds and instruct him on what to watch out for in the coming days.","Once he was finished, Dai Li led the two of them away.","...","Over the next three days, Qin Shaozong was exceptionally busy, arranging for men to pursue the remnants of the Xu and Si provinces, and dealing with the desperate struggles of the Chang'an military patrol and the Yuzhou army.","He didn't neglect the matter of the manifesto, either. After every minor skirmish, Qin Shaozong would order a bulletin to be posted, broadcasting the progress of the war. It was just as the first manifesto had stated: \"The blade is aimed solely at the chief culprit, not at the throne.\"","Although Qin Shaozong left early and returned late, with the lights in the council chamber often burning deep into the night, he still noticed that something was amiss with Dai Li lately.","She wasn't checking the fertilizer records, she spoke much less, and the maids reported that she was eating less. Sometimes she would hold a book for a long time without turning a single page.","As for the nights, he knew she sometimes woke up with a start.","Qin Shaozong figured she was distressed over her sons' injuries, so he simply called the two brothers, who were temporarily barred from battle, and told them to accompany Dai Li to the county market.","Wugang was just a county, its scale incomparable to a commandery, but it was vastly superior to a village. The war was still ongoing, but because the Qingbei allied forces maintained strict discipline over their soldiers, everything in the county remained as usual.","At this time, the streets were bustling with vendors, their cries rising and falling in a lively scene.","Dai Li walked aimlessly down the street, disinterested in everything. She had been pondering the same matter for days, turning it over and over in her mind, only to dejectedly and fearfully admit that she had no safe way to resolve it.","\"Woof, woof—\"","An old man had set up a bamboo cage by the roadside, containing several puppies. The puppies whined inside, their round bellies making them look like adorable little furballs.","Qin Yanzhou was the first to change direction, walking over to the old man.","Seeing him approach, the old man smiled and asked, \"Young master, are you looking to buy a hound? The ones I have here are all bred from top-notch hunting dogs. Raised from a young age, they'll surely grow up to be loyal and fierce. They're not expensive, only twenty coins each.\"","Seeing his older brother go over, Qin Qinian happily followed. \"Second Brother, are you buying a puppy?\"","Qin Yanzhou nodded. \"I'm buying one for Rongrong.\"","Qin Qinian was like a curious child. \"Why are you buying a puppy for Rongrong? Do you two have a secret agreement? When did this happen, and why didn't I know?\"","Qin Yanzhou pursed his lips.","It was a long story. When his mother had initially refused to let him go to the front lines, he had asked Shi Rongyue to help persuade her. In return, he promised to pick out a little white dog for her.","But Dai Li was also here, so Qin Yanzhou couldn't say it outright.","Not getting an answer, Qin Qinian mumbled things like \"You guys aren't letting me play,\" \"What kind of little white dog does she want,\" and \"I'll help look too.\"","Hearing him say he wanted a white dog, the old man proactively pulled two out of the cage. \"Young master, how about these two? The one on the left is a bit sturdier, with just a bit of black on the tip of its tail...\"","Standing a short distance away, Dai Li watched the two of them picking out a puppy, her pupils trembling.","The brothers stood close together. Qin Qinian wasn't as tall as Qin Yanzhou, but that didn't stop him from putting his arm around his brother's shoulder, the two of them huddled together discussing the puppies.","If someone were to say they were blood brothers, any outsider unaware of the truth would believe it.","It was precisely because of their current brotherly affection that Dai Li was deeply terrified, fearing that one day they would turn their swords against each other.","This unease had perhaps existed for a long time, initially just an insignificant seed, hidden deep in a crevice where it couldn't be seen or touched. But with the recent battles, it was as if it had received the nourishment of wind and rain, quickly taking root and sprouting.","Dai Li still remembered the day she was counting the days waiting for Zhou Zhou to return. But she waited and waited, and he never showed up. Unable to sit still, she went to the council chamber, intending to ask Qin Changgeng after he finished his business.","But as soon as she reached the door, she heard Qinian giving a report. Not only had he taken the head of Governor Li of Xuzhou, but he had also wiped out many of the Xuzhou remnants.","This was good news, and many people congratulated him.","Among them, Dai Li heard Cui Shengping's voice, followed closely by Nalan Zhi's. But the latter wasn't praising Qinian; he brought up Zhou Zhou.","A sense of strangeness welled up in her heart.","Later, when the scouts returned and spoke of their daring exploit, she broke out in a cold sweat, while simultaneously hearing the endless stream of praise in the council chamber, flowing like river water.","In that instant, Dai Li felt that sense of strangeness ride the wind of praise, soaring upwards, like oil poured on a raging fire, abruptly reaching its peak.","That gust of wind was so cold, as if it could blow right into a person's bones, not missing a single gap. And in the biting wind, Dai Li seemed to see endless bloodshed and a fight to the death between brothers.","Qin Changgeng's aides had taken sides, and surprisingly, Zhou Zhou actually had supporters behind him too!","Did they dare to take sides because they had received Qin Changgeng's tacit approval? How else would they dare?","And what about Qin Changgeng? What was he thinking? Was he treating Zhou Zhou as a whetstone to sharpen his true heir, or something else?","Before coming to the Great Yan Dynasty, Dai Li was just a publishing house editor; she had never entered politics. Therefore, she readily admitted that her political acumen was indeed lacking.","It was precisely because of this that she felt even more panicked.","If even someone as slow as her could sense that something was wrong, could the hidden conflicts between the two sides be even greater and more difficult to mediate...","For the first time, Dai Li felt that having a husband with too much potential and power was not necessarily a good thing.","It was obvious that Qin Changgeng would not just stop at the position of a marquis; his goal was the throne in the imperial city, the absolute authority to rule over the entire world.","Even if Zhou Zhou had no desire to fight for power, what if he was pushed, forced, and begged to do so in the future? Would he be willing? Could he refuse? Could he escape unscathed?","The concept of being caught in circumstances beyond one's control was never just empty words. Zhou Zhou and Qi Nian were both good children. Even though the latter was not her biological son, she sincerely hoped he would live a peaceful and happy life.","Looking at the two brothers who were on such good terms, Dai Li fell into an uncontrollable state of anxiety.","Neither Qin Yanzhou nor Qin Qinian knew what she was thinking. After carefully comparing the options, the young man picked a little white dog with a purer coat and a sturdier build.","\"Mother?\" Qin Yanzhou turned around holding the puppy. Seeing Dai Li staring blankly at him and Qin Qinian with a somewhat pale face, he asked, \"What is wrong?\"","Dai Li snapped back to reality and forced a smile. \"It is nothing, I just zoned out for a moment.\"","The group continued walking forward and encountered a caravan of merchants. The voices of the merchants drifted over:","\"I heard that both the Xuzhou army and the Sizhou army were utterly defeated. Tsk tsk, it looks like the days ahead will be tough for those nobles in Chang'an.\"","\"Move a tree and it dies, move a person and they thrive. Could they really let themselves be trapped to death in a single city? If they cannot stay in Chang'an, the worst they can do is flee. They can escape to a peaceful place and continue living their lives.\"","Dai Li suddenly stopped in her tracks."]},{"number":165,"title":"Chapter 165","paragraphs":["\"Brother Zhongle, a little white dog!\"","Shi Rongyue looked at the puppy in Qin Yanzhou's hands, her eyes shining as brightly as the golden sun in the sky.","Qin Yanzhou set the little furball down and gently rubbed its head until it whimpered softly. \"Just now at the market, there was an old man selling puppies. I remembered what I promised you before, so I picked one out. See if you like it?\"","As soon as he finished speaking, a crisp \"I like it!\" rang out from opposite him. The young man smiled imperceptibly and patted the puppy's round bottom, signaling the little white dog to walk forward.","The little furball seemed to understand human nature. It really did step forward on its short little legs, wagging its tail like a propeller as it trotted eagerly toward Shi Rongyue.","It was about two months old, with a round head and round body. Its eyes were dark and bright, and its fur was as white as snow, save for the very tip of its tail, which was stained with a touch of ink-black.","Because he gave it to her, Shi Rongyue already liked it. Now, having her fingers licked by the little puppy that ran over to her, her affection for it grew so intense it nearly overflowed.","\"It's so adorable. It will definitely be the most excellent dog in the future.\" Shi Rongyue picked up the furball and rubbed her cheek against its head. \"Brother Zhongle, I'm not good at coming up with names, and since you brought it back, why don't you go ahead and name it?\"","Two pairs of eyes looked at him simultaneously. One pair was as black as an inkstone, while the other was as bright as amber. Both were round and possessed a similar, pure innocence.","Qin Yanzhou frowned in deep thought. Shi Rongyue couldn't help but hold her breath slightly, a stray lock of hair standing up on her head as she waited in anticipation.","After a long while, the young man said, \"It's white, so how about we call it Xiaobai?\"","Shi Rongyue: \"...\"","Seeing her remain silent, Qin Yanzhou guessed she might not like the name. Looking at the puppy's still-wagging tail, he corrected himself, \"Its tail is black, so Little Black Tail would be fitting too.\"","Shi Rongyue: \"...\"","Choosing the lesser of two evils, Shi Rongyue struggled for a moment. \"Actually, Xiaobai is quite good. Let's just call it Xiaobai.\"","Qin Yanzhou nodded. \"Yes, Xiaobai is indeed quite good.\"","After watching the puppy for a little while longer, Qin Yanzhou, who still had studies to attend to, left Shi Rongyue's courtyard.","As soon as he was gone, Shi Rongyue immediately covered the furball's ears and gave them a rub. \"Be a good baby, don't listen to what Brother Zhongle just said.\"","After saying this, she paused, released one hand, and only covered one of the dog's ears. \"Well, you should still listen to half of it. When he calls you Xiaobai in the future, you have to respond to him.\"","\"Woof.\" The puppy wagged its tail.","\"Hmm, what should Xiaobai's real name be?\" Shi Rongyue held the puppy in her arms, squeezing its chubby little paws as she fell into deep thought.","About half a quarter of an hour later, the young girl suddenly lifted the furball high in the air. \"I've got it, we'll call you Boqi! Legend has it that Boqi can devour the ghosts and monsters that cause nightmares. By giving you to me, he has gifted me sweet dreams from now on.\"","\"Woof, woof.\"","*","After returning from the market, Dai Li went straight back to her room, dug out a map, and spread it open.","The Sizhou army had been attacked from both the front and the rear by the Qing-Bei allied forces and was almost entirely wiped out. The ambushing troops from Xuzhou had also been outflanked by the Northern army, who had received the intelligence; Li Lishen died in battle, half the routed army fled, and with the Xuzhou army's granaries burned, the remaining Xuzhou survivors became fish on a chopping block.","Dai Li stared at Chang'an on the map, her gaze heavy.","Given Qin Changgeng's combat prowess, this city definitely wouldn't be able to hold out for long. And once Chang'an was occupied, Yongzhou, including Chang'an, would naturally all fall to the North.","It could be said that now, apart from the southern provinces of Jingzhou and Yizhou... oh, and Qingzhou, the map of the world had basically been pieced together by Qin Changgeng.","However, the young Emperor of Great Yan was still alive. If Qin Changgeng wanted to be legitimate, he absolutely could not do something like the Sima family did, killing the emperor in the streets. Otherwise, for Liu of Jingzhou, who also held heavy military power, it would be like someone handing him a pillow just as he was dozing off—giving him a perfectly justifiable reason to launch a campaign.","Dai Li was glad she had \"woken up\" early, because although Qin Shaozong seemed only one step away from that position, this step would not be an easy one to take.","She still had time and room to maneuver.","The woman's fingertips tapped rhythmically against the desk as her thoughts peeled back layer by layer, pondering the future.","\"What is my wife thinking about?\" Someone suddenly spoke from beside her.","Dai Li was so startled she jolted entirely, her hairs standing on end. If she had a large, fluffy tail behind her, it would definitely have puffed up as if she had been electrocuted.","\"Did I scare you?\" Qin Shaozong hadn't expected her to have such a big reaction. He asked with a smile, \"What bad ideas is my wife scheming up now?\"","He was only teasing and had said it completely casually, but it made Dai Li's heart pound with fear.","Admitting it was absolutely out of the question, so Dai Li quickly turned the tables. \"What nonsense are you saying? I was purely scared by you. How come you didn't make a sound when you came in?\"","\"It is clearly because my wife was too absorbed in looking at the map, yet it becomes my fault.\" Qin Shaozong patted her back as if smoothing down her fur. \"Have you grown tired of staying in Wugang and are anxious to enter the capital?\"","\"A small county has its own local customs and charm. This place is quite nice, I am in no rush.\" In truth, she was wishing she could stay in Wugang a bit longer, hoping Qin Changgeng's pace would slow down.","However, Dai Li's calculations fell through, because she heard the man beside her say, \"In a month at most, you will accompany me to the capital.\"","A crash of thunder echoed in Dai Li's heart. \"So fast? You can wipe out the Yuzhou army in just a month? Right, I heard earlier that Liu of Jingzhou was also heading to the capital. Now that you and Chancellor Dong are fighting fiercely, why hasn't he appeared?\"","Qin Shaozong looked at the map, a cold, dark gleam in his narrow eyes. \"That fellow Liu Zhan is quite cunning. He was the second to declare he was marching on the capital, yet he was also the one dragging his feet. Previously, he sat on the mountain to watch the tigers fight, hoping to pick up a ready-made victory, but after finding it difficult to intervene, he simply retreated back to Yizhou.\"","Dai Li looked thoughtful.","The terrain around Guanzhong was protected by the Qinling Mountains, circling it like a dragon, making it easy to defend and hard to attack. If the troop movement was improper, it would be very easy to get blocked in the gorges. Stuck in a dilemma with no way forward or back, there was indeed a chance of the entire army being annihilated.","\"Once Chang'an is pacified, you should still have quite a few things to wrap up, right?\" Dai Li probed. \"For example, appeasing the young emperor and the courtiers...\"","She mentioned appeasing the young emperor.","Qin Shaozong shifted his gaze back to her and chuckled softly. \"Haste makes waste; focusing on small gains ruins great endeavors. Some things still need to be planned out slowly and steadily.\"","Dai Li was not surprised.","As expected, he had never thought of killing the young emperor.","Dai Li added, \"Qin Changgeng, this year is the first year we are using fertilizer to assist with farming. I want to spend this golden autumn in Yuyang.\"","Qin Shaozong looked at Dai Li without speaking.","Dai Li knew that his failure to agree immediately meant he was unwilling, so she continued, \"After you march into Chang'an, the situation in the imperial court will inevitably undergo major changes. The prominent families of Chang'an have, after all, been entrenched in that treasured land for over a hundred years and have deep roots. Even if you have an army in your hands, since you want to proceed slowly to preserve your reputation, you can't just take drastic, sweeping actions. Back and forth, it will take a few months at the very least. I cannot wait that long.\"","Qin Shaozong's gaze was heavy.","He knew she was right. To properly sort out the territory of Chang'an using a mix of tough and gentle measures, it simply couldn't be done without spending time and energy.","\"It is still early until autumn. We will discuss this matter later,\" Qin Shaozong said in a deep voice.","Dai Li had finally brought it up, so naturally she wanted to strike while the iron was hot. Unwilling to \"discuss it later,\" she immediately said, \"It's not early. It's already July, summer is half over, and it will take another month for you to finish things here. That means by the time the war ends and the dust settles, it will be August. From Chang'an back to Yuyang, even riding fast, it will take about a month.\"","Qin Shaozong replied, \"Then we'll discuss it after the dust settles.\"","In other words, not now. He wasn't going to talk about it now.","Dai Li was slightly choked by his response.","At this time, the sun was setting in the west, and a large swath of brilliant afterglow slanted into the room, making his forehead look even fuller and his features deeper. However, when his usually sharp and authoritative brown eyes looked at her, they were still as fiery as ever.","For a moment, Dai Li wanted to ask him why he allowed the strategists to take sides. What did he think Zhouzhou was? Had he really considered Zhouzhou's future?","A barrage of words rushed to her throat, but Dai Li couldn't utter a single one.","She and Qin Shaozong were a blended family, and the affairs and children of ordinary reorganized families were very sensitive, let alone the fact that Qin Changgeng was only one step away from supreme power over the world.","In order to inherit that position, there were many throughout history who killed their brothers. Even brothers born of the same mother could only helplessly sigh, \"We are born of the same root, why are we in such a hurry to fry each other?\"; not to mention those without blood ties...","She knew Qin Shaozong liked her, but Dai Li wasn't sure how much this \"like\" amounted to. Because to this day, her fundamental interests had never seemed to clash with his.","What if there was a conflict? Would he still be the same? If the final outcome went against her wishes, could she and Zhouzhou still retreat unscathed?","Dai Li had no answers.","She was also afraid to pierce that layer of paper and personally uncover that answer.","\"Madam?\"","The hair by her ear was tucked behind it, and the man's thickly callused fingers brushed against her fair earlobe.","It tickled a little, and Dai Li snapped back to reality. Knowing this man's sharp gaze, she figured he might have noticed her abnormality just now, so she could only say, \"Alright, let's not talk about it for now.\"","*","Inside Chang'an City.","\"...You bastard, you managed to turn such a great situation into a precarious one! As long as the manifesto has been issued, you've suffered that many defeats. I ask you, what face do you have to continue being the General of the Chariots and Cavalry? In my opinion, even pulling a half-crippled soldier from the army would be more useful than you.\" Dong Zhou pointed at Qiu Tong's nose, scolding him thoroughly.","Qiu Tong lowered his head, the veins on his neck bulging and then subsiding. \"In the victory or defeat of an army, strategy is key; many calculations lead to victory, few calculations lead to defeat. Your subordinate acted according to Libationer Zheng's method, and after that surnamed Zheng's high-sounding talk, several provincial governors praised him greatly. But who could have foreseen that this person was only good on paper, an embroidered pillow, and his ability to deceive people was top-notch.\"","In fact, it wasn't just a few provincial governors. At that time, Dong Zhou himself had praised Zheng Yizhi highly. Now Qiu Tong only mentioned Li Lishen and others, saying nothing about Dong Zhou, effectively removing him from the situation.","Dong Zhou paused slightly, his anger shifting. \"Where is Zheng Yizhi? Tell him to roll over here and see me.\"","After a long while, Zheng Yizhi, whose hands and feet were soft, was brought in by the guards. As soon as the guards on both sides let go, he seemed to know what awaited him and directly went soft on the ground, \"Chancellor Dong, spare my life...\"","Dong Zhou caught the man and scolded him fiercely again, finally saying coldly, \"Libationer Zheng is a mediocre talent who ruined the country and delayed military opportunities, allowing treacherous villains to run rampant. Men, drag him out and behead him as a public warning!\"","Zheng Yizhi felt as if he had fallen into an ice cellar. Seeing the soldiers coming to drag him away, he hurriedly said, \"Chancellor Dong, there is someone else who delayed military opportunities! Those strategies I had earlier were all heard from a friend. It was him, he caused our imperial army's great defeat and caused Governor Li of Xuzhou to die in battle.\"","Dong Zhou laughed in extreme anger. \"Absurd, do you think you can escape death by randomly making up a nonexistent person?\"","\"Your servant wouldn't dare.\" Zheng Yizhi prostrated himself on the ground. \"It's just that he is as deeply sinful as your servant, and on this road to the Yellow Springs, the two of us should naturally go together to apologize to Governor Li of Xuzhou.\"","He spoke with utmost sincerity and even blurted out an address in one breath, insisting that the person lived there, begging Dong Zhou to send troops to capture him.","Seeing him speak so firmly, Dong Zhou sent someone to take a trip as he wished. However, when the guards returned, they claimed the house was empty.","\"No one? Impossible!\" Zheng Yizhi reacted strongly, murmuring, \"He once said he came to the capital to seek refuge with relatives and would settle here in the future. How could...\"","The soldier coldly interrupted, \"Your subordinate asked the neighbors, and they all said that family moved away about ten days ago.\"","Zheng Yizhi's pupils contracted.","Ten days ago, that was the day Governor Li of Xuzhou suffered his new defeat.","Dong Zhou couldn't be bothered to say more to him and waved his hand. \"Take him down and behead him.\"","*","Qin Shaozong's prediction was very accurate. He said that Dai Li would be able to accompany him into the capital in at most a month. This was not wrong at all. When the month was almost up, the Yuzhou army suffered a crushing defeat at Hengshui Ford, and the rebel Jiang's head was severed.","Thus, this lightning-fast, vigorous anti-rebel campaign came to an end.","When Qin Shaozong widely issued the manifesto, his target was Governor Jiang of Yuzhou, and he did not include Dong Zhou in it. He positioned this powerful chancellor who controlled the court as a \"loyal subject,\" not saying in the manifesto that he would kill him.","But how could Dong Zhou believe it? He knew that even if Qin Shaozong didn't kill him today, he might tomorrow. Therefore, when the Yuzhou army suffered a new defeat, he fled with his wife and children.","Qin Shaozong was not surprised by this and directly sent two teams of men in pursuit, wanting to see the person alive or a corpse if dead.","Dai Li didn't know the twists and turns of this; she only knew that today she was going to accompany Qin Shaozong into the capital again. The last time they entered the capital, they lived in a residence specially arranged by Dong Zhou, and several provincial governors lived together as neighbors.","Coming back this time, Qin Shaozong didn't move; he still returned here. And out of various considerations, Nangong Xiong also chose his original position, continuing to be neighbors with the people from the North.","Chang'an was still Chang'an, where wealthy families bought wine on the streets of Chang'an, and once a building was raised, it was a hundred feet high, with endless prosperity everywhere.","But this time, Dai Li's feelings were much deeper than before.","On the first day of her return, gold-painted visiting cards fluttered in like snowflakes, making the courtyard as crowded as a marketplace and the carriages as flowing as water. As soon as the sky brightened, people came to deliver gifts, and the people seeking an audience were as numerous as carp crossing the river, uninterrupted from dawn to dusk, often stopping only at the curfew.","Qin Shaozong didn't see any visitors. After resting for two days, he took Dai Li into the palace.","It wasn't a rash audience with the emperor. On the first day he entered Chang'an, he sent a message to the palace, bringing up the matter of Dai Li's enfeoffment again, and told Young Emperor Han that he would come over in two days.","Young Emperor Han took over the throne at the age of eight from the late emperor, who died suddenly from abusing pills. After ascending the throne, he held no real power, and the state affairs were jointly controlled by Empress Dowager Wang and Chancellor Dong.","Qin Shaozong's message was sent to Empress Dowager Wang rather than Young Emperor Han.","People are the knife and chopping block, I am the fish and meat. The fierce wolf has just left, and the vicious tiger comes again.","Never mind how Empress Dowager Wang flew into a rage in the depths of the palace upon receiving the missive, cursing Qin Shaozong for his wolfish ambitions and wishing him a gruesome death. On the surface, she swiftly dispatched edicts to the noble houses of Chang'an, inviting them to the palace banquet that would follow the investiture ceremony.","The schedule was perfectly clear: attend the morning court for the investiture, and hold the banquet in the afternoon.","...","Dai Li followed Qin Shaozong into the palace for the morning assembly. They rode in a carriage, driving straight through the majestic Sima Main Gate.","The Sima Main Gate was a passage reserved exclusively for the Emperor, or for feudal lords seeking an audience with the Son of Heaven. Ordinary officials attending court only ever used the East Gate; they were forbidden from taking the main entrance.","Even when entering through the East Gate, one was required to dismount, proceed on foot, and surrender their weapons before being allowed inside. Yet today, not only did Qin Shaozong pass through the main gate without unbuckling his sword, he also had no intention of stepping down to walk.","He and Nangong Xiong each commanded their own carriage, driving arrogantly through the palace gates until they reached the front plaza of the main hall.","Dai Li stood on the expansive plaza. The sky above was as clear and blue as water, the grounds stretching wide and flat on either side. Before her, the palace buildings towered majestically, and the solemn dignity of the imperial city washed over her.","This was the place of absolute, supreme power in all of Chang'an—no, in the entire world.","She suspected that, aside from Empress Dowager Wang, she was the first woman in the Great Yan dynasty to brazenly set foot in the front hall's domain.","\"Madam,\" a low voice spoke beside her.","Dai Li turned to look at the man at her side.","He wore the tall crown of a military commander and a dark robe, a ring-pommel sword hanging from his waist. His towering, robust physique radiated an extraordinary, commanding presence.","What a magnificent traitor!","Dai Li then looked down at herself. Because of today's investiture, she was also dressed with utmost solemnity. Her long hair was swept into a high chignon, adorned with a golden step-shake and pearl hairpins. A necklace of pure crystal rested against her dark green, curved-hem robe. Jade pendants dangled from her waist, and her cloud-patterned upturned shoes, symbolizing a steady rise to power, peeked out from the front hem of her long skirt. She looked the very picture of demure elegance.","Ah, yes. What a magnificent traitor she was, too!"]},{"number":166,"title":"Chapter 166","paragraphs":["\"...We have heard that praising the virtuous and rewarding great merit is a universal principle since ancient times. The Marquis of Wu'an has quelled rebellion and destroyed traitors; his divine martial prowess is unparalleled. He has protected the Great Yan amidst the swaying storms, and We greatly commend him. We confer upon him the title of Grand Commandant, with an appanage of five thousand four hundred households, and his noble rank and fief shall continue from generation to generation without end...\"","This edict conferring the title of Grand Commandant came suddenly, directly appointing Qin Shaozong as Grand Commandant without any prior hint.","The Grand Commandant was among the highest-ranking officials in the Outer Court, second only to the Emperor. Along with the \"Chancellor\" and the \"Grand Secretary,\" they were known as the Three Excellencies. Although they were said to be equals, the Grand Commandant, who controlled military affairs, was implicitly the foremost of the Three Excellencies.","When Dong Zhou held absolute power over the court, he naturally wouldn't let the position of \"Grand Commandant\" fall to anyone else, so he held the post concurrently. However, he favored civil affairs over military ones. Compared to the murderous aura of a military officer, he preferred the elegant title of Chancellor. Therefore, he ordered people to address him externally as \"Chancellor Dong.\"","Now that the powerful Chancellor had fled, both the positions of Chancellor and Grand Commandant were vacant.","Dai Li thought to herself that this Empress Dowager Wang was quite imaginative.","Rather than being forced to confer titles, it was better to grasp the initiative in her own hands. And the meaning of \"his noble rank and fief shall continue from generation to generation without end\" was: the meritorious subject's noble rank and fief would be passed down from generation to generation, never to be cut off.","But Grand Commandant was only an official position, not a noble rank; only kingships and the twenty ranks of nobility were. Qin Shaozong was only appointed Grand Commandant for quelling the rebellion and destroying traitors this time. Logically, there was no need to mention a noble rank, as it was not a new conferment.","The edict not only mentioned it but also added the phrase \"from generation to generation without end,\" implying that he would forever be a subject, from generation to generation, which could be considered a combination of grace and authority to keep him in a subordinate position.","After the edict was read, Qin Shaozong cupped his hands to express his gratitude, only saying, \"Thank Your Majesty for your appreciation,\" without any intention of kneeling.","The officials on both sides remained silent; no one dared to jump out and find fault. The young emperor sitting above was wooden and dull, while the woman listening to the government from behind the bead curtain seemed furious, causing the bead curtain to sway slightly as she touched it. But in the end, she said nothing, only ordering people to continue reading the edicts.","Next was the edict conferring a title upon Dai Li.","\"...The so-called prosperity of the state relies entirely on the fragrance of virtuous vessels. The keel waterwheel appeared in the countryside, bestowing grace upon the roads; this is truly the merit of Lady Dai. Her exemplary virtue and splendid conduct can inspire the customs. Today, We confer upon her the title of Lord of Wuling with an appanage of two thousand five hundred households, and a fief in Wuling, to commend her labor...\"","Hearing Wuling, Dai Li was stunned.","She knew there was a high probability that conferring a lordship would come with a fief, but she hadn't expected her fief to actually be in Wuling.","The Wuling of this era, because of its many mountainous and hilly areas, had agricultural technology that was backward compared to the Central Plains. Consequently, grain production was limited, and the population was relatively sparse.","But these were not that important; the important thing was that Wuling was in... Jingzhou!","This fief was deep in Jingzhou, in the territory of that Liu of Jingzhou. It was equivalent to digging a piece of meat out of Liu Zhan's stomach to give to her.","She had been made a lord and had a fief, but it also seemed like she hadn't. It was just a nice-sounding title, making her one of the rare female lords of the Great Yan Dynasty, but she had no real power. After all, the fief was in Wuling, too far away for her; she couldn't reach it at all.","Dai Li lowered her eyes. Just as Qin Shaozong had done earlier, she copied his answer now, only thanking the holy grace without kneeling.","Whether it was because they thought she was too arrogant, or because it was rare for a woman to attend court, or for some other reason, Dai Li only felt more gazes falling upon her.","The officials were lined up in the luxurious and grand hall. Although it was morning and the sunlight was bright, a murky mist seemed to rise around them.","In the eyes of the dark figures whose bellies were round and fat from feeding on the fat of the people, green light flickered. They were resentful, fearful, greedy... like hyenas drooling foul saliva, wanting to share the food, yet afraid to approach.","Dai Li turned her head to take in the officials on both sides.","Yes, it wasn't her illusion; they were indeed all fat-headed and big-eared, their belts dragged down quite a bit by their fat bellies.","The conferment of rewards was not yet over. Next to receive a title was Nangong Xiong. He was given the position of Chancellor, unexpectedly standing alongside Qin Shaozong, one civil and one military, together ranking among the Three Excellencies, faintly showing a posture of rivalry.","As for the military officers under the command of the two men, Empress Dowager Wang also picked a few and gave them some painless rewards.","After the court session ended, the palace banquet followed.","The female family members of various households had already received notice and entered the palace at the appointed time. The court officials moved to the Southern Palace, where the upcoming palace banquet would be held.","Shi Rongyue did not follow Qin Yanzhou and Qin Qinian to listen to the conferment of titles, but she and Nangong Zijin were brought over for the latter half of the palace banquet.","The imperial city was exquisitely grand in every way; the beams were made of cloud-top sandalwood, the floors were paved with white Buckingham jade, and there were bright pearls and water jade serving as lamps everywhere in the halls, vividly displaying the word \"luxury.\"","Men and women were separated into different rooms; the women were in the east, and the men in the west. The east was hosted by Empress Dowager Wang, while the west was managed by the young emperor's maternal uncle, Wang Tianchuan.","\"Second Aunt,\" Shi Rongyue brought Nangong Zijin over.","Dai Li was in the first seat below, and the two young girls sat in the positions following hers.","The standard of the palace banquet was very high, with both cold and hot dishes. Beef, which was rare for ordinary wealthy families to see, was like cabbage here; every long table had a plate of it.","In addition, there was tea chicken, meat splashed with sauce, stir-fried shrimp roe, fragrant braised eel, and boiled pigeon soup. It truly included everything flying in the sky, running on the ground, and swimming in the water.","Empress Dowager Wang seemed unwell; she hastily ate her meal, said a few polite words, and unexpectedly left early.","As soon as she left, the atmosphere immediately became a bit more lively. Dai Li, who was already the center of attention, was like a piece of fragrant meat entering a wolf pack; people kept coming up to her table to strike up a conversation.","Not accepting calling cards?","Fine, then we'll talk at the palace banquet.","A woman with a face as round as a jade plate came forward with a wine goblet, smiling broadly. She introduced herself as the wife of the Grand Master of Ceremonies, surnamed Jiang. \"Marchioness... No, I should call you Lord of Wuling or the Grand Commandant's wife. You have just arrived in Chang'an, and I imagine there are many places you are not very familiar with. I wonder if I might have the honor of being your guide and answering some questions for you.\"","The official position of the Grand Master of Ceremonies was very high, second only to the Three Excellencies. Coming forward this time, Jiang Peilan's posture was very low.","But Dai Li still refused, smiling and saying, \"I'm afraid I won't have free time recently; maybe later.\"","The fact that she wanted to leave Chang'an was currently only known to Qin Changgeng. Even Zhouzhou didn't know, and she certainly wouldn't tell outsiders.","Whether Dai Li's \"later\" was true or false, Jiang Peilan immediately agreed anyway.","After Jiang Peilan, the mistresses of various households continued to find topics to chat with Dai Li, either inviting her to tour Chang'an together, recommending some treasured places in Chang'an, chatting about children, or flattering Qin Shaozong and the Northern Army...","Dai Li only felt a faint fragrance floating around, her eyes full of swaying golden lotuses. In the end, she couldn't take it anymore and left the banquet on the pretext of needing to use the restroom.","A foul place like a restroom wouldn't be right next to the banquet hall. Dai Li took Nianxia out of the Eastern Hall and followed a palace maid for about thirty paces before reaching their destination.","After using the restroom, Dai Li didn't want to go back so quickly, so she dismissed the accompanying palace maid and wandered around casually to catch her breath.","She walked aimlessly for a long time. Through the corridor, she saw two somewhat familiar figures approaching from a distance; both were noblewomen who had frequently spoken to her at the banquet earlier. Dai Li immediately felt a headache coming on, really not wanting to deal with them, so she took Nianxia back a few steps and hid in the corner of the palace.","\"She really is lucky. Taking her son with her into a second marriage, she still managed to snag a husband like that. Tsk, she clearly comes from a rustic background, yet now she climbs over our heads, almost ascending to the heavens in a single step.\"","\"She didn't choose him. I heard he sought her out himself. To marry her, he even broke a promise—it seems it was his first time going back on his word in all these years. But don't look at how unmatched her spotlight is now, ignoring us when we speak to her; in the future, she might just be swallowing a whole lot of bitter water.\"","\"What do you mean by that?\"","\"Her beauty is at its peak right now, truly crowning the capital, but what about in ten or twenty years? And men, well, they are all the same. When they see a prettier wildflower outside, they all want a taste. With all these gentle, submissive, beautiful, and fresh young women throwing themselves at him one after another, ready to be eaten just by opening his mouth, why wouldn't he?\"","\"That's true. Remember so-and-so back in the day? Childhood sweethearts with her husband, deeply in love, and they even said her husband would never take a concubine. Look at them now. I heard the Marquis of Pingliang's courtyard just welcomed its fifth young beauty. There will always be someone young and beautiful in Chang'an. When her beauty fades with age, where will her place be? She'll mostly just hear the new girls laughing, not to mention...\"","The two seemed to exchange a look, as if they both thought of a certain aspect.","\"Without a child, it's never secure. Besides, getting pregnant again at her age is very dangerous. Giving birth would cost half her life; she might even report straight to King Yama, saving herself the next ten years of glory altogether.\"","\"Indeed. With two sons in the family not born of the same mother, it will be a life-and-death struggle in the future...\"","\"Ah!\" one of the noblewomen suddenly exclaimed.","The other was startled. Just as she was about to complain to her friend, she saw the other's face turn pale as gold paper. Her heart skipped a beat, and she tremblingly looked over as well.","Not far away stood a stunningly beautiful woman in grand attire. Who else could it be but the very subject of their secret gossip?","Dai Li carefully looked at the faces of the two women. Without saying a single word, she left with Nianxia amidst the terrified pleas of the two women.","Nianxia was furious. As she passed by the two, she deliberately bumped them hard with her shoulder.","When had these noblewomen from prominent families ever been so offended by a maidservant? Their faces looked ugly for a moment, but they dared to be angry but not speak out.","\"Didn't she go back early? Why... why is she wandering around here? It's over. I finally managed to enter the palace with my eldest brother and sister-in-law. If they find out, I'll definitely be in deep trouble.\"","\"I told you long ago to be careful with your words and actions outside, but you just wouldn't listen. How do we clean this up now?\"","\"That's so unreasonable of you to say. You clearly chimed in with me just now.\"","...","Dai Li returned to the banquet, her expression the same as before.","Seeing her return, the noblewomen flocked forward to strike up conversations with her. Dai Li mentioned a few details about the appearances and clothing of the two women she had just encountered, and immediately someone reported their family backgrounds.","One was the sister-in-law of the Prefect of the Shangfang, and the other was the wife of the Prefect of the Capital Sikong. Both the Prefect of the Shangfang and the Prefect of the Capital Sikong were official positions managing royal affairs. In a situation where the ruler was strong and the ministers weak, these two positions would rise in status accordingly. But if it were the other way around, they would not be so popular or valued.","Dai Li gave a slight nod, indicating she understood. When others curiously inquired further, they only got the remark, \"These two have rather loose tongues,\" with no other evaluation.","There were quite a few shrewd people present. Hearing this, they immediately knew what was going on. They quickly agreed, their minds turning secretly.","They weren't important people to begin with, and now that the state of affairs had half changed, one needed to act even more carefully. They absolutely could not associate with those two families in the future...","As the golden sun slanted to the west, the grand palace banquet slowly came to a close.","After the banquet, the crowd dispersed and returned home.","The group returned to the manor. Just as Dai Li was about to step down from the carriage, she heard Qin Qinian and Qin Yanzhou whispering outside.","\"Second Brother, Chang'an is truly extraordinary. How about we go out to explore the markets tomorrow? The treasure pavilions here must be incomparable to Yuyang's. We might even find a few good weapons.\"","\"I have classes tomorrow, so I'm afraid I won't have free time. Don't you have classes?\" Qin Yanzhou replied.","\"I do, but only in the morning. Because Mr. Sheng didn't come to Chang'an, my afternoon classes are canceled, hehehe.\" The youth's tone became noticeably merrier towards the end.","Qin Yanzhou suggested, \"Actually, you could talk to Mr. Cui and have him schedule your afternoon time as well.\"","\"No way. Why would I ask for hardship when things are fine? I'll just leave the afternoon open for now and wait for the teacher to arrange things. Shh, Father is coming. We can't talk about this.\" Qin Qinian quickly shut his mouth.","Dai Li emerged from the carriage. \"Whether he heard it or not, I certainly know about it now.\"","Qin Qinian shuddered all over, as if struck on the head with a club. He pleaded, \"Mother...\"","Dai Li responded with an unreadable tone.","At this time, Qin Shaozong, returning in high spirits from riding, approached. His gaze swept over his two sons, pausing slightly on Qin Qinian, making the latter break out in a sweat. However, he didn't say anything, only asking Dai Li, \"Did you enjoy the palace banquet today, Madam?\"","He and the two brothers had been dining in the West Hall on the other side and were unaware of the situation in the East Hall.","Dai Li said truthfully, \"It was like entering a vegetable market. It felt as though I was the only one selling ingredients, and everyone was itching to come to me with money in hand.\"","Qin Shaozong chuckled. \"A fitting description.\"","The wind direction changed at that moment, and Dai Li suddenly caught a strong whiff of alcohol. She first sniffed towards Qin Shaozong, then turned to look at the two brothers. The setting sun reflected on their faces, dyeing them a shade of orange-red, making it impossible to tell their original color.","\"Have you all been drinking?\" she asked.","Qin Shaozong was probably quite relaxed today. He said boldly, \"How can there be no drinking on such a joyous day? Boys cannot be raised like girls secluded in their boudoirs, not touching a drop of alcohol. How will they share joy with thousands of soldiers in the future? Madam, do not be so restrictive.\"","Dai Li looked at Qin Yanzhou. The young man stood quietly, his left ear, untouched by the sunset, also bright red. She twitched her lips, casually said a few more words, and then left under the pretext of taking a walk to digest her meal.","But though she claimed it was to digest her meal, Dai Li wasn't just taking a stroll. She didn't even bring a maidservant, going alone to Nalan Zhi's courtyard.","Seeing Dai Li visit at sunset, Nalan Zhi showed surprise but swiftly invited her into the room and brewed tea for her. \"May I ask what brings the Lady of the house to my humble abode in person?\"","\"There are some matters weighing on my heart that I cannot figure out no matter how hard I think. I could only come to bother you, Sir, to seek an answer. I hope you will tell me everything you know truthfully.\" Dai Li knelt and sat opposite him at the low table.","Nalan Zhi sat upright and proper. \"I will certainly tell you everything I know.\"","Dai Li said, \"Because of various past events, I once asked you, Sir, to guide Zhouzhou, to help him step out of his isolated island and blend in with people. You did an excellent job; he indeed became much livelier later on, and I will be forever grateful to you. After Zhouzhou reached his crowning age of adulthood, he told me that you changed your previous teaching style and started lecturing him on the Book of Changes, the Great Learning, and the Book of Rites. When I learned of this, by coincidence, I had the chance to ask the Marquis face-to-face if your actions were instructed by him. He admitted it, but he told me, how could the son of the Marquis of Wu'an only know a few words?\"","Daili took a deep breath. Sir, do you think that is all there is to it? Are these principles of cultivating oneself, managing the family, and governing the state really just for practicing calligraphy, without any ulterior motives?","The small stove brewing tea beside them emanated a warm mist. After Daili's words fell, the only sound in the room with its wide-open doors was the bubbling of the boiling water.","Silence, a silence that made Daili's heart tremble, began to spread.","After a long while, she heard a sigh.","There probably are, Nalan Zhi said.","In that instant, all of Daili's hesitation, struggle, fear, and unease... all those complex emotions twisted together like a rope were suddenly plunged into ice water, and then poured right over her head.","The golden hairpin at the woman's temple trembled ceaselessly.","She opened her mouth, but on her first attempt, only a breath of air came out. Her throat was parched to the extreme, as if a fire were burning inside. Only on her second attempt did Daili find her voice. Sir, what do you think Qin Changgeng is planning?","She no longer cared about addressing Qin Shaozong respectfully as the Marquis in front of an outsider.","Nalan Zhi shook his head and said, Whether in employing people or marching into battle, the Lord's actions have always been unconventional. He dared to use a branded criminal like myself; he also dared to lead troops along treacherous mountain paths, deep into uninhabited lands, and finally descend unexpectedly upon the rear of Bairi Pass. Therefore, I do not know the answer to your question. As a subordinate, I can only follow orders.","Before Daili married Qin Shaozong, she and Nalan Zhi had spoken often about refining fine salt, and over time, they had become good friends.","Now, Nalan Zhi offered her a heartfelt truth, Whether the Lord is doing this intentionally or not, the path of Chongle will not be an easy one to walk."]},{"number":167,"title":"Chapter 167","paragraphs":["Even though she was mentally prepared, hearing Nalan Zhi confirm that Zhou Zhou's future was perilous still made Daili dizzy.","Perhaps noticing Daili's pale complexion, Nalan Zhi comforted her, \"Madam, truthfully, no matter what happens, your position will only become more secure. Not to mention Chongle's great contributions in the decisive victory against the Xuzhou army, your previous achievements with the dragon-bone water wheel, the salt stones, and the unheard-of fertile soil are all your merits. No one can deny this...\"","The Madam indeed had not borne the Lord any children, but if a woman was outstanding, her value would far exceed that of ordinary women who only knew how to bear and raise children in the backyard.","Nalan Zhi continued, \"The Lord has never altered or concealed your hard work. He even frequently posts notices to inform the public. Therefore, if there is an abundant harvest this autumn, Madam, you will have bestowed a great blessing upon the people of the world, and even upon future generations. This alone is enough to leave your name in the annals of history.\"","\"Right and wrong, merits and faults, will naturally be judged by later generations, but the present is the present,\" Daili sighed.","Nalan Zhi, however, said in a low voice, \"But you must know that a single word of praise is more glorious than a royal robe; a single word of censure is more severe than an axe. The brush of the historian is sharper than any sword.\"","The water in the pot boiled. Nalan Zhi lifted the clay pot off the charcoal stove and began to brew tea. The hot mist billowed out more intensely, like a spreading veil.","Daili looked at him through the mist and suddenly understood the unspoken meaning in Nalan Zhi's words.","No matter what happened to the two children in the future, whether they fought until their eyes turned red, or one of them was defeated and eliminated, it would not affect her status.","Because she had already left her name in history. She was no longer just the ordinary wife of some warlord, but her own name. This name extended countless invisible threads, flying into the homes of ordinary people and tying themselves to millions of commoners.","An invisible, heavy weight and a layer of glittering golden gauze floated over and enveloped her. Even if there was a storm of blood and rain outside, that golden gauze woven from her merits would be enough to ensure her peace and prosperity for the rest of her life.","It was as if sparks had fallen onto her eye sockets, burning so much that Daili's heart surged with emotion, a tangle of countless thoughts.","She blinked rapidly, trying to wipe away that unusual emotion, and hastily picked up her teacup, blowing gently on the scalding tea to keep herself busy.","Nalan Zhi then spoke of other things, \"Hai Qing comes from the Hedong Cui clan, a descendant of a prominent family. When the Lord initially mentioned Hai Qing and Chong Liang, he said they were already making plans and calculations for the Third Young Master. Meanwhile, Chongle has no one by his side. Since I have become his teacher, it is only right that I plan for him.\"","Daili stopped blowing, and the ripples in the teacup quickly returned to calm. She stared for a moment before saying, \"So after that, you started teaching Zhou Zhou books like the Great Learning?\"","He repeated his previous statement, \"As a subordinate, I can only act according to orders.\"","But he added a slightly emphasized sentence, \"Madam, although Chongle is not the Lord's biological son, as long as you are still here, he is not without a chance of winning.\"","This involved all aspects and far too many things. Even Nalan Zhi could not deny that his Lord, who possessed the ambition to ride the clouds and transform into a dragon and was decisive in killing, cared for his wife to an extraordinary degree.","Daili's lips parted slightly, but ultimately she shook her head. \"Having a chance of winning doesn't mean a guaranteed victory. This matter might succeed, or it might not. Sir, rather than obtaining the great throne after wading through rivers of blood and walking a long and perilous path, I would much rather Zhou Zhou live a smooth, peaceful, and worry-free life.\"","She had already lost her child once, suffering from endless nightmares and sleepless nights.","These dark and gray pasts were like evil spirits locked in a box. Even the slightest recollection brought piercing pain and an everlasting terror.","Nalan Zhi fell silent.","Daili smiled bitterly, \"Qinian is not my biological son, but after spending the past half year together, I know he is a good child, and I truly treat him as family. If Zhou Zhou and I were not here, there would be no competition whatsoever, and he wouldn't even have the possibility of falling into a terrible situation in the future.\"","Before coming to Great Yan, she was just an ordinary citizen, not a bureaucrat, a politician, or a privileged aristocrat. But history is a mirror; it reflects the past and can also faintly project the future.","Once the war of succession began, in the best-case scenario, the loser would be placed under house arrest until death, losing their freedom for life. In the worst-case scenario, not only would the loser be uprooted entirely, but it would also implicate hundreds of thousands of people, and the repercussions could last for a century...","Just like the Rebellion of the Eight Princes in the Western Jin Dynasty, the victims were countless. The social economy suffered a massive blow, and it was even seen as the beginning of the Uprising of the Five Barbarians. Its malicious and far-reaching impact still sends shivers down the spines of later generations.","Granted, Qin Changgeng currently only had two sons, not enough to gather two tables of mahjong like the Rebellion of the Eight Princes, but Daili still did not want to see brothers turn against each other, causing the common people to suffer alongside them.","Nalan Zhi, who had been silent for a long time, raised his eyes. \"Madam, you are wrong about one thing. Even without Chongle, the Lord's achievements might not necessarily be inherited by the Third Young Master.\"","Daili looked at Nalan Zhi in surprise.","A breeze blew from somewhere, brushing away the dust in her memories. She was suddenly pulled back to the day of her son's capping ceremony—no, it should be the night of the capping ceremony.","After returning from the Marquis's mansion, Qin Changgeng was nowhere to be found. She searched the estate and later found him in a courtyard pavilion where weapons were stored.","The room was filled with the smell of alcohol, and the man seemed somewhat drunk. Rarely, he spoke to her about his past.","He also said that Yun Ce had reunited with his biological father. He said, \"Yun Ce said he was sorry to me, that he disappointed me and failed to live up to my cultivation over the years. But if he knew that my older brother died because of me back then, he wouldn't have said such words.\"","At that time, Daili's focus had been on the second half of the sentence, but now, reminded by Nalan Zhi, she finally realized...","Cultivation?","If it was just ordinary cultivation, even if Yun Ce apologized verbally, why would Qin Changgeng take it so hard? Why would he be so depressed that he poured his heart out to her?","So it was definitely not ordinary cultivation!","\"He wanted Yun Ce to succeed him?\" Daili was shocked, but after the shock passed, she inexplicably felt that this was indeed something Qin Changgeng would do.","Nalan Zhi nodded slightly. Having served the North for many years, there were some things he could clearly see. \"That is why I said earlier, the Lord has always acted in an unconventional manner.\"","\"But you said earlier that Mr. Cui and Mr. Sheng were already making plans for Qinian. Could it be that they haven't noticed Qin Changgeng's intentions?\" Daili expressed deep suspicion.","\"Of course not,\" Nalan Zhi gave a negative reply. \"They are the teachers of the Third Young Master. Naturally, they will rack their brains to plan for him—for him, and for themselves.\"","Daili's breath hitched, suddenly recalling the Xuanwu Gate Incident in history. At that time, the person who opened the city gates for Li Shimin was Chang He, a subordinate of his older brother, Li Jiancheng.","And Chang He was the captain of the guards at Xuanwu Gate at the time. After the Xuanwu Gate Incident, he was promoted step by step to the Governor of Qianzhou. In modern terms, a gatekeeping captain of the guards eventually got promoted to the governor of a major province.","What did they rely on? The merit of supporting the emperor's ascension!","Dai Li sighed, a complex, indistinguishable emotion escaping with that breath.","Yun Ce had withdrawn from the competition, but so what? They had just gone around in circles only to return to where they started. The problem remained unsolved.","Nalan Zhi kept his eyes on Dai Li's expression.","\"Madam, have you ever told Chongle what you are thinking and planning in your heart?\"","\"Sir, how should I break this stalemate? Could I simply leave...\"","The two voices sounded at the same time, the former half a beat faster, so that the latter had to stop before finishing.","Both of them froze for a moment.","Nalan Zhi looked at Dai Li in astonishment. He had clearly heard the word \"leave,\" but he wasn't entirely sure if she meant what he guessed she did.","For a moment, neither spoke. Finally, Nalan Zhi said, \"Chongle has come of age and is an adult now. Why don't you ask him what he thinks and listen to his opinion?\"","Dai Li pursed her lips, avoiding Nalan Zhi's gaze, and simply thanked him for the reminder.","...","After finishing a cup of fragrant tea at Nalan Zhi's place, Dai Li took her leave.","It had been dusk when she arrived. Now, as she left, the sky was dark, and the firmament was dotted with stars, as beautiful as a painting.","The main room of the primary courtyard was brightly lit, indicating someone was inside.","Dai Li pushed the door open and entered. As expected, she saw Qin Shaozong sitting by the desk, reading a letter. Whether his good mood from being appointed as the Grand Commandant had lasted until now, or the contents of the letter pleased him, his expression was unusually gentle.","\"My wife has returned.\" Qin Shaozong waved her over. \"Yun Ce's letter just arrived. Tsk, I previously suggested so many noble ladies to him, and he rejected every single one. I actually thought the boy had no worldly desires and was ready to become a monk. It turns out the iron tree had blossomed long ago; he just didn't dare to say it.\"","The gloom in Dai Li's heart dispersed a little. She walked over and asked, \"What do you mean? Which family's young lady has caught his eye?\"","Qin Shaozong stretched out his long arm, scooped her up, and sat her sideways on his lap so they could read the letter together. \"It's the daughter of a merit officer's assistant, Lady Qiao. It turns out Lady Qiao and Yun Ce have known each other for a long time. However, Yun Ce was in poor health a few years ago. Believing he wouldn't recover and not wanting to burden Lady Qiao, and also feeling that his circumstances were too complicated, he didn't dare tell me, and let Lady Qiao marry someone else.\"","A merit officer's assistant was merely a subordinate to the merit officer. It would take several promotions to reach the level of the Colonel Director of Retainers; it wasn't a very high-ranking position.","Dai Li was even more surprised. Just as she was about to look closer at the letter, she heard the man beside her say, \"If Lady Qiao's husband hadn't died of illness, and since she had no children, she probably wouldn't have easily returned to the Qiao family. Who knows how long that boy Yun Ce would have had to wait. In my opinion, half of his sickness was caused by his own suppressed emotions. He hides everything in his heart—it's a wonder he didn't break down entirely. Look at him now, refreshed and energized by a happy event.\"","Dai Li's mouth twitched.","Someone's husband passing away from illness had somehow become a happy event in his mouth.","He then clicked his tongue in dissatisfaction. \"To think my Qin family has such a cowardly descendant. I don't know where our ancestors went wrong. Even if she couldn't be his primary wife at the time, he should have at least kept her by his side. How can a man just hand over the woman he fancies?\"","The more Dai Li listened, the more wrong it sounded. She turned her head and stared at Qin Shaozong.","Noticing Dai Li's gaze, the man, who had drunk quite a bit of wine today, paused and belatedly looked at her.","In the room illuminated by flickering candlelight, neither spoke. Their eyes met, and time seemed to slow down at this moment.","Ultimately, Qin Shaozong let out a low chuckle. He placed his hand on the back of Dai Li's neck, pressing her toward him, while he leaned in and kissed the small, crimson mole between her brows. \"A fair and graceful lady is a gentleman's good mate.\"","Dai Li turned her head away. \"Since Yun Ce wrote to inform you, he and Lady Qiao must have mutual feelings. When we return to Yuyang, his marriage must be settled.\"","Qin Shaozong smiled in agreement. \"Marriage is good. That boy is finally settling down. I'll be able to give an account to my eldest brother and sister-in-law.\"","Knock, knock. Someone knocked on the door outside.","Nianxia's voice rang out, \"My Lord, Mr. Ding sent someone over with a medicinal brew, saying you should drink it while it's hot.\"","Dai Li stood up from Qin Shaozong's lap and walked over to open the door, only to see Nianxia outside holding a small wooden food box.","\"What kind of medicine is this?\" Dai Li smelled a strong herbal scent.","Nianxia shook her head, saying she didn't know. She only explained that she had bumped into Ding Lianxi's servant on her way back to the main courtyard. The servant had asked her to bring the food box over, saying it was for the Lord.","Dai Li carried the item back inside. \"Qin Changgeng, are you injured?\"","The smell of medicine was so strong that she knew what was inside without even opening it. But in her memory, other than that time he returned late at night from the Changle Pavilion with injuries, he had always managed to retreat completely unscathed, even when he personally donned armor to fight against the imperial coalition army.","Why did he suddenly need to drink medicine?","\"I'm not injured,\" he replied. \"This medicine was just prescribed by Congjian to condition my body. He's always nagging in my ear about the ways of health preservation. My ears are getting calluses from listening to him. I couldn't stand his pestering, so I'll just drink it casually.\"","Dai Li was suspicious, feeling that his words were strange.","Having lived with Qin Changgeng for so long, this was the first time she had seen him drink this kind of medicine. And if he had previously refused to drink it even when his ears were callused from the nagging, why was he willing to do it now?","Opening the food box, Qin Shaozong took out the medicine bowl from inside.","The medicine in the bowl was pitch black and had an extremely pungent smell. Just catching a whiff of it made the tip of Dai Li's tongue feel bitter. He seemed to feel the same way; after taking out the bowl, he kept his hand in the holding position but didn't bring it to his lips.","Seeing this, Dai Li was amused. \"So you're actually afraid of bitterness.\"","\"A true man fears nothing. What is there to be afraid of?\" Qin Shaozong said disdainfully.","Dai Li: \"Then drink it.\"","Qin Shaozong put down the bowl. \"It's a bit hot. I'll wait a moment.\"","\"Since Mr. Ding instructed you to drink it while it's hot, its efficacy will surely diminish if it cools down. If you get half the result with twice the effort, you'll have to drink two bowls to make up for it.\" After saying this, Dai Li ignored him and picked up the letter on the desk to read carefully.","Qin Shaozong stared fixedly at the black bowl, and after a moment, he suddenly looked at Dai Li.","Looking at a beauty by lamplight, the more you look, the more charming she appears. Her cold, glamorous, and elegant features were traced by the soft light. With her dark eyelashes half-lowered, her perfectly shaped peach-blossom eyes seemed to shimmer with a precious light. She was graceful, elegant, and breathtakingly beautiful.","Qin Shaozong picked up the medicine bowl. He kept looking at Dai Li, seemingly treating her as some kind of sweet candied fruit, and downed the medicinal brew in one gulp while gazing at her.","It seemed to be truly foul-tasting. Qin Shaozong's long eyebrows knotted together. He endured it for two breaths but ultimately couldn't hold back, grabbing a teacup to wash it down. \"Did that Ding Congjian add goldthread to this?\"","Dai Li teased him. \"Mr. Ding is doing this for your own good. How can you have the nerve to secretly question his painstaking efforts?\"","Qin Shaozong saw her eyes curve in a smile; she looked genuinely happy.","So, his discomfort was what made her happy?","Setting the teacup down with a sharp clack, Qin Shaozong strode over, pulled Dai Li into his arms, and kissed her fiercely. He had just finished his medicine; even though he had followed it with a cup of tea, his mouth was still incredibly bitter.","An indescribable bitterness flooded over, burning through Dai Li's mouth like a raging fire. It meticulously swept over every inch—her soft tongue, her pearly teeth, not even sparing her gums.","As if that were not enough, his thickly calloused thumb pressed firmly against her throat, stroking it repeatedly to coax her into swallowing.","The bitter taste was so overwhelming that it made Dai Li's very heart tremble.","When the kiss finally ended, the smile had transferred to Qin Shaozong's face. Holding her in his arms, he laughed heartily. \"My wife truly shares in my bitterness as well as my sweetness.\"","\"I was only kindly urging you to finish your medicine quickly so as not to waste someone else's good intentions. You really are unreasonable, biting the hand that feeds you.\" Dai Li tried to push him away.","Qin Shaozong did not let go. \"You cannot say that. You bear half the responsibility for this medicine, my lady.\"","\"What does it have to do with me? Let go of me, I need to drink some water.\" Dai Li gave him a hard pinch.","This time, he released his grip.","Dai Li poured herself a cup of water. Just as she was bringing the rim to her lips, she heard him say, \"Since I promised you that we would grow old together and weather the cold winters of life as one, naturally, I cannot break my promise halfway.\"","Dai Li froze, recalling the day he had returned from the Changle Courtyard.","After fighting outside all night, the man had come straight to her. His armor was shattered, his black robes torn to shreds. When his clothes were peeled away, several cuts, both deep and shallow, were oozing blood—he had nearly been sliced to ribbons.","She had told him then that, under normal circumstances, men have shorter lifespans than women. He had angrily dismissed her words as absurd.","But looking at it now, he had actually taken those words to heart...","Dai Li slowly lowered her eyes, letting out a silent, melancholy sigh."]},{"number":168,"title":"Chapter 168","paragraphs":["The brilliant afternoon sunlight poured into the room, illuminating the elegant house and making it even brighter. In the corner, a hollowed-out peony incense burner curled with fragrant smoke, adding a faint scent to the entire room.","Footsteps approached from outside.","Soon, a young man wearing a white robe and a scholar's cap stepped into the main room. At a glance, he saw the woman sitting by the desk. All the maidservants in the room had been dismissed, leaving only the two of them. Mother, you were looking for me?","Qin Yanzhou knelt on the other side of the desk.","Daili looked at her son across the desk, slightly dazed.","When she first sent him to school, he was just a nine-year-old child, carrying a cartoon backpack and a small water bottle around his neck. She hadn't expected him to grow up so quickly in the blink of an eye.","He was taller than her, with broader shoulders. The chubby baby fat from her memory had faded from his face, replaced by clear lines and sharp features.","But, there was no helping it; no matter how old Zhouzhou grew, he would always be a child in her heart.","Mother, did you not rest well last night? What is troubling you? Qin Yanzhou noticed the faint dark circles under her eyes.","Normally, his mother was radiant, even on the night they broke out of Chang'an city. When had she ever looked as haggard as a wilted peony like she did today?","He didn't know if it was an illusion, but he sensed a deep unease radiating from her. This unease seemed to peak as the melancholy in her eyes deepened and the hesitation between her brows slowly turned into resolve.","Daili didn't answer his question. Instead, she asked softly, Zhouzhou, if I were to leave Qin Changgeng and the North, would you come with me?","Why... why would you ask that? Qin Yanzhou's pupils suddenly shrank, and he flew into a rage, no longer referring to Qin Shaozong as father. Did the Marquis of Wu'an make some sort of demand of you?","He thought of the palace banquet yesterday.","They received their titles together, but for the latter half of the banquet, men and women were seated separately. He had gone to the West Hall to dine with the other young masters. Their side hosted a feast in the name of celebration. The hall was filled with fine wine, dancing girls sang and danced, and many men gradually lost themselves in the alcohol.","After a few rounds of drinks, someone stepped forward with a cup to toast that man. The flattery and sycophancy were obvious, and some even took the opportunity of praising him to offer gifts.","The generous gifts varied, including aged fine wines, precious gems and jade, fine steeds, and scantily clad dancing girls...","Could it be that the man's refusal yesterday was just a superficial act to save face, while he was actually tempted, just waiting to go back and settle things with his mother before happily welcoming beautiful women into the manor?","Qin Yanzhou could only think of this reason.","The original agreement only had three clauses. Two involved the children, and one was to constrain the partner. If there was a problem with the children's education, signs would have appeared early on. Why wait until today?","That left only the first clause: the Marquis of Wu'an had a new lover, or perhaps he was itching to have one.","That was what provoked his mother to leave!","Daili hadn't expected Qin Yanzhou to react so strongly, and her mind couldn't keep up for a moment. What demand?","Qin Yanzhou had been burning with anger, but seeing Daili's pure confusion without a trace of grief or sorrow, his anger subsided by half. After he returned from the palace banquet yesterday, didn't he make a demand of you?","Daili's expression shifted slightly. She wasn't slow-witted. Thinking of her son's sudden fury followed by his careful probing, she suddenly remembered that divorce agreement.","Did Zhouzhou misunderstand?","Daili didn't know whether to laugh or cry, but her heart felt warm. Her expression softened. He didn't make any demands of me, and I don't want to leave because of that.","Qin Yanzhou was puzzled. Then why?","Daili looked out the window. The daylight was bright, and the leisurely chirping of birds drifted in. This manor was not located in a particularly secluded place, and the faint hustle and bustle from outside could still be heard.","The mortal world was bustling, and the years were peaceful.","Many thoughts flashed through Daili's mind one by one. She remembered Nalan Zhi suggesting yesterday that she ask for Zhouzhou's opinion.","Daili looked at the tall and straight young man in front of her and finally shook her head. No reason.","She had thought about it all night and felt that seeking out Nalan Zhi had been completely unnecessary. On this matter, as Zhouzhou's teacher, not only could he not give her any useful advice, but he would even interfere with her.","Look, this was what it meant to be a pawn in the game, forced to quietly and inevitably walk the predetermined path. Just as he himself had said, As a subordinate, one can only follow orders.","Moreover, Zhouzhou had knelt before her twice, not only breaking his usual silence but also kowtowing to her, all just to don armor and go to battle.","So did that question really have any meaning?","It didn't, and there was no need to ask, because she already knew the answer.","Mother...","Zhouzhou, you just need to answer me. If... I say if, I were to leave Qin Shaozong, would you come with me? Daili's voice was very soft.","Qin Yanzhou couldn't understand why, since his father hadn't done anything wrong, his mother still wanted to leave. Where exactly did things go wrong? Did something important happen recently that he didn't know about?","And leave? Leave here, and go where?","Did his father know she wanted to leave?","Question after question followed, making Qin Yanzhou's head split with pain. Many faces flashed through his mind: his father's, his teacher's, his younger brother's, and also... a girl holding the little dog Xiaobai, smiling as sweetly as malt sugar.","But in the end, all the faces faded away, leaving only the person in front of him the clearest.","Qin Yanzhou's complex emotions gradually smoothed out, and his gaze became firm. Of course I will go with you. Mother, are you unhappy living here?","Daili's vision suddenly blurred, and tears filled her eyes.","With those achievements of hers, even if Qi Nian was the ultimate victor in the battle for the throne, it would guarantee her a life of luxury in the future.","She knew exactly what the decision to leave meant. It meant that Qin Shaozong's future glory would have nothing to do with her, that the days of living a privileged life would be gone, that she would live a very frugal life for the rest of her days, and that she would be going against her ideal of helping the world when successful.","But none of this outweighed her child's life.","And this act, which she didn't know if it could be defined as self-sacrifice, no longer mattered when she heard her child's concern.","Yes, I'm unhappy. I worry every day, Daili answered.","Seeing the cloud of sorrow over her face, Qin Yanzhou asked in confusion, What are you worried about?","Round and round, they returned to the root cause.","Daili smiled bitterly and shook her head, not mentioning a word about the reason. Zhouzhou, just treat what I just told you as a secret between us mother and son. Don't mention it to anyone.","Qin Yanzhou nodded and agreed, his thoughts turning a few corners at the same time. It seemed his father didn't know about this, and from his mother's tone, once his father found out, he definitely wouldn't let her leave.","The young man slowly lowered his eyes.","...","Walking out of the main courtyard, Qin Yanzhou looked back. His dark eyes took in a small portrait where time had settled many people and events.","A moment later, he withdrew his gaze and left.","*","Brother Zhongle? Shi Rongyue looked in surprise at Qin Yanzhou, who had come looking for her on his own initiative.","Xiaobai, who had been circling at her feet, recognized him. It let out a woof and trotted over happily.","It was still very young, a tiny little ball. Its fur was puffed up, making its legs look especially short. When it ran over, it looked like its chassis was scraping the ground as it hovered along.","Qin Yanzhou leaned over and scooped up the puppy, holding it in his arms. He first rubbed the dog's head a couple of times, petting it until its little tail wagged fast enough to fan up a breeze. Then, he bounced it in his hands a couple of times and evaluated seriously, \"Xiaobai has gotten heavier.\"","Shi Rongyue was delighted. \"Of course he's heavier. Un... Xiaobai eats very hard, having several meals a day!\"","Xiaobai barked twice, lifting his little head high as if filled with pride.","After playing with the dog for a while longer, Qin Yanzhou finally put Xiaobai down. \"Rongrong, regarding the palace banquet yesterday, there are some things I want to ask you about.\"","Shi Rongyue was surprised. \"What is it?\"","Qin Yanzhou asked, \"During the banquet, did my mother encounter anything unusual or anyone specific?\"","Shi Rongyue subconsciously shook her head. \"I don't think so. Second Aunt was sitting right next to me yesterday. Many people at the banquet tried to strike up a conversation with her, but they all kept their boundaries and only offered praises...\"","\"No, wait, there was one thing that was rather unusual.\" As she spoke, she suddenly corrected herself. \"Halfway through, Second Aunt left the table to use the restroom. After she came back, she suddenly asked the people around about two noble ladies and described their appearances. The others naturally told her everything they knew. It turned out that one of them was the sister-in-law of the Shangfang Director, and the other was the wife of the Grand Minister of Works.\"","Qin Yanzhou pressed further, \"What happened next?\"","\"There were quite a few nosy people at the time. After all, Second Aunt hadn't paid much attention to anyone since entering the banquet, so they all asked for the reason. Second Aunt said that those two gossiped too much, and said nothing else after that,\" Shi Rongyue said.","Qin Yanzhou furrowed his long eyebrows tightly.","He understood his mother. She had always been a gentle and dignified woman. Unless she was severely offended, she would never embarrass others in public.","Those two must have said something...","Shi Rongyue couldn't bear to see his brows locked in a frown. Just as she was getting anxious, a flash of inspiration suddenly struck her. \"That's right! Brother Zhongle, I remember Nianxia was following Second Aunt at the time. If you want to know what those two said, perhaps you can go ask Nianxia.\"","Hearing this, the young man smoothed his brows. \"Thank you, Rongrong.\"","*","Having made up her mind to leave with her son, Dai Li began to prepare. Nianxia and Bipo were great helpers, but unfortunately, she couldn't take them along. She had to pack up quietly by herself.","However, compared to that, what was more important right now was getting Qin Shaozong to relent and let her return to Yuyang first.","That man was extremely sharp; his ears would perk up at the slightest sign of trouble. Back when she fled from Nankang, she was still caught and brought back in this ancient era where finding someone was incredibly inconvenient.","She absolutely could not let him notice anything.","At dusk, the couple returned to their room together after finishing dinner. As soon as she got back, Dai Li rummaged through her box, found Qin Yunce's previous letter, and then took out the little booklet she had compiled with records on soil fertilization.","\"Qin Changgeng, I am going back to Yuyang in a couple of days.\" Dai Li didn't ask if it was okay; instead, she brought up the old topic and directly told him she was going back.","Qin Shaozong paused his motion of pouring tea. \"Back to Yuyang?\"","Dai Li waved the letter paper in her hand at him, silently apologizing to Yunce in her heart. \"Yes, I want to go back to Yuyang first. Yunce's marriage has finally shown some promise, so it's better to settle it early. Besides, if we set off recently, it will be exactly autumn when we return to Yuyang. After the harvest, a new round of composting needs to be done, and time cannot be delayed. Meanwhile, Chang'an is newly settled, and it wouldn't be right to have no person in charge here. You definitely have to stay here, so I thought about it, and it's best if we split up and go our separate ways.\"","The process of getting married in this era was very complicated. Unlike modern times where one could just go to the Civil Affairs Bureau, they had to go through the Three Letters and Six Rites before they could become husband and wife.","Qin Shaozong put down the teapot and said nothing.","Seeing him like this, Dai Li knew that the matter could be negotiated within today or tomorrow. If this man disagreed, he would absolutely reject it outright instead of keeping silent.","Dai Li continued, casually painting him a beautiful picture of the future. \"Zhouzhou and I will go back to Yuyang first. You stay in Chang'an with Qinian and Rongrong. Once you finish handling the affairs in Chang'an, you can bring them north, and we can bid farewell to the old year and welcome the new spring together.\"","Perhaps moved by her last sentence, the man finally replied with an \"Mm\" after quite a long while.","Dai Li let out a breath. Just as the heavy stone in her heart fell, she heard Qin Shaozong say, \"Madam, take Qinian and Rongrong along with you.\"","\"That's not appropriate,\" Dai Li subconsciously refused.","Qin Shaozong raised his long eyebrows slightly. \"Why is it not appropriate?\"","Dai Li tried hard to find an excuse. \"You are so busy in Chang'an, you should keep more people by your side who can share your burdens. Plus, Qinian's teacher, Mr. Cui, is still in Chang'an. If Qinian leaves with me, he won't be able to attend his future classes.\"","Qin Shaozong thought for a moment. \"Then take Rongrong with you.\"","Dai Li hesitated. \"Rongrong seems to be good friends with Sixth Miss Nangong next door. Along this journey, she finally has a girl playmate. If she goes back with me...\"","\"Hongying probably misses her. Let her go home early, and she can come back to play after the New Year.\" With just one sentence, Qin Shaozong blocked all the rest of Dai Li's words.","Parents missing their children eagerly was human nature.","Dai Li furrowed her delicate brows, instinctively feeling that this matter was a bit troublesome. She and Zhouzhou would leave on the way back to Yuyang, and the convoy would definitely have no peace because of it. She didn't want this matter to affect the other younger generation...","\"You don't like Rongrong?\" he suddenly asked.","Dai Li shook her head in astonishment. \"Nothing of the sort. Rongrong is great, I don't dislike her.\"","Qin Shaozong narrowed his long, narrow eyes. \"Then what was Madam thinking about just now?\"","Being looked at with such a slightly contemplative gaze, Dai Li's hairs stood on end. She felt like she could hear her blood rushing through her veins. \"Thinking about... things after the parting.\"","Qin Shaozong suddenly smiled, pulling her into his embrace with a chuckle. \"Since the pain of parting is so unbearable to endure, why doesn't Madam go back a little later? Send a letter to Yan San regarding the fertilizer first. He has always been steady in his actions and is reliable.\"","He still didn't want her to leave first.","\"No!\" Dai Li turned her head away. But just as she spoke, her waist and the back of her knees tightened, her feet left the ground, and she was scooped up entirely.","\"For the next few months, I will be sleeping alone in an empty, lonely chamber. I hope Madam can reward me in advance.\" Qin Shaozong carried her into the inner room.","With the parting already decided, Qin Shaozong was particularly fierce tonight, changing several positions in a row and still feeling it wasn't enough.","A fire burned in his eyes as he deeply gazed at the woman beneath him, her black hair scattered all over. Her dark eyelashes were half-wet and clumped together, and her flushed, jade-like face was radiantly beautiful. The bright lights of the inner room fell upon her flawless, creamy skin, seeming to illuminate the fine sheen of sweat.","Sweat beaded on the man's forehead. A drop rolled down his sharp, handsome face, and just as it was about to fall, it was wiped away by a soft, fair hand."]},{"number":169,"title":"Chapter 169","paragraphs":["The news that Dai Li was returning to the North spread like wildfire through the manor. The entire estate bustled with activity as everyone packed and prepared for the journey.","Inside her room, Dai Li listened to the sounds of carriages being loaded back and forth outside, occasionally glancing at the writing materials on her desk. After a long while, she finally closed her door, sat down at the desk, and began grinding ink.","Once the black ink was ready, she spread out a sheet of mulberry paper.","Picking up her brush, Dai Li wrote a letter to Qin Qinian in one smooth breath. Then, taking out a fresh sheet of paper, she carefully wrote three characters: \"Letter of Divorce.\"","This second letter wasn't long, but it took her quite some time to write, even ruining a piece of paper halfway through.","When the final stroke was laid down, Dai Li set aside her brush to let the ink dry. Her gaze fell on the paper, unfocused, simply lost in thought.","A knock on the door suddenly echoed.","\"Madam?\" It was Bipo. She had come to fetch something from the room, only to find the door not just closed, but locked.","Startled from her reverie, Dai Li called out \"Just a moment,\" then folded the now-dry letter.","The door opened.","Bipo quickly cast a sidelong glance inside, but seeing everything looked normal, she suppressed her curiosity. Not daring to ask why her mistress had locked the door, she merely asked for instructions. After receiving a negative reply, Bipo resumed her packing.","She muttered to herself, wondering why both her mistress and Nianxia had been acting so strangely lately. Her mistress was one thing—she was a noble lady with many important and busy affairs, so it wasn't surprising if she encountered some tricky matters.","But Nianxia? They were both servants, and their daily tasks were almost identical. Logically, Nianxia shouldn't be acting this way. Could something special have happened without her knowing?","Nianxia had refused to speak earlier, but hmph, she would find time to interrogate her properly.","Bipo mused idly.","This waiting continued until all the luggage was packed and the procession was ready to depart.","\"Madam, Qin San will also accompany you back to Yuyang,\" Qin Shaozong announced as soon as he entered the room.","Dai Li was surprised. \"Why? Qinian can help you in Chang'an. There's no need for him to return to Yuyang, is there?\"","Qin Shaozong waved it off dismissively. \"That boy runs wild all day. It's a miracle if he doesn't cause trouble. We have no use for him here, so he might as well go back with you.\"","Dai Li frowned slightly, almost imperceptibly. \"But Qinian's studies...\"","\"Without merit to keep him in Chang'an, Qin the Second hasn't been attending classes either,\" Qin Shaozong cut her off.","Hearing his resolute tone, Dai Li knew there was little room for negotiation. \"Alright,\" she agreed first, then asked, \"What about Qinian's own thoughts? Is he willing to go back to Yuyang with me?\"","Qin Shaozong let out a soft scoff. \"He doesn't have to attend classes for a while. That boy is probably so happy he's forgotten his own surname.\"","Dai Li: \"...\"","Qin Shaozong looked around the master bedroom, noticing how empty it felt now that the luggage had been moved to the carriages.","This kind of emptiness had accompanied him every day before his marriage, for over a decade. Yet, returning to it after just a year, he found it incredibly unfamiliar, even uncomfortable.","He furrowed his long brows but said nothing.","Dai Li glanced at a certain chest belonging to Qin Shaozong, thinking that since Qinian was traveling with her, she should retrieve the letter she had prepared for him.","No, perhaps she didn't need to.","The moon rose and set, and in the blink of an eye, a day passed, bringing the day of departure.","Today, Qin Shaozong personally escorted Dai Li out of the city. He didn't ride a horse, choosing instead to share her carriage. \"Although the route from Yuyang to Chang'an is now entirely under our Northern control, and all the major factions have been wiped out, there might still be some small bands of thieves roaming about. Since there's no rush, Madam, please avoid traveling at night.\"","\"The Black Cavalry can take on ten men each, not to mention there are a full four hundred of them escorting me to Yuyang. Thieves block roads to make a living, not to throw their lives away. What thief would dare cross our path?\" Dai Li changed the subject. \"Speaking of time, if I want to go sightseeing along the way, Qin Changgeng, you can't let Commander Bai stop me.\"","Four hundred guards—this number was even larger than when she and Qin Shaozong had traveled south. And this time, escorting her back to Yuyang was Bai Jianping, the Commander of the Southern Garrison of the Black Cavalry.","\"Of course.\" Qin Shaozong didn't think much of it. Stopping to admire majestic peaks or beautiful scenery during a journey was perfectly normal.","\"Then tell Commander Bai yourself.\" Dai Li lifted the curtain and called out for Bai Jianping.","Bai Jianping, confused, rode over. \"My Lady?\"","Dai Li nudged Qin Shaozong with her elbow, prompting him to say, \"On the journey back, follow Madam's instructions. If she wishes to go sightseeing, do not dissuade her.\"","Bai Jianping agreed.","Dai Li let go, and the curtain fell back into place.","\"Satisfied now?\" Qin Shaozong thought Dai Li had been cooped up for too long and was feeling playful, so he added, \"Once the world is at peace and the four seas are calm, I'll take you out to play to your heart's content.\"","Dai Li smiled but didn't say anything.","Qin Shaozong played with one of her hands. \"Madam, you can have someone send me letters along the way, and I will write back to you.\"","Dai Li said okay.","Perhaps because they were about to part, he spoke more than usual, giving her many instructions. When the carriage had traveled twenty miles out of Chang'an, Qin Shaozong said, \"I will definitely return to Yuyang before spring next year. By then, you'll have had your fill of fun on the road. After that, stay obediently in Yuyang and don't run around.\"","Dai Li just gave an \"mm,\" neither agreeing nor disagreeing.","He reached up, resting a hand on the back of her neck, and pulled her toward him until their foreheads were almost touching, face to face. \"What does 'mm' mean? Say 'okay,' say 'I will listen to my husband.'\"","His brown eyes were narrow and restrained, set beneath sharp, prominent brow bones. In the dim light of the carriage with the curtains drawn, his eyes looked even darker. When he stared at someone unblinkingly, they were like a deep pool with a swirling vortex.","Dai Li instinctively tried to turn her head away, but he held her firmly.","\"Why are you hiding? Are you feeling guilty, Madam?\" Qin Shaozong clicked his tongue softly.","Even knowing he might just be speaking casually, Dai Li's heart still pounded fiercely. She took a deep breath, exhaled slowly, and feigned helplessness. \"Okay, I will listen to my husband.\"","He was satisfied.","\"We've come twenty miles already. Let's part here,\" Dai Li said, looking at him, her voice softening. \"Since that matter requires careful planning, I hope you will eat well, be mindful of the changing seasons, balance work and rest, and take good care of yourself.\"","With every word she spoke, his gaze deepened, until it seemed as if they were back in last night's passion. Dark fire burned in his eyes, glowing brightly, as if ready to swallow her whole. \"Madam is truly stingy. Only at parting do you allow this gentle breeze of care to blow over me.\"","Dai Li looked away. \"Remember what I just said.\"","\"I will definitely remember.\"","Qin Shaozong stepped down from the carriage. He waited until the army was completely out of sight before mounting his Red Dragon. \"Let's go back.\"","*","After leaving Chang'an, Dai Li headed north as planned. They traveled for several days, passing through three small counties, before arriving at a small town called Tianchi.","As in the previous three stops, they first found a relay station and booked the entire place to rest.","In the evening, Dai Li said to Bai Jianping, \"Commander Bai, the local customs and scenery here are quite nice. There's no rush to continue our journey just yet. I plan to stroll around the town tomorrow.\"","Bai Jianping agreed without hesitation.","The next morning, Dai Li told the others that she and Qin Yanzhou were going to wander around the town, asking Qin Qinian and Shi Rongyue if they wanted to come along.","Qin Qinian was full of enthusiasm, \"Of course! I'll go with you.\"","Shi Rongyue's gaze shifted slightly to the side, and she softly said she wanted to go too.","Dai Li nodded and led the group of youngsters out. Naturally, Bai Jianping followed them on their outing, bringing along a few soldiers besides himself.","A small county couldn't compare to Chang'an; there was only one cross-street that was somewhat bustling. The area was small and only roughly divided into sections: vegetables and meat were mostly on this end, while daily necessities like fabrics were on that end.","After casually browsing two shops, Dai Li gave Qin Yanzhou a meaningful glance. The latter then said to Qin Qinian, \"There's a pottery shop over there with some interestingly shaped pieces. Do you want to go take a look with me?\"","Qin Qinian instinctively said yes, but after answering, he looked toward Dai Li, \"But...\"","Noticing his gaze, Dai Li smiled, \"You guys go ahead and take Rongrong with you. The shop is just at the corner of the street, not far away. I'll come find you after I finish looking around here.\"","After speaking to the youngsters, Dai Li also sent Bai Jianping over. Bai Jianping didn't disobey; although he went along, it wasn't as if no one was left to guard Dai Li, so he wasn't worried.","After they left, Dai Li calmly looked at the two remaining guards. She called one over and asked him to go to a nearby shop to buy something; once he left, Dai Li bought a large batch of items and asked the shopkeeper to deliver them to her door.","However...","\"Madam, are you sure your relay station is located there? Why do I remember there being no relay station in that area?\" the shopkeeper asked, puzzled.","\"Is that so?\" Dai Li looked hesitant, turning to call the only remaining soldier, \"Tell the shopkeeper the exact address of our relay station. I'm going next door to find Zhouzhou and the others.\"","Leaving this sentence behind, Dai Li stepped outside. The soldier had only followed her for two steps when he heard Dai Li say from the doorway, \"You stay here and don't worry, he seems to be coming back.\"","This \"he\" referred to the person who had just been sent out.","Hearing this, the soldier stopped.","Dai Li, who had walked to the doorway, looked back and then to her left. One soldier was talking to the shopkeeper to leave the address, while the other was paying.","Neither of them noticed her side.","Dai Li smiled and took an envelope out of her sleeve.","When the soldier finished speaking with the shopkeeper and turned around, he saw the mistress, who had previously said she was going to find her son, standing on the street opposite the shop, holding a letter in her hand.","\"Mistress?\" The soldier hurried forward in a few quick steps.","Dai Li waved the letter at him, \"A letter just arrived from the North.\"","The soldier was stunned.","A letter from the North? Where was the messenger?","Just as the doubt arose, he heard Dai Li say, \"The messenger has been traveling for a long time, likely rushing day and night without rest. I told him to go find a place to rest first.\"","The soldier nodded. His gaze inadvertently caught sight of his companion still buying things nearby, and a trace of oddity suddenly welled up in his heart.","However, this slight doubt,","upon seeing Dai Li's calm face, vanished quickly like a pebble thrown into a river.","The mistress was acting completely normal, and besides, the letter used the exact wax seal from their Northern territory. What could possibly be wrong?","Not long after, Qin Yanzhou and the others returned.","Dai Li waved the letter in her hand, \"Rongrong, Colonel Yan sent a letter saying something seems to have happened at your home, and he suggests you return to Yuyang quickly.\"","Shi Rongyue froze, and recovering her senses, hurriedly asked what happened.","\"Colonel Yan didn't entirely talk about the Shi family's affairs in the letter; most of it involves crops and fertilizer. He didn't go into detail about your family,\" Dai Li said, handing her the letter to read.","Shi Rongyue took it and saw that the beginning of the letter reported information about composting, and only at the very end was the Shi family mentioned.","It was a very brief sentence, just as vague as Dai Li had said, without any specific reasons. This half-hidden truth only made one more anxious.","Qin Qinian stood beside her and read the letter as well, but it was as if he hadn't read it at all. Seeing Shi Rongyue's anxious face, he bluntly said, \"Since something has happened at home, you should go back early.\"","Dai Li: \"This is not the place to discuss matters. We'll talk again when we return to the relay station.\"","*","Upon returning to the relay station, Dai Li dismissed Bai Jianping, leaving only the youngsters. \"Qinian, I want to ask a favor of you.\"","This was the first time Qin Qinian had been entrusted with something by an elder in such a pleading tone, and this person was his deeply admired mother. Immediately, a rush of hot blood shot to his head, \"Tell me, your son guarantees it will be done!\"","Dai Li slowly lowered her eyes, \"I will give you half of the soldiers. I want to ask you to escort Rongrong back to Yuyang.\"","Qin Qinian stood frozen on the spot, \"What, what do you mean by this? Aren't you going back to Yuyang with us?\"","\"It's not that I'm not going back, I just want to go back later,\" Dai Li sighed faintly. \"It's rare to come out and play. Whenever I think about how dizzyingly busy it will be after autumn, I don't want to go back so early. Besides, you are Rongrong's little cousin and have a close relationship with the Shi family. After escorting Rongrong back, you can conveniently visit the Shi family to see if they need any help, and do your best to assist them.\""]},{"number":170,"title":"Chapter 170","paragraphs":["\"...What? You want to split the troops?\" Bai Jianping was dumbfounded.","Dai Li nodded, \"Qinian and Rongrong will head back to Yuyang first, while Zhouzhou and I will take our time. We have four hundred men; we'll split them in two. Send two hundred soldiers to accompany them ahead.\"","\"But...\" Bai Jianping hesitated. He wanted to say it wasn't very safe.","Dai Li continued, \"When the Marquis and I traveled south from Yuyang to receive the title, we only had three hundred escorts. We even took a detour to Chunmiao Mountain to wipe out bandits along the way, and didn't we still arrive in the capital safely? Now, two hundred is indeed less than three hundred, but the entire North has been settled and is our own territory, so what is there to fear? Not to mention that the Xuan Cavalry are all brave and battle-tested, the most elite soldiers.\"","Bai Jianping opened his mouth, but couldn't say a word. He was completely speechless.","The mistress's words were reasonable, but for some reason, his heart felt like a piece of linen blown into the sky by the wind, unable to settle down.","Taking in his micro-expressions, Dai Li added, \"Don't worry, Garrison Commander Bai. I have already sent a message to the Marquis, and he will know about this very soon.\"","Bai Jianping first breathed a sigh of relief, but then suspicion arose in his heart, \"You sent someone to deliver a message?\"","Four hundred soldiers naturally couldn't be accommodated in one relay station, so they were scattered among various stations in the city. But Bai Jianping recalled the events of yesterday and today, and no one was missing, nor had he heard anyone mention that someone had been sent to deliver a letter.","\"Yes, the soldier who came from the North yesterday to deliver a letter to me, I sent him to Chang'an. Since he came from Yuyang, he must know other news, so I conveniently had him go and report to the Marquis,\" Dai Li said.","Bai Jianping let out an \"Oh\" and said no wonder.","Dai Li smiled and said nothing.","After handling Bai Jianping, the team was quickly split in two. The other half of two hundred men was led by Qin Qinian, while the rest remained with Dai Li.","Dai Li actually wanted Bai Jianping to go back with Qin Qinian, but this Garrison Commander Bai refused no matter what and insisted on following her. Going too far is as bad as not going far enough, so she didn't try to persuade him anymore after being rejected.","Since there was an \"emergency at home,\" they naturally couldn't delay, so the luggage was quickly separated and they were ready to go.","Dai Li looked at the little girl with her hands resting on the window sill of the carriage, sticking her head out, and the young boy riding on the horse. \"Qinian, Rongrong, I wish you a safe and smooth journey.\"","Qin Qinian: \"You too, Mother.\"","\"Take care, Second Aunt.\" Shi Rongyue looked at Qin Yanzhou and held the furball up to the window. \"Brother Chongle, you also take care. Xiaobai and I will come play with you next year.\"","\"Woof!\" The puppy wagged its tail.","Qin Yanzhou curled his lips, but that slight arc quickly fell again.","\"Let's set off. The sooner you leave, the sooner you get home,\" Dai Li urged.","The team set off, gradually walking away in the morning light.","Dai Li watched from afar, a similar yet slightly different melancholy rising in her heart again. Barring any accidents, she would never see Qinian and Rongrong again in this life.","The sun sets after noon, and the moon wanes after it is full. There is no perfection in life. It's good enough if everyone can be safe and sound in the future...","Letting out a long breath, Dai Li stopped looking at the receding convoy. \"Zhouzhou, let's go back.\"","*","After staying in the small town of Tianchi for another two days, Dai Li finally continued her journey. According to the original itinerary, she should have traveled all the way north, passing through Bingzhou to get to Yuyang in Youzhou.","But in reality, after only passing through two small counties, Dai Li ordered a change of route. No longer taking the land route, she wanted to take a boat east from the ferry crossing and enter Sizhou.","This seemed like a sudden whim, shocking Bai Jianping so much that his voice rose two pitches. \"Mistress, you want to change to the water route?\"","Dai Li nodded and said of course. \"The great river flows from west to east. Traveling east by boat is faster than taking a carriage, and since we said we were going to enjoy the scenery, how can we not take a boat? Besides, Sizhou is now also in the Marquis's hands. Although he hasn't had it for long, it has been consolidated, and the heads of some important towns have been replaced. The officials of the counties, large and small, all recognize our token. Switching to the water route, apart from taking a slightly longer way, is perfectly fine.\"","After the \"Imperial Army\" led by Dong Zhou was defeated, the leaders of the Si, Yu, and Xu provinces died one by one, and their territories were quickly divided up by Qin Shaozong and Nangong Xiong, with the former taking the lion's share.","Not to mention Sizhou, even the eastbound route through Yuzhou and Xuzhou would be unimpeded for them.","Bai Jianping listened in a daze.","What the mistress said was correct. The major forces in the north had basically been wiped out by the Marquis and were no longer able to pose a threat to them, but deep down, he still didn't want to change to the water route...","Bai Jianping tried to persuade her, \"Mistress, many of our soldiers from the North get seasick. Changing to the water route, I'm afraid many brothers won't be able to adapt. If there's any unexpected situation then, it might be difficult to respond to the emergency.\"","How could Dai Li not know that some people couldn't travel by boat? \"How about this: the seasick soldiers will take the land route. It just so happens that we have many carriages, and it's not realistic to bring them all on the boat, so it's best to leave them to them. Those who can't take the boat will drive east, and those who can will come with me. We'll meet up later, and the final destination will be Chen County.\"","The Chen County she mentioned was a small county in Yuzhou.","Hearing that she had even decided on the meeting place, Bai Jianping's heart skipped a beat, and he hurriedly tried to persuade her again, \"Mistress, although the Si and Yu regions have largely been pacified, the death of a major force does not mean that all the small bandits have scattered. If we split the troops again, it would be like a blind man riding a blind horse, approaching a deep pool in the middle of the night—extremely dangerous. Please reconsider!\"","Dai Li remained unmoved. \"Garrison Commander Bai, you're worrying too much. Yuzhou has been settled, and a few hidden small bandits are nothing to fear. When the Marquis left the city, he told you to follow my instructions and that if I wanted to travel, you shouldn't stop me. Why is it that after only ten days, Garrison Commander Bai has forgotten what he promised back then?\"","Her tone wasn't particularly angry, just very cold, but Bai Jianping, who was used to her normal way of speaking, knew that she was very unhappy.","Seeing his miserable expression, Dai Li suddenly took a step \"back.\" \"Let's put aside the matter of how to allocate the soldiers for the water and land routes for now. I must trouble Garrison Commander Bai to count how many of the remaining two hundred soldiers can travel by boat. If the number is small, I will send another letter to the Marquis explaining the situation and see if he can dispatch some more people over.\"","These words were logical and well-thought-out in every aspect, but Bai Jianping just felt that something was off.","\"Garrison Commander Bai?\" Dai Li asked when he didn't respond for a long time.","Bai Jianping suddenly snapped back to reality and had to agree.","Dai Li smiled. \"I leave this matter to you. Zhouzhou and I will go out first to inquire about the boats at the ferry crossing.\"","Looking at Dai Li's back, Bai Jianping suddenly realized where the strangeness just now came from:","Was the mistress really this lively and fond of traveling?","He recalled the past, remembering the winter hunt last year. At that time, they accompanied the Marquis to hunt, but the mistress stayed in the camp and didn't go along.","There was also the journey south to the capital. Once, when passing by Qifeng, he accidentally heard that the Marquis wanted to take the mistress to climb high and look far, but she refused, saying she had no interest.","Could it be that at that time, she was burdened by the matter of receiving the title and worried about the various things after arriving in the capital, so she was in no mood to play?","Bai Jianping couldn't figure it out, nor did he have an answer.","A shallow cloud of suspicion enveloped him.","And the result of his suspicion was that Bai Jianping worked incredibly slowly. When Dai Li asked him to count how many of the remaining two hundred soldiers did not get seasick, he spent three whole days on the task before finally reporting the number to her.","\"Madam, there are forty-two people who can travel by boat, including myself.\" Bai Jianping observed Dai Li. Seeing that she wasn't the least bit angry at his dawdling, the doubts in his heart grew even deeper.","Dai Li noticed his scrutiny and guessed that he was suspicious.","This was normal. After all, her current style of doing things was vastly different from the past. If he wasn't suspicious, he would have to be incredibly careless, and such a careless person could never have fought his way out of a thousand Xuanxiao Cavalrymen to secure the position of a garrison commander.","Dai Li concealed the dark gleam in her eyes. Now was not the time. She had to wait until Bai Jianping's suspicion reached its peak before making her next move. \"Forty-two people isn't a lot, but it isn't a small number either. A small tower ship couldn't even hold forty-two people.\"","Bai Jianping choked.","A small boat indeed could not hold forty-some people, but was that really the right point of reference?","Dai Li continued, \"Previously, Zhouzhou and I went to the ferry crossing to investigate. This Min River is not as large as the major rivers, so the largest ships that appear here are medium-sized tower ships; there are no large vessels. Speaking solely of medium-sized ships, about ten pass through the ferry every day, over ninety percent of which are cargo ships, with the occasional painted pleasure boat. And those merchant fleets doing business are the easiest to negotiate with, as long as you offer them enough silver.\"","Bai Jianping stammered slightly, \"Y-you even found all that out?\"","And that wasn't all. Dai Li had even made a decision. \"I plan to divide those forty-two people into three teams of a dozen or so each, taking three separate boats.\"","Bai Jianping immediately felt a headache coming on.","Dai Li acted as if she couldn't see his silent resistance. \"The rest of the men will take the carriages and travel by land. Traveling downstream by boat is faster than riding horses, so the boat unit will definitely be ahead. Every time the boat fleet stops at a town to rest, they will wait for the land unit to arrive, briefly reunite, and then part ways again.\"","Bai Jianping's brows had not relaxed since a moment ago. \"Madam, this matter is of great importance. I hope you will allow me to go back and study the map first.\"","Dai Li agreed.","Dai Li returned to her quarters, but instead of going to her own room, she went to Qin Yanzhou's.","\"Mother, did Commander Bai agree?\" The young man stood by the desk, and spread out upon it was the very map Bai Jianping had just said he was going to study.","Dai Li closed the door. \"He didn't agree immediately. He said he needed to go back and look at the map. Actually, this is just right. If we rush through this journey, the Green Lotus Sect might not have time to organize their forces and catch up, which would be truly troublesome later on.\"","She had never forgotten the Green Lotus Sect, that colossal entity hiding in the shadows. Since the North and the Imperial Court were successively consolidated by Qin Changgeng, the Green Lotus Sect seemed to have shifted toward the Bashu region.","Thinking of how the Green Lotus Sect had \"invited\" her before, Dai Li guessed that they would likely want to \"invite\" her again this time.","Her escort was only two hundred men—no, once they took the waterway, she would only have a few dozen Xuanxiao Cavalry by her side. It was true that the Xuanxiao Cavalry were outstanding in combat, but this number was far fewer than usual.","It was a once-in-a-lifetime opportunity; if missed, who knew when the next one would arise.","Of course, given the time Qin Changgeng attacked Xuzhou and played the \"oriole behind the mantis stalking the cicada,\" she guessed the Green Lotus Sect would be very cautious and would thoroughly check for ambushes in the vicinity.","If the soldiers traveling by land were excluded, there truly were no ambushes. Because Qin Changgeng was completely unaware of this matter from start to finish, the only people she had at her disposal were these two hundred men.","Dai Li confirmed with her son again, \"Zhouzhou, are you sure that very few of the Green Lotus Sect's followers have exceptional martial skills?\"","\"Yes.\" Qin Yanzhou recalled the past. \"When I was still in the mountains, following Liudao, the place we lived only had two martial arts training grounds, neither of which was large. One was for young children, and the other for adults. There were less than fifty children training with me, and the number of people in the adult arena next door was even smaller.\"","Dai Li looked thoughtful.","She had heard her son mention \"the mountains\" before; that was where they lived during the year of the great famine. \"The mountains\" was considered a fairly important stronghold for the Green Lotus Sect, yet in such an important place, the scale of the training grounds was surprisingly inadequate.","Qin Yanzhou said in a low voice, \"Mother, Liudao is actually quite a conceited man. When he used to teach Diting and White Elephant, what he mentioned most was the strategy of killing three warriors with two peaches. Rather than using brute force, he reveres strategy and takes pride in being the mastermind behind the scenes.\"","Dai Li suddenly smiled and shook her head. \"Perhaps it's not entirely out of his own genuine desire; there must be some degree of helplessness involved. I heard that fifty years ago, the Green Lotus Sect supported a rebel prince's usurpation of the throne, but it ended in failure. Afterward, the rebel prince was executed, and the Green Lotus Sect also suffered heavy losses. After such an ordeal, their vitality was definitely severely damaged, and it's hard to say how much of their capital remains.\"","Pausing for a moment, the brightness between Dai Li's brows deepened a bit. \"As the saying goes, poverty breeds scholars while wealth breeds warriors. Few of them practice martial arts to begin with, let alone achieve any significant results.\"","For the common people at the bottom of society, \"martial arts\" was very expensive.","High-intensity training inevitably increased one's appetite. Originally, a bowl of wheat rice could fill the stomach, but after practicing martial arts, one had to eat two bowls. Practicing martial arts sporadically wouldn't work, and as the time spent on martial arts increased, the time available for farming or making a living would inevitably shorten. This equated to only investing without producing, not to mention that buying weapons and hiring martial arts instructors both required silver.","Money was needed everywhere, and many people at the bottom simply couldn't afford it. And the followers of the Green Lotus Sect overwhelmingly came from the bottom rung of society.","Worry flickered in Qin Yanzhou's eyes. \"Mother, this opportunity is indeed rare for them, and the Green Lotus Sect will definitely go all out. I'm worried that if they see no hope of capturing you alive in the end, they might simply decide to kill you.\"","The difficulty of capturing someone alive versus just bringing back a corpse was not on the same level at all.","Dai Li patted her son's shoulder, her heart not heavy in the slightest. With Zhouzhou's martial arts skills, those cultists certainly wouldn't be able to hurt him. \"Don't worry, we still have time to think of a few more countermeasures to ensure absolute safety. We have to go through this eventually after leaving Qin Changgeng. Using the North as a borrowed knife to strike at the Green Lotus Sect now is much better than trying to resist them alone in the future.\"","When the snipe and the clam grapple, the fisherman profits.","She wanted to fish in troubled waters and be that profiting fisherman.","If the Green Lotus Sect didn't come, well, then she would just have to initiate another, very troublesome plan.","Bai Jianping tossed and turned in his room all night with the map, thoroughly studying the vicinity of the Min River. The next day, he went to find Dai Li with dark circles under his eyes.","Bai Jianping said earnestly, \"Madam, we will proceed eastward in two groups just as you suggested earlier. However, we don't have many soldiers on our side who can travel by boat. To be safe, I recommend hiring a group of armed escorts in the small towns to accompany us on the water journey. Oh, and we also need to send a letter to the Marquis.\"","If they didn't have enough manpower, then they would just hire a group of martial artists, or simply charter an entire ship. It wasn't as if the Marquis couldn't afford that bit of silver anyway.","Dai Li froze.","Whether it was an illusion or not, Bai Jianping felt that the way Dai Li was looking at him right now was very strange. \"Madam?\"","Dai Li coughed lightly. \"Commander Bai, you truly are a fascinating person.\"","This sounded like a compliment, but it made all the hairs on Bai Jianping's body stand on end.","The Madam was praising him! But why did it make him feel so uneasy?"]},{"number":171,"title":"Chapter 171","paragraphs":["Daili nodded and asked Bai Jianping, \"It is necessary to send a letter to the Lord. Captain Bai, do you have anything you wish to say to him?\"","Bai Jianping said yes, \"There are some recent developments that need to be reported to the Lord.\"","Daili replied, \"Perfect, I also have many private words to share with him. How about this: after you finish writing your letter, give it to me. I will pack it together with my family letter, saving the messenger the trouble of carrying multiple parcels.\"","Bai Jianping's mind spun for a moment.","Give the letter to the Mistress first, and then send it to the Lord together? Could it be that the Mistress did not trust him and worried he might speak ill of her to the Lord in the letter?","How could that be!","The Lord had already agreed to let her go sightseeing; as a subordinate, how could he defy orders? His report would be absolutely objective, merely stating the facts without any emotional coloring of complaint or accusation.","However...","\"Alright,\" Bai Jianping agreed. He thought to himself that since the Mistress wanted to inspect it, he would let her inspect it.","Daili smiled in satisfaction.","Bai Jianping wrote his letter very quickly. An hour after their conversation, he came to find Daili with the letter in hand.","The mulberry paper was simply folded, not even sealed with wax. He handed it over just like that. \"Mistress, my letter is finished. I will have to trouble you to pack it in when the time comes.\"","Daili said it was no trouble at all.","As soon as the door closed, she unfolded Bai Jianping's letter without the slightest psychological burden.","Qin Shaozong was a man who disliked dragging things out, and this style was also reflected in how he managed his subordinates. The military reports and daily summaries from his men were always written quite briefly, and Bai Jianping's letter was no exception.","It was only three lines long, mentioning her intention to change their route to the waterways. It also specifically highlighted that very few soldiers would be accompanying her on the water route, and that they planned to hire a group of martial artists to travel with them.","After reading Bai Jianping's letter, Daili took out a stack of mulberry paper, ground some ink, and began writing her own letter. She didn't have that much to say, so she simply wrote the characters very large, taking up as much space as possible.","Once the paper was used up and folded, it looked quite thick.","Daili carefully sealed it with wax, completing a letter ready to be sent to Chang'an. Meanwhile, right beside her hand, Bai Jianping's report lay quietly.","It had not been put into the envelope at all.","With the letters dealt with, Daili did not immediately call for someone to deliver them. Since it was supposed to contain \"many private words,\" it naturally had to be delayed a bit longer.","Right now, renting boats and hiring martial artists were the pressing matters.","As the golden sun set in the west that day, painting the earth in a brilliant, warm orange hue, a tall and slender young man returned, stepping through the sunset.","Daili was waiting on the first floor of the inn. Seeing her son return after a day of running around, she took a cup and poured him some tea. \"Zhou Zhou, you've worked hard today. Have a sip of tea and rest. Did you manage to hire the martial artists?\"","\"There is only one escort agency in this county, with a total of seven guards. They are all willing to make the trip with us.\" Qin Yanzhou was terribly thirsty; after speaking, he drained the tea in his cup in one gulp.","Bai Jianping was also nearby. \"Only seven? Seven people won't be of much use. It would be best to find thirty... No, too many wouldn't do either. It would be terrible if they turned against us and took control.\"","The Great Yan Dynasty had been severely ravaged by corrupt officials and parasites in recent years. Many people lost their land and could no longer survive, forcing them to become bandits. Since the money came quickly, killing people like flies gradually became their so-called \"righteous path.\"","Many of these scattered petty thieves did not amount to much, but once they gathered into a group of a hundred or so, it could be called a bandit menace, enough to attract the attention of local authorities.","Bai Jianping rested his chin on his hand and pondered for a moment. \"There are bandits in the mountains and pirates on the water. The locals are far more familiar with the routes than we outsiders are. Seven will have to do. Since there aren't enough martial artists here, we will just hire more elsewhere. Mistress, I personally think we can set off first, and when we reach the next town, we can hire another batch of martial artists. The total number can be kept under fifteen.\"","Daili said, \"Excellent.\"","Bai Jianping then asked Qin Yanzhou, addressing him by the official title that had still not been revoked since his sneak attack on the Xuzhou military granary. \"Commandant, have you negotiated everything with the boatmen?\"","Qin Yanzhou replied, \"I have booked three boats. We agreed to set sail at noon the day after tomorrow.\"","Bai Jianping didn't ask why it was the day after tomorrow. After all, it was common for cargo ships to load and unload goods at the port. He asked, \"Mistress, is your letter finished?\"","From here back to Chang'an, it would take four days of non-stop travel day and night. It would be best to send the letter out before leaving the small town.","Daili replied with sound reasoning, \"Not yet. Zhou Zhou was out during the day and hasn't had time to write his letter yet. We will send them together once he finishes.\"","Bai Jianping nodded in understanding.","The sun rose and set, and a day passed in the blink of an eye. Today, Qin Yanzhou took a few soldiers out again and did not return until dusk.","Bai Jianping was still thinking about sending the letter, so he asked again. The reply he received was that Qin Yanzhou wanted to include today's events in his letter, so the letters would be sent out tomorrow.","The battle-hardened Captain Bai opened his mouth to speak. The previous clouds of suspicion floated back, and alongside his surprise and doubt, an inexplicable trace of unease arose. However, this hint of strangeness was too subtle, like the drizzle in spring, brushing past his cheek without leaving much of a trace.","Bai Jianping hesitated for a long while before slowly nodding.","On the third day, the very day they were to set sail at noon, Bai Jianping came to look for Daili early in the morning. He asked her for the letters, saying he would have them sent back to Chang'an by fast horse.","This time, Daili did not refuse him. She took out a rather thick envelope, already sealed with wax. \"I leave it in your capable hands, Captain Bai.\"","Bai Jianping weighed it in his hand and felt amused. Good heavens, this was quite heavy. Even though the Lord and the Mistress were not a young couple, their relationship was truly excellent; many people could not compare to them.","Having received the letter, Bai Jianping immediately summoned two soldiers, ordered them to travel together, and ride post-haste back to Chang'an. Only after personally watching the messengers ride off did the tense string in his heart finally loosen a bit.","They were boarding the ships today. Their luggage had mostly been packed yesterday. Now, several carriages transported it to the port first, and then the luggage would be transferred onto the tower ships.","The deck of one of the tower ships was much more spacious than the others. Bai Jianping suggested to Daili, \"Mistress, I see that the deck of this ship is quite open. Why don't we unhitch the horses and push your carriage onto the ship? That way, it will be easier for you to retrieve things later.\"","The gangway connecting to the cargo ship was much wider, allowing two to three people to walk side by side, so pushing the carriage up would not be difficult.","Daili's gaze fell upon the carriage. This carriage was one of the wedding carriages used when she and Qin Changgeng got married. It was made of top-quality scented rosewood. There was a saying, \"An inch of rosewood is worth an inch of gold,\" which referred exactly to this type of yellow rosewood.","Not only were the materials excellent, but the interior furnishings were also meticulously designed. The seats were spacious, the low cabinets were elegant, and there were many hidden compartments; every single detail was exquisite.","Daili sighed in her heart. Forget it, it was better not to ruin this fine carriage. \"No, parking the carriage on the deck will take up too much space and make it inconvenient to enjoy the scenery from the ship. Just carry the chests and boxes aboard.\"","Bai Jianping followed her orders.","The weather today was clear and bright. The early autumn afternoon sunlight enveloped the two-story tower ships docked by the port. A gauze-like brightness fell upon everyone and spread across the river, reflecting a sparkling brilliance on the rippling surface of the water.","Dai Li looked at the sparkling river and whispered to Bai Jianping, \"Garrison Chief Bai, I have heard that some river bandits disguise themselves as peddlers. When passengers let their guard down, they rob and kill them. Their methods of committing crimes are not limited to placing knockout incense in the rooms or drugging the food.\"","Bai Jianping's heart skipped a beat.","Dai Li turned to look at him. Her dark eyes, black as lacquer, reflected the sunlight like a mirror. \"When traveling, we must act with caution. Our group is a bit conspicuous. It might be better if the cooks on the ship were replaced by our own people.\"","Moving box after box of luggage, anyone could see that their group was quite wealthy.","Bai Jianping nodded. \"You are right. Speaking of which, when I was chatting with two escort guards this morning, one of them also mentioned this. He suggested we take control of the ship's kitchen. However, when I negotiated with the ship owner earlier, he did not agree...\"","He sighed helplessly. \"Perhaps just as we are guarding against them, they are also guarding against us.\"","The tower ship was transporting a large batch of goods, every single one valuable. Taking your money to give you a ride was fine, but completely giving up the kitchen was out of the question.","Dai Li thought for a moment and said, \"Then we will just cook our own meals, and do not mix the ingredients. If they are uneasy, they can send someone to watch the kitchen door while we cook.\"","Bai Jianping nodded, saying he thought the same. Then, he probed cautiously, \"Madam, how is it that you are so clear about all these twists and turns?\"","Dai Li smiled. \"I read it in books, and heard about it in teahouses.\"","Before long, all the luggage was loaded onto the ship.","As the boatman fiercely pulled the hemp rope by the mast, the huge rolled-up canvas came crashing down like flowing water, and then slowly billowed out in the wind.","Riding the wind, the tower ship gradually moved away from the shore.","Standing on the deck, Dai Li gazed at the soldiers left behind at the ferry crossing, unable to help but space out a little.","Inside Chang'an City.","Two fast horses entered the city through the north gate. They slowed down while passing through the bustling market, and once they finally made it through, they sped up again, heading straight for their destination.","The guards at the entrance of the Qin Manor recognized their comrades. Knowing that they had accompanied Dai Li back to Yuyang a few days ago, and now seeing the two return travel-worn, they asked with a smile, \"Back to deliver a letter?\"","Xun He nodded in confirmation and asked about Qin Shaozong, \"Is the Marquis in the manor today?\"","\"What a coincidence. He and Governor Nangong just left not long ago. You will have to wait,\" the guard said.","Xun He looked up at the sky. It was exactly the end of the noon hour, neither early nor late. \"It seems I can take a short nap.\"","Having traveled day and night, Xun He was utterly exhausted. He unsaddled the horses, handed over the letters, and then found the room where he used to stay on duty, falling asleep the moment his head hit the bed.","...","Qin Shaozong returned during the Shen hour. As soon as he returned to the manor, he heard from Hu Bao that there was a letter from Dai Li.","\"She finally remembered that she still has a husband in Chang'an,\" he said cheerfully. And when he received that rather thick letter, the shallow traces left by time at the corners of the man's eyes deepened. His smile was rich, and he repeatedly praised, \"Not bad, not bad.\"","Seeing his superior in such a good mood, Hu Bao finally breathed a sigh of relief. Recently, the prominent families in Chang'an had not been very well-behaved, which had made the Marquis extremely furious. Dark clouds had loomed over the manor, but now the skies had finally cleared.","Qin Shaozong took the letter back to his room.","The doors of the master bedroom were wide open, and the sunlight was bright. On the display shelf, which had been emptied significantly, sat only a single incense cage. However, because the mistress had taken all the maidservants with her, this flowing-cloud cast-bronze gilded incense cage had not been tended to for a long time, and now it was merely a decoration.","Accompanied by a few bird chirps outside the window, Qin Shaozong broke the wax seal.","To Qin Changgeng, respectfully wishing you peace:","How have you been recently? Is everything going smoothly in Chang'an? Great endeavors must be pursued gradually; you must not be impatient, nor should you let anger damage your health over such matters. Early autumn has arrived, and the temperature difference between day and night in Chang'an is vast. I hope you will follow the principle of keeping warm in spring and staying cool in autumn to regulate your energy and preserve your health, and take good care of yourself.","Reading up to this point, Qin Shaozong surprisingly found that the page had already ended.","He turned the page.","Next, she mentioned a few of the younger generation, describing their daily lives and adding one or two minor anecdotes.","Before he knew it, he turned another page.","This time, she spoke of some of the things she had seen and heard along the way, telling him about the local customs of a small county. She also mentioned that the local snacks were tempting, and that some master chefs were hidden in the markets, proving that experts truly come from among the common people, which was truly amazing.","At the very, very end, she wrote:","...When a sage is born in times of peace, the universe is destined to settle soon. You are like a tiger catching the wind, a dragon soaring through the clouds, a true great man of the current era. However, the sage sits high up in the nine heavens; you must guard against arrogance and impatience. I hope you will return only after your matters are concluded.","Your wife Dai Li, bowing her head.","Unwittingly, Qin Shaozong had flipped through that thick stack of mulberry paper. The man furrowed his long brows, dissatisfied that he had finished reading it in the blink of an eye, and flipped back to the very beginning.","He started reading from the beginning again.","This time, Qin Shaozong's reading speed was much slower than before, but even so, he still felt like he had to turn the page after only reading for a short while.","Flip, flip, flip, flip...","Without realizing it, he had reached the end again.","\"It looks like a thick stack, so how can there be so little? Is this fox slacking off?\" After Qin Shaozong finished this mocking sentence, he froze.","It was not that he had never seen Dai Li's handwriting before. She had written two booklets on fertilizer, and had also written letters to Yan San, who was in Yuyang.","In his memory, her letter back then seemed much denser than his current one.","Furrowing his brows in thought for a moment, Qin Shaozong finally stood up. He rummaged through a small box in the room and found one of Dai Li's record books.","This booklet was the same size as the spread-out mulberry letter paper. Placing the two side by side to compare, the difference was immediately apparent.","The characters on the left were several sizes larger, while the ones on the right were smaller, exactly like the difference between an adult and a twelve or thirteen-year-old youth.","Qin Shaozong fetched some new paper, quickly ground some ink, picked up his brush, and then copied the family letter he had just received, using Dai Li's previous font size.","After copying the entire thick stack of letters, it only took two and a half sheets of paper, not even making up three full letter pages.","Qin Shaozong stared at the three sheets of paper in front of him, his gaze dark and unreadable. After a moment, he raised his voice and said, \"Where is Madam's messenger? Tell him to come here.\"","The guards outside received the order and went down.","A long while later, two sets of footsteps approached.","Xun He was woken up halfway through his sleep. With sleepy eyes and yawning incessantly, he slapped his face hard before entering the room to wake himself up.","Qin Shaozong knew their names, and now he casually picked one to ask, \"Xun He, how has Madam been recently? Did you encounter anything strange on the return journey?\"","Xun He answered truthfully, \"No. After parting ways with the Second Young Master and the others, Madam has been doing very well. She was even happily preparing to go sightseeing and enjoy the scenery.\"","The man standing not far away abruptly stood up from the desk."]},{"number":172,"title":"Chapter 172","paragraphs":["Qin Shaozong's movements were so terrifyingly violent that even the heavy red sandalwood desk in front of him shook.","\"What did you say? Qin San and Madam parted ways? When did this happen?\" Qin Shaozong's face was as dark as water. \"Tell me everything in detail, Xun He, without missing a single thing!\"","The heavy pressure rolled over them like a wave. Xun He and the person beside him were both deeply shaken, and whatever sleepiness they had left dissipated completely.","The Marquis was a good superior who cared for his subordinates. In the past, when they rushed back on horseback, they could go rest after delivering their letters. Given how much the Marquis valued the mistress, he wasn't surprised that they would be summoned for questioning later.","But this was... too fast, wasn't it?","His mind raced, but outwardly Xun He dared not be negligent. He hurriedly recounted the important events that occurred along the way after Dai Li left Chang'an.","He started from when they left the city, saying that Dai Li was in no hurry and the procession moved very slowly. Then he mentioned that Yan San sent a letter later, vaguely mentioning an incident with the Shi family and urgently summoning Shi Rongyue back. He also said that Dai Li still had a desire to travel, so she split the procession in two. Half of the troops rushed back to the north, while the remaining half accompanied Dai Li to travel eastward...","The veins on Qin Shaozong's forehead throbbed. He didn't finish listening. As soon as he heard \"split the troops,\" he couldn't help but scold angrily, \"Nonsense!\"","Xun He's breath hitched. While feeling terrified, he was also filled with doubts.","Something was wrong. Why was the Marquis's reaction so strong? After the messenger from the north brought Commandant Yan's letter, he clearly received the mistress's order to head to Chang'an.","Could it be that the Marquis didn't know about this?","Where did things go wrong? Did the messenger meet with an accident on the way, so the Marquis in Chang'an never received the letter?","Thinking this, Xun He asked, \"Marquis, before heading east, the mistress sent a messenger to Chang'an. Did you not receive the letter?\"","Qin Shaozong's face was ashen.","Of course not!","This stack of letters from home today was the first communication since she left.","The reason he felt something was off was entirely because her handwriting was different from usual, which made him suspicious and prompted him to summon the messenger for details. And this inquiry revealed something terrible: she had actually parted ways with Qi Nian, and even planned to go sightseeing afterwards!","Qin Shaozong didn't answer, but seeing his face, Xun He already knew the answer. His heart thumped, and he couldn't even speak clearly. \"M-Marquis, could it be...\"","Xun He didn't dare say what followed \"could it be.\"","The fire in Qin Shaozong's heart soared, but at the same time, something slowly sank.","The letters looked thick, but in reality, there were only two and a half pages. As for the messenger who claimed to be heading to Chang'an, he was nowhere to be found. Whether he met with an accident on the way or if such a person never existed was hard to say.","There was also the parting of ways midway. Four hundred people were split in half, leaving only two hundred by her side. Xun He also said she happily prepared to go sightseeing.","Heading east, sightseeing?","Heh, would they take a boat later?","Perhaps because of past experiences, and more than once, Qin Shaozong keenly sensed a different atmosphere. \"What happened next? Keep talking.\"","Xun He swallowed hard, wanting his fellow messenger to report. He had started it, so it should be someone else's turn now. He couldn't bear all the thunderous wrath alone!","However, when he stealthily glanced sideways, Xun He was shocked. He didn't know if his comrade beside him was scared or for some other reason, but the man was actually spacing out.","\"Xun He.\" A heavy voice pressed down from above.","Xun He cursed his bad luck inwardly and hurriedly answered to report the rest.","As Qin Shaozong expected, Dai Li's \"preparation\" for sightseeing became \"in progress.\"","Not only was she taking the waterway, but she also split the original two hundred people again. Some took the land route, while less than fifty people accompanied her.","Qin Shaozong suddenly asked, \"Did Bai Jianping write a letter to me?\"","Xun He actually knew about this. Back then, he was the one who found the paper for Platoon Leader Bai to write the letter. \"Yes...\"","But before he could finish, the heavy sandalwood desk not far away was violently kicked over by the man. The inkstone and unused paper on the desk either crashed to the ground or fluttered in the air.","It was a complete mess.","Qin Shaozong's eyes glinted sharply, as if shooting fire.","The seemingly thick and quite bluffing letters from home; the complete lack of mention in the letters about Qin San and her heading east; the supposedly dispatched but missing messenger; Bai Jianping's vanished letter; the second splitting of troops after the first; and finally, the less than fifty accompanying people...","Each incident was a small anchor point, outlining a speculation that made Qin Shaozong furious and unable to accept.","This fox was trying to escape again!","His brown eyes tightened, and his heart pounded as if it were going to explode. The veins connected to his heart twitched with pain, and his internal organs were violently pulled.","Anger, confusion, bewilderment, and a bitterness worse than medicinal soup mixed together, causing Qin Shaozong's vision to darken for a moment.","And just when Xun He thought he didn't even dare to breathe, someone spoke:","\"Marquis, this subordinate has an important matter to report.\"","Xun He couldn't control his head-turning movement, staring dumbfounded at his comrade beside him.","No, brother, why are you so reckless? Stroking a tiger's whiskers won't end well!","The man braced himself and said, \"Before I left, the mistress privately instructed me, saying that if I encountered your thunderous wrath after delivering the letter, I should tell you that she left a letter in the main bedroom. It contains the reasons, and she hopes you will read it carefully and think it over before making a decision.\"","Qin Shaozong strode forward and lifted the soldier, who had half-kneeled in fright, with one hand. \"What else did she tell you?\"","\"N-nothing else. The mistress only instructed that. This subordinate recited it all the way here and didn't dare to miss a single word.\"","Qin Shaozong let go. \"Where was the procession when you left?\"","Xun He quickly reported a place name.","Qin Shaozong said in a deep voice, \"Pass down my order. Have Qiao Wangfei immediately organize the East Platoon. I'm traveling light and far!\"","The two received the order and exited the room.","Once they left, Qin Shaozong scanned the room. The main bedroom was divided into an outer and inner room. The outer room had an incense table, a curio shelf, soft chairs, and small tables. A painting of a solitary fisherman in a straw cape on a cold river hung on the wall.","The inner room had a yellow rosewood openwork makeup case inlaid with gold and jade, placed next to a wooden clothes rack and chest. Deepest inside was a spacious and exquisite canopy bed, with carved patterns on its sturdy square posts.","Since she left, there were fewer items in the room, but many large furnishings remained.","Qin Shaozong went straight to the canopy bed and picked up Dai Li's pillow first. It was empty underneath. He continued to search other things, from the makeup case to the box for small items, and then to the wooden chest for clothes, but found nothing.","After a round of rummaging, Qin Shaozong calmed down a lot, but this calmness was only a shallow layer, like a large bowl inverted over the roaring flames, preventing them from rising higher once they reached the top.","With a furrowed brow, Qin Shaozong surveyed his surroundings again, paused at the heavy clothes chest for a moment, and finally suppressed his anger to lift it.","There really was a letter pressed under the clothes chest. Qin Shaozong laughed out of extreme anger. Such a heavy chest, she actually went to the trouble of lifting it just to hide a letter.","With a \"bang,\" the heavy chest was casually dropped. Qin Shaozong bent over to pick up the letter, and only when he grabbed it did he realize it wasn't one letter.","It was two.","One letter was addressed \"To Qinian,\" and the other \"To Changgeng.\"","With a cold expression, Qin Shaozong took the letter addressed to him and broke the wax seal.","To Changgeng, wishing you peace in recent days:","Seeing these words is like seeing me in person. You have the ambition to transform into a dragon, and in the future, you will surely bring peace to the world. As the saying goes, those high up in the temples of the court worry for their people; you have a compassionate heart, and I have never doubted that the common people will eventually see the end of their suffering.","For the public, I am deeply joyful; for us personally, I am deeply worried.","I have realized that there seem to be opposing forces behind Zhou Zhou and Qinian, like the tip of a needle against an awn of wheat, neither willing to yield. Reading the historical records and reflecting on the past and present, I see that the disasters of succession struggles inevitably lead to siblings slaughtering each other and the peril of the ancestral temple. I cannot help but feel heartbroken and must remain vigilant.","You and I have been married for nearly a year, and our family has been harmonious. I originally wished to grow old with you and share the cold winters of our lives together.","However, we are husband and wife, but also parents. Zhou Zhou is my own flesh and blood, and I also treat Qinian as my own son. It is not my wish to see either of them fall in battle in the future. To prevent a future internal strife that would implicate our family and the destiny of the state, after much deep thought, I have painfully drafted this letter of separation, so that we may part ways and find our own peace.","I will write only this much for now and will not go into further detail.","I humbly pray that from now on, the nation will be peaceful, our descendants will be safe, all your wishes will be fulfilled, and all your paths will be smooth.","Respectfully yours, Daili.","Qin Shaozong panted heavily. It was as if he had swallowed a gust of salty, damp wind that scraped against his throat again and again. His limbs and bones were similarly seized by this icy emotion, as if he had plunged into an ice cave.","Until...","His gaze inadvertently moved downward, and he noticed a slight indentation at the very bottom of the letter.","The originally smooth paper had a very shallow little pit, seemingly caused by a water stain that had dried. Because the paper was not torn, this small, shallow pit was not obvious; a careless person would never have noticed it.","Qin Shaozong paused, staring at it for a long while. Then, without hesitation, he opened the letter Daili had left for Qin Qinian. The two letters were similar in length, but the one she wrote to Qin Qinian consisted mainly of instructions and advice.","He read it quickly and then carefully felt the letter paper from top to bottom. This sheet of paper was perfectly smooth, with no small pits or wrinkles of any kind.","The tall and imposing man held the letter, his head lowered. His face was not very clear in the room where the sunlight was gradually dimming. The fury and other emotions radiating from him seemed to have settled down compared to just a moment ago, making his mood difficult to fathom.","Tucking the two letters into his robe, Qin Shaozong strode outside. Just as he stepped out of the main courtyard, he saw Nalan Zhi and Cui Shengping approaching together. Both men were walking hurriedly with solemn expressions.","\"My Lord,\" the two men bowed and cupped their hands toward Qin Shaozong.","Qin Shaozong stopped and said expressionlessly, \"Wugong, Haiqing, you have come at the perfect time. I need to leave Chang'an for a few days. I leave all matters within Chang'an in your capable hands.\"","Hearing Qin Shaozong say he was leaving, Nalan Zhi and Cui Shengping showed no surprise on their faces. In fact, that was exactly why they had come.","Cui Shengping hurriedly said, \"You must not, My Lord. The Yu clan is finally showing signs of relenting. How can you leave at a time like this?\"","Qin Shaozong sneered, \"Courtesy before force. Reasoning with them is just giving them a bit of face. If the Yu clan still dares to put on airs, the worst we have to do is find a random excuse to uproot them completely, treating it as another instance of killing the chicken to warn the monkeys. Besides, living on piles of money in Chang'an all these years and colluding with the Wang and Dong clans, how could they not have committed deeds like sucking the fat of the people and tearing apart bones for firewood? Do they really think they are something special?\"","After reaching middle age, the arrogance of Qin Shaozong's youth had been reined in significantly. The truly piercing sharpness, cold pride, and disdain seemed to have slowly faded with the passage of time. Aside from the occasional unforgiving remark, he was mostly steady and tolerant at other times.","It had been a long time since he had shown such overt aggressiveness on the surface like today.","Cui Shengping hastily advised, \"My Lord, it is true that killing the chicken to warn the monkeys is useful. But this action must be measured. If we repeat this old trick time and time again, I fear you will earn a reputation for being bloodthirsty. If it causes panic among the prominent families of Chang'an and forces them to band closely together, it will be very disadvantageous for our future endeavors.\"","\"My mind is made up. Haiqing, you need not advise me further,\" Qin Shaozong said, his gaze sweeping over him coldly. \"If you feel you lack the ability to handle the upcoming situation, you may seek a pointer or two from Wugong or Zhang Quanshu next door.\"","Cui Shengping's heart was greatly shaken, his thoughts extremely complicated, and he was momentarily left speechless.","Leaving those words behind, Qin Shaozong walked past the two men and left without looking back.","On the outskirts of Chang'an.","After receiving his orders, Qiao Wangfei swiftly assembled the troops. As soon as Qin Shaozong arrived, they quickly followed him and galloped toward the east.","A thousand miles away, Wuwen County.","Wuwen County was the third small county Daili had arrived at after traveling by water.","In the first small county, which was also the place where they split their forces again, Daili hired seven armed escorts. The second small county did have an escort agency, but unfortunately, they were busy with other tasks, leaving no one available for hire.","Continuing eastward for a stretch, Daili searched for an escort agency again after arriving in Wuwen County.","Not long ago, they managed to hire some people.","They hired eight martial artists, which, added to the previous seven, made a total of fifteen people, exactly the number originally planned.","Qin Yanzhou walked up beside Daili and whispered, \"Mother, among the eight newly hired escorts, the one with dark hair on the corner of his mouth is not very honest. I think I caught a familiar scent from him. This person might be a believer.\"","Daili replied, \"Then the fish has taken the bait.\""]},{"number":173,"title":"Chapter 173","paragraphs":["Inside a small courtyard in Wuwen County.","\"Sir, I had them confirm it three times. We are certain that after Lady Dai split her forces in the small county of Tianchi, the only ones by her side, apart from those traveling with her by water, are a group of Xuanxiao Cavalry traveling by land. The two groups combined still total two hundred people, with no additions.\"","\"Furthermore, whether in Tianchi at the beginning, Baiming at the previous ferry crossing, or now in Wuwen, Lady Dai has not stayed for a short time. Every time she arrives in a new town, she spends a lot of time in eateries and grocery stores, rarely returning empty-handed.\"","In the simple and unadorned courtyard, Diting stood beneath an osmanthus tree, holding a cluster of golden osmanthus flowers as brilliant as fireworks.","While listening to his follower's report, the man's pale, slender fingers brushed through the cluster of golden osmanthus. He casually plucked a single flower, but instead of holding it to admire or smell, he merely gave it an indifferent glance and mercilessly tossed it onto the ground. \"After she arrived in the new town, did she meet up with the team she had separated from earlier?\"","\"Yes,\" the follower replied. \"Traveling by water is faster. After Lady Dai arrived in the town first, she would always meet up with the main force before setting off again.\"","Diting suddenly asked, \"She must have changed ships along the way, right?\"","The follower blurted out, \"How did you know?\"","Diting merely chuckled lightly.","Since they were transporting goods, it was impossible for the shipowners not to care about time. She was so leisurely; even if she offered silver, not all shipowners would be willing to accept it.","However, he couldn't be bothered to explain this to others.","\"It's good that she can change ships. Our opportunity lies only on the rivers. Have someone arrange for small boats.\" Diting plucked another osmanthus flower, but this time he didn't throw it on the ground. Instead, he crushed the flower juice with the pads of his fingers. \"We must hurry with this matter and get it done before any potential reinforcements arrive.\"","*","Dai Li settled in at the relay station in Wuwen County. After resting quite leisurely for two days, she finally waited for the travel-worn land forces to arrive.","Just like last time, after the two groups met up, they handed over what needed to be handed over and reported what needed to be reported. Everything proceeded step by step.","Bai Jianping returned from outside. \"My lady, I went to the ferry crossing to ask. Two tower ships indicated they could take us for a leg of the journey. One of them is more spacious but relatively old; the other is smaller but has the advantage of being new. Which one do you prefer, or should we just take both and merge two of our three squads into one?\"","Their forces on the water were divided into three squads. On the way from Tianchi to Wuwen, because the boatmen were in a hurry, they had changed ships twice.","In other words, only one tower ship and the personnel on it had remained exactly the same, accompanying them from the very beginning until now.","Dai Li's fingertips tapped quickly on the desk a few times. \"We'll take the large ship; we won't need the small one. Have Song Asan and his squad come over and ride the large ship with us. As for Zhang Danchen and his men, they will continue on the original ship. There's no need for them to change.\"","The \"Song Asan\" and \"Zhang Danchen\" she mentioned were both lieutenants under Bai Jianping's command.","Bai Jianping nodded. \"Merging two squads into one means you will have more people by your side. That's good.\"","Dai Li: \"When did you arrange with the shipowner to set sail?\"","Bai Jianping said the middle of the Chen hour tomorrow morning.","Dai Li asked him again, \"Does the large ship have small boats prepared for emergencies? If not, it's best to prepare one or two. I accidentally heard that water bandits used to haunt this stretch of the waterway. Although I later inquired carefully and learned that was over a decade ago, it's always better to be safe than sorry.\"","Bai Jianping suddenly realized, \"It is still you, my lady, who thinks thoroughly. I will go handle it right away.\"","*","In the blink of an eye, a night passed. As the eastern sky turned white and the town slowly awakened from its silence, a new day arrived as promised.","Today they were to go to the ferry crossing to board the ship at the middle of the Chen hour, so Dai Li got up a bit earlier than usual. However, this \"early\" was entirely relative to herself.","The ferry crossing in the morning was already extraordinarily bustling.","Various sizes of cargo ships and boats were lined up like shuttles. Familiar boatmen and merchants gathered together; after clearing their money and goods, they left with faces full of smiles. There were also young merchants who looked like fledglings, wandering around among the ships, going back and forth to compare goods.","Suddenly, a small commotion arose in this little market at the ferry crossing.","The ferry crossing in the small county was not very exquisite. It was not paved with bluestone slabs like in large commanderies, nor was it as tidy as a big city. Occasionally, there were a few dead fish and rotten shrimp on the road, baked by the sun until they rotted and stank.","The ferry official here was as lazy as officials in many other places. Like a fat cat that didn't like to move, he rarely came out of his exclusive room.","But today, the rarely seen ferry official seemed to have been replaced with a new core. He was busily running back and forth around the group led by a young woman wearing a veiled hat.","He was extremely attentive, following closely step by step, the corners of his mouth almost grinning to the roots of his ears. Where was his usual dismissive attitude towards boatmen and fish merchants?","\"Who is that? To actually have Ferry Official Gao accompany her, what a grand display.\"","\"It's not just Ferry Official Gao. That man wearing green clothes with a round belly is clearly Magistrate Chen. Tsk, I wonder which noble family's dignitary is traveling, surrounded by attendants. There must be at least fifty people accompanying her. Old Sun, do you think it's possible she might have her private troops sweep up all my fish goods?\"","\"Stop joking. Just these little fish and shrimp of yours? How could they catch a noble's eye? Furthermore, when such wealthy families travel, their cooks prepare top-grade ingredients well in advance; there is no need to buy things at the last minute.\"","\"Speaking of which, if it were over a decade ago, such a grand traveling party would most likely attract the Wuwen water bandits. I still remember how brutal and unreasonable that overlord of the waters was back then. He loved targeting those tall tower ships to slaughter the fat sheep.\"","\"You said it yourself, that was over a decade ago. Nowadays, the area around Wuwen is very peaceful. Besides, she has so many troops; what could possibly happen?\"","\"True.\"","...","The owner of the large tower ship newly rented yesterday was surnamed Zhou. He was in his forties or fifties, with a round figure, and smiled like a Maitreya Buddha, looking very easy to get along with.","He ordered his subordinates to set up the boarding plank early to respectfully welcome the fat sheep... no, the distinguished guest on board.","Dai Li took off her veiled hat and smiled at the person in front of her. \"For the next leg of the journey, I will have to trouble you, Captain Zhou.\"","\"Taking people's money and doing their bidding loyally; you are too polite.\" Captain Zhou bowed his waist a bit lower.","After exchanging a few pleasantries with him, Dai Li looked at her upcoming resting place.","The tower structure of this tower ship was located in the middle and rear of the ship, occupying about half the space. In front stood a tall mast, with a small piece of white cloth tied to the top, fluttering in the wind.","On the mast, rolled-up canvases were gathered together. At about three-quarters of the way to the top, there was a small circular disc similar to a lookout tower, which could hold about one person.","Net-like hemp ropes hung down from above, connecting all the way to the small disc. Climbing up the ropes was the only way to reach the small disc. On both sides of the deck, square wooden boxes half the height of a person were piled up one by one.","These wooden boxes were very old. Some of the wooden boards had been touched so much that they gleamed with a woody luster; who knew how many years they had been used.","Strangely enough, the boxes were not completely sealed. The side with the lid had a few holes the size of chicken eggs, but there seemed to be a layer of cloth covering the inside. It was gray and murky, making it impossible to see what was inside.","Perhaps they were some fruits and vegetables that needed to be placed in a cool and well-ventilated area. Song Asan thought to himself idly.","The tower ship was three stories high, and Dai Li's party occupied the entire third floor and half of the second.","Once everyone boarded, the gangplank was retracted, and the large tower ship, which had caught the attention of all the boatmen and merchants at the Wuwen ferry crossing, slowly pulled away from the shore.","Time slowly flowed by, and the golden sun gradually slanted to the west, signaling the arrival of the evening meal.","Bai Jianping, as usual, sent their own cooks to borrow the kitchen. However, the soldiers returned and said, \"Commander Bai, they have already prepared dinner for us.\"","\"What is going on? Didn't we agree with Shipmaster Zhou earlier that we would prepare our own dinner?\" Bai Jianping frowned.","The soldier scratched his head. \"We did. But maybe the ship merchants are greedy for money, so they're going out of their way to be accommodating.\"","This wasn't an isolated incident. When they first chartered the boat, it was the same. They had clearly stated they would prepare their own meals, but the merchants still sent over snacks or after-dinner fruits.","Bai Jianping said, \"Decline it. We don't need any of it.\"","With the meals arranged, Bai Jianping thought the day's matters were settled. Yet, just as he was about to eat, the Second Young Master walked in. The Commandant usually dined with the Mistress. Could something have happened?","While Bai Jianping was feeling puzzled, Qin Yanzhou got straight to the point. \"Commander Bai, there is a man in the escort guard team with a black hairy mole by his mouth. I just saw him sneaking suspiciously into a room on the first floor.\"","Of course, this statement was a lie.","But Bai Jianping didn't know that. He drew in a sharp breath. \"To think we actually hired someone with light fingers?\"","The first floor was the area where the ship merchants lived.","Bai Jianping was deeply disgusted. \"He boarded the ship with us. If a theft occurs, won't the blame fall on us? Dealing with a petty thief is a small matter, but ruining the Mistress's reputation is a big deal.\"","Growing angrier as he spoke, Bai Jianping immediately declared, \"I will go apprehend him.\"","\"Hold on, Commander Bai!\" Qin Yanzhou stopped him. \"To catch a thief, you need to catch them with the loot. I only saw him acting suspiciously; I didn't actually catch him stealing anything. Besides, he has likely already left. If we grab him now without proof or evidence, and he adamantly denies it, it will only make us look like we are throwing our weight around.\"","Bai Jianping calmed down.","He then listened as Qin Yanzhou continued, \"Several martial artists were hired along with him. However, it is currently unclear whether this is just a personal issue with him, or if we inadvertently hired a whole den of thieves. Commander Bai, it would be better to first take inventory to see if anything is missing, and to strengthen our guard tonight to prevent any thefts from occurring. Once we reach the next town, we can replace this entire batch of men.\"","Bai Jianping agreed.","After Qin Yanzhou left, the battle-hardened commander stood by the window for a long time.","The window was wide open, and the moisture-laden wind from the river blew in, carrying a few hints of the fishy smell of aquatic goods, which wasn't a pleasant scent. And blowing in along with it was a cloud of suspicion.","This strange feeling had been present ever since they split their forces, though it was initially suppressed by the Mistress's words, \"I have already sent word to the Marquis.\"","Later on, the Mistress changed her usual quiet demeanor and insisted on sightseeing, causing the doubts to resurface. And now, his confusion was like an inkstone being constantly ground with an inkstick, its color growing increasingly dark.","The Second Young Master just said someone sneaked into the first floor.","Why didn't he catch him when he saw it? He himself said that to catch a thief, you need the loot. If he had quietly followed him at that moment, wouldn't he have caught the man red-handed?","Or perhaps, that man was no petty thief at all, and...","Bai Jianping shivered, breaking out in a thin sweat at his own terrifying conjecture. He stepped out of his room and ordered, \"Arrange two extra shifts to stand guard together tonight.\"","He hoped he was just overthinking things, and he hoped the Second Young Master was simply too lazy to catch the thief himself, which was why he didn't step forward.","...","Inside a room at the far end of the tower ship's first floor.","\"It's nightfall, but they look very vigilant to me. There are many soldiers on guard tonight. Brother, what should we do?\"","\"What's the rush? It takes three days by water from Wuwen to reach the next county. It's normal for them to be cautious on the first day of sailing. Haste makes waste. Just wait.\"","\"Of course I can wait, but I'm afraid those dozen or so brothers can't.\"","\"They traveled through the night to get here and haven't slept a wink. Now they have food, drink, and a place to sleep. Why wouldn't they be able to wait?\"","\"Then I won't touch the white cloth on top. I'll swap it for the red one tomorrow... Brother, it's tomorrow night, right?\"","\"Tomorrow night it is. The day after tomorrow, the ship should be near Xin County. With so many people around, it will be inconvenient to make a move.\"","...","The thick black night faded with time. When the horizon took on the pale color of a fish's belly, yesterday had become a completely turned page.","Bai Jianping leaned against the railing and gazed into the distance, watching the green mountains on both banks retreat and the white waves tumbling on the river. As the fishy wind blew against him, his confusion only deepened.","Nothing happened last night. It was a peaceful night.","Could it be that he was overthinking everything?","Perhaps the lack of troops on this journey had put him under too much pressure, causing him to have these baseless fantasies.","His heart remained restless and uneasy.","And this uneasiness peaked after another sunset, just as he was about to fall asleep, when there was a sudden knock on his door.","The person outside the door took Bai Jianping by surprise.","It was Dai Li.","Her words astonished Bai Jianping even more: \"Commander Bai, I suspect we have boarded a pirate ship.\""]},{"number":174,"title":"Chapter 174","paragraphs":["Bai Jianping's pupils trembled slightly, and then he heard himself asking in a calm tone, \"Madam, why do you say this?\"","It was strange. He should have been dumbfounded, but that wave of surprise was inexplicably shallow, like a rising tide on a beach—seemingly turbulent, but when stepped into, it didn't even reach the knees.","Dai Li said hesitantly, \"There is something wrong with the incense in my room. When the windows are closed tight, I feel drowsy, my consciousness seemingly sinking into water, unable to float up. But if I open the window to look at the river view or step outside, I feel much more energetic. Later, I had the maid remove their incense burner, and the effect was almost immediate; that exhausting drowsiness disappeared.\"","As she finished speaking, she saw the muscles in Bai Jianping's jaw tighten, and added, \"Of course, that is just my suspicion. They could also say that the incense was lit to let me rest more and spare me the suffering of seasickness. Furthermore...\"","Dai Li's voice lowered a pitch. \"Today on the deck, I thought I saw a few crossbows. Would a civilian ship have such things? I haven't traveled much by boat, so I'm not too sure.\"","Bai Jianping seemed to hear a clang. Ah, it was the sharp sword suspended up high finally falling.","Ordinary hunters use bows, the most common being the long-siyah bow. The structure of a crossbow is much more complex, requiring bronze-cast trigger mechanisms.","How could such heavily regulated items be so easily obtained?","Bai Jianping said without hesitation, \"Madam, Zhang Danchen and the others are following right behind us. I will find an excuse to have the two ships sail side by side and let them come over.\"","Dai Li stopped him. \"It is already late at night. This ship owner surnamed Zhou has a large vessel; who knows how many people are actually on board? Rashly notifying the rear will only alert the enemy. It's better to wait until we reach the next town and then suddenly change our minds and replace them.\"","Bai Jianping didn't speak, just stared at Dai Li, and suddenly blurted out, \"Madam, did you already know?\"","Dai Li paused, her eyes flashing slightly. \"Know what?\"","\"Many things. For example, that there is a problem with this ship, or that our journey by water might not go smoothly,\" Bai Jianping said.","Dai Li raised a hand to smooth her hair at her temples, her voice gentle. \"Commander Bai must be joking. I am no immortal, so how could I have the ability to foresee the future? Besides, the Marquis and I are husband and wife; we are one, and our interests are closely linked. Why would I knowingly walk into a tiger's den?\"","Bai Jianping choked on his words. He actually had many questions he wanted to ask.","He wanted to ask why she didn't inform him immediately when she saw the crossbows on the deck. It was still daylight then, wasn't it? Many things that were now too late to do wouldn't have been too late then. He also wanted to ask why she insisted on dividing the troops; why the initial letters were delayed time and time again; and even more, what was the cause behind all these anomalies?","But he couldn't bring himself to ask any of it.","Not to mention that he didn't have the status to pursue the matter; even if he were qualified, the Madam, who had already denied it, wouldn't necessarily be honest.","\"It's getting late. I will go back and rest first.\" Dai Li took her leave.","After stepping out of the room, she didn't go back directly, but walked all the way to the end of the third floor.","Leaning against the railing and looking out from here, one could see the deck piled high with cargo and the tall mast. The white flag at the top of the mast had been replaced by a red one at some unknown time. The bright red flag fluttered in the wind, its rippling curves looking like churning waves of blood.","On the small circular platform under the mast used for keeping watch, a dark figure was currently standing. However, due to the height difference between the two, Dai Li couldn't see the person's face clearly.","But she knew he was there.","Setting out from Wuwen, it would take two nights and three days to reach the next town. And with many people in the town, it was not a good place to start a rebellion.","The first night had already passed; only tonight remained...","She could wait, but the Green Lotus Cult could not.","How many days had it been since the messenger set off for Chang'an City? Oh, it had been seven days. If the reinforcements hurried, they would still need two days to arrive.","She had a premonition that it would be tonight!","A thin layer of fog rose over the river. In the misty fog, the surrounding ships were cloaked in a half-hidden haze, and the green hills on both banks also became blurred, like some indifferent onlookers standing by.","Dai Li turned and went back to her room.","What needed to be hinted at had been hinted at; what needed to be arranged had been arranged. The rest was just waiting—waiting for the prey to fall into the trap!","Dai Li changed her clothes and went to sleep fully dressed. With things on her mind, she didn't sleep too deeply tonight, so when the first unusual sound erupted, she woke up immediately.","Sitting up while holding the quilt, Dai Li shook her head and soon heard someone pounding bang, bang on her door outside.","\"Madam!\" It was Nianxia's voice, sounding very urgent. \"We seem to have encountered water bandits.\"","Almost as soon as the last word fell, the door was suddenly pulled open. Nianxia couldn't help but be stunned, astonished by how quickly the person inside opened the door, and...","Madam had actually changed out of her dress!","She was wearing a black riding habit, the belt tied very neatly, not at all looking like it had been fastened in a hurry.","Nianxia stood frozen in place.","Dai Li walked past her out the door, leaned against the railing at the doorway, and looked down. She saw several dark figures scurrying across the deck below, sprinting towards the cabins, inevitably clashing with the crew members along the way.","Snow-white blades clashed with a clanging sound, and sharp shouts rang out continuously in the dark night, startling an unknown number of sleepers awake.","The area below quickly descended into chaos.","But compared to the melee on the deck, Dai Li was more concerned about the small boats rapidly approaching the side of the tower ship, or those already clinging to it.","Dark figures rode on the boats. These people quickly tossed the grappling hooks in their hands upwards. The multi-pronged iron hooks caught the edge of the ship, the ropes pulled taut, and the men below climbed up like geckos.","There were also black-clad men who had already boarded but were not in a hurry to charge forward. They spread out in a belt-like formation around the ship, efficiently assisting their companions who were still boarding.","Everything was methodical and orderly.","At a glance, it was clear that this was no spur-of-the-moment action, but a carefully planned operation.","\"Madam, the water bandits are coming in fiercely. Looking at their numbers... there must be no less than a hundred of them! What should we do?\" Nianxia also saw the chaos below.","Dai Li remained silent, merely casting her gaze further out, trying to find where the small boats were coming from. However, her field of vision was limited; she could only glimpse the night prowlers flowing endlessly from the edges on both sides, but could see nothing more specific.","Dark clouds drifted in the sky, obscuring half the bright moon, and the fog on the river seemed to have grown a bit thicker.","Heavy and hurried footsteps pounded on the wooden floorboards as Bai Jianping, with a longsword hanging at his waist, rushed over. Seeing Dai Li already changed into a riding habit so early, deep horror surged in his eyes. Many things he hadn't dared to think about before were now popping up uncontrollably, like fish gasping for air in a stifling summer pond.","\"Madam, water bandits are attacking. The next hour will be quite turbulent. Please prioritize your safety and stay in your room; do not run around.\" His emphasis was on the last sentence.","Dai Li didn't look at him. She narrowed her eyes and gazed downward, where the dark figures on the deck were entangled in combat with the crew and the successively arriving Xuanxiao Cavalry.","The distance was a bit far, and as the fighting went on, Dai Li could no longer distinguish which were the crew members and which were her soldiers.","\"I'm afraid it won't be resolved in an hour.\" Dai Li stared at a certain spot below. \"Two on two, with the crew assisting on the side, and our side still cannot take them down quickly. If it isn't because fighting on a ship hinders the display of our true strength, then it means there's a mole...\"","\"Bang!\" A loud explosion suddenly erupted from below.","A wooden lid suddenly flew off one of the stationary crates on the deck. One after another, like a domino effect, eighty to ninety percent of the crates on both sides burst open.","Dark figures darted out from the crates. Carrying heavy objects and brandishing gleaming, snow-white blades, they joined the fray.","The area below descended into utter chaos.","Bai Jianping's face instantly drained of color.","These weren't just a few scattered petty thieves; an entire group had been hiding in the shadows. What else was there to understand? They had truly boarded a pirate ship!","The situation gradually shifted, the scales slowly tipping as their initial overwhelming advantage faded away.","\"Xuanxiao Cavalry, be on guard against all crew members and martial artists!\" Bai Jianping's voice rang out like a massive bell, loud enough for even the soldiers who hadn't yet descended to the deck to hear.","\"My Lady, please do not worry too much. Although the enemy currently outnumbers us, the corridors are narrow. As long as we hold the stairs, one man can hold off ten thousand,\" Bai Jianping comforted her.","They had nearly thirty Xuanxiao Cavalrymen. Even if they split off a small portion of their forces to eliminate the bandits, they wouldn't be throwing themselves into the tiger's mouth.","\"Defending is a good strategy, but the premise is that this tower ship can remain steady.\" Dai Li looked at the flames suddenly erupting below, a dark glint flickering in her eyes. \"Someone set a fire. It's hard to say if the ship can last until sunrise tomorrow.\"","Bai Jianping's heart skipped a beat, and he quickly looked down.","It was exactly as she said!","On the deck, where the wooden crates had been stacked, streaks of fiery serpents now flared up. The long flames slithered along trails of spilled oil, quickly licking across a large area.","\"My Lady, where is Commandant Qin?\" Bai Jianping belatedly realized that Qin Yanzhou was missing.","The rooms of the mother and son were only separated by the maidservants. There was no reason for the Second Young Master to still be sound asleep when the Lady was already awake.","Dai Li replied, \"Zhou Zhou went to help.\"","Bai Jianping made a prompt decision. \"My Lady, please stay on the third floor and do not wander about. I will lead men to eliminate the enemy and put out the fire.\"","This tower ship absolutely could not sink!","He raised his voice to summon several soldiers who hadn't yet gone downstairs, ordering them to guard Dai Li closely without taking a single step away. Then, Bai Jianping himself led a few men and charged downstairs with imposing momentum.","Downstairs was a complete mess.","Bloodstains were everywhere, and decapitated corpses lay scattered haphazardly in all directions. Old cargo crates had been hacked to pieces during the struggle. Was there any place that wasn't in shambles?","Bai Jianping looked around. At first, he thought it wouldn't be difficult to find Qin Yanzhou by the light of the fire. However, after checking several places and even asking quite a few foot soldiers, he received nothing but negative answers.","None of them had seen him?","How strange. Where on earth did the Second Young Master go?","Casually slitting the throat of a petty thief who tried to ambush him, Bai Jianping was just about to split off a few men to fight the fire when he suddenly heard someone yell in horror:","\"Oh no, they are scuttling the ship!\"","Bai Jianping's heart pounded violently. Listening closely, he could indeed hear the continuous thudding of hammering mixed in with the clashing of swords and sabers. He could no longer worry about putting out the fire; he hurriedly sent men to search everywhere for those chiseling at the ship.","\"Have you seen the Second Young Master? ...No? Then pay attention. Once you spot the Second Young Master, absolutely do not let him be left alone.\"","The deck was in total chaos. Those who had gone mad with bloodlust focused on their opponents, while those who hadn't focused on their surroundings. Therefore, almost no one noticed—","On the circular observation platform propped high up on the mast, a tall and slender figure had been constantly observing the scene below.","He took in everything: the small boats continuously approaching the large ship, the iron grappling hooks flying up one after another, the two groups of men locked in fierce combat, and even the people quietly scuttling the ship in the shadows.","The young man made no sound, allowing Bai Jianping to lead his men rushing around. Only after a thorough search did they finally find the saboteurs.","The enemy came prepared, and coupled with the fact that there was a mole on the ship, Bai Jianping was ultimately a step too late. The hole was carved large enough, the wooden planks were pulled away, and river water poured in endlessly.","The massive hull let out a sorrowful wail like a sinking whale, and the originally stable tower ship slowly tilted to the side.","Right at this moment, Qin Yanzhou leaped down, stepping on the hemp rope net hanging from the mast to quickly descend from the observation platform.","Not long after he came down, Song Asan spotted him.","\"Commandant Qin, Garrison Commander Bai was looking for you for a long time just now. So you were here!\" Song Asan was overjoyed.","Qin Yanzhou asked, \"Where is he? I have an urgent matter to discuss with him.\"","\"Come this way.\"","The few men carved a bloody path, going down from the deck to the bottom hold, and finally found a disheveled Bai Jianping at the leak in the cabin.","Bai Jianping was overjoyed to see Qin Yanzhou, not even bothering to ask where he had been. \"Commandant Qin, this ship cannot be saved. It is only a matter of time before it sinks; we must evacuate as soon as possible! There are small boats prepared on the ship, as well as wooden buckets and crates, and we can also use the skiffs the bandits came in. Plus, Zhang Danchen's ship is up ahead, so retreating shouldn't be difficult. The only thing is...\"","Bai Jianping couldn't help but feel pained. \"We must travel light this time. I'm afraid we won't be able to bring our baggage and supplies.\"","The Lady's trunks and chests would likely all end up at the bottom of the river after tonight. Fortunately, their horse carriages hadn't been brought onto the ship; otherwise...","Bai Jianping suddenly froze. In that instant, a strange thought flashed through his mind, but just as he was about to grasp it, he suddenly heard the young man in front of him say, \"Commander Bai, the enemy spared no manpower or resources to set up this trap. They are likely risking everything on a single throw and will not rest until they achieve their goal. Merely retreating will most likely not allow us to escape. Why don't we take a drastic measure and strike at the root of the problem!\"","The thought vanished without a trace, and Bai Jianping subconsciously asked, \"How do we strike at the root?\"","Qin Yanzhou replied, \"The enemy's tower ship is directly behind us, no more than a hundred paces away. Why don't we turn around and ram into it! Exchanging our damaged ship for their intact one will completely eliminate the hidden danger on the river.\"","Bai Jianping's heart pounded with fear. For a moment, he didn't know whether to ask how Qin Yanzhou knew the enemy's exact location, or whether he had thought clearly about the consequences. \"But, but...\"","\"This is the only superior strategy,\" Qin Yanzhou said in a deep voice. \"If we just perform a normal evacuation, how can the small boats we take contend with the tower ship behind us? It is still unknown how many vanguards are left inside the enemy's ship. Only by crushing their main base in one fell swoop can we secure a sliver of hope for survival.\"","Bai Jianping fell silent.","Song Asan gasped, his face showing hesitation.","\"There is no time to lose. If we delay any longer, it will be impossible to turn the ship around, and we will only be fish on the chopping block, at the mercy of others!\" Qin Yanzhou was exceptionally forceful. \"Song Asan, gather some men and follow me.\"","Seeing the calm face of the person in front of him, with his pitch-black pupils and eyes like cold blades, displaying a rare fierceness, Song Asan's heart was greatly shaken, and he couldn't help but voice his compliance.","After agreeing, he realized it was inappropriate and looked toward his direct superior. In the darkness, Song Asan could vaguely see the other man's brows knitted tightly together.","\"Time is tight, do not hesitate!\"","Bai Jianping let out a long breath. \"Understood.\"","The group split into two. One team carried their swords toward the ship's helm, while the other fought their way back onto the deck, climbed the hemp nets again, and rolled up the hanging sails.","To turn the ship around, they first had to shed its forward momentum. The Xuanxiao Cavalrymen were agile and coordinated perfectly. In a matter of moments, they had rolled up the sails.","At first, the men in black and the boatmen on the deck did not understand what was happening, until the bow of the ship slowly began to turn.","A quick-witted person saw through Qin Yanzhou's intention. \"Oh no, they're turning the ship around!\"","This tower ship was a hot potato; anyone it crashed into would be out of luck. Yet, taking the initiative to strike and stop it from turning around by ramming it wouldn't work either. If a perfectly good ship crashed into it, wouldn't they both take on water together?","Since it couldn't be touched from the outside, it could only be stopped from the inside.","\"Hurry and seize the ship's helm!\"","...","Dai Li was situated on the third floor. It was high up with a wide field of vision, allowing her to take in the chaos below.","Amidst the clashing of swords, the bow of the ship changed direction, and on the mist-covered river, she spotted the faint silhouettes of ships looming not far away.","Dai Li felt a wave of relief, knowing that the plan was already more than halfway to success.","Not far away.","\"Sir, the ship ahead has changed course!\" A man leaning against the railing on the second floor of the rear tower ship widened his eyes in shock. \"How could this be? We coordinated from the inside and outside, laying down an inescapable net. Our numbers are more than three times those of the North, and we acted quietly in the night. With such the element of surprise, how could we still fail to take them down? Sir, what should we do?\"","This matter was of great importance, so Diting had also boarded the ship. Seeing the situation, he hesitated for only a moment before ordering his ship to turn around as well.","The enemy's ship was likely already riddled with holes; its sinking was a certainty, merely a matter of time. As long as they employed a strategy of delay, they could naturally drag the enemy down without shedding a single drop of blood.","\"Quick, lower the sails and turn around!\"","Tonight blew a north wind, not an east or west wind. Therefore, as long as the angle of the sails was adjusted properly, heading south or north made little difference.","\"Damn it, the distance is a bit too close. I'm afraid it's too late.\"","\"Stay steady, don't panic. Our ship is smaller than theirs, so our turning is naturally much more agile. As long as nothing goes wrong, we will definitely be able to retreat unscathed.\" However, just as Diting's words fell, his expression changed.","Like parched earth cracking after a severe drought, his calm composure shattered into irreparable fissures. Diting raised his hand in disbelief.","The wind blew from the front, slipping through his fingers, causing the back of his robes to flutter wildly.","The wind direction had changed.","It had originally been a north wind, but now an east wind was blowing! This section of the river ran east to west; as soon as an east or west wind picked up, it would affect them.","The tower ship ahead successfully turned around and hoisted its sails again. Carried by the wind and wreathed in fire, it charged forward with overwhelming momentum. Knowing they couldn't avoid it, Diting hurriedly ordered an escape route to be prepared. \"Quick, lower a few vanguard boats!\"","Quicker than words could tell, the already short distance between the two ships rapidly closed. The tower ships collided, blasting a deafening roar across the river in the dead of night.","Terrifying waves surged on the river, and scattered wood splinters were quickly swept away. The people and objects on the ship tumbled and staggered in all directions.","Qin Yanzhou was well-prepared. He had ordered the few men around him to tie themselves to the wooden railings with hemp ropes. After enduring the initial massive shock, he immediately untied the long rope. \"Follow me.\"","The large ship lacked sufficient speed and impact force to snap the enemy vessel in half directly. At this moment, the bow of the large ship was embedded into the hull of the opposing ship, connecting them in a T shape.","The collision had ultimately damaged their foundations. The two ends of the T gradually splintered and slowly tilted inward, while the large ship also began to list to the side.","Qin Yanzhou led his men and charged to the bow, leaping onto the opposite ship from where the two vessels were locked together. \"The enemy leader is a young man around twenty-three or twenty-four years old. He favors white clothing. Find him quickly and kill him!\"","Song Asan, who was accompanying him, obeyed the order. At this moment, he had absolutely no time to ponder why the Second Young Master knew this so clearly.","The ship was in total chaos. Someone had set a fire, and the flames spread, illuminating half the sky. Qin Yanzhou moved swiftly through every area, even grabbing quite a few people to interrogate.","\"S-Sir fell down just now,\" one of the captured men stammered.","Qin Yanzhou's gaze sharpened. He quickly walked to the edge and peered down. Amidst the constantly crashing waves, he saw a patch of floating white.","Something wasn't right...","Alarm bells suddenly rang in his head. Qin Yanzhou spun around to block, using his long saber to deflect a sharp arrow with a loud clang. He abruptly raised his eyes, only to see a young man dressed only in his inner garments holding a longbow not far away. Seeing Qin Yanzhou looking over, the man quickly drew the bowstring taut and let loose a second arrow.","Seeing that the second arrow missed, Diting felt slightly disappointed. He tossed the longbow aside and drew his long saber. \"Mingdeng, I trust you have been well since we last met.\"","\"Did Liudao come?\" Qin Yanzhou asked coldly.","Diting chuckled softly. \"I've disappointed you. This time, only I fell into your trap.\"","With things developing to this point, how could he not know this was a setup? If it weren't a trap, how could the other party act like a prophet?","Heh, the dignified Madame Taiwei, just one step away from becoming the mother of the nation, yet she was willing to risk her own life.","Qin Yanzhou stepped forward and slashed with his saber.","Diting shifted his footing, sliding three inches away to dodge the blade, and said at the same time, \"Mingdeng, although you and I were not born of the same root, we have been brothers for many years. Do you really want to put me to death? If it weren't for my bitter pleading back then, how would Uncle have raised you as his own son!\"","The saber in Qin Yanzhou's hand struck faster and faster, its trailing edge even producing afterimages. Tempered with the color of fire, it was like the scythe of an Asura, leaving bloody gashes across Diting's arms and shoulder blades wherever it passed. \"I have long since repaid what I owed you. Also, you've slacked off on your training.\"","Diting struggled to resist, but the wrist holding his saber couldn't stop going numb and trembling. In the end, he actually couldn't maintain his grip on the blade.","Qin Yanzhou knocked Diting's weapon away with a single strike. As he shifted his blade, the tip pierced slightly into the other man's chest.","Diting jolted violently and swiftly retreated while clutching his chest. Knowing that saying more now was useless, he actually flipped backward and voluntarily plunged into the river.","The ship's hull was still tilting, gradually shifting from horizontal toward a right angle. Seeing Diting fall into the river, Qin Yanzhou took two steps to the railing and looked down. The river waters were turbulent, and he could faintly see the man's silhouette.","The young man took a deep breath, brought over a wooden barrel, and smashed it down, but it missed.","He smashed a wooden crate down next, but it still missed.","Seeing this, Diting down below let out a hearty laugh. \"Mingdeng, it seems heaven never seals off all exits! As long as the green hills remain, we shall meet again.\"","Qin Yanzhou's eyes were cold and dark. Many thoughts flashed through his mind, but in the end, only one was the clearest. He quickly removed his saber and other heavy objects, propped his arms on the wooden railing, and jumped off the ship as Diting's expression drastically changed.","Water splashed in all directions. The young man quickly surfaced after entering the river. Sweeping his long arms to the side, he swam next to Diting and forcefully shoved his head underwater.","Diting struggled madly. Seeing that he couldn't break free, he simply dragged Qin Yanzhou down to sink together with him.","Violent ripples surged up, blooming into a blood-red hue, as if dragons and snakes were dancing beneath the water. But slowly, the ripples calmed down. A long while later, a figure broke the surface with a splash and hugged the wooden barrel."]},{"number":175,"title":"Chapter 175","paragraphs":["The morning sunlight spilled across the earth, the thin mist was dispersed, and the dew-stained grass leaves slowly unfurled.","On this crisp autumn morning, a small boat was sailing downstream along the river. In the small vanguard boat were three people, two men and a woman, who appeared to be Dai Li and Qin Yanzhou, who had escaped from the tilting multi-story boat, and... Bai Jianping.","Bai Jianping sat cross-legged at the bow of the boat, resting his chin on his hand, in a daze.","The situation had been urgent last night, the firelight had dimmed as the boat sank, and the surroundings were pitch black. It was difficult to distinguish the people who had fallen into the water from those who had escaped by boat, and the scene was in utter chaos.","Not long after the two ships collided, he woke up as if from a dream, immediately abandoned everything, and set his mind on finding the mistress. Not to mention, he was lucky and quickly found her—","At the time, the mistress was boarding a small boat.","He immediately boarded the same boat with her, and later there were water bandits trying to board the boat, the chaos of which need not be mentioned. Anyway, by the time he came to his senses, he realized that in addition to him and the mistress, there was only one soldier on the boat.","The small boat circled the two sinking multi-story boats, and soon after they met the second young master. The space on the vanguard boat was limited, so the soldier had to take another boat.","Later, the river mist thickened, and in order to avoid the water bandits, they somehow got separated from the other boats.","Having held it in all night, Bai Jianping finally couldn't help but ask, \"Mistress, you actually did this on purpose, didn't you? You clearly knew early on that you would encounter water bandits blocking the way, but why didn't you reveal anything to me? I have served the Marquis for more than ten years, am I not worthy of your trust?\"","Dai Li shook her head and said, \"Platoon Commander Bai is mistaken. They are not water bandits, they are believers of the Green Lotus Sect.\"","Bai Jianping's body shuddered.","Dai Li smiled and sighed: \"That small leader of the Green Lotus Sect is cunning and highly suspicious. If I set up a trap with great fanfare, he definitely wouldn't come. At first, more than forty people traveling by water wasn't a lot, and later less than thirty people sharing a large multi-story boat was indeed few, but how can you catch tiger cubs without entering the tiger's den?\"","\"But...\"","Dai Li added: \"It's not that I don't trust you, quite the opposite, it's precisely because I trust Platoon Commander Bai to this extent that I dared to act so boldly. You see, aren't we all safe and sound now, everything is fine.\"","Bai Jianping felt that this made sense, but something still didn't seem right.","Dai Li ended the previous topic, \"Zhou Zhou, let's dock here, and then we'll walk to find a place with people nearby.\"","Bai Jianping turned around and saw that the mist had cleared a lot, and the river was bright and open. Let alone people and boat shadows, even birds were rare. Their small boat sailed downstream, leaving light ripples on the peaceful river.","The young man rowing the boat heard this and slowly steered the small boat to the shore.","Bai Jianping sat at the bow of the boat, he was the first to get off, and then turned back to help Dai Li ashore. And when he went to help Qin Yanzhou, he didn't expect that the young man had just stood firm when he suddenly struck him on the back of the neck with a hand chop while he was turning around.","This blow was fast, ruthless, and accurate, making Bai Jianping's eyes widen. Before the shock in his eyes could dissipate, he fell forward with a \"boom\".","Dai Li turned back to the boat and took out a hemp rope prepared in advance from an inconspicuous box.","Qin Yanzhou suddenly said, \"Mom, I plan to take off his clothes before tying him up, this will buy us more time, so leave the rest to me.\"","Dai Li: \"...\"","Dai Li looked at her serious son, touched her nose, and felt that this child was not purely cold in nature, but also had a lot of bad ideas in his stomach.","Well, like his father.","Dai Li: \"Okay, I'll leave it all to you, I'll wait for you ahead.\"","After Dai Li left, Qin Yanzhou took Bai Jianping to a place far away from the water bank, and then stripped him clean, not even leaving a pair of underpants.","After tying his hands firmly, he pulled out a rope and tied him to a tree trunk, and finally Qin Yanzhou took away the pile of clothes, but left a small dagger not far away, out of Bai Jianping's reach.","This was the only thing he left behind.","Wild beasts lie low during the day and come out at night, and this place is not far from Xin Commandery, so there is no need to worry about this naked Platoon Commander Bai being carried away by wild beasts.","*","After the golden crow rose to the middle of the sky, it slowly slanted westward.","Horses' hooves rumbled, and a hundred iron cavalry kicked up dust on the official road. The leading man was burly and stalwart, with deep eyebrows and eyes. He was majestic and upright while riding, making people look at him with awe. Any merchant caravan they encountered quickly made way.","He was travel-worn, his eyes were full of red blood vessels, and he hadn't shaved for an unknown amount of time, with a layer of stubble on his jaw.","At the city gate, commoners were whispering:","\"Have you heard? There's a bandit infestation on the Min River between Wuwen and Xin Commandery!\"","\"How could I not have heard? My third granduncle's brother-in-law is a boatman, and he said that a multi-story boat collided on the river last night, and a loud noise was heard from far away. Tsk tsk, these water bandits from who knows where are really rampant, but they were unlucky, kicked an iron plate, and capsized in the gutter.\"","\"What do you mean by that?\"","\"It is said that there was a noble on the hijacked multi-story boat, and the noble brought many private troops on the trip, all of whom were strong and powerful, no less than the soldiers of the government office. When these two groups of people met, didn't they break each other's heads? In short, the water bandits didn't gain any advantage.\"","\"Heh, you speak with such certainty, but how do you know the water bandits didn't gain an advantage? Those white stripes on the waves floating on the river are the most cruel and familiar with water nature.\"","\"Do you think I'm lying to you? Of course it was the floating corpses on the river that 'said' it! And today, when it was just dawn, I met a few men soaking wet on the road. I reckon they are mostly private troops of noble families.\"","The commoner touched his chin regretfully, \"I thought they wanted to take my donkey cart to Xin Commandery, so I could take the opportunity to earn a few copper coins, but I didn't expect them to just ask for directions and then turn back. I guess they are going back to the place of the incident.\"","Qin Shaozong listened to the floating whispers and looked in the direction of the sound. It turned out to be two coachmen gathered together talking in low voices.","They were now at the west city gate of Xin Commandery, waiting to enter the city, and must have come from the east like him.","Qin Shaozong thought for a moment and immediately made a decision, \"Mo Yanyun, you lead a team of men to enter the city first to visit the local governor, and I will lead men back.\"","If nothing unexpected happens, his wife was supposed to arrive in Xin Commandery today, which is why he rushed straight here. But looking at it now, he was a step too late, and some things had already happened.","Mo Yanyun received the order and led a team of men into the city.","Qin Shaozong turned his horse around and planned to lead men back. As a result, after riding for less than a mile, he met a... beggar.","At first, Qin Shaozong didn't pay attention to this person. After all, the person had disheveled hair, was bare-chested, and only had a piece of ragged sackcloth that was about to fall off wrapped around his waist. He wore a pair of extremely sloppy straw sandals that exposed his big toes, and coupled with his rough skin and dark complexion, it was really hard to shake off the identity of a refugee.","But as it happens—","\"Marquis!\" A sound like a cuckoo weeping blood.","Not to mention Qiao Wangfei beside him, even Qin Shaozong, who was often unperturbed, was startled.","Gazes fixedly looked over.","\"Old Bai?\" Qiao Wangfei was dumbfounded and kept asking questions, \"How did you end up like this? I heard that there are water bandits making trouble nearby, could it be that those water bandits are so poor that they even begrudge leaving a set of clothes?\"","Bai Jianping was overwhelmed with mixed feelings, but just then a breeze blew past. He immediately stopped caring about spilling his bellyful of sorrow and hurriedly tugged down the torn sackcloth around his waist, which had been blown up by the wind.","But his buttocks were still chilly.","A merchant caravan passed by, and a child sitting on a cart said to his father beside him, \"Daddy, that man is not wearing pants, shame on him!\"","The father hurriedly covered the child's mouth, \"Children's words carry no harm, please don't take offense, sir.\"","Bai Jianping: \"...\"","\"Bai Jianping, where is Madam?\" Qin Shaozong asked in a deep voice.","Bai Jianping tugged at the rag he had managed to beg from a traveler while giving a concise report of last night.","He started from when Dai Li came looking for him to say there was something wrong with the incense burner in her room, and then talked about the boat collision and the melee that followed, and finally how he was knocked unconscious.","Bai Jianping was both aggrieved and shocked. After explaining everything, he couldn't help but ask: \"My Lord, why do you think Madam did this?\"","He had thought about it all day and still couldn't figure it out.","Her husband was rising step by step, the backyard was peaceful, and Madam's position as the legitimate wife was as stable as Mount Tai; while her own son had made extraordinary contributions in the army, making all the gentlemen look at him with new eyes, and the soldiers praised him incessantly.","Her future was bright, so why would she abandon the light for the darkness?","No, you couldn't say she abandoned the light for the darkness. If the person killed last night was indeed the leader of the Green Lotus Sect, then Madam could never have joined the Green Lotus Sect.","Qin Shaozong's face grew colder and darker, \"Where did you wake up this morning? Take me there immediately.\"","A clever soldier hurriedly gave his clothes to Bai Jianping, who didn't care about being in public and put on the top first, then quickly pulled on the sackcloth to serve as pants.","Qin Shaozong rubbed the space between his eyebrows.","Bai Jianping got on his horse, \"My Lord, that place is by the riverbank, an area unreachable by official roads. The last stretch into the mountain forest cannot be ridden on horseback. And when I woke up this morning, I didn't find any trace of that small boat, so it's not impossible that Madam and the Second Young Master took the waterway.\"","Hearing this, Qin Shaozong called Qiao Wangfei's name, \"There is a ferry crossing in both Xin Commandery and Wuwen County. You are fully responsible for the search of these two ferry crossings. Remember to be careful and would rather catch the wrong person than let them go.\"","Qiao Wangfei cupped his hands and took the order.","Qin Shaozong added: \"Hu Bao, lead people to strictly screen the city gates in the southeast, northwest, and four directions of Xin Commandery.\"","Hu Bao took the order.","The team was divided into another part.","When Bai Jianping trekked over the mountains and ridges on foot, it took him almost a whole day to reach Xin Commandery. Now they rode horses, first taking the official road, then abandoning the horses and entering the mountain forest, taking less time.","However, by the time Qin Shaozong arrived at the place where Bai Jianping woke up in the morning, the sky was already completely dark.","They held torches and walked with the fire.","The flames illuminated a corner of the forest, and everything under the firelight was ordinary. Ordinary bushes, ordinary dead leaves, ordinary vines, everything was as ordinary as could be.","Bai Jianping hesitated for a moment, but finally said: \"My Lord, it is dark now, why don't we take a short rest? The only towns nearby are Xin Commandery and Wuwen. It's only been a day, Madam and the Second Young Master couldn't have gone far. Let's rest and build up our strength first.\"","Qin Shaozong looked around the forest, his eyes narrowed slightly, \"Is there a village nearby?\"","Bai Jianping really knew the answer to this question.","When he heard that Dai Li was taking the waterway, he felt inexplicably uneasy, so he studied the map for a long time, looking all the way from the Min River to the geographical terrain and population gathering places near the waterway.","Because of this, even though he was thrown into the wilderness, he was still able to walk to Xin Commandery as quickly as possible.","Bai Jianping raised his hand and pointed in a direction: \"There is a small village just behind that mountain. I happened to meet a convoy today and asked them about the size of the village. They said the village is very small, with no more than fifty households.\"","A small population meant that once a stranger entered the village, the whole village would know about it in no time.","Bai Jianping tried to persuade Qin Shaozong again, \"My Lord, if we don't rest, the soldiers and horses won't be able to hold on...\"","The men were fine, but every one of the military horses ridden by the Xuanxiao Cavalry was a top-quality breed. He had followed Qin Shaozong in battles across the country on horseback. Compared to the prominent families sitting high in the temples of Chang'an, Bai Jianping, who came from a humble background, cherished horses very much.","Qin Shaozong said indifferently: \"The ones in the team are basically the soldiers escorting Madam.\"","He took the official road and met the land-traveling team that had separated from Dai Li midway. Qin Shaozong then changed shifts, and the soldiers and horses that had followed him from Chang'an all stopped to rest, and the ones accompanying him were replaced by the more than a hundred people from the land-traveling team.","It could be said that except for the generals, everyone else had rested and was not exhausted.","Bai Jianping choked and tried to persuade Qin Shaozong to take care of his health.","Qin Shaozong turned a deaf ear, called ten people, and ordered a squad leader to lead the team to the small village overnight.","\"This place is in the middle of nowhere. If Madam doesn't go to the small village, the only options are Xin Commandery and Wuwen. And Xin Commandery is closer than Wuwen, and it is already strictly guarded. Once Madam and the Second Young Master enter the city, it won't be easy for them to leave quietly. A bow kept drawn for too long will lose its strength. It's just one night, why don't you take a rest? If you fall ill, My Lord, there will be no one to command, which will instead delay the progress.\" Bai Jianping tried to persuade him earnestly.","Qin Shaozong let out a breath of stale air and finally said, \"Let's rest here for the night.\"","Bai Jianping was overjoyed.","They returned to meet up with the squad guarding the horses. The soldiers scattered to gather firewood, built a fire by the official road to keep warm, and made do for the night in the wild.","Qin Shaozong leaned against a tree and sat down. His face was weathered and his eyes were bloodshot. It had been two days since he last slept. The soldiers around him were sleeping haphazardly, some even snoring, but he didn't feel sleepy at all.","The fire burning in his heart was still burning, not stopping for a moment, as if it was going to burn holes in his internal organs.","Qin Shaozong looked up at the bright moon in the sky.","The bright moon hung high, its light shining brightly, shining on him, but not only on him.","So far away, out of reach.","Qin Shaozong slowly closed his eyes, his hand resting on the hilt of the sword at his waist, his long fingers tapping it rhythmically.","It takes three days and two nights to travel from Wuwen to Xin Commandery by waterway. If she continued to travel west by boat, she would arrive at the Xin Commandery ferry crossing this afternoon.","But she probably wouldn't take the waterway.","The reason was simple. After she disappeared, Zhang Danchen, who was on another tower ship, would definitely send people to look for her on the Min River. And the vanguard boat had no sails, so its speed couldn't compare to a boat with sails. If she continued on the waterway, she would inevitably be caught up by those behind.","As for the village, although he sent a team of people there, Qin Shaozong privately felt that the chances of that fox going there were very small.","A village with fifty households was too small. Any stranger entering could not hide the news, so it was definitely not a good place to go.","He took the land route, which was the official road, from Chang'an through Wuwen County, and finally to Xin Commandery. After meeting that land-traveling squad, every large or small team he encountered next was strictly inspected, but there was no trace of her. From this, it could be seen that the fox definitely didn't go in the direction of Wuwen.","If she didn't turn back, she could only go to Xin Commandery, and then change her route from Xin Commandery to other places.","But just to be safe, he had to have people search the nearby mountains tomorrow.","His only advantage was time.","*","Dai Li and Qin Yanzhou arrived at Xin Commandery at noon.","Instead of going straight to the ferry crossing to transfer, Dai Li took her son to a medical clinic first.","Qin Yanzhou had not rested for a single moment last night. Between scaling heights to scout the enemy's movements, charging into battle with his blade drawn, and eventually falling into the water, he had been through a lot. When Dai Li later examined her son, she found two blade wounds on his body. Consequently, as soon as they entered the city, she took him straight to the medical clinic to get his injuries treated first.","Once they left the clinic, the famished mother and son made a detour to an eatery to appease their rumbling stomachs.","As winter approached, the days grew shorter and the nights longer. By the time Dai Li and Qin Yanzhou emerged from the eatery and purchased two new sets of travel gear for their long journey, the sun was already setting in the west. It was simply too late to leave the city now.","Exhausted, Dai Li massaged the space between her eyebrows. She had slept very little the night before, and her son had not rested at all. Thus, she made a decision: \"Let's stay at an inn for the night and set off early tomorrow morning.\"","Following her \"disappearance,\" the main convoy would undoubtedly search the river for her, perhaps even sending word to the overland group to join the search. Since all their time would be consumed by the search effort, they certainly would not head straight for Xin Commandery.","By the time they regrouped with Bai Jianping, she and Zhou Zhou would be long gone from Xin Commandery. As for the reinforcements from Chang'an, she had previously estimated that they were still about two days away...","Therefore, leaving tomorrow morning would leave her and Zhou Zhou with more than enough time.","Or so Dai Li thought to herself."]},{"number":176,"title":"Chapter 176","paragraphs":["Xin Commandery, Xinglong Inn.","A knock sounded on the door, followed by a voice drifting in from outside, \"Mom, can I come in?\"","Dai Li, who was getting ready to rest, paused for a moment. She walked over and unlocked the door. \"Zhou Zhou, what is it?\"","The young man entered. He had changed into a fresh set of clothes and was dressed neatly, not looking at all like he was about to go to sleep. \"I have something I want to ask you.\"","The guest rooms at the inn rarely had separate inner and outer chambers. The room contained only a bed, a desk, and a few wooden chairs; it was exceedingly simple. Dai Li walked over to the desk, poured her son a cup of water, and asked with a smile, \"You were up all night yesterday. Why don't you go rest first?\"","Qin Yanzhou shook his head and said he wasn't tired.","Dai Li said, \"Alright, then what is it that you must ask before you can sleep?\"","\"Mom, you didn't give me an answer before. Now that we have left the Marquis of Wu'an, could you tell me your reason for wanting to leave?\" Qin Yanzhou looked at her steadily.","Back when he was told they were leaving, aside from being stunned, he was mostly confused, unable to understand his mother's choice. Later, he sought out Nianxia and managed to get some information out of her. It turned out that two noblewomen had been gossiping at a palace banquet.","But initially, he thought his father had found a new lover, yet his mother's reaction didn't seem like she was worried about that...","Unable to make sense of it, Qin Yanzhou simply came to ask for the reason directly. He had a premonition that he would get his answer this time.","Dai Li froze, not expecting him to come for this. She opened her mouth to say something, but looking at the tall young man whose face had lost almost all of its youthful baby fat, she swallowed some of her words back down.","\"Sit down,\" Dai Li lowered her eyes.","Qin Yanzhou took a seat.","Dai Li poured herself a cup of tea as well and slowly began to explain, \"It all started when you acted as a scout and led troops to track the Xuzhou army. You hadn't returned for a long time, so I wanted to go find Qin Changgeng to ask for news. But just as I reached the door, I heard them discussing matters. Later, a soldier even reported that you, Zhou Zhou, burned down the Xuzhou army's granary with less than twenty men...\"","Dai Li propped her forehead on her hand. Her thick eyelashes lowered, making her look even more fatigued. \"You achieved a great merit. Mom was very happy and proud of you. I even sighed in admiration that my son is just as outstanding no matter what era he is in. But my happiness didn't last long before I heard the two gentlemen in the hall speaking.\"","As if recalling that moment, Dai Li pressed her lips tightly together before continuing, \"It is no exaggeration to say that after hearing it, I felt a chill rise from my heart. Goosebumps covered both my arms and even my back. It was terrifying.\"","Qin Yanzhou couldn't help but lean forward. \"Who was speaking at the time, and what did they say?\"","\"Your teacher Nalan, and Qinian's teacher Mr. Cui,\" Dai Li said.","\"What did they say?\" Qin Yanzhou frowned.","Those two were both core figures in the North, and it was said they had followed the Marquis of Wu'an for over a decade or two.","His teacher was even on good terms with his mother. He truly couldn't imagine what outrageous things they could have said to make his mother's expression change so drastically. Not to mention that all the generals were present at the time; they had no reason to...","Dai Li slowly raised her eyes. \"Nalan praised you, and Mr. Cui praised Qinian. It was like they were fighting in a ring, neither willing to yield. And the advisors who praised you or Qinian rarely praised the other party. Zhou Zhou, you should be able to see that it is only a matter of time before Qin Changgeng claims the throne. When that time comes, the vast new dynasty will also need an heir. Who will this crown prince be? Will it be you, or Qinian...\"","\"Mom, I have never thought about those things.\" Qin Yanzhou was stunned.","Dai Li said softly, \"I know you haven't. But even if you don't, there will always be people who do. Your teacher will, your teacher's close friends will, and your comrades who are like brothers to you will too. When you completely represent their interests, your own thoughts often won't matter anymore.\"","Qin Yanzhou stiffened.","Dai Li blinked her sore eyes. \"The current Qin Changgeng does treat us very well, but the human heart is always hard to control. I don't know if he will remain the same ten or twenty years from now. Furthermore... regarding Nalan taking sides, I don't believe he hasn't noticed at all, yet he never mentioned it to me. I'm afraid. I'm afraid he will use you as a whetstone for Qinian, and I'm afraid my child will eventually die in a bloody power struggle.\"","This was a thorn in her heart. Every time it was lightly touched, it pricked her so much that she couldn't sit still.","Such a major matter that concerned the future fates of so many people, why didn't Qin Changgeng talk to her about it?","Was it because he felt she was just a woman and there was no need? Or did he not want her to interfere, so he simply didn't bring it up? Or perhaps, he had never trusted her from the very beginning?","The night was deep. The inn was not luxurious, and there was only a single lamp in the room, casting a dim light.","Dai Li looked at her son's face, clearly divided by light and shadow, and tears welled up in her sore eyes. \"I'm sorry, Mom made this decision on her own. I know that compared to this life of hiding, you definitely preferred how things were before. I also understand that this goes against your ambitions. But I really...\"","The tears in her eyes finally fell. Dai Li choked with emotion, \"Last time, I didn't know that school bus would get into an accident, so I couldn't stop it. But this time, I had a premonition. I really couldn't just ignore it.\"","A handkerchief was handed over.","\"Mom, actually, things are much better now than in the beginning. When I was still in the Green Lotus Sect, and still at the Fan Manor, I never thought that one day I would be able to break free from that sect and reunite with you.\" Qin Yanzhou smiled faintly. \"Teacher once said that if things don't go as planned in the end, please believe that heaven must have made other arrangements.\"","Dai Li stared at him blankly, as if she wasn't quite looking at him. A bizarre and vivid scene flashed before her eyes.","A little boy carrying a small backpack with a cartoon water bottle hanging around his neck waved to her, then turned around and gradually walked away with his back to the setting sun.","At the same time, a tall and slender young man walked toward her against the setting sun. The large and small figures crossed paths. The small figure walked further and further away, while the young man drew closer and closer until he finally stood before her.","He was taller and stronger than her, full of vitality, like a large tree one could lean against for shade.","Dai Li's face was covered in tears, and she sobbed uncontrollably.","*","The golden sun climbed over the horizon, flapping its wings a couple of times as it slowly soared higher. Xin Commandery, awakened by the sunlight, was incredibly bustling. A commandery was one level higher than a county; even as a smaller commandery in Yuzhou, Xin Commandery still had a population of over a hundred thousand.","The Xinglong Inn was situated at the edge of the busy market. People came and went all around, and the noise of the crowd was deafening.","\"Have you heard? A noble from above has arrived in the commandery.\"","\"How could I not have heard? All four city gates are sealed... No, you can't say sealed, more like strictly inspected. I wonder what they're looking for? Could it be that the river bandits from the Min River snuck into Xin Commandery the day before yesterday?\"","\"Who knows. But having more guards in the city is a good thing overall. Didn't Uncle Zhao say his house was burgled the other day? This time, those petty thieves will definitely be like turtles hiding in their shells, not daring to make a move.\"","...","Qin Yanzhou stood by the open window, blankly listening to the idle gossip of the passersby below. A few breaths later, his expression suddenly changed drastically.","Tossing his washcloth into the basin, he quickly walked to the door, pulled it open, and headed out.","The light outside the door was even brighter. The daylight was in full glory; it was long past the early morning when he and Dai Li had agreed to set off yesterday.","Qin Yanzhou had woken up late.","He hadn't slept for a day and a night prior, and had done a lot of physical labor. Plus, after Dai Li's confession last night, he was thinking about the future, so even though his body was exhausted, he couldn't fall asleep right away.","As a result, once he did fall asleep, he accidentally overslept.","\"Mother,\" Qin Yanzhou knocked on the door next door.","He knocked for quite a while before the door opened. Behind it stood Dai Li, her eyes heavy with sleep and her dark hair disheveled, clearly having just woken up as well.","\"Mother, it is already the hour of Si,\" Qin Yanzhou said.","That single sentence instantly scared away the last remnants of Dai Li's sleepiness.","The hour of Si, ten in the morning!","\"Oh no, we woke up late,\" Dai Li said with a headache.","Her emotions had fluctuated wildly last night. After crying, she was utterly exhausted, not to mention she had barely closed her eyes for most of the previous night, which was why she slept until now. Had she not been woken by her son, Dai Li could have slept for another two hours before getting up.","\"So be it. It doesn't matter if we are a little late; we still have time to leave the city now,\" Dai Li quickly composed herself.","However, as soon as she spoke, she saw her son shake his head.","\"Mother, I heard that several city gates of Xin Commandery have been placed under martial law this morning.\" Qin Yanzhou looked at his mother's suddenly pale face and said softly, \"It seems the Marquis of Wu'an's men have found their way here.\"","It felt as though something exploded in her mind. Dai Li grew dizzy and reached out to hold the doorframe just to steady herself. \"Are you sure they are really his men?\"","Qin Yanzhou truthfully replied that he wasn't certain. Seeing Dai Li looking dazed, he said, \"Mother, I will go find out the truth and be back soon.\"","Before he could even take a step, his arm was grabbed.","\"Zhou Zhou, don't go! There are quite a few soldiers from the North who recognize you. If it really is Qin Changgeng's men, you might be discovered the moment you step out.\" Dai Li was filled with worry.","Qin Yanzhou explained, \"Yesterday I saw a few children playing at the back door of the inn. They are likely the children of the hired help or locals from the neighborhood. Mother, I won't go far. I'll just ask them to help me find out what's going on and return shortly.\"","Only then did Dai Li let go of him.","After her son left, Dai Li was filled with anxiety.","Could it be that Bai Jianping successfully regrouped with the river troops and informed everyone of her \"defection\"?","But that didn't make sense either. If that were true, how could he be certain that she and Zhou Zhou were in Xin Commandery, rather than having crossed the mountains to go somewhere else? Or perhaps someone received them and they simply changed routes back to Wuwen. After all, if she had taken the official road back to Wuwen at that time, he wouldn't have known!","A move as grand as directly locking down the city gates sounded very much like a certain someone's style.","But how could it be, so fast?","...","The time spent in a daze passed especially quickly. It felt like just a blink of an eye for Dai Li before the person who had just left returned.","\"Mother, I have bad news.\"","Qin Yanzhou's expression was complicated. \"The children said there are no less than twenty soldiers guarding the city gates. And Xin Commandery has four gates, meaning nearly a hundred men just for guard duty, which already exceeds the total number of soldiers traveling by water. Moreover, there are many more military patrols going back and forth in the city, all wearing uniform black armor...\"","Even though she was mentally prepared, Dai Li's vision still darkened for a moment.","More than a hundred men, black armor, the Xuanxiao Cavalry.","Qin Changgeng might have come in person.","Dai Li murmured, \"It's over, he is going to find us...\"","\"Xin Commandery is so large, far beyond comparison to a small county. Furthermore, we didn't use our own travel passes to check into the inn yesterday, so he won't know,\" Qin Yanzhou comforted her.","Dai Li's brows were tightly furrowed; she was not as optimistic as he was.","This was not her first time running away. Having experienced this twice before, she knew deeply that Qin Changgeng was not only extremely sharp, but also incredibly meticulous.","More importantly, he held great power and had the authority to mobilize the army. All inns, shops, and residential houses in the city would unconditionally cooperate with his search.","Although she and Zhou Zhou used fake passes to check into the inn, the time of their check-in couldn't be faked. As long as Qin Changgeng sent someone to the inns to check the travelers who checked in yesterday, and specifically filtered for a man and a woman traveling together like her and Zhou Zhou, he would absolutely be able to lock onto his target swiftly.","Dai Li first explained this to her son, then said, \"Zhou Zhou, those children at the door are already somewhat familiar with you. Why not bribe them again and have them help keep an eye on the entrance? If any soldiers come to the inn to ask questions today, have them place a bunch of wildflowers at the entrance of the back alley.\"","Qin Yanzhou nodded and agreed. \"Mother, if we can't stay at this inn, how about we spend the night in the East District? The East District is where the commoners gather. If we offer them some silver and come up with an excuse, staying there shouldn't be a problem.\"","Dai Li rubbed her temples, not telling her son that the very first time she was caught and taken back was in exactly that kind of urban village. She only said tactfully, \"We can't stay long in the East District either. As long as they post notices widely and attach a heavy reward, the commoners at the bottom will surely act like sharks smelling blood.\"","Qin Yanzhou pursed his lips.","\"However, making do for a night or two shouldn't be a big problem. Zhou Zhou, I have an idea. Why don't we go ask around about the wealthy households in Xin Commandery...\"","*","Xin Commandery.","\"My Lord Marquis, we have a discovery!\"","Bai Jianping returned with quick steps, looking excited. \"The old physician in the medical clinic on the West Street has seen the Madam and Qin the Second. They indeed went to the clinic.\"","Hearing this, the crease between Qin Shaozong's brows finally softened a little.","The night before last, the \"water bandits\" attacked the ship fiercely, their numbers far exceeding the soldiers from the North. According to what Bai Jianping said, Qin the Second had taken up a sword and joined the battle at that time.","Fighting in the dark, on an unstable ship, outnumbered by the enemy, the chances of getting injured were certainly much higher than usual. And given how much she valued her son, once they escaped, she would definitely take him to a medical clinic to treat his wounds first.","Therefore, after returning to Xin Commandery today, he immediately dispatched men to the various medical clinics in the commandery without stopping to rest.","This investigation indeed yielded clues.","This was good news. It proved his previous assumption was correct; she was indeed in Xin Commandery!","\"When did that old physician treat them yesterday?\" Qin Shaozong asked.","Bai Jianping replied, \"He treated them at noon. Qin the Second had a knife wound on his shoulder and another on his back. By the time they were treated, it was already the beginning of the hour of Wei.\"","\"They didn't rest all night the night before last, arrived at Xin Commandery at noon yesterday, left the clinic at the hour of Wei, and still needed to prepare their luggage for a long journey afterwards.\" The man suddenly let out a low, deep laugh. Even though he was laughing, it exuded the oppressive feeling of an impending storm. \"She definitely hasn't left! Pass down the order: strictly search all inns, big and small, in the commandery. Focus heavily on any male and female traveling pairs who checked in yesterday.\"","Bai Jianping cupped his hands to accept the order. He was just about to go carry it out when he was stopped by his superior.","Qin Shaozong turned the jade thumb ring on his finger. \"Have people post notices around the city. I remember the East District of Xin Commandery is a mixed bag, mostly inhabited by poor families. That kind of place is the easiest to hide in. Post more notices over there. At the same time, send five squads of men to beat gongs and drums, making sure to inform every household that they are forbidden from taking in outsiders. Violators will be thrown in prison.\"","\"Yes, My Lord.\""]},{"number":177,"title":"Chapter 177","paragraphs":["\"Today is the fourth day of putting up notices everywhere. We've sent out quite a few people and searched all the hostels in the commandery. But it's strange, we've actually found nothing.\" Bai Jianping cupped his chin and frowned.","Qiao Wangfei guessed, \"Could it be that the mistress and the second young master have already left?\"","\"But that's impossible, isn't it? Didn't Hu Bao say that no traces of them were found at the several city gates?\" Mo Yanyun frowned.","Qiao Wangfei said in a low voice, \"Don't forget, when we first met the second young master, he clearly had scars on his face, but later they were gone. He seems to be well-versed in the art of disguise. Is it possible...\"","Hu Bao shook his head and said, \"Impossible. The lord had specially instructed me earlier to have the soldiers pay more attention to those women with ugly faces but a figure similar to the mistress, especially those with a head of black, soft, and smooth hair.\"","A face can be covered, a figure can be made plump by stuffing clothes, and walking with a hunched back can also make one shorter.","But hair, which is nourished by blood and qi, is black and shiny if it is black and shiny, and withered and yellow if it is withered and yellow. It's not easy to change.","The hall quieted down, and the few people looked at each other.","Mo Yanyun hesitated and said, \"Were the people the old physician at the clinic saw really the mistress and the second young master? Could it be that he was old and his eyes were blurry so he saw wrong? After all, he is old. Otherwise, how can we explain that with notices flying everywhere, all hostels strictly investigated, and the military patrols out in full force, we still haven't found them.\"","Bai Jianping: \"Impossible to see wrong! The woman the old physician mentioned was wearing a black riding outfit. I guarantee with my head that she is absolutely identical to the mistress that night.\"","Qin Shaozong held a small tiger-shaped brush rest and played with it, not saying a word, listening to their argument.","\"Clack.\" The small brush rest was put down heavily.","Like a startling block being struck, the hall quieted down again.","\"Madam must still be in Xin Commandery. Just wait. She can't hide for long.\" Qin Shaozong pulled out one from the mountain of visiting cards. \"Write a reply to Prefect Huang. I will visit him tomorrow.\"","*","Xin Commandery is located in Yu Province. Although its scale is not as large as other commandery cities, it has the Min River flowing in front of its door, and a river course flowing from below. The two rivers do not converge, but form a sideways \"eight\" shape, sandwiching Xin Commandery in between.","Where there are rivers, there are naturally cargo ships. The coming and going of ships and convenient transportation have brought it an economy that other commanderies and counties envy.","As the prefect of Xin Commandery, Huang Shichang, although he has a penchant for lust, has managed to survive several storms of power changes safely because he is generally fair and very good at adapting to the situation.","Now that he has received the reply, Prefect Huang immediately ordered his servants to sweep the houses and clear the rooms, ready to welcome the distinguished guest.","The doors and windows were polished, and baskets of ingredients were transported into the kitchen, not limited to what flew in the sky, walked on the ground, and swam in the water. In addition, dancers and serving maids also had to be carefully arranged. Every one of them must be as beautiful as a flower, making Grand Commandant Qin feel comfortable. It would be best if he could open his mouth and ask for a few to take away.","The front arrangements were not difficult, but when it came to the women mentioned later, the butler was a little unsure.","Xin Commandery is more prosperous than other commanderies, and Huang Shichang has a rich family background. He loves beauties, and there are more than ten courtyards in his mansion to house the flowers he picked everywhere.","They are all flowers, but the difference between them is huge.","Some are in full bloom and highly favored by the master; some, although their colors are still the same, have been put aside by the master who likes the new and loathes the old; and some used to crown the small town but are defective for one reason or another, no longer as bright as before.","Anyway, it's a cluster of flowers, and a large area of pavilions and courtyards is fully occupied by beautiful concubines.","The manager considered and asked, \"Prefect, regarding tomorrow's banquet, do you think the beautiful concubines from Qingfeng Courtyard and Luohua Courtyard should participate?\"","The two pavilions and courtyards he mentioned were exactly where Huang Shichang housed his old flames. The beauties' flowering period has not passed, but they are no longer liked by the master.","\"Of course.\" Huang Shichang dug out a few outstanding old flames' names from his mind again. \"Let Lengyu and Xiao Tong come forward to serve.\"","The butler complied.","Time flew by, and in the blink of an eye, a night had passed. When the red sun just barely showed a corner, the heavy main door of the prefect's mansion was opened to the extreme.","The main door was opened early, but it was nearly noon when a group of men and horses came from a distance neither slowly nor hurriedly.","The master of the mansion had long been waiting on the side. When the man on the tall horse flipped down, Huang Shichang hurried forward to bow: \"Welcome Grand Commandant Qin to stop at my humble abode. My humble house is honored by your presence!\"","Qin Shaozong looked down at this short prefect who only reached his chest. The other party's small eyes narrowed very cleverly, like a dog wagging its tail. \"No need to be so polite. Prefect Huang is the parent official of Xin Commandery. I should have visited earlier, but due to official duties, it has been delayed until today. I hope Prefect won't blame me.\"","Huang Shichang hurriedly said, \"Grand Commandant Qin's grace of condescending to visit is higher than a mountain; the light of your arrival has shone on my humble family. Today is my good fortune of three lifetimes. How could there be any 'blame'?\"","Qin Shaozong tutted lightly in his heart. This Prefect Huang's political achievements are mediocre. It turns out that all his efforts are spent on flattery.","Huang Shichang hurriedly welcomed Qin Shaozong into the room, letting him sit at the head of the hall, while he sat below. As for the other accompanying military generals, they lined up in rows below.","Qin Shaozong came before mealtime. After taking his seat, he exchanged pleasantries with Huang Shichang for a long time. Seeing that the time was about right, the latter clapped his hands and asked people to serve food and wine.","*","Commandery Prefect's Mansion, Luohua Courtyard.","Dai Li sat in the room, watching Xiao Tong put on makeup in front of the mirror, making final preparations.","Xiao Tong looked at Dai Li from the bronze mirror: \"Qinghe, the manager said that a distinguished guest came to the mansion today, and he is a noble from Chang'an. Wish me luck. Maybe after today, I can leave the prefect's mansion and go to Chang'an with the distinguished guest.\"","The woman in the bronze mirror had an extremely beautiful face, but there was an old hypertrophic scar on her left face, pulling from the corner of her eye to her jaw, destroying the beauty of her whole face.","Xiao Tong had seen quite a few such dancers with defective faces. The commandery prefect's wife was jealous during her lifetime, and it was not that she hadn't looked for dancers to vent her anger on. There were several unlucky ones in the mansion whose faces were scratched, and they were the ones who were ruined by the mistress.","Prefect Huang probably felt somewhat guilty, so he set up a courtyard to raise them, treating it as raising a few more cats and dogs.","But...","This Qinghe, who moved into Luohua Courtyard a few days ago, looked very unfamiliar, like a newcomer. But the prefect's wife has been dead for two years. She remembered that among the disfigured dancers, there seemed to be no one with this name.","\"I wish you get what you want,\" the \"Qinghe\" in the bronze mirror said.","Xiao Tong hooked her red lips and withdrew her gaze. \"Thanks to your auspicious words.\"","Who cares why? There are many beautiful concubines in the mansion. Today, a few sent by some officials or merchants come in; tomorrow, a few Prefect Huang found himself come in; and the day after tomorrow, one or two are sent out. Coming and going like this, sometimes even the minor managers here can't remember the people.","After adjusting her attire, Xiao Tong gracefully left the pavilion and courtyard.","Dai Li looked at her back, slowly exhaled, and calmed her suddenly accelerated heartbeat.","The fact that she would hide among the concubines of a wealthy family was actually inspired by her past. When she first arrived in this different world, she mingled in the backyard of the Jiang family in Nankang Commandery.","She found that as long as the number of concubines was large enough, or there was a huge generation gap or estrangement between the concubines, there were loopholes to exploit.","But now, Xiao Tong seemed to be a little suspicious.","It was also because she came in a hurry at first. She directly climbed over the wall and came in. She was not well prepared and accidentally went to the wrong courtyard. She originally wanted to go to Pingqiu Garden, which was said to house disfigured girls, but ended up here. She also happened to have some inquiries and small requests, and finally she just went with the flow and settled down.","\"It should be fine...\" After comforting herself, Dai Li's thoughts drifted to her son who also sneaked into the mansion.","She didn't know how Zhouzhou was doing now.","A handyman, pulling weeds all over the yard, should be fine, right.","Xiao Tong went, and returned at the end of the un-hour. When she went, she was full of energy and pride, but when she came back, she was like a little cabbage that had been exposed to the wind and sun, and she had no energy at all.","\"What kind of people are they?\" Xiao Tong kept complaining, \"It's fine if the noble person at the top looks down on us, but one of his subordinates clearly talked happily with me, fed me wine, praised my beauty many times, and I also saw him very moved, why did it fall short of success?\"","Dai Li knew earlier that there would be distinguished guests today, but she hadn't heard the manager or other beauties mention who the visitors were. Now hearing Xiao Tong's description, her heart skipped a beat, \"Are the guests all tall and strong men?\"","Xiao Tong first said yes, and then said that Lord Huang called the noble person at the top the Taiwei, \"That's the Taiwei! The Emperor is young, shouldn't everything in the court follow the Taiwei?\"","Dai Li pursed her lips.","The distinguished guest today was indeed Qin Changgeng.","\"Have they left?\" Dai Li asked.","Xiao Tong nodded and said, \"Naturally. Today Lord Huang only set up a luncheon, not a dinner.\"","*","After drinking and eating well, the guests returned happily.","After being sent out of the main gate by Huang Shichang, Qin Shaozong rode the Red Dragon back, the reins pulled very loosely, letting the horse walk slowly.","A group of military generals behind him were discussing just now.","\"The scale of this new county is not large, I didn't expect it to be quite prosperous, this Lord Huang has some family background!\"","\"In the final analysis, the transportation here is convenient, extending in all directions, both water and land routes work, so naturally there are many merchants passing by. Coming from the south and going to the north, everyone comes to take a look.\"","\"Hey, don't tell me, there are really many beauties in that hall just now, gentle, hot, cold, charming, it's simply a variety of beauties, it dazzles my eyes. Tsk, this Huang Shichang is a man who knows how to enjoy life. With so many beauties, can he remember them all? Maybe they are not even on the list.\"","Qin Shaozong suddenly stopped the horse.","The force of braking the horse was a bit strong, and suddenly, his Red Dragon stopped, snorted unhappily, and stomped twice on the spot.","\"Lord?\" Bai Jianping and others also stopped their horses.","\"What did you just say?\" Qin Shaozong looked sideways at Mo Yanyun.","Mo Yanyun was stunned. That overly sharp and cold gaze made his brain crash for a moment, and he stammered: \"W-what?\"","Remembering just now, Mo Yanyun whispered: \"I said there are many beauties in that hall...\"","Qin Shaozong: \"Not this sentence.\"","Mo Yanyun racked his brains to recall, and tentatively said: \"This Huang Shichang is a man who knows how to enjoy life...\"","Qin Shaozong stopped talking, and his long fingers holding the reins quickly tapped the leather rope.","He suddenly remembered a past event.","When she was in the Jiang Mansion in Nankang County, she used the pseudonyms \"Feng Chun\" and \"Songlan\", and hid in the backyard, as flexible as a swimming fish.","Now the posthouses in the county have been searched, the city gates are under martial law, and people have been sent to the eastern district to screen again and again, but there is still no sign of that fox. It's as if she disappeared out of thin air.","Will she repeat her old trick?","Qiao Wangfei reacted, \"Lord, do you suspect that the mistress is hiding in the Huang Mansion?\"","Qin Shaozong: \"She may not be at Huang Shichang's place, she may also be hiding in another large household in the county. Don't alert the snake, send someone to secretly investigate the number of concubines kept by the large households in the county first.\"","After this order was given, before sunset that day, Qin Shaozong got a piece of information.","The mulberry paper listed a group of prominent families in the new county. The information was very detailed. Who was in the family, whether the parents were still alive and the family had not been divided, the number of domestic servants, female servants, and female family members were all clearly marked with numbers.","Qin Shaozong picked up the wolf-hair brush and crossed out all the families with less than a hundred female servants. And with this exclusion, there were only a few families left on the paper, which could be counted on one hand.","The man's long fingers placed on the table tapped lightly, and according to the situation of each family, he crossed out two more large households.","Those who hadn't divided the family and several brothers still lived together, at first glance there were many female family members in the mansion, but when distributed to each branch, it was actually just like that.","The Huang family of the County Governor Huang Shichang was heavily circled by Qin Shaozong.","Huang Shichang's parents had passed away, and he only had two younger sisters born of the same mother, who both married out of town. The collateral branch of the Huang family was still in the new county, but they didn't live with him.","In Huang Shichang's mansion, there were only his children, as well as room after room of beauties and servants.","After pondering for a moment, Qin Shaozong wrote a visiting card, and then called Bai Jianping outside, \"Send the card to the Huang Mansion. In addition, have someone keep a close eye on the gates of the Huang, Jiang, and Zhao families.\"","\"Yes.\"","*","Huang Mansion.","Obviously the banquet had ended smoothly, and Qin Changgeng had also left with his subordinates. However, for some unknown reason, Dai Li felt inexplicably uneasy.","She guessed secretly, and finally attributed the uneasiness to her roommate Xiao Tong's growing curiosity about her.","\"Qinghe, where are you from?\" Xiao Tong stared at Dai Li intently.","Dai Li said her hometown was in the south.","Xiao Tong smiled, \"I see you indeed look like you came from a water town. By the way, how did you enter the mansion?\"","Dai Li lowered her eyes, feeling a bit annoyed in her heart, \"Actually it's nothing more than the word 'luck'. I unfortunately ruined my face earlier, and originally thought that the rest of my life would be poor and destitute, but I didn't expect that there would be a silver lining, and I was unexpectedly taken in by Lord Huang.\"","Xiao Tong smacked her lips at this.","Tsk, it's like a riddle, she said it, but it seems like she didn't say anything.","She wanted to ask more carefully, but heard someone coming in a hurry outside. Xiao Tong was puzzled, she seemed to hear Manager Li's voice.","The person outside spoke again, it was really Manager Li!","Xiao Tong hurriedly went out, and saw the manager say to her: \"Xiao Tong, ask all the people in your garden to come out.\"","\"Manager Li, what happened?\" Xiao Tong asked.","Manager Li scolded: \"Why ask so much? Come out when you are told to come out, go to the hall, the distinguished guest has an important matter.\"","The word \"distinguished guest\" entered the room, drifted into Dai Li's ears, shocking her so much that her pupils shrank, and she subconsciously curled her fingers.","Another distinguished guest? And asking all the girls in the garden to go out, what is this for?","Could it be that the young manager was acting on Qin Changgeng's order? But he just came yesterday, and she didn't hear Xiao Tong say that something went wrong at the banquet, why would he suddenly return?","With a messy heart, Dai Li saw that among the girls who came out of the room one after another, one stopped and looked back at her, as if wondering why she hadn't left yet.","Dai Li had to get up too, and went to the yard with the other girls. She intentionally hunched her back to make herself close in height to the girls next to her, and stood at the back with her head down, successfully blending into the flowers.","Manager Li, who hadn't noticed an extra person, said, \"Are all the people in Luohua Garden here? Follow me.\"","After leaving the courtyard, they met girls from other quarters, and their procession grew larger.","After walking a short distance, Daili slowed her pace and quietly shifted toward the back of the line, but unexpectedly, Xiao Tong, who was beside her, noticed.","\"Qinghe, what is wrong?\" Xiao Tong asked.","Daili showed a distressed expression. \"I think I ate something bad and need to make a trip to the latrine. Do not tell the steward yet. I will be back very soon and will head straight to the main hall afterward.\"","\"Alright then, go quickly and come right back.\"","The people nearby were not familiar with Daili and minded their own business. They were not as caring as Xiao Tong and did not say anything.","Daili secretly slipped away from the procession.","The Main Hall.","Qin Shaozong looked expressionlessly at the young women lined up in a single row stretching from inside the hall all the way to the front courtyard.","Huang Shichang's small mustache twitched. His mood was a rollercoaster, unable to figure out what this newly appointed Grand Commandant was plotting, but that did not stop him from showing his loyalty.","Seeing that the concubines were all standing properly and neatly lined up, Huang Shichang hurriedly smiled and said, \"Grand Commandant Qin, all the beautiful concubines from my backyard are here. Whomever catches your eye, please feel free to take them away. To be able to serve by your side is a blessing they have cultivated over three lifetimes.\"","Qin Shaozong merely gave a noncommittal grunt in response.","The burly man walked past the sea of beauties. Some of the women cast amorous glances with watery eyes, some were intimidated by his imposing aura and subconsciously bowed their heads in fear, while others seemed to realize this could be a turning point in their lives, their eyes shining brightly.","Bai Jianping, Qiao Wangfei, and the others were also looking, but after scanning through the hundred or so women, they found nothing.","\"Are there any missing?\" Qin Shaozong asked in a deep voice.","How would Huang Shichang know if anyone was missing? He did not even remember exactly how many women were in his backyard. He immediately called over two stewards and ordered them to do a headcount and report back.","It took a full half hour to finish the count. The steward said, \"Reporting to Grand Commandant Qin, they are all here.\"","Qin Shaozong, however, suddenly raised his voice, \"If any of your friends made an excuse to leave not long ago, whoever steps forward to report it will be rewarded with one hundred taels of silver, a house, a fine shop, and will be freed from their slave status.\"","His words shocked everyone present, and an incessant uproar broke out all around.","Huang Shichang looked at Qin Shaozong in astonishment. \"Grand Commandant, what are you...\"","The rest of his words came to an abrupt halt because he saw Qin Shaozong raise a hand toward him, making a gesture to stop.","Qin Shaozong said, \"I will say this one last time. Whoever reports it will be rewarded! This is your only chance. If I leave, the bounty will be considered void.\"","The surroundings became so quiet that one could hear a pin drop.","A moment later, a trembling female voice spoke up, \"Qing... Qinghe just went to the latrine. I do not know if she has returned yet.\""]},{"number":178,"title":"Chapter 178","paragraphs":["Dai Li stayed in the latrine, pricking up her ears to listen to the movements outside.","This area was a compound where concubines lived. The Prefect had issued an order to gather everyone, and they all followed the order and walked out. With a large number of women, the sound of footsteps, whispers, and the clinking of accessories intertwined like a hymn.","The \"song\" went from high to low, and the flock of flowers went away.","Dai Li waited patiently for a moment until it was completely quiet outside before she peeked out.","Sure enough, there was no one.","She hesitated, wondering if she should go back to Luohua Courtyard. This place was not far from Luohua Courtyard, and it would only take a short walk to sneak back.","But if she popped her head out now, what if she was bumped into? That would be really bad, and it might backfire.","Thinking of this, Dai Li decided to stay a little longer.","The distinguished guest the steward mentioned was probably Qin Changgeng. If he couldn't find anyone, he would definitely leave. It was just a matter of time, and she just had to wait.","Although she had made up her mind, for some reason, Dai Li felt increasingly uneasy. Negative emotions seemed tangible, as if turning into sharp chirps exploding in her ears, making her breathe rapidly and her blood flow accelerate.","Her meridians throbbed, clamoring for her to leave quickly.","Dai Li steadied her mind and decided to trust her sixth sense, just as she believed Zhou Zhou was still alive when she first arrived here.","Pushing the door open a crack, Dai Li peeked out secretly. Well, it was still empty.","She gently pushed the door open and slipped out. Dai Li knew that once she left, she had to return to Luohua Courtyard as quickly as possible, so she ran out.","Her heartbeat was deafening, and Dai Li, who was so nervous that her ears were ringing, didn't hear the footsteps.","The latrine was filthy, so it was set in a corner. There were only two ways out of here: north or west. And Luohua Courtyard was in the north.","Dai Li naturally rushed north, but after running only two or three steps, she suddenly heard a sharp shout like a thunderclap.","\"Dai Li!\"","That familiar male voice was stern and cold, like a dragon soaring and a tiger roaring, startling Dai Li so much that her hairs stood on end and her hair almost stood up. She didn't look over there, but subconsciously sped up and rushed forward.","Qin Shaozong was already suppressing his anger, and seeing this, it was as if a knife had been plunged into his heart, spreading fine and dense pain. He stiffened for a moment, and then his anger flared up three feet high, and he lunged forward in one step to catch her.","He was in his prime, used to rolling on the battlefield, and never slacked off in his daily morning exercises. Plus, he was much taller than Dai Li, so catching her, who didn't exercise much, was a piece of cake.","Xiao Tong, who was leading the way, and Huang Shichang and others who were accompanying them, watched in astonishment as Qin Shaozong took a few steps forward, like a goshawk fighting a rabbit, quickly, ruthlessly, and accurately grabbed the woman in green, and hoisted her onto his shoulder neatly.","\"Qin, Grand Commandant Qin?\" Huang Shichang couldn't even speak clearly.","The other party didn't give him any look, carrying the woman with a scar on her cheek and walking quickly outside.","Xiao Tong was stunned, only feeling that something had shattered with a \"bang\". It turned out that the noblemen in Chang'an had such peculiar tastes, preferring the incomplete over the whole!","Bai Jianping came back to his senses and said to Huang Shichang, who was still dazed, \"Prefect Huang, the Marquis has something to attend to and must take his leave first. Let's gather another day.\"","There was no explanation for just now, nor did he say when \"another day\" would be. This polite remark only revealed one piece of information: they were leaving.","When Dai Li was first caught and hoisted up, she was terrified. Her abdomen pressed against the man's solid shoulder. Driven by the instinct to survive after losing her balance, her arms subconsciously wrapped around his neck, and her legs instinctively struggled.","Unexpectedly, just as she kicked, she was spanked on the buttocks.","\"Behave yourself!\" Qin Shaozong was full of anger.","Although he had quickly taken a few steps, turned the corner, and left the sight of Huang Shichang and others, being spanked in broad daylight made Dai Li's cheeks turn red with blood. \"Put me down, I'll walk by myself.\"","Qin Shaozong turned a deaf ear.","Seeing that he didn't respond, Dai Li became anxious. Just because that short stretch of road was deserted didn't mean there would be no one behind them, so she softened her tone and said to him, \"Qin Changgeng, carrying me like this makes my stomach uncomfortable.\"","The man stopped and put Dai Li down without saying a word.","Just as Dai Li breathed a sigh of relief, her feet left the ground again. Only this time, instead of being hoisted onto his shoulder, she was carried in his arms.","Just now, Dai Li couldn't see Qin Shaozong's face, but now that she was turned to the front, she saw it clearly. He probably hadn't groomed himself carefully for a long time. The stubble on his jaw wasn't shaved clean, making him look a bit rougher than usual.","He looked straight ahead and walked on his own, not looking at her, but the lines on his jaw were as clear as a blade, and his muscles were taut. The heavy majesty and sharpness suppressed his anger, like thunder rumbling on the Black Sea, about to strike but not yet striking.","How could Dai Li not know that he was extremely angry? It was just that they were still outside, so he hadn't settled the score with her yet.","The melancholy and panic in her heart were hard to stop, but she couldn't deny that when the male voice calling her name fell, the uncertainty and hesitation about drifting in the future were all blown away by the wind, disappearing completely.","The dust settled.","By the time Dai Li came back to her senses, Qin Shaozong had reached the front courtyard of the Huang Residence. His horse was pacing leisurely in the front courtyard, occasionally destroying Prefect Huang's flowers and plants.","Seeing its master striding over, Chijiao trotted over to meet him.","Qin Shaozong put Dai Li on the horse's back, and then neatly mounted the horse and sat behind her. He controlled the reins with one hand, and his other large hand tightly gripped the slender waist of the woman in his arms. It was unknown whether he was afraid she would fall off the horse or unwilling to let her run away without a word again.","The main gate of the Huang Residence was wide open, with only two soldiers guarding the left and right to prevent the horses from running out. Now it was convenient for Qin Shaozong to leave.","Chijiao was squeezed lightly on the belly and immediately ran out of the residence.","Qin Shaozong had been staying in the posthouse these days. He declined the residences given by the major households in the commandery and just waved his hand to rent a posthouse as a place to stay.","The posthouse was not far from the Huang Residence, and they didn't have to pass through the busy market. Chijiao galloped with all four hooves. To Dai Li, it seemed that the horse had reached its destination in the blink of an eye.","The heat source against her back left. Seeing that he had dismounted, Dai Li grabbed the saddle with both hands and wanted to use the momentum to get down. However, before she could move, her waist tightened. He held her waist and carried her down, walking quickly into the posthouse like the wind.","\"Marquis.\" Seeing his superior return carrying a woman, the soldier was startled at first, and when he saw who it was, he couldn't help but be overjoyed.","The mistress had been found! They finally didn't have to soak in the ice cellar every day.","The wooden stairs of the posthouse were stomped heavily, making a thumping sound, urgent and heavy, and Dai Li's heart was surging.","\"Qin Changgeng...\" she tried to call him.","But the man completely ignored her. Just like when he picked her up in the Huang Residence, he looked straight ahead and didn't even glance at her.","Qin Shaozong carried her up the three flights of stairs in one breath without stopping. Kicking open the door, he walked straight in and threw Dai Li onto the couch.","A dark shadow like a dark cloud loomed over her. Before Dai Li could raise her eyes, her chin was pinched and lifted by three fingers like pliers.","Their eyes finally met.","Dai Li saw the new white hair at his temples and the fine lines at the corners of his eyes, which seemed deeper than in her memory.","And inside this dimly lit tent, those bloodshot brown eyes resembled a swirling lake, ready to pull someone into their depths at any moment.","\"Did you let the words I said back in Nanyang County go in one ear and out the other, Madam?\" Though he was looking at Dai Li, every word seemed to be squeezed through his clenched teeth, as if he wanted nothing more than to tear her to pieces.","Nanyang County was the place where she had been caught during her journey south, the second time she had left him.","\"If you dare run away again, I'll break your son's legs!\"","\"I won't beat Qin Yanzhou... But if you dare run away again, we'll have another one, and when he grows up, I'll break both his legs.\"","Those words drifted across time and space to echo in her mind.","Dai Li's pupils contracted, and she shook her head in panic. \"No, Qin Changgeng, don't hit...\"","\"I told you, even if you run to the ends of the earth...\"","The two voices overlapped, then both came to a halt.","After a moment of stunned silence, the veins on Qin Shaozong's forehead throbbed violently; he had clearly recalled those other two sentences as well.","His anger surged even higher, far surpassing what he had initially felt. Yet, it was not merely anger; his chest ached terribly, as if a pot of boiling oil had been poured right over his heart, burning through his flesh. The very core of his heart seemed to blister under the scalding heat, only for those blisters to be violently pierced by sharp needles.","Dai Li knew this boded ill. She noticed his rapid breathing and the bulging veins on his large hand gripping the edge of the bed. He was clenching his fist with such excessive force that his long, well-defined knuckles were turning completely white.","He was furious; it seemed that nothing she could say right now would be appropriate.","Dai Li decided not to say anything at all. Trembling, she reached out and wrapped her arms around the man's neck. Seeing that he did not resist, she leaned in and kissed him. At first, it was just a light peck, like a dragonfly skimming the surface of the water to leave a mark, before she pulled back to look at him.","Qin Shaozong remained expressionless, though the emotions swirling in his eyes were deeply complex. It was hard to tell if it was pure fury or something else entirely—it was as potent as aged wine and as uncontrollable as a raging fire. On the surface, however, his expression was icy, clearly suppressing his wrath.","Dai Li leaned in to kiss him again, but this time, the kiss was much deeper.","After a few breaths of their lips and tongues entwining, those brown eyes flickered. Shedding his previous cold indifference, he suddenly reached out, wrapped his arms tightly around the woman's waist, and pulled her firmly against him, simultaneously deepening the kiss.","He kissed her fiercely, pouring into it all the frustration and anxiety of his days of travel, along with the blazing fury of learning she had left. The wildfire that had consumed him slowly condensed, turning into a deep, heavy quagmire that roared as it dragged Dai Li in and drowned her.","Dai Li felt a slight pain on the tip of her tongue; she even had the fleeting illusion of tasting blood.","The wet sounds of their kissing echoed, exceptionally clear in the quiet, undisturbed daylight.","Dai Li was trapped in the corner. In front of her was his burning chest, and on either side were his iron-like arms clamping her in place. His entire body was astonishingly hot, as if even his exhaled breath carried sparks, resembling a piece of red-hot iron that would sizzle and release a cloud of steam the moment it touched water.","The space in the corner of the bed was limited. Unable to move, Dai Li could only surrender to his thorough kiss.","When Qin Shaozong finally pulled back slightly, she did not even wait to catch her breath. \"Qin Changgeng, I'm so sorry I didn't tell you about this beforehand.\"","He sneered. \"Saying this only after kissing me, trying to use a honey trap on me—is this your idea of an apology, Madam?\"","Dai Li pretended not to hear this and continued, \"You've already read the letter I left for you, haven't you?\"","The veins on his forehead twitched, as if a surging anger was boiling beneath them. Just as he opened his mouth to speak, a soft, fair hand gently caressed his cheek.","\"Changgeng, please listen to me first.\"","The man paused, letting out only a cold scoff, but did nothing else.","Dai Li said softly, \"If I had a choice, I truly wouldn't have wanted to leave. Since we married, you have done exceptionally well; you are an excellent husband. Our family is well-off, providing a life of luxury, and I am not so detached from the world that I can ignore all material comforts. Furthermore, the matter regarding the fertile lands hasn't completely concluded. How could I not want to see Yuyang's golden autumn with my own eyes this year?\"","It was unclear which of her words had managed to soothe him, but Qin Shaozong's tone lost some of its initial ferocity. Still keeping a cold face, he asked, \"Then why did you run, Madam?\"","Dai Li slowly withdrew her hand. \"That supreme throne in Chang'an will be yours sooner or later. If I don't leave, what will become of Zhou Zhou and Qinian in the future? Do you really expect me to just stand by and watch those two brothers reach the point of taking up arms against each other? Qin Changgeng, I cannot do that!\"","Qin Shaozong was a man who responded well to a soft approach but resisted a hard one. After being caught by him, Dai Li had made up her mind to use gentleness to overcome his harshness, planning to slowly explain everything to him. Having weathered many storms in his life, he would surely understand her concerns.","However, now that she had truly been pushed into a corner with nowhere to retreat, Dai Li realized that everything was spiraling out of her control.","After all, she was not a precise machine and could not eliminate the interference of her own emotions, just as she had been unable to draft the Letter of Divorce for him in one smooth stroke.","All the late-night anxieties she had no one to confide in, the deep unease of not being trusted, and the profound confusion of endlessly tossing and turning while trying to guess the future—all of it erupted like an unstoppable flash flood in the face of his cold questioning.","\"Nalan is clearly taking a stand for Zhou Zhou, openly competing against Master Cui. As their superior, do not give me that nonsense about this not being under your instruction. You kept the things you did in the dark from me, telling me absolutely nothing. I was left with no choice but to figure it out on my own.\"","Dai Li's emotions grew increasingly agitated. \"Using history as a mirror, one can understand the rise and fall of dynasties. The consequence of leaving those two brothers alone will inevitably lead to internal strife, making them sworn enemies! Even you, Qin Changgeng, will likely not meet a good end in the future. How can you expect me to stay? You left me absolutely no room to stay!\"","In the past, when Li Shimin and Li Jiancheng vied for power, Emperor Taizong ultimately emerged victorious, resulting in his brother's defeat and death. At that time, Emperor Gaozu was directly placed under house arrest and forced to name his second son as the Crown Prince. Later, he became the Retired Emperor, allowing his second son to take the throne.","Of course, Dai Li did not believe that Qin Shaozong, a man who had spent half his life on the battlefield, was an exact parallel to the historical figures she knew.","But the saying remained true: \"Using history as a mirror, one can understand the rise and fall of dynasties.\" Even if events did not follow that exact historical trajectory without a single deviation, there would undoubtedly be similarities.","After all, that was the ultimate authority over the world, possessing an absolute and unreasoning power over life and death. Like turning stone into gold, whoever received its favor could experience a meteoric rise, elevating their entire clan alongside them. The same held true for life and death—if the ruler commanded a subject to die, the subject had no choice but to die.","In the face of such absolute power, how many people could truly keep their hearts as still as water and remain entirely unmoved?"]},{"number":179,"title":"Chapter 179","paragraphs":["After Dai Li's outburst, the room grew so quiet that one could hear a pin drop. The atmosphere became increasingly frigid.","Having vented her frustrations, Dai Li's vision blurred for a fleeting moment. She wanted to turn her head away to avoid looking at the man before her, but he chose that exact moment to raise his hand.","His long, calloused fingers brushed against the reddened corners of her eyes, wiping away the tears that were on the verge of falling. His movements were clumsy, clearly showing he was unaccustomed to doing such things.","A breeze blew in through the windowsill. In this silent concession, the tense atmosphere in the room slowly began to circulate.","\"So fond of shedding tears. When you wrote me that letter of divorce, how many sheets of paper did you ruin with them?\" Qin Shaozong's fingertips, which had just brushed away her tears, felt inexplicably hot.","\"...I did not,\" Dai Li stiffened, attempting once again to turn her head away from him.","But after wiping her tears, Qin Shaozong smoothly halted her movement, forcing Dai Li to face him. Her eyes were red, as was the tip of her nose; right now, she looked less like a cunning fox and more like a red-eyed bunny.","\"Still denying it? The bottom of the letter was completely soaked through,\" Qin Shaozong teased.","Being repeatedly called out with glaring evidence, Dai Li grew annoyed. Under normal circumstances, she would have definitely lost her temper or stormed off. But right now, she could not escape, nor was it wise to add fuel to the fire at such a critical juncture.","Dai Li could only purse her lips and remain silent.","Seeing her silence, Qin Shaozong paused for a moment before saying, \"I never intended to keep it from you forever.\"","Dai Li's emotions surged, and a trace of resentment slipped into her voice. \"Never intended to keep it from me forever? Did you mean to wait until I found out on my own, just like now, before confessing to me?\"","\"I originally planned to be completely open and honest with you once I returned to Yuyang,\" Qin Shaozong said calmly.","As for what happened next, he didn't say. There was no need to; after that, she had wanted to just walk away and never even considered returning to Yuyang.","Dai Li could feel her pulse pounding fiercely in her veins. She didn't know if he was telling the truth or not. But at this point, the truth of that statement no longer mattered.","What mattered was what came next.","\"Then, what are your plans?\" Dai Li lowered her eyes. As she asked this, she subconsciously clutched a small section of her skirt, wrinkling the green fabric.","Qin Shaozong did not answer her directly. Instead, he spoke of his past intentions. \"A long time ago, perhaps over a decade ago, my intended heir was actually Yun Ce.\"","Dai Li froze. She was surprised, yet somehow not entirely so. On the night of Yun Ce and Zhou Zhou's coming-of-age ceremony, Qin Changgeng had gotten drunk alone in the armory, and he had revealed a hint of this back then.","\"Yun Ce was precocious. A book that an ordinary child would take five days to learn, he could finish reading in less than three. Furthermore, over the past three generations of his mother's Jiang family, apart from the mediocre middle generation, every other generation has produced brilliant minds. As for that boy Qi Nian...\" The veins on his forehead seemed to bulge for a second.","\"He is good with his fists and occasionally shows quick wit, but when it comes to studying, he is a lost cause. His essays are full of errors, and the books in his room do nothing but gather dust. Although you once mentioned he had some sort of dyslexia, in my view, even without it, that boy would never have the patience to sit still for a whole day. Moreover, Qin San is simple-minded and easily swayed; he cannot bear the tearful pleas of those close to him. Though Yun Ce is not my biological son, if my elder brother had not swapped commands with me on the battlefield back then, I might have perished in the sand. Therefore, I felt it was fitting for him to take over everything in the future.\"","Although the feudal dynasties of China were not as rigidly bound by the bloodline-exclusive aristocratic systems of Western Europe, it was not as if they did not care about lineage at all.","Thus, Dai Li probed, \"Did everyone under your command have no objections at the time?\"","Qin Shaozong answered truthfully, \"Of course not. In the early days, there were still members of the Wei family within the Northern faction, as well as those secretly allied with the Wei clan. They all tried to make me change my mind.\"","Dai Li saw him suddenly smile.","It was not the teasing, playful smile from earlier. This smile was drenched in the scent of blood, like a fierce tiger catching the scent of an intruder in its territory, about to open its gaping maw.","\"There don't seem to be any members of the Wei clan under your command now.\"","Qin Shaozong's eyes darkened. \"They were either killed or exiled, so naturally there are none now. Years ago, when my Qin family faced disaster, we were forced into a marriage alliance with the Wei family. After the Wei daughter gave birth to Qin San, the Wei family had already taken a large enough piece of the pie. Yet they later wanted to arrange a child marriage for Qin San, trying to monopolize his matrimony as well. It was pure delusion.\"","He did not despise ambition; in fact, he admired those who strove for advancement. But the prerequisite was that such people possessed genuine talent and a clear sense of self-awareness.","When greed crossed the line, and one no longer knew their own limits, it became a case of a snake trying to swallow an elephant out of sheer insatiability.","He loathed Qin San's maternal family. It was simply because the entire Wei clan, apart from the deceased great-grandfather, were all foolish and greedy.","Dai Li saw him reveal that chilling smile once more. He said, \"In short, those self-righteous old fools who fiercely advocated that 'only my bloodline can inherit my achievements' have been practically wiped out.\"","This was the path Qin Shaozong had initially paved for Qin Yun Ce, but a mishap occurred when his nephew turned twelve.","Seeing his smile fade and his whole being seemingly shrouded in heavy clouds, Dai Li guessed that something else must have happened later. This could be inferred from the fact that Cui and Sheng were now Qi Nian's teachers and were fighting fiercely on his behalf.","\"Later on... did Yun Ce fall ill?\" Dai Li asked gently.","The moon seemed to have risen, dispersing the invisible dark clouds with its soft, pale light.","Qin Shaozong stared unblinkingly at the woman before him. She was still as clever as ever. Pinned in the corner by him, her eyes were rimmed with red, and washed by tears, her pupils appeared even more translucent, like two black pearls submerged in a cold spring.","Her eyes clearly reflected his image—a bit inquiring, a bit apprehensive, and holding a trace of sorrow for Yun Ce. Meanwhile, the hesitation and fear she had shown just moments ago were slowly fading away without her even realizing it.","That wicked little thing, curled up like a ball of a fox, was slowly and tentatively exposing her soft underbelly once again.","As long as he was patient, just waited a little longer...","He couldn't wait!","The sound of blood roaring through his veins was so deafening, rushing straight to his head with unstoppable force, making him cease all rational thought in that instant. Other desires gnawed at his mind, taking over his brain inch by inch.","The place in his chest that once felt as if it had been scorched by boiling oil, a ruined wasteland covered in countless blisters, suddenly felt as though a soothing ointment had been gently applied.","And so, the piercing pain began to dissipate, and new flesh slowly grew over the festering wounds.","Reaching out to pull the woman from the corner, Qin Shaozong lowered his head and kissed her.","Dai Li was still waiting for his answer, completely unprepared for what happened next.","Compared to the ferocity of his initial approach, this kiss was somewhat softer, yet no less greedy. He plundered her mouth, capturing her soft, red tongue and sucking relentlessly.","He kissed her fiercely, but Dai Li felt that he was no longer as angry as before. The first time, he had made the tip of her tongue ache, but now...","Suddenly, the tip of her tongue was bitten. Dai Li gasped in pain, her thoughts coming to an abrupt halt.","Qin Shaozong pulled back slightly. Cupping the side of her face with his hand, his rough thumb caressed her moist lips. With a hint of displeasure in his eyes, he murmured, \"Distracted?\"","\"...We were just talking about Yunce.\" Daili didn't want to take the blame for this. It was clearly him who wasn't playing by the rules, so how could everything be blamed on her?","He gave a noncommittal \"Mm,\" accepting the remark with a straight face, not feeling at all that the sudden change in topic was inappropriate.","Qin Shaozong lowered his hand. \"Yunce was born prematurely, so his health has never been very robust. Aside from nearly dying of grief when his parents passed away, he also suffered a major illness at the age of twelve. At that time, when he was critically ill, quite a few people started entertaining other ideas.\"","The age difference between the two cousins wasn't large, only three years. That year, Qin Yunce was twelve, and Qin Qinian was nine. One was a fledgling young boy, while the other was, in the eyes of many, an uncarved jade that could still be molded.","When the former was tottering and clearly unable to hold things together, one couldn't blame others for choosing a better tree to roost in.","For him to call it a major illness, Daili guessed that Qin Yunce must have been hanging by a thread at the time. She thought for a moment, \"You probably didn't stop Mr. Cui and the others back then, did you?\"","Qin Shaozong replied with an \"Mm.\"","He indeed hadn't stopped them. Yunce was sick for over two years, relapsing constantly. When he was doing well, it looked as if he would be completely cured by the next day, but when he was doing poorly, his breath was as faint as a thread.","Qin Shaozong suddenly clicked his tongue lightly, whether out of irritation or disappointment. \"During the two-plus years Yunce was ill, I also tried to groom Qin San. But that boy really turned out exactly as I initially judged, without the slightest deviation. He is soft-hearted and easily swayed by others, lacking his own decisiveness in major matters. Such a person can at most hold a sword on the battlefield; if forced to wield the sharp blade of power, he would easily cut his own hands.\"","He paused, feeling somewhat frustrated by his failure to meet expectations. \"Furthermore, he gets dizzy just looking at words. If he truly sat in my position, there would absolutely be no shortage of letters and official documents. He can't read them, and he makes mistakes when writing. Could he really have others do it for him every time? Once or twice is fine, but if this goes on for a long time, it will inflate the ambitions of certain people, allowing them to use his name to further their own ends.\"","Daili looked at him for a moment and suddenly said, \"Other warlords have many heirs. The children of Fan of Yanzhou can't be counted on two hands, and I heard that Governor Nangong also has several sons. At that time, when Yunce was ill and Qinian didn't meet your expectations, didn't you think about having other children?\"","Medical care in this era was backward, and the infant mortality rate was much higher than in modern times. For wealthy families, the more heirs, the better. If one unfortunately didn't grow up, wasn't there always another?","By the same logic, if this one lacked great talent, another might have it. Moreover, they didn't lack money and could afford to raise many children, so why not?","With the Qin family's wealth and status, if he, as the clan leader, wanted children, she figured there would absolutely be many young women fighting to bear them for him.","Qin Shaozong held one of her hands in his palm, squeezing Daili's fingertips and examining the lines on her palm. \"I did think about it in the past. At that time, Yunce's life was in imminent danger, the boy Qinian was unusable, and having no successor was detrimental to stabilizing morale. But having heirs isn't something you just do on a whim; many aspects need to be considered...\"","\"The child's birth mother cannot have a family background that is too high or too low. If it's too high, she wouldn't be willing to be a concubine, and her maternal family might become a second Wei clan. But if it's too low, the child would easily be looked down upon in the future, making it difficult to establish authority, and there would be no maternal family to help.\" Qin Shaozong was different from other warlords. When the Qin family married into the Wei family back then, they were of lower standing. Furthermore, after the Wei daughter passed away, he had even made a vow that if he were to remarry, he must marry a Wei daughter.","Since daughters of other prominent families couldn't obtain the position of primary wife, the loss incurred here would have to be compensated from somewhere else.","Qin Shaozong was unwilling to cut off other flesh to feed them.","\"Whether a child has natural talent really can't be seen right after birth. Placing all bets on a single chance offers slim hope of winning. If I decided to take this path, it would inevitably require having more children to compare.\" Qin Shaozong didn't look up, still looking at that fair palm, and said with considerable disgust, \"Troublesome.\"","He had no intention of turning his backyard into a colosseum, nor did he want to spend those turbulent times entertaining people from the Li family today and dealing with guests from the Zhao family tomorrow. Therefore, the matter was delayed again and again, and a decision was never made.","Until—","Qin Yunce's condition finally took a turn for the better.","His nephew's health still wasn't very robust, but it was barely passable. Qin Shaozong didn't want to go through the hassle, so he simply tossed aside his advisors' suggestion to have more children and select the best.","Thinking about it now, it was fortunate he hadn't listened to them, otherwise, he would never have caught this wicked fox.","\"Madam previously said they all received my instructions, which is why Wugong took Qin the Second's side and went head-to-head with Shengping and the others. This statement is both right and wrong. During the two years Yunce was severely ill, Shengping and Zhongliang taught Qin San quite a few times and formed some master-disciple bonds. Their plotting for Qin San stemmed from personal motives; I did not instruct them.\" Qin Shaozong raised his eyes to look at her at this moment.","Daili's pupils contracted slightly, and her heart, which had not yet settled, uncontrollably surged with huge waves.","Right and wrong? This man only denied half of it, saying he hadn't instructed Cui Shengping to plot for Qinian.","Then Zhouzhou...","Daili subconsciously tried to pull her hand back, but it was firmly grasped by his large palm. Her throat felt dry, and she even stuttered at first, \"Qin, Qin Changgeng, Zhouzhou has never received that kind of education. He doesn't understand imperial statecraft, and he has no background. No one can help him. Not to mention, he is only your stepson, not your biological son. If he were to inherit your position, in the eyes of the gentlemen, that would be power falling into the hands of an outsider. How could they ever agree?\"","It wasn't that Daili, as a mother, was deliberately putting down her son, but rather that everything she said was an objective fact.","She was extremely anxious, but he relaxed instead, even smiling leisurely. \"Wugong said that Qin the Second is very good at studying, extremely skilled at drawing inferences and integrating knowledge. I'm not worried about his studies.\"","Daili choked slightly.","Both she and Zhouzhou's father had good educational backgrounds, and the son they had produced had excellent grades since childhood, never making her worry about his studies. She used to be proud of this, but she never expected that it would now become the source of her headache.","Daili then changed her tune, \"Then let's not talk about studying. Zhouzhou has no background...\"","\"He does!\" Qin Shaozong cut her off. \"Madam, you are Qin the Second's backing.\"","Daili was astonished. \"Me?\"","Qin Shaozong said, \"The keel waterwheel is renowned throughout the world, saltpeter ice is highly sought after by noble families, and the millions of military funds for my northern lands all come from Madam's hands. Not to mention that now there is the emergence of fertile soil, which can fill the homes of commoners with abundance.\"","Although some of it was obtained through early transactions, regardless of the private causes, in the eyes of the gentlemen and the people of the world, all of these came from her hands.","Prestige is something invisible and intangible, yet it is extremely important. Without prestige, one cannot establish authority; when one's own conduct is upright, things will be done without issuing orders.","And the prestige she had gained would provide shelter for Qin the Second.","Seeing that she was still in a daze, Qin Shaozong added, \"Of course, I will also be his backing. In the future on the battlefield, I will inevitably guide him a thing or two.\"","The south had not yet been pacified, and he was bound to have a battle with Liu Zhan later on. When fighting on the battlefield, the outstanding ones would surely gain military merit.","This was his carefully considered decision. Although Qin the Second had suffered for ten years, the docility in his character had not been completely wiped out. As for the proof, it was the bandit suppression at Chunmiao Mountain.","The fact that he was willing to lose a bet with his wife just to save a soldier meant that, in the future, he would also value brotherhood and treat Yun Ce and Qin San well.","Dai Li's mind was in a tangled mess. She didn't know whether to fret over her son having to go to the front lines in the future, or to feel helpless in the face of his well-founded reasoning.","\"How could you do this? They... they won't accept it either...\" Dai Li murmured.","She did not spell it out, but Qin Shaozong understood perfectly.","A heavy darkness settled in his eyes. \"Dai Li, I am no saint. I admit I have selfish motives in doing this. Qin the Second, just like you, hails from a utopian paradise. I will likely never witness the wonders of that mysterious place in my lifetime; I will never see a ship travel ten thousand miles in a single day, nor will I see an eternal abundance of livestock. During his ten years out in the world, Qin the Second has witnessed extreme suffering. Precisely because of this, he can never forget the peace and comfort of his birthplace. In the future, when the new dynasty is established, the so-called golden age of universal peace will still seem lacking in his eyes.\"","When sitting in a position of high power, the greatest danger is having one's eyes and ears shielded from the truth. When the supreme ruler asks, 'Why do they not eat meat?', is that not a tragedy for the common people?","Many emperors are wise and brilliant in their early reigns, but as their empires become firmly established and endless praises pour in, they inevitably grow complacent and arrogant, believing that their prosperous era has no room left for improvement.","Such emperors eventually lose their way. Whether they begin seeking immortality, pursuing the path of deities, or indulging in wine and women, they never regain their original ambition.","Qin Shaozong let out a sudden, brief laugh, marveling at the workings of fate. The path he had paved for Yun Ce years ago—which he had once thought was all for naught—had unexpectedly proven useful many years later. \"As for your final concern, my lady, it is easily resolved. Those who were particularly stubborn were eradicated years ago. Even though Qin the Second is not related to the Qin family by blood, as long as he marries a young lady from my Qin clan, he will gain a powerful family by marriage, and his descendants will carry the Qin bloodline.\"","This was his deepest and most unspeakable selfish desire. He and she were destined never to have a child sharing both their bloodlines, a fact he deeply regretted.","But as long as Qin the Second walked this path, his wish would be fulfilled in an alternative way.","Dai Li felt as if a clap of thunder had exploded in her ears. She nearly jumped out of her skin. She had been trapped in the corner by Qin Shaozong, and they had only pulled apart slightly after their kiss to speak. Now, Dai Li grabbed his arm tightly. \"Qin Changgeng, you explicitly promised me that you wouldn't interfere with Zhouzhou's marriage...\"","Qin Shaozong knew she would react this way. His gaze darkened. \"I did promise you that. But what if he likes her himself? Would you still forbid it?\"","Dai Li froze, confusion mingling with the lingering shock in her eyes. \"What do you mean? Who does he like?\"","Qin Shaozong gently removed her hand from his sleeve and, with a smooth pull, drew the woman from the corner into his embrace. \"Who do you think gave Shi Rongrong that silly dog she carries around every day? Qin the Second has taken her out riding on more than one occasion.\"","Dai Li opened her mouth, but the sheer volume of information hit her like a flash flood, leaving her dizzy and utterly speechless.","So the Qin woman he had mentioned was Hongying, and the young lady of the Qin clan was Rongrong.","Zhouzhou and Rongrong?","Qin Shaozong continued, \"I arranged for Shi Rongrong and Qin San to return to Yuyang with you, both because I wanted Rongrong to have more time to spend with Qin the Second, and because I wanted to keep Qin San away from Chang'an. I didn't want him getting swept into this still-chaotic struggle for power while Qin the Second was absent.\"","He had originally planned to explain everything to her after he returned to Yuyang, but plans could never quite keep up with the unexpected. She had left behind a letter of divorce and fled with her son without a word.","Qin Shaozong raised a hand to caress her brow. A fierce glint flickered in his dark brown eyes, a mixture of bitter unwillingness and deep defeat. \"When I saw that divorce letter, I felt nothing but hatred. I hated your lack of trust, and I loathed myself for not being Qin the Second's biological father, which meant I could never earn your complete and utter devotion.\"","When he said the word \"hatred,\" it was spoken with such profound, teeth-gritting intensity that it seemed as if his very chest had been torn open by the violent emotion, allowing all his helplessness, frustration, and jealousy to come surging out.","The usually aloof and arrogant man, a true favorite of heaven, displayed a rare, subtle vulnerability.","\"I...\" Dai Li wanted to say that she didn't distrust him, but looking into those bloodshot brown eyes, the comforting lies simply died on her lips.","At the time, she truly hadn't believed him. She hadn't trusted that a man who held half the world in his hands, who had no blood ties to her and was merely a husband she married halfway through life, would go to such great lengths to meticulously scheme a secure future for her and Zhouzhou.","And this distrust had gradually fermented into a restless anxiety during his long periods of silence, making it impossible for her to turn a blind eye to it any longer.","It wasn't that she had never considered having an open and honest conversation with him, but such thoughts were like stones tossed into a river, sinking out of sight in an instant.","Qin Changgeng was right. The root of all this truly lay in her lack of trust.","She had never truly trusted him."]},{"number":180,"title":"Chapter 180","paragraphs":["\"I'm sorry,\" Dai Li lowered her eyes and bowed her head.","The next moment, a rough, large hand gripped her jaw, lifting her chin.","He looked resentful and angry. The force of his fingers was strong, sinking slightly into her soft flesh. \"Dai Li, an apology is never what I wanted.\"","After lifting her face, he saw that her peach-blossom eyes were covered in a layer of moisture, tears threatening to fall, and the rims of her eyes had turned red again.","Qin Shaozong paused, and the pressure of his fingers lightened by a fraction, but his tone remained fierce, even unreasonably overbearing. \"No crying, no trying to muddle your way out of this. Speak!\"","The two were so close to each other. Dai Li was held tightly by the waist against his chest, their breaths mingling. She felt as if she could smell the scent of gunpowder suppressing sparks of fire.","Looking into those sharp, piercing brown eyes, she felt like she was being intensely stared down by a fierce tiger in the forest.","However, unlike other vicious brutes who would truly crush bones and suck marrow, she knew his fierceness was just a facade, nothing more than an intimidating aura.","Raising her hand to gently touch his broken eyebrow, her fingertips tracing the shape of his brow until they met the fine lines at the corner of his eye, Dai Li said softly, \"From now on, I will discuss everything with you, okay?\"","Her softened voice was like a gentle breeze blowing in spring.","The tip of Qin Shaozong's brow lifted imperceptibly, but quickly lowered again. \"Is that all?\"","He was not satisfied.","Dai Li thought about it but couldn't come up with anything else for the moment. This man's mind was as deep as an oceanic abyss. If he hadn't spoken plainly just now about his various plans for the future, she never would have guessed them even if she racked her brains.","So Dai Li asked him quietly, \"Then what do you want? We can discuss it.\"","She used a completely accommodating tone. Hearing this, Qin Shaozong let out a heavy breath. It was impossible to tell if he was satisfied or not, he merely asked, \"Will you ever write another Divorce Letter in the future?\"","This question was easy to answer. Dai Li shook her head and said she wouldn't.","She didn't have a problem with Qin Changgeng as a person; she was just worried about her son's future safety. Since he wasn't using Zhou Zhou as a stepping stone, she naturally wouldn't think of leaving.","Qin Shaozong gave a sound of acknowledgment, his expression still very cold. \"Next, I ask, you answer.\"","Just as Dai Li nodded, she heard him ask, \"You said earlier that if you had a choice, you wouldn't want to leave either. Is that true?\"","Dai Li was slightly startled.","He had clearly just confirmed the matter of the Divorce Letter, but turning around, he asked her a similar question again. It was only in this moment that Dai Li suddenly realized she wasn't the only one harboring distrust.","He didn't trust her either.","It was just that compared to her doubting whether he would treat Zhou Zhou as his own, his insecurity clearly lay elsewhere...","The man before her was a veteran of the battlefield, his skin a deep shade from the sun and wind. His facial contours were rugged and sharp, with a broken eyebrow, deep-set eyes, a straight nose, and thin lips. His physique was also very tall and imposing, with broad shoulders, a narrow waist, and a heroic posture. Sitting sideways on the couch at this moment, he gave off a majestic presence, like a descending mountain.","The hero who commanded armies on the battlefield was now pursing his lips, his light brown eyes watching her unblinkingly. Qin Shaozong showed no other expression, but she could sense a hint of apprehension radiating from him.","Dai Li's emotions surged. That strange feeling she had when she heard him methodically planning their future resurfaced. It felt as if a little mound of earth in the depths of her heart was being continuously pushed upward by something—something persistent, stubborn, and unyielding.","Finally, a tiny green shoot broke through the soil.","It was so small and fragile, unable to withstand violent storms or any devastation, but it truly existed.","Dai Li remained silent for a long time, only looking at him with a complex gaze that Qin Shaozong could not understand.","It was the first time he had seen her reveal such an expression. He couldn't clearly describe what it was exactly, but being gazed at by her like this, he felt as if his heart, cheeks, and spine were being brushed by a gentle, fair hand. A wave of fiery numbness flared up, shooting into his skull and exploding, then spreading down his spine to his limbs and bones, making him tremble uncontrollably.","The long arm Qin Shaozong had wrapped around her waist tightened, and he leaned in closer, asking urgently, \"Is it that hard to answer? Open your mouth and speak.\"","Dai Li sighed softly, helplessly admitting to a certain fact, as if resigning herself to fate.","Seeing her sigh, Qin Shaozong's brow twitched. The heart that had just been soaring instantly sank to the bottom of a valley, while an inexplicable fire, a mix of sorrow and anger, flared up within him.","He couldn't fathom what was so difficult about the question that she wouldn't even try to coax or deceive him, and instead sighed. Did talking to him really make her that uncomfortable?","However, in the very next instant, the fair hand from his illusion just now became reality.","\"I'm not leaving. I'll live a good life with you from now on.\" Seeing him just staring at her intently, Dai Li didn't know if he was suspicious or simply hadn't processed it yet.","She continued, \"I used to think you were a dutiful and responsible husband, but from today onward, you are my beloved.\"","Some people would draw a direct equal sign between husband and beloved, but Dai Li felt they were different. A husband could be a partner in a marriage of convenience; but a beloved was a title that only existed when there was mutual affection.","She wasn't someone who couldn't tell good from bad, and what he had done truly moved her. If Zhou Zhou's future was secure and stable, what would be wrong with her falling in love?","Yes, falling in love after marriage.","Dai Li smoothed over the shallow crease between his brows. \"My heart reaches out to you, and your heart is known to me; together morning and night, walking until the break of dawn.\"","Qin Shaozong didn't fully grasp the modern nuance of the word beloved, but it didn't stop him from understanding the meaning of the word itself, and the emotion in those bright, shining eyes.","His pupils suddenly contracted. His chest still felt as if it were on fire, but unlike the unbearable stinging pain from just a moment ago, the flames now were only a scalding warmth that did not hurt.","A tidal wave of trembling that made his hairs stand on end surged through him. Qin Shaozong held her tightly, his rough, large hand stroking her jaw and lips over and over again. \"What you just said, say it one more time.\"","This man's hands were full of calluses and his strength was not small. Dai Li's cheeks hurt from his rubbing, even giving her the illusion of being scraped by sandpaper.","\"Say it one more time, Madam,\" he urged desperately.","Dai Li didn't speak. Instead, she grabbed his collar, pulled him close, and answered him with a kiss.","Qin Shaozong paused, the muscles of his back twitching beneath his black robe. He embraced her tightly, then followed the momentum to press her forward as they fell back.","Dai Li was pushed onto the couch, and a dense shower of kisses fell upon her—first on her lips, then her cheeks, forehead, and temples, not even sparing the unremoved scar on her face.","The intense kisses made it impossible for Dai Li to even open her eyes. Suddenly, the heavy weight of the man above her propped himself up. As soon as her vision cleared, she saw Qin Shaozong looking at her with a burning gaze.","\"Has Madam already fallen for me?\" his voice was deep, carrying the unique magnetism of a mature man.","This man's gaze was passionate and direct. Even though they had done much more intimate things, being stared at and pressed by him like this gave Dai Li a rare hint of shyness.","However, she didn't have an avoidant personality; if it was true, it was true, and if not, it wasn't. Although that layer of emotion was far from being unforgettable or capable of moving mountains and draining seas, the affection genuinely existed.","Therefore, under his torch-like gaze, Dai Li gave a light nod.","Almost instantly, he smiled. His smile was hearty and uninhibited, rarely devoid of any other deep or mocking emotions, and the volume was loud.","Daili didn't doubt that he could be heard laughing all the way at the stairs; this man wished everyone in the relay station knew how delighted he was. The blush on her face deepened, and she reached out to cover his mouth. \"Qin Changgeng, keep your voice down.\"","Not long after covering it, Daili quickly pulled her hand back, the slightly damp part of her palm itching. \"I haven't washed my hands, and you don't even mind the dirt.\"","\"When have I ever minded you?\" he said.","But after saying this, the corners of the man's raised mouth pressed down, cold and stern. \"Even if Madam says she loves me, it doesn't change the fact that you ran away from home without a word. If this matter is not severely punished, and only treated lightly, it's tantamount to indulgence, and you will definitely do it again.\"","Daili: \"...\"","She didn't expect that after going around in circles, they would return to the beginning. The only difference was probably that he was no longer furious.","\"Then what does Grand Commandant Qin want to do?\" Daili asked helplessly.","Qin Shaozong used practical actions to tell her. The green dress Daili was wearing was torn by him.","Yes, torn open.","The material of the clothes worn by the dancers in the Huang Residence was very ordinary. Even to add to the fun for certain guests with fetishes during their playtime, the material of the beauties' clothes was specially made very thin, even in the increasingly cool autumn.","Qin Shaozong reached out and pulled, tearing a strip of cloth with a \"rip.\" He said dissatisfiedly, \"You don't stay well at home, but insist on running away to wear this ragged thing.\"","This man's reaction was so obvious, pressing against her with a strong presence, completely like an arrow on the bowstring. Daili knew what he wanted to do. \"Get up, you can't be licentious during the day. Do it at night.\"","Qin Shaozong remained unmoved, not retreating half a step. He folded the long \"rag\" he had just torn off and tied it over Daili's eyes. \"Alright, it's dark now.\"","Daili was both angry and amused. Just as she was about to say something, this man pressed down again, suppressing her words along with it.","This kiss was three parts less angry than the one just now, but even more greedy. With her vision deprived, other senses became incredibly clear. The contact of lips and tongues brought a tremor, and the smacking sound of water seemed a bit louder.","The rough large palm seemed to hold a cluster of fire, and wherever it passed, a wave of heat rose.","Qin Shaozong felt the response.","It wasn't that she hadn't reacted when they were intimate in the past. Of course, she had, but after she personally said she loved him, he belatedly realized that the two were worlds apart.","In the past, she was perfunctory and ignored him. She would only give him feedback when she was in the mood or comfortable. It was nothing like her current enthusiasm.","Qin Shaozong gritted his teeth, so full of hatred that the roots of his teeth ached slightly. What kind of bitter life had he been living before?","Just as Daili was about to be pulled into the hazy pool of desire by him, she suddenly remembered something. \"Qin Changgeng, you didn't lock the door!\"","Earlier, when this man carried her into the room, he kicked the door open with his foot and didn't care about it afterward.","The weight on her lightened. The man covering her got up, but he didn't leave directly. Daili heard the sound of fabric tearing again, followed by a large palm reaching over, grabbing her two wrists one after another, putting them together, and tying them neatly.","Only after tying the person did he get off the bed to lock the door.","He went quickly and returned quickly. When Qin Shaozong came back, he saw that the woman on the bed still maintained the posture she had before he left.","Her long hair, like a cloud, was scattered. Her face was like a silver plate, and the red mole between her eyebrows was delicate and dripping. Her cheeks were flushed with pink, and her slightly parted red lips were moist. The abrupt fake scar on her face inexplicably lost its ferocity, unexpectedly giving birth to a bit of pitiful cuteness.","Her clothes had long had nothing to do with being neat. The front overlapping collar was wide open, and the deep white, like a pile of snow, seemed to be spring water melted from a holy mountain, bright and dazzling.","Qin Shaozong didn't immediately get on the bed. Instead, he stood in front of the bed, watching her tentatively move her head closer to her hands after regaining her senses from the haze, attempting to take off the thin strip covering her eyes.","He chuckled lightly, and only then did he get back on the bed, catching Daili red-handed. His large palm scooped from behind and patted her plump curve. \"Dishonest, you should be punished.\"","Just now, when he went to lock the door, Daili calmed down a bit, and her thoughts couldn't help but drift to her son.","It wouldn't take long for Zhou Zhou to know what happened in the Huang Residence. Once her son knew she was taken away by Qin Changgeng, he would definitely come looking for her.","She had to end this quickly.","So Daili opened her mouth to provoke him. \"If the Grand Commandant isn't feeling inadequate, then hurry up.\"","Veins bulged on Qin Shaozong's forehead. He lowered his head and blocked those annoying red lips. After kissing thoroughly, he slowly moved down, using his lips and tongue to feel the thrumming of her fragile veins, intertwining and blending with her.","*","It was almost half an hour later that Qin Yanzhou learned of all that had happened in the Grand Administrator's Residence. He immediately dropped his broom and ran out of the residence without hesitation.","The two servants next to him stared wide-eyed and called out to him twice, but the young man didn't look back, seeming to have a momentum of never returning.","\"Really, this Yan Er is very strange. It's one thing that he doesn't talk to others usually, but now he's so unruly. He's just a distant relative of a steward. Ha, does he really think he's a master?\"","\"Don't mind that weirdo.\"","...","Qin Yanzhou directly jumped over the wall and out of the residence, heading straight for a certain relay station in the commandery. During the few days he hung out in the Huang Residence, he intentionally or unintentionally gathered outside information, so he knew where that person was staying.","The relay station's door was bright and clean. Two tall figures stood in front of the door. They were actually Bai Jianping and Mo Yanyun. The two seemed to know that Qin Yanzhou would come and waited at the door.","Upon seeing him, Mo Yanyun immediately said, \"Second Young Master, don't worry. The Madam is fine.\"","\"Which floor and room is my mother in?\" Qin Yanzhou asked as he walked inside.","The two didn't speak. Seeing this, the young man went upstairs by himself, intending to check from the highest floor one by one. Bai and Mo couldn't persuade him, so they had to follow behind him.","As a result, as soon as the three of them reached the third floor and before they had walked a few steps to the side, they heard a female voice float over. \"Qin Changgeng, don't push your luck!\"","This voice seemed angry and reproachful, with a strong momentum. Even without seeing the person, one could guess that there were no extreme events happening in the room.","Qin Yanzhou stopped abruptly, turned around, and slowly walked back.","Mo Yanyun gasped inwardly. He thought about how furious the Marquis was when he came, raging like thunder for several days in a row, like dark clouds pressing down on the city, threatening to destroy it. He originally thought that after finding the Madam, the terrifying thunder in the sky should finally fall. He didn't expect... just this?","Instead, the one losing her temper was someone else.","Bai Jianping thought roughly the same, but he had other thoughts. He said resentfully, \"Second Young Master, next time, please show mercy. Spare my neck, and also leave me a few more clothes.\"","Qin Yanzhou coughed lightly. \"I'm sorry. I promise there won't be a next time.\"","*","Daili slept all the way until dusk. What surprised her was that at this time, her back was still pressed against a warm wall of flesh, and the bedcovers were also very warm. A sturdy long arm rested on her waist, pulling her inward, and even breaths fell on the side of her neck.","In the past, when she woke up, Qin Shaozong was nowhere to be seen. He was either out for morning exercise or dealing with official business. He would never still be in bed.","Daili turned over and faced him.","The setting sun slanted in through the window, and the light in the room wasn't considered dim. In the un-dissipated daylight, Daili quietly looked at the face of the man in front of her. When he was asleep, he had a bit less prestige than during the day and didn't look so fierce.","Dai Li reached out a finger, first touching the crease between his brows, trying to smooth it out.","She had just noticed it; perhaps because he had been frowning so often lately, the once barely visible crease was now much deeper.","It made him look weighed down by heavy thoughts.","Dai Li extended another finger, using both her index and middle fingers to try and stretch the crease flat. However, before she could move much, her hand was caught by a large, raised palm.","He slowly opened his eyes. His light brown pupils, like agates in a clear stream, held a rare softness. Have you suddenly realized how handsome your husband is?","Indeed, I have. Dai Li nodded. In a relationship, she was never stingy about offering emotional support and validation to her partner.","She thought he would be pleased, but unexpectedly, the man revealed a look of teeth-gnashing resentment. Before Dai Li could even ask why, he pulled her into his arms and lowered his head to kiss her.","Although she didn't understand which of his nerves had snapped, Dai Li, who naturally enjoyed kissing her lover, accepted it completely.","He paused for a second, then pressed her closer and kissed her even more fiercely.","When the long kiss finally ended, Qin Shaozong held her as he sat up. Gripping Dai Li's waist, he said angrily, So my wife was merely humoring me in the past.","Dai Li was speechless.","How was she supposed to respond to that?","Previously, her definition of Qin Changgeng was just a bedmate, plus Zhou Zhou's stepfather. She was only making a life with him as partners; what need was there to talk about feelings?","Unable to answer, she simply changed the subject. Dai Li touched the side of his cheek. How many days has it been since you shaved this stubble? It's incredibly prickly. Go shave it quickly.","She pulled open her collar to take a look; sure enough, a large patch of her skin had been rubbed red by him just now.","The Han Dynasty was the peak of bronze mirror development in China, and the Great Yan, which was similar to the Han, was no different. Every room in the relay station was equipped with a small bronze mirror. Dai Li first washed her face in front of the mirror and peeled off the fake scar on her face.","Once she had freshened up, she stepped aside to give the spot to Qin Shaozong.","To her surprise, the man was still sitting in front of the small table with no intention of getting up. He merely beckoned to her, Come here, Madam.","Dai Li was confused. What is it?","He suddenly reached out and pulled her. Caught off guard, Dai Li fell into his lap. Then, her hand grew heavy as a short blade was placed into it. Help your husband shave.","The short blade was only three inches long, much lighter than ordinary daggers. Dai Li pushed open the sheath and saw a cold, piercing gleam. The blade itself was barely thicker than a cicada's wing.","It was a fine blade, sharp enough to cut a falling hair in half.","And right now, this sharp blade was in Dai Li's hand, less than a palm's distance from Qin Shaozong's neck.","Dai Li shifted her position, making sure not to point the tip at him. Qin Changgeng, I haven't used this before.","Qin Shaozong astutely caught the underlying meaning in her words. She had just never used this method to shave someone; it didn't mean she had never helped another man shave.","He clicked his tongue in displeasure. If you haven't used it before, use it now. There is a first time for everything.","Dai Li argued with him for a bit, but ultimately couldn't win. She had no choice but to have someone bring hot water and soap pods.","She first soaked a cloth in the hot water, then took it out to apply a hot compress to Qin Shaozong's jaw, steaming the hair roots to soften them. Only then did Dai Li apply the soap.","Lathering the soap into a foam, she coated his cheeks. Holding the blade, Dai Li spoke in a low voice, Don't move in a moment, and don't speak either. I'm telling you in advance, I'm a little squeamish around blood. If I accidentally cut you, you'll have to finish the rest yourself.","His long fingers curled around her dangling sash, twirling it playfully. Alright, whatever Madam says.","Dai Li's attention was highly concentrated as she slowly used the blade to scrape away Qin Shaozong's emerging stubble. She didn't dare get distracted in the slightest, afraid that a moment of carelessness would slice off a chunk of his flesh.","Compared to Dai Li's intense concentration and nervousness, Qin Shaozong was much more relaxed and leisurely. He played with the young lady's sash, occasionally supporting her waist, completely ignoring Dai Li's earlier command not to move.","Not only were his hands moving, but his gaze was also quite bold. He carefully traced Dai Li's face with his eyes, then moved down along her fair neck, looking here and peering there, completely oblivious to the concept of restraint.","Unable to bear the distraction, Dai Li had to move the blade away and stop. Qin Changgeng, can you behave yourself?","That's quite unreasonable of you to say, Madam. I am much better behaved than you; I have never run away from home, Qin Shaozong raised an eyebrow.","Dai Li was speechless.","Was he never going to let this go?","However, since they were on the topic, Dai Li took the opportunity to bring it up with him. Zhou Zhou has come of age and is now an adult. I think we need to talk to him about your plans.","The last time she left the Northern Territory, she had hidden the reason from her son. This kind of act first, report later behavior would only happen this one time.","Up to you, he said.","Using a hot towel to wipe away the last bit of foam, Dai Li raised her hand to feel his smooth jaw, very satisfied. It seems my skills are pretty good. I didn't nick your skin at all.","He smoothly pushed the responsibility onto her. Then I will leave the matter of shaving to Madam from now on.","Dai Li thought about it. Alright.","The muscles on the side of Qin Shaozong's jaw suddenly tightened. That stark contrast between heaven and earth appeared again, making his teeth itch with frustration. On one hand, he was happy and intoxicated by her, but on the other hand, he couldn't help but recall her past perfunctoriness and imagine the other men who might have received such treatment from her.","Heh, good thing they were all dead.","As if an unnamed fire was burning in his heart, Qin Shaozong raised his arms to tightly encircle the woman on his lap, burying his face in the side of her neck and taking a bite.","Dai Li hissed, drawing in a sharp breath.","The sensation on the side of her neck quickly turned into something else. Dai Li tossed the blade back onto the table and grabbed his long hair with both hands to pull him away. Qin Changgeng, you're biting the hand that feeds you!","Qin Shaozong looked at the redness on the fair skin before him. The crimson mark was incredibly vibrant, like a stamped seal. He rubbed it with his long fingers. Mine.","Dai Li pursed her lips. She couldn't speak for other men, but the one in front of her, who was used to being domineering and forceful, still needed to be disciplined. Otherwise, he would take a mile when given an inch, and life would be impossible.","Dai Li cupped his cheeks with both hands, trying to warn him. You can't just bite people out of nowhere. That's the behavior of an uncivilized beast. It's not something a gentleman would do, nor does it fit your current status as the Grand Commandant.","Qin Shaozong watched her red lips open and close. What are you babbling about? Let me kiss you again."]},{"number":181,"title":"Chapter 181","paragraphs":["Qin Yanzhou saw Dai Li again just as the sun was about to set. His mother had changed her clothes. The cheap cyan outfit from the Huang Manor was nowhere to be seen; instead, a mother-of-pearl white dress shimmered brilliantly in the evening light.","He looked Dai Li up and down, his heart finally settling completely. He first called out, \"Mother,\" and then addressed the tall man walking behind her, \"Father.\"","They hadn't had dinner yet, so the three of them now sat at the same table to eat.","After the meal, Dai Li said to her son, \"Zhouzhou, come with me. I have something important to discuss with you.\"","Qin Yanzhou was confused. His gaze quickly flicked to Qin Shaozong, only to see the man's expression was as usual, revealing nothing. After his mother spoke, he also stood up.","Dai Li returned to her room first. She stood by the door, watching her son enter, and then peeked outside. Seeing that Qin Shaozong was also coming, she didn't close the door immediately.","Having eaten and drunk his fill, his pace was leisurely.","Seeing Dai Li looking at him, the man curled his lips into a smile. As he entered the room, taking advantage of Qin Yanzhou's blind spot, he touched Dai Li's stomach and whispered, \"Why did my wife eat so little for dinner? Are you saving your appetite to eat something else tonight?\"","Dai Li's first reaction was to look at her son. Seeing that Qin Yanzhou hadn't noticed, she pinched the waist of the man in front of her. \"Can you be a bit more decent in front of the younger generation?\"","He said meaningfully, \"It seems what my wife is thinking of isn't an ordinary late-night snack either. Great minds think alike.\"","Dai Li was speechless.","Feeling a flush of heat rise on her cheeks, Dai Li simply looked away from him and turned to the young man standing by the table. \"Zhouzhou, have a seat.\"","Mother and son sat across the table from each other.","Qin Shaozong sat on a soft chair not far away, holding a letter from an unknown source, clearly not intending to directly participate in their conversation. Dai Li ignored him and began to brew tea.","As winter approached, the temperature dropped day by day, and drinking hot tea brought a lot of comfort.","After placing charcoal under the clay stove to boil water, Dai Li looked at Qin Yanzhou opposite her. \"Zhouzhou, last time I didn't tell you anything and just made you leave the North with me. I acted on my own, and Mom apologizes to you.\"","Qin Yanzhou immediately wanted to speak but was stopped by Dai Li raising her hand, signaling him to let her finish.","Dai Li looked at her tall, grown-up son across the table and sighed deeply. \"You've grown up and are no longer ignorant. As an adult, you have the right to know your future and make your own choices. No matter what my reasons were back then, it was wrong of me not to tell you.\"","\"I have never blamed you!\" Qin Yanzhou couldn't help but say.","Dai Li smiled. \"I know, but these are two different things. Just because I am treated with forgiveness doesn't mean I can take it for granted and pretend nothing happened.\"","The man not far away had put down his letter at some point, his deep gaze fixed on their direction. The woman sitting by the table wore a mother-of-pearl white dress, her profile beautiful and serene, as if her whole being was radiating a soft, warm glow.","In Qin Shaozong's memory, he had never heard a single apology from his parents or ancestors.","The ruler is the master of the subject, and the father is the master of the son.","Even among blood relatives, superiors always held unquestionable authority over their subordinates.","What was right was right, and what was wrong was also right!","Subordinates only needed to obey their superiors, with no other options. This was part of the \"Three Fundamental Bonds and Five Constant Virtues,\" regarded as the natural order of things.","However, watching the scene before him, Qin Shaozong suddenly understood why Qin the Second, despite living ten years of hellish days, miraculously retained a compassionate side to his character.","It was a bright, high-hanging moon that had illuminated him.","Qin Shaozong knew he had completely inherited the unyielding nature of his forefathers. Even if he were wrong in his life, he would never bow his head to his children, because just imagining it was something he couldn't accept outside those \"Three Fundamental Bonds and Five Constant Virtues.\"","But at this moment, looking at her gently apologizing to her son, Qin Shaozong bizarrely felt that it was not only harmonious but also quite attractive.","\"...Zhouzhou, setting aside factors related to me, do you yourself want to go to the battlefield?\" Dai Li asked.","The change of topic was sudden. The young man was slightly startled, but he quickly nodded, \"I do.\"","Worried that Dai Li wouldn't believe him, Qin Yanzhou added, \"Mother, I think I can no longer live that kind of peaceful, uneventful life.\"","Those ten years were like a red-hot branding iron, scorching his fair skin black and leaving scars that would never fade for a lifetime. His personality and way of life had undergone earth-shattering changes, and now he was accustomed to a life of bloody slaughter and turbulent ups and downs.","He could never go back to how he was...","However, compared to his previous puppet-like numbness, he now had comrades-in-arms and brothers to whom he could entrust his back. Every battle, big or small, no longer brought him the exhaustion of \"surviving another day,\" but an indescribable sense of fulfillment.","Dai Li's eyes felt a momentary sting of tears. She quickly lowered her gaze. \"Do you remember the concerns I mentioned to you back at the Xinglong Inn?\"","Qin Yanzhou nodded and said he remembered.","Since his mother had brought it up on her own, he had a premonition that what they were going to discuss next was precisely this \"concern.\"","No, saying they were going to discuss it might not be accurate. There must be a solution, otherwise his mother wouldn't be so calm.","\"Your father's intention is for you to succeed him in the future,\" Dai Li said softly.","Qin Yanzhou's eyes widened uncontrollably. He subconsciously looked at the man not far away, only to see him stand up and walk over, then take a seat beside his mother, casually picking up the boiling teapot to pour water into the cups.","\"Your mother speaks the truth. I do indeed have this plan. When I initially had Wugong teach you other subjects, part of the reason was to see how you fared in your studies, and the results were decent. And you, kid, leading some twenty men to burn down the Xuzhou army's granary, that wasn't bad either,\" Qin Shaozong said mildly.","He rarely praised people, and often his words were harsh. Earning a \"decent\" or \"not bad\" from him was already considered rare in the eyes of people like Bai Jianping.","\"But Qinian, he...\" Qin Yanzhou didn't know what to say. He wanted to ask if Qinian knew about this. He also wanted to ask if Qinian would accept it.","\"Qin the Third has his own path to walk,\" Qin Shaozong said calmly. \"Even without you, this burden wouldn't fall on him to carry. He probably had a premonition about this a long time ago.\"","Steam rose from the cups. Qin Shaozong looked straight across the table, his gaze as sharp as a snow blade. \"This is power, but it is also a responsibility. However great the former is, the latter is equally heavy. It can decide the life and death of tens of thousands, and in the future, it will require you to constantly bear the hatred of the nation in your heart and the worries of the court on your brow. Qin the Second, do you want to accept it?\"","It wasn't a matter of willingness, but of desire.","His preference for Qin Yanzhou was one thing, but if Qin Yanzhou himself lacked the boldness and determination, then no amount of approval or personal bias would matter.","The steaming mist seemed to form a thin veil, and also appeared like a mirror.","Qin Yanzhou felt as if he saw many, many things in that mirror: fluttering red flags, dining halls that never lacked food, but also dilapidated thatched huts, emaciated starving commoners, and corpses of those who died of hunger exposed in the wilderness.","He seemed to hear the words his teacher had once spoken:","\"A scholar must be broad-minded and resolute, for his burden is heavy and his journey is long. If he takes benevolence as his burden, is it not heavy? If he ceases only with death, is it not long? Chongle, in this life, one must always do something meaningful so as not to live in vain. If one day you possess the power to change the world, your teacher hopes you can be brave, neither fearing nor shrinking back, and realize what you once said: 'May the country be prosperous and the people at peace, each content in their own work.' You are not fighting alone; by your side are me and many others willing to help you.\"","At that time, Qin Yanzhou had not understood the latter half of his teacher's words, but now, when the question \"Do you want to take it on?\" fell between them, the clouds parted to reveal the sun.","The faint confusion in the young man's eyes dissipated in an instant, entirely replaced by unwavering determination. Qin Yanzhou stood up and bowed deeply to his parents sitting across the table. \"Thank you, Father, for not giving up on me. Your son will certainly do his utmost to shoulder this responsibility. I will never disappoint you and Mother.\"","\"Do not thank me so quickly. There is still one matter I have yet to discuss with you, boy,\" Qin Shaozong beckoned for him to sit back down, then looked at Dai Li beside him.","Dai Li met his gaze and immediately knew what that matter was.","It was the major matter of marriage!","Dai Li was deeply conflicted. On one hand, she felt that arranged marriages were a toxic relic of the past and that her son should spend his life with someone he truly loved. But on the other hand, she knew very well that Qin Changgeng's support for Zhouzhou's succession was tightly bound to a marriage alliance with the Shi family.","Previously, Qin Changgeng had claimed that the two young people had feelings for each other. How much truth there was to those words, Dai Li herself did not know.","Qin Shaozong's original intention was for her to speak with their son. After all, her approach was much gentler than his, and she had always kept a close eye on Qin the Second's marriage prospects.","As a result, after waiting and waiting, he noticed her twiddling her fingers. Her slender, pale fingers were flushed with an unusual red from the blood rushing to them.","Fine. If he waited for her to speak, the roosters would crow at dawn before she could utter a single word. He would have to do it himself.","Qin Shaozong reached over and grasped Dai Li's hand beneath the table, stopping her from continuing to ravage those poor fingers. At the same time, he spoke: \"Qin the Second, what do you think of Shi Rongrong as your wife?\"","Without any preamble or build-up, he cut straight to the chase, exceptionally decisive.","Dai Li was startled and instinctively turned her head to look at Qin Shaozong.","Qin Yanzhou froze, his expression looking somewhat at a loss.","Qin Shaozong merely held Dai Li's hand, not looking at her at this moment. Seeing that the young man did not answer, he added, \"Then let me change the question. Do you dislike Shi Rongrong?\"","This time, Qin Yanzhou reacted. He slowly shook his head.","Qin Shaozong gave a neutral hum and said, \"You have no prominent noble family supporting you from behind. This is one of your shortcomings. Under normal circumstances, this weakness could be ignored, but since you will shoulder heavy responsibilities in the future, it cannot be disregarded.\"","Feeling the delicate hand in his grasp moving as if trying to break free, Qin Shaozong slid his fingers up from beneath her clenched fist, using a deft touch to uncurl it, and then slowly stroked her soft palm with his rough fingertips.","On the surface, however, Qin Shaozong's expression remained perfectly calm. \"I once made a three-point pact with your mother, and one of the conditions was that I would not monopolize your marriage arrangements. Therefore, I am not telling you to marry Shi Rongrong right this instant. It is merely a proposal. After all, you do not dislike her, and she is deeply devoted to you. The Shi family is my younger sister's marital family, and Patriarch Shi was once my father's right-hand man in the past. There is no shortage of outstanding youths among their clan members, making them a perfectly suitable source of support for you.\"","Qin Yanzhou's pupils contracted for a moment. \"She is devoted to me...\"","\"You have come of age and are an adult now. I have said all I need to say. Go back now; your mother and I are going to rest,\" Qin Shaozong said, immediately shooing him away.","Qin Yanzhou stood up and left.","The moment he was gone, Qin Shaozong immediately chuckled. \"Madam, that boy Qin Yanzhou absolutely has thoughts in his heart.\"","Dai Li felt that something was not quite right, but she could not articulate it. \"Why do you say that?\"","\"I said so much just now, but the only thing that boy heard was the part about her being devoted to him.\" Qin Shaozong pointed at the teacup on the opposite table. \"Moreover, the tea has been sitting there for so long, yet he didn't take a single sip. If that isn't a sign of a distracted mind, what is?\"","Dai Li looked across the table and saw that it was true; their son's teacup was still full.","Logically speaking, whether as a guest or otherwise, one should finish the tea poured for them before leaving as a sign of politeness.","\"It is understandable. Love arises from unknown origins. Just think back—I never knew I would come to adore you this much either, Madam,\" Qin Shaozong said as he poured out the tea.","Dai Li could not help but retort, \"You didn't adore me. You were clearly just lusting after my looks.\"","Qin Shaozong laughed and told her she was talking nonsense.","\"Talking nonsense?\" Dai Li tugged at his arm, making him face her. \"Back then at the Jiang Manor, wasn't it you who wanted to bed me the moment we met?\"","\"That only proves I fell in love with you at first sight, Madam.\" Qin Shaozong's eyes held a smile as he didn't forget to boast, \"I must say, my eye for people is truly sharp. I spotted the very best at a single glance.\"","Dai Li brought up the old score. \"You have the nerve to say that! I was nearly scared to death by you back then!\"","Qin Shaozong reached out and pulled her into his embrace, letting Dai Li sit on his lap as he looked at her closely. \"At that time, Madam, you fed me basket after basket of lies. All I saw was someone bursting with absolute audacity; I certainly didn't see where you were afraid.\"","Dai Li muttered, \"It was just scary.\"","\"It was your husband's fault. Tonight, I will properly compensate you, with interest.\" Qin Shaozong suddenly swept her up into his arms and headed toward the bed."]},{"number":182,"title":"Chapter 182","paragraphs":["Nanyu Commandery in the North, the Shi Residence.","\"Mother, Mother! I heard that Second Uncle and Second Aunt have returned. Can I go to Yuyang?\" Shi Rongyue ran into the room happily and asked Qin Hongying.","Compared to her high spirits, Qin Hongying's expression was very indifferent. \"Earlier, I asked you to go play with your younger cousin, but you refused, claiming you were aching here and uncomfortable there. Now that your Second Uncle and the others are back, you suddenly look refreshed and are in a rush to go to Yuyang.\"","Shi Rongyue stopped in her tracks, her round eyes blinking. \"Because I'm curious. Yes, very curious! I can't figure out why Second Aunt lied to me back then, so I want to go find her and ask.\"","Qin Hongying's eyes were long like her brother's, naturally carrying a fierce look. At this moment, she raised her eyes to look at her only daughter and said sternly, \"Are you going to find your Second Aunt, or are you hoping to see someone else?\"","Shi Rongyue paused, then asked timidly, \"Mother, are you unhappy about me going to pay my respects to Second Aunt?\"","Qin Hongying laughed out of anger. The good daughter she had raised with her own hands was now playing mind games with her. \"When did I say I was unhappy...\"","\"Okay, Mother, I'll go prepare right away.\" Shi Rongyue turned around and tried to run.","\"Shi Rongyue, get back here!\" Qin Hongying slammed the table and stood up. The sound of her slamming the table was so loud that the cups on it slightly bounced.","The young girl who had run to the door froze, then slowly turned back. \"Mother, are you angry?\"","Qin Hongying's chest heaved violently with anger. \"You have the nerve to ask? I told you earlier to spend more time with Qinian, did you do as I said?\"","Shi Rongyue lowered her head and stayed silent, only showing Qin Hongying her two hair whorls.","Qin Hongying's anger eased a little. \"Rongrong, Mother is doing this for your own good. Since you are destined to marry back into the Qin family, it is best to add family ties to family ties. That child Qinian isn't some ugly or useless fellow. Besides, I watched him grow up; I know him inside and out, and his character is impeccable. What more could you be picky about?\"","Shi Rongyue still kept her head down and said nothing.","Seeing this, Qin Hongying sneered coldly. \"Don't even think about Daili's biological son. As for that puppy you brought back from the south, starting today, it is not allowed to be kept in your courtyard. Let Maidong and the others...\"","\"You can't do that!\"","Shi Rongyue, who had been unresponsive just now, suddenly raised her head, her eyes wide open. \"Mother, you can't do that. I want to raise Boqi myself!\"","Qin Hongying's eyes seemed to hide blades. \"Do you like that Qin the Second?\"","This was a question, but her tone was calm and without the slightest bit of surprise.","Having her girlish secrets laid bare, a faint blush spread across the tips of Shi Rongyue's ears, but she was quickly startled by how certain her mother sounded.","She panicked for only a few breaths before quickly calming down. Her round eyes looked directly at her mother. \"Yes, Mother, I like Brother Chongle.\"","\"Shi Rongyue, did everything I told you before about the pros and cons just go in one ear and out the other?\" Qin Hongying was exasperated at her failure to meet expectations. \"Qin the Second is not a good match. Besides having Daili as his biological mother, what abilities does he have...\"","\"How could he not have any? Back then, it was Brother Chongle who led men to burn the Xuzhou army's granary. He can wield a pen to stabilize the world and wield a blade to secure peace. In what way is he not capable?\" Shi Rongyue retorted.","Qin Hongying had not gone south with the army and did not know about the matters in Xuzhou, but that didn't stop her from mocking, \"Stabilize the world? Is it his turn to stabilize this world! You are just young and attracted to beauty. If you ask me, you've just been blinded by his good looks.\"","Shi Rongyue retorted loudly, \"That's not true! Brother Chongle is just cold on the outside but warm on the inside; he is actually a very gentle person. Besides, if I purely liked his appearance, I would have fallen in love with him at first sight.\"","Qin Hongying sneered, \"Do you dare say that you didn't have a good impression of him the first time you saw him?\"","Shi Rongyue paused for a moment, then honestly nodded and said, \"Alright, maybe a little. After all, someone as handsome as Brother Chongle is indeed rare in this world. But this is just human nature. Didn't you also think Father was handsome back then, which is why you chose him over Uncle Yang?\"","Qin Hongying almost choked on her breath, not expecting that the one or two pieces of gossip her daughter had heard in the past would become her excuse for arguing now. \"Shi Rongyue, do you think I can't bear to beat you?!\"","The Qin family was a family of military generals, and Qin Hongying was a daughter of a tiger general. She was not above using physical discipline when educating her children. All of her children had been taught a lesson this way; the only difference was that the boys were beaten more, and the girls less.","The last time Shi Rongyue was disciplined was when she was eleven, when she shook off her maidservants and secretly climbed the wall to go out and play.","Shi Rongyue's eyes slowly turned red. \"Even if you want to beat me, I still believe so. Mother, I'm not like those rich young ladies in the storybooks who are dead set on marrying a man with nothing. Brother Chongle is capable in his own right, has military merits and an official position, and Second Uncle values him highly. Second Aunt is also amazing, and he is a disciple of Mister Nalan. He definitely deserves to be called a young talent. Both he and my younger cousin are children of the Qin family, so why do you treat them so differently?\"","\"You're asking me why?\" Qin Hongying had a terrible headache. It turned out that this girl truly hadn't listened to a single word she had told her last time.","Just as she was about to twist her ear and properly reason with her, Qin Hongying heard her daughter continue:","\"Besides, back when you said Second Uncle planned for me to marry back into the Qin family, he didn't specify which child it would be, did he? The fact that he didn't specify means he definitely doesn't dislike Brother Chongle. He might even support my idea. Mother, why are you stopping me?\"","Qin Hongying was stunned for a moment, and then anger welled up in her heart. \"People in high positions never speak too explicitly. Do you really think your Second Uncle meant something else? Don't use him to pressure me.\"","After saying this, Qin Hongying didn't want to talk to her daughter anymore. She shouted directly outside, \"Maidong, take your young lady back and don't allow her to step out of the courtyard! Also, move that white dog to another courtyard to be raised.\"","\"You can't take Boqi away!\"","*","By the time Daili returned to Yuyang again, it was already early winter.","Snow was falling heavily in the northern winter. Although they had missed the autumn season, it did not stop Daili, wrapped in a cloak, from going with Qin Shaozong to inspect the granaries in various places.","All the fields that had been fertilized back then yielded outstanding results. There was a bumper harvest this autumn, and the granaries were filled to the brim. There was even a rare spectacle of the granaries being unable to hold everything, forcing the soldiers to work overnight to build extensions.","\"Not just this year, it will be the same next year,\" Qin Shaozong patted the shoulder of the military instructor Jin Duole, signaling him to calm down. \"Since we have enough grain, don't be stingy. Make sure to provide the soldiers and warhorses with the best supplies. If nothing unexpected happens, there will be a fierce battle with the south next year.\"","Jin Duole's mouth hadn't stopped smiling since he saw the granaries. Hearing Qin Shaozong's words, he hurriedly nodded in agreement, then bowed deeply to Daili. \"My Lady, you have solved the worries of food for millions of people. Your merits will last for a thousand autumns, and your grace will benefit ten thousand generations. With your help, the North is like a fish in water, like a tiger with wings!\"","Daili smiled. \"Mister Jin, you flatter me. I just did what I could. I cannot bear such praise as lasting for a thousand autumns and ten thousand generations.\"","Not quite adept at handling the fanatical, god-like reverence of others, Dai Li exchanged a few perfunctory words before quickly pulling Qin Shaozong away.","Trudging unevenly through the thick snow, Dai Li suddenly asked the man beside her, Qin Changgeng, what you just told Jin Duole about going to war next year, is it true?","Qin Shaozong replied, Naturally.","Will you personally lead the troops into battle then? Dai Li asked. She remembered that back in Wugang, when facing the joint encirclement of several provinces, he had not taken to the battlefield himself, choosing instead to command from the rear.","Qin Shaozong gave her another affirmative answer: I will. The situation in the south is different from the coalition forces. The south has only one leader, Liu Zhan, so they are not a disorganized mess. Only by leading from the front can our momentum be unstoppable.","Dai Li reached out to hold his hand and asked a completely unrelated question, When is your birthday?","Qin Shaozong felt both annoyed and amused. He was annoyed that she had never paid attention before and remembered absolutely nothing about him. Now, knowing he would surely be displeased, she was trying to placate him with a sweet gesture.","What a sly little fox!","Gripping her soft, pale hand in return, Qin Shaozong said, The second day of the fourth month. Remember it well, my wife.","He gave her hand a gentle squeeze. When I asked for your birthday before, you avoided the question. Surely you can tell me now?","After he said this, Qin Shaozong noticed an unnatural expression on her face. His long, narrow eyes narrowed slightly. Are you also born in the fourth month?","Dai Li replied, ...No.","Qin Shaozong asked, Then when is it?","Dai Li looked away. The second day of the fifth month.","Qin Shaozong's face darkened. Both were on the second day, separated by a mere month, yet she still hadn't remembered his.","Seeing his displeasure, Dai Li quickly offered, For your birthday this year, I will give you a special gift.","Qin Shaozong raised an eyebrow. What is it?","I can't tell you right now. You'll know when the time comes. Dai Li wanted to keep it a secret.","Qin Shaozong chuckled softly. Your husband is very much looking forward to it.","At that moment, Dai Li looked up as if sensing something. It's snowing!","Qin Shaozong reached out to catch a snowflake just as it was about to land on her head. My wife, another year has passed.","Dai Li turned to look at him.","Meeting her gaze, Qin Shaozong gently placed the tiny snowflake he had caught onto her hair. With a smile in his eyes, he said, My wife and I shall grow white-haired together.","Dai Li also smiled. Does this count as growing white-haired together? Then what will it be when we truly have a full head of white hair in the future?","Qin Shaozong replied, In the future, it will be having a house full of children and grandchildren.","Dai Li murmured in thought. Given Zhouzhou's current age, in modern times he would only be in college. A house full of children and grandchildren... that felt so far away.","As if knowing what she was thinking, Qin Shaozong added, The marriage procedures of prominent families are complicated and cannot be taken lightly. The standard process takes at least six months to a year. Even though Qin the Second has already taken my handwritten letter to the Shi family in Nanyu to pick her up, he is ultimately just bringing Shi Rongrong over to spend the Spring Festival. As for the formal proposal and matching of birth dates, even if everything goes smoothly, they won't happen until after autumn next year.","Dai Li was a bit worried. Will Hongying agree to this?","In all fairness, if she had raised a daughter like a precious jewel, and someone arranged her marriage without her knowing anything about it, she definitely wouldn't stand for it.","If some greenhorn boy came knocking on her door at a time like that, simply cursing him out would be letting him off easy.","I have previously mentioned to Hongying about having Shi Rongrong marry back into the Qin family. Qin Shaozong looked toward the direction of Nanyu Commandery. Seeking education, seeking medical treatment, seeking a wife, all these involve the word seek. His father's path to taking a wife was fraught with difficulties and long obstacles. As my son, wouldn't it be inappropriate for him to obtain a wife without expending the slightest bit of effort?","Dai Li was speechless.","Dai Li couldn't help but reach out and pinch him. Qin Changgeng, are you gloating over his misfortune?","You wrong me deeply, my wife. I possess nothing but the sincere heart of a loving father, Qin Shaozong said with a smile.","Dai Li had originally thought her son's trip to Nanyu Commandery would take at least four or five days before he returned. The distance was one factor, and negotiating with the Shi family would inevitably take time.","Yet, in less than two days, her son was back, and returning with him was Shi Rongyue.","Contrary to Dai Li's expectations, the normally neat and tidy little girl now looked like a cotton ball that had rolled around in the dirt several times. While she hadn't quite degraded to the state of the former Bai Jianping, all traces of her refined, noble young lady demeanor had completely vanished.","Rongrong, where have you been? Without waiting for the little girl to answer, Dai Li looked at Qin Yanzhou. Zhouzhou, where did you take her?","Qin Yanzhou replied, ...I ran into her on the road.","Woof! A little white dog on the ground wagged its tail.","Dai Li took a moment to process this sentence before looking at Shi Rongyue in astonishment. The latter offered a shy smile, looking as sweet and soft as a piece of candy, showing absolutely no sign of the boldness required to run away from home.","Dai Li gasped in lingering fear. How could you be so reckless, child? Even though the northern lands are relatively peaceful now, Nanyu and Yuyang aren't exactly close. If something had happened to you on the road, what would your family do?","Second Aunt, I brought people with me. My mother has a group of private troops gifted by Second Uncle, and I am quite close to two of them. Earlier, when my mother had some issues with Boqi... uh, with me, I secretly contacted them and asked them to escort me to Yuyang. The little girl smiled innocently.","She didn't go into the specific details, but Dai Li still felt her heart pound with fear, knowing that the journey must not have been simple. You really are too reckless, child...","But there was nothing to be done. Now that she was already in Yuyang, Dai Li couldn't possibly refuse to let Shi Rongyue stay for even a moment and just stuff her back into a carriage to send her home. Dai Li had no choice but to say, Then I will write a letter to Hongying to let her know you are here.","Qin Yanzhou spoke up, Mother, I have already sent a letter to the Shi family, and I sent Father's handwritten letter along with it.","If the distance between Yuyang and Nanyu were folded in half, he had encountered Shi Rongyue on the Yuyang side. At that time, sending her back home would have been a longer journey, and she hadn't wanted to return anyway, so they had no choice but to split up the tasks.","Dai Li let out a breath of relief. It's good that a letter has been sent. It's cold outside, don't just stand at the door. Come inside.","Heating stoves were placed in the four corners of the hall, making the temperature much higher than outside. After entering the room, Shi Rongyue took off her dusty cloak, revealing a dress in similarly cool tones underneath. It was a very ordinary dress, lacking the luxurious elegance of a noble young lady she usually possessed.","Perhaps because she had left in a hurry, Shi Rongyue had only casually tied her hair into double buns. Between the exhausting journey and her just taking off her coat, the bun on the left side had tilted slightly, with a few strands of hair sticking out.","Qin Yanzhou walked behind her, looking at the slightly drooping bun with its stubborn strands of hair sticking out, and his fingertips twitched. He looked away, but a moment later, his gaze returned to it.","Raising his hand, he gently smoothed those few stray strands of hair, attempting to make them lay flat. However, faster than the hair's submission was the girl turning around.","Her round eyes looked at him like two pieces of light-colored amber. She broke into a wide smile. Brother Chongle, did you have something to tell me?","For a brief moment, Qin Yanzhou felt as if he had seen a small golden sun rising. He heard a sigh of resignation in his own heart."]},{"number":183,"title":"Chapter 183","paragraphs":["Shi Rongyue stayed at the Yuyang Marquis Manor just like that, still living in her previous courtyard.","As for Nan Yu's side, whether shocked by Qin Shaozong's handwritten letter or dealing with some other headache, they only sent someone to deliver two carriages of Shi Rongyue's belongings later on, and there was no further movement.","With an extra girl in the house, the manor also saw a lot more laughter and cheer.","Dai Li didn't interfere with how the younger generation got along. Firstly, dating requires space, and it's inappropriate for parents to meddle and question everything. Secondly, she had her own things to busy herself with.","Yuyang had a golden autumn this year, and after the harvest, a new round of composting had to be done in the winter to prepare for next year's war.","Qin Shaozong tentatively scheduled the war for next summer.","It had to be said, this timing was quite \"cunning.\" Usually, wars would only start after autumn, when the busy autumn harvest had passed, grain was stored away, and both the soldiers and civilians were free. Only with both time and provisions secured would they consider fighting.","In the past, both sides operated this way.","But Yuyang had a massive bumper harvest this year, with particularly high grain yields, so Qin Shaozong decided not to take the usual path.","The enemy lacks what we have; the advantage is ours.","Qin Shaozong looked at Dai Li, who had returned even later than him, and asked for the second time, \"Madam has been very mysterious lately, leaving early and returning late. What exactly are you doing?\"","Dai Li gave the same excuse as last time, \"I'm busy! You have your business, and I have mine.\"","Last time, seeing her speak so seriously, Qin Shaozong thought it was about the composting. But now the tail end of the bitter winter had passed, spring had arrived, and it was time to enter the sowing period. Composting was no longer needed, yet she still claimed to be busy.","As for what exactly she was busy with, she refused to tell him.","Qin Shaozong made up his mind to get to the bottom of it. \"Madam runs outside all day. Could it be there is gold to pick up out there?\"","Dai Li inexplicably laughed. \"You could say that. It does have a little bit to do with 'gold'.\"","\"Confess truthfully at once, or don't blame this official for being impolite.\" Qin Shaozong grabbed the woman's slender waist with both hands and lifted her directly onto his lap. His hands were very broad, with long fingers and distinct knuckles. Using both palms, he could almost entirely encircle Dai Li's waist.","Dai Li knelt with her knees apart against the couch, one hand pressing against his chest, trying to put some distance between them. \"What great authority the Grand Commandant has. May I ask how you intend to be impolite?\"","Qin Shaozong just smiled without saying a word, letting his moving hands tell her exactly what he intended to do.","\"Qin! Changgeng! Hahaha... stop it!\"","Her waist was full of ticklish spots. Dai Li laughed so hard she trembled like a delicate flower branch, but she simply couldn't get off his lap. Finally, she laughed until she had no strength left, hanging her head and resting her forehead against his broad shoulder, panting heavily.","Qin Shaozong's palm slid along the curve of her waist. He wrapped one arm around her, used the other hand to lift her up, and then stroked the corner of her eye where she had laughed until tears formed. \"What has Madam been busy with these days?\"","Dai Li conceded defeat; this guy was really using torture to extract a confession. She said weakly, \"Qin Changgeng, rein in that damn controlling desire of yours. Aren't the soldiers outside enough for you to torment? Aren't the children at home enough for you to discipline? Why must you control me too?\"","\"Not control you? You would turn the world upside down,\" Qin Shaozong scoffed coldly.","Dai Li sighed. \"Trust me, you definitely don't want to know right now.\"","Qin Shaozong raised an eyebrow. \"In that case, I'll go ask Qiao Wangfei.\"","These days, she went out early every morning and headed to a residence in the commandery with Qiao Wangfei, staying there for the entire day. She didn't even come back for lunch, returning only when the sky grew dark.","Qin Shaozong didn't suspect his wife had taken a fancy to another man. After all, Qiao Wangfei couldn't compare to him in any aspect—he was neither as powerful and influential, nor as tall and handsome, and he also had a legal wife at home. This wicked fox almost didn't even fancy him, so how could she take a liking to a mere platoon commander?","However, this didn't stop Qin Shaozong's curiosity.","\"Don't go asking Platoon Commander Qiao.\" How could Dai Li let him go? If Qin Changgeng really investigated this, she definitely wouldn't be able to hide it. \"I have proper business that I need his help with. I'm not messing around.\"","He remained unmoved. \"Confess truthfully.\"","Dai Li rolled her eyes at him. \"I told you it's proper business! Why do you have to manage everything? It's one thing to manage the soldiers outside, but isn't dealing with a myriad of state affairs enough to keep you busy? You come back and still want to manage me. Anyway, don't meddle in this matter. When the time comes, you'll know.\"","\"When is 'when the time comes'?\" Qin Shaozong seemed to have only heard the last sentence.","This man's hands were getting restless again. Dai Li was so pestered by him that she had no choice but to say, \"Wait until the second day of the fourth month.\"","The second day of the fourth month was his birthday, which was only a few days away.","Qin Shaozong suddenly laughed heartily, his firm chest rising and falling continuously. Held in his arms and forced to lean against his chest, Dai Li felt the endless vibrations and his powerful, rhythmic heartbeats.","Sigh, forget it, she wouldn't hold it against him.","Qin Shaozong didn't press the matter any further, but the \"torture to extract a confession\" was replaced by something else, and a romantic spring atmosphere spread within the bed curtains.","After one round, Dai Li leaned against the brocade pillow with slightly damp temples. Her beautifully shaped peach-blossom eyes were half-closed. Satisfied, she entered a state of post-coital tranquility.","However, that rough, large hand was still exploring everywhere like a swimming fish, as if searching for treasure at the bottom of the sea, delving here and checking there. It was also like a tiger patrolling its territory, always liking to leave marks as signs, which was quite annoying.","Unable to bear the disturbance, Dai Li swatted his hand away. \"Time to sleep. I still have to wake up early tomorrow.\"","But just as she finished speaking, she clearly felt something poking her. Dai Li's eyes couldn't help but widen. \"You still...\"","Facts proved that he was in high spirits and indeed wanted to go for another round. \"Madam, wrap your legs around.\"","Dai Li hadn't taken a nap during the day, and right now her eyelids were almost glued shut. Hearing his words, she shuddered. \"Didn't you go to the military camp during the day? How have you still not used up all that brute strength of yours?\"","He only smiled without speaking, continuing to busy himself.","Swaying along with him, Dai Li thought groggily that a man with too much energy was only suited to be a leader, not a husband.","*","In the blink of an eye, the second day of the fourth month arrived.","This day was no different from the past—equally clear and bright, with a gentle and pleasant breeze. But for many people, especially the prestigious and noble families of Yuyang, today was of extraordinary significance.","They woke up before dawn, ordered their servants to recount the heavy gifts they had prepared in advance, and then loaded them onto carriages to transport to the Marquis Manor, striving to make their family the first to deliver a gift.","As for the people themselves...","Visiting cards had been sent long ago, but that person's intention was not to host a grand banquet, but only to have a casual meal with family.","However, the so-called \"casual meal\" in the Marquis Manor wasn't really just inviting a few family members as claimed externally. The core leadership team of the North all came. Dai Li and Qin Shaozong sat at the head, while the military generals and advisors sat in rows below.","Delicious dishes were neatly arranged on the tables, including both hot and cold dishes, as well as sweets. In addition, on every long table sat a pot of lamb wine, which was good for the spleen and stomach and replenished vitality.","The North in early spring still carried a chill, but the atmosphere in the hall was lively. Coupled with the nourishing and warming wine, even though there was only one charcoal brazier placed in the corner, it was still surprisingly warm.","Mo Yanyun stood up with his cup. \"Since the Marquis won't allow us to present congratulatory gifts today, this subordinate can only toast you with wine. I wish you good health, smooth sailing in all endeavors, and a victorious start in the upcoming battle with the South!\"","The other military generals raised their cups in unison to congratulate him, and Qin Shaozong smiled in response.","After several rounds of drinks, someone could not help but ask, \"Why didn't the Lord accept our congratulatory gifts?\"","The banquet turned away prominent families without invitations, but for the military officers and aides, they could only choose one between their presence and their gifts. Either the person came, or the gift arrived. Naturally, they chose to attend the banquet in person. As for the congratulatory gifts...","They could just find another excuse to present them on another day.","Qiao Wangfei had also consumed quite a bit of wine. Unable to keep his mouth shut after holding it in for months, he burst out, \"That is naturally because the Madam is about to make her move! With the Madam's gift present, whatever we offer would be like mere stars trying to outshine the bright moon, completely not worth mentioning. The Lord refusing our gifts was to save our face!\"","\"Oh? You know about it?\"","\"How could it not be worth mentioning? I prepared several jugs of ten-year-old medicinal wine. It can invigorate the blood, dissipate bruises, and strengthen the body. How is that not worth mentioning?\"","\"And me, I found two top-tier hunting falcons, already fully trained and perfect for communication. How could they be mere starlight?\"","\"What exactly did the Madam prepare?\"","...","The crowd chattered all at once.","Sitting at the head of the hall, Qin Shaozong listened to their arguments. He was not without his own burning curiosity, so he knowingly asked, \"Madam has prepared a gift for me?\"","Since the atmosphere had already reached this point, Daili did not hide it anymore. She first nodded, then called out loudly to the outside, \"Bring it in!\"","Shortly after she spoke, two soldiers walked in, carrying a wooden chest as tall as a person, one on the left and one on the right.","The wooden box was not entirely sealed. The side facing the head seat and the top had their wooden boards removed. The front was covered only by a piece of red silk draped from top to bottom, secured at the four corners with small iron nails.","\"What is this, to be packed in such a tall box?\"","\"Looks like a vase.\"","\"Your head must be filled with sloshing water. If there were a vase inside, why would Qiao Wangfei say nothing could surpass it? Given this height, it looks a bit like a weapon.\"","\"A weapon could just be presented directly. Why put it in a box?\"","Daili stepped down from the head seat. Just as she reached the large box and was about to turn around, she caught a glimpse of a dark shadow following closely beside her from the corner of her eye. Qin Shaozong had actually followed her down. It seemed he was quite impatient.","Daili did not keep them in suspense any longer and directly pulled the red cloth down.","A sudden gleam appeared in Qin Shaozong's eyes, and his pupils abruptly shrank.","Inside the box was a suit of armor.","The entire set of armor was propped up by a wooden pole inside. The helmet at the top was at the exact same height as Qin Shaozong, evidently designed according to his physique.","The armor as a whole featured gold and dark iron colors. Both sides of the helmet had upward-curling ear guards, and a Taotie beast with its massive mouth wide open sat on top, exuding a magnificent and imposing aura.","Unlike the mainstream armor of the Great Yan Dynasty, this suit featured two oval metal plates on the chest and back. The plates were forged as a single piece, which helped to disperse impact forces, allowing it to withstand attacks from nearly hundred-pound bows and cavalry lances.","Thousands of fish-scale and rectangular armor pieces were densely and methodically woven together, resembling the sparkling golden ripples on a lake.","Furthermore, the skirt armor was no longer the traditional one-piece design. It was divided into left and right pieces that reached the knees, with front and back groin guards covering the middle to protect the crotch area.","It should be known that current skirt armors wrapped from front to back like an apron, consisting of only a single piece. A one-piece skirt armor inherently made horseback riding quite inconvenient, so some cavalrymen did not wear skirt armor at all, or wore very short ones. Thus, even if they wore armor, it protected the top but neglected the bottom.","Obviously, the armor before Qin Shaozong had no such drawbacks. Not only did it offer excellent protection, but it was also exceptionally domineering. There was no military general who would not love it, and even a layman would be awed by it.","\"This is the Mingguang Armor, your birthday gift,\" Daili said with a smile.","The Mingguang Armor. Some say it was the foremost among the dozen or so types of armor in the prosperous Tang Dynasty, and even the pinnacle of ancient Chinese defensive equipment.","The Book of Zhou once recorded: When You wore the Mingguang iron armor, he was invincible. The enemies all said, This is an iron beast, and they all hastily avoided him.","The people on both sides could not see the contents of the box, but they could clearly see Qin Shaozong's expression. The man, who had always been as steady as a mountain, instantly had his eyes light up. His face glowed red, and he could not help but reach out to touch it. His affection for it was completely beyond words.","Someone could not sit still any longer and left their seat to take a look.","Upon looking, that person took a sharp breath. His eyes shone, unable to bear looking away, and he practically drooled. \"How incredibly majestic!\"","Where there was one, there was a second. The crowd left their seats one after another.","The hall exploded into a clamor.","\"Madam, why have I never seen this armor before? Which master forged this?\"","\"Lord, could you let me touch it? No, you should lend it to me to try on.\"","\"Move aside, do not push me! Sigh, how about we take apart the other wooden boards of the box? That way we can see it more clearly.\"","The wooden boards were quickly removed. Qin Shaozong swatted away several paws that wanted to touch the Mingguang Armor. He first took down the helmet, and then the upper armor. He could not bear to part with it and actually felt somewhat reluctant to wear it. After lingering over it for a few moments, he looked at Daili beside him, his gaze burning.","\"Why are you looking at me? Try it on and see if it fits,\" Daili chuckled.","Qin Shaozong put it on right then and there.","His stature was taller than that of an ordinary man, and he was also more muscular. After donning this gleaming golden Mingguang Armor, he appeared even more heroic and majestic, like a heavenly deity descending to the mortal realm.","Qin Shaozong raised his arms, bent his elbows, and twisted his waist to turn sideways. He found it to be a perfect fit, unmistakably tailored to his exact measurements. Moreover, despite the armor clearly having so many scales, there was absolutely no sense of clumsiness or sluggishness; it was comfortable everywhere.","Bai Jianping, Mo Yanyun, and the others stared with straight eyes. If the person before them was not their superior, they would have definitely stripped that Mingguang Armor off him on the spot and put it on themselves.","\"Walk out into the front courtyard and take a look,\" Daili patted his arm.","The sunlight was just right. As soon as Qin Shaozong stepped into the courtyard, the Mingguang Armor on his body shone even brighter. It was as if his entire person was glowing.","Qin Qinian's eyes were dazzled, but he still could not bear to look away. He eagerly walked up to Qin Shaozong, looking incredibly envious. \"Father, could you lend it to me to wear once? Just once! I beg you...\"","Qin Shaozong cast a sidelong glance at him. \"Go stand under that tree.\"","Qin Qinian followed his gaze to look at the tree in the front courtyard, then turned his head back in confusion. \"Why? Are you planning to take off the armor there?\"","Qin Shaozong sneered. \"It is cool over there. Roll over there and stay put.\"","Daili was speechless.","Seeing Qin Qinian's disappointed face, Daili said, \"Qinian, do not rush. You will have one too.\"","Several gazes instantly swept over. Daili pretended not to notice. \"Your father's birthday was imminent, so we rushed to make his set of Mingguang Armor first. Yours and Zhou Zhou's sets will take a few more days to finish. Just wait a little while.\"","Well, a certain someone was satisfied."]},{"number":184,"title":"Chapter 184","paragraphs":["The footsteps of spring faded away, and summer closely followed. Soon, the day of Qin Shaozong's planned military expedition arrived.","Dai Li had previously been titled Lord Wuling in Chang'an, with her fiefdom in Wuling. Wuling was located in the heartland of Jingzhou. At that time, the Empress Dowager had held her nose and granted Dai Li the title, feeling displeased, so she simply threw her a useless piece of land.","It was just an empty title, sounding nice but yielding absolutely no tax revenue.","However, Qin Shaozong had now found a different approach. The official reason for his expedition was precisely: to collect taxes in Wuling!","In name, it barely made sense. As for whether Liu Zhan would open the city gates wide to welcome this tax-collecting army, that was another matter entirely.","Dai Li would not depart with Qin Shaozong this time. She still had some matters to handle in Yuyang. Once finished, she would travel south to Chang'an with Shi Rongyue.","She would wait for his triumphant return in Chang'an.","Outside the city, the army was lined up in an orderly fashion. The stalwart man, wearing a taotie helmet and gleaming armor, looked down at his wife before him. He raised a hand to adjust the gold filigree butterfly hairpin on her head, then smoothed out its long beaded tassels. The two hunting falcons Mo Yanyun gifted us are quite good. We each have one. My lady, remember to write to me.","Dai Li felt helpless. He had said this once before going to sleep last night, and she hadn't expected him to say it again right before leaving. I will write to you whenever I have free time, alright?","That would be best, Qin Shaozong curled his lips.","Dai Li said solemnly, The journey ahead is long and arduous with mountains and rivers. Husband, take good care of yourself. There is no need to rush for success in the war. In terms of supplies and troops, our side has a great advantage. Victory is only a matter of time. I will wait for your triumphant return in Chang'an...","She originally wanted to say more, but as she spoke, she suddenly realized that this scene and these words felt very much like an ominous flag in movies and television dramas, so she quickly stopped.","The curve of Qin Shaozong's lips deepened. My lady, call me that one more time.","Dai Li paused for a moment before understanding. Qin Changgeng really loved hearing her call him husband. He had listened to it all night yesterday and still hadn't had enough; he wanted to hear it again now.","But in broad daylight, in front of a crowd, to specifically call him that...","Forget it. He was about to march off to war. She couldn't refuse him this small request.","Dai Li smiled slowly, I wish my husband victory upon the first battle and a safe return home.","This expedition will take at least half a year, and at most a year and a half. My lady, wait for my return. Qin Shaozong took a deep look at her before turning around. The wind blew his red cape behind him. The stalwart figure vaulted onto his horse, the cape billowing in a sharp arc, like a fierce tiger baring its fangs and claws.","Dai Li looked at her two sons, who were also wearing armor, and warmly admonished them. Her words might sound boring to others, nothing more than telling them to eat well, pay attention to safety on the battlefield, not to act recklessly, and to keep an extra eye out.","Qin Yanzhou and Qin Qinian listened very seriously.","We will remember Mother's teachings.","We will remember Mother's teachings.","Dai Li smiled and patted their shoulders. Go on.","As the armored cavalry rumbled away, the smile on Dai Li's lips slowly faded, and her vision blurred. She took out a handkerchief and wiped the corners of her eyes, feeling a tight ache in her chest.","However, Dai Li's melancholy did not last long, because that very night, a messenger falcon flew back. She looked at the small message tube on the falcon's leg, then at the bird flapping its wings begging for food, not knowing whether to laugh or cry.","He had only just left.","Dai Li took the letter and unrolled it. His handwriting was as flamboyant as ever, unable to hide his wild arrogance, and the words in the letter had absolutely nothing to do with the word subtle.","We have been apart for less than a day, yet I am already madly missing you. In the past, I never found military life difficult, but now without you by my side, the iron armor feels soaked in the cold moonlight, and I toss and turn, unable to sleep. I greatly miss last night, tossing in the red waves with you to express my longing.","I think of you, I miss you, I want to embrace, kiss, and linger with you.","Write back to me. A million kisses to you.","Dai Li's cheeks flushed slightly.","This man really dared to write anything. What if the falcon delivered it to the wrong place, or the tube accidentally fell off and someone else saw it? Where would she put her face?","Though she muttered complaints about him, Dai Li still ground some ink and picked up a brush to write him a reply.","On the evening of the second day, the messenger falcon returned again.","He was somewhat dissatisfied upon receiving her reply.","My dearest's reply was too perfunctory, leaving my heart full of sorrow and depressed without a smile. I only hate that I do not have wings to fly back to Yuyang and teach you hand-in-hand how to write a reply.","The military journey is tormenting, but your undergarments have comforted me greatly...","Write back to me. A million kisses to you.","Dai Li covered her face with her hands, blocking her eyes, pretending she hadn't seen the line your undergarments have comforted me greatly, but the heat rising on her face was quite burning, making it impossible for her to deceive herself.","Before he left for the expedition, he had taken several of her undergarments. Fine, let him take them. It wasn't as if she didn't know what he used them for in private.","But knowing it was one thing; him blatantly writing it on paper and sending it back was another.","Dai Li wrote him back.","Qin Changgeng! You are not allowed to write private matters on paper. What if someone else sees it? Do you have no shame?","She even specifically drew a displeased emoticon on the letter paper (◣_◢)","He replied: ...The little drawing is very cute. Seeing it is like seeing my dearest. Kisses to it.","A general in the field is not bound by the sovereign's commands. The messenger falcon is extremely reliable. No one can catch even a glimpse of this. My dearest, just put your heart back in your stomach.","Write back to me. A million kisses to you.","...","In the beginning, after the army left, Dai Li received letters from Qin Shaozong every day. But gradually, every day turned into every other day, and then into every few days.","Dai Li knew that he was getting further and further away.","This time she stayed in Yuyang not only to handle the logistical work for the army but also to attend to an important matter:","Arranging the engagement for Zhou Zhou and Rongrong.","In this era, marriages among prominent families were extremely complicated. Going through the three letters and six etiquettes took a long time. The initial steps of presenting betrothal gifts, asking for the bride's name, matching the birthdates, and sending the formal betrothal gifts were all handled single-handedly by Dai Li.","By the time she finished with all these matters, a season had unknowingly passed, and time had arrived at the bountiful autumn.","Thanks to the great harvest last year, the promotion of fertilizer required no effort at all. The commoners in the north all knew that this was a powerful tool that could drastically increase the grain yield of their fields.","Since ancient times, good things had always been fought over; there was no reason to push them away. Therefore, after this year's great harvest, the new round of composting did not require Dai Li to post notices widely or beat gongs and drums to urge people on. Every household in the north was highly enthusiastic.","Composting required manure and soil. During that time, the streets of Yuyang and its surrounding cities were exceptionally clean. There were no cow or horse droppings to be seen on the roads. Even if fresh manure had just hit the ground and its heat hadn't dissipated yet, it would be picked up by someone immediately.","It had to be said that the promotion of composting had, to some extent, made a significant contribution to the city's sanitation.","...","On the other hand, Dai Li organized the grain and forage harvested this year, and then set off south to escort the supplies with Shi Rongyue and the military instructor Jin Duole. Before heading south to Chang'an, she had already received a letter from Qin Shaozong telling her that the war was about to begin.","With the battle about to start, it was no longer just a march. The letters from now on would decrease. He hoped for her understanding, and more importantly, hoped she wouldn't forget to miss him.","Sure enough, after this family letter representing that the flames of war have been ignited, the frequency of letters from the south indeed dropped significantly. Sometimes it took half a month to receive a single letter.","Though his letters came slowly, Dai Li continued to write to him as usual, one letter every seven days. Sometimes she had messengers deliver them, and sometimes she used the returning messenger falcons.","In the letter, he told him about the engagement of the younger generation, about the golden autumn in Yuyang, and also that he was going south soon.","Dai Li was also sending letters on her way to Chang'an. She learned that he successfully led the army to take Tianmen Pass, drove straight in, and broke several cities in succession; she also knew that he set a trap and killed a certain enemy leader from Jingzhou who came to sneak attack, and discovered from clues that the Qinglian Sect and Jingzhou Governor Liu Zhan were mixed together; she also knew what merits her two sons had achieved respectively.","When Dai Li arrived in Chang'an, the war in the south became more intense. The Northern Army, led by Qin Shaozong, kept its pace and continued to penetrate deeply, faintly deciding the outcome.","The advancement of the war situation brought a lot of chain reactions. The specific manifestation was that the Taiwei Mansion could receive several baskets of visiting cards every day, and those who wanted to visit were as numerous as carp crossing the river; if a family in Chang'an held a grand banquet, they would always send an invitation to Dai Li.","Whether she arrived or not was another matter, but they would definitely invite her.","Dai Li accepted very few of those visiting cards that fluttered like snowflakes, and only went to banquets two or three times, participating little. Seeing that they couldn't invite her, the prominent families simply changed their way and sent gifts.","If the person couldn't be invited, the gift had to arrive.","Gold, silver, jewelry, and rare treasures should always be liked!","With the current war situation, the northern forces were likely to grow further. When her husband returned in triumph, the universe might be changed. Now giving more gifts to his wife and letting her blow pillow talk when the time came would be good.","The abacus was loud, so loud that it reached Dai Li's ears, and was directly rejected by her.","She was not interested in precious ornaments, but she liked jewelry very much. However, there were plenty of them in the Marquis's Mansion. Which of the pieces in the makeup box in Dai Li's room was not priceless? As for other things, no matter how rare they were, they couldn't be rarer than modern high technology.","Therefore, Dai Li's heart was completely still.","The days passed like flowers and plain, and in a blink of an eye, the severe winter had passed, and it entered the chilly early spring.","Holding hot tea, Dai Li curled up in the snow-white fox fur cloak, her thoughts scattered. Calculating the time, it had been more than half a year since Qin Changgeng went to war. He said that the shortest time was half a year, and the fastest time was a year and a half. Now half a year had passed, and she didn't know how the war was going over there.","His last letter was more than a month ago, and this time the interval was longer than before. Alas, communication in ancient times was really inconvenient. How good it would be if there was a mobile phone...","The hot tea in her hand unknowingly lost its temperature. Dai Li put down the cup and grabbed the teapot on the small charcoal stove next to her to pour tea for herself.","But she was distracted when pouring water. The mouth of the pot was not aimed at the teacup. The boiling hot tea poured on the table and quickly scraped down along the table surface.","Dai Li sat next to the table. It was not until the boiling water on the table scraped down onto her leg that she shook violently, suddenly threw away the teapot, and hurriedly stepped back.","\"Madam!\" Nianxia went to the kitchen and saw this scene when she returned. Her face changed in shock, \"I'll go call the mansion doctor over.\"","Dai Li stopped her, \"The clothes are thick, so I didn't get burned much.\"","\"Quickly change your wet clothes.\" Nianxia hurried inside to find clothes for her, and couldn't help complaining: \"Where is Bipo, why isn't she serving by your side?\"","\"It's normal for people to have three urgencies. She went to the toilet. Besides, this is also my own carelessness.\" Dai Li took off her cloak and took off the wet dress one by one. Looking at her slightly red thigh, she reached out and touched it.","It hurt a little, but it was bearable.","Looking at her red skin, Dai Li's heart beat fast. For some reason, she felt inexplicably panicked.","\"I'll go get you some ointment.\" Seeing that she didn't want to see the mansion doctor, Nianxia had to say.","This time Dai Li did not refuse.","After a long while, Bipo ran back excitedly, \"Madam, the Taiwei has sent a letter!\"","Dai Li was startled, and then overjoyed. After she came to Chang'an, the letters from the south were much fewer. Including today's, she had only received two letters from Qin Shaozong.","Unable to wait for Nianxia to come back, she went directly to the hall.","The travel-stained messenger saw Dai Li, first bowed and greeted her, and then took out an envelope with sealing wax from his arms, \"Mistress, the Marquis said that everything is fine in the army, and asked you not to worry. Please check the letter.\"","Seeing that the dark circles under his eyes were heavy and he looked tired, Dai Li called the mansion guards to take him to rest. After the messenger left, she didn't take the letter back to the main courtyard to read, but opened it directly in the hall.","The weight of the letter was not much different from that sent by past messengers, but after unfolding it, Dai Li found that something was wrong.","Qin Shaozong's handwriting was easy to recognize, with iron strokes and silver hooks, penetrating the back of the paper, and that arrogant spirit was exactly the same as him. However, the handwriting of the letter in her hand was much more restrained, and the strokes restrained the sharp edge, which was clearly her son Qin Yanzhou's own handwriting.","Zhou Zhou used to write letters to her, but his own and those he wrote on behalf of Qi Nian accounted for at most 30% in total, and the remaining 70% belonged to Qin Changgeng. Sometimes the father would even eat alone, leaving no room for his son at all.","But now, there was no trace of Qin Changgeng's handwriting on the paper.","Dai Li read the sentence \"My father has been very busy recently, so I wrote it on his behalf\" in her son's letter twice, and her brows frowned deeper and deeper.","Wrote on his behalf?","This was something that had never happened before.","Thinking of what the messenger said, Dai Li couldn't help but ask someone to bring back the messenger who had just been taken to rest.","\"Mistress, what are your orders?\" The messenger lowered his head.","Dai Li looked at him unblinkingly, \"The Marquis had an accident on the battlefield, didn't he?\"","This was a question, but there was not much doubtful tone.","The messenger subconsciously looked up, his face changed drastically, \"Mistress...\"","Seeing his appearance, Dai Li understood everything. She fell into an ice cellar in an instant. It was clearly early spring, but the sunshine outside couldn't dispel the chill. That invisible cold wind poured into her lungs, making her cold all the way to the depths of her spine.","\"Tell me the truth!\" Dai Li said in a deep voice.","Having been with Qin Shaozong for a long time, even Dai Li herself didn't realize it. At this time, her expression and surrounding aura were a bit similar to him, with sharp cold light in her eyes, angry and majestic, very powerful.","The soldier was startled, and forgot the instructions he was given when he came for a moment, and couldn't help saying, \"The Marquis was shot by an arrow on the battlefield...\"","Dai Li's brain buzzed, and the blood color on her face faded. If it wasn't for Bipo supporting her in time, she might not have been able to stand firm.","After the first sentence was finished, the soldier knew it was bad. But the spilled water couldn't be recovered, he had to quickly say: \"The Marquis was wearing the Mingguang armor, and the enemy already knew its power, so that arrow was not aimed at the vital parts.\"","Dai Li bit her lip, using the pain to dispel her dizziness, \"How is the Marquis now?\"","The soldier actually shook his head and said he didn't know exactly, but said, \"Since the Marquis was shot, he has never been out of the military tent, but Mr. Ding said that the injury is not serious, but he needs to rest.\"","Dai Li also asked other things, such as the frontline war situation after Qin Shaozong was injured, and the reactions of high-ranking military generals in the army, as well as the frequency of Mr. Ding entering and leaving the main tent.","The most important things were not hidden, and the messenger answered all the subsequent questions asked by Dai Li.","So Dai Li learned that the battle that injured Qin Shaozong ultimately resulted in a great victory for the Northern Army. A group of military generals represented by Qiao Wangfei performed their respective duties after breaking the city.","And the military doctor Ding Lianxi didn't stay in the main tent all the time except at the beginning. The time he went in and out subsequently was also very regular, once in the morning, noon, and evening, for half an hour each time.","Daili frowned in deep thought.","The messenger suddenly remembered something. Before I left, the Marquis instructed me to ask you for some letters so I could bring them back with me.","Daili asked, Did you see him?","The messenger shook his head and said no, explaining that he was only passing on a message.","Daili said, You have endured a hard and exhausting journey. Go and get some rest for now.","She walked slowly back to the main courtyard. Upon returning, she spread the letter out again and read it carefully once more. The letter made absolutely no mention of Qin Changgeng being injured; it merely spoke of various matters following victories big and small, reading much like casual family chatter.","Daili tapped her fingertips absently against the desk.","For now, it seemed the army's morale was still stable, and Mr. Ding was not guarding him day and night as one would a patient whose life hung by a thread.","Looking at it this way, his injuries could not be too severe.","Rationally, Daili knew he was likely not in imminent danger. After all, the protective capability of the Mingguang armor was not made of paper; it absolutely lived up to its reputation as the finest armor of the prosperous Tang Dynasty.","Emotionally, however, another voice kept whispering in her ear:","If his life was not in peril, why would a proud and unyielding man like Qin Changgeng remain inside his military tent for days on end, failing to show his face before the soldiers?","Taking a step back, even if the injury was a ruse to confuse the enemy, should that not only involve the battlefield? Why would he deceive her as well, all the way in Chang'an?","So it definitely was not a ruse!","Something had truly happened to him...","Daili felt restless and anxious. As she turned the possibilities over and over in her mind, an idea emerged from the hazy fog and gradually became clear.","She looked out the brightly lit window at the delicate, beautiful flower buds slowly coming into bloom, took a deep breath, and slowly exhaled.","Bipo, help me pack a simple travel bag. Nianxia, go invite Mr. Jin over. Tell him I want to make a change to the personnel assigned to deliver supplies to the army."]},{"number":185,"title":"Chapter 185","paragraphs":["Transporting grain was no spring outing. The mission had to prioritize the frontline, leaving no room for the convoy to dawdle. That was why Dai Li and the logistics grain team traveled day and night, hurrying nonstop for six full days before finally reaching Gengshui in Jingzhou.","Gengshui City was not a border town of Jingzhou; it sat deep in the region's heartland. This spoke volumes about how far south Qin Shaozong had fought, seizing city after city over the past half year and amassing extraordinary battle merits.","Gengshui City had already fallen, but its streets could not hold the entire Northern Army. Qin Shaozong had no intention of disturbing the local people, so his troops remained camped outside the city in the countryside.","The moment the grain convoy arrived at the frontline military camp, it immediately sparked a wave of excitement. With provisions finally here, every soldier was overjoyed. The great victory they had won not long ago could now be properly celebrated with a grand feast!","But then...","\"Madam?\" Mo Yanyun thought his eyes were playing tricks on him, but after rubbing them and looking again, he saw the bright-eyed woman in a black riding outfit, with fair skin and vivid red lips. Who else could she be but their Madam?","\"Madam, what on earth are you doing here?\" Mo Yanyun hurried over to greet her. \"The journey must have been tough. Let me make you a pot of hot tea to refresh yourself.\"","Dai Li cut straight to the point. \"Where is Qin Changgeng? Is he in the main tent?\"","Mo Yanyun's expression shifted, a mix of awkwardness and hesitation crossing his face. \"...Yes, he is.\"","Hearing his confirmation, Dai Li immediately headed for the large military tent topped with a red tassel at the center of the camp. Mo Yanyun scurried after her, keeping pace step by step. \"Ah, Madam, please don't worry too much. In fact... His Lordship is no longer in any mortal danger now.\"","Dai Li's breath caught, her heart feeling as if it had been tossed into a dye vat or a bonfire, so tangled she could no longer tell if the ache in her chest was sourness or raw distress. \"He is safe now—so that means he was in mortal danger before?\"","Mo Yanyun avoided her gaze, too nervous to speak a word.","Dai Li did not press him further, instead quickening her steps toward the tent.","It was high noon now, and with sufficient grain supplies, the soldiers were served three full meals a day. Just then, Dai Li spotted a mess sergeant carrying a food box toward the main tent. She stopped him in his tracks and took the food box from his hands.","The second Dai Li lifted the tent flap and stepped inside, a strong, heavy stench of medicinal herbs assailed her nostrils, so thick she felt for a split second that she had fallen straight into a giant vat of medicinal brew.","The main tent was not spacious, unlike the master bedroom in the Marquis's Manor which was divided into an inner and outer chamber. So Dai Li caught sight of the man lying on the soft couch in the far corner at once.","He was dressed in a plain black inner robe, a thin quilt draped over his abdomen, his eyes closed as he slept. Judging purely from his appearance, Qin Shaozong looked no more than a little pale, with no obvious signs of injury.","But she knew him well. Qin Changgeng was a man of boundless energy; even with only two hours of sleep a day, he would still be full of vigor. From what Qiao Wangfei and the others had told her, it was common for him to stay awake for a full day and night straight when leading troops in past campaigns.","Now it was broad daylight, and the war had temporarily drawn to a close with no urgent matters demanding his attention—yet he was fast asleep...","Dai Li stood watching him for a long moment, then tiptoed over and set the food box down on the low table. The wooden box tapped against the wooden table, and even with all her care to move as gently as possible, the faint sound still carried.","Perhaps because he had not heard the usual footsteps approaching, the man on the couch twitched his brows. Still with his eyes shut, he spoke, \"Leave the things here and go out.\"","Dai Li noted that his voice did not have the usual robust energy, though it was far from weak and threadbare, and the tight knot in her chest loosened a little. \"Food tastes best when eaten hot.\"","The man on the couch jolted awake, sitting straight up in a single swift motion. Halfway through the movement, he pulled at some hidden injury, his whole body stiffening for a moment, his face flushing a ghostly pale for a split second. But he only twitched the corner of his jaw, letting no other flicker of pain show on his face.","Dai Li was startled by his sudden move. \"What are you doing? Stay lying down properly!\"","Qin Shaozong's eyes blazed bright as he looked her over from head to toe, as if making sure he was not seeing her in a dream. Only after he confirmed she was real did he wave at her to come closer. \"How did my lady come here?\"","\"Of course I came to see you. All you wrote in your letters were nice, pleasant words, but you never told me a single bit of the real situation. Where is the sense in only reporting good news and hiding all the bad?\" Dai Li walked over, but did not sit down beside the couch, even when Qin Shaozong shifted inward to make space for her.","Qin Shaozong said nothing, just smiled as he reached for her hand, trying to pull her onto the couch to sit with him.","Dai Li stood her ground, not wanting to crowd his injured body. \"I heard you took an arrow on the battlefield, and after you got wounded, you did not leave your military tent for several days. Where exactly are you hurt? What did Doctor Ding say? Was there something wrong with your bright light armor? Otherwise, how could you have been injured so badly?\"","One question after another came pouring out, but the man being asked did not answer a single one. The corners of his mouth just lifted higher and higher, until he finally let out a low, soft laugh.","Seeing that he still had the mood to laugh, Dai Li, who had been tormented by anxious fire all the way here, grew angry. She spoke in a sharper tone. \"I am talking to you, Qin Changgeng. Stop being so playful and pull yourself together! These are all very serious questions!\"","\"It's just a minor injury, no big deal.\" Qin Shaozong pulled her onto the couch to sit down. \"When did my lady set off for Jingzhou? Did you run into any trouble on the road?\"","He brushed off the whole matter with that one light line about a minor injury, saying nothing else at all, as if the stiffness he showed when he got up a moment earlier never existed. Instead, he started asking her questions.","Dai Li felt a tight knot in her chest. The worry, hesitation and fear she had carried all along the journey, along with the wild, uncontrollable thoughts that had plagued her through one sleepless night after another, were now fermenting and surging in her veins, turning into a rush of hot blood that flooded her face and stung her eyes.","She did not want to sit at all, and abruptly shot to her feet. \"Qin Changgeng, why are you still exactly the same?! You never tell me anything! I did not press you for answers in the past, but now even when I ask, you still keep quiet. You take every big and small matter all on your own. Have you ever spared a thought for how I feel? Is that any way for a husband to act?!\"","Qin Shaozong saw her eyes turning red, and his head felt like it was about to split open. \"Don't cry, my lady, I didn't mean to...\"","He tried to get off the couch.","\"Don't you dare move! Who told you to get up? Who gave you permission to get up? Stay lying down properly!\" Dai Li snapped at him.","The man had no choice but to still his movements. \"Fine, fine, I won't move. Don't cry, my lady. When you cry, I feel so uneasy that my whole body aches.\"","\"That's just nonsense. Don't try to shift the blame onto me! Your whole body aches because of your injuries, what does that have to do with me?\" Dai Li turned her eyes away from him.","Qin Shaozong sighed, and reached for her hand again. Dai Li tried to shake him off, but the moment she moved her hand, she heard a very exaggerated gasp of pain.","Dai Li pressed her lips tightly together, knowing full well he was faking it. The real discomfort he had felt was back when he first got up a moment earlier, and he had barely even shown it. She had only moved her hand a little, not punched him at all, so he was just pulling a cheap pity trick.","There was no end to the dissatisfaction bubbling up in her heart, but Dai Li still did not pull her hand away in the end. She let him pull her back to sit on the couch again.","Dai Li sat sideways, not facing him.","\"I have fought on the battlefields for many years. Those wounds are nothing but superficial scrapes to me. But you, my lady...\" Qin Shaozong raised his hand to brush over her red, tear-stained eye corners, his fingers gently grazing the wet dark eyelashes there. \"Seeing your tears feels like ten thousand arrows piercing my heart. It makes me so restless that I cannot sit still.\"","\"You'd be restless? I think you were perfectly at ease when you were lying to me,\" Dai Li snapped, turning her head to glare at him.","Qin Shaozong said in a low voice, \"I never meant to deceive you. I just wanted to wait until I returned victorious to tell my wife...\"","Even under her furious glower, Qin Shaozong did not change his expression. \"Dai Li, I am your man. No man worth his salt would let his own wife weep day after day. Even if the sky were to fall, you would never need to concern yourself with it. I would hold it up for you.\"","Dai Li ground her teeth in frustration. \"Qin Changgeng, can you rein in that damned overbearing male ego of yours? We are husband and wife. Spouses should be honest with each other. You were so injured you couldn't even leave your military tent, yet you still claimed it was just a minor nothing. What if—\"","She could not bring herself to finish the rest of the sentence. Her voice choked up, and her vision blurred completely.","Qin Shaozong was never afraid of her sharp scoldings, nor of her giving him the silent treatment. But he was utterly helpless the moment he saw her tears. In a slight panic, he reached for something on the couch to wipe her face. \"Don't cry. There are no 'what ifs'. I promise you. Your husband is as fit as can be, and I will live a long, full life right alongside you.\"","Dai Li felt the cloth against her face was far too large, big enough to wrap around her entire cheek. She grabbed his wrist and pushed his hand a little further away. The more she looked at that \"handkerchief\", the more familiar it seemed.","Thin ribbons hung down from it, apricot in color, with one side embroidered with meticulous peony patterns.","It was her own belly band!","This little undergarment was crumpled beyond recognition, all wrinkled like pickled vegetables, and it smelled a little odd too. She had no idea how many times it had been mishandled behind her back.","The heavy sorrow in her chest was suddenly cut short, left hanging halfway up and halfway down, making her throb with a headache. She pinched the bridge of her nose, then snatched the belly band right out of Qin Shaozong's hand, folded it quickly, and stuffed it under his pillow.","Out of sight, out of mind.","Qin Shaozong chuckled at the sight. \"Why, are you disgusted even by your own things?\"","Dai Li did not want to recall what had just been pressed all over her face. \"Qin Changgeng, where are you injured exactly?\"","Qin Shaozong said, \"My right shoulder blade.\"","That was why his right arm barely moved, making it impossible for him to hold a brush and write letters.","\"Didn't you wear your bright shining armor on the battlefield?\" Dai Li frowned and asked him.","Bright shining armor had shoulder guards that covered the shoulders thoroughly. There was no reason for the battle-hardened Qin Changgeng, fully kitted out in armor, to get shot by a stray arrow so badly that he had to stay bedridden for days.","Qin Shaozong said, \"I did wear it.\"","\"Then tell me the truth, no more hiding anything. I'm already in the military camp now. Even if you won't tell me, I can just ask Doctor Ding, or Zhou Zhou and the others,\" Dai Li said sternly.","Qin Shaozong had not wanted to tell her, afraid the news would upset her. But he knew very well that if he kept it hidden, she would do exactly as she said and go ask someone else. So he tried to play it down as much as he could. \"In the battle before, Liu Zhan sent out every single one of his elite generals. First they fought us head-on in a narrow pass, then they dueled with us right under the city walls. In several small skirmishes one after another, every soldier that fought me aimed for my right shoulder. After all, that's the hand that holds weapons. If you can't strike at the heart, going for the second-best target is only natural. I didn't think much of it at the time...\"","They attacked, but he was no pushover. He blocked and struck back to take down his foes. But there were too many people on the battlefield, swords and blades had no eyes, and it was impossible to defend against every single thing.","The enemy attacked again and again. Those elite generals were like mad dogs, or as if they had lost their minds, fighting with total disregard for their own lives. Even though he had plenty of generals by his side, he still got grazed repeatedly by the blunt end of a blade. It wasn't anything serious. He had deflected over seventy percent of the force from every strike beforehand, and the remaining force was all absorbed by the bright shining armor.","After fending off wave after wave of attacks, the right pauldron on his armor had inevitably sustained damage. It was not completely broken to pieces, but it was certainly nowhere near as intact as it had been originally.","\"... Later, some bystanders shot several arrows at me with heavy bows, and one of them got past my guard,\" Qin Shaozong said. Seeing her face pale slightly, he quickly added, \"It's just an arrow wound. Before I married you, your husband marched north and fought south for years, and I've had countless arrow scars all over my body. Besides, with the Bright Light Armor blocking the way, that arrow didn't actually pierce very deep.\"","He spoke so casually, but Dai Li's heart was pounding with fright. Seeing that he was still trying to downplay the situation and gloss over the truth, she snapped at him, \"You're lying again, aren't you? If that arrow really didn't go in deep, why did you never step out of the military tent after you got hit? Tell me everything, don't keep anything from me.\"","Qin Shaozong stroked her back gently, just like how one would soothe a flustered little animal. \"The reason I stayed in the military tent the whole time was, first, to make Liu Zhan think his scheme had succeeded, and second, to mislead the Qinglian Sect.\"","At the end of his sentence, Qin Shaozong let out a mocking chuckle. \"Those big rats hiding in plain sight are the hardest to catch. The moment they sense any disturbance or realize things are going south, they can run faster than anyone else. If I were unharmed, that Liudao person Qin the Second mentioned would definitely withdraw from Geng City immediately.\"","Dai Li had heard from Qin the Second that the sect leader's two nephews had been eliminated, which meant he had lost his most important right-hand men. Now that Qin Shaozong had started a war with Liu Zhan, he was certain that with old grudges and new hatred piling up, that man would not be able to stay put any longer.","There was a very high chance that Liudao was in Geng City!","And the moment Geng City fell, he had ordered the city gates sealed at once, with Qin the Second leading the search to hunt the target down.","Dai Li's brows were still tightly furrowed. Even though he had laid out all these reasons, she still felt something was off.","Just a moment ago, he had clearly been in severe pain when he got up, his rest during the day had been genuine, and there had been that obvious hesitation on Mo Yanyun's face back then...","\"You still plan to keep it hidden from me, huh? Fine, then I'll go ask Doctor Ding myself. You rest well, my lord,\" Dai Li said as she stood up again.","Qin Shaozong's expression changed slightly.","Right at that moment, Ding Congjian's voice came from outside, \"My lord, I've come to change your dressing.\"","Dai Li thought this was perfect timing, and quickly led Ding Congjian inside. The latter was stunned for a moment when he saw she had come all the way to the military camp, then subconsciously glanced at Qin Shaozong.","That tiny action did not escape Dai Li's notice.","She immediately stepped sideways, blocking Ding Congjian's line of sight to Qin Shaozong. \"Doctor Ding, my lord just told me his injury is not serious at all. He doesn't want to keep lying still, and he even said that after so many days, his wound has almost healed, and he doesn't want to go through the trouble of changing dressings anymore.\"","\"How can that be allowed? Scraping the bone to remove the poison is no trivial matter!\" Ding Congjian blurted out.","The second the words left his mouth, he saw the color drain completely from Dai Li's face, turning as pale as a sheet. Ding Congjian froze, and hurriedly walked around her to look at Qin Shaozong, only to see his lord glaring at him fiercely.","His heart sank, and he thought to himself that he was in big trouble. The mistress had tricked him!","Just as he was about to say something to smooth things over, Dai Li spun around sharply. \"Qin Changgeng, you've really grown capable...\"","Before she could finish her sentence, tears started streaming down her face.","Qin Shaozong had been sitting on the couch this whole time, but the moment he saw those hot tears rolling out of her eyes, it was as if needles had pricked the cushion under him, and he could not stay seated any longer.","\"You get back to lie down right now! You won't listen to the doctor, and you won't listen to me either. Why don't you just sprout a pair of wings and fly straight up to the sky?\" Dai Li chided him.","Qin Shaozong did not lie back down. He walked over to take her hand, and said in a low voice, \"My dear wife, save me some face. Congjian is still here. Once he leaves, you can scold me however you want.\"","\"What good is saving face when your life is almost gone? Why cling to those empty formalities?\" Dai Li said with a cold sneer.","Ding Congjian kept his eyes fixed on his nose and his mind fixed on his breath, not daring to make a sound, and even wishing he could vanish on the spot.","Qin Shaozong raised his hand to wipe the tears off her face. \"You are not going to lose your life. Refusing treatment is the real danger. Now that I have pulled through, everything will be fine. Stop crying, my lady. The sight of your tears truly pains my heart. Speaking of which, we owe it all to that Mingguang armor. If not for it, the arrow would have sunk much deeper, and the poison would have been far harder to clear.\"","Dai Li would not look at him, and turned to speak to Ding Congjian instead. \"I must trouble you, sir, to change his dressing now.\"","\"Wait outside for me, my lady,\" Qin Shaozong said, knowing she could not bear to see the wounds.","Dai Li did not leave the tent. She only turned her back, and faint rustling sounds came from behind her. All the while, Qin Shaozong did not let out even a small grunt, acting as if he was not even there.","Ding Congjian finished changing the dressing quickly. Soon he tidied everything up, gave a few notes on post-treatment care, and then hurried to leave, afraid that if he stayed a moment longer, he would overhear things he had no business hearing.","\"Lady Dai,\" he called out.","Dai Li did not want to turn around, but she was also worried that the man would get off the couch on his own and tear his wounds open, so she had to turn around.","\"QIN! CHANG! GENG!\" Dai Li rushed over, half anxious and half furious, when she saw that he was indeed trying to get out of bed. \"Where have your ears gone? Why did you not listen to a single word Doctor Ding said? Are you tired of living? Let me be honest with you. I have no strict principles, and I do not value chastity that much. If I become a widow again, I will not say no to finding a new man.\"","\"How dare you?\" He did not react much to any of her previous words, but that last line made him fly into a rage.","\"Why wouldn't I dare? You always say I have the guts of a bear and a leopard all over me. Finding a new man is hardly anything at all, isn't it?\" Dai Li pushed him back down onto the couch. Seeing how furious he was, and worried that his wounds would split open, she softened her tone and added, \"That's why you have to live a long, long life. Best to live a full hundred years, and grow old together with me.\"","Qin Shaozong gripped her hand tight. It was hard to tell if he was angry or deeply moved, as overwhelming emotions surged in his chest, making his heart race and his mind feel full to bursting. He could only press a firm, heavy kiss to her wrist. \"Rest assured. I will never break my promise to you.\"","Dai Li was just about to check his wounds carefully, when a voice came from outside the tent. \"Father, Liudao has been arrested.\"","It was Qin Yanzhou's voice.","Dai Li froze, and was just about to get up to see the situation, when she heard Qin Shaozong speak. \"We spent nearly half a month hunting him down like looking for a needle in a haystack, and finally we have him. Bring him in!\"","Someone outside said, \"Bring more ropes, tie him up a few more times. Even though both his hands are crippled, it's better to be safe than sorry.\"","Soon the tent curtain was lifted. Dai Li saw Qin Yanzhou and Qin Qinian drag a man in, one on each side.","The man was dressed in a white robe, lean and thin, with large dark bloodstains on the fabric. He looked about six parts similar to Diting, fair-skinned and clean-jawed. Even though the years had left a few lines of weathering at the corners of his eyes, he still carried an uncanny, almost ethereal air of a Taoist immortal.","When Liudao stepped into the tent, he saw there was more than just Qin Shaozong inside. His gaze fell on Dai Li, and in an instant he figured out exactly who she was. He suddenly laughed softly and shook his head. \"I thought you were just like me, someone who yearned for that paradise where everyone is equal. It seems I misjudged you after all.\"","He did not say her name out loud as he spoke, but the answer was clear in his eyes.","The veins on Qin Shaozong's forehead tensed up.","\"You scoundrel! Who do you think you are, to speak to my mother like that?\" Qin Qinian burst into anger and kicked him hard.","Liudao took the full force of that kick without dodging, spitting out a mouthful of black blood. \"Lady Dai, you have been blinded by the allure of power. One day you will regret ever standing at his side. What good is the position of empress? It pales in comparison to the thrill of reshaping the entire world.\"","\"Hand over the list of the Qinglian Sect's core members, and I will grant you a swift death,\" Qin Shaozong said coldly.","Yet from start to finish, Liudao did not so much as glance at Qin Shaozong, as if he found him beneath his notice or simply did not care. His eyes were fixed only on Dai Li. \"I was just a step too late. If you had met me first, who knows what the world would look like today. Everything could have turned out differently...\"","If Qin Shaozong had still managed to hold his temper a moment earlier, he could no longer restrain himself now. He flew into a rage, shot to his feet, drew the sharp sword from the side of the couch with his left hand, and strode over, ready to slice Liudao's head off with a single strike.","Qin Yanzhou hurried forward to stop him. \"Father, we do not have the list yet.\"","Qin Shaozong shoved him away. \"This man has lost all his most trusted lieutenants, the Qinglian Sect has been dealt a devastating blow, and you, Qin the Second, are already familiar with the sect's ways of operating. Even if we never get the list, it will only take a little extra effort to handle the rest. They cannot possibly stir up any real trouble. Stand aside. I will kill him today no matter what.\"","But before Qin Shaozong could raise his sword, thick streams of black blood gushed from Liudao's seven orifices, exactly the same way the White Elephant had died suddenly before. He had taken poison in advance, and the toxin had already run its course, killing him instantly.","Qin Shaozong was so furious that he hurled his sword to the ground. \"He got off far too easily. Chop his corpse into eight pieces and throw it into the unmarked common graveyard outside the city to feed the stray dogs!\"","Qin Yanzhou and Qin Qinian then carried the body out together. The military camp was located on the outskirts, not far from that unmarked graveyard.","When they arrived at the site, Qin Yanzhou did not dismember the body and discard it as Qin Shaozong had ordered. Instead, he had his men dig a deep pit, and laid Liudao's lifeless body gently into it, completely intact.","\"Second Brother, why are you giving him a whole body and a proper burial? He does not deserve to rest in peace,\" Qin Qinian said, sounding rather reluctant.","After patting down the last handful of soil over the grave, Qin Yanzhou said calmly, \"Think of it as me repaying the last bit of kindness I owed him.\"","Once the task was done, Qin Yanzhou led the others away. He did not look back. A gust of wind picked up, swirling dead leaves across the ground as it brushed past the lone, silent grave.","In the battle at Gengshui, all the key fierce generals of the Jingzhou Army were cut down by Qin Shaozong's blade. Their cities fell, their forces were routed, and Liu Zhan had to lead his troops in a retreat again and again.","As if they had agreed on the timing, Nangong Xiong led his army out of Yizhou at that very moment, attacking the Jingzhou Army from the flank while Qin Shaozong's northern forces pressed in, sandwiching them between two fronts.","The subsequent south-north conflict dragged on for four full months before a final outcome was reached. It ended with Liu Zhan taking his own life by the sword, and the southern forces being completely wiped out.","From that point on, looking across the entire realm, the only piece of land not under Qin Shaozong's control was Qingzhou, the home base of Nangong Xiong.","Before Qin Shaozong could make his next move, Nangong Xiong came to the northern military camp in the dead of night. The two of them talked inside the command tent for more than an hour, and finally walked out side by side, both smiling and appearing perfectly pleased with the discussion.","When news of the recapture of Jingzhou and Yizhou reached the imperial court, Empress Dowager Wang could not sit still for a single moment.","Now that Liu Zhan was defeated, there was no one left in the whole realm who could check Qin Shaozong's power. The problem was no longer simply whether the young emperor would lose his authority - it was whether he would even keep his life.","If they did not step down, they would die. If they yielded the throne, they might still get to live out the rest of their days in comfort and plenty.","It was not a difficult decision to make. When Qin Shaozong returned to the capital in triumph after the campaign, an imperial edict for the emperor to abdicate the throne in his favor was issued.","\"...The realm under heaven is not the domain of a single individual, but the shared domain of all people under heaven. Only a virtuous ruler can occupy the throne to ensure the eternal stability of the state and the well-being of all countless subjects. Today, Qin Changgeng, the Marquis of Wu'an of the Qin clan, possesses the literary talent to secure the nation and the military prowess to pacify its borders. All within the four seas look to him with admiration and pledge their allegiance; this is truly the mandate of Heaven and the will of the people...\"","According to historical records, Emperor Yanren abdicated the throne to Emperor Taizu of Ning in the 45th year of Yongde, bringing the Great Yan Dynasty to a complete end. A brand new, world-renowned Great Ning Dynasty, as dazzling as a bright pearl in the pages of history, slowly unfurled its grand chapter.","The 45th year of Yongde was also the first year of Shengjing, when Emperor Taizu of Ning ascended the imperial throne. On the very same day of the same month and year, Dai Li, the biological mother of Emperor Chengzong of Ning, was conferred the title of Empress Shengwu. From then on, the two sovereigns ruled the realm side by side.","...","Dai Li, clad in the formal imperial robes of an empress, ascended the Wangxing Terrace in the imperial palace together with Qin Shaozong. Standing at this high vantage point, they could clearly overlook the entire imperial city and the rolling landscapes stretching far into the distance.","Gazing at the beautiful scenes spread across the city, Qin Shaozong pulled the person beside him into his arms and said joyfully, \"My lady, our empire's land is as picturesque as a fine painting.\"","\"Your words are a little premature,\" Dai Li said with a soft laugh. \"The new dynasty is still in a state of disarray after years of upheaval. We can only claim our land is truly picturesque once we have restored and rebuilt everything.\"","\"You are right...\"","[I have sailed through countless trials and hardships, no longer carrying the recklessness and impulsiveness of my younger days. I know full well that a chasm once lay between us, and I understand clearly the price we must pay to stay together through every season. Even so, I still want to break through every obstacle, to walk hand in hand with you until our hair turns white in old age.]"]}]);
